hadiths[2856]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i informed us in Mecca, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Maysarah told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us The reciter Yazid, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, Ibn Ajlan told me, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most perfect of believers in faith are those with the best character.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1 - The author did not talk about it, and it is true"
"2","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most perfect of believers in faith are those with the best character.” This is an authentic hadith that was not narrated in The two Sahihs, and it is authentic according to the condition of Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj, as he cited hadiths by al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Muhammad. Ibn Amr, and he cited Muhammad Ibn Ajlan as evidence: “This hadith was also narrated, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. And Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, on the authority of Anas. It was narrated by Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Aisha. And I fear that Abu Qalabah did not hear it, on the authority of Aisha.”"
"3","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Balj, and Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Sulaym, who is Abu Balj, and this is the wording. The hadith of Abu Dawud, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun, speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever is pleased to find... The sweetness of faith, so let a person love only for the sake of Allah.” This hadith was not included in the two Sahih books, and they were all cited as evidence by Amr ibn Maymun. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Muslim cited Abu Balaj as evidence, and it is an authentic hadith for which no defect is preserved.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 3 - It is not used as evidence, meaning Abu Balaj"
"4","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas Al-Qatbani, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, that Omar went out to the mosque one day and found Muadh ibn Jabal at the grave of the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was crying, so he said: What makes you cry, Muadh? He said: A hadith I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, makes me cry. He says: “The slightest bit of hypocrisy is polytheism, and whoever is hostile to God’s saints has committed God prevailed in battle. Indeed, God loves the righteous, the pious, and the hidden, who, even if they are absent, are not missed, and if they are present, they are not recognized. “Their hearts are lamps of guidance, they emerge from every darkness.” “This is an authentic hadith and it was not narrated in the two Sahih books. They all used Zayd bin Aslam as evidence, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Companions, and they all agreed on Using as evidence the hadith of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas Al-Qabbani, and this is an authentic Egyptian chain of narration, and no defect is preserved for it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4 - It is true and has no defect"
"5","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Abu Al-Tahir told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Maysara told me, on the authority of Abu Hani al-Khawlani, Humaid bin Hani, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, faith creates in the inside of one of you just as a garment creates character. So ask God to renew faith in your hearts.” “This is a hadith that was not narrated in the two Sahih books, and its narrators were trustworthy Egyptians. Muslim argued in the Sahih with the hadith that he narrated on the authority of Ibn Abi Umar. On the authority of Al-Muqri, on the authority of Haywa, on the authority of Abu Hani, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, God Almighty wrote down the destinies of creation before He created the heavens and the earth” (Hadith).
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 5 - Its narrators are trustworthy"
"6","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told me, Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Anbari told me, Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, On the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If The servant’s sin has a black spot marked on his heart. If he repents, he will be cleansed of it. If he returns, it will increase until it becomes greater in his heart. That is the Ran that God Almighty mentioned him: “No, but it settled over their hearts” [Al-Muttaffin: 14]. This is an authentic hadith that was not narrated in the two Sahih books, and Muslim used as evidence the hadiths of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 6 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary in this place"
"7","Imam Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued to be asked about the Hour until it was revealed: ‘Why do you remember it to your Lord? Its end} [Al-Nazi’at: 44] “.” This is a hadith that was not included in the two Sahih books, and it is preserved and authentic according to their conditions together. They were together cited as evidence by the hadiths of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa’id, that they bore witness against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If the servant says: No There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest. His Lord spoke the truth to him, saying: My servant spoke the truth, there is no god but Me and I alone. And when he said: There is no god but God Alone, with no partner. His Lord spoke the truth to him when he said: My servant spoke the truth. There is no god but Me, and I have no partner. And when he said: There is no god but God, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him belongs Praise, he said: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no god but I. Mine is dominion and praise is mine. And when he said: There is no god but God and there is no power nor strength except in God. He said: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no power or strength except through Me. This is an authentic hadith that was not included in the two Sahih books, and they all used as evidence the hadith of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Abu Saeed, They all agreed on the evidence based on the hadiths of Israel ibn Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8 - Shu’bah and others stopped him"
"9","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he told me Amer bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Maafiri al-Hubli, said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin al-Aas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings be upon him: “Indeed, God will single out a man from my nation as the head of creation on the Day of Resurrection, and will spread over him ninety-nine records, each record Like this, then he says: Do you deny any of this? Have you been wronged by my memorizing scribes? He says: No, O Lord. Then He says: Do you have an excuse? So he says: No, O Lord, and he says: Yes, you have done us a good deed, and there has been no injustice done to you today. So he brings out a card in which I bear witness that there is no wrong done to you today. There is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He says: O Lord, what is this card with these records? He said: You are not being wronged. He said: So the records were placed on a palm, and the card was on a palm, so the records were scattered and the card was heavy, and it was not heavy with it. The name of God is something. This is an authentic hadith that was not narrated in the two Sahih books, and it is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, as he cited Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli as evidence, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas, Aamir Ibn Yahya Masri, trustworthy, Al-Layth Ibn Saad, an imam, and Yunus Al-Muaddeeb: trustworthy, agreed to narrate it. In the two Sahihs “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 9 - This is according to Muslim’s condition"
"10","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews divided into seventy-one groups or seventy-two sects, and the Christians are like that, and my nation will be divided into seventy-three sects.” This is a hadith that is abundant in principles. “It has been narrated On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Abdullah bin Amr, and Awf bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Muslim cited Muhammad ibn Amr as evidence, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and they all agreed to use al-Fadl ibn Musa as evidence, and he is trustworthy. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 10 - Muslim did not invoke Muhammad ibn Amr alone, but rather by joining him with others."
"11","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari narrated to us about Marw, Ibrahim bin Hilal narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq narrated to us, Al-Hussein narrated to us. Ibn Waqid, Muhammad Ibn Salih Ibn Hani told us, Abu Sa`id Muhammad Ibn Shazan told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Fadl Ibn Musa, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The covenant between us Among them is prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission and no defect is known to it in any way. They all cited Abdullah bin Buraidah as evidence, on the authority of his father, Muslim used Al-Hussein bin Waqid as evidence, but they did not narrate it using this wording, and this hadith is authentic evidence for both of their conditions.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 11 - It is true and no defect is known to it"
"12","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Qais bin Unif told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not see any deeds.” Abandoning it out of disbelief other than prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 12 - He did not talk about it, and its chain of transmission is valid"
"13","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever commits a crime, God will hasten it for him.” His punishment in this world, God is more just than to praise His servant’s punishment in the Hereafter, and whoever commits a wrongdoing, God will protect him and pardon him. God is too generous to go back on something He has pardoned.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and they all cited Abu Juhayfa, on the authority of Ali, and they agreed on Abu Ishaq, and they all invoked Al-Hajjaj bin Muhammad, and Muslim protested against Yunus bin Abi Ishaq.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 13 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"14","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jawhari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Yusuf told us, Al-Nadr bin Muhammad, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, Iyas bin Salamah told us, my father told me, that he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he came to him. A man with a horse of his own, led by Aqoq, and with a foal of his own following her, and he said: Who are you? He said: “I am a prophet.” He said: What is a prophet? He said: “Messenger of God.” He said: When will the Hour come? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is unseen, and no one knows the unseen except God.” He said: Show me your sword, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him his sword. The man shook him and then returned it to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But you were not able to do what you wanted.” He said: And it was. . . He said: Go to him and ask him about these qualities. “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it, and they all agreed on the proof through Iyas bin Salamah. On the authority of his father, and Muslim cited this particular chain of transmission as evidence, and he narrated it, on the authority of Ahmad ibn Yusuf, without a hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 14 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"15","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he told us Awf bin Abi Jamila, and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Khalas, and Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever goes to a fortune teller or soothsayer and believes him in what He says, “He has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “This is an authentic hadith, according to all of their conditions, from the hadith of Ibn Sirin, and they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari narrated, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Ruh, on the authority of Awf, On the authority of Khalas, and Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the story of Musa that he turned away.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 15 - According to their condition"
"16","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub, the memorizer of dictation, told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Quraysh bin Anas told us, Habib bin The martyr, and Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Al-Shahid, Humayd Ibn Hilal told us, Hassan Ibn Kahil told us, and in the hadith of Ibn Abi Adiy Kahn, he said: I sat in a gathering in which Abd al-Rahman Ibn Samurah, and I do not know him, so he said: Muadh bin Jabal told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and his family and grant them peace, said: “There is not a soul on earth that dies who does not die.” “If she associates anything with God, bearing witness that I am the Messenger of God, this will return to a heart that is certain that God will forgive her.” He said: So I said: Did you hear from Muadh? Then the people rebuked me, so he said: Leave him, for he did not speak badly. Yes, I heard it from Muadh ibn Jabal. Muadh claimed that he heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith. Trustworthy people have circulated it, but not all of them reported it with this wording. What I have - and God knows best - is that they neglected it for Hassan. Ibn Kahil, and it is said: the son of a soothsayer, because only Humaid Ibn Hilal Al-Adawi is known to have narrated from him. Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned that Qurrah ibn Khalid also narrated from him, and they were all narrated on the authority of a group of trustworthy people who had no narrator. Except one, so they are obliged to bring out something like it, and God knows best.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 16 - Hasan, authenticated by Ibn Hibban"
"17","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad bin Mutarrif, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiya, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Modesty And shame are two branches of faith, and obscenity and rhetoric are two branches of hypocrisy.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and they used its narrations on the authority of the last of them as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 17 - This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs"
"18","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, told us. Zuhair bin Muhammad, on the authority of Salih bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Umamah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The vulgarity of faith, the vulgarity of the faith.” “A Muslim has invoked Salih ibn Abi Salih al-Samman as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 18 - Muslim protested against Saleh"
"19","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Yahya Sulaym bin Amer said: I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Worship your Lord, pray your five daily prayers, fast every month, pay the zakat on your wealth, and obey those who command you. You will enter the Paradise of your Lord.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and we do not know of any reason for it, and they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari and Muslim used the hadiths of Sulaym bin Amir as evidence. And all of its narrators are agreed upon.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 19 - According to Muslim’s condition and we do not know of any reason for it"
"20","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Asadi in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu`bah told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Salamah, speaking, on the authority of Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, who said: A Jew said to his friend: Take us to this Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and ask him about this verse: {And We gave Moses nine clear signs} [Al-Isra: 101] and he said: No. You call him a prophet, for if he had heard you, he would have four eyes. He said: So he asked him, and he said: “Do not associate anything with God, and do not steal, and do not Do not commit adultery, and do not kill the soul that God has forbidden except in a just manner, and do not commit sorcery, and do not consume usury, and do not go with an innocent person to someone with authority to kill him. And do not slander a chaste woman, and you, Jews, have a special obligation not to transgress on the Sabbath.” So they kissed his hand and his foot, and said: We bear witness that you are a prophet. He said: “What prevented you from surrendering?” They said: David, peace be upon him, prayed that a prophet would not cease from his descendants, and we fear that the Jews will kill us. This is an authentic hadith. We know of his fault in one way or another, but they did not narrate it, nor did Al-Safwan ibn Assal mention a single hadith. I heard Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, and Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah asked him, and he said: Why did they leave the hadith of Safwan bin Assal at all? He said: “Because the way to him was spoiled.” Al-Hakim said: “Abu Abdullah meant by this the hadith of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, because they left Asim bin Bahdala. As for Abdullah bin Salama Al-Muradi, also called Al-Hamdani, and his nickname is Abu Al-Aliyah, for he is one of the great companions of Ali and Abdullah. He narrated on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Jabir bin Abdullah, and other companions. Abu Al-Zubayr Al-Makki narrated on his authority. And a group of followers
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 20 - It is true and we do not know its reason"
"21","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told me, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told me, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told me, Ibn Abi Dhib told me, On the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “By God, he does not believe, and God does not believe.” He believes, but God does not believe.” They said: What is that, O Messenger of God? He said: “A neighbor from whose calamities his neighbor is not safe.” They said: What are his calamities? He said: “His evil.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this. Rather, they narrated the hadith of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He who does not feel safe from his neighbor’s calamities will not enter Paradise.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 21 - In the two Sahihs there is something like this for the lame"
"22","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Salman the two jurists told us, saying: Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan told me, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the believer is the one from whom the people are safe, with their blood and their property safe.” They agreed to exclude one party. The hadith: “A Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe,” and they did not include this addition, but it is valid according to the condition of a Muslim, and in this “The hadith is another addition to his condition, which they did not mention.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 22 - Muslim did not publish the second half"
"23","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told me, he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most complete of the believers is the one from whose tongue the Muslims are safe.” And his hand. “And another valid addition to their condition, but they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 23 - The most perfect of believers did not emerge"
"24","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan bin Ahmad al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam, and Abdullah bin Saleh said: Al-Layth told us, Abu Hani Al-Khawlani told me, on the authority of Amr bin Malik Al-Laythi, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Shall I not inform you of the believer? He is the one to whom people trust themselves and their property, the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the Mujahid is the one who strives himself in “Obedience, and the emigrant is one who renounces sins and sins” and another addition to the condition of a Muslim, and does not expel them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 24 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"25","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, And Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A believer is one whom people feel safe from, and a Muslim is one whom Muslims are safe from.” From his tongue and his hand, and the emigrant is he who shuns evil, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, no servant will enter Paradise from whose harm his neighbor is not safe.” “Another addition, authentic and sound, from the narration of the wounded in the text of this hadith, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 25 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"26","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Suleiman bin Harb told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Amr Muhammad told me Ibn Jafar Al-Adl, Yahya Ibn Muhammad told us, Ubayd Allah Ibn Muadh told us, Ubayy told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, he said: Abdullah Ibn Mu’adh told me. Al-Harith, and he praised him well, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, and he said: “Beware of injustice, for injustice will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of indecency and indecency, and beware of miserliness, for only those who were Before you were stingy. He commanded them to sever one another, and they severed it. And miserliness, so they became miserly. And immorality, so they became immoral. Then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, that is. Is Islam better? He said: “That the Muslims will be safe from your tongue and your hand.” That man or someone else said: O Messenger of God, which migration is best? He said: “To abandon what your Lord dislikes.” He said: “And migration is two migrations: the migration of the present, and the migration of the deserter, so the migration of the deserter: to respond When he is called, and he obeys when commanded, and the emigration of the present is the greatest calamity and the best reward.” They all narrated the hadith of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, in brief, but they did not narrate this hadith, and they agreed on Amr bin Murrah and Abd Allah bin Al-Harith Al-Najrani. As for Abu Kathir Zuhayr bin Al-Aqmar Al-Zubaidi, he heard Ali and Abdullah and the Companions after them. This exact hadith is narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah [p. 56]."
"27","Ali bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban told us, Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Fudayl bin Iyad, On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zuhair bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of injustice,” and he mentioned the hadith in its length. “And for these additions that we mentioned on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr” is valid evidence of Muslim’s condition from the narration of Abu Hurairah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 26 - They agreed on Amr on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Najrani. As for Abu Katheer Zuhair bin Al-Aqmar Al-Zubaidi, he heard Ali and Abdullah, and Al-A’mash narrated it on the authority of Amr"
"28","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, and Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ishaq - and the pronunciation for him - Ahmad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Milhan told us, Ibn Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of indecency and obscenity, for God He does not like the obscene and the obscene, and beware of injustice, for it will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of miserliness, for it was called upon by those before you. So they shed their blood, and those before you called upon them, so they severed their ties of kinship, and those before you called upon them, so they made lawful their sanctities.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 28 - Narrated by Al-Layth and Al-Nabil on his authority"
"29","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub al-Faqih told us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib told us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is not one who stabs, nor curses, nor is obscene, nor “The obscene one.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They used these narrators as evidence from the last of them, then they did not narrate it. The most that can be said is In it, there is no one among the companions of Al-A’mash and Isra’il ibn Yunus Al-Subai’i, their chief and master, and Al-A’mash participated in a group of His sheikhs, so it is not denied that he is unique in this hadith. And the hadith has another witness to their condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 29 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"30","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us: from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi: from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: from his father: from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"The believer is not a slanderer (ta'yan), nor a curser (la'an), nor obscene (fahish), nor vulgar (badhi)."""" """"And this hadith has a second witness, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, which must be mentioned even though its chain is not on the condition of the two Shaykhs (Bukhari and Muslim)."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 30 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis.There is another witness regarding this hadith from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i. It must be mentioned, even if its chain of transmission does not meet the conditions of the two Sheikhs."
"31","Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mati informed us in Kufa: al-Husayn ibn al-Hakim al-Hiri narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us: Sabah ibn Yahya narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Layla: from al-Hakam: from Ibrahim: from Alqamah: from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: """"The believer is not a slanderer, nor obscene, nor vulgar."""" """"Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, even though he is attributed with poor memory, is one of the jurists of Islam and their virtuous ones, and from the elders of the children of the Companions and the Followers from the Ansar, may Allah's mercy be upon them."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 31 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"32","Abu Muhammad Da'laq ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi narrated to us in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sayigh narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us: from Amr, mawla of al-Muttalib: from al-Muttalib: from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Whoever does a bad deed and hates it when he does it, and does a good deed and rejoices in it, he is a believer."""" """"They have cited the narrators of this hadith, the last of them, and it is authentic on their condition, but they did not output it; rather they output it in the sermon of Umar ibn al-Khattab: 'Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed, he is a believer,' and it has a witness with this wording."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 32 - On the condition of the two (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"33","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Saffar informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qadi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: from Zayd ibn Salam: from his grandfather Mamtur: from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked by a man, who said: O Messenger of Allah, what is faith (iman)? He said: """"When your good deed pleases you and your bad deed grieves you, then you are a believer."""" He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sin (ithm)? He said: """"When something troubles your chest, then leave it."""" And thus narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak and Ma'mar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 33 - Ma'mar and Ali ibn al-Mubarak followed him, and it is on the condition of the two. As for the hadith of Ali ibn al-Mubarak..."
"34","Makram ibn Ahmad al-Qadi narrated to us: Abu Qilabah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir informed me: from Zayd ibn Salam: from his grandfather Abu Salam, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): What is faith? He said: """"When your good deed pleases you and your bad deed grieves you, then you are a believer."""" And as for the hadith of Ma'mar..."
"35","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San'ani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: from Zayd ibn Salam: from Abu Salam: from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: What is faith? He said: """"Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed, he is a believer."""" """"All these hadiths are authentic, connected, on the condition of the two Shaykhs."""""
"36","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jabir informed me: he said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir say: I heard Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i say: We camped with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at a place, so I woke up at night, and I saw nothing in the camp longer than the rear of my saddle; every person and his camel had stuck to the ground. So I went among the people until I reached the Prophet's (peace be upon him) sleeping place, but he was not in it. I placed my hand on the bedding, and it was cold. So I went out among the people saying: {Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return} [al-Baqarah: 156] - the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has been taken away. Until I went out of the entire camp, I looked at a darkness and threw a stone, and I went to the darkness, and behold, it was Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. And there was a sound before us like the humming of a millstone, or like the sound of pebbles when the wind hits them. Some of us said to others: O people, stay put until morning comes or the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) comes to you. He said: We stayed as Allah willed, then he called out: """"Is there Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and Awf ibn Malik?"""" We said: Yes, indeed. So he came to us, and we walked with him, not asking him about anything nor informing him of anything. He sat on his bedding and said: """"Do you know what my Lord gave me a choice of tonight?"""" We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: """"He gave me a choice between admitting half of my Ummah into Paradise, and intercession. So I chose intercession."""" We said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among its people. He said: """"It is for every Muslim."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of Muslim, and they did not output it. Its narrators are all trustworthy on the condition of both of them, and it has no defect. And there is nothing in the other reports of intercession saying 'it is for every Muslim'."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 36 - On the condition of the two."
"37","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us. And Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi informed us in Marw: Ahmad ibn Sayyar narrated to us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us. They said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Najih: from his father: from Ibn Abbas, who said: """"The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) never fought a people until he invited them."""" """"This hadith is authentic from the hadith of al-Thawri, and they did not output it. And Muslim cited Abu Najih, the father of Abdullah, whose name is Yasar, and he is from the mawali of the Meccans."""" And it has been narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with this wording. And they both agreed on outputting the hadith of Abdullah ibn Awn: 'I wrote to Nafi', mawla of Abdullah ibn Umar, asking him about fighting before invitation, so he wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq... the hadith, and in it: the invitation was before the fighting.' [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 37 - Muslim cited Abu Najih Yasar al-Makki."
"38","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ali al-Sirafi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Salama ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us: he heard Rabi'ah ibn Abbad al-Du'ali say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at Mina in their dwellings before he migrated to Medina, saying: """"O people, Allah commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him."""" He said: And behind him was a man saying: """"O people, this man commands you to leave the religion of your fathers."""" So I asked: Who is this man? They said: Abu Lahab. """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of the two Shaykhs, and its narrators to the last of them are trustworthy, reliable. Perhaps they or one of them imagined that Rabi'ah ibn Abbad has no narrator other than Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, and Abu al-Zinad Abdullah ibn Dhakwan has also narrated this exact hadith from him."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 38 - On the condition of the two."
"39","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab informed us, in Hamdan: Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us: my father informed me: Rabi'ah ibn Abbad al-Du'ali informed me: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in the Jahiliyyah at the market of Dhu al-Majaz, and he was saying: """"O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will succeed."""" He said: He repeated it many times, and the people were gathered around him following him. And behind him was a man, cross-eyed, with two braids, bright-faced, saying: """"He is a Sabian, a liar."""" So I asked: Who is this? They said: His uncle, Abu Lahab. """"And I only cited Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad following them, for they both cited him together."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 39 - Rather I cited Ibn Abi al-Zinad, for they both cited him."
"40","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Salih ibn Rustam narrated to us: from Ibn Abi Mulaykah: from Aisha, who said: An old woman came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was with me. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: """"Who are you?"""" She said: I am Jaththamah al-Muzaniyyah. He said: """"Rather you are Hassnah al-Muzaniyyah. How are you? How is your condition? How were you after us?"""" She said: Good, by my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah. When she left, I said: O Messenger of Allah, you turn to this old woman with such attention? He said: """"She used to visit us during Khadijah's time, and keeping good ties is from faith."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of the two Shaykhs, for they agreed on citing its narrators in many hadiths, and it has no defect."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 40 - On the condition of the two and it has no defect."
"41","Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Anbari narrated to us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Karabisi informed us: Safwan ibn Salih al-Dimashqi narrated to us. They said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us: from Abu al-Zinad: from al-A'raj: from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them enters Paradise. He is Witr (One) and loves the Witr - He is Allah - there is no god but Him: al-Rahman, al-Rahim, al-Malik, al-Quddus, al-Salam, al-Mu'min, al-Muhaymin, al-Aziz, al-Jabbar, al-Mutakabbir, al-Khaliq, al-Bari, al-Musawwir, al-Ghaffar, al-Qahhar, al-Wahhab, al-Razzaq, al-Fattah, al-Alim, al-Qabid, al-Basit, al-Khafid, al-Rafi', al-Mu'izz, al-Mudhill, al-Sami', al-Basir, al-Hakam, al-Adl, al-Latif, al-Khabir, al-Halim, al-Azim, al-Ghafur, al-Shakur, al-Ali, al-Kabir, al-Hafiz, al-Mughith."""" And Safwan said in his hadith: al-Muqit. And to this went Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq in Mukhtasar al-Sahih: al-Hasib, al-Jalil, al-Karim, al-Raqib, al-Mujib, al-Wasi', al-Hakim, al-Wadud, al-Majid, al-Ba'ith, al-Shahid, al-Haqq, al-Wakil, al-Qawiyy, al-Matin, al-Waliyy, al-Hamid, al-Muhsi, al-Mubdi, al-Mu'id, al-Muhyi, al-Mumit, al-Hayy, al-Qayyum, al-Wajid, al-Majid, al-Wahid, al-Samad, al-Qadir, al-Muqtadir, al-Muqaddim, al-Mu'akhkhir, al-Awwal, al-Akhir, al-Zahir, al-Batin, al-Wali, al-Muta'ali, al-Barr, al-Tawwab, al-Muntaqim, al-Afuww, al-Ra'uf, Malik al-Mulk, Dhu al-Jalal wa al-Ikram, al-Muqsit, al-Jami', al-Ghani, al-Mughni, al-Mani', al-Darr, al-Nafi', al-Nur, al-Hadi, al-Badi', al-Baqi, al-Warith, al-Rashid, al-Sabur."""" """"This is a hadith they both output in the two Sahihs with authentic chains, without mentioning the names in it. The defect with them is that al-Walid ibn Muslim singled out narrating it at length, and mentioned the names in it, and no one else mentioned them. And this is not a defect, for I know no difference among the imams of hadith that al-Walid ibn Muslim is more trustworthy, more precise, more knowledgeable, and greater than Abu al-Yaman, Bishr ibn Shu'ayb, Ali ibn Ayyash, and their peers among the companions of Shu'ayb. Then we looked and found the hadith has been narrated by Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Hisham ibn Hassan together, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him) at length."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 41 - They did not output the names due to al-Walid's singularity with them, and that is not a defect, for al-Walid is more trustworthy and precise than Abu al-Yaman and Ali ibn Ayyash."
"42","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab narrated to us, in Hamdan: the Amir Abu al-Haytham Khalid ibn Ahmad al-Duhli narrated to us, in Hamdan: Abu Asad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Balkhi narrated to us: Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani and Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: they said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sufyan al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn ibn al-Tarjuman narrated to us: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us: from Muhammad ibn Sirin: from Abu Hurayrah: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names. Whoever enumerates them enters Paradise: Allah, al-Rahman, al-Rahim, al-Ilah, al-Rabb, al-Malik, al-Quddus, al-Salam, al-Mu'min, al-Muhaymin, al-Aziz, al-Jabbar, al-Mutakabbir, al-Khaliq, al-Bari, al-Musawwir, al-Halim, al-Alim, al-Sami', al-Basir, al-Hayy, al-Qayyum, al-Wasi', al-Latif, al-Khabir, al-Hannan, al-Mannan, al-Badi', al-Wadud, al-Ghafur, al-Shakur, al-Majid, al-Mubdi, al-Mu'id, al-Nur, al-Awwal, al-Akhir, al-Zahir, al-Batin, al-Ghaffar, al-Wahhab, al-Qadir, al-Ahad, al-Samad, al-Kafi, al-Baqi, al-Wakil, al-Majid, al-Mughith, al-Da'im, al-Muta'ali, Dhu al-Jalal wa al-Ikram, al-Mawla, al-Nasir, al-Haqq, al-Mubin, al-Ba'ith, al-Mujib, al-Muhyi, al-Mumit, al-Jamil, al-Sadiq, al-Hafiz, al-Kabir, al-Qarib, al-Raqib, al-Fattah, al-Tawwab, al-Qadim, al-Witr, al-Fatir, al-Razzaq, al-Allam, al-Ali, al-Azim, al-Ghani, al-Malik, al-Muqtadir, al-Akram, al-Ra'uf, al-Mudabbir, al-Malik, al-Qadir, al-Hadi, al-Shakir, al-Rafi', al-Shahid, al-Wahid, Dhu al-Tawl, Dhu al-Ma'arij, Dhu al-Fadl, al-Khallaq, al-Kafil, al-Jalil, al-Karim."""" """"This hadith is preserved from the hadith of Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, abbreviated without mentioning the additional names in it. All of them are in the Quran. And Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Tarjuman is trustworthy, even though they did not output him. And I only made it a witness for the first hadith."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 42 - Rather they weakened him, meaning Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Tarjuman."
"43","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, in Hamdan: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn Babawaih narrated to us: they said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us: Affan, Muhammad ibn Kathir, and Abu Amr al-Hawzi narrated to us: they said: Shu'bah narrated to us: Salimah ibn Kuhayl informed me: he said: I heard Isa - a man from Banu Asad - narrating, from Zirr: from Abdullah: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Superstition (tiyarah) is shirk, but Allah Almighty removes it by trust (tawakkul)."""" """"And this Isa is: Ibn Abi Asim al-Asadi, Kufan, trustworthy."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 43 - Isa ibn Abi Asim is trustworthy."
"44","Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz narrated to us with the authenticity of what we mentioned: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah informed me: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Khallad al-Bahili narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Shu'bah: from Salimah ibn Kuhayl: from Isa ibn Asim: from Zirr: from Abdullah: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Superstition is from shirk, and a safe haven, but Allah removes it by trust."""" """"This hadith is authentic in its chain, its narrators are trustworthy, and they did not output it."""" And Isa ibn Asim al-Asadi has also narrated from Adi ibn Thabit and others. And Shu'bah, Jarir ibn Hazim, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih and others have narrated from him."
"45","Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad, and Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: they said: Yahya ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Jarir informed us: from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah al-Nakha'i: from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Whoever swears by other than Allah has disbelieved."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of the two Shaykhs, for they cited the like of this chain and output it in the Book, and it has no defect, and they did not output it. And it has a witness on the condition of Muslim, for he cited Sharik ibn Abd Allah al-Nakha'i."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 45 - On the condition of the two; Ibn Rahwayh narrated it from him like this."
"46","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Amr ibn Mansur al-Adl narrated to us: they said: Amr ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali informed us: Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah: from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah: from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: """"Every oath sworn by other than Allah is shirk."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 46 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"47","Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Tuqani narrated to us: Abu Yahya Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Maysarah al-Makki narrated to us. And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar and Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: they said: Bishr ibn Musa informed us. They said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Abu al-Aliyah came to me and a companion of mine, and said: Come, for you two are younger and more retentive of hadith than me. So he went with us until we came to Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi. He said: Narrate to these two your hadith. Nasr said: Uqbah ibn Malik narrated to us, and he was from his tribe. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent a military detachment, so they raided a people. A man from the people strayed, and a man from the detachment followed him with his sword drawn. The stray man said: I am Muslim. He did not pay attention to it, so he struck him and killed him. The news reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he said a severe word, and it reached the killer. While the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was delivering a sermon, the killer said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the one who said it only said it seeking refuge from being killed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him of the people and continued his sermon. Then he said it a second time: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the one who said it only said it seeking refuge from being killed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned away from him and from those before him of the people and continued his sermon. Then he could not bear but to say it a third time: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, the one who said it only said it seeking refuge from being killed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned to him, and distress was recognized in his face, then he said: """"Allah Almighty has refused for me the one who kills a believer."""" He said it three times. """"This hadith is output like it in the authentic Musnad of Muslim, for he cited Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah. As for Uqbah ibn Malik al-Laythi, he is a Companion whose hadith is output in the books of the imams in existence. And I have clarified my condition at the beginning of the book that I output the hadith of the Companions from the last of them, if the path to them is authentic. And Yunus ibn Ubayd has followed Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah in narrating from Humayd on the condition of Muslim."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 47 - On the condition of Muslim."
"48","Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Qadi informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Humayd narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: from Yunus ibn Ubayd: from Humayd ibn Hilal: from Bishr ibn Asim: from Uqbah ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: """"After that, what is the matter with a man who kills a man while he says: I am Muslim?"""" The killer said: O Messenger of Allah, he only said it seeking refuge. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said thus and disliked his statement, and turned his face away from him. Then he said: """"Allah has refused for the one who kills a Muslim, Allah has refused for the one who kills a Muslim."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 48 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"49","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Yahya al-Adami narrated to us, in Baghdad: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Awwam narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammam informed us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us. And Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Habban al-Ansari informed us: Abu al-Walid and Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: they said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us: from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, who said: Shaybah al-Khudari informed me: that he witnessed Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Three things I swear to: Allah does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share. The shares of Islam are fasting, prayer, and charity. And Allah does not take charge of a servant then entrust him to other than Him on the Day of Resurrection. And a man does not love a people except Allah makes him with them. And the fourth, if I swore to it, I would hope not to sin: Whatever Allah covers for a servant in the world, He will cover for him in the Hereafter."""" Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: When you hear a hadith like this narrated by Urwah from Aisha, then preserve it. Shaybah al-Hadrami, al-Bukhari output him, and he said in al-Tarikh: And he is called al-Khudari. He heard Urwah and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. And this hadith is authentic in chain and they did not output it."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 49 - Nothing was output for him, meaning Shaybah al-Hadrami, except by al-Nasa'i; this hadith has obscurity in it."
"50","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub al-Faqih narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us. And Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us. And Ali ibn Isa narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us. They said: Hushaym narrated to us: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind: from Abi Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad: from Fadalah al-Laythi, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: I want Islam, so teach me some laws of Islam. He mentioned prayer, the month of Ramadan, and the times of prayer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you mention hours in which I am occupied. But teach me a comprehensive statement. He said: """"If you are occupied, then do not be occupied from the two 'Asrs."""" I said: And what are the two 'Asrs? And it was not in my people's language. He said: """"Fajr and Asr."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of Muslim, and they did not output it. In it are wordings they did not output with another chain. Most beneficial of them is the mention of the laws of Islam, for it is in the hadith of Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Dawud, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, and it is not on the condition of one of them. And Hushaym ibn Bashir was contradicted in this chain from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, a contradiction that does not harm the hadith but rather strengthens it."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 50 - On the condition of Muslim."
"51","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us. And Ali ibn Isa narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us. They said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: from Dawud: from Abi Harb: from Abd Allah ibn Fadalah: from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me, and among what he taught me was that he said: """"Guard the five prayers."""" I said: These are hours in which I have occupation. So tell me a comprehensive matter that if I do it, it suffices me. He said: """"Guard the two 'Asrs."""" He said: And it was not in our language. I said: And what are the two 'Asrs? He said: """"A prayer before the rising of the sun, and a prayer before its setting."""" """"And Abi Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili is a major Tabi'i, with him from the major Companions, his hearing from Fadalah ibn Ubayd al-Laythi is not limited. For Hushaym ibn Bashir is a preserver known for preservation, and Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti is a man of a book. And this in general is like what Muslim output in the Book of Faith: the hadith of Shu'bah from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhib, and after him from Muhammad ibn Uthman from his father."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 51 - And Hushaym was contradicted; Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated it from Abi Harb from Abd Allah ibn Fadalah from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me."
"52","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anazi informed me: Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us. They said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us: from Khalid ibn Ma'dan: from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Indeed Islam has a light and a minaret like the minaret of the road."""" """"This hadith is authentic on the condition of al-Bukhari, for he narrated from Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani and cited Thawr ibn Yazid al-Shami. As for Khalid ibn Ma'dan's hearing from Abu Hurayrah, it is not far-fetched, for al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated from Thawr ibn Yazid from him that he said: I met seventeen men from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). And perhaps a doubter doubts that this text is anomalous. Let him look in the two Books to find among the anomalous texts that have only one chain what he wonders at, then let him measure this against them. Another hadith with this chain."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 52 - Not far-fetched that Khalid met Abu Hurayrah."
"53","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: from Thawr ibn Yazid: from Khalid ibn Ma'dan: from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: """"Islam is that you worship Allah, not associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, enjoin good, forbid evil, and greet your family. Whoever falls short of any of them has left a share of Islam. And whoever leaves all of them has turned his back on Islam."""" """"This hadith is like the first in uprightness."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 53 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"54","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, in Hamdan: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ali informed me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Shall I not teach you - or he said: Shall I not guide you - to a word from under the Throne, from the treasures of Paradise? You say: There is no power and no strength except with Allah. Then Allah Almighty says: My servant has submitted and surrendered."""" """"This hadith is authentic and no defect is preserved for it, and they did not output it. And Muslim cited Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym."""" [Comment from Talkhis al-Dhahabi] 54 - Authentic, no defect for it."
"55","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told me, and Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq, they said: Ali bin Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, and Abu Ali al-Hussein bin Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Abbas Al-Bajli, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad mentioned, he said: My father told me, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If two men entered Islam and emigrated, one of them would have left Islam until the oppressor returns.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of both sheikhs, and it was not narrated by Abd Al-Samad bin Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed, trustworthy and trustworthy, and they all narrated it.” He has no hadith other than his own, on the authority of his father, Shu’bah, and others.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 55 - They emanated from him, meaning Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, a hadith that was unique to Abd al-Samad on the authority of his father and Shu’bah."
"56","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hussein Al-Hairi narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, and Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, they said: Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ ibn Yazid told us, Ibn al-Haad told us, that Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id told us that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a servant commits adultery, faith leaves him, and he is like a shadow. If he is removed from it, faith returns to him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They used its narrations as evidence, and it has a witness according to the conditions of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 56 - According to their condition"
"57","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, and Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr told us, In Baghdad, Bishr bin Musa told us, saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri told us, Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin al-Walid told us, on the authority of Ibn Hujayrah, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever commits adultery and drinks alcohol, God will remove from him Faith is like a person taking off a shirt from his head. “Muslim cited Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah and Abdullah ibn al-Walid as evidence, and they were both Levantines.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 57 - Muslim argued with Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujairah and Abdullah ibn al-Walid"
"58","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, I am Muhammad bin Ghalib, I am Musa bin Ismail, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Modesty and faith are united together, so if One of them was raised, the other was raised.” “This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions. They used its narrations as evidence and did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 58 - According to their condition"
"59","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Yahya bin Razin told us, Harun bin Marouf told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, Abu Sakhr, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is accustomed, but there is no good Among those who do not get to know each other and do not get along with each other.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 59 - The reason for this is its interruption, because this Abu Hazim is Al-Madini, not Al-Ashja’i, and he did not meet Abu Sakhr Al-Ashja’i, nor did Al-Madini meet Abu Hurairah."
"60","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Al-Nadr bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Muqaddami told us, Fudayl told us Ibn Sulaiman, Musa bin Uqba told us, he heard Ubayd Allah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no servant who worships God, does not associate anything with Him, performs prayer, pays zakat, and avoids sins except He entered Paradise. He said: So they asked him: What are the major sins? He said: “Associating partners with God, fleeing the advance, and killing oneself.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 60 - Ubayd Allah, on the authority of his father Salman Al-Aghar, only Al-Bukhari included him."
"61","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Yahya told us, I am Yazid bin Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh bin Hani, on the authority of Al-Miqdam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hani, that when he came to see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: O Messenger of God, anything? Does it require Paradise? He said: “You must speak well and give food.” “This is a straight hadith and has no defect, and they did not narrate it. The reason they have for it is that Hani bin Yazid has no narrator other than his son Shurayh. I presented the condition at the beginning of this book that if we cannot find a narrator for a well-known companion other than a single well-known Tabibi, we can use him as evidence. We authenticated his hadith, since it is authentic according to both of their conditions. Al-Bukhari had used as evidence the hadith of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Mirdas. Al-Aslami, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used as evidence the hadith of Qais, on the authority of Adi bin Amira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Who did we use it for a work? “And they have no narrator other than Qays ibn Abi Hazim. Likewise, Muslim has used as evidence the hadiths of Abu Malik al-Ashja’i, on the authority of His father and the hadiths of Majzaa bin Zahir Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, so they were all obligated to use as evidence the hadith of Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on their condition. Al-Miqdam and his father were among the largest of the followers, and Hani bin Yazid was a delegation to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 61 - It is authentic and has no defect"
"62","Just as Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Yazid bin Al-Miqdam bin Shuraih told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Shuraih bin Hani, he said: Abu Hani bin Yazid told me that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard him. May God bless him and grant him peace. They called him Abu al-Hakam, so he said: “Indeed, Allah is the Judge. Why are you nicknamed Abu al-Hakam?” He said: If my people disagree, I judge between them and both sides agree. He said: Do you have a child? He said: Shuraih, Abdullah, and Muslim Banu Hani. He said: “Who is the eldest of them?” He said: Shurayh. He said: “You are Abu Shurayh. So they prayed for him and his son.” “I mentioned in the Book of Knowledge, in mentioning veterans, Shuraih ibn Hani, for he embraced pre-Islamic times and Islam, and did not see the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he became numbered among the Successors.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 62 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"63","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Khishnam bin Al-Siddiq narrated to us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Al-Muqri narrated to us. Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Muqri told us, Harmala bin Imran Al-Tajibi told us, Abu Yunus Sulaym bin Jubayr, Abu Hurairah’s client, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited {Indeed, God has All-Hearing and All-Seeing} [An-Nisa: 58] So he placed his finger of supplication over his eyes and his thumbs over his ears. This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it. Muslim cited Harmala bin Imran and Abu Yunus as evidence, and the rest are agreed upon, and for this hadith “A witness to the condition of a Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 63 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"64","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told me, Hisham bin Saad told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It was not from There will be no temptation greater than the temptation of the Antichrist until the Hour comes, and there is no prophet but he warned his people, and I have not informed you of anything about him. A prophet before me told about it.” He put his hand on his eye and then said: “I bear witness that God Almighty is not one-eyed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 64 - It was narrated by Zuhair and Muawiyah on the authority of Zaid"
"65","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I was with the group. He said: “Do you have any money?” I said: Yes, he said: “From what money?” I said: From camels, horses, slaves, and sheep. He said: “If God gives you wealth, let him see it on you.” He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Do your people’s camels produce healthy ears, so you go to the razor and cut off their ears and say: ‘It is a sea’,” and you split them or split them open? Its skins, and you say: They are sacred, so you prohibit them for you and your family? “He said: I said: Yes. He said: “Everything that God has given you is permissible for you, and God’s helper is stronger than your helper, and God’s Moses is more powerful than your Moses.” “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission, and it was narrated by a group of Kufan imams, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and Abu Al-Za’ara’ Amr ibn Amr followed Abu Ishaq Al-Subaie’i In his narration on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, they did not narrate it; Because Malik ibn Nadlah al-Jashmi has no narrator other than his son, Abu al-Ahwas, and Muslim narrated, on the authority of 25 Abu al-Malih ibn Usama, on the authority of His father, and he has no narrator other than his son. Likewise, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, and this is more important than all of that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 65 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"66","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Abi Uthman al-Tayalisi told us, Affan told us, and Abu Salamah told us, they said: We told us: Hammad, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Hadba told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said in this verse: “And when his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He made it” [Al-A’raf: 143] “appearing from it.” Destiny of this
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 66 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"67","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Sakan, Abu Salamah told us, and Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, they said: We told him: Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read {He said, “My Lord, show me that I may look at You} [Al-Araf: 143] He said: “So he came out of the light like this, and pointed with his hand to half of the fingertip of his little finger, and struck Hammad’s chest with it.” He said: “Fasak.” The mountain. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"68","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf ibn Ya`qub told us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman told us, Musa ibn Uqba, Ubayd Allah bin Salman Al-Aghar told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ There are three whom God loves and laughs at: The one who, when a group is discovered, fights after it himself for the sake of God Almighty. This is an authentic hadith, and they cited all its narrators as evidence, and they did not narrate it. Rather, they included in this section the hadith of Abi al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abi Huraira, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “God laughs at two men.” The hadith on jihad.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 68 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"69","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Affan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, I am Muhammad. Ibn Ghalib and Muhammad Ibn Mahmoud Al-Bunani said: Abdul Aziz Ibn Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib Ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu Yahya Ibn Ja`dah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Whoever is in His heart was full of arrogance. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, I would like my clothes to be new, my head to be oily, and the straps of my sandals to be new. He said: He mentioned things until he mentioned the connection of his whip, so he said: “That is beauty, and God is beautiful and loves beauty, but arrogance is a distortion of the truth.” And he despised the people.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and they all used its narrations as evidence, and it has another witness, according to Muslim’s condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 69 - Al-Ihtijja with his narrations"
"70","Abu Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, be safe from pride. Should I wear a nice suit? He said: “God is beautiful and loves beauty.”"
"71","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, dictating, Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Ismail bin Ja’far told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God called Gabriel and sent him to Paradise, and he said: Look. And what We have prepared therein for its people. He said: By your might, no one will hear of it unless he enters it. So it is surrounded by calamities. He said: Return to it. So he looked at it and came back and said: By Your glory, I was afraid that no one would enter it. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. It was narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, with additional wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 71 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"72","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Marzuq told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God created Paradise, he said: Oh Gabriel, go and look at it. He said: So he went and looked at it, and said: No one will hear of it unless he enters it. Then he surrounded it with calamity. Then He said: Go and look at it. He said: So he went and looked at it and said: By Your glory, I feared that no one would enter it. Then He created Hell. He said: O Gabriel, go and look at it. He said: So he went and looked at it and said: No one will hear of it and enter it. He said: So he covered it. With desires, then he said: Go and look at her, he said: So he went and looked at her, and said: O Lord, by Your glory, I feared that no one would remain. Unless he enters it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 72 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"73","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani and Ibrahim ibn Ismat al-Adl told us, saying: Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad ibn Sa’id ibn Sa’id told us. Al-Asbahani, Yahya bin Yaman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and he said to her And for the earth: “Come, willingly or by compulsion.” He said to the heavens: Bring out your sun, your moon, and your stars. And He said to the earth: Divide your rivers and bring forth your fruits. They said: We will come willingly. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and the companion’s interpretation according to them is a chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 73 - According to their condition"
"74","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, with Marwa, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Malik bin Anas, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Darabardi informed me, about Marwa. Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told me, and Ahmad bin Muhammad told me Al-Anazi, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, they said: Al-Qanabi narrated to us, in what was read to Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd bin al-Khattab, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar al-Juhani, that Omar bin al-Khattab was asked about this verse, {And when he took Your Lord is from the children of Adam, from their backs, their descendants} [Al-A’raf: 172]. Omar bin Al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, being asked On her authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God created Adam, then He wiped his back with His right hand and produced from him offspring, and he said: I created These will go to Paradise and they will do the deeds of the people of Paradise. Then he wiped his back and produced offspring from it, and said: I created these for the Fire and for the deeds of The people of Hell will do “.” This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 74 - It contains transmission"
"75","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Kulthum bin Jabr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “God took the covenant from the back of Adam.” So he brought forth offspring from his loins and scattered them before him like atoms, then he spoke to them and said: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we testified lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, “Indeed, we were unaware of this,” or you say, “Our fathers only participated before, and we were descendants after them. Will you destroy us because of what the false people did? This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and Muslim cited Kulthum ibn Jabr as evidence.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 75 - Muslim argued with Kulthum"
"76","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Humaid Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The day God spoke to Moses, he was wearing a cloak. Wool, wool trousers, a wool sleeve, a wool cloak, and sandals made of the skin of an unintelligent donkey.” “They all agreed to use as evidence the hadith of Saeed bin Mansour, and this Humaid is not the son of Qays al-Araj. Al-Bukhari said in history: Humaid Ibn Ali Al-Araj Al-Kufi denies the hadith, and Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith Al-Najrani uses it as evidence, and Muslim alone used Khalaf Ibn Khalifa as evidence. This is a major hadith in Sufism and theology, and they did not narrate it, and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Ismail bin Ayyash.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 76 - This Hamid is not Ibn Qays"
"77","Ali bin Hamshadh and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Abdullah bin Daoud Al-Tamar told us, on the authority of Ismail. Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You must wear woolen clothing. The sweetness of faith in your hearts.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 77 - His leg came from a weak path"
"78","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid al-Hafiz told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shayban told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashyab told us, Shayban bin Abd told us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was on some of his travels and he was almost He walked among his companions, and he raised his voice with these two verses: “O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour will be a great thing on the day you see it.” Every nursing woman will be amazed at what she has suckled, and every pregnant woman will give birth to her child, and you will see people drunk, but they are not drunk, but the punishment of God is severe.} [Al-Hajj: 2] . When his companions heard that, they urged Al-Muti and knew that he was saying something, so when they gathered around him, he said: “Do you know what That day? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “That is the day when Adam will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: O Adam, be sent into the fire, and he will say: And he was not sent. Fire? He says: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine go to Hell and one to Paradise. With a laugh, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he said: “Know and give glad tidings, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creatures. They did not have anything but multiplied it, Gog and Magog and whoever is destroyed from among the children of Adam and the children of Satan.” He said: This was explained to the people. He said: “Know and give good tidings, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are only like a spot on the arm of an animal or like a mole on the side of a camel.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in its entirety, and what I have is that they were embarrassed about that for fear of being sent, and Al-Hasan heard From Imran bin Husayn, and most of these additions in this text are from Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, and it is authentic according to He conditioned them all, but not one of them brought him out” [p. 82].
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 78 - Sahih chain of transmission: Al-Hasan heard from Imran"
"79","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Anas, said: When this verse was revealed {O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a great thing} [Al-Hajj: 1] to his saying God Almighty {But the punishment of God is severe} [Al-Hajj: 2] upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was on his way, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. They all agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, some of this text.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 79 - They reported the hadith of Al-A’mash on the authority of Abu Salih on the authority of Abu Sa’id"
"80","As Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, in Baghdad, and Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani, in Kufa, they said: Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Absi told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God says: O Adam, and He says: I am here with you and I am happy, and all goodness is in your hands.” He said: He says: “Bring out the fire.” He mentioned the hadith briefly, without mentioning the revelation and others. It was narrated by Al-Bukhari, on the authority of Omar ibn Hafs, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash. It was narrated by Muslim, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Waki’."
"81","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Abdul Salam told us, and Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, they said: Abu Kurayb, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Beware of the supplications of the oppressed, for they ascend to heaven as if they were evil.” “Muslim cited Asim ibn Kulayb as evidence, and the rest of the narrators of this hadith agreed to use them as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 81 - Muslim protested against Asim"
"82","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Muqaddami told us, Fudayl told us Ibn Sulaiman, Musa Ibn Uqba told us, Ishaq Ibn Yahya told me, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I Master of the people on the Day of Resurrection, and there will be no pride. There is no one but that he will be under my banner on the Day of Resurrection, waiting for relief. And with me is the banner of praise. I walk and the people walk with me until I come to the gate of Paradise, then I open it and it is said: Who is this? So I say: Muhammad, and it is said: Welcome Muhammad, so when I see my Lord, I kneel before Him, prostrating, looking at Him. This is a great hadith in terms of attributes and visions, and it is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 82 - According to their condition and they did not take it out"
"83","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Biruti told us, my father told me, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Mukhlid Al-Jawhari told us in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Masisi, Al-Awza’i told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Abu Ishaq told us Al-Fazari, narrated by Al-Awza’i, and this is the wording of the hadith of Abu Al-Abbas. He said: Rabia bin Yazid and Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Sibani narrated to me, They said: Abdullah bin Fayrouz Al-Dailami told us, he said: I entered upon Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas while he was in a wall of his in Taif, called him. Al-Waht, and he was lecturing a young man from Quraysh, and that young man committed adultery by drinking alcohol, so I said to Abdullah bin Amr: Characteristics that inform me about you. He narrated it on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If someone drinks alcohol, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings, so the boy became confused. He took his hand from Abdullah’s hand, then he turned away. The wretched is the one who is wretched in his mother’s womb, and he who leaves his house only wants to pray at home. The sanctified one came out of his sin as on the day his mother gave birth to him.Abdullah bin Amr said: Oh God, I do not make it permissible for anyone to say against me what I did not say. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever drinks alcohol excessively, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, God will accept his repentance. If he returns, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings.” I do not know about the third or fourth time. He said: “If he returns, it is God’s duty to give him water from the stench of vinegar on the Day of Resurrection.” He said: And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, God created His creation in darkness, then bestowed upon them His light, so whoever is struck by that light On that day, something will be guided, and whoever makes a mistake will go astray, and for that I say, “The pen has dried up in the knowledge of God.” And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Solomon the son of David asked his Lord for three and He gave him two, and we hope that he gave him the third. He asked him for a ruling that coincides with His ruling, so he gave it to him, and he asked him for a kingdom that no one after him should have, so he gave it to him, and he asked him: “Is there a man who leaves his house who does not want Except for prayer in this mosque, so that he will emerge from his sin as on the day his mother gave birth to him. We hope that God has given it to him.”Al-Awza’i said: Rabi’ah bin Yazid narrated this hadith to me between Al-Maqsalat and Al-Jas’ir. This is an authentic hadith. The imams circulated it, and they used all its narrators as evidence, then they did not narrate it, and I do not know of any reason for it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 83 - According to their condition and there is no defect for it"
"84","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaym told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Qatada al-Sulami, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He says: “God created Adam, then He created the creation from his back, then he said: These are for Paradise, and I do not care, and these are for Hell, and I do not care.” He said: So it was said: Oh Messenger of God, so what should we do? He said: In agreement with destiny. This is an authentic hadith. They agreed to use its narrations as evidence, from the last of them to the Companions, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Qatada from Banu Salamah from The Companions, and they all cited Zuhayr bin Amr as evidence, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he has no narrator other than Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, and likewise Al-Bukhari cited as evidence the hadith of Abu Sa’id bin Al-Mu’alla, and he has no narrator other than Hafs bin Asim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 84 - On their condition to the Companion"
"85","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, Abu Malik told us Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is the Creator of every maker and his work.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 85 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"86","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Muqaddami told us, Al-Fudayl bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is the Creator of every maker.” And I made it.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"87","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid bin Zurayi narrated to us, Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, said: I said: O Messenger of God, incantations with which we used to seek ruqyah, and medicines with which we used to seek treatment. Will you respond to the decree of God Almighty? He said: “It is God’s decree.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Then they did not narrate it, and Muslim said in his compilation regarding what Mu’ammar made a mistake in Basra, that Mu’ammar narrated He mentioned it twice, and once he said: On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khuzama, on the authority of his father. Al-Hakim said: In my opinion, this does not explain it, for Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar followed Muammar bin Rashid in his hadith on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa And Saleh, even if he is in the third class of the companions of Al-Zuhri, then someone like him may be cited as a martyr.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 87 - According to their condition"
"88","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us, in Baghdad, and Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi, in Marw, they said: Abu Qalabah narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Humaid told us, Saleh bin Abi Al-Akhdar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, he said: I said: O Messenger of God Are incantations with which we used to seek protection and medicines with which we were treated? Are they considered to be from the decree of God? He said: “It is from the decree of God.”"
"89","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hussein bin Maimun told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hassan bin Ibrahim told us Al-Kirmani, Saeed bin Masruq told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abi Burdah bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Abi Burdah, he said: I came to Aisha and said: O mother, Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The birds flowed according to their ability, and it was He is pleased with the good omen.” The two sheikhs argued as evidence that the narrators of this hadith were narrated by the last of them, other than Yusuf bin Abi Burdah, and what I have is that they did not They neglect him out of injury or weakness, but rather because he rarely talks, for he is very dear to talk.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 89 - They did not go out to Yusuf while he was difficult to talk to"
"90","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Tamim Al-Handali told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim, Sufyan told us, and Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, They said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “He does not believe.” The servant until he believes in four until he bears witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God. He has sent me with the truth, and he believes in the resurrection after death. And he believes in destiny.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and some of Al-Thawri’s companions were negligent in narrating it, and this is something that we do not care about.”"
"91","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of a man, On the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something similar. “Abu Hudhayfah Musa bin Masoud Al-Nahdi, and if Al-Bukhari uses him as evidence, then he is very delusional and cannot be judged against Abu Asim Al-Nabil. And Muhammad bin Kathir and their peers. Rather, he is bound to make a mistake if he disagrees with them, and the evidence for what I mentioned is the follow-up of Jarir bin Abdul Hamid. Al-Thawri in his narration, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Ali, and Jarir are among the most knowledgeable people about the hadith of Mansour.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 90 - According to their condition"
"92","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ishaq bin Ismail Al-Talqani told us, Jarir told us, and Muhammad bin Salih told us Bin Hani, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, and Muhammad bin Shazan told us, saying: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No servant will believe until he believes in four things: He bears witness that there is no god but God alone.” He has no partner, and I am the Messenger of God. He sent me with the truth, and he will be sent after death, and he believes in destiny in its entirety.”"
"93","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, and Shayban bin Abi Shaybah told us, They said: Jarir told us, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Yazid bin Salih told us, and Muhammad bin Aban told us, they said: We told him: Jarir bin Hazim said: I heard Abu Raja al-Attardi saying: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The affairs of this nation will continue to be a conspiracy - or he said it is close - as long as they do not speak about procreation and destiny.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and we do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 93 - According to their condition and there is no defect for it"
"94","Da'laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, in Baghdad, Musa bin Harun and Salih bin Muqatil told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us Al-Anazi, and Ahmad bin Ali Al-Abar, and Ahmad bin Sahl bin Hamdawayh Al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, They said: Ahmad bin Janab al-Masisi told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God has divided among you your morals just as He has divided among you your livelihood, and God gives the world to those who love and to those who do not love. Only those who love are given faith.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was narrated alone by Ahmad ibn Janab al-Masisi, and it is one of our conditions in this book that we produce trustworthy individuals. If we do not find a reason for it, and we found for Isa bin Yunus in it, following one of them from the condition of this book, which is Sufyan bin Uqba. Qabisa's brother
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 94 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"95","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Mihran bin Harun Al-Razi informed us, Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas Al-Razi informed us - and he is your favourite, Al-Razi - Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hamawayh al-Razi narrated to us, Sufyan bin Uqba, brother of Qubaisa, narrated to us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, and Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Zubaid, On the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, God has divided among you your morals as He has divided among you Your livelihood, and God gives money to those who love and those who do not love, and He does not give faith except to those who love, and if God loves a servant, He gives him faith.” . “As for the follower who is not a condition of this book, he is Abd al-Aziz bin Aban, and the hadith is known about him. He was authenticated by two followers of Isa bin Yunus, then a follower of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Zubaid, who is Hamza Al-Zayat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 95 - It was narrated by Abdul Aziz bin Aban, but it is not a requirement of our book on the authority of Al-Thawri."
"96","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Ali bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, Harun bin Yusuf told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, they said: Sufyan told us, and the pronunciation is by Al-Humaydi, we told Al-Zuhri, Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me, he said: I heard Kurz bin Alqamah say: A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God Does Islam have an end? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes, whichever family, Arab or non-Arab, God wants good for them, He will enter Islam upon them, then Trials fall as if they were shadows.” Followed by Muhammad bin Rashid, and Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 96 - They did not narrate it on the authority of Urwa on the authority of Karaz, who was a Companion
 As for the hadith of Muammar"
"97","So Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abdan told us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Kurz bin Alqamah, said: A Bedouin said: O Messenger of God, does Islam have an end? He said: “Yes, either.” A family of Arabs and non-Arabs. God intended good for them and introduced Islam to them. Then temptations occur as if they were shadows. “This is an authentic hadith, and it has no defect, and they did not narrate it because Urwa was alone in narrating it, on the authority of Kurz ibn Alqamah, and Kurz ibn Alqamah was a companion of A narration of his hadith in the Musnads of the Imams. I heard Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz, saying: From what Muslim and Al-Bukhari are obligated to narrate is the hadith of Kurz bin Alqamah. “Does Islam have an end?” Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrated it, and al-Zuhri and Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays narrated it on his authority. Al-Hakim said: “The clear evidence for what Abu Al-Hasan mentioned is that they all agreed on the hadith of Itban bin Malik Al-Ansari, who prayed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is in his house and he has no narrator other than Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’.”"
"98","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Abu Abdullah told us Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh, said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Abu Abdul Rahman told us. Al-Muqri, Haywa bin Shurayh told us, Abu Hani Humaid bin Hani Al-Khawlani told us that Abu Ali Al-Janabi told him that He heard Fadalah bin Ubaid narrate that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Blessed is he who is guided to Islam and whose livelihood is sufficient and content.” . “This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, and I have heard that he narrated it with another chain of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 98 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"99","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar told me, they said: Al-Hussein bin Fadl told us. Al-Bajli, and Abu Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Ibrahim Al-Hadha’ told me, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Sulayman bin Al-Harith told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him He said: “O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and Muslim used Uthman al-Shahham as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 99 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"100","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzaki told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, and Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, they said: Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Hasani, Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, and Ibrahim bin Abi A student, they said: Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Hasani told us, Malik bin Sa’ir told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O people, I am only a mercy that guides.” “This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, as they all cited Malik ibn Sa’ir as evidence, and the only trustworthy narrators are acceptable.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 100 - Given their condition and the uniqueness of trustworthiness, it is acceptable"
"101","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqqi told us, Ubayy told us, Abdullah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Awf Al-Shaybani said: I heard Ibn Omar saying: “We lived for a period of our time, and faith was given to one of us before the Qur’an. The Surah is revealed to Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he learns what it permits and what it prohibits, and what should be stopped from him regarding it, as you know. The Qur’an,” then he said: “I have seen men to one of whom was given the Qur’an and he recited from its beginning to its end, neither knowing what it was commanded nor He rebuked him, and he did not scatter anything that should be stopped with him like a tamper.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 101 - According to their condition and there is no reason for it"
"102","Abu Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, they said: Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farawi told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Mawwal Al-Qurashi told us, Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Qutaybah ibn Sa’id told me, Ibn Abi al-Mawwal Abdul Rahman told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Mawhib Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Abu Bakr Ibn Muhammad Ibn Amr Ibn Hazm, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Six have been cursed, may God curse them and every prophet will be answered: the one who denies by the power of God, the one who adds to the Book of God, and the one who rules with tyranny.” He humiliates whoever God honors, and he honors whoever God humiliates, and he who deems permissible what God has forbidden, and he who makes permissible from my family what God has forbidden, and he who abandons my Sunnah.” Al-Bukhari cited Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawwal as evidence, and this is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and I do not know of any reason for it, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 102 - It is true and I do not know of any reason for it"
"103","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz informed us in dictation in the month of Rabi’ al-Akhir in the year three hundred and ninety-three, Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abu al-Nu’man Muhammad bin al-Fadl told us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Jawhari told me, and the wording for it, Muhammad ibn Ishaq told us, Muhammad ibn Muammar bin Rabi’i Al-Qaisi, Abu Hisham Al-Mughirah bin Salamah Al-Makhzoumi told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Assam, Yazid bin Al-Assam told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Muhammad, have you seen? A paradise as wide as the heavens and the earth, so where is the Hell? He said: “Have you seen the night that has covered everything and where has it placed the day?” He said: God knows best. He said: Thus God does whatever He wills. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 103 - According to their condition, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"104","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father told me, and Ali ibn Hamshadh told us, we told us Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, Muhammad bin Rafi’ and Muhammad bin Yahya told us, they said: Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, On the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not know whether he followed a prophet or not? I do not know whether Dhul-Qarnayn was a prophet or not? I do not know whether the punishments are expiations for those who fulfill them or not? . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 104 - According to their condition, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"105","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Bahz bin Asad told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “When God created Adam, He fashioned him and left him in Paradise as God willed. He left him, so Satan began to surround him, and when he saw that he was hollow, he knew that he was a creature who could not control himself.” “This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, and I have heard that he included it at the end of the book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 105 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"106","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, he said: It was read to Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad while I was listening. Quraysh bin Anas, Muhammad bin Amr told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will surely follow the traditions of those before you, one cubit after another, and an cubit A cubit, and a hand span and a hand span, until if they entered a lizard’s den, you would enter it with them.” He said: It was said: O Messenger of God, the Jews and Christians. He said: “So who So? . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 106 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"107","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abi told us, Al-Amash told us, Al-Minhal bin Amr told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, Al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Zazan Abi Umar, he said: I heard Al-Baraa ibn Aazib saying: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. At the funeral of a man from the Ansar, we ended up at the grave, and when he did not say anything yet, he said: So we sat around the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he looked at the sky and looked at the earth, and raised and lowered his gaze three times, then said: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of The grave.” Then he said: “When a Muslim man is on the verge of the Hereafter and is cut off from this world, the Angel of Death comes and sits by his head. And angels descend from heaven as if their faces were the sun, and they have with them shrouds from the shrouds of Paradise and spices from the spices of Paradise, and they sit therein for a long period of time. Sight. He said: “Then the angel of death will say: O reassured soul, come out to forgiveness from God and His satisfaction.” He said: “Then it will come out dripping as if A drop flows from the waterskin, and they do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye.Then they ascended with it to heaven, but they did not pass by a host of angels except that they said: What is this good soul? They say: So-and-so, the son of so-and-so, with the best of his names. When he reaches heaven, the gates of heaven are opened for him. Then he will send him on his way from every heaven. They bring it up to the next heaven, until it reaches the seventh heaven, then it will be said: Write its letter in the two highest heavens, then it will be said: Return my servant to The earth, for I promised them that from it I created them and to it I will return them and from it I will bring them out another time, so his soul will be returned to his body. Then the angels come to him and say: Who is your Lord? He said: So he says: God, and they say: What is your religion? He says: Islam, and they say: Who is this man who came out among you? He said: Then he says: The Messenger of God. He said: Then they say: And how do you know? He said: Then he says: I read the Book of God, so I believed in it and believed in it. He said: Then a herald calls from the sky, “He has spoken the truth, so spread a bed for him from Paradise and clothe him from Paradise and show him his place in Paradise. He said: And his grave will be extended for him and the spirit and scent of Paradise will come to him. He said: And he will do that to them. A man with a beautiful face, well-dressed, and a pleasant scent appears to him, and he says: Give good tidings of what pleases you. This is your day which you were promised.So he says: Who are you when your face is a face that brings good tidings? He said: Then he says: I am your righteous deed. He said: Then he says: My Lord, establish the Hour so that I may return to my family and my wealth. Then he recited {God establishes those who believe With firm words in the life of this world and in the Hereafter} [Ibrahim: 27]. As for the immoral person, when he is on the verge of the Hereafter and cut off from this world, the angel of death comes to him, and he sits by his head and the angels descend. Their faces are black, they carry sackcloth, and they sit there as far as the eye can see. Then the angel of death says: Come out, you wicked soul, to the wrath of God. And he became angry and said: Then his body would be torn apart, and the veins and nerves would be cut off with it, just as wet wool is extracted from the wool of thick hair. He said: Then they will stand up. To Him, so that they would not call Him into His hand for the blink of an eye, and they would ascend with it to heaven. They would not pass by a host of angels except that they would say: What is this spirit? Malicious? He said: They say: So-and-so has the ugliest of names. He said: And when he is taken to heaven, the gates of the heavens are closed without him. He said: And it is said: Write. His letter in Sijin, he said: Then it will be said: Return my servant to the earth, for I promised them that from it I created them and to it I will return them and from it. I will take them out another time. He said: Then he throws his soul until it falls into his body.He said: Then he recited {And whoever associates anything with God, it is as if he had fallen from the sky and the birds had snatched him up or the winds had carried him to a deep place} [Al-Hajj: 31]. He said: Then the angels come to him and say: Who is your Lord? He said: Then he says: I do not know, then a herald calls from the sky saying, “He has lied, so spread a bed for him from the Fire, and clothe him from the Fire, and show him his place from the Fire.” He said: Then his grave will be constricted for him until its ribs are divided into one another. He said: And its scent and heat will come to him. He said: That will be done to him, and it will be represented to him. A man with an ugly face, foul-smelling clothes, and a stinking odor. He says: “Rejoice in what will make you miserable. This is your day, which you were promised.” He said: Then he says: Who are you? Your face is the face that brings good tidings of evil. He said: And he says: I am your evil deed. He said: And he says: My Lord, do not establish the Hour.

 [p. 95]"
"108","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Amri told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Ali bin Al-Mundhir told me, Muhammad bin Fadl told us, Al-A’mash told us, so he mentioned it. With a similar chain of narration. And he said at the end of it: Ali bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us after his news, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl. My father narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, something like This hadith refers to the hadith of Al-Bara’, except that it said: “Lie down as the pious do, for the first believer, and it will be said to the immoral person: “Lie down, overwhelmed.” So what? There is no living creature on earth except that it has a share in his body. It was narrated by Sufyan bin Saeed, Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj, and Zaida bin Qudamah. They are the imams who have memorized, on the authority of Al-A’mash, as for the hadith of Al-Thawri."
"109","So Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, and I asked him, Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Souri told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said the salaam at a funeral, so we came to the grave, but he did not say hello.” He mentioned the hadith. As for the hadith of Shu’bah
 [p. 96]"
"110","So Abu Saeed bin Abi Bakr bin Abi Uthman told me, may God have mercy on them, and I asked him. Ali bin Muslim Al-Asbahani told us, with Al-Ray, told us Ammar bin Raja, Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Barsani told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Baraa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the hadith of the grave.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 110 - Based on their condition, they used the premise as evidence

 As for the hadith of Zaydah,"
"111","So Abu Saeed Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Muawiyah bin Amr Al-Azdi told us, Zaydah told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “We prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the funeral of a man. Of the Ansar” - he mentioned the lengthy hadith of the grave -. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They all cited as evidence Al-Minhal bin Amr and Zazan Abi Omar Al-Kindi, and in this hadith It has many benefits for the Sunnis and suppresses the innovators, and they did not mention it in a long way, and there is evidence for their condition that proves its authenticity.”"
"112","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad, the grammarian, told us in Baghdad, and Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Yaqoub told us about the origin of his book, saying: Thana Yahya bin Abi Talib, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned He greeted the believer and the unbeliever, then mentioned a part of the hadith of the grave. The authenticity of this hadith has been demonstrated by the original and the witnesses, and perhaps someone is delusional and imagines that the hadith that is.

 [p. 97]"
"113","Abu Al-Hussein Abdul-Samad bin Ali bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Kazzal told us, Abu Ibrahim told us Al-Tarjumani, Shuaib bin Safwan told us, Yunus bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari Al-Tai, I heard Al-Baraa bin Azib said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the funeral of a man from the Ansar, so we came to the grave, and when he Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down and faced the Qiblah and we sat around him.” Then he mentioned the hadith. “This hadith is explained by it, but it is not like that, because what Abu Al-Bakhtari mentioned in this hadith is an illusion from Shuaib bin Safwan, according to the consensus. “The trustworthy Imams” according to his narration, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabbab, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zazan, that he heard Al-Bara’. Tell us that what you mentioned is correct: Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nasr al-Khalidi, dictating in Baghdad, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ibrahim bin Ziyad Sablan, narrated by Abbad bin Abbad, said: I came to Yunus bin Khabab, in Mina, at the minaret, while he was telling the story, and I asked him about the hadith about the torment of the grave. So he told me about it."
"114","Abu Amr Ismail bin Bujayd bin Ahmad bin Yusuf Al-Sulami informed me. Abu Muslim informed Ibrahim bin Abdullah. Abu told us Amr Al-Darir, Mahdi bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabbab, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us - and the pronunciation is his -, Abdullah told us Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told me, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Khabab, on the authority of Al-Minhal Ibn Amr, on the authority of Zazan, On the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, and in the hadith of Abbad bin Abbad, he heard Al-Bara’ bin Azib say: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. At a funeral, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on the grave and we sat around him” - and he mentioned the hadith in its length -. “This is the authentic and preserved hadith of Yunus bin Khabbab.” Thus, it was narrated by Abu Khaled Al-Dalani, Amr bin Qais Al-Mala’i, and Al-Hasan bin Abdullah Al-Nakhai, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr. “As for the hadith of Abu Khaled Al-Dalani,”
 [p. 98]"
"115","So Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Sari bin Yahya Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, Abu Khaled al-Dalani told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr. “As for the hadith of Amr bin Qais Al-Malali,”"
"116","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ahmad bin Bishr al-Marthadi told us, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Shaybah told us Khaled Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr. “As for the hadith of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah,”"
"117","So Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah told us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, they all said: On the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Baraa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the like. “These chains of narrations that I mentioned are all authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"118","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Mu’afia bin Sulayman Al-Harrani told us, Fulayh bin Suleiman, Hilal bin Ali - who is Ibn Abi Maimunah - told me on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Bilal They were walking through Al-Baqi’, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Bilal, do you hear what I hear?” He said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, I do not hear it. He said: “Don’t you hear the people of the graves being tortured?” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Shu’bah,” on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “If you had not been buried, I would have asked God about him so that he would make you feel the torment of the grave.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 118 - According to their condition"
"119","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi, and Bahr bin Nasr bin Saqiq Al-Khawlani. Al-Rabi’ said: He told us, and Bahr said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Hisham bin Saad told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, Abu Sa`id al-Khudri entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sick, wearing a piece of velvet, and he placed his hand on it and found that it was hot. On top of the velvet, and Abu Saeed said: How intense is the heat of your father-in-law, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is how hard it is for us.” affliction and the reward will be multiplied for us.” Then he said: O Messenger of God, who is the most afflicted of people? He said: “The prophets.” He said: Then who? He said: “The scholars.” He said: Then who? He said: “Then are the righteous.” One of them would be afflicted with poverty until he could find nothing but an abaya to wear, and he would be afflicted with lice until it killed him. And one of them was more happy with calamity than one of you with giving. “Abu Al-Abbas told us, on the authority of Bahr in the Musnad, and on the authority of Al-Rabi’ in the benefits, And I combined them both. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. Hisham bin Saad was cited as evidence, and there is much evidence for it, including the hadith of Asim. Ibn Bahdala, on the authority of Mus’ab Ibn Sa’d, on the authority of his father, there are methods by which he can be followed and remembered, and Al-Ala’ Ibn Al-Musayyab followed Asim Ibn Bahdala on His narration on the authority of Musaab bin Saad”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 119 - According to Muslim’s condition and there is much evidence"
"120","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told me, in what I read to him from the original letter of his letter, I am Muhammad bin Ghalib, Amr bin Aoun told us, Khaled told us Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Alaa Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Mus’ab Ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which people are most afflicted? He said: “The prophets, then the example and the example. If a man is strict in his religion, the man will be tested according to the extent of his religion, then whoever has a strong religion will be heavy.” His affliction, and whoever’s religion is weak, his affliction is weak.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it is witnessed by what"
"121","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Isra’il al-Jawhari told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, and Abu al-Hussein told us Ibn Tamim Al-Qantari, Ja’far Ibn Muhammad Ibn Shakir told us, Affan told us, Hammad Ibn Salamah, Hammad Ibn Zaid, and Aban Al-Attar told us, and Abd told us Allah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sharik bin Abdullah told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Shayban told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir, Sufyan told us, and Abu Amr bin Abi Saeed Al-Nahwi told me, Al-Hussein bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Raqi told us, Uqba told us Ibn Makram, Salam Ibn Qutayba told us, Hisham Ibn Abi Abdullah told me, and Muhammad Ibn Ali Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Ahmad Ibn Hazim bin Abi Gharza, Ahmad bin Yunus, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, saying: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, all of them on the authority of Asim bin Abu Al-Najood, and this is the wording of the hadith of Shayban bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Musab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Who is the most afflicted person? He said: “The prophets, then the example, then the example. A man will be tested according to his religion. If he is sincere in religion, then his trial will be severe, and if he is gentle in his religion. He will be tested according to his religion, and the affliction will not continue until the servant is allowed to walk on the earth without any sin.”"
"122","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Al-Qasim bin Zakaria Al-Mutraz Al-Muqri narrated to us, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Qutayi narrated to us, Omar bin Ali narrated to us. Al-Muqaddami, Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ If the term of one of you is in a land that God has confirmed for him a need for it, and when he has reached the maximum of his days, he causes him to die, then the earth will say: On the day Resurrection: O Lord, this is what you have entrusted to me. The two sheikhs used the narration of this hadith on the authority of the last of them, and Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami agreed to narrate it in the two Sahih books. Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Wahbi followed him on his chain of transmission, on the authority of Ismail
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 122 - According to their condition"
"123","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Al-Abbas Al-Iskandarani Al-Adl told me, in Mecca. Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahid told us. Al-Homsi, Abu Al-Hasan Katheer bin Ubaid bin Numayr Al-Madhaji told us, Muhammad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you lands on a land that has been made available to him Then he ascends to it, and his maximum impact is upon him, and he is caught in it, and the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: My Lord, this is what You have entrusted to me.” It was narrated by Hushaym, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled.”"
"124","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman Al-Hadrami told us, Musa bin Muhammad bin Hibban told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: If The term of one of you was on land for which he had a need, and God will fulfill it for him, and the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: My Lord, this is what You have entrusted to me. “.” This hadith was transmitted by three trustworthy narrators on the authority of Ismail, and Sufyan bin Uyaynah agreed with him, so we adhere to what we stipulated in narrating Increased confidence in the connection and chain of transmission, then this hadith has evidence on the condition of the two sheikhs, including some."
"125","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, and Bukayr bin told me The Sufi blacksmith, in Mecca, Abu Muslim told us, Abbad bin Musa told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, and the pronunciation for him, he informed us Muhammad bin Ghalib, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Matar bin Okhams, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God decrees death for a man in a town, He grants him a need therein.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 125 - According to their condition"
"126","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Matar bin Akamis Al-Abdi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not made a man’s term on a land unless it has been made his own.” “There is a need therein.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They all agreed to narrate a group of the Companions in which each one of them had only one narrator, and he had Another witness from a trustworthy narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 126 - Its narrators are trustworthy"
"127","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, and Bakr bin Al-Haddad told me, In Mecca, Abu Muslim told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, they said: Hammad told us, Ayyub told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin told us. Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Ismail told me, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Abu Azzah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “If God wanted to take possession of a land from a servant, He created a need for him.” This is an authentic hadith, and its narrations on the authority of the last of them are trustworthy, and I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Mu'in say: The name of Abu Azzah Yasar bin Abd has a companion. As for Abu Al-Malih, I heard Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz saying: Al-Bukhari and Muslim must narrate the hadith of Abu Al-Malih on the authority of Abu Azzah. Al-Bukhari used as evidence the hadith of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Buraidah, and the hadith of Abu Izzah was narrated by a group of trustworthy and memorized scholars."
"128","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari narrated to us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, and Abu Al-Tayyib Tahir bin Yahya Al-Bayhaqi narrated to me. From the origin of his book, Khali al-Fadl bin Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, saying: Ahmad bin Janab al-Masisi told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, On the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Farafafah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is not generous, and the ungodly is despicable and mean.” He was followed by Ibn Shihab, Abd Rabbuh bin Nafi’ al-Hannat, and Yahya bin al-Dharays, on the authority of al-Thawri in establishing this chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 128 - Hajjaj is a worshipper. There is nothing wrong with him
 As for the hadith of Abu Shihab"
"129","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Bakr Yaqoub bin Yusuf al-Mutawa’i told us, in Baghdad, Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Muhammad told us. Al-Mubaraki, Abu Shihab narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Farafafah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is ungrateful and generous, and the ungodly is a vile despicable person.” “As for the hadith of Yahya ibn al-Dhurays, Muhammad ibn Humayd recorded it. This is a hadith that the predecessors of al-Thawri’s companions connected with, and he corrupted it. Those who came later than him, and as for Al-Hajjaj bin Farafsa, the two imams did not narrate it, but I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: Al-Hajjaj bin Farafsa is okay with him, and Abd al-Rahman bin Ma’in said: Abi Hatim: I heard my father say: Hajjaj bin Farafafah is a righteous and devout sheikh, and he has a witness, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who established its chain of transmission."
"130","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Bishr bin Rafi’ told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is not generous, and the ungodly is a mean and mean person.”"
"131","I heard Abu Saeed bin Abi Bakr bin Abi Othman, saying: I heard Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq, saying: I heard Ahmed bin Yusuf Al-Sulami, saying: I heard Abd al-Razzaq, saying: I was in Mecca and Waki` ibn al-Jarrah spoke to me about reading to him and his son the book of wills. So I said: When I arrived in Mina, I would narrate it. When I arrived in Mina, I carried my letter and narrated it to him, then I went to Mecca to visit, and Abu Usama met me, and he said To me: Oh Yemeni, that Rawasi boy deceived you, so I said: What did he deceive me? He said: I carried your letter to him and told him, and I said: It is not surprising that he deceived me. Bishr bin Rafi’ told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is not generous, and the ungodly is a vile and despicable person.” He said: So he took the one out and said: He dictated to me. I said: By God, I will not dictate to you, so he left. I heard Ali bin Isa, saying: I heard Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya, saying: The father of the tribes Al-Harithi is Bishr bin Rafi’. Al-Hakim said: “Bishr bin Rafi’, I only mentioned him as a witness, and our sheikhs have spoken about him, and I found another witness for him from a hadith. out"
"132","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, Ismail bin Qutaibah narrated, Yahya narrated to us, Kharijah narrated, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hussein Ibn Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Asbat Al-Harithi, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “The believer is ungrateful, and the ungodly is vile and mean.” “This hadith was narrated by the imams, and some of the narrators established its chain of transmission. As for the two sheikhs, they did not use Al-Hajjaj ibn as evidence. Farafafidah or Bishr ibn Rafi’"
"133","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali Al-Warraq told us, and his surname is Hamdan, Abu Salama Musa bin Ismail told us, Abu Salamah Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah, Yunus bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a person with a treaty... Without its right, he did not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance is present from a distance of five hundred years.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and we found Hammad bin Salamah as a witness to it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 133 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"134","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Hamdoun bin Ziyad told us, Abu Yusuf Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Qalusi told us, Sharik bin Al-Khattab Al-Anbari, Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Who “If he kills a person by making an unjustifiable treaty, God forbids him from Paradise, and he is not allowed to smell its fragrance, and its fragrance is present from a distance of five hundred years.” “As for the saying of those who said: Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj”"
"135","So Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abbas bin Al-Walid told us, Abdul-Ala bin Abdul-Ala told us, Yunus bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Thurmalah, on the authority of Abu Bakra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a soul by making a treaty without its right, God will forbid him Paradise.” Al-Hakim said: “Our Sheikh Abu Ali Al-Hafiz used to judge based on the hadith of Yunus ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Al-Araj, to whom the heart is at ease.” This is a chain of narration and that is another chain of narration, one of them does not explain the other, for Hammad bin Salamah is an imam.” Sharik ibn al-Khattab, a trustworthy sheikh from the people of Ahwaz, also followed him over him, and God knows best."
"136","Abu Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi, in Marw, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Mukhlid Al-Jawhari, in Baghdad, told us: He said: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Saeed bin Amer Al-Dabai told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Alqamah bin Waqqas, He said: There was an idle man who used to go in on the princes and make them laugh, so my grandfather said to him: Woe to you, so-and-so, why did you go in to these people and make them laugh? I heard Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrate that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The servant To speak a word from God’s pleasure, not thinking that it will reach what it has conveyed and God will be pleased with it for him until the Day of Resurrection, and the servant Let him speak a word out of God’s displeasure, not thinking that it will reach what it did, so that God will be displeased with it until the day he meets him.” “This is an authentic hadith. Muslim cited Muhammad ibn Amr as evidence, and his chain of narration was established on his authority by Sa`id ibn Amir, as I reported it like this above. It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri, Ismail bin Jaafar, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi, Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi and others. As for the hadith of al-Thawri.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 136 - This is correct"
"137","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told us, Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuaib al-Harrani told us, Jdi told us, Musa ibn Ayaan, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “A man speaks a word out of God’s displeasure, not knowing whether it will reach what it does, so God records His displeasure for him until On the Day of Resurrection, a man will utter a word pleasing to God, not knowing whether it will reach what it has, so God will record His satisfaction for him until The day he meets him.” “As for the hadith of Ismail bin Jafar”"
"138","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Ayyub al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Jafar told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “One of you speaks a word pleasing to God, and he does not think that it will achieve what it has conveyed, and God will record for him His satisfaction with it.” Until the day he meets him, and one of you utters a word out of God’s displeasure, and he does not think that it will achieve what it has conveyed, God will write it down against him. His anger will last until the day he meets him.” “As for the hadith of Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, it was narrated by Muslim.”"
"139","So Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Ibn Al-Darawardi told us, Muhammad bin Amr told me Ibn Alqamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Bilal Ibn Al-Harith, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “One of you is speaking By the word is of God’s pleasure, and he does not think that it will attain what it has attained, but God records for him His satisfaction with it until the day he meets him, and indeed one of you So that he may speak a word out of God’s displeasure, and he does not think that it will reach what it has conveyed. God writes His displeasure with it until the day he meets him.”"
"140","So Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, my father told me, on the authority of His father, Alqamah bin Waqqas, said: A man of honor passed by him while he was in the market of the city, and he greeted him. Alqamah said to him: O so-and-so, yours is Merciful and truly yours, and I saw you entering these princes and speaking to them as God wished to be spoken, and I heard Bilal ibn Al-Harith Al-Muzani, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “One of you speaks a word from God’s satisfaction. He does not think that she will attain what she has attained, but God will record for her His satisfaction for her until the day he meets him. And if one of you speaks With a word from the displeasure of God, he does not think that it will reach what it did, so God writes down His displeasure against him for it until the day he meets him.” Alqamah said: Woe to you, so consider what you say and what you speak about. Perhaps the words I heard from Bilal bin Al-Harith prevented me. “Malik bin Anas failed to narrate this hadith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, and did not mention Alqamah bin Waqqas.”"
"141","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Darabardi told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told us, and Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Maslamah told us Al-Anazi, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, they said: Al-Qanabi told us, in what was read to Malik, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin told us. Ali bin Ziyad, Ibn Abi Uwais told us, Malik told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man utters a word pleasing to God. He did not think that it would reach what it did.” So God records for him His satisfaction with it until the day he meets him, and indeed a man speaks a word out of God’s displeasure, not thinking that it would reach. “So long as she reaches it, God will record for him his wrath therein until the day he meets him.” Al-Hakim said: “This does not weaken the consensus that we mentioned, but rather it increases our confirmation with a follower like Malik. However, there is something wrong with the statement. They said it with an addition in establishing its chain of transmission.”"
"142","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Asim told us, Ahmad bin Suleiman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan told us Ibn Makram Al-Bazzar, and Muhammad Ibn Maslamah Al-Wasiti, they said: Yazid Ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Bahz Ibn Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: I heard the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Woe to the one who tells lies and the people laugh at him. Woe to him, woe to him.” This is a hadith narrated by Sufyan bin Saeed, Al-Hammadan, Abd al-Warith bin Saeed, Israel bin Yunus, and other imams, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim. “I do not know of any disagreement among most of the imams of narrators regarding the justice of Bahz ibn Hakim, and that his hadiths are combined, and Al-Bukhari mentioned him in Al-Jami’ al-Sahih, and this hadith bears witness to the hadith of Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, which we mentioned previously.” Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri narrated, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, and he narrated on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah Al-Daba’i, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Haidah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 142 - This is evidence of Bilal’s hadith"
"143","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, and Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl told us, they said: Ahmad bin Yunus told us, and Ahmad bin Muhammad told me Al-Anazi, and the pronunciation for him, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, Ahmad bin Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: Omar said: O Messenger of God, I heard so-and-so mentioning and praising goodness. He claimed that you gave him two dinars. He said: “But so-and-so did not He says that, and between one hundred and ten of me have narrated it.” He said: Then he said: “And one of you will leave me with his question, completely confused.” Ahmed said: Or something similar, “And it is nothing but fire.” He said: Then Omar said: O Messenger of God, why do you give it to them? He said: “What should I do?” They ask me questions, but God refuses me to be stingy.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.” It was narrated by Abdullah bin Bishr Al-Raqqi, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 143 - According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs"
"144","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Qabbani told us, Dawud bin Rashid told us, Muammar bin Suleiman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Omar, who said: Two men entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted them and asked him about something, so he called for two dinars for them, and behold, they returned well. Then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But so-and-so does not say anything.” That, and I gave him between ten and a hundred, so what does he say about that, for one of you gives charity from me without being aware of it, but it is He has a fire.” So I said: O Messenger of God, how do you give him something when you know that he has a fire? He said: “So what should I do? They refuse to do anything except to ask me, and God does not allow me to be stingy.” “As for Mu`tamar bin Sulaiman al-Raqqi, they did not narrate it, and Muslim narrated it, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr al-Raqqi, but this hadith is not a defect. Because of the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, he is a witness to it with another chain of narration.”"
"145","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Kathir bin Zaid told us, he said: I heard Salim, speaking, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “A believer should not be a curser.”"
"146","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Kathir bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim should not be a curser.” Salem said: I never heard Ibn Umar curse anything. “This is a hadith that was transmitted by a group of imams, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zaid, then Hammad ibn Zaid alone narrated it from him. As for the two sheikhs, They did not narrate on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, who is a sheikh from the people of Medina and whose surname is Abu Muhammad, I do not know him. He is mistaken in The narration, but he left it due to the scarcity of his hadith, and God knows best.” There is evidence for this hadith in different wording, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Abu Al-Darda’, and Samurah ibn Jundub, the like of which makes the hadith authentic. Condition of the two sheikhs
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 146 - It was chained by ‘iddah and Hammad ibn Zaid narrated it as endowment only
 As for the hadith of Abu Hurairah"
"147","So Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi, and Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, saying: Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “It is not the case that you who curse are truthful.” He was followed by Israel bin Yunus, on the authority of Abu Husayn"
"148","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “It is not combined that you who curse be truthful.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Darda"
"149","So Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us, Al-Mu’afia bin Imran told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, and Abu Hazim, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, she said: I heard Abu al-Darda’ say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, he says: “Those who curse will not be martyrs or intercessors.” “Muslim narrated it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 149 - This was narrated by Muslim
 As for the hadith of Samurah ibn Jundub:"
"150","Ali bin Hamshadh and Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydlani told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not curse with the curse of God, nor with the wrath of God, nor with the fire.” “These hadiths that he narrated in this chapter, with their different wording, are all with an authentic chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 150 - Its chains of transmission are authentic"
"151","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Muradi told us, Hajjaj bin Suleiman told us. Ibn al-Qamari, and he died before Ibn Wahb. Abu Ghassan al-Madani told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Saad al-Sa’idi, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “Indeed, God is generous, loves generosity, loves high morals, and hates the immoral.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 151 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"152","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, and Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Maslama, Othman bin Saeed told us, they said: Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Fudayl bin Iyad told us, Al-San’ani Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is generous, loves generosity, and excels in morals, and hates ""Sufsafaha."" “This is an authentic hadith with all its chains of narration. It was not narrated by Hajjaj bin Qamari, a trustworthy and trustworthy sheikh from the people of Egypt, and perhaps they turned away from it.” Taking him out is because the revolutionary forced him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 152 - Ahmed bin Yunus narrated it alone on his authority"
"153","As Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abdan told us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard Abu Hazim, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Kariz Al-Khuza’i, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is Generous and loves generosity, and excelling in matters. And he hates - or he said: he hates her immorality - “.” This does not weaken the hadith of Sahl bin Saad, as I mentioned above, regarding the acceptance of additional narrations from trustworthy narrators, and God knows best.”"
"154","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, and Ahmad bin Ibrahim told us, they said: Hammad told us Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Saq’ab Ibn Zuhayr, and Muhammad Ibn Salih Ibn Hani told me, and the wording is his. Ibrahim Ibn Abi Talib told us, Abu Talib told us. Qudama, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubay told us, he said: I heard Al-Saq’ab bin Zuhayr, narrating, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abd. Allah ibn Amr said: A Bedouin wearing a robe of brocade draped with brocade came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: This companion of yours He wants to exalt every shepherd and son of a shepherd, and to humble every horseman and son of a horseman. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up and sat down, and said: “When Noah was present with him, When he died, he called his two sons and said: I will convey to you the commandment: I command you to do two things and forbid you to do two things: I forbid you to do polytheism and arrogance. And I command you both: There is no god but God, for the heavens and the earth and all that is in them were if they were placed on one side of the scale and there is no god but God on the other side. The other was more important than the two of them, and if the heavens and the earth and what is in them were a circle and La ilaha illa Allah was placed over them, it would divide them both. And I command you to praise God and praise Him, for they are the prayer of all things and by them all things are provided.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It was not narrated by Al-Saq’ab bin Zuhayr, for he is trustworthy and the hadith is low. I heard Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Omar He says: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hatim saying: I asked Abu Zur’ah about Al-Saq’ab bin Zuhayr, and he said: Trustworthy, and he is the brother of Al-Ala’ bin Zuhayr, and this is of the kind that says: If a trustworthy person reaches him, it will not harm him to send someone else” [p. 113]."
"155","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi informed me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Ibn Abi Umar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin He became a Muslim. He said: A man said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: I have never seen a man give more money to a shepherd than Muhammad. Then he mentioned him in a similar way.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 154 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"156","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Asim Al-Razi told us, Ibn Numayr, Yahya bin Ayyub, and Abu Musa told us. Al-Ansari, Mansour bin Abi Muzahim, and Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin told me Musa, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Tayalisi, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Shuja’ bin Mukhlid and Ismail bin Salem told us, saying: Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, and in the hadith of Ismail bin Salem, Abu Bakr told us Husayn, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: I was sitting with Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad, and the heads of the Kharijites were brought. Whenever a leader came, I said: To Hell. Then Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari said: Do you not know, my nephew, that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The torment of This nation was placed in its world. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it, and there is an authentic witness for it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 156 - According to their condition and there is no reason for it"
"157","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Musa bin Harun, and Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, they said: Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Zakaria told us, On the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd al-Nakhai, who was trustworthy, on the authority of al-Hasan bin al-Hakam al-Nakhai, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yazid, He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The torment of my nation in this world.”"
"158","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us, in Marw, Abu Qalaba al-Raqqashi told us, Azhar bin Saad told us, Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, he said: The plague was mentioned by Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, so Abu Musa said: We asked about it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your brothers - or he said: your enemies - are from the jinn, and they are yours as witness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” This is how it was narrated by Abu Awanah, on the authority of Abu Balaj."
"159","Abu Al-Taher Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Dahqan told me, Abu Bakr bin Raja bin Al-Sindi told us, Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, And Muhammad bin Abi Attab, they said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father Abdullah bin Qays, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 158 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"160","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us Al-Tanafisi, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Ayyub reported, they said: Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever plays with dice He has disobeyed God and His Messenger.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it due to an illusion that occurred to Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind due to his poor memory of it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 160 - According to their condition"
"161","Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I heard Abdullah Bin Saeed bin Abi Hind, narrating on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Musa, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever plays with heels - or He said, “By the Kaaba, then he has disobeyed God and His Messenger.” “This is something that does not weaken or explain the hadith of Nafi’, as Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Hadi followed Nafi’ on the narration of Sa’id bin Abi Hind.”"
"162","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioning dice “disobeyed God.” And His Messenger disobeys God and His Messenger, and whoever strikes with its heels plays with it.”"
"163","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala Al-Attar told us, in Mecca, we told us Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saskiski, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The choice Servants of God who observe the sun, the moon, the stars, and the canopies in remembrance of God. Bishr bin Musa said: This hadith was not reported by Al-Humaydi in his Musnad. “This is an authentic chain of narration, and Abd al-Jabbar al-Attar is trustworthy, and Muslim and al-Bukhari have used Ibrahim al-Saskiski as evidence. If something like this is authentic, Uprightness is not harmed by the weakness of the one who corrupted its chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 163 - Its chain of transmission is authentic"
"164","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari informed us, on the authority of Marwa, and Abu Al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saskiski said: Our companions told me, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, that he said: “The most beloved of God’s servants to God are those who make God beloved to people.” And those who observe the sun and the moon. “This does not invalidate the first nor does it explain it, for Ibn Uyaynah is a trustworthy hafiz, and so is Ibn al-Mubarak, except that he brought other chains of narration, such as meaning The first hadith"
"165","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anbari told us, They said: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, and Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Saeed bin Al-Thaqafi told us. Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Advise me. He said: “You should worship God and not associate anything with Him, perform prayer, pay zakat, fast the month of Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House and perform Umrah, and listen to And you obey.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Its narrations from the last of them are trustworthy, and they did not narrate it as a precaution for what.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 165 - According to their condition"
"166","I heard Ali bin Issa, saying: I heard Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, saying: Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ubaid told me Allah bin Omar Al-Amri, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, said: A Bedouin came to Omar and asked him about religion, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, teach me Religion, he said: “You bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and you perform prayer, and pay zakat, and fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House, and you must In public, beware of secrets, and beware of everything of which you are ashamed. He said: When you meet God, you say: Omar ibn al-Khattab commanded me to do this, and he said: “O servant of God, take this, and when you meet God Almighty, say whatever you wish.” Al-Qabbani said: I said to Muhammad bin Yahya: Which of the two is preserved, the hadith of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, or Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar? He said: Muhammad bin Yahya’s hadith is more similar to Al-Hasan. Al-Hakim said: “May God be pleased with Muhammad bin Yahya. He refrained from answering, out of caution for contradicting his saying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Leave that which causes you doubt.” To that which does not cause you to doubt.” And if he contemplated the two hadiths, it would appear to him that the wording is different, and they are two hadiths with a chain of transmission and a story, and they are not memorized. By Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, other than the hadith of the emirate, and Al-Darawardi was the only one to narrate it, and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Jumahi is trustworthy and trustworthy, It was narrated on his authority by someone other than Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, on the basis that Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah is also trustworthy and trustworthy.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 166 - It was said that this is more like it"
"167","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza Al-Ghifari told us, Ubaid Allah told us Ibn Musa, Israel reported, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Masruq, on the authority of Saad Ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar said: No, by my father, so the Messenger said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not swear by your fathers. Whoever swears by anything other than God has committed polytheism.”"
"168","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, he informed us Sufyan, on the authority of his father, and Al-A’mash, and Mansour, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar used to swear and my father forbade him, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever swears by anything besides God has committed polytheism.” The other said: “It is polytheism.”"
"169","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, On the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever swears by anything other than God has disbelieved.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, I entrusted it to the Book of Faith to express polytheism in it, and in the hadith Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Israel, “He has disbelieved.” As for the two sheikhs, they only narrated it from the hadith of Salem and Nafi’ and Abdullah bin Dinar, On the authority of Abu Omar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Omar: “Indeed, God forbids you from swearing by your fathers” only, and this is not that."
"170","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam Al-Masry told us, Abu Ghassan, on the authority of Hassan bin Attiya, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Affection and modesty: two parts of Faith, obscenity and stupidity: two types of hypocrisy. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it and there is a valid witness according to their conditions.”"
"171","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih narrated to us in Al-Tabaran, and Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih, in Bukhara, they said: Saleh narrated to us. Bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Modesty is a part of faith, and faith is in Paradise, and obscenity is a part of indifference, and indifference is in Hell.” “And he has two witnesses to the condition of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 171 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"172","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdus told us, Othman bin Saeed told us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise, and obscenity is part of faith.” Indifference, and indifference in Hellfire.”"
"173","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, and Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Yahya, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid bin Zurayi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among the believers most complete in faith is the one with the best character and the kindest to his family.” “The narrators of this hadith on the authority of the last of them are trustworthy according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 173 - There is a break"
"174","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Quraysh said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Call on your Lord to make Safa for us. We will go and believe in you. He said: “Will you do that?” They said: Yes, so he called, and Gabriel came to him and said: God recites peace upon you and says: If you wish, Al-Safa will turn into gold, so whoever disbelieves after that. I tortured him with a punishment that I would not torture anyone else in the world, and if you wish, you could open for them the doors of repentance and mercy. He said: “Rather, the door of repentance.” And mercy.”"
"175","[Page: 120] Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Muhammad bin Many, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, so he mentioned it with its chain of transmission and the like. “This is an authentic and preserved hadith from the hadith of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail and Imran bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, a major follower who is used as evidence. They neglected this hadith - and God knows best - because of a disagreement that occurred from Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhayl regarding its chain of transmission, and Yahya was very disingenuous towards his father.”"
"176","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Amrawayh Al-Saffar told us about Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Ahwas bin Answer: Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhayl narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Quraysh said: O Muhammad, pray Your Lord will turn Al-Safa into gold and we will believe in you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you do it?” They said: Yes, so Gabriel came and said: Be sure, then Gabriel came and said: O Muhammad, God has given you what you asked for if you wish, in the morning. As-Safa is yours in gold, and whoever disbelieves after that, I will punish him with a punishment that I will not punish any of the worlds, and if you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance. And repentance. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The door of repentance and mercy is dearer to me.” “This illusion does not weaken the hadith of Al-Thawri, for I do not know Imran bin Al-Ja’d among the Successors. Rather, Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated on the authority of Imran bin Abi Al-Ja’d. As for Imran bin Al-Ja’d, he is one of the followers of the Successors.”"
"177","Da'laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid Al-Makki told us, Sa'id bin Mansour told us, Ya'qub bin Abd told us Al-Rahman, and Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Omar, and the client of al-Muttalib, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever does an evil deed and hates it while he does it, and does a good deed and is pleased with it, then he is a believer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. I mentioned in the previous sermon of Omar that he was a collector and that they They did not bring it out, and this is also in other than that word.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 177 - According to their condition"
"178","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Qubaisa told us, and Abu Al-Abbas bin Ahmed bin Muhammad told us Al-Mahboubi, Bamrou, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Dharr, fear God wherever you are, and follow a bad deed with a good one.” wipe it out, and treat people with good manners.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 178 - According to their condition"
"179","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Harmala bin Imran Al-Tajibi told me that Abu Al-Samt Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Mahri told him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that Muadh bin Jabal wanted to travel, so he said: O Messenger God has advised me. He said: “Worship God and do not associate anything with Him.” He said: O Messenger of God, increase me. He said: “If you do evil, do good.” He said: O Messenger of God. Increase me, he said: “Be upright and improve your character.” “This is a hasan hadith with an authentic chain of narration from the narration of the Basrais, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 179 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"180","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Asim told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {those who avoid major sins and immoralities} [An-Najm: 32] He said: This is when a man commits an immoral act and then He repents from it. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O God, if You forgive, You will forgive everyone and any of Your servants, not Alma?” . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Rather, they narrated the hadith of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: I have not seen anything closer to remorse than what Abu Hurairah said: The son of Adam is destined for his share of adultery, Hadith. What I have is that they left the hadith of Amr bin Dinar for the hadith which “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 180 - According to their condition"
"181","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr bin told us Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Shu’bah told us, Mansour told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in this verse {Except for the blame} [An-Najm: 32] He said: “He who is aware of the sin and then abandons it. Did you not hear the poet say:
 [The sea of rage]

 If You forgive, O God, You will forgive greatly...and any servant of Yours who does not suffer.”
 » This omission does not weaken the first chain of transmission, as Zakaria ibn Ishaq is a trustworthy narrator, and Ruh ibn Ubadah narrated from him, on the authority of Zakaria, and he “I mentioned in the chapters of this book the narration of interpretations from the Companions.”"
"182","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Surayj bin al-Nu’man told us, Fulayh bin Sulayman told us, On the authority of Hilal bin Ali, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of my nation will enter Paradise except Who refused? They said: Who refuses, O Messenger of God? He said: “Whoever disobeys me has refused.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it has another chain of narration, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, according to their conditions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 182 - According to their condition"
"183","Ahmad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told me, On the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will enter Paradise except those who refuse. And he strayed from God like the straying of a camel.” There is also a witness to this, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili."
"184","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abu Khaled, he said: Abu Umamah Al-Bahili passed by Khaled bin Yazid bin Muawiyah and asked him about the softest word he heard from The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “All of you will enter Paradise except those who stray from God. The camel to its people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 184 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"185","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told me, Muhammad ibn Sirin, and Khalas, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God has one hundred mercies, of which He distributed mercy among the people of This world has expanded them until their appointed time, and He has delayed ninety-nine for His guardians. Indeed, God Almighty will take that mercy which He has apportioned. between the people of the world up to ninety-nine, and He will complete it with one hundred mercies for His friends on the Day of Resurrection.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed in it on the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman in brief, then Muslim reported it, from the hadith of Abdul-Malik ibn Abu Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, is more complete than the two hadiths and has evidence of the consistency of the hadith of Awf.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 185 - According to their condition and taken out of it"
"186","Abu Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Hajjaj bin informed us Abu Zainab, who said: I heard Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God created on the day He created The heavens and the earth are a hundred mercies, each mercy as equal as the heavens and the earth. So He divided mercy among all creatures, and He delayed nine. And ninety mercies for Himself, so when on the Day of Resurrection He returns this mercy, it will become one hundred mercies with which He will have mercy on His servants.” There is another witness and an explanation of it, on the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 186 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"187","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, my father told me, Al-Jariri told me, On the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri, Jundub narrated to us, who said: A Bedouin came and saddled his mount, then mounted it, and prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, he came to his camel, unhitched it, then mounted it, then called out: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not Do not share our mercy with anyone. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What do you say, is it more lost or his camel?” Didn't you hear what he said? They said: Yes. He said: “He has prohibited a vast mercy. Indeed, God created one hundred mercies, and He sent down a mercy by which He showed compassion to the creatures, whether jinn, humans, or animals. And he has ninety-nine. Do you say, “Is it a stray or his camel?”"
"188","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Uday Ibn Thabit and Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. One of them referred him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, Gabriel He used to put clay in Pharaoh’s mouth for fear that he would say, “There is no god but God.”"
"189","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, he told me Adi bin Thabit, and Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he mentioned “that Gabriel started putting clay in Pharaoh's mouth for fear that he would say: There is no god but God, and God will have mercy on him. Or he said: For fear that God would have mercy on him. An authentic hadith, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 189 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"190","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ishaq, and Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail ibn Ulayya told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Hamza bin Abdullah bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying during some of his prayers: “O God, give me a simple reckoning.” When he left, I said: Oh Messenger of God, what is the reckoning? He said: “He looks at his book and ignores it. Indeed, whoever’s reckoning is discussed on that day, O Aisha, will perish, and all that It befalls the believer, God casts from him even a thorn that pricks him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever’s account is discussed will be punished.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 190 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"191","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi told us, Abu Al-Mujah told us, Abdan told us, Abdullah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam told us Al-Ghasani, on the authority of Damra ibn Habib, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The wise one is he who humbles himself and does After death, and the incapable person is he who follows his own desires and hopes against God.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 191 - No, by God, I mean, not according to Al-Bukhari’s condition, as Al-Hakim Abu Bakr said, and it is valid."
"192","Abu Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Muhammad bin Abd told us. Al-Aziz bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, Hussein bin Othman bin Abdul-Rahman, and Abdul-Rahman bin Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman told me. Ibn Awf, on the authority of Amer Ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer is an infidel.” “They agreed on Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid, and this is a strange and authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it due to the ignorance of this Muhammad bin Abd al-Aziz al-Zuhri.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 192 - What they produced is strange and authentic due to the ignorance of Muhammad"
"193","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Uthman Al-Adami told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Hajjaj bin Nusayr told us, Shaddad bin Saeed told us, and he told me Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Harami bin Amara told us, Shaddad told us Ibn Sa`id Abu Talha al-Rasibi, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This nation will be gathered into three groups: a group who will enter Paradise without reckoning, and a group who will be given a simple account and then they will enter Paradise. And a group of people will come on their backs like mountains anchored with sins. Then God will be asked about them, and He knows best about them, and He will say: Who are these? They say: These are your servants. He says: Take it away from them and assign it to the Jews and Christians and admit them into Paradise with My mercy. This is an authentic hadith from the hadith of Harami bin Amara according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. As for Hajjaj bin Nasr, I attributed it to Harami. Because I exalted in it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 193 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"194","Ali bin Bandar Al-Zahid told me, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Faryabi told me, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna Al-Zaman told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, He said: There was a boy on the back of the road, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by, and people were with him. When the boy’s mother saw the people, she feared that her son would have intercourse with her, so she heard So she carried him and said: My son, my son. The people said, O Messenger of God: This woman would not have her son thrown into the Fire, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “And God does not throw His beloved into Hell.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 194 - According to their condition"
"195","Ahmed bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, he said: It was read to Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi while I was listening. Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth narrated to me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “O Messenger of God, one of us commits a sin.” He said: “It will be written against him.” He said: “Then he should ask forgiveness from it and repent.” He said: “It will be forgiven and he will repent.” And God does not tire until you tire.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 195 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"196","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Zakaria told us Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Waki’ reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The great sins from the beginning of Surah An-Nisa until {If you avoid the great sins that you are forbidden} [An-Nisa’: 31] From the beginning of the surah there are thirty verses «. This is an authentic hadith according to the stipulation of the two Sheikhs, and it must be narrated according to what I stipulated in the interpretation of the Companions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 196 - According to their condition, which is a companion’s interpretation"
"197","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, dictating, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Muadh bin Hani told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Sinan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of his father, that he narrated to him and he had a companion, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Indeed, the saintly friends of God are those who perform the five prayers that were prescribed for him. He fasts Ramadan, and he expects his fast to be rewarded. He feels that he has a right, and he gives the zakat on his wealth as he expects it, and he avoids the sins that he forbade. God on her behalf. Then a man asked him and said: O Messenger of God, what are the major sins? He said: “They are nine: associating others with God, killing the soul of a believer unjustly, fleeing on the Day of Battle, consuming an orphan’s property, and consuming usury. And he slandered the chastised woman, disobedience to Muslim parents, and declaring the Sacred House lawful before you, whether alive or dead. Then he said: “He will not die.” A man who did not commit these major sins, perform prayer, and pay zakat unless he was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a house whose doors were made of Gold. “They cited as evidence the narrators of this hadith other than Abd al-Hamid ibn Sinan. As for Umair ibn Qatada, he was a companion and his son Ubaid was agreed upon. Taking it out and using it as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 197 - Umair ibn Qatada is a companion, and they did not mention Abd al-Hamid. He said, “I told him due to his ignorance, and Ibn Hibban trusted him.”"
"198","It was narrated to us by Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Bishr ibn Hajr al-Sami narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Al-Munakadir said: Abdullah bin Abbas and Ibn Amr met, and Ibn Abbas said to him: “Which verse in the Book of God do you most hope for?” Abdullah bin Amr said: {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of God’s mercy} [Az-Zumar: 53] And he said: “But say Abraham {My Lord, show me how You bring the dead to life. He said, “Do you not believe?” He said, “Yes, but so that my heart may be at peace.” [Al-Baqarah: 260] This is for what is in the breasts and whispers. Satan is God’s approval from the words of Abraham, when He said, “Have you not believed?” He said, “Yes.” [Al-Baqarah: 260] “. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 198 - There is a break"
"199","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Amr Ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Al-Muttalib, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man will With his good character, he stays awake at night and fasts during the day.” “This is a hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and the one who witnessed it is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 199 - According to their condition"
"200","Abu Sa`id Ismail bin Ahmad Al-Baji told us, Abu Ya`la told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamil Al-Aruqi told us, Hibban bin Hilal told us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God will convey to the servant “By his good character, such as fasting and prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 200 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"201","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim Al-Yamimi told us, My father told me that Ikrimah bin Khalid bin Saeed bin Al-Aas Al-Makhzoumi told him that he met Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said To him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we are Banu al-Mughirah, a people among whom there is pride. Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say anything about that? Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no man who is arrogant in himself and arrogant in his walk except He met God while He was angry with Him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 201 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"202","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Suraqa bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? “The defeated, the weak, and the people of Hell, all of them arrogant, arrogant and arrogant.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 202 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"203","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Abi Uthman al-Tayalisi told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding what he narrates on the authority of his Lord Almighty, he said: “Pride is my cloak. Whoever disputes my cloak, I will cut off.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Muslim narrated it via Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, without This word
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 203 - Narrated by Muslim"
"204","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He rides a donkey, wears wool, seizes a sheep, and shows respect to the guest.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 204 - According to their condition"
"205","Abu al-Tayyib Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Hayri told us, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Nu`aym al-Madani told us, Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim, Shayban Abu Muawiya told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rides a donkey, wears wool, seizes a sheep, and shows respect to guests.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Rather, I mentioned it in these places because this is a part of faith and it has There is evidence that Zaban was alone with him, and they did not bring him out.”"
"206","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, on the authority of Zaban bin Faid, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever abandons clothing while he is able Out of humility before God, God called him to the heads of creation, so that he could have the choice of wearing the garment of faith whichever he wished.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 206 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"207","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ali bin al-Madini told us, Sufyan told us, Ayoub bin Aidh Al-Tai, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab went out to the Levant, and with us was Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. So they came to a ford, and Omar was upon a camel of his, so he dismounted, took off his socks, and placed them on his shoulder, and took the reins of his she-camel and entered with it. The ford, and Abu Ubaidah said: O Commander of the Faithful, you are doing this. You take off your socks, put them on your shoulders, and take the reins. Your camel, and you go through labor with it? I am pleased that the people of the country honored you, so Omar said: “Oh, no one else said, ‘Abu Ubaidah, I made him a punishment for the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, we were the most humiliated of people, but God honored us with Islam, so no matter how much we ask for honor other than what God honored us with, God will humiliate us.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, because they all cited as evidence Ayyub ibn Aidh al-Tai and the rest of its narrators, and they did not narrate it and there is evidence from a hadith. Al-A’mash, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 207 - According to their condition"
"208","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Qays. Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, said: When Omar came to Syria, the soldiers met him wearing an izar, slippers, and a turban, and he was holding his head. His camel was wading through the water, and he said to him - meaning someone said - O Commander of the Faithful, did the soldiers and the patriarchs of the Levant meet you while you are in this state? Omar said: “We are a people whom God has honored with Islam, and we will not seek honor through anything else.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 208 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"209","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amer, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of this. He said: “He is not among us who does not have mercy on our young and knows the rights of “Our eldest,” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Abdullah bin Amir Al-Yahsbi as evidence, but they did not narrate it.” The well-known hadith is witnessed by the hadith of Muhammad bin Ishaq and others, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather. And in the hadith of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “And he enjoins what is right and forbids what is wrong,” “I only left it out because the narrator of Laith bin Abi Salim”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 209 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"210","Abu Ahmad Hamza ibn al-Abbas al-Uqabi told us, in Baghdad, Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham told us, Nu`aym ibn Hammad told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi, Bamrou, Ahmed bin Sayyar told us, Warith bin Ubaid Allah told us, they said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Khalid bin Mahran Al-Hadha reported on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Blessing is with “I am the greatest of you.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 210 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"211","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ali bin Hamshadh told us, he told us Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, they said: Yahya told us - meaning Ibn Sa’id - Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I deprive you of the rights of the weak, the orphan and the woman.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 211 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"212","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Beiruti told us, my father told me, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i said: Abu Kathir al-Zubaidi narrated to me, on the authority of his father, and he was sitting with Abu Dharr. He said: So he collected hadith and met Abu Dharr while he was At the middle Jamarat, and people were surrounding him, he said: So I sat next to him until my knees touched his knees, and I forgot that hadith and everything slipped away from me. I wanted to ask him about it, so I raised my head to the sky and began to remember, so I said: O Abu Dharr, guide me to a deed that if a servant does it, he will enter into Paradise. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you believe in God?” I said: O Messenger of God, is there action that comes with faith? He said: “He is satisfied with what God has provided for him.” I said: O Messenger of God, if he is destitute, he has nothing? He said: “He speaks kindly with his tongue.” I said: What if he is weak and his tongue does not express it? He said: “Let him help someone who is defeated.” I said: If he is weak and has no strength? He said: “Let it be made for a clumsy person.” I said: What if he is a clumsy person? Then he turned to me and said: “What do you want to do good for your friend?” He said: “He leaves the people behind him who harmed him.” I said: O Messenger of God, this is not all that matters. He said: “By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, not a single strand of them A servant would do it seeking the face of God, but it would take him by the hand on the Day of Resurrection and would not leave him until it admitted him to Paradise.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Abu Kathir al-Zubaidi as evidence in his book, and his name is Yazid bin Abd al-Rahman bin Udhaynah, and he is A well-known Tabi’i is called: Abu Kathir the blind man, and this hadith was not narrated by him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 212 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"213","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harith told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Al-A'mash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, on the authority of his father, Al-A'mash said: I do not know of it except on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Be careful in everything is good, except in doing the hereafter.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 213 - According to their condition"
"214","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, in Egypt, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman bin Abi Dhabab, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When He created God gave Adam and breathed the spirit into him. He sneezed and said: Praise be to God. So he thanked God, God willing, and his Lord said to him: May God have mercy on you, O Adam. And he said To him: O Adam, go to those angels to a group of them sitting, and say: Peace be upon you. So he went and they said: May the peace and mercy of God be upon you. And his blessings. Then he returned to his Lord and said: This is your greeting and the greeting of your children and their children. So God said to him with his hands clasped: Choose. Whichever you want, he said: I have chosen the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are a blessed right hand. Then he spread it out, and behold, in it was Adam and his descendants, and he said: What Lord? Who are these? He said: Your descendants. Then, behold, every human being has his age written between his eyes, and behold among them is a man whose light - or he said: of their light - is not written. He is only forty years old. He said: O Lord, increase his lifespan. He said: That is what was written for him. He said: For I have granted him sixty years of my life. He said: You and that. He said: Then he will reside in Paradise as long as God wills. Then Adam was descended from it, preparing for himself. Then the angel of death came to him, and Adam said to him: You hastened, a thousand years were written for me. He said: Yes, but you granted your son David sixty years of them, but he denied, so his descendants denied, and he forgot. Then his offspring forgot. On that day We were commanded about the Book and the witnesses.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab as evidence, and it was narrated on his authority by someone other than Safwan. I only narrated it from the hadith of Safwan because I mentioned it and it has an authentic witness” [p. 133].
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 214 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"215","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ali, the jurist Al-Shashi, told us about others. They said: Abu Bakr Orouba told us, Mukhlid bin Malik told us, Abu Khalid told us. Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 215 - True"
"216","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, Hisham bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Bashar and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, they said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Do you wonder that the privacy was for Abraham, and the speech was for Moses? And the vision is of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it, and it has a valid witness, on the authority of Ibn Abbas regarding the vision.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 216 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"217","Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad al-Shargawshuni al-Bukhari told us in Bukhara, saying: Saleh told us about him. Ibn Muhammad Ibn Habib Al-Hafiz, Muhammad Ibn Al-Sabbah told us, Abu Sa’id Ahmad Ibn Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad Ibn Yahya Al-Halwani told us, Muhammad told us Ibn al-Sabbah al-Dulabi, Ismail ibn Zakaria told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, and Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw And his Lord gave him peace. And it has a third witness with an authentic chain of narration.”"
"218","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us about Marwa, Sa`id ibn Masoud informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw his Lord.”"
"219","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He saw him twice. Such and such hadith was relied upon by the two sheikhs in this regard, the narrations of Aisha bint Al-Siddiq, Ubayy bin Ka’b, Abdullah bin Masoud, and Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Gabriel on him. Peace. “All of these news that I mentioned are true, and God knows best.”"
"220","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Razi told us, Abu Zar’ah Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Karim Al-Razi told us, and Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz, dictating, Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ayyub Al-Mukhurami told us, and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, about Marwa, narrating Abu Al-Mujih Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told us: Saeed bin Muhammad Al-Jarmi told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Wasil told us, Muhammad bin Thabit Al-Bunani told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Al Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The prophets have pulpits of gold.” He said: “So they will sit on them, and my pulpit, which I will not sit on - or sit on - will remain standing.” In the hands of my Lord for fear that He will send me to Paradise and spare my nation after me, so I say: O Lord, my nation, my nation, and God Almighty says: O Muhammad What do you want me to do to your nation? Then I will say: O Lord, hasten their reckoning. Then they will be called and brought to account. Some of them will enter Paradise by the mercy of God. And some of them will enter Paradise through my intercession. I did not stop interceding until I was given a check for men who had been sent to Hell, and I would bring an angel who is the custodian of Hell. He will say: O Muhammad, you have not left for the Fire due to the wrath of your Lord any remnant of your nation. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, except that the two sheikhs did not use Muhammad bin Thabit al-Bunani as evidence, and he has few hadiths, and his hadiths are collected as evidence. “And the hadith is strange in its reports of intercession, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 220 - The hadith is objectionable"
"221","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jabir told me, he said: I heard Sulaym bin Amir, saying: I heard Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, saying: We stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at a house, and I woke up from night, and if I did not see anything longer than the back of my journey, every man and his camel were stuck to the ground, so I got up and moved through the people until I fell to The sleeping place of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was not in it. I put my hand on the bed and it was cold. I went out and socialized with the people. And I say: “{To Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return} [Al-Baqarah: 156] The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taken until I left the entire army and saw It was dark, so I threw a stone, so I went into the blackness, and I saw Muadh bin Jabal and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and before us there was a sound like the sound of a millstone or... Like the sound of a hill when it is struck by the wind. Then we said to one another: O my people, stand firm until morning or the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes to you. He greeted us, so we stayed for as long as God wished, then he called out, “Are Muadh bin Jabal, Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and Awf bin Malik the sinners?” So we said: Yes, so he came to us and we left without asking him anything and he did not tell us until he sat down on his bed and said: “Do you know what he has given me the choice to do?” My Lord tonight? So we said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “He gave me a choice between letting half of my nation enter Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.” So we said: Oh. Messenger of God, pray to God to make us among its people.” He said: “It is for every Muslim.” “This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. He cited Sulaym bin Amir as evidence, but the rest of his narrators are agreed upon, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Saeed bin Abi Arouba and Hisham bin Sanbar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Awf bin Malik. “As for the hadith of Saeed”"
"222","[Page: 136] Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, he said: He told us: Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Abi Ziyad told us, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Abdah bin Suleiman told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali told them that Awf bin Malik said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of his travels.” He mentioned Hadith. “As for the hadith of Hisham al-Dastawai.”"
"223","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari and Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muadh told us. Ibn Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and he mentioned The hadith is long. “This hadith of Qatada is an authentic hadith according to their condition, but they did not narrate it.” This hadith was narrated by Abu Qalaba Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Jarmi, on the authority of Awf bin Malik [p. 137]."
"224","Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Tamimi told me, Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Ishaq bin Shaheen told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us, about Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in some of his battles, but we ended up in the same place. One night, we did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his place. And, behold, the camels had placed their mounts, and behold, I was with ropes, and behold, Muadh ibn A mountain confronted me and I confronted it and said: Where is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Behind me, and he mentioned the hadith. “This is authentic from the hadith of Abu Qilaba, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.” This hadith was narrated, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of Awf bin Malik. “With an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 221 - He mentioned the text and said, “This is according to Muslim’s condition.”"
"225","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hussein bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Qattan Al-Raqqi informed us, Muhammad bin Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Hammad Abu Bakr Al-Wasiti, Khalid bin Abdullah bin Khaled Al-Wasiti told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, that they were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in some of his battles. Awf said: Then I heard a shaking behind me. Like the sound of a millstone, then I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in enemy land, guards would be over him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man came to me from my Lord giving me a choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.” Then Muadh bin Jabal said: O Messenger of God, you have recognized my strength, so make me one of them. He said: “You are one of them.” Awf bin Malik said: O Messenger of By God, you know that we have left our people and our property desiring for the sake of God and His Messenger, so make us one of them. He said: “You are one of them.” So we concluded. The people had revolted, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sit down.” So they sat down, as if none of them had stood up. He said: “He came to me, coming from my Lord, so he gave me the choice.” between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.” They said: O Messenger of God, make us among them. He said: “It is for those who died.” He associates anything with God.”"
"226","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Sulaiman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi told us, Ali bin Hashim told us Bin Al-Barid, Abdul-Jabbar Bin Al-Abbas Al-Shibami narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun Bin Abi Juhaifah Al-Suwai’i, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Bin Al-Aqma Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Aqeel Al-Thaqafi, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a delegation from Thaqif, and we blocked one of the roads of Medina until... We opened the door, and there is not a man among the people more hateful to us than a man whom we can approach. So we entered, and he greeted us and pledged allegiance to us, so we did not leave from him. There is not among the people a man more beloved to us than a man from whom we have left. So I said: O Messenger of God, have you not asked your Lord for a kingdom like the king of Solomon? He laughed and said: “Perhaps your companion in the sight of God is better than the king of Solomon. God did not send a prophet without giving him a call. Some of them were He took a worldly life for it and was given it, and among them was he who supplicated for it against his people and they were destroyed because of it. Indeed, God gave me a supplication and I hid it. With my Lord as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection.” “Muslim cited Ali bin Hashim as evidence, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Aqeel al-Thaqafi is a companion. Our imams may have cited him as evidence in their Musnads. As for Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Abbas, for he is the one who collects his hadiths and prepares their Musnads in the Kufayyin.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 226 - It is not fixed"
"227","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Ali told us Bin Muhammad bin Issa, they said: Abu Al-Yaman Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ Al-Bahrani told us, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “I have been shown what will befall my nation after me, and some of them have shed the blood of others, and This is from God, as was done before the nations before them. So I asked him to appoint me as my guardian on the Day of Resurrection as an intercession on their behalf, and he did.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. The reason they have for it is that Abu Al-Yaman narrated it twice.” He once said: On the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas. He once said: On the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, on the authority of Anas. “We have presented the statement regarding something like this, that it is not denied that the hadith is narrated by an imam from among the imams on the authority of two sheikhs, and he once narrated it on the authority of This, and once about that.” Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Omar told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Sa’id told me, Ibrahim bin Hani told us. Al-Naysaburi. He said: Abu Al-Yaman told us: The hadith is the hadith of Al-Zuhri, and the one I told you on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, I made a mistake in it with a paper that I turned over. Al-Hakim said: “This is like taking someone by the hand, for Ibrahim bin Hani is trustworthy and trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 227 - According to their condition"
"228","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd informed us Al-Razzaq, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, and Abu Bakr bin Zangwayh told us, And Abu Bakr bin Askar and Ishaq bin Zurayq told us: Abdul Razzaq told us, and Ali bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Yusuf Al-Sulami told us, we told him Abdul Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “My intercession is for the people of my nation who commit great sins.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they narrated the hadith of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, with its length, and whoever imagines it.” This word from the hadith is a misconception, as this intercession contains the suppression of the innovations that differentiate between intercession for the people of minor matters. And the major sins, and there is evidence of this wording on the authority of Qatada and Ash’ath bin Jabir Al-Hadani.”
 As for the hadith of Qatada"
"229","So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Sahl bin Abdul-Aziz Al-Majwiz told us, and Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, they said: We told us: Al-Khalil bin Omar bin Ibrahim, Omar bin Saeed Al-Abh told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Intercession for those who commit great sins from my nation.”
 As for the hadith of Ash’ath bin Jabir"
"230","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi informed us, and Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, they said: Sulayman bin Harb, Bastam bin Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath Al-Hadani, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “My intercession for the people of great sins. “My nation.” “And he has a valid witness to the condition of a Muslim.”"
"231","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Tanisi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My intercession for the people of my nation who committed major sins.” “They all cited Zuhayr bin Muhammad Al-Anbari as evidence.” Muhammad bin Thabit Al-Bunani followed him, on the authority of Jafar"
"232","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Bashar, and Ishaq bin Mansour told us, they said: Abu Dawud told us, Muhammad bin Thabit al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He said: “My intercession is for the people of my nation who commit sins.” Abu Ja’far said: And Jabir said to me: O Muhammad, whoever is not among the people of sins, what is his? And for intercession?"
"233","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Rajab in the year three hundred and ninety-three. Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Malhan informed us, Yahya ibn Bukayr informed us, Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Salim ibn Abu Salem, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Mu’tab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he heard him say: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what has your Lord returned to you? In intercession? He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I thought that you were the first to ask me about that, because of what I saw of your eagerness for knowledge. With His hand, because I am concerned about their defeat at the gate of Paradise, it is more important to me than the completion of my intercession, and my intercession for whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely. His heart confirms his tongue, and his tongue confirms his heart.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, for Mu’awiyah bin Mu’tab is an Egyptian from the Tabi’een, and Al-Bukhari narrated the hadith of Amr bin Abi Amr Mawla al-Muttalib, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, who is the happiest of people with your intercession, hadith, without This word, and the meaning is close to it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 233 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"234","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Nadr bin Salamah Al-Jarudi told us, Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Al-Ma’mal told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadala, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of his grandfather Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God says God Almighty: Take out from the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and in whose heart is an atom’s weight of faith. Take out from the Fire whoever says: No. There is no god but Allah, or remember me, or fear me in a position.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not include the saying “Whoever remembers Me or fears Me in a place.” Abu Dawud continued, emphasizing his narration and condensing it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 234 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"235","Abu Muhammad Yahya bin Mansour told us, Abu Bakr al-Jarudi told us, Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abu Dawud told us, Mubarak bin Fadala, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God says: Get out of Hellfire whoever remembers Me or fears Me in a place.”"
"236","Abu Omar and Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, Khaled, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Ibn Abi Al-Jada’, who said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “They will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation, more numerous than the Banu Tamim.” “This is Abdullah bin Abi Al-Juda’a, a famous companion. He was mentioned in the Musnads, and he was one of the Companions who lived in Mecca.”"
"237","Tell us that what you mentioned is correct, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Shaqiq said: I sat with a people of whom I was the fourth, and one of them said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “They will enter Paradise.” Through the intercession of a man from my nation, more than the Banu Tamim.” He said: We said: “Beside you, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Beside me.” I said: You heard it from the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, and when he got up, I said, “Who is this?” They said: This is Ibn Abi Al-Jada’. “This is an authentic hadith. They used its narrations as evidence, and Abdullah bin Shaqiq Tabi’i used it as evidence. However, they left it out due to the uniqueness of what was mentioned above. Al-Tabābi’i, on the authority of the Companions”"
"238","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl, and Abu Amr bin Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Zahid told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ali told us, Yahya told us. Bin Yahya, Abu Muawiya reported, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais Al-Asadi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Uqish, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are no two Muslims who execute three people who have not yet reached the age of breaking oaths, but God admits them to Paradise by His mercy.” They said: O Messenger of God, and the one of two. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, from my nation there will be someone who will enter Paradise, through his intercession, is greater than harm, and among my nation there are those who will worship Hell until he becomes one of its corners.” “This hadith has an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim, and Al-Harith ibn Uqish narrated his hadith in the Musnads of the Imams, and it is of the type that we presented. It was mentioned only by one Tabibi on the authority of a man from among the Companions. This is how Shu’bah narrated it, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 238 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"239","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Al-Mundhir bin Al-Walid Al-Jaudi told us, My father told me, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Uqish, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “A man from my nation will enter Paradise and will intercede for more than one who harms.”"
"240","Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Ayyub Al-Tusi told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Handali told us, Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Ruqi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will be the imam of the prophets, their preacher, and the companion of their intercession, without any pride.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 240 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"241","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Hudhayfah Al-Nahdi told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Muhammad Ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Tufayl Ibn Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the day On the Resurrection, I was the imam of the prophets, their orator, and the companion of their intercession, without any pride.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it because Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel bin Abi Talib was alone, and because of the evil that was attributed to him. Memorization, and it is trustworthy and trustworthy among our early imams.”"
"242","Abu Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I know of a word that a servant would not say truly from his heart and die in that state unless God forbids him.” On fire, there is no god but Allah. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording or with this chain of transmission.” They only agreed on the hadith of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Itban bin Malik, the long hadith at the end: “And God has forbidden the Fire from anyone who says: No.” There is no god but Allah “Hadith. They also narrated it from the hadith of Shu’bah, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, and Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of al-Walid Abi Bishr, on the authority of Hamran, on the authority of Uthman, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but God will enter Paradise.” There is no mention of Umar in it, and it has a witness with this chain of transmission on the authority of Uthman, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 242 - According to their condition"
"243","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Uthman bin Omar, and Ruh bin Ubadah told us, they said: We told us: Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Ubaid, he said: I heard Hamran bin Aban, he said: I heard Uthman bin Affan, and he spoke little. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever knows that praying for him is a right and an obligation will enter Paradise.”"
"244","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman bin Bilal told us, he told me Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais, on the authority of Salman bin Bilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yasar Al-Araj, that he heard Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, He narrates, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Three people will not enter Paradise: the disobedient to his parents, the cuckold, and the man of women.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. The focus is on the narration of Ayyub ibn Sulaiman, as he did not mention Umar in its chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 244 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"245","Abu Al-Hasan Ubayd Allah bin Ahmad Al-Tajer told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdullah bin Saleh, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Harmala bin Yahya told me, Ibn Wahb reported, Muawiyah ibn Salih informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Nawwas ibn Samaan, The companion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God gave an example of a straight path. On both shoulders of the path there are two fences in it. Opened doors, and on the doors are loose curtains, and on the path there is a caller who calls, saying: O people, take the path all together and do not deviate, and a caller calls On the path. If one of you wants to open any of those doors, he says: Woe to you, do not open it, for if you open it, you will enter it. So the path: Islam, and the curtains: the limits of God, and the opened doors are forbidden by God, and the caller at the head of the path is the Book of God, and the caller from above is a preacher “May God be remembered in the heart of every Muslim.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 245 - According to Muslim’s condition and there is no reason for it"
"246","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl informed us, saying: Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar informed us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid informed me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Sa’ib, that Abdul-Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Azhar, He told him, on the authority of his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is only like a believing servant when he is afflicted with… Thunder and fever are like an iron that enters a fire, and its impurity goes away, but its goodness remains.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and what I have is that they left it because Abdul Hamid did not narrate it on the authority of his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 246 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"247","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ told me, Khalid told me Ibn Yazid, that he heard Abu Al-Zubayr Al-Makki, speaking, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon some of his family. It is pain accompanied by fever. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Umm Muldam.” A woman said: Yes, so may God curse her. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not curse her, for she washes away - or removes - the sins of the children of Adam just as furnace removes the impurities from iron.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 247 - According to Muslim’s condition and there is no reason for it"
"248","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya and Abu Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Qasim Al-Adawi told us, saying: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq, Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Friends are three: Either a friend, and he says to you: What you have given, and what you have retained, is not yours.” That is Malik, or Khalil, and he says: I am with you until you come to the king’s gate, then I will come back and leave you. These are your family and your clan. They will accompany you until you reach your grave, then they will return and leave you, or Khalil will say: I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you exit, that is your job. He says: By God, you were one of the three who were least in charge of me. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. They all cited Al-Hajjaj ibn Al-Hajjaj as evidence, and I do not know of any reason for it, and they did not narrate it according to This is the case, and he has a witness who narrated it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 248 - According to their condition and there is no reason for it"
"249","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr ibn Hazm heard Anas ibn Malik informing the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Three people follow a believer after his death: his family, And his money and his work. Two of them will return and one will remain. His family and his wealth will return and his work will remain.” Imran al-Qattan followed al-Hajjaj and narrated the hadith in its entirety."
"250","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no servant but that he has three companions,” so he mentioned the hadith in its length, similar to the hadith of Ibrahim bin Tahman, “And he has Another witness to the condition of a Muslim.”"
"251","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith told us, Hammad, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The example of a believer and the example of a punishment is that of a man who has Three of his friends said to him: I am yours, take from me what you want and leave what you want, and the other said: I am with you, I will carry you and place you, so if you die I left you. He said: This is his family. The third said: I am with you. I will go in with you and I will go out with you whether I live or die. He said: This is his work.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 251 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"252","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Amr al-Hurashi told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Abd al-Rahman told us. Ibn Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Kharijah Ibn Zayd Ibn Thabit, he said: Zayd Ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me So I learned the Jewish writing for him, and he said: “By God, no Jews believe in my writing.” So I learned it, and half a month did not pass before I mastered it. He said: “I would write to him when he wrote, and I would read to him when he wrote to him.” “They all cited Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, and this is an authentic hadith, and I do not know of anything other than the permission to learn the writing of the People of the Book.” This hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 252 - This is correct"
"253","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Hussein Al-Mu’allim told me, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Qutay’i - and the pronunciation is his - informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu'allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, said: It was reported to me that Abu Sabra bin Salamah Al-Hudhali heard Ibn Ziyad asking about the basin. The basin of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: What I see is the truth, after he asked Abu Barzah Al-Aslami, Al-Baraa bin Azib, and Aidh bin Amr, He said: I do not believe these people. Abu Sabra said: Shall I not tell you a healing hadith? Your father sent me money to Muawiyah, and I met Abdullah bin Amr, and he told me what he said, and I wrote it down with my pen, what he heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And I did not add a word nor subtract. He told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not like the obscene nor the indecent, and the one who The soul of Muhammad is in His hand. The Hour will not come until immorality, indecency, severing of family ties, and bad neighborliness will appear, and the trustworthy person will be betrayed and trusted. The traitor, and the example of a believer is like a bee that ate a perfume, placed a perfume, and dropped a perfume, and it did not spoil or be broken, and the example of a servant A believer is like a fine piece of gold that was blown on and came out good. It was weighed and did not diminish. And he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Your destination is a basin whose width is as long as it is, and it is farther than the distance between Aila and Mecca, and that is the distance of a month, in which are the likes of the stars. Jugs, its water was whiter than silver, and he drank from it and never felt thirsty again. Ibn Ziyad said: No one told me a hadith like this. I bear witness that the basin is a right and an obligation. He took the document that Abu . And in the hadith of Abu Usama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Sabra. “This is an authentic hadith. The two sheikhs agreed to use as evidence all of its narrators except Abu Sabra al-Hudhali, who is a major and clear follower. Its mention in the Musnads and histories is not disputed, and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah” [p. 148]."
"254","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, On the authority of Abu Sabra Al-Hudhali, he mentioned the hadith in its length"
"255","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told me, Ruh bin Aslam told us, Shaddad Abu Talha, Abu Al-Wazi’ Jabir bin Amr Al-Rasibi told us, he said: I heard Abu Barza, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “The basin from Aila to Sana’a is as wide as it is long. In it are two drains pouring from Paradise, one of which is paper and the other is gold, sweeter than Honey is colder than snow, whiter than milk, and softer than butter. It contains pitchers as large as the stars in the sky. Whoever drinks from it will not be thirsty until He will enter Paradise.” He said: Ayoub added to it, on the authority of Abu al-Wazi`, on the authority of Abu Barza, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “It will descend into the hands of the believers.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He used as evidence two hadiths on the authority of Abu Talha al-Rasibi, on the authority of Abu al-Wazi’, on the authority of Abu Barza, and he is a stranger. It is authentic from the hadith of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Abu al-Wazi’, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 255 - Gharib is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim"
"256","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ammar bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Shu’bah told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are not part of a hundred thousand.” Part of those who visit the basin. They asked him: How much were you? He said: “Eight hundred or nine hundred.” “This Abu Hamzah Al-Ansari is Talha bin Yazid, and Al-Bukhari cited him as evidence.”"
"257","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, and Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Musa reported, Jarir and Abu Muawiya told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “You are not one part out of a thousand of those who will come to me at the Fountain on the Day of Resurrection.” He said: So we said: To Zaid: How many were you that day? He said: Between six hundred and nine hundred. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but they left it out due to the number of disagreements in its text, and God knows best.” There is evidence to support the condition of Muslim, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, in mentioning the basin without this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 257 - Perhaps they left it due to the difference in number"
"258","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub al-Adl informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Ja`far ibn Aoun informed us, Abu Hayyan Yahya informed us Bin Saeed bin Hayyan Al-Taymi Taim Al-Rabab, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, who said: I witnessed Zayd bin Arqam and Ubayd Allah bin Ziyad was sent to him, and he said: What hadiths have I heard from you that you narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, claiming that he will have a pool in Paradise? Then he said: That Messenger narrated to us We promised him, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: You lied, but you are an old man and have become senile. He said: My ears heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, meaning I heard him say: “Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in the Fire.” I did not lie to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"259","Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told me, Abu Sahl Hassan bin Sahl Al-Labbad told me, Abu Saleh Abdullah bin Saleh told me, Al-Layth, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He left the group by a hand’s breadth, and he has taken off the collar of Islam from his neck until he returns to it.” He said: “And whoever dies without an imam of the group, then His death was the death of pre-Islamic times.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed him and said: “O people! Between Kufa to the Black Stone, and its vessels are as many as the stars, and I saw people from my nation when they approached me, a man came out against them and said: Take them on my behalf. Then another group came and he did the same to them, but he did not escape from them except like a camel. He said: Abu Bakr is one of them, O Prophet. God said: “No, but they are a people who will go out after you and walk in retreat.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Al-Hajjaj bin Muhammad also narrated it, on the authority of Al-Layth, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 259 - According to their condition"
"260","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna, and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Musaddad told us, Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, He said: I entered upon Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad while they were discussing the basin. He said: He said: Anas came to you. He said: O Anas, what do you say about The pelvis? He said: I said: “I did not think that I would live until I saw people like you walking in the basin. I have left behind me old women, not one of them praying a prayer.” Unless she asks her Lord to place her in the basin of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it, but it has a valid witness on the authority of Humaid according to their conditions.”"
"261","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, about Marwa, Abu Al-Mujah told us, Abdan told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Abdul-Hamid told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, He said: I entered upon Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad and they were hesitating about mentioning the basin, then he mentioned something similar to it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 260 - According to their condition"
"262","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, that Abdullah bin Khabbab told them. He said: Khabbab told me that he was sitting at the door of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he came out while we were sitting, and he said: “Listen.” We said: We heard, O Messenger of God. He said: “There will be princes after me, so do not believe them.” With their lies and do not help them in their oppression, for whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their oppression will not return to the basin.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” This was witnessed by the famous hadith on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah, although there was disagreement over it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 262 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"263","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Wasiti told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Malik bin Mongols, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out against us one day while we were in There are five Arabs and four non-Arabs in the mosque. He said: “Do you hear?” We said: We heard, twice. He said: “Listen, there will be princes after me, so whoever enters upon them and confirms their lies and helps them in their oppression.” He is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to the basin. And whoever does not enter upon them and does not believe their lies and does not help them in their injustice is “He is from me and I am from him and the basin will return to me.” It was narrated by Mas’ar bin Kadam and Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Asim Al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ajra. “As for the hadith of Al-Thawri.”"
"264","So Abu Muhammad al-Isfaraini told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Harun bin Ishaq al-Hamdani told us, Muhammad bin told me Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Asim al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah, he said: He came out The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came upon us, and we were nine, and between us was a red-colored man. He said: “Indeed, there will be princes after me, so whoever believes them.” With their lies and helping them in their injustice, he is not of me, and I am not of him, and the basin will not be returned to me. And whoever does not believe them in their lies and does not help them in Their injustice is from me and I from it, and the basin will return to me.” Jabir bin Abdullah witnessed what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ka’b bin Ujrah."
"265","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ka’b ibn Ujrah: “May God protect you, O Ka’b bin Ujrah, from the leadership of the fools.” He said: What is the leadership of the fools? He said: “There will be princes after me who do not follow my guidance and do not follow my Sunnah. So whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their injustice, Those are not of me, and I am not of them, and they will not return to my coffin, and whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their injustice, those are of me. And I am one of them, and they will return to my basin, O Ka’b bin Ajrah. Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is an offering - or he said: proof - """
"266","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Ayyash bin Al-Walid Al-Raqam told us, Abd Al-Ala bin Abd told us. The highest, a praiseworthy narration, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I entered Paradise, and behold, I was at a river with tents running along its two sides.” The pearl, so I thrust my hand towards the water stream, and when I touched it, I exclaimed, so I said to Gabriel: What is this? He said: This is the Kawthar that your Lord Almighty has given you. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 266 - According to their condition"
"267","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us, Fulayh bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Ali, On the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Paradise is a hundred levels, and between every two levels is the distance between the heavens.” And the earth, and Paradise is one of the highest levels thereof, and from it gush the rivers of Paradise, so if you ask God, ask Him for Paradise.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” He has authentic evidence with a similar chain of transmission, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed."
"268","Abu Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Harun bin Marouf told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Fulayh bin Sulaiman told me, on the authority of Hilal bin Ali, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. It was also narrated with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 267 - According to their condition"
"269","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, and Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, they said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Paradise is a hundred degrees between each Two degrees as between the heaven and the earth, and Paradise is the highest degree and from it gush the rivers of Paradise. So if you ask God, ask Him. Paradise »"
"270","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mihran told us, Ubi told us, Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Hayy told me, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, in Paradise there are rooms whose outside can be seen from Its interior and its interior are from its exterior.” Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: “For the one who speaks kindly, eats good food, and spends the night standing while the people are asleep.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They all cited as evidence Hayy, who was Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Mazhaji, the companion of Suleiman bin Abd. The king, and it is called his master, but they did not expel him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 270 - According to their condition"
"271","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Anas, in the Almighty’s saying {At the Sidrat al-Muntaha} [An-Najm: 14], that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It has been raised for me.” A sidra tree whose end is in the seventh heaven, its stems are like the hills of Hajar, its leaves are like the ears of an elephant, two visible rivers emerge from its stem. And two deep rivers. He said: I said: O Gabriel, what are these? He said: As for the two who are inside, they are in Paradise, and as for the two who are visible, they are the Nile and the Euphrates. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context. And he has a strange witness from the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, with a valid chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 271 - According to their condition, they did not take him out in this manner"
"272","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Aslami told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The Sidra was raised for me, and behold, four rivers: two visible rivers, and two hidden rivers. As for the visible ones, they are the Nile and the Euphrates, and the The two interiors will flow in Paradise, and I was brought with three cups: a cup containing milk, a cup containing honey, and a cup containing wine, so I took what was in it. So I drank the milk, and it was said to me, ‘You and your nation have become fitrah.’” Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah said: “I said to our Sheikh Abu Abdullah, why did they not narrate this hadith? He said: Because Anas bin Malik did not hear it.” From the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he only heard it from Malik bin Sa’saa.” Al-Hakim said: “Then I looked and saw the letters that he heard from Malik bin There is no hardship other than this. Let the seeker of this knowledge know that the hadith of the Ascension Anas heard some of it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some of it from Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, and some of it is from Malik bin Sa`sa’ah other than this, and some of it is from Abu Hurairah.”"
"273","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Abu Sinan Dirar bin Murrah told us, on the authority of Muharib Ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people of Paradise are twenty and one hundred rows. These The nation has eighty rows of it.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and it has evidence from the hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 273 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"274","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Labid bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan told us Al-Ahwazi, Al-Hasan bin Al-Harith told us, Mu’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, we told him Abdullah bin Omar, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people of Paradise will be one hundred and twenty in rows, eighty of which will be from this nation.” “It was sent by Yahya bin Saeed and Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of al-Thawri.”"
"275","It was narrated by Al-Harith bin Hasira, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God told us God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while we were around him: “How are you, a quarter of the people of Paradise?” We said: A lot. He said: “How are you with the third?” He said: We said: That is more. He said: How are you and the half? We said: That is more. He said: “The people of Paradise are twenty and one hundred rows, of which you are eighty rows.” He said: We said: Those are the two-thirds, O Messenger. God, he said: “Yes.” “Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud did not hear most of the rumors from his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 275 - Abd al-Rahman did not hear from his father"
"276","Abu Qutaibah Salam bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami informed us, in Mecca, Musa bin Harun told us, Salamah bin Shabib told us, Al-Faryabi told us, Sufyan told us Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise. He said: God Almighty says: Do you desire anything, that I may give you more? They say: Our Lord, and what is more than what You have given us? He said: He says: “Rizwani is the greatest.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Al-Ashja’i followed Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi on its chain of transmission and text.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 276 - According to their condition"
"277","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman told us. Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise. God Almighty said: Shall I inform you of something greater than this? They said: Yes, and what is greater than this? He said: Al-Ridwan."
"278","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hatim Al-Adl told us about Marw, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr reported, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Death will be brought on the Day of The Resurrection will be in the form of a salty ram, and it will be said: O inhabitants of Paradise, and they will rise in fear and fear for fear of leaving what they are in. It will be said: Do you know this? They say: Yes, this is death. Then it will be said: O people of Hell. They will rise, rejoicing that they will emerge from what they are in. It will be said: Do you know this? They will say: Yes, this is death. Then he will command it and it will be slaughtered on the bridge, and it will be said to the two parties: Eternity as long as you find no. “He will die therein forever.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, as Yazid ibn Harun has proven it and transmitted it in all the narrations from him, and Al-Fadl ibn Al-Fadl agreed with him. Musa Al-Sinani and Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr “.” As for the hadith of Al-Fadl bin Musa” [p. 157]."
"279","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Halim Al-Marwazi told us, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection” - so he mentioned the hadith in a conditional manner -. “As for the hadith of Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed.”"
"280","So Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bundar told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, - so he mentioned it with its chain of transmission in a circumstance -, On the authority of Abu Hurairah. “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate this hadith other than this wording from the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 278 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"281","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Fakihi informed us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Abi Masarra told us, told us Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Azraqi, Muslim bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, On the authority of Amr bin Maymun Al-Awdi, he said: Muadh bin Jabal rose among us and said: “O children of Awud, I am the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. You know The return to God, then to Paradise or to Hell, and a residence without fear, and eternity without death in bodies that do not die.” This is an authentic hadith. Its chain of transmission is Meccan, and Muslim bin Khalid al-Zanji is the imam of the people of Mecca and their mufti, but the two sheikhs attributed it to the hadith “It is not of his making, and God knows best.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 281 - Sahih chain of transmission"
"282","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, and Abu Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of Abu Musa, in His saying, the Almighty, “And for whoever fears a place His Lord is two gardens} [The Most Gracious: 46] He said: “Two gardens of gold for those who came before, and two gardens of silver for those who follow.” This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim. They did not take him out like this.” They only narrated it from the hadith of Al-Harith bin Ubaid and Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “two gardens of silver” the hadith, and it does not contain any mention of the predecessors or those who follow. I heard Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz, saying: I heard Abu Al-Fadl Al-Wazir, saying: I heard Ma’mun Al-Misri, saying: I told my father Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa’i: Why did Muhammad bin Ismail abandon the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah? He said: “By God, Hammad bin Salamah is better and more truthful than Ismail bin Abi Uwais,” and he mentioned a long story similar to the replacement by Al-Harith bin Ubaid, on the authority of Hammad
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 282 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"283","Abdullah bin Omar bin Ali Al-Jawhari told me about Marwa, from the origin of his book, Yahya bin Sasawayh bin Abdul Karim told us, Suwayd bin Nasr, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The Day of Resurrection is like the time between noon and afternoon.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, provided that Suwayd bin Nasr preserved it, as he is trustworthy and trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 283 - According to their condition"
"284","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Halim informed us, Abu Al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurarah bin Awfa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Day of Resurrection for the believers will be like the time between noon and afternoon.”"
"285","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Abdul Rahman Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdullah bin Yazid told us, Sa’id bin Ayoub, Abu Sakhr told me, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Omar had a friend from the people of Syria who was writing to him, so Abdullah bin Omar wrote to him, I have heard that you spoke about something concerning fate, so be careful not to write to me, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is “There will be people in my nation who deny destiny.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Abu Sakhr Humaid bin Ziyad as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 285 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"286","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us dictation, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The Qadariyyah are the Magians of this nation. If they fall ill, then do not “You shall visit them, but if they die, you shall not witness them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, if it is authentic that Abu Hazim heard it from Ibn Umar and he did not narrate it and witness it.”"
"287","What?
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 286 - According to their condition, if it is authentic, according to Abu Hazim, hearing on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both.
 The book of knowledge"
"288","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam Al-Misri told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abu Yahya Fulayh bin Sulaiman Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar Al-Ansari, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever learns knowledge of what he seeks for the pleasure of God will not learn it except to achieve a purpose through it.” In this world, no one will know Paradise on the Day of Resurrection.” “This is an authentic hadith whose chain of narration is trustworthy, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. He attributed it and transmitted it on the authority of Falih Jama’ah, other than Ibn gift
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 288 - According to their condition"
"289","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Sirri told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Jawhari told us, In Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari and Al-Hasan bin Halim told us about Marw, saying: Abu Al-Mawjih, they said: Saeed bin Mansour Al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Tuwalah, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever learns knowledge seeking the pleasure of God should not learn it except to achieve by it a purpose in this world. He will not find it.” He knew Paradise.” Fulayh said: And he knew its scent. This hadith was narrated with two authentic chains of narration, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah and Ka’b bin Malik, may God be pleased with him. About them
 As for the hadith of Jabir"
"290","So Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, and Ahmad told us Bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, they said: Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not learn knowledge in order to boast of it to the scholars or Compare with the fools about it, and do not favor the council because of it. Whoever does that, the Fire will be the Fire.”"
"291","Abu Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Shaybani told us, from the origin of his book, Ahmed bin Hammad Al-Tajibi told us, in Egypt, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us: I heard Ibn Jurayj speaking on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, so he mentioned something similar to him. “This is the chain of transmission of Yahya bin Ayyub al-Masry, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, so he conveyed it and Yahya agreed to narrate it in the two Sahih books, and he sent it Abdullah bin Wahb, I am following the principle that I followed in accepting the increase in confidence in the chains of transmission and the texts.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 290 - Narrated by Ibn Wahb, so he sent it"
"292","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: And I heard Ibn Jurayj narrates that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not learn knowledge in order to boast of it to the scholars, nor to compete with the foolish by it, nor to That you may speak about it in the assemblies, and whoever does that, the fire will be the fire.”
 As for the hadith of Ka’b bin Malik"
"293","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibn Abi Uwais told us, my brother told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever seeks knowledge in order to show off to scholars, or to compete with fools, or to accept people benefiting from it, will go to Hell.” “The two sheikhs did not narrate anything about Ishaq bin Yahya, but I made him a witness to what I presented of their conditions, and Ishaq bin Yahya was one of the nobles. Quraysh
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 293 - They did not bring it out for Ishaq, but rather brought it out as a witness"
"294","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, from the origin of his book, and Abu Ali Al-Hafiz asked him about it. Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, they said: Nu’aym bin Hammad, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father Jubayr, he said: He rose The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was filled with fear, so he said: “May God bless a servant who heard my words and understood them, then conveyed them to those who did not hear them, for perhaps a pregnant woman A jurisprudent who has no jurisprudence, and perhaps someone who carries jurisprudence to one who is more knowledgeable than him. There are three things that the heart of a believer should not neglect: sincerity of work for the sake of God, And obedience to those in authority, and adherence to the community of Muslims, for their call surrounds them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. It is one of the rules of the narrators, and they did not narrate it. As for Al-Bukhari, he narrated in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Hammad He is one of the imams of Islam and his origin is from the hadith of Al-Zuhri, other than the hadith of Salih ibn Kaysan, as it was narrated by Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar from Authentic aspects, on the authority of Al-Zuhri.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 294 - According to their condition"
"295","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Abu Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Ya’la, Abu Khaythamah told us, they said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, and Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin told me Abdullah Al-Jawhari, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ya’la told us, Yahya told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid al-Tanafisi told us, and Ahmed bin Khalid told us Al-Wahbi, they said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Muzaffar Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Harun told us, Sulayman bin Omar told us, Yahya told us Ibn Saeed Al-Umayyad, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, and Abu Amr Muhammad Ibn Ahmad Ibn Ishaq Al-Adl told me, Muhammad Ibn Khuzaym told us Al-Dimashqi, Hisham bin Ammar narrated to me, he said: Sa’id bin Yahya Al-Lakhmi narrated to me, Ibn Ishaq narrated to me, and Ali bin Issa narrated to me, and the pronunciation for him, narrated to me. Musaddad bin Qatan, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up in fear of Mina, and said: “May God protect a servant who heard my statement, so he understood it and then led it to Whoever does not hear it, then perhaps he is carrying jurisprudence for whom he has no jurisprudence, and perhaps he is carrying jurisprudence to one who is more understanding than him. There are three that the heart of a believer should not neglect: Sincere work is for God, sincere advice is for those in authority, and adherence to the community, for their call will be behind them.” These trustworthy people agreed to narrate this hadith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Abdullah bin Numayr alone disagreed with them, He said: On the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Salam, who is Ibn Abi al-Janoub, on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Ibn Numayr is trustworthy, and God knows best, then We looked at it and found Al-Zuhri following it, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr.”"
"296","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, we told him My father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Amr ibn Abi Amr, the client of al-Muttalib, narrated to me on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Huwayrith, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr. Ibn Mut'im, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying while he was in fear of Mina: “May God have mercy on the servant who heard my statement. So he understood it and then delivered it to the one who did not hear it. Perhaps there are three people carrying jurisprudence who do not have it, and perhaps there are three people who carry jurisprudence to someone who has more understanding than him. The heart of the believer is dear to them: sincerity in work, advising those in authority, and adherence to the community, for their call is from behind them and faithful The chapter is on the authority of a group of companions, including Omar, Othman, Ali, Abdullah bin Masoud, Muadh bin Jabal, Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas. And Abu Hurairah, and Anas, may God be pleased with them, and a number of others.” And the hadith of Al-Numan bin Bashir is according to the condition of authenticity.”"
"297","I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub more than once, saying: Ibrahim bin Bakr Al-Maruzi told us, in Bayt al-Maqdis, Abdullah bin Bakr told us Al-Sahmi, narrated to us Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, and he said: “May God bring light to the face of the person who heard my article and carried it. Perhaps he will carry jurisprudence other than a jurist, and perhaps he will carry jurisprudence to someone who is more knowledgeable than him.” The heart of a believer is dear to them: sincerity in work for God Almighty, advising those in charge, and adhering to the community of Muslims. In the authentic Musnad, Muslim cited the hadith of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that he said: I saw our Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. One day he said hello, filling his stomach with dung. On the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Nu’man, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to straighten our ranks, hadith. “Hatim bin Abi Saghira and Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi agreed to expel them.” It was narrated, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 297 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"298","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Nahwi told us, in Baghdad, al-Qasim bin al-Mughirah al-Jawhari told us, and Ahmad bin Sahl told us Al-Faqih, in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, they said: Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, On the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that he said: “He welcomed the will of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And peace be upon him, he advises us of you.” “This is an authentic and proven hadith due to the agreement of the two sheikhs on using Saeed bin Sulaiman, Abbad bin Al-Awwam and Al-Jariri as evidence, then Muslim protested.” With the hadith of Abu Nadhrah, I have enumerated eleven originals for it in the authentic musnad by al-Jariri, and they did not reproduce this hadith, which is the first hadith in The merit of the students of hadith, and no defect is known to it. This hadith has hadith narrations collected by the scholars of hadith, on the authority of Abu Harun Al-Abdi, on the authority of Abu Saeed, And Abu Harun is among those who remained silent about him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 298 - According to Muslim’s condition and there is no reason for it"
"299","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no man who takes a path seeking knowledge, except that May God make the path to Paradise easy for him, and whoever’s deeds are slowed down by him, his lineage will not be quickened by him.” Abu Muawiyah followed him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 299 - According to their condition
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Numayr:"
"300","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, and the wording is his, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever follows a path in search of knowledge, God will make it easy for him.” A path to Paradise.” “This is a hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and the wording that he attributed is redundant and someone else left it off. As for seeking knowledge, there is no difference. According to Al-Amash in his chain of transmission."
"301","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakra Bakkar bin Qutaybah bin Bakkar Al-Qadi, in Egypt, told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Ishaq bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, said: I was with Ibn Abbas and a man came to him and I died to him with a uterus a long way away. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Know your lineages and maintain your ties of kinship, for there is no closeness to a kinship if it is severed, even if it is near, nor far away.” It is hers when she arrives, even if she is far away.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and neither of them narrated it. Ishaq bin Saeed is the son of Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas. Al-Bukhari used most of his narrations on the authority of his father as evidence, and for this hadith there is a witness and a similar narration in the evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 301 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"302","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Yusuf bin Salman told us, Hatim bin Hatim told us. Ismail, Abu Al-Asbat Al-Harithi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Learn your lineages and maintain your ties of kinship.” Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya, saying: The father of the tribes Al-Harithi is Bishr bin Rafi’"
"303","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told us, Musa told us Bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad, they said: Abu Hudhayfah told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aqeel, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of His father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, which country is evil? He said: “I don’t know.” When Gabriel came to him, he said: “O Gabriel, which country is evil?” He said: I do not know until I ask my Lord. So Gabriel departed and stayed as long as God wished for him to stay, then he came and said: O Muhammad, you asked me what... Is the country evil? And I said, “I do not know,” and I asked my Lord, “Which country is evil?” He said, “Its markets.” “All of them cited the narrators of this hadith as evidence except Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, and Al-Bukhari was the only one who cited Abu Hudhayfah as evidence. This hadith is the basis of what the scholar said: I do not know, and he has a witness, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 303 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"304","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Hasan Al-Jabri told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim bin Abdullah bin Masoud Al-Sulami, Abdan bin Uthman, and Saad bin Yazid Al-Farra’ told us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Amr bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Oh Messenger of God, which country is evil? He said: “I don’t know.” Then when Gabriel came to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: O Gabriel, which country is evil? He said: I do not know until I ask my Lord. So Gabriel set off and stayed as long as God wished for him to stay, then he came and said: O Muhammad, you asked me which country it is. Evil? And I said: I do not know, and I asked my Lord which country is evil? He said: “Its markets.” “This Amr bin Thabit is the son of Abi Al-Miqdam Al-Kufi, and it is not according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Rather, I mentioned him as a witness, and the narration of Abdullah Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated it until he urged me to take it out, for I had suffered from it in a way that was not reliable.”"
"305","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Numan told us, Amr bin Thabit told us, so he mentioned it in a similar way. “And Abd al-Samad bin al-Nu’man is not a condition of this book.” There is another witness to this hadith from the hadith of Ibn Umar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 304 - Amr is Ibn Abi Al-Miqdam. It was narrated on his authority by Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Nu’man, but he is weak."
"306","Abu Hafs Omar bin Muhammad al-Tajibi told us, in Mecca, in the house of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ishaq bin Ismail told us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger By God, which place is best? He said: “I don’t know.” Then he said: Which places are evil? He said: “I do not know.” He said: “Ask your Lord.” He said: When Gabriel descended, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was asked which place is best and which Is the place evil? So I said: I do not know. Then Gabriel said: I do not know until I ask my Lord. He said: Then Gabriel rose up violently, almost being struck by shock. Among them is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then God said: O Gabriel, Muhammad asks you which place is best? So you said: I do not know, so he asked you which places are the worst, and you said: I do not know, and the best places are the mosques, and the worst places are the markets.”"
"307","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abu Abdullah bin Yaqoub, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Sufyan told us, and Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Omar told me, Ahmed told us Ibn Salamah, Abd al-Rahman Ibn Bishr told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The people are about to strike the livers of camels, but they will not find a scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of Medina.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and Ibn Uyaynah might have made it a narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 307 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"308","As Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jarrahhi told us, in Marw, Abdan bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Hafiz told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Alaa and Muhammad bin Maimun said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, a narration, he said: “People are about to strike the livers of camels.” The hadith. “This is not something that weakens the hadith, for Al-Humaydi is the arbiter of his hadith due to his knowledge of it and his frequent acquaintance with it, and he was Ibn Uyaynah, he says: We see this scholar as Malik ibn Anas."
"309","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abu Sakhr, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever comes to this mosque of ours will learn or teach something good.” He is like a person who strives in the cause of God, and whoever does anything other than this is like a man who sees something that he likes but does not have it. Perhaps he said: He sees the people praying but does not have it. “From them, and he sees those who remember but are not from them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 309 - Haywa followed it on the authority of Abu Sakhr, and it is according to their conditions, and I do not know of any reason for it."
"310","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us, Abu Yahya Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Ahmed bin Zakaria bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Yazid al-Muqri, followed by Haywa ibn Shuraih, Abu Sakhr told me that Sa`id al-Maqbari told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever enters this mosque of ours to learn or teach goodness is like a mujahid in the path of God. And whoever enters it other than that is like looking at what does not belong to him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They used all of its narrators as evidence, then they did not narrate it. I do not know of any reason for it. Rather, it has a third witness to it. He conditioned them all.”"
"311","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, On the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning only wants to learn good things.” Or he teaches it, he has the reward of a complete Hajj pilgrim, so whoever goes to the mosque with no intention of doing anything except to learn something good or teach it, he will have the reward of a complete Hajj. The argument. “Al-Bukhari cited Thawr ibn Yazid as evidence in the principles, and Muslim narrated it in the evidence. As for Thawr ibn Yazid al-Dili, he is in agreement. ""on him""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 311 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"312","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, in the Musnad of Anas, Yahya bin Mansour Al-Harawi narrated to us, Ahmad bin Nasr Al-Muqri Al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jawhari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told me, Surayj bin Al-Numan, Abu Awanah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “An exhausted person who is not satisfied: an exhausted person in Knowledge is not satiated, and one who is exhausted in this world is not satisfied.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and I did not find any defect for it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 312 - According to their condition, and I did not find a reason for it"
"313","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Khams bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: Abu Hurairah came to Ka’b asking about him while Ka’b was among the people, and Ka’b said: “What? What do you want from him? He said: As for me, I do not know anyone among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who has a better memory of his hadith than me. Ka’b said: “As for you, you did not You will find someone who seeks something but is not satisfied with it for a day, unless he seeks knowledge and seeks this world.” Then he said: “You are a Ka’b, for I am an example.” Here I come. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and the companion’s saying: ‘I have a better memory of the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than anyone else.’ It is included in its Musnads.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 313 - There is a break"
"314","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid Al-Qatwani told us, Hamza bin Habib told us Al-Zayat, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The virtue of Knowledge is more beloved to me than the virtue of worship, and the best of your religion is piety.”"
"315","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq al-Sarraj told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Khalid told us Ibn Mukhlid, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of al-Amash, on the authority of Musaab ibn Saad, so he mentioned it similarly. He did not mention the ruling. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. This arbiter, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan, is trustworthy, and he established the chain of transmission. His father was Bakr bin Bakkar."
"316","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin Mandah Al-Asbahani told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us Sa’dan and Ahmad bin Abdul-Wahid said: Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Hamza al-Zayat told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Musaab bin Saad, On the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something similar. “Then we looked and found Khaled bin Mukhlid more steadfast, more memorized, and more trustworthy than Bakr bin Bakkar, so we awarded him more.” It was narrated by Abdullah bin Abdul-Quddus, on the authority of Al-Amash with another chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 314 - according to their condition"
"317","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told us, Abbad bin Yaqoub told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Quddus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The virtue of knowledge is better than the virtue of worship, and the best of your religion Piety"
"318","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, and he told me Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani, my grandfather told us, Ibn Abi Uwais told us, my father told me, on the authority of Thawr bin Zayd Al-Dili, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and said: “Satan has despaired of being worshiped in your land.” But he was satisfied to be obeyed in anything other than that of the deeds you despise, so beware, O people, for I have left something among you as soon as you hold fast. With it, you will never go astray. The Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, every Muslim is a Muslim brother. Muslims are brothers, and it is not permissible for anyone to Of his brother’s wealth, except what he gave him willingly. And do not be unjust, and do not return to disbelief after me, some of you striking the necks of one another.” “Al-Bukhari cited the hadiths of Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim cited Abu Uwais as evidence, and all of his narrators are agreed upon, and this hadith is a sermon. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, agreed to narrate it in the Sahih: “O people, I have left among you what you will never go astray after him if you hold fast to it.” The Book of God, and you are responsible for me, so what do you say? The mention of adhering to the Sunnah in this sermon is strange and in need of it. I found evidence for it from the hadith of Abu Hurairah
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 318 - Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim cited Abu Uwais Abdullah as evidence, and his origin is in the Sahih."
"319","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti informed us, Dawud bin Amr Al-Dhabi told us, Salih bin Musa told us Al-Talhi, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ “Indeed, I have left among you two things after which you will never go astray: the Book of God and my Sunnah, and they will not be separated until they return to me at the Fountain.”"
"320","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Daoud Suleiman bin Daoud, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: There were brothers during the era of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them would come to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the other would practice the profession. Then the professional complained to his brother to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Perhaps you You will be provided with it.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and its narrations on the authority of the last of them are proven and trustworthy, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 320 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"321","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Darabardi informed us of Marw, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Qadi informed us, Abu Muammar informed us, Abd informed us. Al-Warith, on the authority of Al-Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, that Muawiyah came out of the bath of Homs and said to his servant: Bring me my clothes. He put them on, then he went in. He entered the Homs Mosque and prayed two rak'ahs. When he finished, he saw people sitting. He said to them: Why are you sitting? They said: We prayed the obligatory prayer, then the storyteller narrated it. When he finished, we sat down and remembered the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Muawiyah said: There is no A man who met the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spoke less about him than I did. Indeed, I will tell you about two characteristics that I preserved from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: There is no man who is in charge of people and has other men standing at his head. He would like to have many adversaries and enter Paradise. He said: I was with One day the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the mosque and saw some people in the mosque sitting. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What makes you sit?” They said: We prayed the prescribed prayer, then we sat studying the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “When God mentions something, His remembrance increases.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Abdullah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami heard more than one hadith from Muawiya.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 321 - according to their condition"
"322","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, dictating in the month of Ramadan in the year three hundred and seventy-three, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Isfahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, said: “When the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down, their conversation - meaning jurisprudence - would take place unless a man recited.” Surah or command a man to recite a surah. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it and it has a reliable witness on the authority of Abu Sa’id.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 322 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"323","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: “Remember the hadith, for remembering the hadith stimulates the hadith.” “It was narrated in the hadith, based on the hadith, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib and Abdullah bin Masoud, with authentic hadiths according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.”
 As for the hadith of Ali"
"324","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, he reported in a whisper, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Buraidah said: Ali, may God Almighty be pleased with him, said: “Remember the hadith, for unless you do it, it will be studied.”
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud"
"325","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Yahya Al-Hammani told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: “Remember the hadith, for the remembrance of the hadith is his life.”"
"326","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, said: “All the hadith we heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Our companions used to talk to us, and we were busy. In taking care of camels. “This is a hadith with chain of transmission on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Subaie’i, and it is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it has no defect, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 326 - True"
"327","Abu Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ishaq bin Issa Al-Tabbaa told us, Fudayl bin Ayyad, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “You listen, and it is heard from you, and it is heard from those of you who listen.” Jarir bin Abdul Hamid informed him, on the authority of Al-A’mash
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 327 - according to their condition and there is no reason for it"
"328","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, Musa bin Harun told us, and Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Naim told us, they said: Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You hear and he hears from you and he hears from those who hear from you.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it has no defect, and they did not narrate it.” On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud and Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “In the hadith of Thabit bin Qays also mentioned the third layer.”"
"329","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Asim told us, Thawr bin Yazid told us, Khaled bin Maadan told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Amr Al-Sulami, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer for us, then he came upon us, so He preached to us a sermon from which hearts were shaken and eyes shed tears, so we said: O Messenger of God, as if it were a farewell sermon. So he commanded us. He said: “I command you to fear God, listen, and obey. And if an Ethiopian slave is appointed over you, whoever of you lives will see... There is a lot of difference, so you should adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Rightly Guided Caliphs, the Mahdi, bite upon it with your molars, and beware of newly-invented matters, for all A misguided heresy.” “This is an authentic hadith with no defect. Al-Bukhari cited as evidence Abd al-Rahman bin Amr and Thawr bin Yazid, and this hadith was narrated in The first book of holding fast to the Sunnah, which I have, is that they, may God have mercy on them, thought that it had no narrator on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan other than Thawr Ibn Yazid, and Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Al-Harith narrated his hadith in the two Sahihs, on the authority of Khaled Ibn Ma’dan.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 329 - It is authentic and has no defect"
"330","Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Hanthali told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, from Banu Sulaym, from the people of Suffah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to us one day, and he stood up and advised the people, comforted them, and warned them. He said what God wished for him to say, then he said: “Worship God and do not associate anything with Him, and obey those to whom God has entrusted you with command, and do not dispute the matter with those in charge of it.” Even if he were a black slave, you must adhere to what you know of the Sunnah of your Prophet and the rightly-guided caliphs, and bite your teeth with the truth.” “This is an authentic chain of narration according to all of their conditions, and I do not know of any defect in it. Damra bin Habib followed Khalid bin Ma’dan on the narration of this. The hadith on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Sulami.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 330 - According to their condition, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"331","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mal told us, Al-Fadl told us Ibn Muhammad, they said: Abu Salih told us, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Salih, and Abu Bakr Ahmad Ibn Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah Ibn Muhammad told us Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Amr Al-Sulami said that he heard Al-Irbad bin Sariyah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, preached to us a sermon from which I fell asleep. eyes, and hearts were frightened by it, so we said: O Messenger of God, this is a farewell admonition, so if you pledge to us, he said: “I have left you on Its nights are as white as its days. No one will deviate from it after me except one who perishes. And whoever of you lives will see much difference. So you have to do with what you have learned of. My Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Rightly Guided Caliphs after me, and you must obey me, even if it is an Abyssinian slave, then bite it with your mohawks.” Asad bin Wada’ah Yazid said in this hadith: “The believer is like a camel whose nose is not restrained.” Abdul Rahman bin Amr continued his narration, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariya, three trustworthy and proven imams of the people of the Levant.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 331 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 Among them is Hajr ibn Hajr al-Kala’i."
"332","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, Musa bin Ayyub al-Nasabi told us, Safwan bin Salih al-Dimashqi told me: Al-Walid bin Muslim al-Dimashqi told us, Thawr bin Yazid told me, Khalid bin Maadan told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Amr Al-Sulami and Hujr bin Hajr Al-Kala’i said: We brought Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, and he was one of those about whom the They came to you to carry them. You said, “I cannot find anything to carry you.” They turned away, with their eyes overflowing with tears, saddened that they would not find anything to spend.” [Al-Tawbah: 92] So we greeted us and said, “We have come to you as visitors and visitors.” Al-Irbad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer one morning, then he came. Upon us, he preached to us an eloquent sermon that made our eyes shed tears and our hearts feared. Someone said: O Messenger of God, as if it were a sermon. Farewell, what do you promise us? He said: “I advise you to fear God, listen, and obey, and if it is an Ethiopian slave, then whoever of you lives will see much difference, so you must My Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Rightly Guided Caliphs, the Mahdi, so adhere to it and bite upon it with your molars, and beware of newly invented matters, for all “Innovated matter is an innovation, and every innovation is an error.”
 Among them is Yahya bin Abi Al-Mutta’ Al-Qurashi."
"333","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa bin Zaid Al-Tanisi narrated to us, Amr bin Abi Salama Al-Tanisi narrated to us, Abdullah bin Al-Tanisi narrated to us. Al-Alaa bin Zubr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Al-Mutta’, who said: I heard Al-Irbad bin Sariyah Al-Sulami saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us. One morning, he gave us a sermon, from which our hearts were filled with tears, and our eyes were filled with tears. He said: So we said: O Messenger of God, you have given us your sermon. A farewell sermon, so he entrusted us. He said: “You must fear God - I think he said: and hearing and obedience - and you will see after me a severe disagreement - or A lot - So adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Mahdi Caliphs, bite on it with your mohawks, and beware of newly-invented women, for every innovation is a misguidance. Among them is Ma`bad bin Abdullah bin Hisham al-Qurashi, but the path to him is not a requirement of this book, so I left it and I have investigated it in the correction. This hadith is some investigation of what my diligence led to and was written about it, as the imam of the imams of hadith Shu’bah said in the hadith of Abdullah Ibn Ata’, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amir, when he asked him for Basra, Kufa, Medina, and Mecca, then the hadith returned to Shahr Ibn Hawshab So he left him, then Shu`bah said: Because something like this is true for me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was more beloved to me than my father, my children, and the people. All together, this hadith has been authenticated, praise be to God, and may God’s blessings and peace be upon Muhammad and his entire family.”"
"334","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Muawiyah told me Bin Salih, and Abu Al-Nasr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, and the wording is his, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, Rabi’ah bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Yazid bin Amira, that Muadh bin Jabal, When death approached him, they said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, Hosanna. He said: Sit me down, then he said: Indeed, knowledge and faith are in the world. He sought them out and found them. He said that three times, and they sought knowledge with four people: with Uwaimir Abi Al-Darda’, and with Salman. Al-Farisi, and with Abdullah bin Masoud, and with Abdullah bin Salam, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He is Ten in Paradise. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Yazid bin Amira Al-Saskiski, the companion of Muadh bin Jabal, and Makhoul Al-Dimashqi testified that Yazid Thus, from what Makhoul cites on the authority of Yazid, following Abu Idris Al-Khawlani.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 334 - according to their condition"
"335","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, he told me Al-Numan bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Makhoul, said: Muadh bin Jabal was in pain one day while Yazid bin Amira Al-Zubaidi was with him, so Yazid cried for him, so he said to him Moaz: What makes you cry? He said: It makes me cry because what I used to ask you every day has been cut off from me. So Muadh said: “Knowledge and faith are two screens, stand up and touch them.” Yazid said: And with whom should I seek them? Muadh said: “With four people: with Uwaimir Abu Darda, with Abdullah bin Masoud, with Salman Al-Farisi, and with Abdullah.” God Ibn Salam, for it was said: He will be the companion of ten people in Paradise.” Yazid said: I said: And with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and he said: “Do not ask him about “Something, for he is busy with you.” Al-Zuhri narrated part of this hadith, on the authority of Abu Idris."
"336","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Nuaym bin Hammad told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, Ibn Shihab told me, On the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, he said: Knowledge and faith are in their place, whoever seeks them will find them."
"337","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bakr told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, On the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Abla, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, that he said: Awf bin Malik said Al-Ashja’i: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, looked at the sky one day and said: “This is the time for the flag to be raised.” Then a man from the Ansar said to him: Ibn Labid said to him: O Messenger of God, how can knowledge be raised when it has been proven in the Book and hearts have humbled it? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If I consider you to be one of the most learned scholars of the people of Medina,” then he mentioned the misguidance of the Jews and Christians, as In their hands of the Book of God. He said: I met Shaddad bin Aws and told him the hadith of Awf bin Malik. He said: Awf has spoken the truth. Shall I not tell you the first? Is that raised? I said: Yes, he said: Humility until you do not see anyone humble. “This is correct, and the two sheikhs have cited all its narrators as evidence, and the witness to this is Shaddad ibn Aws, as Jubayr ibn Nufayr heard the hadith. From all of them,” and from a third of the Companions, who was Abu Al-Darda’.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 337 - Sahih, as evidenced by evidence"
"338","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari and Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked up to the sky and then said: “This is the time for knowledge to be stolen from the people so that it does not They could steal something from him.” He said: Then Ziyad bin Labid Al-Ansari said: O Messenger of God, how can he embezzle from us when we have read the Qur’an? By God We will certainly recite it, and we will certainly recite it to our women and our sons. He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ziyad. Indeed, I would have counted you among the jurists of the people of Medina. This is the Torah and the Gospel for the Jews and Christians, so what is it of no use to them? . Jubayr said: I met Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and I said to him: Don’t you listen to what your brother Abu al-Darda’ says? And I told him what he said. He said: Abu al-Darda’ spoke the truth. Dress up, if you wish. I will tell you about the first knowledge that raises humility from people. You are about to enter the community mosque and you will not see a humble man in it. “This is an authentic chain of narration from the hadith of the Basrians.” There is a fourth witness to the authenticity of the hadith, and he is Ubadah ibn al-Samit. “Perhaps he is delusional that Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated it once on the authority of Awf ibn Malik. Al-Ashja’i, and once on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, so the hadith becomes lengthy, but this is not the case, as the narrators of the two chains of narration are all trustworthy and Jubayr bin Nufayr. Al-Hadrami is one of the greatest followers of the Levant. If all the chains of narrations are authentic, then it appears that he heard it from all the Companions. The clear evidence for what I mentioned is that the hadith was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Ziyad bin Labid Al-Ansari, whose review was mentioned by the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace in the two hadiths.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 338 - Its chain of transmission is authentic"
"339","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Ibn Labid Al-Ansari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the time The disappearance of knowledge.” Shu’bah said - or he said: “The time for the disappearance of knowledge” - they said: How is it, when we have the Book of God that you teach it to our children and their children? He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, Ibn Labid. I thought you were nothing but the wisest of the people of Medina. Don’t the Jews and Christians have the Book of God in them?” The Torah and the Gospel did not benefit from it at all.” “The hadith has been proven beyond doubt by the narration of Ziyad bin Labid with such a clear chain of transmission.”"
"340","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Muawiyah told me Ibn Salih, Abd al-Wahhab Ibn Bakht told me, on the authority of Zirr Ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Assal al-Muradi, that he came to ask him about Something, he said: What can I do to you other than that? He said: I did not work for you except for that. He said: “Then give good news, for there is no man who goes out in pursuit of knowledge except that the angels extend to him “Her wings are satisfied with what he does until he returns.” “This is an authentic chain of narration, for Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bakht is one of the trustworthy and reliable people of Basra from among those whose hadith is collected, and they used it as evidence, but they did not They narrate this hadith, and the focus of this hadith is on the hadith of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Zirr, and they turned away from it completely, and it is on the authority of Zirr bin “Hubaysh has trustworthy witnesses other than Asim bin Bahdala, and among them is Al-Minhal bin Amr, and they agreed on it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 340 - Its chain of transmission is authentic"
"341","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, A’im told us, Al-Sa’q bin Hazan told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, On the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: A man from Murad came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his name is Safwan ibn While he was in the mosque, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “What brings you?” He said: Seeking knowledge. He said: “For the angels lower their wings to the seeker of knowledge, satisfied with what he does.” - And he mentioned the hadith - “This is well known. This is Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Basri, a trustworthy memorizer. Al-Bukhari relied on him in a sentence of This hadith was narrated on his authority in the Sahih, and Sinan bin Farroukh disagreed with him in this hadith, so he narrated it on the authority of Al-Saqq bin Hazan” [p. 181]."
"342","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Maamari, and Muhammad bin Suleiman told us, they said: Shaiban told us, Al-Sa'q bin Hazan, Ali bin Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zurr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: Safwan narrated Ibn Assal Al-Muradi, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. - So he mentioned the hadith -. “Abu Janab al-Kalbi narrated it, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, and Abu Janab does not cite his narration in this matter as evidence. The Book »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 341 - Shaiban disagreed with him"
"343","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Fudayl told us, Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, Abu Your Honor, Talha bin Musarrif told me that Zar bin Hubaysh came to Safwan bin Assal and said: “What brings you to me?” He said: I began to seek knowledge. He said: “No one does what you did for him except that the angels lowered their wings for him, content with what you did for him.” He makes. “And we mentioned in this hadith something that does not weaken this hadith. A group of people narrated it as a chain of narration, and a group of people discontinued it, and the one who narrated it is better. And the increase from them is acceptable.”"
"344","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr told us, dictating in Baghdad, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Hammad told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he told me Muhammad bin Thawr, told us by Ibn Jurayj, he said: Al-Amash came to Ata’ and asked him about a hadith, so he narrated it, so we said to him: “You narrated this” and he Iraqi? He said: Because I heard Abu Hurairah speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it, he will be brought with it on the Day of Resurrection.” He was bridled with a bridle of fire.” “This is a hadith that people circulated with many chains of transmission that were collected and cited, and this chain of transmission is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. I mentioned Our Sheikh, Abu Ali, has memorized this chapter. Then I asked him whether any of these chains of narrations are authentic, regarding a gift, and he said: No, I said: Why? He said: Because Ataa did not hear it from Abu Hurairah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 344 - according to their condition"
"345","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Wasiti told us, Azhar bin Marwan told us, Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed told us, Ali bin Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it, God will curb him on the Day of The Resurrection will come with a bridle of fire.” “So I told him, ‘Azhar ibn Marwan or your sheikh, ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti, made a mistake about it, and it is not unlikely that they were mistaken.’”
 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshaz narrated to us the hadith, saying: Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, Muslim bin Ibrahim narrated to us, we narrated Abdul-Warith bin Saeed, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever was asked Of knowledge that he had but concealed it, God will bridle him with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection.” “Abu Ali approved of it and confessed it to me. Then when I collected the chapter, I found a group in it who mentioned hearing a gift from Abu Hurairah, and we found The hadith, with an authentic and indisputable chain of transmission, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr.”"
"346","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abdullah told me Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever conceals knowledge, God will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.” “This is an authentic chain of narration from the hadith of the Egyptians, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it has no defect, and it is on the authority of a group of companions other than Abu Hurairah. May God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 346 - According to their condition and there is no reason for it"
"347","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: I heard Sufyan Ibn Uyaynah, narrating, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Aamir al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Qarzah ibn Ka’b, who said: We went out to seek Iraq, so Omar ibn al-Khattab walked with us to He shouted, performed ablution, and then said: “Do you know why I walked with you?” They said: Yes, we are the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. You walked with us. He said: “Indeed, you are coming to the people of a town who have a recitation of the Qur’an.” Like the sound of bees, do not reveal to them narratives lest they distract you. Strip away the Qur’an and say little about the narrations from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Go ahead, and I am your partner.” When Qarza presented it, they said: Tell us. He said: Ibn al-Khattab forbade us. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It has ways in which it can be combined. It is mentioned by Qardha bin Ka’b Al-Ansari, a companion who heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it is a condition of ours regarding the companions that we do not turn away from them. As for the rest of its narrators, they used it as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 347 - It is authentic and has methods"
"348","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told me, Ahmad bin Najdah told me, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Zar’ah, On the authority of Amer bin Saad Al-Bajli, he said: I went to see Qardha bin Ka’b, Abu Masoud, and Zayd bin Thabit, and they found my maids singing. So I said to them: Are you doing this while you are the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: “If you are listening, otherwise go ahead, for the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has given us permission to have fun at a wedding, and to cry at the death’s doorstep.”"
"349","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Sa’id bin Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Naimah, on the authority of Abu Uthman Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says against me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire, and whoever consults his brother and advises against him in a manner other than He has betrayed him, and whoever issues a fatwa that is not proven, his sin is on the one who issued it.” Followed by Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 349 - Yahya bin Ayyub continued it, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, in a similar manner. They used his narrations except for Amr, and he documented it."
"350","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Naimah, the infant of Abd al-Malik bin Marwan, who was a truthful person, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him repent.” His building is in Hell, and whoever issues a fatwa without knowledge, the sin of him is upon the one who issues it. And whoever advises his brother about a matter knows that the right path is in Someone else has betrayed him.” “This is a hadith which the two sheikhs used as evidence for its narrations other than this one, and it was authenticated by Bakr bin Amr Al-Maafiri, who is one of the imams of the people of Egypt. “Our need for a word of confirmation in the fatwa is great.”"
"351","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Sa’id bin Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Hani Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There will be At the end of time, people from my nation will tell you something that you and your fathers have not heard, so beware of you and them.” “This is a hadith that Muslim mentioned in the book’s sermon with the anecdotes, but he did not mention it in the chapters of the book, and it is authentic according to all of their conditions. “It is needed for wounding and correction, and I do not know of any reason for it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 351 - Muslim mentioned it in the sermon, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"352","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Hassan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, And Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “Being frugal in the Sunnah is better than striving in innovation.” . It was narrated by Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith."
"353","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah, the same. “This is an authentic hadith with a chain of transmission based on their condition, and they did not narrate it.” Rather, in this type, they narrated the hadith of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah: “But they are two things: guidance and speech. The best speech is the speech of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 352 - According to their condition"
"354","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, Al-Layth told us, and Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour told me Al-Adl, and Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi, they said: Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Saeed bin Abi told me Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his brother Abbad bin Abi Saeed, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make supplication and say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the four things: from knowledge that is not beneficial, a heart that is not humble, a soul that is not satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard. This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it, as they did not narrate Abbad bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, not because of any harm in it, but because of the scarcity of his narration and the lack of it. “The need for it.” It was narrated by Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and he did not mention his brother Abbad.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 354 - True"
"355","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Suleiman told us, Saeed bin Amr Al-Ash’athi told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Hamdani and Harun bin Ishaq said: Abu Khaled Suleiman bin Hibban told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray and say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the four things: knowledge that is not beneficial, and a heart that does not submit. A soul that is not satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard.” There is authentic evidence from the narration of Anas bin Malik on the condition of Muslim."
"356","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, by Muhammad bin Nu’aym, by Qutayba bin Saeed, by Khalaf bin Khalifa, on the authority of Hafs, the son of my brother Anas, on the authority of Anas said: It was one of the supplications of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “O God, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is not beneficial, a heart that is not humble, and a soul that is not satisfied. And a supplication that is not heard.” At the end of that, he says: “O God, I seek refuge in You from these four.” “It has informed me that Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj narrated it from the hadith of Zayd bin Arqam, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 356 - This is according to Muslim’s condition"
"357","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Dair told us in Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, and Abu Qutaybah Sallam bin Fadl Al-Adami told us, in Mecca, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i, Zayd bin Hubab told us, Laith bin Saad Al-Masry told us, Khaled bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Quraysh said to me: You are writing on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he is a human being who gets angry as People get angry, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, the Quraysh are saying: You are writing on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He is only a human being and gets angry just as humans get angry. He said: Then he pointed to his lips and said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, whatever comes out of Between them is the truth, so write. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, based on the abrogation of the hadith, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not narrate it, and they used all of its narrators as evidence. Except for Abd al-Wahid bin Qais, who is a sheikh from the people of the Levant, and his son Umar bin Abd al-Wahid al-Dimashqi is one of the imams of hadith. Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays narrated on the authority of a group of companions, including Abu Hurairah, Abu Umamah al-Bahili, and Wathilah ibn al-Asqa’. May God be pleased with them. Al-Awza’i narrated hadiths from him. “And for this hadith there is a witness. They agreed to quote it for the sake of brevity.” On the authority of Hammam ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said: None of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has more hadith than me except Abdullah. Ibn Amr, because he used to write and I did not write. On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Wahb ibn Munabbih, on the authority of his brother Hammam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and the like. “As for Abd al-Wahid ibn Qais, and his hadith on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, I found evidence for it from the hadith of Amr ibn Shuaib.” I heard Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih, saying: I heard Al-Hasan bin Sufyan, saying: I heard Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanzali, He says: If the narrator on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib is trustworthy, then he is like Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, then as for the hadith of the witness
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 357 - True"
"358","So Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abdul Rahman told me Bin Salman, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khalid, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that Shuaib, narrated to him and Mujahid, that Abdullah bin Amr, narrated to them He said: O Messenger of God, shall I write what I hear from you? He said: “Yes.” I said, when angry and when satisfied? He said: “Yes, I should only say the truth.” So let the seeker of this knowledge know that no one has ever spoken about Amr bin Shuaib. Muslim only spoke about Shuaib hearing from Abdullah bin Amr, so if the hadith came on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul By Allah bin Amr, it is authentic, although I only mentioned it as a witness to the hadith of Abd al-Wahid bin Qais, and this particular hadith was narrated. On the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak"
"359","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Yahya bin Saeed, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, and the pronunciation is his, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahek, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: I used to write down everything I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And I wanted to memorize it, but the Quraysh forbade me and said: You write down everything you hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Is there a human being who speaks in contentment and anger? He said: So I stopped, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Write. By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing has come out of it except what is true,” and he pointed to it with his hand. “The narrators of this hadith have cited as evidence the last of them other than this Walid, and I think he is Al-Walid ibn Abi Al-Walid Al-Shami, for he is Al-Walid Ibn Abdullah, and the scribes taught his father. If that was the case, then Muslim would have used it as evidence, and the narration was authentic on the authority of Amir The believers, Omar bin Al-Khattab, said: “Restrict knowledge to the Book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 359 - If Al-Walid is the son of Abi Al-Walid Al-Shami, then he is according to Muslim’s conditions."
"360","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abd King bin Abdullah bin Abi Sufyan, that he heard Omar bin Al-Khattab say: “Restrict knowledge to the Book.” “And likewise the narration on the authority of Anas bin Malik is authentic according to his statement, and it was attributed from an untrusted source. As for the narration from his statement.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 360 - A similar statement from Anas is correct"
"361","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told us, Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Thumama, on the authority of Anas, that he used to say to his sons: “Restrict knowledge to the Book.” “It was transmitted by some Basra scholars, on the authority of Al-Ansari, and also attributed by the sheikh of the people of Mecca, not on the authority of Ibn Jurayj.”"
"362","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, and Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told me, in Bukhara, Saleh told us. Bin Muhammad bin Habib, they said: Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ma’mal told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Restrict knowledge.” I said: What is the restriction? He said: “His writing.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 362 - Ibn Al-Mu’mil is weak"
"363","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marwa, Al-Harith bin Muhammad told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Jarir bin Hazim told me, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, I said to a man from the Ansar: Come, let us ask. “The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, are many today.” He said: “And it is astonishing for you, O Ibn Abbas. Do you see that people are in need of you and in The people of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whoever was among them. He said: “So I left that and began to ask the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And if the story reaches me about the man, I go to his door and he says, so I lay my robe on his door, and he blows the dust on me and he comes out. He sees me and says: O cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what has brought you here? Will you send for me and I will come to you? So I say: “No, I have the right to come to you.” He said: Then I ask him about the hadith. Then this Ansari man lived. Until he saw me and people had gathered around me asking me questions, so he said: “This boy was wiser than me.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and it is the basis for seeking hadith and respecting the hadith narrator.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 363 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"364","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub ibn Yusuf al-Adl told us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata told me, Ibn Jurayj, Yunus bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, who said: The people dispersed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Natil, the brother of the people of the Levant, said to him: Oh Abu Hurairah, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, the first of people Three people will be judged therein on the Day of Resurrection: A man who was martyred and was brought to him and his blessings were made known to him, and he recognized them and said: What did you do in them? He said: I fought in your cause until I was martyred. He said: You lied. You only wanted so-and-so to be said to be bold. It was said, and he would be ordered to be dragged along. His face until he was thrown into the fire. And a man learned knowledge and read the Qur’an, and it was brought to him. He made known to him his blessings, and he recognized them, and said: What did you do about them? He said: I learned knowledge and read the Qur’an and applied it to you. He said: You lied. You only wanted it to be said that so-and-so is a scholar, and so-and-so is a reader. It was said, so he was commanded. With it, he was dragged on his face until he was thrown into the fire. And a man to whom God gave all kinds of wealth, and it was brought to him, and He made known to him His blessings, and he recognized them, and said: What did you do with them? He said: I never left anything that you would like me to spend on without spending on it for you. He said: You lied. You only wanted it to be said that so-and-so is generous. It was said, So he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context, and Yunus bin Yusuf is the son of Amr bin Hamas who narrated “On the authority of Malik bin Anas in Al-Muwatta’, and Malik Al-Hakam in everyone who narrated on his authority, and Muslim narrated it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 364 - according to their condition and they did not take him out in this manner"
"365","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told me, from the origin of his book, Ubaid bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Hafiz, known as Al-Ajl, informed us. Ibrahim bin Ziyad Sablan, Abbad bin Abbad told us, Yunus, who is Ibn Ubaid, told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Three will perish at the reckoning: the generous, the brave, and the knowledgeable.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to their conditions, and it is strange and anomalous, except that it is a summary of the first hadith, and there is a witness for it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 365 - On their condition, and he is strange and abnormal"
"366","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: Abu Hurairah said: “Had it not been for the punishment of God against the People of the Book, I would not have spoken to you anything.” Then he recited {And when “Allah took a covenant from those who were given the Book: ‘You will make it clear to the people and you will not conceal it.’” [Al Imran: 187] “. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and I do not know of any reason for it nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 366 - I do not know of a reason for it"
"367","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Asim bin Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of his father, He said: Abu Hurairah used to stand next to the pulpit on Fridays, throw the heels of his sandals into his arms, then grab a pomegranate. Al-Minbar, says: Abu Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Al-Sadiq said Al-Masduq, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then said in part of that: “Woe to the Arabs because of the evil that has approached.” Then he heard the movement of the compartment door as he exited. The imam sat down. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Thus, the purpose is not to authenticate the hadith ‘Woe to the Arabs from the evil that has approached’. Take it out, but its purpose is to make it desirable to narrate the hadith on the pulpit before the imam emerges.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 367 - There is a break"
"368","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman narrated, Al-Shafi’i narrated, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us. The jurist, and the pronunciation for him, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Nadr Salem, the servant of Omar bin Ubaid Allah bin Muammar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “I will never find any of you reclining on his couch.” A command comes to him from My command, from what I have commanded or forbidden, and he says: I do not know. We have followed whatever we found in the Book of God. Sufyan bin Uyaynah established this chain of narration and it is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. What I have is that they left it due to a difference of opinion. The Egyptians in this chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 368 - On their condition and abandoning it"
"369","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Malik told me, On the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I do not know a man who reclines and gets the command. “Of my affairs, of what I have commanded or forbidden.” He says: “We do not know. This is the Book of God, and this is not in it.”"
"370","He said: Al-Layth bin Saad told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he acknowledged that he said while the people were around him: “I do not know of any of you to whom something of My commands that I have commanded or forbidden comes to him while he is leaning on His couch, and he says: “Whatever we find in the Book of God, we will act upon it, otherwise no.” Al-Hakim said: “I am following the principle that I established in the sermon of this book, that an increase in trustworthiness is acceptable, and Sufyan bin Uyaynah is a memorizer.” He is trustworthy and proven, and he reported and memorized it, and we relied on his memorization after we found two witnesses to the hadith with two authentic chains of narration, as for one of them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 370 - Sufyan Hafez, proven, so we adopted it"
"371","So Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdoos informed us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, that Muawiyah bin Salih, Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed him, and Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us. My father told me, Abd al-Rahman told us, and he is the son of Mahdi, Muawiyah bin Saleh told us, Al-Hasan bin Jabir told me that he heard Al-Miqdam bin Ma’di speak of Al-Kindi, the companion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade things on the Day of Khaybar, including the domestic donkey and other things. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ It is about to be that a man among you will sit on his couch and narrate my speech and say: Between me and you is the Book of God, so whatever we find lawful in it we make lawful, and whatever we find lawful in it we make lawful. We found in it something forbidden and we forbade it, but the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only forbade it as God forbade it. “As for the second hadith”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 371 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"372","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Khalifa Al-Aquli Anbar told us, Muslim bin told us Ibrahim, Uqba bin Khaled Al-Shinni told us, Al-Hasan told us, he said: While Imran bin Husayn was speaking about the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he said He had a man: O Abu Nujaid, tell us about the Qur’an. Imran said to him: “You and your companions are reciting the Qur’an. Were you talking to me about prayer and what?” What are its limits? Did you tell me about zakat on gold, camels, cows and other types of wealth? But I witnessed and you were absent.” Then he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enjoined on us such-and-such in zakat.” And the man said: You have given me life. May God keep you alive. Al-Hasan said: That man did not die before he became one of the Muslim jurists. Uqba ibn Khalid al-Shinni is one of the trustworthy people of Basra and their worshipers, and he is a noble narrator. His hadiths are combined, but they do not reach the completion of the ten days of prayer. He prayed May God bless Muhammad and his entire family
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 372 - The obstacle to Abed’s trustworthiness"
"373","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujayr, he said: Tawus was praying two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer, and Ibn Abbas said to him: “Leave her.” He said: He only forbade them from taking a ladder to connect them. That is until sunset. Ibn Abbas said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer, and I do not know whether he will be punished for it or not.” He will be rewarded because God Almighty says: {And it is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decided a matter, that they should have the best} [Al-Ahzab: 36] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it agrees with what we mentioned earlier of urging people to follow the Sunnah, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 373 - according to their condition"
"374","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Yaqoub told me Al-Thaqafi, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Omar Al-Hudhi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, said By Ibn Masoud, by Abu Darda, and by Abu Dhar: “What is this hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I think it is their imprisonment in Medina.” until he was injured”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 374 - It was narrated by Affan and others on his authority, meaning on the authority of Shu’bah"
"375","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hassan bin Ali bin Bahr Al-Bari told us, Abdullah bin Jafar told us Al-Barmaki, Maan bin Issa told us, Malik bin Anas told us, Abdullah bin Idris told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, so he mentioned the hadith with a chain of transmission similar to it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and the denial of the age of the Commander of the Faithful to the Companions is due to the large number of narrations, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. There is a Sunnah in it, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 375 - according to their condition"
"376","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, that “one day he narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he trembled and trembled.” His clothes,” then he said: “Or something like this.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and there is evidence in it, on the authority of Abdullah.”"
"377","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Ali bin Hakim told us, Sharik told us, and Ali bin Abdullah Al-Halimi, Al-Abbas Al-Dawri told us, Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli told us, Sharik told us, so he mentioned something similar to it. “This is a hadith that is based on the principles of prevention, based on the abundance of narration and the encouragement of mastery in it. They agreed on the authority of Israel on the authority of Abu Husayn, and he protested. Muslim by Sharik bin Abdullah, and he is to be used as evidence, but they did not narrate it and he has another witness to their condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 376 - according to their condition"
"378","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, Ibn Aoun, Muslim bin Abi Imran told me, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, he said: I was not mistaken - and Ibn Aoun I rarely made a mistake - on the eve of a Thursday, I went to Ibn Masoud, but I did not hear him say anything. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Until that evening, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I looked at him and saw that his shirt was unbuttoned and swollen. His jugular, sunken eyes.” Then he said: like this, or above that, or close to that, or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said."
"379","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told me, that Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abu Shihab told us, and Abu Shihab told us Al-Qasim Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Susi told us, Abu Ali Muhammad bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Abu Shihab told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Awdhi told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, Abu Shihab told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Ka’b bin Malik, He said: I heard Abu Qatada saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying while he was on the pulpit: “Beware of talking too much about me. So whoever says about me should only say the truth, and whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.” In the hadith of Muhammad bin Ubaid, Ibn Ka’b and others told me, on the authority of Abu Qatada. “This is a hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, and it contains very difficult words, and they did not narrate it. There is evidence for it with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abu Qatada.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 379 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"380","It was narrated to me by Ali bin Hamshadh, Musa bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Musa told us, Attab bin Muhammad bin Shudhab told us, Ka’b bin Abdul Rahman told us. Ibn Ka'b Ibn Malik, on the authority of his father, said: I said to Abu Qatada: Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I am afraid That my tongue slips by something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not say. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Beware of too much… Speaking about me, whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"
"381","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ali bin Ja’far Al-Madaini told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Enough with a man.” It is a sin for him to narrate everything he heard.” “Muslim mentioned this hadith among the stories that he mentioned in the sermon of the book on the authority of Muhammad bin Rafi’, and he did not narrate it as proof. He is trustworthy in his place in the book, and Ali bin Ja`far al-Madani is trustworthy, and he warned us at the beginning of the book to use more trustworthy people as evidence. A group of people from Shu'bah sent him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 381 - Muslim mentioned it in an authentic sermon"
"382","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi informed us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub, Hafs bin Omar told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “It is enough sin for a man to narrate everything he hears.”"
"383","Abu Amr Ismail bin Nujaid bin Ahmad bin Yusuf Al-Sulami, may God have mercy on him, told me. Muhammad bin Ayyub informed us. Muhammad bin Sinan informed me. Al-Awqiqi, Ibn Al-Mubarak reported, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abbas recited {and no one knows its interpretation except Allah and those who are firmly rooted in knowledge} [Al Imran: 7] Then he said: “We used to memorize hadith, and hadith was memorized from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until you rode “Difficult and humiliating.” “This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and there is another witness like it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 383 - according to their condition"
"384","Abu Ali Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Ali bin Al-Muthanna told us, Harun bin Marouf told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “We were speaking on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if he did not lie to him, so when The people rode through hardship and humiliation. We abandoned talking about him, and may God’s prayers and peace be upon Muhammad and his family.”"
"385","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, that Yahya bin Maymun al-Hadrami told him on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ghafiqi, who said: The last thing that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrusted us with. That he said: “Adhere to the Book of God, and you will return to a people who love to talk about me - or a word similar to it - so whoever has memorized something, let him tell it.” And whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in Hell.” “The narrators of this hadith on their authority can be used as evidence. As for Abu Musa Malik ibn Ubadah al-Ghafiqi, he was a companion who lived in Egypt, and this The hadith is among the things we narrated on the authority of the companion, if the path to it is correct, although the meekness of al-Juhani also narrated on the authority of Malik ibn Ubadah. Al-Ghafiqi, and this hadith combined two strange words: one of them was his statement: “You will return to a people who love to talk about me.” The other: “Whoever memorizes something, let him narrate it.” A group of the imams of Islam have held that a hadith narrator has no right to narrate something that is not He preserved it, and they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 385 - Its narrators are cited as evidence, and Abu Musa Malik bin Ubadah is a companion of"
"386","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, and the pronunciation is his, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim told us Ibn Musa, Al-Walid Ibn Muslim told me, Abd al-Rahman Ibn Zayd Ibn Jabir told me, Busr Ibn Ubayd Allah al-Hadrami told me, Abu Idris Al-Khawlani said that he heard Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman say: People were asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about goodness, and I was I ask him about evil for fear that it will overtake me, so I said: O Messenger of God, we were in times of ignorance and evil, so God brought this goodness. Is this good from evil? He said: “Yes, and there is smoke in it.” I said: What is its smoke? He said: “A people who follow guidance other than my guidance. Some of them are recognized and denied.” I said: And will there be good after that evil? He said: “Yes, preachers at the gates of Hell, whoever responds to them, they will throw him into it. I said: O Messenger of God, describe them to us. He said: They are of our kind and speak with our tongues. I said: What do you command me to do if I realize that? He said: “Adhere to the group of Muslims and to their imam.” I said: What if they do not have an imam or a group? He said: “Then withdraw from all those groups, even if you bite the root of a tree until death overtakes you while you are like that.” This hadith was narrated in The two Sahih books are like this, and they also included it briefly from the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani. I only included it in the Book of Knowledge because I did not find a hadith from the two sheikhs indicating that consensus is an argument other than this, and I have excluded in these places from the hadiths of this chapter unless They bring it out, the first hadith of which “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 386 - They brought it out"
"387","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Ibrahim bin Hilal Al-Buzanjardi told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Ahmad, the jurist Al-Bukhari, told us, in Nishapur, then Abu Al-Mawjih, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sufi told us, in Mecca, Al-Hasan bin Ali told us. Al-Maamari, Al-Hasan bin Issa told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told me, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail told me the reader and the pronunciation. To him, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak reported, Muhammad bin Suqa reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, On the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar addressed us with the tax collector, and he said: I stand among you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood among us, and he said: “I advise you My companions, then those next to them, then those next to them, then the lie is spread until a man swears and is not called to swear, and he bears witness but is not cited. So whoever among you wants the joy of Paradise, let him stick to the group, for Satan is with one and he is farther away from the two. Will they not be alone? A man with a woman, unless the third of them is Satan - he said it three - and you must join together, for Satan is with one and he is of the two. Farther away. Indeed, whoever is pleased with his good deeds and displeased by his evil deeds, he is a believer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. I do not know of any disagreement among the companions of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak regarding the establishment of this chain of narration. On his authority, and they did not narrate it, and he has two witnesses, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa. The like of them may be cited in such places, as for the first witness. [P. 198]."
"388","So Abu Ahmad Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Hashimi told us in Kufa, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Balawi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Marri told us, Al-Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, gave a speech With the tax collector, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us and took my place among you, and he said: “Treat my companions well,” so he mentioned the hadith in a similar way. “As for the second witness”"
"389","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Sinan Al-Wasiti told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us. Al-Dawraqi and Ahmad bin Mani’ said: Al-Nadr bin Ismail Al-Bajli narrated to us, Muhammad bin Suqa narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: Omar addressed us with the tax collector, and he said: I stand among you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood among us, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar way. “As for the disagreement in this hadith on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, it is summed up in part for me, and what I have is that the two imams narrate this. The hadith is from that disagreement between the imams over Abd al-Malik regarding it, and these chains of narrations cannot be explained by these chains of narrations emerging from them.” We narrated it with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with them both.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 387 - according to their condition"
"390","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Abu Sa’id Abd al-Rahman bin Ahmad told me. The muezzin, Ahmed bin Zaid bin Harun Al-Qazzaz told us, in Mecca, they said: Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Ibrahim bin Muhajir told me. Ibn Mismar, on the authority of Amer Ibn Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab stood at the tax office and said: May God have mercy on the man who heard He understood my article. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing among us as I stand among you. Then he said: “Guard me among my companions, then those after them. Then those who follow them - three - then the commotion will increase, and lying will appear, and a man will bear witness but will not be martyred, and he will swear and will not be called to swear, from Whoever of you loves the joy of Paradise, then he must go to the group, for Satan is with one, and he is farther away from the two. Should they not be alone with a man? With a woman, Satan is the third of them. Whoever is pleased with her good deeds and whose evil deeds displeases him is a believer.” “The second hadith, regarding what scholars have used as evidence that consensus is proof, is a hadith in which there is disagreement from Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman in seven ways: So the first aspect of it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 390 - This is correct"
"391","What """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 391 - If Khalid had memorized it, we would have ruled it authentic. Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Asam told us, in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us. Khaled bin Yazid Al-Qarni, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “God will never unite this nation to go astray,” and he said: “The hand of God is upon the group, so follow the greatest mass, for he is the one who “An anomaly, an anomaly, in the Fire.” “Khaled bin Yazid Al-Qarni, this is an old sheikh of the Baghdadis. If this hadith had been preserved, we would have ruled it authentic. The second disagreement about it is based on The pilgrim"
"392","What Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman told us, Abu Sufyan Al-Madini told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not gather This nation is forever misguided, and the hand of God is upon the community, so whoever deviates will be in the Fire.” “The third dispute is over the one who performs Umrah."
"393","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim did not tell us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, Al-Mu’tamir told me, Suleiman Al-Madani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will not unite my nation in misguidance.” Never. “The fourth disagreement is over the one who performs Umrah regarding"
"394","What Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Amri told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darhami told me, Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman told me, on the authority of Sufyan, or Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will not unite my nation Never go astray, and the hand of God is upon the group like this - and He raised His hands - for whoever strays will go into Hellfire.” “Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq said: I do not know this Sufyan and Abu Sufyan, and the fifth dispute is over the one who performs Umrah.”"
"395","What Abu Al-Hussein Abdul-Samad bin Ali bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Khalid bin Abdul Rahman told us, Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He does not combine “By God, this nation - or he said, my nation - will never go astray, and they follow the Great Sawad, for whoever strays will be in Hell.” Omar bin Jafar Al-Basri told us: Thus in the book of Abu Al-Hussein, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Al-Dhayal. Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah said: “If this had been preserved from the narrator, it would have been a condition of authenticity. The sixth disagreement is over the one who performs Umrah regarding it.”"
"396","What Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Sahl bin Ahmad bin Othman Al-Wasiti told us, from his book, Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Sufyan bin Sufyan Al-Madani said: On the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will never unite my nation in error, and God’s hand will be upon the group like this, so follow the black people.” The greatest, for whoever strays will be in Hell.” “The seventh disagreement over the one performing Umrah is"
"397","What Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Bazzar told us, Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, Sulaiman Abu Abdullah Al-Madani told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “God will never unite my nation - or he said the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him - in error, and God’s hand is upon the group.” And he said with his hand outstretched: “Indeed, whoever strays will go into Hell.” Al-Hakim said: “There has been a dispute regarding the attribution of this hadith from Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman, and it is one of the pillars of the hadith in seven aspects. We are not able to judge that all of them are presumed to be wrong based on what is correct, according to what he said on the authority of Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Suleiman bin Sufyan. Al-Madani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, and when we say this, we attribute the narrator to ignorance and thus we distort the hadith, but we We say: Al-Mu`tamar bin Sulaiman is one of the imams of hadith, and this hadith was narrated from him with chains of transmission like which the hadith is authentic, so it is necessary to That it has an origin in one of these chains of transmission, then we found evidence for the hadith other than the hadith of al-Mu’tamir, whose authenticity I do not claim nor make any judgments about. Rather, I have to mention it due to the consensus of the Sunnis on this rule of Islam, so whoever narrated this from him Hadith from the companions Abdullah bin Abbas”"
"398","Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, dictating and reading, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Khalid told us, Salama bin Shabib told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibrahim bin Maimun reported, Abdullah bin Tawus informed me, that he heard his father, narrating that he heard Ibn Abbas, narrating, that the Prophet prayed God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “God will never unite my nation - or he said this nation - in misguidance, and God’s hand is upon the group.”"
"399","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibrahim told us Ibn Maymun Al-Adni, who was called the Quraysh of Yemen, and he was one of the diligent worshippers. He said: I said to Abu Ja`far: By God, Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will never unite my nation upon misguidance. May God bless the community.” Al-Hakim said: “This Ibrahim bin Maymun al-Adni was modified by Abd al-Razzaq and praised by him, and Abd al-Razzaq is the imam of the people of Yemen. And modifying it is proof.” This hadith was narrated on the authority of Anas bin Malik
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 399 - Ibrahim, edited by Abd al-Razzaq and authenticated by Ibn Ma’in"
"400","It was narrated to us by Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl, Muhammad ibn Issa ibn al-Sakan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Mubarak Abu Suhaim narrated to us, Mawla Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib, Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he asked his Lord four things: “He asked He asked his Lord that he would not die of hunger, so that was granted. He asked his Lord that they would not unite in error, so that was granted. He asked his Lord that they would not apostatize. disbelievers, so that was given to him, and he asked his Lord not to be defeated by an enemy of theirs, so he would not There will be grief among them, but that was not granted.” “As for Mubarak bin Suhaim, he is one of those who do not follow such a book, but I mentioned him out of necessity. The third hadith on the scholars’ argument that consensus is proof"
"401","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Khalid bin Wahban, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever separates from the group by even a span has stripped off the bond of Islam from his hands.” His neck"
"402","Jarir bin Abdul Hamid Al-Dhabi followed him, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Khalid bin Wahban, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever disagrees with the group of Muslims by even a hand, has taken off the collar of Islam from his neck.” “Khalid bin Wahban was not criticized in his narrations, and he is a well-known Tabi’i, but the two sheikhs did not narrate it.” This text was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, with an authentic chain of transmission, according to their condition.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 402 - Khaled did not weaken"
"403","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abu Salih told us, Al-Layth told me, Yahya bin Saeed told me, he said: Khaled bin Abi Imran wrote to me, saying: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever leaves the group by even a hand span has taken off the collar of Islam from his neck until he returns to it.” And he said: “Whoever dies and does not He is the imam of a group, so his death was a death of ignorance.” “The fourth hadith indicates that the consensus of scholars is proof”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 403 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"404","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi, in Egypt, told us, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “I command you to do five words that God has commanded me with: congregation, hearing, obedience, migration, and jihad in the path of God. He left the group within a span of a hand, having removed the veil of Islam from his head unless he returns.” Thus, it was narrated in full length by Muawiyah bin Salam and Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir. As for the hadith of Muawiyah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 404 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"405","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, that Hafs bin Omar Al-Amri told them, saying: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, and Zaid bin Salam told me that he heard Abu Salam say: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has commanded me to do five things that I should do with them.” - He mentioned the hadith in its length - “As for the hadith of Aban bin Yazid, on the authority of Yahya bin I refuse a lot."
"406","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Tamim bin Muhammad told us, Hadba bin Khalid told us, Aban bin Yazid told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Zaid, He told him that Abu Salam told him that Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God commanded Yahya ibn “Zechariah gave me five things to do with them, and he commanded the Children of Israel to do them.” - So he mentioned the hadith - and said in it: “Indeed, God commands me to do five.” So he mentioned it at length - “This is an authentic hadith according to what we established in the Companions, since we did not find for them except one narrator, then Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari A well-known companion, I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Mu’in, saying: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari He has companions, and this word in the hadith has a witness, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 406 - They did not narrate it because Al-Harith excluded Abu Salam from it"
"407","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Abdullah bin Ghannam bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, my father told me, Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Muawiyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever separates from the group by a span will enter Hell.” . “The fifth hadith indicates that consensus is proof”"
"408","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Darabardi told us about Marw, Ahmad ibn Issa al-Muzani told us, Al-Uqabi told us, and Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq Al-Faqih, and the pronunciation for him, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Al-Uqabi told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever leaves a nation, or returns to being an Arab after his migration, has no proof.” “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Ziyad bin Riyah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever separates from the community and dies dies a pre-Islamic death,” and this text is different from that. The sixth hadith indicates that consensus is proof.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 408 - They agreed to bring out Abu Hurairah in a case like this"
"409","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman Al-Qari told us, Kathir bin Abu Kathir Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, who said: I came to Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman on the nights when people were marching to Uthman, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “Whoever separates from the group and disdains the leadership will meet God and will have no proof.” Abu Asim followed him for a long time.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 409 - True"
"410","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, Abu Asim told us, Kathir bin Abi Kathir told us, he told me Rab’i bin Harash, he came to Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman with a cold, and his sister was under Hudhayfah: O Rab’i, what have your people done? That was the time when people went out to Othman. He said: Some of them had gone out. He said: Some of them came to me. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: “Whoever separates from the group and disdains the leadership will meet God and will have no argument before God.” “This is an authentic hadith, for Kathir ibn Abi Kathir was a Kufi who lived in Basra.” Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan and Issa bin Yunus narrated on his authority, but he was not mentioned with a trace. “The seventh hadith indicates that consensus is proof”"
"411","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Fakihi informed us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Zakaria bin Abu Masarra, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa told us, Abu Hani told me that Abu Ali Al-Janabi Amr bin Malik told him, On the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “There are three about whom you will not be asked: A man who left the group and disobeyed.” His imam and he died as a disobedient, and a female slave or male slave who escaped from his master and died, and a woman whose husband was absent from her and he had sufficed her with the necessities of this world, so she displayed herself as a beauty. After him, do not ask about them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They used all of its narrators as evidence and did not narrate it, and I do not know of any reason for it. The eighth hadith states that consensus is proof.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 411 - According to their condition, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"412","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab informed us, about Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The prescribed prayer refers to the prescribed prayer.” What is written after it is atonement for what was between them, and Friday to Friday, and month to month - meaning from the month of Ramadan to the next month. Ramadan is an expiation for what came between them.” Then he said after that: “Except for three.” So I knew that that was something that had happened, so he said: “Except for associating others with others.” By God and he broke the deal and abandoned the Sunnah.” I said: O Messenger of God: As for associating partners with God, we know it, so why did he break the deal and abandon the Sunnah? He said: “As for breaking the deal: to pledge allegiance to a man with your oath, then turn to him and meet him with your sword, and as for abandoning the Sunnah: it is to depart from “The group.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib bin Abi Al-Sa’ib Al-Ansari as evidence, and I do not know of any reason for it. The ninth hadith states that consensus is proof.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 412 - According to Muslim’s condition, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"413","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, he said: Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Dawud bin Amr Al-Dhabi told us, they said: Nafi’ bin Omar Al-Jumahi told us, Umayyah bin Safwan told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Zuhair Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of His father, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, through prophecy or prophecy, saying: “You will soon recognize the people of Paradise from the people of Hell” or He said: “The best of you are among the worst of you.” It was said: O Messenger of God, with what? He said: “With good praise and bad praise, you are witnesses to one another. “Some.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and Al-Bukhari said: Abu Zuhair Al-Thaqafi heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his name is Muadh. As for Abu Bakr bin Abu Zuhair is one of the major followers, and the chain of transmission of the hadith is authentic, but they did not narrate it. We have mentioned nine hadiths with authentic chains of transmission that support the argument by consensus, and I investigated them in order to investigate the doctrines of the Imams. “The predecessors, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 413 - Sahih Chapter: Concerning reverence for the scholar “These are authentic reports regarding the command to respect the scholar when gathering with him and sitting before him Of what they did not produce”"
"414","Abu Al-Hasan Maymun bin Ishaq Al-Hashimi told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attardi told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Azib, he said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to a funeral. A man from the Ansar. So we ended up at the grave, and when he was gone, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down and we sat around him as if he were on our heads. “The bird” - and he mentioned the hadith - the authenticity of this hadith has been proven in the Book of Faith, and they did not narrate it."
"415","Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Khatib informed us about Marw, Ibrahim ibn Hilal al-Buzanjardi informed us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq, Al-Hussein bin Waqid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, who said: “When we sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we did not We raise our heads to Him in reverence for Him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not remember any defect for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 415 - According to their condition, and I do not remember a defect for it"
"416","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar, Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Zaidi told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hassan Al-Qadi told us, Bhamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Amr Muhammad bin Ja’far told me and the pronunciation for him, we told him Yahya bin Muhammad, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, he heard Usama bin Sharik say: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions were with him as if they had birds on their heads. So I saluted and sat down, and then Bedouins came and asked him about things until they said: He sought treatment, he said: “Take treatment, for God Almighty has not created a disease without creating a cure for it.” So they asked him about some things, and he said: “Servants of God, there has been a cure for it.” Haram, not if someone borrows from someone unjustly, that is distress and ruin. They said: O Messenger of God, what is the best thing that has been given to people? He said: “Good manners.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it. The reason for it according to Muslim is that Usama bin Sharik did not narrate from him except Ziyad, and he narrated on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar on his authority is that I have based this book of mine on the narration of the Companions, even though they had only one narrator, and there are ways of transmitting this hadith. Our way is to publish it, by the will of God Almighty, in the Book of Medicine.”"
"417","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Attab Al-Abdi told me in Baghdad. Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Yazid Al-Rammahi, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amer, Salih bin Rustum narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Qart, he said: I entered The mosque, and behold, there was a group as if their heads had been cut off, and then behold, a man was speaking to them, and behold, it was Hudhayfah. He said: The people were asking the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about good, and I used to ask him about evil “- and he mentioned the hadith in its length -.” The text of this hadith was included in the two books, but I included it in this place in order to listen to the hadith narrator and how to respect him. They did not mention this word in the two books.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 416 - True"
"418","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Al-Hakam bin Atiya told us, On the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, none of us raised his head except Abu Bakr and Omar. They used to smile at him and he smiled at them.” “This is a hadith that was unique to Sheikh Al-Hakam bin Attiya and is not a requirement of this book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 418 - This is unique to the ruling and is not a condition of this book"
"419","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Sayyar bin Hatim told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, said: Salman was in a group remembering God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by them and came to them intending to Until he approached them and they stopped speaking out of respect for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “What were you saying? For I saw mercy descending upon you, and I wanted to share it with you.” “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it, and they used Ja’far bin Sulaiman as evidence. As for Abu Salamah Sayyar bin Hatim Al-Zahid, he is a worshiper. His era, and Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated extensively about him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 419 - True"
"420","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Amash told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us. My father, Al-A’mash told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Jarudi told us, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, And Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Today a man asked me about something and I don’t know what to say to him. He said: Have you seen? A polite, energetic man keen on jihad, he says: Are our leaders planning against us things that we cannot count? He said: So I said: “By God, I do not know what to tell you except that we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so perhaps he would not command anything without So we did it, and he is nothing like the dust of this world except like a hole whose purity has been drunk and its dirt remains, and none of you will remain well as long as he fears it. God Almighty, and when something troubles him, he comes to a man and asks him and he heals him. By God, it is almost certain that you will not find him.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and I think it is because there is a pause in it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 420 - According to their condition"
"421","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Malik bin Khair al-Ziyadi, on the authority of Abu Qateel, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is not among us who does not honor our elders. He has mercy on our little ones, and knows our world.” “Malik bin Khair al-Zayyadi is a trustworthy Egyptian, and Abu Qabil is a great Tabi’i.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 421 - Malik is a trustworthy Egyptian"
"422","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Ali bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: {Obey God and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [An-Nisa: 59] He said: “Those who are endowed with jurisprudence and goodness.” “This is an authentic hadith with a witness, and the companion’s interpretation is supported by a chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 422 - This is true and there is evidence"
"423","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salama al-Anbari told me, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {Obey God and obey the Messenger and those in charge among you} [An-Nisa: 59] meaning: “The people of jurisprudence and religion, and people who are obedient to God who teach people the principles of their religion and enjoin upon them what is right and forbid them from what is evil, So God obligated their obedience.” “These are hadiths that speak of the humility required of scholars towards those they teach.”"
"424","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari informed us about what happened, Abu Al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid reported, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, that Hafsa said to Omar: Don’t you wear a softer garment than Your clothes, and you eat better food than this food of yours, and God has opened the matter for you and expanded your provision? So he said: “I will dispute with you within yourself. Then he mentioned the matter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the hardship he was facing because of the hardship of life. He continued to remember until she cried, and he said: “I have said “I will share with them their difficult life, so that I may be able to live with them in their comfortable life.” “This is an authentic hadith according to their condition, as Mus’ab bin Saad used to visit the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was one of the great followers of Children of the Companions, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 424 - There is a break"
"425","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, and Ahmad bin Salman told us Al-Faqih, he said: It was read to Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad, who is the son of Abdullah al-Raqqashi. Ubayy narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The generosity of a believer is his religion, his chivalry is his mind, and his character is sufficient for him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it and he has a witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 425 - Rather, Muslim, meaning Muslim bin Khaled Al-Zanji, is weak and has a witness"
"426","Abu Saeed Ismail bin Ahmad told us, Muhammad bin Hussein bin Mukarram told us, in Basra, Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The believer’s generosity is due to his religion. His chivalry is his mind, and his character is sufficient for him.”"
"427","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Abu Sa`id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You do not help people with your money.” “And may they be satisfied with your kindness and good manners.” Narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 427 - I said Abdullah means Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Maqbari and wah"
"428","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Dagholi told us, Muhammad bin Mishkan told us, Yazid bin Abi Hakim told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who narrated it, saying: “You do not help people with your money.” “And may they be satisfied with your kindness and good manners.” “This is an authentic hadith, its meaning is close to the first, except that they did not narrate it, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed.”"
"429","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Samaan bin Bahr Al-Askari Abu Ali told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us Al-Ammi, my father told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Kindness to people Its owner protects against evil, pests, and destruction, and the people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter. I heard Abu Ali al-Hafiz say: I did not write this hadith except on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Saffar, and Muhammad bin Ishaq and his son from We did not know the Basraeen, and he said, “The people of good deeds in this world.” It was narrated in more than one direction, on the authority of Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Al-Munkadir bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir. “And the one who is afflicted, even if they do not bring it out, it will be mentioned in the evidence.”"
"430","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Amr bin Muhammad al-Naqid told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told me Abd al-Rahman al-Taffawi, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in the Almighty’s saying {Take pardon} [Al-A’raf: 199] He said: “He commanded God told His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to show pardon in people’s morals.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and he used Al-Taffawi as evidence and did not narrate it, and it was said about it on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 430 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"431","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr said: “God did not reveal this verse except regarding the morals of people {Take pardon} [Al-A’raf: 199] and He commanded custom.” And turn away from the ignorant.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was said about this on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, but it is not according to his conditions.”"
"432","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad informed us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, he informed us Muammar, on the authority of Bahz ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imprisoned a man from his people under an accusation, so a man from He led his people to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was delivering the sermon, and he said: O Muhammad, why are you imprisoning my neighbor? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was silent and said: Some people say that you forbid evil and consider it permissible. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What do you say?” So I began to speak between them for fear that he would understand it and make a supplication against my people after which they would not succeed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued. He greeted until he understood it, then he said: “They said?” Or was the one who said it among them? By God, if I had done so, it would have been the same as they were. They would have left their neighbors.” The statement was presented in the Sahih of Bahz ibn Hakim, “He is of no use.” Repeating it on the grounds that the evidence for this hadith is mentioned in the two Sahih books. Among them is the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah: The Messenger swore God, may God bless him and grant him peace, an oath, and a man from the Ansar said: This is an oath that was not intended for the sake of God, and from it is the hadith of Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas: I was walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was wearing a thick Najran garment. So a Bedouin pulled out his cloak - the hadith - and among them is the hadith of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Anas in the story of Hunayn, “Don’t bother me.” To this tree. “And other than that which would be too long to mention.”"
"433","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Omar bin Rashid, servant of Abdul Rahman, told us Bin Aban bin Othman Al-Taymi, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Dhib Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Three of those who were among it, God took him into His care, and covered them with His mercy. And bring him into His love. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “He who, when he is given, is grateful, and when he is able, he is forgiven, and when he becomes angry, he withdraws.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Omar bin Rashid is a sheikh from the people of Hijaz, from the region of Medina. The greatest hadith scholars narrated from him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 433 - Indeed, it is false"
"434","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Sahl Bishr bin Sahl told us, Abu Salih Abdullah bin Saleh told me, he told me Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala al-Aslami, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: When Omar bin al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, took office On his authority, he addressed the people on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he thanked God and praised him, then he said: “O people, I have learned from you. You make me feel harsh and harsh with me, and that is because I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was his servant and servant, and it was as he said. God {to the believers is Compassionate and Merciful} so I was before Him like a drawn sword unless He sheathed me or forbade me from a matter, so I would desist; otherwise “I came to people to a soft place.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and Abu Salih Al-Bukhari cited it as evidence. As for Saeed’s hearing on the authority of Omar, there is disagreement about it, and more Our imams said that he heard from him, and this is a well-known translation in the Musnads.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 434 - Munkar Hadith"
"435","Abu Hamid Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Shuaib Al-Faqih told us, Sahl bin Ammar told us, Muhadhar bin Al-Muwari told us, Saad bin Saeed Al-Ansari told us, On the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Al-Muttalib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever is easy-going and gentle Soon God will burn him with fire.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 435 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"436","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Fakihi informed us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abu Abdul Rahman told us Al-Muqri, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever gives a fatwa to people without knowledge, his sin will be on the one who gave him a fatwa.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and I do not know of any reason for it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 436 - According to their condition, and I do not know of any reason for it"
"437","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, On the authority of Ata’ ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not write anything about me except the Qur’an from whomever wrote it.” He narrated anything from me except the Qur’an, so let him erase it.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. The reports of Abdullah bin Amr regarding his permission to write have been presented.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 437 - According to their condition"
"438","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Salim al-Maflooj told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Abi Ishaq told us, On the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “Not all of us heard the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We had an estate and jobs, but people did not lie.” On that day, the absent witness will speak.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and Muhammad bin Salem and his son Abdullah are taken as evidence. As for the Sahih of Ibrahim Bin Yusuf bin Abi Ishaq. Al-Bukhari included it in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 438 - According to their condition"
"439","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Buraidah, He said: Ibn Abbas was, “If he was asked about something and it was in the Book of God, he would say it, but if it was not in the Book of God and it was from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he said something about it that he said about it, and if it was not on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something about him that he said about what Abu Bakr and Omar said about it, then if not Abu Bakr and Omar had something to say about him and he expressed his opinion.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it contains a pause, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 439 - According to their condition"
"440","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Idris Al-Awdi, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he reported the hadith to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “It is not appropriate to lie in any way.” And there is no jest, nor for a man to promise his son and then not fulfill him. Indeed, truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise, and lying He guides to immorality, and indeed immorality leads to the Fire. Indeed, it is said of the truthful person: He is truthful and righteous, and it is said of the liar: He lied and is immoral, and indeed the man Let him tell the truth until he is recorded with God as truthful, or lie until he is recorded with God as a liar.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. Rather, narrations have been repeated that support most of these words, so if its chain of transmission is authentic. “It is valid according to their condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 440 - According to their condition"
"441","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, and Wahb bin Baqiyya Al-Wasitian told us, They said: Khaled bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews split into one or seventy-two sects, and the Christians split into one or seventy-two sects, and my nation will split With seventy-three sects.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and it has evidence, including:”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 441 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"442","What Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abu Al-Mawjih Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl told us Ibn Musa, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr, Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews dispersed over Seventy-one sects, and the Christians are like that, and my nation is divided into seventy-three sects.”"
"443","Among them is what Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani narrated to us, Abu Al-Yaman Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ Al-Bahrani narrated to us, Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Azhar bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abi Amer Abdullah bin Luhay, he said: We performed Hajj with Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, when we came to Mecca, he was informed of a storyteller who was telling stories to the people of Mecca, a servant of Banu Farukh, so Muawiyah sent to him and said: You were ordered to do this. Stories? He said: No. He said: What prompted you to cut the story without permission? He said: We are creating knowledge that God Almighty has taught us. So Muawiyah said: If I had come forward To you, I would have cut off a group of you. Then he stood up when he prayed the noon prayer in Mecca and said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the People of the Book have become divided in their religion.” over seventy-two sects, and this nation will divide into seventy-three, all of them in Hell except one, which is the community, and he will emerge from my nation. There are people with whom these desires trade, just as a dog trades with its owner. Not a vein or joint remains of it without entering it. By God, oh “O Arabs, if you do not follow what Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought, then it is better that you do not follow it.” “These are the chains of narration upon which the argument is established in authenticating this hadith. This hadith was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas and Amr Ibn Awf Al-Muzani with two chains of narration, one of which is unique to Abdul Rahman bin Ziyad Al-Afriqi, and the other is Kathir bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, and no The argument is established by them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 443 - These are chains of narration upon which the argument is based, as for the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr"
"444","So Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Thabit bin Muhammad Al-Abid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They will come to My nation has never brought upon the Children of Israel an example like the example of a sandal for a sandal. Even if there were among them someone who had intercourse with his mother openly, the same would be in my nation. Indeed, the Children of Israel divided into seventy-one sects, and my nation will divide into seventy-three sects, all of which will be in Hell except one sect.” So he was told: What is one? He said: “This is what I and my companions are today.” As for the hadith of Amr bin Awf Al-Muzani"
"445","So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, and Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, they said: Ismail bin Abu Uwais, Kathir bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Awf bin Zaid told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: We were sitting around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in his mosque, and he said: “You will follow the ways of those before you, like a sandal with a sandal, and you will take the same as they did, if only by a span.” Then a span, or a cubit by a cubit, or a full by a cubit, even if they entered a lizard’s den, you would enter into it. Indeed, the children of Israel separated to go to Moses on Seventy-one sects, all of them astray except one sect: Islam and their group, and they divided over Jesus, son of Mary, over one of them. And seventy-two sects, all of them astray except one sect, Islam and their group. Then they will be divided into seventy-two sects, all of them All are astray except one group: Islam and their group.” Another [p. 220] The Book of Knowledge The Book of Purity"
"446","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation in Dhul-Hijjah in the year three hundred and ninety-three. Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, he said: It was read to Abdullah bin Wahb. Malik bin Anas told you, Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Adl told us about Marw, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Isa Al-Qadi told us, Al-Qa’nabi told us about what was read to Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdullah al-Sanabihi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the servant performs ablution So he rinsed his mouth, the sins came out of his mouth. If he rinsed his mouth, the sins came out of his nose. Then, when he washed his face, the sins came out of his mouth. His face, until they come out from under the fingernails of his eyes, so when he washes his hands, the sins come out from his hands until the sins come out from under the fingernails. His hands, so when he wipes his head, sins come out from his head until they come out from his ears. So when he washes his feet, sins come out from his ears. His feet until they come out from under his toenails, then his walking to the mosque and his prayers are voluntary.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it and there is no defect in it. Rather, they narrated some of this text from the hadith of Hamran, on the authority of Othman and Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, not entirely, and Abdullah al-Sanabihi, a famous companion and Malik al-Hakam in the hadith of al-Madani. I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: Ata bin Yasar narrated on the authority of Abdullah Al-Sanabihi, also called: Abu Abdullah, Al-Sanabihi, the companion of Abu Bakr Abdul Rahman bin Usayla, and Al-Sanabihi, the companion of Qais bin Abu Hazim is called: Al-Sanabih ibn Al-Aasar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 446 - No (meaning incorrect)"
"447","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, and Abu Amr Muhammad bin Kathir told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin told us Ja`far al-Quta’i, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be steadfast and you will not be counted, and know that the best of your religion is prayer, and it does not neglect Ablution except a believer. . »"
"448","Al-Shaybani in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Qadi Al-Zuhri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, Al-Amash told us, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Omar told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Thawban, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Be steadfast and you will not be defeated, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and no one will maintain ablution except a believer.” Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir continued Al-A’mash in this narration on the authority of Salem"
"449","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayoub, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu al-Fadl bin Ibrahim told us, Ja`far bin Muhammad told us Bin Al-Hussein, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki’ reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be steadfast and you will not be counted, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and no one performs ablution except a believer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and I do not know of any reason for it that could explain the like of this hadith, except an illusion on the part of my father.” Bilal Al-Ash’ari and they were talking about Abu Muawiyah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 449 - According to their condition and there is no cause for it except the illusion of Abu Bilal Al-Ash’ari"
"450","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hussein bin Yasar Al-Hannat told us, in Baghdad, Abu Bilal Al-Ash’ari told us, Muhammad bin Khazim, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be steadfast and you will not be counted, and know that there is good Your deeds are prayer, and none will perform ablution regularly except a believer.”"
"451","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Abu Thabit Muhammad bin Ubaidullah told us, Abdullah told us Al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak’ahs in which he did not forget, his previous sins will be forgiven.” ""His sin"""
"452","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Abu Thabit told us, Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, He reminded him of something similar. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and I do not remember a weak reason for it, and they did not narrate it. Muhammad ibn Aban misled Zayd ibn Aslam in The chain of transmission of this hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 452 - According to Muslim’s conditions and there is no cause that weakens him. Tell us. . ."
"453","Ibn Salih, Muhammad bin Aban told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings be upon him: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then prays two rak’ahs in which he did not forget, his previous sins will be forgiven.” “This is an illusion on the part of Muhammad ibn Aban, and it is a weak hadith that cannot be used as evidence, and Muslim used Hisham ibn Saad as evidence.”"
"454","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Madani told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, On the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, the client of Suleiman bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, that Abu Ubaid, he said to him: Narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, more than once, and not Two or three times. He says: “When the believing servant performs ablution, rinses his mouth and rinses his mouth, the sins come out from the corners of his mouth. If he washes his hands Sins are scattered from his fingernails, so if he wipes his head, sins are scattered from the ends of his head. If he stands and prays two rak’ahs, he will accept In them, with his heart and his eyes turned to God Almighty, he freed himself from his sins just as his mother had given birth to him.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to their conditions, and they did not narrate it, and Abu Ubaid is an old Tabi’i and it is not denied that he heard it from Amr ibn Absa.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 454 - According to their condition"
"455","Abu Muhammad Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khawas told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, and the word for it is: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Hadba bin Khalid told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, he said: Sharhabeel bin Hasanah said: Who is the man who can tell us about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So Amr said. Ibn Absa: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not once or twice, until he counted five times, saying: “If a Muslim offers his ablution So he washed his palms, his sins came out from between his fingers and the tips of his fingertips. So when he washed his face, his sins came out from between his fingers and the tips of his fingertips. his beard, and when he wipes his head, his sins come out from the tips of his hair, and when he washes his feet, his sins come out from the soles of his feet.”"
"456","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Al-Harith bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Dhabab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult times, walking one’s feet to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer washes away sins completely.” . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 456 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"457","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, saying: Abu Amr Al-Dareer told us, Hassan bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The key to prayer is ablution. Its prohibition is takbeer, and its permissibility is submission. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and the evidence for it is many on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Nadra, as he narrated it Abu Hanifa, Hamza al-Zayat, Abu Malik al-Nakhai and others, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, and the most famous chain of transmission in it is the hadith of Abdullah bin Muhammad Ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of Ali, and the two sheikhs turned away from the hadith of Ibn Aqeel at all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 457 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"458","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Abu Usama told us, and Abdullah bin Musa told me, Ismail told us Ibn Qutayba, Abu Bakr, and Uthman, the sons of Abu Shaybah, told us, they said: Abu Usama told us, and Abu al-Walid al-Faqih told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shirawih, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd God bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water found in desert land and the accompanying water. wild animals and animals, and he said: “If the water is two small amounts, nothing will make it impure.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They all used all of its narrators as evidence and did not narrate it, and I suspect that they, and God knows best, did not narrate it.” Because of a dispute over Abu Usama over Al-Walid ibn Kathir.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 458 - On their condition and leaving it to dispute"
"459","As Da’laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, in Baghdad, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us Abu Usama told us, and Ali bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein told us Bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, and Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, they said: Muhammad bin Uthman bin Karama told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jaafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water. And the animals and wild animals that accompany it. He said: “If the water is two ounces, it will not carry impurity.” “And thus it was narrated by Al-Shafi’i in Al-Mabsut, on the authority of Al-Thiqah, and he is Abu Usama without a doubt about it.”"
"460","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told me, and Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Abu Ja’far told us Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salama al-Faqih, in Egypt, Ismail bin Yahya al-Muzani told us, they said: Al-Shafi’i told us, and Al-Rabi’ said: Al-Shafi’i told us, Al-Thiqah reported, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jaafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the water is two ounces, it does not contain any impurity - or he said: impurity - «.” This is a disagreement that does not weaken this hadith, as the two sheikhs all cited Al-Walid ibn Kathir and Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jaafar as evidence, but they linked it to Abu Usama to Muhammad ibn Ja`far, then he narrated to him once about this and once about that, and the evidence for it.”"
"461","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Ali Al-Isfaraini did not tell me about the origin of his book, and I asked him. Ali bin Abdullah bin Mubashir told us Al-Wasiti, Shuaib bin Ayyub told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr, and Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water and what comes with it. Animals and wild animals. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the water is two ounces, it will not carry impurity.” “The authenticity of the hadith has been authenticated and proven with this narration, and it appears that Abu Osama narrated the hadith, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of all of them, Shuaib bin Ayyub al-Sarifini is trustworthy and reliable, and so is the path to him. Al-Walid bin Kathir followed his narration on the authority of Muhammad bin Jafar bin Al-Zubair Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yasar Al-Qurashi»"
"462","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalid Al-Homsi told us, Ahmad bin Khalid Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Khalid told us Ishaq, and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marwa, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father Ibn Omar, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was greeted and asked about the water found in desert land and the animals and wildebeest that accompany it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the water is As much as two times, he does not carry any malice.” This is how it was narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, Zaida bin Qudamah, Hammad bin Salamah, Ibrahim bin Saad, and Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak. Yazid bin Zuray’, Sa’id bin Zaid, brother of Hammad bin Zaid, Abu Muawiyah, and Abdah bin Sulaiman. It was narrated by Abdullah, on the authority of Ubaid. Allah bin Abdullah. “And I worship God all with the authenticity of what I mentioned.”"
"463","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, And Hadba bin Khaled, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Al-Mundhir bin Al-Zubair, who said: I entered with Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin He was told an orchard in which there was a place of water in which was the skin of a dead camel, so he performed ablution from it. I said: Would you perform ablution from it while there was the skin of a dead camel in it? So he told me on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If water reaches two or three gulps, nothing will defile it.” This is what he told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Sufyan, and it was narrated by Affan bin Muslim, and other scholars, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, but they did not mention it. Or three"
"464","Da'laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, Bayan told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir, Iyad told me, he said: I asked Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri and said: One of us prays and does not know how many he has prayed. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If one of you prays and does not know how many times he has prayed, let him prostrate twice while sitting, and when Satan comes to one of you and says: You “You have told something, so let him say, ‘You lie,’ unless he feels a scent in his nose or hears a sound with his ear.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. This Iyad is Ibn Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, and they all cited him as evidence. They did not narrate this hadith due to a disagreement about it from Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, as he did not memorize it, so he said: On the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hilal bin Ayadh or Iyadh bin Hilal, and this is not explained by consensus. Yahya bin Abi Kathir believed that this The chain of transmission from him, and the continuation of Harb Ibn Shaddad in it. It was also narrated by Hisham bin Abi Abdullah Al-Dastawa’i, Ali bin Al-Mubarak, Muammar bin Rashid and others, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi A lot. As for the hadith of Hisham
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 464 - On their condition and they left it due to the disagreement of Aban Al-Attar on the authority of Yahya, as he did not memorize it."
"465","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ayyad, that he asked Abu Sa`id al-Khudri and he mentioned something similar. As for the hadith of Ali bin Al-Mubarak."
"466","So Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hamdoun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Salamah bin Junada told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Mubarak, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad, he mentioned something similar. As for the hadith of Muammar"
"467","So Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar informed us, about Yahya, on the authority of Iyad, mentioned something similar. Al-Bukhari and Muslim agreed to present various hadiths in the two authentic musnads that prove that touching is less than intercourse, including The hadith of Abu Hurairah, “The fornication of the hand is touching,” the hadith of Ibn Abbas, “Perhaps you have touched it,” and the hadith of Ibn Masoud, “Establish prayer at two ends of the day.” There remain authentic hadiths about them in interpretation and other matters.”"
"468","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani and Abu Abd al-Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Tajir did not narrate to us. They said: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah, Al-Uqabi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “There was not a day or less.” There was a day when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go around all of us, kissing and touching what was below the level. When he came to the one that was... That day it was established by her.”"
"469","Among them is what Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad bin Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, in His Almighty saying {or have you touched women} [An-Nisa: 43] He said: “It is something short of intercourse and includes ablution.”"
"470","Among them is what Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “The qiblah is from touch, so perform ablution from it.”"
"471","Among them is what Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me: Muhammad bin Ayyub informed me, Ibrahim bin Musa, and Yahya bin Al-Mughirah informed me, They said: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, that he was sitting with the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, what do you say about a man who has sex with a woman who is not permissible for him? So he did not leave anything. . . “Perform ablution well, then stand up and pray.” He said: And God Almighty revealed the verse “Establish prayer at both ends of the day and at the end of the night” [Hud: 114] the verse, He said: He said: “Is it for me in particular or for Muslims in general?” He said: “Rather, for believers in general.” “These hadiths, which I mentioned, are that the two sheikhs agreed However, they are mentioned in the two books with differences, and all of them are valid and indicate that it is the touching that necessitates ablution but not intercourse.”"
"472","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us Aamim, and Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz narrated to me, and the pronunciation of it, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz told us, Khalaf bin Hisham narrated to us, they said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, that Urwa was with Marwan bin Al-Hakam and was asked about touching the penis, but he did not see anything wrong with it. He said: Urwah: Busra bint Safwan told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you leads to mentioning him, then do not He prays until he performs ablution.” So Marwan sent guards to Busra, and the messenger returned and said: Yes. Hisham said: My father used to say: “If he touches his penis, females, or private parts, he should not pray until he performs ablution.” “This is how Hammad ibn Zaid narrated this hadith, in which he mentioned hearing Urwa from Busra. Ibn Hisham was succeeded by a trustworthy man, and he is one of the imams of The readers, and what indicates the authenticity of the narration of the majority of Hisham bin Urwa’s companions, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Busra, among them Ayoub bin Abi Tamimah Al-Sakhtiyani, Qays bin Saad Al-Makki, Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Uyaynah, Abd Al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim, and Yahya bin Saeed, Hammad bin Salamah, Muammar bin Rashid, and Hisham bin Hassan,And Abdullah bin Muhammad Abu Alqamah, Asim bin Hilal Al-Barqi, Yahya bin Tha’labah Al-Mazni, and Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jumahi, Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Hinai, Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar, Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Taffawi, and Abdul-Hamid bin Jafar Al-Ansari. . . ., Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, Yazid ibn Sinan al-Jazari, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Al-Aziz, Haritha bin Harama Al-Fuqaimi, Abu Muammar, Abbad bin Suhaib and others. A group disagreed with them about it, and they narrated it on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Busra, among them was Sufyan bin Saeed. Al-Thawri, and a narration on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, and a narration on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, Malik bin Anas, Wahb bin Khalid, and Salam bin Abi Mutee, Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami, Abdullah bin Idris, Ali bin Mushar, Abu Usama and others. It was mentioned that there was a dispute over Hisham ibn Urwa among his companions, so we looked and saw the people who confirmed that Urwa had heard from Busra. greater,Some of them are better preserved than those who transmitted it on the authority of Marwan, except that a group of imams who memorized it also mentioned Marwan regarding it, including Malik ibn Anas, Al-Thawri, and their counterparts. A group of those who did not consider this disagreement thought that the report was weak because the imams of hadith refuted the hadith. Marwan, so we looked and found a group of trustworthy and memorizers who narrated this on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Busra, Then they mentioned in their narrations that Urwa, he said: Then after that I met Busra, and she told me the hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. As Marwan told me about it, this indicates the authenticity of the hadith and its confirmation according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and the disagreement and doubts were removed from it, and it was proven Hearing Urwah from Busra: Among the ones we mentioned about hearing Urwah from Busra was Shuaib bin Ishaq al-Dimashqi."
"473","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Bushanji told us, Al-Hakam bin Musa told us, Shuaib told us Ibn Ishaq, Hisham Ibn Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, that Marwan told him, on the authority of Busra bint Safwan, who had accompanied the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever touches his private parts, let him perform ablution.” Urwah said: So I asked Busra and she confirmed what he said, and among them was Rabi’ah bin Uthman al-Taymi."
"474","Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us about others, they said: Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ibn Abi told us Fudaik, Rabi’ah bin Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Busra bint Safwan, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution.” Urwah said, “I asked Busra and she believed him.” Among them was Al-Mundhir bin Abdullah Al-Hazzami Al-Madini."
"475","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told me, Muhammad bin Asbagh bin Al-Faraj told us, Abi told us, Al-Mundhir bin told us Abdullah Al-Hazami, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Busra bint Safwan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution.” Urwa denied it, so he asked Busra, and she believed him. Among them was Anbasa bin Abdul-Wahid al-Qurashi."
"476","Abu Muhammad Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khawas told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Suleiman al-Hadrami told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban, Anbasa bin Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Busra, that she said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever touches his private parts should not pray until he performs ablution.” He said: So I brought Busra and she told me just as Marwan told me about her. She said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying that, and among them was Abu Al-Aswad, Humaid bin Al-Aswad Al-Basri, Al-Thiqah Al-Ma’mun."
"477","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, he said: I heard Ali bin Al-Madini, He mentioned the hadith of Shuaib bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, in which he mentions hearing Urwa from Busra, and Ali said: This is what guides you. Although Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan had memorized it, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Busra bint Safwan, and he She accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you touches his penis, he should not pray until he performs ablution.” . “Urwah denied that, so he asked Busra, and she believed him. . . Hazm Al-Ansari, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Zuhri, Abu Al-Zinad Abdullah bin Dhakwan Al-Qurashi, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Urwa, Abu Al-Aswad Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Nawfal Al-Qurashi, Abdul-Hamid bin Jaafar Al-Ansari, and Al-Hasan bin Muslim Bin Yannaq, and other followers and followers. As for Busra bint Safwan, she is one of the ladies of Quraysh."
"478","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Abdul Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib Al-Nasa’i told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami, Mansour bin Salamah Al-Khuza’i told us, he said: Malik bin Anas said to us: “Do you know who Busra bint Safwan is?” She is the grandmother of Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan and his mother’s mother, so know her.” [p. 233]"
"479","Muhammad ibn Yusuf the muezzin told us, Muhammad ibn Imran al-Nasawi told us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr told us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri told us, he said: Busra bint Safwan bin Nawfal bin Asad is one of the women who sold allegiances, and Waraqah bin Nawfal is her paternal uncle. Safwan bin Nawfal has no descendants except from Before Busra, who is the wife of Muawiyah bin Mughirah bin Abi Al-Aas, “This hadith was narrated on the authority of a group of companions and followers, on the authority of Among them were Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them, Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Amra The daughter of Abd al-Rahman al-Ansariyya, Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaika, Marwan ibn al-Hakam, and Suleiman ibn Musa. We narrated on the authority of Busra. Bint Safwan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, there are five hadiths other than this hadith, and it has been proven from what we have mentioned that Busra Bint was famous. Safwan, and the name of ignorance was lifted from her with these narrations. “We have narrated the obligation of ablution after touching the penis on the authority of a group of companions. And the female companions, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among them are: Abdullah bin Omar, Abu Hurairah, Zayd bin Khaled Al-Juhani, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas and Jabir bin Abdullah. . Umm Habiba, Umm Salamah and Arwa. . .
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 479 - Sahih hadith. . My father told me, Nafi’ bin Abi Nu’aym told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever touches his private parts, let him perform ablution.” This is an authentic hadith. It was witnessed by the famous hadith: on the authority of Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Ubayy. Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. The narration was authenticated on the authority of Aisha bint Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, that she said: “When a woman touches her private parts, she performs ablution.”"
"480","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad Al-Farwi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub informed Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman, Al-Shafi’i informed, Al-Qasim bin Abdullah informed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubaid. Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “If a woman touches her private parts with her hand, she must perform ablution.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 480 - True"
"481","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us from the origin of his book, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria told us. Al-Asbahani, on the authority of Mahrez bin Salamah Al-Madani, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “If a woman touches her private parts, she performs ablution.” “This is a debate that took place between the imams of the Huffaz scholars on this subject.”"
"482","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah Al-Adl Al-Hafiz narrated to us, with Marwa, Abdullah bin Yahya Al-Qadi Al-Sarkhasi narrated to us, Raja’ narrated to us. Ibn Murjah Al-Hafiz said: “We gathered in the Al-Khaif Mosque, I, Ahmad Ibn Hanbal, Ali Ibn Al-Madini, and Yahya Ibn Ma’in, and they debated over the matter.” He touched the penis, and Yahya bin Mu’in said: He should perform ablution with it. Ali bin Al-Madini said according to the view of the Kufans and imitated their opinion, and Yahya protested. Ibn Mu'in, based on the hadith of Busra bint Safwan, and Ali ibn al-Madini used as evidence the hadith of Qays ibn Talq, on the authority of his father, and he said to Yahya ibn Mu'in: How? The chain of transmission of Busra and Marwan is similar, but a policeman was sent until he returned her answer to him. Yahya said: Then that did not convince Urwa until he came. Busra, so he asked her and she told him the hadith. Then Yahya said: Most of the people spoke about Qays ibn Talq and that his hadith is not taken as evidence, so he said Ahmad ibn Hanbal, may God be pleased with him: Both matters are according to what you said. Yahya said: Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he performed ablution. Whoever touches the penis. Ali said: Ibn Masoud used to say: He does not perform ablution with it, but rather it is a part of your body. Yahya said about whom? He said: On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah, and if Ibn Masoud and Ibn Omar meet and disagree, then Ibn Masoud He preferred to be followed, so Ahmad ibn Hanbal said to him: Yes, but Abu Qais al-Awdi does not use his hadith as evidence, so Ali said: Abu Qays al-Awdi told me Nu'aym Thana Mas'ar, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, he said: I do not care whether I touch him or whether I fear, so Ahmad said: Ammar and Ibn Umar are equal. Whoever wants can take this, and whoever wants can take this. Yahya said: Between Umayr bin Saeed and Ammar bin Yasser there is a battle."
"483","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Makki told us, and Ali told me Bin Issa, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “We were We pray with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we do not perform ablution from a place where we can stand.” Abu Muawiyah and Abdullah bin Idris followed him, on the authority of Al-A’mash. “As for the hadith of Abu Muawiyah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 483 - According to their condition"
"484","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, so he mentioned him. By chaining it to something similar. “As for the hadith of Abu Idris” [p. 235]."
"485","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, On the authority of Al-A'mash, he mentioned something similar. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 485 - According to their condition"
"486","Muhammad bin Salih and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, and Abu Al-Walid reported. Al-Faqih, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, they said: Abdullah bin Al-Muthanna Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Thumama, on the authority of Anas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, never took off his shoes during prayer except once. He took them off, and the people took them off, and he said: “What’s the matter with you?” They said: I took them off, so we took them off, so he said: “Gabriel told me that there was filth or harm in them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. He used Abdullah bin Al-Muthanna as evidence and did not narrate it, and the well-known hadith on the authority of Maimoon bears witness to it. The one-eyed one
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 486 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"487","Muhammad bin Salih and Ibrahim bin Asmah told us, they said: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, They said: Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail told us, Zuhair bin Muawiya told us, Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took off his shoes and said: “Gabriel told me that. . . . » . . . ."
"488","Qais bin Anif told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydlani told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Musa, they said: Ismail bin Ja’far told us, Muhammad bin Amr told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the doctrine goes further “.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. This was witnessed by the hadith of Ismail bin Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 488 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"489","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Abdul Hamid Al-Hamani told us, Ismail told us Ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to relieve himself, he would go as far as No one sees him.”"
"490","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Surayj bin Al-Nu’man told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Musa bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about sea water, and he said: “Sea water is pure.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and its evidence is many, but he did not narrate it, so it is the first of its evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 490 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"491","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata told us, and Abu Bakr bin Nasr, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa narrated to us, Al-Qanabi narrated to us, all of them, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Saeed bin Salamah, a servant of Al Al-Azraq, that Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: A man asked the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, we are sailing by sea and carrying with us a little water. If we perform ablution with it, we will become thirsty. Shall we perform ablution with sea water? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is pure, its water is permissible.” Malik bin Anas continued his narration, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq and Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Muzani. As for the hadith of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ayyub bin Zazan told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, he said: Abu Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad told us Bin Abi Bakr, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, Safwan bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abi A Burdah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to it. ."
"492","Al-Kaylini in Al-Ray, Saeed bin Kathir bin Yahya bin Humaid bin Nafi’ Al-Ansari told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Sa`id bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, who is from Banu Abd al-Dar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came A group of people sailing on the sea greeted him and said: O Messenger of God, we are sailing on the sea and getting some water, so we perform ablution with it. We are thirsty. Is it appropriate for us to perform ablution with sea water? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Its water is pure and its dead things are permissible.” Al-Jallah Abu Kathir followed Safwan bin Sulaym’s narration. This hadith, on the authority of Saeed bin Salamah"
"493","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bakr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, Al-Jallah Abu Kathir told me, that Ibn Salamah Al-Makhzoumi, told him, that Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah told him, that He heard Abu Hurairah say: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day when a hunter came to him and said: O Messenger of God, we are setting out on We want to hunt by the sea. One of us carries the tool with him and hopes to catch the catch soon. Perhaps he will find it as well, and perhaps he will not. He hunts until he reaches a place by the sea that he did not think he would reach. Perhaps he will have a wet dream or perform ablution. If he bathes or performs ablution With this water, perhaps one of us will die of thirst. Do you think that we should wash with it or perform ablution with sea water if we fear that? He claimed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bathe with it and perform ablution with it, for its water is pure and its dead bodies are permissible.” “Muslim has argued that Al-Jalah Abu Kathir has argued, and Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari and Yazid bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi have followed Saeed bin Salamah. Al-Makhzoumi narrated this hadith, but there were disagreements about it."
"494","Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, my grandfather told me, Amr bin Zurarah told me, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abu Burdah, on the authority of a man, from Banu Mudlij, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar."
"495","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. Suleiman bin Bilal said, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 493 - Muslim argued with Al-Jalah, and as for the hadith of Yazid bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi"
"496","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told me, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, Khalid told me Bin Yazid, that Yazid bin Muhammad al-Qurashi told him, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A group came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They said: We are fishing in the sea and we have some fresh water. Perhaps we fear thirst. Is it appropriate for us to perform ablution with water? The salty sea? He said: “Yes, perform ablution with it.” And he continued. . . . . “Al-Bukhari, this is Yazid bin Muhammad al-Qurashi in history, and Al-Layth bin Abi Burdah narrated on his authority, and among them was Sa’id bin al-Musayyab.”"
"497","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Ya’qub Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Yunus told us, in Egypt, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Sahm, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Rabi’ah told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He was asked The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked about sea water: Should we perform ablution from it? He said: “What is pure is its water, and what is permissible is its dead meat.” Among them is Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman."
"498","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja bin al-Sindi told us, Abu Ayyub Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi, Muhammad bin Ghazwan told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about performing ablution with sea water, and he said: “It is purification, its water is permissible to make its dead meat.” Al-Hakim said: “I have narrated in the continuations of Imam Malik ibn Anas in the paths of this hadith on the authority of three people who are not a condition of this book, and they are: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Muzani, and Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qadami. He only told me that he would know It is known that these are the follow-ups and evidence for this origin with which Malik published his book Al-Muwatta and was circulated by Islamic jurists, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless them from his time until our present time, and such a hadith cannot be explained by the ignorance of Saeed bin Salamah and Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, since the name of ignorance has been removed from them by these actions.” This hadith was narrated on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, Abdullah bin Abbas, Jabir bin Abdullah, Abdullah bin Amr and Anas. Ibn Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is similar to it. As for the hadith of Ali
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 498 - Saeed bin Salamah and Al-Mughirah are both ignorant"
"499","So Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Nasawi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Sa`id told us, Ahmad bin al-Husayn bin Ali told us, my father told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about sea water, and he said: “Its water is pure.” “The solution is his death.” “As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas, we have mentioned it.” As for the hadith of Jabir"
"500","So Abdul-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Shuaib narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr narrated to us, Al-Mu’affa bin Imran narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said about al-Bahr: “Its water is pure and its dead bodies are lawful.” As for the hadith Abdullah bin Amr"
"501","So Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hakam bin Musa told us, Haql bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sea carcass is lawful, and its water is pure.”"
"502","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, and Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, they said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Tha'labah Al-Khushani, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I said: O Messenger of God, in the land of the People of the Book they drink Liquor, and they eat pigs. What do you see in their vessels and pots? So he said: “Leave it as long as you find any desert on it, then if you find no desert on it, wash it with water - or he said, sprinkle it with water -” Then he said: “Cook in it and eat.” Hammad said, and I think he said: “And drink.” This is how Shu`bah narrated it, on the authority of Ayoub."
"503","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna, Muhammad bin Ayyub, and Ahmad bin Omar bin Hafs told us, they said: Amr bin Marzuq, Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: We are people of the Book on common land, so what should we do with their utensils? He said: “Leave whatever insects you find, and if you do not find any, wash them with water, then cook them.” This is how it was narrated by Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba"
"504","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Makram told us, Nasr bin Ali told us, Abu Ahmad told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the vessels of the polytheists, and he said: “Wash it, then cook in it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it, so they explained it with the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah and Hushaym, on the authority of Khaled, since Abu Asma al-Rahbi added in the chain of transmission, it is also authentic. It is necessary to narrate it in the authentic hadith on the condition that Abu Qalabah heard from Abu “alopecia”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 504 - According to their conditions, as for the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah"
"505","So Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about irrigation, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Abu Salamah told us, and Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, they said: We told him: Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu Asma’ al-Rahbi, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, that he said: O Messenger of God We are in the land of the People of the Book, so we cook in their pots and drink in their utensils? He said: “If you do not find anything else, make it cheaper.” As for the hadith of Hushaym"
"506","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: We will invade and travel in the land of the polytheists, and we will need one of their utensils to cook in. He said: “Wash them with water, then cook in them. And benefit from it.” “Both chains of narrations are authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"507","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib informed us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata informed us, Saeed bin Abi told us Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the skins of wild lions.”"
"508","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub, and Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, they said: Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, we told him Yazid bin Zuray’, Sa’id told us, so he mentioned something similar. It was narrated by a sheikh from the people of Basra, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Minhal, and he said in it: On the authority of Shu’bah, but it is an illusion on his part. “This chain of narration is authentic, as Al-Malih’s father’s name is Aamir bin Usama, and his father is Usama bin Umair, a companion from Banu Lahyan. Narrated by Al-Bukhari and Muslim. His hadith is in the Musnads, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 507 - True"
"509","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, They said: Ibrahim bin Musa Al-Razi told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Zayd, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, On the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “was brought two-thirds of a mudd of water, and he performed ablution and began to massage his arms.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 509 - According to their condition"
"510","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Ali ibn al-Madini informed us, and Ahmad ibn Jafar Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, they said: Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during the illness in which he died: “They poured on me seven water-sacrifices, the vessels of which were not permissible, so that I might entrust them to the people.” Aisha said: So we made him sit in Hafsa’s bathtub. Copper, and we poured water on him, and he started indicating to us that we had done so, then he left. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it because Hisham bin Yusuf al-San’ani and Muhammad bin Humaid al-Ma’mari did not mention Umrah in Its chain of transmission
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 510 - According to their condition, as for the hadith of Hisham"
"511","So Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydlani told me, we told him. . . ., On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness in which he was arrested: “Pour on me seven water bladders.” As for the hadith of Abu Sufyan Al-Maamari"
"512","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Humayd told us, about Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness in which he died: “Pour on me some Seven close-ups. “Both chains of narrations are authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"513","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mal told me, Al-Hasan bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told us Ibn Al-Musayyab, they said: Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Sulaiman bin Bilal told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, my father told me, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority, she said: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr entered with a siwak with which he used to cleanse himself.” So I said to him: “Give me this siwak, O Abdul Rahman.” So he gave it to me, so I bit it off, then chewed it, and gave it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sat with it while he was leaning on my chest.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 513 - According to their condition"
"514","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Samad Allan informed us, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn Hayyan informed us, Uthman ibn Hayyan informed us. Ali, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he prays two rak’ahs during the night, then he goes out and fasts.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 514 - According to their condition"
"515","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, and Abu Zakaria told us Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, they said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: Muhammad bin Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The superiority of a prayer that is performed properly over a prayer that is not performed is seventy times.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 515 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"516","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Yahya told us Bin Muhammad bin Yahya, Abdullah bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, they said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, Abdul Rahman Al-Sarraj told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would impose They must use the siwak to perform ablution, and I delayed the evening prayer until midnight.” . . . On the authority of Abu Hurairah in this matter, and they did not mention the word “fard” in it, and it is correct according to all of their conditions, and it has no defect and there is evidence for it. With this word “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 516 - They did not produce the word fardat, and it is according to their condition and has no defect."
"517","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told me, Khalifa bin Khayyat told me, Ishaq bin Idris Al-Basri told us, Omar told us Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Abar, Mansour told me, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Tammam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have imposed upon them the siwak at every prayer, just as I have imposed upon them ablution.”"
"518","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym and Muhammad bin Shazan told us, they said: Qutayba bin Sa’id told us, and Abu told me Bakr bin Abdullah told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Makhzoumi told us, Yaqoub bin Abi Salamah told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer for the one who has no ablution, and no ablution For those who do not mention the name of God upon him. Narrated by Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Musa Al-Makhzoumi"
"519","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdoos told us, Uthman bin Saeed told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, Muhammad bin Saeed told us. Musa, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer for the one who does not perform ablution. And there is no ablution for the one who does not mention the name of God upon him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and Muslim cited Ya’qub bin Abi Salamah Al-Majshun as evidence. Abi Salama dinar, but he did not produce it, and he has a witness.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 519 - It has an authentic chain of narration"
"520","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Kathir bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Rabih bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer for the one who does not perform ablution, and does not “Ablution for whoever does not mention the name of God over him.” So Ali bin Bandar Al-Zahid told me, Omar bin Muhammad bin Jubayr told me, Abu Bakr Al-Athram told us. He said: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and he was asked about someone who performs ablution and does not say the name, and Ahmad said: The best narration in this hadith is Kathir ibn Zayd."
"521","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdus Al-Abdusi Al-Abdi told me, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told me, and Abu Bakr Muhammad told me Bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us: Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, they said: Khallad bin Yahya Al-Sulami told us, Hisham bin Saad told us, Zaid bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, would you like me to show you how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution? “So he called for a vessel containing water So he scooped a scoop, rinsed his mouth and sniffed, then he took another and joined his hands with it, and washed his face, then he took another and washed his right hand, then He took another scoop and washed his left hand, then he took a handful of water, wiped his hand, wiped his head and ears with it, then scooped another scoop. Another time he spread on his right foot, which had the sandal on it, and on the left foot like that, and he wiped the bottom of the sandals. Then he said: “This is the ablution of the Messenger of God.” May God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution once upon a time, and this is comprehensive, and this hadith of Hisham bin Saad is explained.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 521 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"522","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi, he said: Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit. Ibn Sabra, on the authority of his father, that he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and mentioned things, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Perform ablution thoroughly.” And wet your fingers, and if you inhale, adulterate, unless you are fasting.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it, and it is, in sum, what we said: they turned away, on the authority of the companion from whom only one person narrated it. They all cited some of this type as evidence. As for Abu Hashim Ismail bin Katheer Al-Qaari, he is one of the prominent Meccans. He narrated this from him. “The hadith itself is not revolutionary. A group of them includes Ibn Jurayj, Dawud bin Abd al-Rahman al-Attar, Yahya bin Sulaym, and others.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 522 - Sahih as for the hadith of Ibn Jurayj"
"523","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, and the pronunciation is his, Abu al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ismail bin Kathir narrated to me, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabrah, on the authority of his father, who was an expatriate from Banu al-Muftafiq, that he came to Aisha. And a companion of his were looking for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but they did not find him. So Aisha fed them dates and porridge, and they did not wait until he came. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, began to sit down, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: “Has anyone fed you?” So I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. Then I said: O Messenger of God, tell us about prayer. He said: “Perform ablution perfectly, and cross your fingers. If you inhale it, then eat it, unless you are fasting.” As for the hadith of Dawud bin Abd al-Rahman al-Attar"
"524","So Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi informed us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Burdiyah Al-Makki told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Dawud bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman Al-Attar, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabrah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you inhale then adulterate, unless you are fasting, and do not strike your female counterpart as you strike your female slave.” As for the hadith of Yahya bin Sulaym"
"525","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Yahya bin Sulaym told us, On the authority of Ismail ibn Kathir, who said: I heard Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabrah, speaking, on the authority of his father, who said: I was a delegate of Banu al-Mundafiq to the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about ablution. He said: “Perform ablution thoroughly, pass between your fingers, and go to extremes in it.” Inhalation, unless you are fasting. There is evidence for this hadith on the authority of Ibn Abbas."
"526","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Qaridh Ibn Shaybah, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan Al-Marri, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Scatter twice, or Three”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 526 - This is evidence of a bastard’s news"
"527","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, and he informed us Ahmad ibn al-Quta’i, and the word for him is: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, he informed Israel, On the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, he said: I saw Uthman. He performed ablution, washed his face, sniffed his nose, rinsed his mouth three times, and wiped his head. And his ears, the outside and inside of them, and he mixed his beard three times when he washed his face before washing his feet, then he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He will do what you saw me do.” “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Uthman after his ablution, and they did not mention in their narrations the cutting of the beard three times, and this An authentic chain of narration. They cited all of its narrators other than Aamir bin Shaqiq as evidence, and I do not know of any criticism of Aamir bin Shaqiq in any way. There is authentic evidence regarding grooming the beard on the authority of Ammar ibn Yasir, Anas ibn Malik, and Aisha, may God be pleased with them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 527 - Ibn Ma’in classed it as weak, then he said, “It has an authentic witness,” as for the hadith of Ammar."
"528","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Mansouri told me, we told him Harun bin Yusuf, Ibn Abi Omar told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Hassan bin Bilal, that he saw Ammar bin Yasser He performs ablution and combs his beard, and he is told: Will you comb your beard? He said: “What is stopping me when I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combing his beard?” . Sufyan said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Hassan bin Bilal, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And as for the hadith of Anas bin Malik"
"529","So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Muhammad bin Wahb bin Abi Karimah told us, Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution and combing his beard. with his fingers beneath it,” and said, “This is what my Lord has commanded me.”"
"530","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Muhammad bin Wahb told us, Marwan bin Muhammad told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad Al-Fazari told us, On the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performing ablution and combing his beard,” and he said: “With this My Lord has commanded me.” As for the hadith of Aisha"
"531","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Hilal bin Fayyad told us, Omar bin Abi Wahb told us, on the authority of Musa bin Tharwan, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaid Allah bin Kuraiz, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when He performed ablution through his beard.” “This is authentic evidence regarding wiping the insides of the ears.”"
"532","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ahmad bin al-Nadr al-Azdi told us, Muhammad bin Amr, an additional narration, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Humaid al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performed ablution So he wiped the insides of his ears and the outsides of them. He said: Ibn Masoud used to command that. “Zaida bin Qudamah is trustworthy and trustworthy. He narrated it on the authority of Al-Thawri, and others authenticated it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 532 - Zaida is trustworthy and someone else stops him"
"533","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Khalil told me Al-Asbahani told us Musa bin Ishaq Al-Ansari told us Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us Abdul Rahman bin Thabit told us, tell me Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performed ablution twice.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” This is witnessed by the famous mursal hadith, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution once, then said: “This is the function of ablution,” then he performed ablution twice, then said: “This The mediator is part of the ablution for which God doubles the reward for its performer twice” - the hadith in its entirety -
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 533 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"534","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He performed ablution once in a while, combining rinsing his mouth and nose.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 534 - They took out the first part"
"535","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Dawud bin Qais Al-Farra told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “performed ablution room by room.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”"
"536","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Maamari told us, in Medina, Abdullah told us Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Dawud Ibn Qays, and Malik Ibn Anas, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yassar, on the authority of Usama Ibn Zaid, on the authority of Bilal, He said: “I entered the markets with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he went for his needs.” He said: “So he came and I gave him water and he performed ablution and then left.” To take his arms out of his pocket, but he was not able, so he took them out from under the robe, so he performed ablution and wiped over his socks.” “This is an authentic hadith from the hadith of Malik bin Anas, and it is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it contains a great benefit, which is that: They did not narrate the hadith of Safwan bin Assal about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping over the socks in the city, and mentioning the timing in it, but they agreed Based on the information of Ali bin Abi Talib and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, may God be pleased with them, regarding wiping over the socks. . . . “The markets are a famous place among the city’s shops, and the hadith is famous about Dawud bin Qais Al-Farra.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 536 - According to their condition"
"537","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the markets and went for his needs, and Bilal was with him. Then they left and I asked Bilal what? made? He said: “He performed ablution, washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his socks.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, as he cited Dawud ibn Qais as evidence.”"
"538","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, then Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Abi Ubaid told us By God, in Egypt, Abdul Aziz bin Imran bin Miqlass and Harmala bin Yahya told us, saying: Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin told me Al-Harith, on the authority of Hibban bin Wasi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd Al-Ansari, who said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He performs ablution and takes water for his ears, other than the water with which he wiped his head. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, if it is transmitted from this Ibn Abi Ubaid Allah, then they all supported it with all its narrators.” Abu Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Ali, and he witnessed what
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 538 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"539","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us more than once, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Harmala bin Yahya told us, Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Hibban ibn Wasi’, that his father told him that he heard Abdullah ibn Zayd that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “wiped his ears with water other than the one he wiped with.” with his head.” “This clarifies the meaning of the first, and it is just as true.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 539 - True"
"540","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us Ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bint Mu’awwidh, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “wiped his ears, the insides and the outsides.” “They did not use Ibn Aqeel as evidence, and he was upright in hadith and respected in honor.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 540 - Ibn Aqeel Mustaqeel Al-Hadith"
"541","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir and Abu Dawud told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he reported Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, Sulaiman bin Harb, and Hafs bin Amr bin Murrah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, he said: We entered upon Ali, may he be pleased with him. By God, on his behalf, I and two men, a man from among us, and a man from Banu Asad. He said: So he sent them for a need and said: “You are both sick, so treat your religion.” He said: Then he entered the exit, then he came out, so he called for water and washed his hands, then he began to recite the Qur’an, and it was as if we had denied it, so he said: “It is as if you You denied it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to relieve himself, read the Qur’an, and eat meat, and he did not withhold it from Reciting it is something that does not constitute ritual impurity.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and the two sheikhs did not use Abdullah bin Salamah as evidence, so the focus of the hadith is on him, and Abdullah bin Salamah is not impugned. “in it”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 541 - True"
"542","Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr and Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haraz informed us of Mecca in others. They said: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, they said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you comes to his family Then he wanted to do it again, so he should perform ablution, for he would be more energetic to do it again.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording, rather they narrated it as saying ‘let him perform ablution’ only, and they did not mention it.” “Therein” because it is more active for the oud “and this is a word that Shu’bah used alone, from Asim, and the uniqueness of something like it is acceptable to them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 542 - They did not mention the end of it"
"543","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab told us. . . Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi, Saeed bin Kathir bin Ufayr, and Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukayr told us, they said: Al-Layth bin told us Saad, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qais, he said: I asked Aisha, I said: How was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? What does he do in case of impurity, whether he takes a bath before he sleeps, or sleeps before he takes a bath? She said: “He did all of that. Maybe he took a bath and slept, and maybe he performed ablution and slept.” I said: Praise be to God, who made the matter expansive. Narrated by Muslim. In the Sahih, on the authority of Qutaibah, he did not mention its evidence in words. Ghudayf bin Al-Harith followed him, on the authority of Aisha
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 543 - Narrated by Muslim"
"544","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr told us Al-Darabardi, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Burd bin Sinan, on the authority of Ubadah Bin Nasi, on the authority of Ghudayf bin Al-Harith, who said: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, about the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, washing himself from ritual impurity, and she said: “Maybe he took a bath before he slept, and maybe he slept before he took a bath.” He was followed by Khams bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Burd"
"545","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Abdul Rahman bin Hammad told us, whispering to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Ghudayf bin Al-Harith, who said: I said to Aisha: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was afflicted with ritual impurity, he would wash himself from the beginning. Or at the end of it? She said: “Perhaps he did ablution at the beginning, and perhaps he did ablution at the end.” I said: God is the greatest. Praise be to God, who has made the matter expansive, and may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Our Master Muhammad, his family and all his companions"
"546","Abdullah bin Musa told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Muafia bin Suleiman told us, Zuhayr told us, Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Zuhair told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray the two rak’ahs before the morning prayer, and I do not see him performing ablution after washing.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. It has a witness according to the conditions of Muslim, a summary and explanation, and the narrator did not doubt it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 546 - According to their condition"
"547","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, he said: I read to a partner, and he told us Ali bin Issa, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he “does not perform ablution after washing.” There is authentic evidence for him on the authority of Ibn Umar."
"548","Omar bin Ja’far Al-Basri told me, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Makram told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, Abd Al-Ala told us, Abd told us Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about ablution after washing, and he said: “Which ablution is better?” From washing? . Al-Hakim said: “Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ is trustworthy, and someone else has trusted him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 548 - Ibn Bazi’ is trustworthy, and others authenticated him"
"549","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, he said: I read to a partner, and Abd told me Allah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, Ismail bin Zakaria told us, they said: Harith bin Abi Matar told us, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to “warm himself with it after washing.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and its evidence is on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, and the way to them is corrupt”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 549 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"550","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Zaid bin told me Al-Hubab, on the authority of Abu Muadh, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “had a rag with which he dried himself after “Ablution.” “Abu Muadh, this is Al-Fadl bin Maysarah Basri. Yahya bin Saeed narrated from him and praised him, and it is a hadith that was narrated on the authority of Anas. Ibn Malik and others, but they did not narrate it.”"
"551","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, in Egypt, Safwan bin Issa told us, Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Marwan Al-Asfar said: I saw Ibn Omar leaning his camel facing the Qiblah, then he sat urinating towards it, so I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, Isn't this forbidden? He said: “This is only forbidden in space, so if there is something between you and the qiblah that covers you, then there is no problem.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. He cited Al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan as evidence, but they did not narrate it.” And he has a witness on the authority of Jabir, “Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 551 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"552","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saeed told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Aban bin Salih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had “forbidden us to look back.” “The Qiblah or we face it with our private parts if we spill water, then we see him before his death urinating facing the Qiblah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 552 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"553","Abu Hafs Omar bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Abu Kamil told us, Yusuf bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Othman, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The price of a dog is evil and it is even more evil.” From him. “This is a hadith whose narrators are all trustworthy. If it is transmitted from Yusuf bin Khalid al-Samti, then it is authentic according to the conditions of al-Bukhari, and I have cited it due to the severity of the hadith. There is a need for it, and the two sheikhs used something like it in more than one place, which would take a long book to explain.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 553 - Yusuf Wah"
"554","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, he told me Utba bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Talha bin Nafi’, that he narrated to him, saying: Abu Ayyub, Jabir bin Abdullah, and Anas bin Malik Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this verse: “In it are men who love to purify themselves. And God loves those who purify themselves.} [At-Tawbah: 108] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people of Ansar, God has indeed praised you with goodness in purification.” What is this purification of yours? They said: O Messenger of God, we perform ablution for prayer and to wash ourselves from impurity. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is there anything else besides that?” They said: No, except that when one of us came out of the stool he liked to clean himself with water. He said: “He is that one.” “This is a major and authentic hadith in the Book of Purity, for Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shabur and Utbah bin Abi Hakim are among the imams of the people of the Levant. The two sheikhs only took the basis of the narrations, and such a hadith should not be left to him. Ibrahim bin Yaqoub said: Muhammad bin Shuaib is the most knowledgeable of people. According to the hadith of the Syrians, and there is evidence for it with an authentic chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 554 - True"
"555","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Abi told us, on the authority of Sharhabeel Bin Saad, on the authority of Uwaim bin Sa’idah Al-Ansari, then Al-Ijli, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the people of Quba: “Indeed, God has done good.” Praise be to you for purification.” And he said: “In it are men who love to purify themselves.” [At-Tawbah: 108] until the verse ended, and he said to them: “What is this purification? . . . ,. . . ."
"556","My father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban Al-Ansari told us, then Al-Mazani Mazin Bani Al-Najjar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Ibn Omar, he said: I said to him: Have you seen Abdullah Ibn Omar’s ablution for every prayer, whether he was pure or impure, on whose authority was he? He said: Asma’ bint Zayd bin Al-Khattab narrated to him that Abdullah bin Hanzalah bin Abi Amir Al-Ghasil narrated to her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, commanded ablution at every prayer, whether pure or impure. When that was difficult for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he ordered the use of the siwak. At every prayer, ablution is removed from them, except in the event of an event.” Abdullah thought that he had the strength to do that, so he did it until he died. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform ablution for every prayer, so when the year of the conquest came, he performed all the prayers with one ablution.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 556 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"557","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Sadaqah bin Left, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, who is Aqeel bin Jabir, whom Salamah Al-Abrash called, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, in the battle of Dhat al-Riqa’ of palm trees, a man of the Muslims wounded a woman of the polytheists. When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, departed, Her husband came while he was absent. When he was told the news, he swore that he would not stop until he would shed blood among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he left. He followed in the footsteps of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down to a house and said: “Who is there to trouble us this night?” So a man from the immigrants and a man from the Ansar were appointed as delegates, and they said: We, O Messenger of God. He said: “So be with the mouth of the people.” He said: And he was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his companions came down to Al-Shaab from the valley. When the two men went out to the mouth of Al-Shaab, Al-Ansari said to Al-Muhajiri: Yes. Would you like the night to be sufficient for you? He said: Sufficient for me at the beginning of it. So the Muhajiri lay down, and the Ansari stood up and prayed. He said: A husband came. The woman, and when he saw the man’s figure, he knew that he was the lady of the people. He said: He shot him with an arrow and put it in it. He said: So he took it off and put it in and it remained firm. He was standing and praying, then he shot him with another arrow and put it in it. He took it off and put it in and remained standing and praying, then he returned the third arrow to him and put it in it. So he took it off and put it down, then he knelt down, then his companion got up and said: Sit, for he stood firm and jumped up, and when the man saw them he knew that he had vowed. With it, he fled, and when Al-Muhajiri saw the blood on the Ansari, he said: Glory be to God, why didn’t you give me a reward the first time he shot you? He said: I was in A surah that I recited, but I did not like to interrupt it until I had completed it. When he continued to shoot, I knelt down and gave you permission. I swear to God, had I not lost By the way, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to cut myself off before I cut it off, or execute it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Muslim used the hadiths of Muhammad bin Ishaq as evidence, as for Aqeel bin Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari. He is in better condition than his brothers Muhammad and Abd al-Rahman, and this is a narrow Sunnah. Our imams believed in this hadith that blood coming out of Other than that, the event does not necessitate ablution.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 557 - True"
"558","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, Ishaq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubayy told us, he said: I heard Muhammad. Ibn Ishaq, he says: Sadaqa ibn Yasar informed me, on the authority of Aqeel ibn Jabir, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to it. Abu told us Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Muhammad bin Ali Al-Warraq, nicknamed Hamdan, told us, Abu Yahya Abdul-Samad bin Hassan Al-Marudhi told us, Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, and the wording is his, Ali bin Abdul Aziz informed us, narrated to us Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar, Qasim bin Yazid Al-Jarmi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade those who defecated from speaking, for God hates that.”"
"559","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Ali bin Harb told us, Al-Qasim bin Yazid Al-Jarmi told us, and Zaid bin Abi Al-Zarqa told us, on the authority of Sufyan, On the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He forbade those who defecated from speaking, and said: “God hates that.” “This is Iyad bin Hilal Al-Ansari, a sheikh of the followers and well-known among the people of Medina. He came to Al-Yamamah, and what you mentioned is true.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 559 - True"
"560","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad Al-Hafid told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Sallam bin Ibrahim Al-Warraq told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad bin Hilal, he said: Abu Saeed Al-Khudri told me, he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “Do not let two men go out and excrete, exposing their private parts, for God hates that.” “This is an authentic hadith from the hadith of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyaad bin Hilal Al-Ansari, but he neglected it due to a dispute between the companions of Yahya bin Abi Kathir is in it, and some of them said: Hilal bin Ayadh, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ismail ruled in history that it Iyad bin Hilal Al-Ansari, Abu Saeed heard from him, Yahya bin Abi Kathir heard from him, Hisham, Muammar, Ali bin Al-Mubarak and Harb said it. Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, and I heard Ali Ibn Hamshadh, saying: I heard Musa Ibn Harun, saying: Al-Awza’i narrated it twice, He once said: On the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hilal bin Iyaad. Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of a mursal. Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi was telling Iyad bin Hilal about it, then he doubted it, so he said: Or Hilal bin Iyad. It was narrated on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi Ali bin al-Madini, Ubayd Allah bin Omar al-Qawariri, and Muhammad bin al-Muthanna, so they agreed on Iyad bin Hilal, which is correct. Al-Hakim said: “Two of our imams, such as Al-Bukhari and Musa bin Harun, have ruled that it is valid, according to the statement of the one who established this chain of narration. On the authority of Iyad bin Hilal Al-Ansari, and Al-Bukhari mentioned evidence regarding it in which the hadith was authentic, and Muslim narrated the meaning of this hadith. Abu Kurayb, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Hubab, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not look at a man’s private parts, and a woman should not look at a man’s private parts.” “The Woman” - Hadith -"
"561","Abu Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Abu Amer told us Al-Kharaz, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When one of you performs the ritual prayer, let him perform Witr, for God loves Witr.” Witr, do you not see the heavens as seven, and the earths as seven, and the tawaaf? And he mentioned some things. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in these terms. Rather, they agreed on “whoever performs ijtamarah should only use it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 561 - Munkar and Al-Harith is not a mayor"
"562","Abu Al-Abbas told Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, about Yusuf. Ibn Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, said: I entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and I heard her saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He came out of the toilet and said: “Your forgiveness.”"
"563","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukair narrated to us, Israel, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would get up from the excrement He said: “Your forgiveness.” “This is an authentic hadith, for Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah is one of the trustworthy people of Abu Musa’s family, and we did not find anyone disputing it. He mentioned hearing his father from Aisha, may God be pleased with her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 563 - Sahih and Yusuf is trustworthy"
"564","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Hanbal bin Ishaq told us, Qubaisa told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Hasan bin Halim told us Al-Marwazi, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “One of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath due to ritual impurity, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution.” And he greeted, or bathed in its bounty.” Shu'bah followed him from Samak"
"565","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, and Abu Ali Al-Hussein told us. Ibn Ali Al-Hafiz, Muhammad Ibn Ishaq told us, Muhammad Ibn Yahya Al-Quta’i told us, Abu Ali told us, Ali Ibn Al-Abbas Ibn Al-Walid told us Al-Bajli, Ahmed bin Al-Miqdam told us, they said: Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to perform ablution from a vessel, and one of his wives said: O Messenger of God, I have performed ablution from this. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed ablution and said: “Water cannot be made impure by anything.” Al-Bukhari used as evidence the hadiths of Ikrimah, and Muslim used the hadiths as evidence. Samak bin Harb, and this is an authentic hadith regarding purity, and they did not narrate it, and no defect is preserved for it."
"566","Abu Sa`id Ismail bin Ahmad al-Jurjani told us, Muhammad bin al-Hasan al-Asqalani told us, Harmala bin Yahya told us, Ibn Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Utbah, who is the son of Abi Hakim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that it was said to Omar bin Al-Khattab, “Tell us about the difficult hour,” and Omar said: We went out to Tabuk in the heat of the day. So we stayed at a place where we were afflicted with such thirst that we thought our necks would be cut off, to the point that a man would slaughter his camel and squeeze out its dung. So he drinks it and puts what remains on his liver. Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of God, God has taught you good in supplication, so pray for Him. He said: “Do you like that?” He said: Yes, so he raised his hands and did not return them until the sky said, so it became dark, then it poured out and they filled what they had, then we went to see and nothing happened. We find it passing the army. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. He included a strange Sunnah in it, which is that if water is mixed with it, it leaves something that can be eaten.” His meat did not make it impure, for if it had made water impure, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not have permitted a Muslim to put it on his liver until He defiles his hands.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 566 - According to their condition"
"567","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Hamida bint Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Kabsha bint Ka’b bin Malik, who was under Ibn Abi Qatada, that Abu Qatada went in and she poured water for him to perform ablution, then a cat came to drink from it, so Abu Qatada listened to her from the vessel until she drank it. Kabsha said: He saw me looking at him, and he said: Do you wonder, my niece? So I said: Yes, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not impure, it is one of the things that go around you, and the circumambulations.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it as being the same as they originally narrated it in leaving it, except that they all testified to Malik ibn Anas that it The ruling on the hadith of Al-Madani, and this hadith is what Malik authenticated, and he cited it as evidence in Al-Muwatta’, and despite that, it has a witness with a chain of transmission. Sahih” [p. 264]."
"568","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa, the judge in Bukhara, told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Jafar told us. Al-Razi, Sulayman bin Musafa bin Shaybah Al-Hajbi told us, he said: I heard Mansour bin Safiya bint Shaybah, speaking, on the authority of his mother Safiya, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. . . . . . . . “The conditions of the two Sheikhs were authenticated against this, but they did not narrate it either.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 567 - True"
"569","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us in Bukhara, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, dictating from his book in the year Two hundred and ninety-six, Abu Bakra Bakkar ibn Qutayba, the judge of Fustat, told us, Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Qurra ibn Khalid, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “To purify the vessel of one of you if a dog licks in it is to wash it.” Seven times, the first with dirt, and then with the kitten like that.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. Abu Bakra is trustworthy and trustworthy, and whoever imagines that Abu Bakra will be alone with him, on the authority of Abu Asim, but Abu Asim was the only one to mention it, and it is a proof.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 569 - On their two conditions"
"570","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Faqih told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah told us, and Hammad bin Al-Hasan bin Anbasa, they said: Abu Asim told us, Qurrah bin Khalid told us, Muhammad bin Sirin told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “The purification of the vessel if a dog licks in it is to wash it seven times, first with dirt, and the cat once or twice.” “Qurrat Yashāk”"
"571","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Qasim bin Zakaria al-Muqri told us, Ali bin Muslim told us, Abu Asim told us, Qurrah bin Khalid told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad told us Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “On a cat once or twice” - meaning, washing the vessel if he has engulfed it. The pussy. “Ali bin Nasr al-Jahdhami was healed, on the authority of Qurrah, in explaining this word.”"
"572","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Ma’shar al-Hasan bin Sulayman al-Darimi told us, Nasr bin Ali told us, Ubayy told us, Qurrah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The purification of the vessel of one of you if a dog licks in it is to be washed seven times. The first of them to be in the dirt. Then Abu Hurairah mentioned the cat. I don’t know. He said: once or twice. Nasr bin Ali said: I found it in my father’s book in another place, on the authority of Qurrah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, in the book with a chain of narration, and in The kitten is standing still. He was followed in the arrest of the male cat by Muslim bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Qurrah."
"573","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Barqi told us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq told us, Muhammad informed us Ibn Ayyub, Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Abu Khalifa told us, they said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Qurra told us, Muhammad bin Sirin told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, in The cat licks in the vessel. He said: “It should be washed once or twice.” “It has been proven that the ruling of Sharia refers to the hadith of Malik bin Anas regarding the purification of cats, and God knows best.”"
"574","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, On the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to He was performing ablution from a waterskin, and he was told that it was dead, so he said: “His tanning removes its impurity, or its impurity, or its impurity.” “This is an authentic hadith, and I do not know of any defect in it, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 574 - It is true and I do not know of any reason for it"
"575","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is sufficient for whoever The ablution is one mudd, and from impurity is the saa’. Then a man said to him: That is not enough for us, Jabir. He said: “It is enough for someone who is better than you and more powerful.” “Poetry.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 575 - According to their condition"
"576","So Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Hasanjani told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Yahya bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib bin Zaid, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “was brought two-thirds of a mudd. So he performed ablution and started massaging his arms.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Habib ibn Zayd as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 576 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"577","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, and Ali bin Jesus, and the word for him, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Harun bin Ishaq told us, Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: “We used to perform ablution, men and women, and wash our hands in one vessel at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.” They only agreed on the hadith of Aisha in this regard. “This hadith has a unique witness to it, Kharijah ibn Mus’ab, and I mention it, seeking reward from what I witness of the large number of people’s obsessions in their prayers. Water
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 577 - According to their condition"
"578","Ali bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Saleh bin Jamil told us, Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Abu Dawud told us, Kharijah bin Musab told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Yahya bin Damrah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “There is a devil who performs ablution, and he is called Al-Wahlan, so beware of him, and beware of the whisperer of water.” “And there is witness with another chain of transmission that is more authentic than this.”"
"579","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Saeed told us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Naama, that Abdullah bin Mughaffal heard his son saying: Oh God, I ask you for the white palace to the right of Paradise, When I entered it, he said: O my son, ask God for Paradise and seek refuge with Him from Hell, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He There will be in this nation a people who will practice ritual purity and supplication.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 579 - There is a transmission"
"580","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Milhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Haywa bin Shuraih, on the authority of Uqba ibn Muslim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Juzz al-Zubaidi, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Woe For the heels and the soles of the feet from the Fire.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not mention the soles of the feet.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 580 - They did not bring out the soles of the feet"
"581","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Hasan bin Bishr Al-Hamdani told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade a man to enter the water unless he was wearing an apron.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 581 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"582","Abu Muhammad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, And Musaab bin Shaybah, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that she told him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “He should perform four ritual ablutions from ritual impurity, on Friday, from washing the dead, and from cupping.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 582 - Narrated by Abu Nu’aym on the authority of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"583","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal in the year three hundred and ninety-four, Abu Jafar informed Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani of Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani, Yahya bin Sulaym told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I entered Fatima came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while she was crying. He said: “My daughter, what makes you cry?” She said: O my father, why should I not cry while these chiefs of Quraysh are in the Hijr, holding each other with Al-Lat, Al-Uzza, and Manat, the other third, if only... If they saw you, they would have risen up and killed you, and there was not a man among them who did not know his share of your blood, so he said: “O my daughter, bring me ablution.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution and then went out to the mosque. When they saw him, they said: Here he is, so they lowered their heads and fell. Their chins were between their hands, but they did not raise their eyes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a handful of dirt and covered them with it and said: “Shah! “Faces.” Not one of his pebble struck a man except that he was killed on the Day of Badr as an unbeliever. “This is an authentic hadith. They all cited Yahya ibn Sulaym as evidence, and Muslim cited Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khathim as evidence, and they did not narrate it, and I do not know It has a reason, and the Sunnis are among the people most in need of opposing what was said that ablution did not occur before the descending of the table, but rather the descending of the table. In the Farewell Pilgrimage, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in Arafat, and he has a valid, speaking witness that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was performing ablution, and he commanded He performed ablution before the migration and did not perform it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 583 - True"
"584","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastawayh Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, Abu Tawbah Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi`, Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, on the authority of al-Abbas ibn Salim, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Amr ibn Absa, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was the first time he was sent while he was in Mecca, and at that time he was in a low state, so I said: What are you? He said: “I am a prophet.” I said: What is a prophet? He said: “The Messenger of God.” I said: Has God sent you? He said: “Yes.” I said: What did he send you with? He said: “To worship God, to break idols and religions, and to join the ties of kinship.” I said: Yes, what He sent you with. I said: Who will follow you on This? He said: “Slave and free” - meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal - and Amr used to say: You saw me when I was a quarter, or a fourth of Islam. He said: So I converted to Islam. I said: I follow you, O Messenger of God. He said: No, but follow your people. When you are informed that I have left, follow me. He said: So I joined my people. I was anticipating news of him and his departure, until Rebekah came from Yathrib, and I met them and asked them about the news. They said: The Messenger has left. May God bless him and grant him peace from Mecca to Medina. I said: He came to it? They said: Yes. He said: So I journeyed until I came to him. I said: Do you know me, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes,You are the man who came to me in Mecca.” So I began to spy his privacy, and when he left, I said: O Messenger of God, teach me what God has taught you and be more beautiful. He said: “So ask.” Whatever you want.” I said: “Which night do I hear?” He said: “In the middle of the night, pray whatever you want, for the prayer is witnessed and written down until you pray the morning prayer. Then shorten it until the sun rises and you raise the chain of one or two spears, for it rises between the horns of a devil, and the disbelievers pray for it, then pray as long as You wish, for prayer is witnessed and written until the spear reaches its shadow, then shorten it, for Hell will be burned and its gates will be opened. The sun, pray as long as you want, for the prayer is witnessed and written, then pray until you pray the afternoon prayer, then shorten it until the sun sets, for it sets between the horns of a devil, and the unbelievers pray for them, and when you perform ablution, wash your hands, for if you wash your hands, your sins will come out of your arms, and then You have anointed your head, and your sins have gone out from the ends of your hair; then when you have washed your feet, your sins have gone out from your feet. If you abide in Your sitting will be a reward for your ablution, and if you stand up and remember your Lord, praise Him, and bow to Him two rak’ahs, approaching them with your heart, you will be Of your sins as on the day your mother gave birth to you.” He said: I said: O Amr, know what you are saying.You are saying a great thing. He said: By God, I have grown in age and my end is approaching, and I would not be able to lie, even if I had not heard it from the Messenger of God. I did not speak to him, may God bless him and grant him peace, except once or twice, but I heard him more than that. This is what Abu Salam told me on his authority, on the authority of Abu Umamah: Unless I make a mistake or add something, then I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him. “He has gone out.” Muslim Some of these words are from the hadith of Al-Nadr bin Muhammad Al-Jurashi, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Shaddad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Umamah. He said: Amr bin Absa said: This hadith of Abbas bin Salim is more correct and more complete than the hadith of Ikrimah bin Ammar."
"585","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, my father told me, Al-Walid told me Ibn Ubayd Allah Ibn Abi Rabah, that Ata’ told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man became impure in the winter, so he asked and was ordered to wash, so he did. Then he died, and that was mentioned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “What is theirs? They killed him. God will kill them.” Three times: “God has made the sacred place - or tayammum - pure.” “This is an authentic hadith, for this Al-Walid bin Ubaid Allah is the son of my brother Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, and he has very few hadiths.” It was narrated by Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, and it is narrated after this. There is another witness to him on the authority of Ibn Abbas.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 585 - True"
"586","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he raised it in the Almighty’s saying: {And if you are sick or on a journey} [An-Nisa: 43] He said: “If A man should avoid surgery for the sake of God, or sores, or smallpox, and is afraid that if he performs ghusl he will die, so he should perform tayammum.”"
"587","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said regarding the urine of an infant: “The boy’s urine should be sprinkled on him, and the girl’s urine should be washed off.” “This is an authentic hadith, for Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili refused to hear it from Ali, and according to their condition it is authentic, and he did not narrate it and he has two authentic witnesses. ""one of them""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 587 - According to their condition"
"588","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Al-Mukhareq, on the authority of Lubaba bint Al-Harith, who said: Al-Hussein urinated on the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: Bring your dress so that He washed him and said: “It is washed with female urine and sprinkled with male urine.” The second witness:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 588 - True"
"589","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Yahya told us Ibn Al-Walid, Mahal bin Khalifa Al-Tai told me, Abu Al-Samh told me, he said: I was the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Hasan, or Al-Hussein, was brought. So he urinated on his chest, so they wanted to wash him, so he said: “Sprinkle him with a sprinkle, for he is washed with the urine of a female slave and sprinkled with the urine of a boy.” “The two sheikhs reported on the boy’s urine, the hadith of Aisha and Umm Qais bint Muhsin, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him,” ordered water to be poured on the urine. The boy, “As for the mention of the girl’s urine, they did not expel it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 589 - True"
"590","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Bazzaz and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Mukhlid Al-Jawhari informed us, saying: Thana Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi, Muhammad bin Katheer Al-Masisi told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If one of you steps on his shoes in a way that is harmful, then the dirt is purifying.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 590 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"591","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid Al-Bayruti told us, my father informed us, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, he said: I was informed that Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari narrated, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If “If one of you steps on his shoes in harm’s way, the dust is pure for them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, for this Muhammad ibn Kathir al-San’ani is authentic, and the mention of Ibn Ajlan has been preserved in its chain of transmission, but no He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 591 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"592","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abdullah bin Khayran told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abbas bin Al-Walid Al-Raqqam told us, Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hudayn bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Muhajir bin Qunfud said that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was urinating, and he greeted him, but he did not respond to him until he performed ablution, then apologized to him. And he said: “I hate to mention God except in a state of purity - or he said: in a state of purity - «.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Muslim narrated the hadith of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was urinating, so he greeted him and did not respond to him until he performed ablution and then apologized to him, and said: “ I hate to mention God except in a state of purity - or he said: - in a state of purity. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 592 - According to their condition"
"593","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us, in Rayy, Muhammad bin Al-Farah Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hakima bint Umaymah bint Ruqaqiqa, on the authority of her mother, that she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a cup made of sticks underneath “His bed he urinates in at night.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and a strange Sunnah, and Umaima bint Ruqayqah is a famous companion, and her hadith in Al-Wahdan was narrated to the imams. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 593 - True"
"594","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, my grandfather told us, I am Sa’id bin Abi Maryam, Nafi’ bin Yazid told me, Haywah bin Shuraih, that Abu Sa`id al-Himyari told him on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of the three curses: excrement.” In the fields, on the side of the road, and in the shade of wasteland.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 594 - It is true that Muslim was the only one with the hadith of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “Beware of the cursers.” They said: What is the curse? He said: “The one who abandons himself on the road.”"
"595","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari informed us, Abu Al-Mawjih Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Muammar told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, and the pronunciation is his, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin told us Hanbal, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told me, Muammar told me, Ash’ath told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “None of you should urinate in his bath and then wash himself in it, or perform ablution in it, for most of it is obsessiveness.” “The wording is for the hadith of Ahmad. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it and have a witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 595 - According to their condition"
"596","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abdullah, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Al-Rahman Al-Himyari - I think it is - on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade any of us from combing our hair every day, or urinating in the “His ablution”"
"597","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Muafia bin Sulayman told us, Zuhayr told us, Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Arqam, that he went out as a Hajj, or a Umrah performer, and people were with him while he was leading them, so one day He led the morning prayer and then said: Let one of you come forward. He went into the open air and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If one of you wants to go to the outdoors and pray the prayer, let him start in the outdoors.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it has witnesses with authentic chains of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 597 - According to their condition"
"598","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Yusuf bin Musa Al-Marwazi told us, Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told us, Shuaib bin Ishaq, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Yazid ibn Shurayh al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “It is not permissible It is permissible for a man who believes in God and the Last Day to pray while having an injection until it is relieved.”"
"599","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, and Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah told us Bin Ahmad, my father told me, they said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abi Jazra, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin told us. Hazm, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, who said: We were with Aisha and her food was brought, and Al-Qasim bin Muhammad stood up to pray, and she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. God, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “He should not pray in the presence of food, nor should he defend himself from the wicked.”"
"600","Ahzaz bin Ahmad bin Hamdoun Al-Munawi told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, he said: “The Messenger of God came to us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so We brought out water for him in a bowl of water, and this man performed ablution.” “An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.” There is evidence for it from the hadith of Aisha.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 600 - According to their condition"
"601","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I used to wash in a bull.” ""from a resemblance"""
"602","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a troop, and they were struck by cold, so when they came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commanded them to wipe over the headbands and turbans.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on wiping over the turban other than this wording, and it has Witness
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 602 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"603","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin told me Saleh, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Maqil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution He was wearing a Qatari turban, so he put his hand under the turban and wiped the front of his head, but did not remove the turban.” “This hadith, even if its chain of transmission is not a condition of the Book, then it contains a strange word, which is that he wiped over part of the head, and did not wipe over the other. ""His turban""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 603 - If true, it would indicate wiping part of the head"
"604","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ghassan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdullah bin Daoud told us, and Abu Ali told us Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz, Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Nasr narrated, Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darhami narrated to us, Abdullah bin Daoud narrated to us, on the authority of Bukayr Ibn Aamir, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah Ibn Amr Ibn Jarir, that Jarir “urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over the socks” and said: “What prevents me from wiping?” I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, anointing. They said: That was only before the revelation of the Message. He said: I did not embrace Islam until after the revelation. The table. “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it with this wording that requires it.” They only agreed on the hadith of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Jarir, and it is in it. Ibrahim said: They liked the hadith of Jarir because he converted to Islam after the table was revealed, and Bukayr ibn Amir al-Bajli was a trustworthy and honorable Kufi. The hadith is collected in the trustworthy narrators of the Kufans.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 604 - Sahih and Bakir is trustworthy"
"605","Abd al-Rahman bin Hassan al-Asadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu`bah told us, and he told us Muhammad bin Jafar Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh Al-Anbari told us, Abi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs bin Omar bin Saad, heard Abu Abdullah, the client of Banu Taim bin Murrah, narrating, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, that Abdul Rahman bin Awf asked Bilal about the ablution of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “He used to go out to relieve himself, so I would bring him water and he would perform ablution and wipe over his body.” His turban and his miter.” “This is an authentic hadith, for Abu Abdullah, the client of Banu Taym, is known for its authenticity and acceptance. As for the two sheikhs, they did not narrate any mention of it.” Wiping over those who are certain”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 605 - True"
"606","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Al-Hasan told us Bin Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Bukayr bin Amir Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “He wiped over his socks,” and I said: O Messenger of God, I forgot. He said: “Rather, you forgot. This is what my Lord Almighty and Majestic has commanded me to do.” “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the paths of the hadith of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, may God be pleased with him, in the survey, and they did not narrate his statement, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is what my Lord commanded me, “and its chain of transmission is authentic.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 606 - True"
"607","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Yahya bin Muin told us, Amr bin Al-Rabi’ told us. Ibn Tariq, Yahya Ibn Ayyub reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Razin, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Yazid Ibn Abi Ziyad, he said: Yahya Sheikh said From the people of Egypt: On the authority of Ubadah ibn Nusayy, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Amara, who prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two qiblahs. He said: O Messenger of God, should I wipe over the socks? He said: “Yes.” He said: “One day.” He said: “And two days.” He said: “And three?” He said: “Yes, whatever you want.” “Ubayy ibn Amara is a well-known companion, and this is an Egyptian chain of narration. Not one of them was attributed to being injured, and Malik ibn Anas went to this. And they did not bring it out.”"
"608","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Al-Abbas told me Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi, Ahmad ibn Sayyar told us, Muhammad ibn Kathir told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Sufyan. Ibn Al-Hakam, or Al-Hakam Ibn Sufyan, said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated, he would perform ablution and wipe himself off.” “This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, but they left it out due to doubt about it, and that is not something that weakens it.” It was narrated by a group, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Sufyan, and Ibn Abi Najih followed Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir on His narration is also subject to doubt
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 608 - According to their condition"
"609","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of a man, from Thaqif, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “urinate and then sprinkle his private parts.”"
"610","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, and Abu Yahya Al-Samarqandi told us, Muhammad bin Nasr, Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, and the pronunciation is his, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Ansari, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Sharik and Jarir told us, all of them, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: Abdullah said: “We were We do not perform ablution from a place of resting place, nor do we wrap our hair or clothing.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not mention the place of birth.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 610 - They did not mention Al-Muwatta’"
"611","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrik, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Do not enter The angels are a house in which there is an image, nor a dog, nor a side.” “This is an authentic hadith. Abdullah bin Yahya is one of the trustworthy people of the Kufans, and they did not mention junub in it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 611 - Sahih and Abdullah is trustworthy"
"612","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna reported, they said: Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Maqsam, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “He should give in charity a dinar, or half a dinar.” “This is an authentic hadith. They all used Miqsam ibn Najda as evidence. As for Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, he is Abu al-Hasan Abd. Al-Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Jazari is trustworthy, trustworthy, his witness and his guide.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 612 - True"
"613","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl did not tell us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam bin Mutahir told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan Al-Jazari, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “If he gets it in the blood A dinar, and if the bleeding occurs, then half a dinar.” “This hadith was transmitted and also stopped, and we are on the basis upon which we have established that the statement is the statement of the one who supports it and connects it if it is trustworthy.”"
"614","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qattan told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Shaybah, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to command us immediately after our menstruation to cover ourselves and then He will deal with us, and which of you controls his Lord, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to control his Lord? . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording, rather they narrated it in this chapter” Hadith Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to order one of us, if she was menstruating, to We will lie together, then he will have sex with us.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 614 - According to their condition"
"615","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Amer Abd Al-Malik bin Amr Al-Aqdi told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Abd told us Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of his uncle Imran bin Talha, on the authority of His mother, Hamnah bint Jahsh, said: I was having a heavy menstrual period, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask him for a fatwa and inform him. I found it in the house of my sister Zainab bint Jahsh, and I said: O Messenger of God, I am a woman having a heavy, heavy menstruation. What you see in her is... You prevented me from praying and fasting. He said: “I prepared celery for you, for it removes the blood.” She said: It is more than that, but it is more ice-cold. The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I will command you to do two things. Which one you do is more sufficient for you than the other, and if you are strong in doing them, you know best.” The Messenger of God said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “This is only one of the attacks of Satan, so you will menstruate for six days, or seven days, according to the knowledge of God Almighty.” Glory be to Him, then wash yourself until you see that you have been cleansed and cleansed, then pray for twenty-three nights, or twenty-four nights. And the days and my fasting, for that is sufficient for you. Likewise, do every month as women menstruate, and as they purify themselves according to the times of their menstruation and purification. If you are able to delay the noon prayer and hasten the afternoon prayer, then you should wash yourself and combine the two prayers, the noon and afternoon prayers, and delay the sunset prayer and hasten the prayer. dinner, then you wash and combine the two prayers, so do my fasting, if you are able to do that.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And this I like both things.” “The two sheikhs agreed to extract the hadith about istihaadah from the hadith of Al-Zuhri and Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that Fatima bint Abi Jahsh I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it does not contain these words that are in the hadith of Hamnah bint Jahsh, and the narration of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel. Ibn Abi Talib. He is one of the nobles of Quraysh and has the most narrations, but they did not use it as evidence. Its evidence is the hadith of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of a stolen woman’s necklace, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. The hadith of Abu Aqeel Yahya bin Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Bahiya, on the authority of Aisha, and her mention in this place is lengthy.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 615 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"616","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, and Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh was under the supervision of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. She had her period for seven years, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is not menstruation, but it is a sweating, so wash yourself.”"
"617","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, and Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Umm Habiba had her menstrual period while she was under Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. Seven years, then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded her, saying: “When your menstrual period comes, give up prayer, and when it comes, wash and pray.” “The hadith of Amr bin Al-Harith and Al-Awza’i is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Rather, Muslim narrated the hadith of Sufyan bin Uyaynah And Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah followed Al-Awza’i on this narration of his, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of these words. “It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 617 - According to their condition"
"618","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, Muhammad bin Amr, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh, that she was having menstruation, so he told her The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it is menstrual blood, it is recognizably black blood. If that is the case, refrain from praying, and if the other So perform your ablution and pray, for it is only a vein.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 618 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"619","Abu Sahl bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Jafar told us, Adi bin Asim told us, Suhail bin Abi Salih told us, and he told us Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Wahb bin Baqiya told us, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Asma’ bint Umays, who said: I said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh had had her menstrual period so-and-so since so-and-so and did not pray, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Glory be to God, this is from The devil is to sit in a corner, and if she sees yellow color on the water, she should bathe once for noon and afternoon, and for sunset. The evening meal is one bath, and she bathes until dawn and performs ablution in between that.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with these words.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 619 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"620","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Abu Al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, all of them, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Umm Atiya, may God be pleased with her, said: “We used to not consider turbidity or yellowness to be anything.”"
"621","Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Umm Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Umm Atiyya - who had pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace - she said: “We used to not regard turbidity or yellowness after purification as anything.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. The mother of Al-Hudhayl is Hafsa bint Sirin, so her son’s name is Al-Hudhayl and the name of Her husband is Abd al-Rahman, and al-Hudhayl bin Abd al-Rahman narrated the chain of transmission on the authority of his mother.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 621 - According to their condition"
"622","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Yunus bin Nafi’, on the authority of Kathir ibn Ziyad Abi Sahl, who said: Massa Al-Azdiyya told me, she said: I performed Hajj and went to Umm Salamah and said: O mother Believers, Samurah ibn Jundub ordered women to perform the menstrual prayer, and she said: “They should not perform it. The woman was one of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” She remained in the postpartum prayer for forty nights, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not order her to perform the postpartum prayer. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and I do not know of its meaning other than this and I have witnessed it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 622 - True"
"623","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqashi told us, Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Uthman told us Ibn Saad Al-Qurashi, Ibn Abi Mulaika told us, he said: My aunt Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh came to Aisha and said: I am afraid of falling into Hell. I miss the prayer for the year and two years and do not pray. She said: Wait until the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes. He came and Aisha said: This is Fatima. She says such-and-such, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “Tell her to stop praying every month on the days it is recited, then to bathe every month.” One day of washing, then purification at every prayer, and to clean yourself and be cleaned, for it is only a symptomatic disease, or an attack from the devil, or a sweat. ""It was cut off."" “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it with this wording, and Othman bin Saad the writer is Basri, trustworthy, and honorable in the hadith. His hadith is collected.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 623 - No"
"624","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Musa Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Bilal Al-Ash’ari told us, Abu Shihab told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Hassan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uthman Ibn Abi Al-Aas, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A time for women in their postpartum Forty days. “This is a dear Sunnah. If this chain of transmission is transmitted from Abu Bilal, then it is authentically mursal, for Al-Hasan did not hear from Uthman ibn Abi Al-Aas, and he has a witness with a similar chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 624 - Abu Bilal Al-Ash’ari narrated it alone on the authority of Ibn Shihab. If it is safe from him, then it is an authentic mursal, as Al-Hasan did not hear from Uthman ibn Abi Al-Aas, and he has a witness."
"625","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Junaid told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Amr bin Al-Husayn told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ulatha, on the authority of Abdah bin Abi Lubaba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The postpartum woman waits forty nights, so whoever feels pure before that is pure, and if it exceeds forty then she is pure.” In the same way as a woman undergoing menstruation, she bathes and prays, but if she is overcome by blood, she performs ablution for every prayer.” “Amr ibn al-Husayn and Muhammad ibn Ulatha are not among the conditions of the two sheikhs, but I mentioned this hadith as an astonishing witness.”"
"626","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad al-Nahwi told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail al-Sulami told us, Abd al-Salam told us Ibn Muhammad al-Homsi, whose surname is Sulaym, Baqiyya Ibn al-Walid told us, Al-Aswad Ibn Tha’labah told me, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn Nasi, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Uthman, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a postpartum woman has had seven days of childbirth, then she sees that she is pure, then she should bathe. And pray.” Muslim cited Baqiyya ibn al-Walid as a martyr, and as for Al-Aswad ibn Tha’labah, he is a well-known Syrian, and the hadith is strange in this regard.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 626 - Gharib and Al-Aswad are well-known Syrians"
"627","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, On the authority of Amr ibn Bojdan, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The spoils were collected with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “O Abu Dharr, go to it.” So I went to Al-Rabdah, and I was becoming janubah, so I stayed for five or six days, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Abu Dharr So I remained silent, and he said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, Abu Dharr. Woe to your mother.” So he called a maid and she brought a cup of water, so she covered me with a dress and I covered myself. With the camel, so I took a bath and it was as if I had thrown a mountain off of me, and he said: “The good level is the ablution of a Muslim, even if it lasts for ten years, so if you find water Then let your skin touch it, for that is better.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it since we did not find a narrator for Amr bin Bojdan other than Abu Qalaba al-Jarami, and this is what I stipulated about it. It is proven that they came out like this in places in the two books.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 627 - True"
"628","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, and another man, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Qays, a servant Amr bin Al-Aas, that Amr bin Al-Aas, was with a troop, and they were struck by a severe cold the likes of which he had never seen, so he went out for the morning prayer, and he said: By God, I had a dream last night, but by God, I have never seen hail like this. Has anything like it passed over your faces? They said: No, so he washed his forearms, performed his ablution for prayer, then prayed with them. When he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he asked the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “How did you find Omar and his companions for you?” So they praised him well and said: O Messenger of God, he prayed with us while he was in a state of junub. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to Amr and asked him. So he told him about that and about the hail he had encountered, and he said: O Messenger of God, God said: {And do not kill yourselves} [An-Nisa: 29] even if I wash myself. I died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at Amr. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and what I have is that they explained it.” With the hadith of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, who
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 628 - According to their condition"
"629","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, he said: It was read to Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad while I was listening, he said: Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, we told him My father, he said: I heard Yahya bin Ayyub speaking, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, On the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, he said: I had a dream on a cold night during the Battle of Dhat al-Silsil, and I feared that if I performed ghusl I would perish, so I performed tayammum, then I prayed with my companions in the morning prayer, and they mentioned it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “O Amr, did you pray with your companions while you were in a state of ritual impurity?” So I told him about the one who prevented me from washing, and I said: I heard that God says: {And do not kill yourselves. Indeed, God is ever Merciful to you} [An-Nisa: 29] The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed and did not say anything. “This hadith of Jarir bin Hazim does not explain the hadith of Amr bin Al-Harith, which linked him to the mention of Abu Qais, for the people of Egypt are more knowledgeable about their hadith than The people of Basra"
"630","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Uthman Saeed bin Uthman Al-Tanukhi told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told me, Ata’ told us Ibn Abi Rabah, that he heard Abdullah Ibn Abbas tell that a man was wounded during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then He was afflicted with a wet dream, so he bathed and died. This reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “They killed him, God killed them. Was there no cure for the eye? The question is.” We learned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about that and he said: “If he had washed his body and left his head where the wound had been.” “It was narrated by Al-Haqal bin Ziyad, and he is the one who confirmed the companions of Al-Awza’i, and he did not mention Al-Awza’i hearing from Ata’.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 630 - According to their condition"
"631","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Ali bin Mukhlid Al-Jawhari told us, in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Abd told us Allah bin Salih, Haql bin Ziyad informed us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan informed us, Al-Hakam bin Musa informed us, Hakal narrated to us, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, he said: Ata’ said: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man suffered an injury during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, and he became impure, so he asked for a fatwa and was ordered to wash, so he washed and died. This reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “They killed him, God killed them. Was the question not the cure for the eye?” Ata’ said: I was informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked after that, and he said: “If he washed his body and left where the wounds were, that would be sufficient.”"
"632","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul Rahman bin Hassan bin Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Asadi told us, in Hamadan, Umair bin Mirdas told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Nafi’, Al-Layth Ibn Sa’d told us, on the authority of Bakr Ibn Sawadah, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: Two men went out in They traveled, and the time for prayer came, but they did not have water, so they made dry ablution on good terrain, and prayed, then they found water at the appointed time, and one of them repeated the prayer and ablution. The other did not return, then they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him. He said to the one who did not return: “You have fulfilled the Sunnah, and I suffice for you.” Your prayer.” And he said to the one who performed ablution and came back: “You will be rewarded twice.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, for Abdullah bin Nafi’ is trustworthy.” This chain of transmission was transmitted on the authority of Al-Layth, and others sent it. [P. 287]."
"633","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Milhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Amira bin Abi Najiya, on the authority of Bakr ibn Sawada, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar, and God knows best.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 632 - According to their conditions, Ibn Nafi’ is trustworthy and unique in his connection"
"634","Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ali bin Dhabyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Tayammum consists of two strokes: a stroke to the face, and a stroke to the hands up to the elbows.” The two sheikhs agreed on the hadith of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar regarding tayammum, and he did not They narrated it with this wording, and I do not know of anyone who transmitted it from Ubayd Allah, other than Ali bin Dhabyan, who is truthful, and Yahya bin Saeed, Hushaym bin Bashir and others, and Malik bin Anas narrated it on the authority of Nafi’ in Al-Muwatta’ with a wording other than this, except that a conditional statement in the sanad Al-Saduq Al-Hadith, if someone else stopped him.”"
"635","Abu Ja`far bin Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mansour, Commander of the Faithful, told us in Dar al-Mansur in Baghdad. Al-Haytham bin Khaled told us, Abu Nu`aym narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Arqam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: “We performed tayammum with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he beat us.” With our hands on the good level, then we shook our hands and wiped our faces with them, then we struck another blow on the good level, then we shook our hands, So we wiped our hands from the elbow to the palm of the hair, from the outside and inside of the hair.” “This is an explained hadith, but I mentioned it as a witness because Sulaiman ibn Arqam is not a condition of this book, and we have stipulated that something similar to it be mentioned in Evidence »"
"636","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Uqabi told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Issa Al-Madani told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, and Muhammad bin Salih told us Bin Hani, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Harun bin Abdullah told us, Shababah told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Daoud Al-Harrani, on the authority of Salem, And Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said regarding tayammum: “Two strokes: a stroke to the face, and a stroke to the hands up to “The elbows.” Suleiman bin Abi Dawud also did not narrate it, but we mentioned it in the evidence. We have narrated the meaning of this hadith on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"637","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Ezra Ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: A state of impurity has befallen me, and I have been in a state of ritual impurity. dust, and he said: “Strike like this,” and he struck the ground with his hands and wiped his face, then he struck with his hands and wiped with them up to the elbows.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 637 - True"
"638","Ali bin Hamshadh and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Uthman bin Muhammad Al-Anmati told us, Harami told us. Ibn Amara, on the authority of Ezra Ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Tayammum is done in two strokes: one stroke to the face, and a blow to the hands up to the elbows.”"
"639","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Amr bin Muhammad bin Abi Razin told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performing tayammum in a place called Murbid al-Naam while he was seeing The houses of the city. “This is an authentic hadith that was only narrated by Amr bin Muhammad bin Abi Razin, and it is authentic, and they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari and others, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 639 - Amr was the only one to narrate it, and he is truthful, and it was authenticated by Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari and others."
"640","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muhammad bin Haitham told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: “Ibn Umar performed tayammum at the head of a mile or two from Medina, so he prayed the afternoon prayer and came forward while the sun was setting.” high and he did not repeat the prayer.”"
"641","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir al-Juhani, he said: I left the Levant for Medina on Friday, and entered Medina on Friday. So I went to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said to me: “When did you put your socks on your feet?” I said: On Friday. He said: “Did you remove them?” I said: No, and he said: “You are correct in the Sunnah.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” And there is another witness on the authority of Uqba bin Amir.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 641 - According to the condition of Muslim and he has a witness"
"642","Abu Muhammad Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Isfaraini told us, Al-Hussein bin Ishaq Al-Tustari told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair, Al-Mufaddal bin Fadala told us, he said: I asked Yazid bin Abi Habib about wiping over the socks, and he said: Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told me Al-Balawi, on the authority of Ali bin Rabah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that he informed him that he came to Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, for a year. He said Uqba: I was wearing one of those thick slippers, so Omar said to me: “When did you take care of their clothing?” So I said: I wore them on Friday, and this is Friday, and he said to me: “You have followed the Sunnah.” The narration was authentic on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he did not specify a specific time in wiping over the socks. This hadith was narrated on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “With an authentic chain of narration, its narrations on the authority of the last of them are trustworthy.” However, he is quite anomalous.”"
"643","It was narrated to us by Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi, Al-Miqdam bin Dawud bin Talid Al-Ru’ayni told us, Abdul Ghaffar bin Dawud Al-Harrani, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr, and Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you performs ablution and puts on his socks, he should pray in them, and wipe over them, then do not take them off if he wishes, except in case of ritual impurity.” “This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, and Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud is trustworthy, but he does not have any narration from the people of Basra on the authority of Hammad.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 643 - According to Muslim’s condition, Abdul Ghaffar only mentioned it, and he is trustworthy, and the hadith is abnormal."
"644","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl and Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told us, saying: Ahmed bin Nasr told us, we told him Abu Nu`aym, Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba, Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shuraih bin Hani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “What is the matter with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing since it was revealed to him? Al-Furqan. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” They agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah. He said: “He came The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was a people’s turmoil and urinated while standing. It was narrated on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, he said: Omar said: “I have not been standing since I embraced Islam.” And on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Who It is impudence to urinate while standing. It was narrated, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the excuse on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he urinated while standing"
"645","Abu Imran Musa bin Saeed Al-Hanzali told us, in Hamdan, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Mahan Al-Karabisi told us, Hammad bin Ghassan told us. Al-Jafifi, Maan bin Issa told us, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “urined He stood up from a wound in his hamstring.” “This is an authentic hadith narrated alone by Hammad bin Ghassan, and all of its narrators are trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 645 - Hammad is weak by Al-Daraqutni"
"646","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rinsing his mouth and sniffing from one palm, and he did That is three times. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.” Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Shafi’i, may God have mercy on him, who said: If he combined them from one hand, then it is It is permissible, but if he separates them, he is more beloved to us.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 646 - According to their condition"
"647","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Asad bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Bakr bin Muhammad told us Al-Sayrafi, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Qubaisah told us, Sufyan told us, and Ahmad bin Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Waki’ told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabra, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “When you perform ablution, cross your fingers.” “This is a hadith that they used most of its narrators as evidence, then they did not narrate it due to the uniqueness of Asim bin Laqit bin Amir bin Sabra, on the authority of his father. By narration, and we have presented the statement regarding it and there is a witness to it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 647 - They did not take it out because Asim was alone with his father and he had a witness."
"648","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram al-Bazzar told us, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Sa`d bin Abd al-Hamid bin Ja`far told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If “You have performed ablution, then mix your fingers and toes.” “I think this Salih is the master of twins. If that is the case, then it is not a requirement of this book. Rather, I cited him as a witness.”"
"649","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Issa bin Al-Musayyab told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us Zar’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the homes of a group of people from the Ansar, but there were houses other than them that he would not come to. This was difficult for them, so they said: O Messenger of God, you come to the house of so-and-so and do not come to our house. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, there is a dog in your house.” They said that there were cats in their house, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Felines are seven.”"
"650","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Issa bin Al-Musayyab told us, and Yahya bin told me Mansour Al-Qadi, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki’ reported on the authority of Issa bin Al-Musayyab, something similar. “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it, and Issa bin Al-Musayyab alone narrated it on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, but it is truthful and has never been criticized.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 649 - Abu Dawud said he is weak, meaning Isa bin Al-Musayyab, and Abu Hatim said he is not strong."
"651","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: We were with Salman Al-Farisi on a journey and he relieved himself, so we said to him: Perform ablution until we ask you about a verse from The Qur’an, and he said: “Ask me. I have not touched it, so he recited to us what we wanted, and there was no water between us and him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not take it out to make it authentic.” It was also narrated by a group of trustworthy people, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Salman [p. 293],"
"652","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Badr Shujaa told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and he told us Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Ubayy, and Abu Muawiya told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Salman, so he mentioned it in a similar way."
"653","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ali Al-Warraq, whose nickname was Hamdan, told us, Affan told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The torment of the grave is greater than urine.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it, and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Abu Yahya al-Qatat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 653 - According to their condition, and I do not know of a reason for it and there is evidence for it"
"654","Ali bin Isa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Yahya, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who transmitted it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The general punishment of the grave is due to urine.”"
"655","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If “If one of you starts praying, let him hold his nose and then leave.” Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami, Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi and others followed him, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa. “It is valid according to their condition, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 655 - According to their condition"
"656","It was narrated to us by Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani, by Jiddi, by Nu’aym bin Hammad, by Al-Fadl bin Musa, by Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you murmurs during his prayer, let him hold his nose.” And let him leave and perform ablution.” I heard Ali bin Omar al-Daraqutni, the memorizer, saying: I heard Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i al-Sayrafi, saying: “Everyone from among the imams of the Muslims who issues a fatwa He only took it from this hadith.”"
"657","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Al-Amash told us, and Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ishaq, Bishr Ibn Musa informed us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Hasanah, he said: Amr bin Al-Aas and I set out, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us with a piece of paper in his hand, or something similar to a piece of paper. He covered himself with it and urinated. While he was sitting, I said to my friend: Haven’t you seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinate like a woman urinates? He said: So he came to us and said: “Don’t Do you know what happened to the companion of the Children of Israel? “When someone’s urine got on him, he would rub it with a scissor.” He said: “So he forbade them from doing that, and he was tortured in his grave.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 657 - According to their condition"
"658","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muawiyah told us, and Abu Bakr told me Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, and Abu Bakr bin told us Ishaq, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, all of them, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Hasnah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated while he was covered with a cloak, so they said: Do you urinate like a woman urinates? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When the Children of Israel urinated on one of them, they would cut him off with the utensils, and he forbade them from doing so.” He will be tortured in his grave.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is a condition of the two Sheikhs until it is conveyed. Zayd ibn Wahb was the only one to narrate it on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"659","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Al-Hassan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Uthman bin Saeed told us Al-Darimi, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, my father told me, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “What The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has been standing ever since the Criterion was revealed to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 659 - According to their condition"
"660","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed about Al-Muqaddam. Ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Aisha swear by God that no one saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “urinating standing up since it was revealed.” The criterion is upon him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and what I have is that when they agreed on the hadith of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Hudhayfah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to a group of people, and he urinated while standing and found the hadith of Al-Miqdam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. He opposed it, so they left it, and God knows best, and there is evidence for him from the hadith of the Meccans.”"
"661","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Muhammad bin Mahdi told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw me May God bless him and grant him peace. I was urinating standing up. He said: “O Umar, do not urinate standing up.” He said: I have not urinated standing up yet. It was narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding it."
"662","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Muammar informed us, about Ash'ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should urinate in his bath, for In general, he is obsessive. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but there is a witness to their conditions.”"
"663","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Uqba ibn Sahban, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, who said: “It was forbidden or forbidden to urinate in the bathing place.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 663 - According to their condition"
"664","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Muhammad ibn Nu’aym told me, Qutayba ibn Sa’id told me, Ismail ibn Ja’far told me, both of them, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of the cursers.” They said: What are the cursers, O Messenger? God? He said: “The one who abandons himself in the path of the Muslims and in their shadow.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he narrated it on the authority of Qutaibah, and it has a witness on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin with an authentic chain of narration, and the wording is not This and he did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 664 - Narrated by Muslim"
"665","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Muthanna told us, Kamil bin Talha told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Sirin told us, he said: He said A man told Abu Hurairah: You gave us a fatwa about everything, until it is about to give us a fatwa about the dirt. He said: Then Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about everything. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever spills his blood on a busy Muslim road, upon him will be the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind.” “Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ansari is one of those whose hadiths are collected among the Basrans, and he is very powerful in hadith.”"
"666","Ali bin Hamshadh narrated to us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Al-Muthanna bin Muadh Al-Anbari narrated to us, Muadh bin Hisham narrated to us, and Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, Muhammad bin Bashar, Abbas Al-Anbari, and Ishaq bin Mansour - Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: He informed, and the others said: He told us. - Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sargis, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should urinate in burrow
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 666 - According to their condition: “And when you sleep: extinguish the lamp, for the mouse will take the wick and burn it on the people of the household, and recline on Watering cans, brewing the drink, and closing the doors.” So it was said to Qatadah: What is disliked about urinating in the hole? He said: “These are the dwellings of the jinn.”"
"667","I heard Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari, Yahya bin Muhammad, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah, saying: He forbade urinating in The Burrow, according to the report of Abdullah bin Sarjis that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should urinate in the Burrow.” Qatada said: They are the dwellings of the jinn. “I do not refuse to say that it is the dwelling place of the jinn, because this is what Qatada said. This hadith is in accordance with the conditions of the two sheikhs, as they cited all His narrators, and perhaps someone is delusional and thinks that Qatada did not mention hearing it from Abdullah bin Sargis, and this is not unlikely, as he heard Qatada was from a group of companions from whom Asim bin Sulaiman al-Ahwal had not heard, and Muslim invoked the hadith of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarges, who lives in Basra, and God knows best.”"
"668","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin With Al-Wayh, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, saying: Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These toilets are dying, so if one of you enters the toilet, let him say: I seek refuge in God from “The abomination, the unclean, the accursed Satan.” Muslim used as evidence a hadith of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, and Al-Bukhari cited as evidence Amr ibn Marzuq, and this The hadith is disputed according to Qatada. Narrated by Saeed bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Awf Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 668 - Both of them mean this hadith and No. 669 according to the condition that it is correct"
"669","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Awf Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These crowds It is dying, so if one of you enters it, let him say, “I seek refuge in You from wickedness and evil things.” “Both hadiths are a condition of authenticity, and they did not narrate it with this wording, but rather they agreed on the hadith of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas By mentioning seeking refuge only.”"
"670","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abdullah bin Ayyub bin Zazan Al-Dair told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, they said: Hadba bin Khalid told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri - he said: And I only know him. On the authority of Al-Zuhri - on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he entered the toilet, he would put on his seal.”"
"671","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ubaid bin Abd al-Wahid told us, Ya’qub bin Ka’b al-Antaki told us, Yahya bin al-Mutawakkil al-Basri told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “wore a ring engraved with Muhammad, the Messenger of God, and when he entered the toilet he put it on.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. They only narrated the hadith about the engraving of the ring.”"
"672","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {Among them are men who love to purify themselves} [At-Tawbah: 108] He said: When this verse was revealed, he sent a Messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Uwaim bin Sa’idah, and he said: “What is this purification with which God praised you?” They said: O Prophet of God, it did not come out. There is a man among us, and not a woman who has excreted without washing his anus - or he said: his seat -, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then in this case.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim.” Salama bin Al-Fadl narrated it like this, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq. And the hadith of Abu Ayyub is his witness
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 672 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"673","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, They said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Wasil bin al-Sa’ib al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, and Ibn Surah, on the authority of his uncle Abu Ayyub, he said: They said: O Messenger of God, among these are among them men who love to purify themselves, and God loves The purified ones} [At-Tawbah: 108] He said: “They used to cleanse themselves with water, and they did not sleep the whole night.” This is the last thing that came to us from the “Book.” Purity” according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, as long as it was not included in the beginning of the Book of Prayer, a chapter on the times for prayer"
"674","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Sammak, Al-Thiqah Al-Ma’mun told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Uthman bin Omar, Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Al-Aizar, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him He asked: Which work is better? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.” I said: Then what? He said: “Jihad for the sake of God.” I said: Then what? He said: “Being kind to one’s parents.” “This is a hadith known by this word as Muhammad bin Bashar Bundar, on the authority of Uthman bin Omar, and Bundar is one of the memorizers who are well-versed and proven.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 674 - According to their condition"
"675","Ali bin Issa told us, in others, they said: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bundar told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Al-Izar, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What is the work? Better? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.” “This word was authenticated by the agreement of the two trustworthy narrators, Bundar bin Bashar and Al-Hasan bin Makram, based on their narrations on the authority of Uthman bin Omar, and he It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and there is evidence in this regard, including them.”"
"676","Abu Sa`id Ismail bin Ahmad al-Jurjani did not tell us, Muhammad bin al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Hajjaj bin al-Sha’ir told us, Ali bin Hafs told us. Al-Madaini, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Al-Izar, who said: I heard Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, who said: The owner of this house told us, and he referred to Abdullah bin Masoud went home and did not name him. He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which deed is best? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.” I said: Then what? He said: “Jihad for the sake of God.” I said: Then what? He said: “Being kind to one’s parents, even if I had sought it, it would have increased for me.” “This hadith was narrated by a group on the authority of Shu’bah, and no one mentioned this word except Hajjaj ibn al-Sha’ir, on the authority of Ali ibn Hafs, and Hajjaj. A trustworthy person, and Muslim used Ali ibn Hafs al-Madani as evidence, including:"
"677","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu`bah told us, Ubaid al-Mukhtab told me, he said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani speaking, on the authority of a man, one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.” “The man is Abdullah bin Masoud, because the narrators unanimously agree on Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, and among them”"
"678","What Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, in Egypt, Ali told us Ibn Ma'bad, Ya'qub Ibn Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Good Actions: Prayer at the beginning of its time. “This Ya’qub ibn al-Walid is a sheikh from the people of Medina who resides in Baghdad, and there is no requirement of this letter except that it is a witness on the authority of Ubayd Allah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 678 - Ya’qub is a liar, meaning Ya’qub bin Al-Walid"
"679","Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Adl, the grammarian, told me, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Ruqi told me, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah Al-Amiri, in Kinda in the Ashjaj Council, Muhammad bin Himyar Al-Homsi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar Al-Amri, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which work is best? He said: “Prayer at the beginning of its time.”
 And from there"
"680","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Salamah Mansour bin Salamah Al-Khuza’i told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar Al-Omari, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Ghanam, on the authority of his great-grandmother, Al-Dunya, on the authority of his grandmother, Umm Farwa, - she was among those who pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, She was one of the first emigrants, because she heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was asked about some actions, and he said: “Prayer for the beginning of its time.” . This is a hadith narrated by Al-Layth bin Saad, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman, Qaza bin Suwayd, and Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Ghanam. “As for the hadith of Al-Layth bin Saad”"
"681","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Ahmed bin Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Maafiri told us, in Egypt, we told him. Ali bin Abdul Rahman Allan, Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Ghanam Al-Ansari, on the authority of his grandmother, his father’s mother, Al-Dunya, on the authority of Umm Farwa, his grandmother, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something similar. I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: Abdullah narrated Ibn Umar, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Ghannam, but his brother Ubayd Allah Ibn Umar did not narrate from him"
"682","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Nadr, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not pray at its later time until May God take him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and from Al-Layth there is another chain of narration for it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 682 - According to their condition"
"683","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Qutayba bin Sa’id told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Hilal, on the authority of Ishaq bin Omar, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not pray until its later time.” Twice until God took him.” He has another witness from the hadith of Al-Waqidi, but it is not a condition of this book."
"684","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us, in Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Ali Al-Azraq told us, Muhammad bin Omar told us, Rabi’ah bin Othman, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, last a prayer until the Last Time, until God takes it.”"
"685","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, and the word for it is: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us. My father told me, Ismail told us, and he is the son of Aliya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, he said: Abu Ayoub was a conqueror and Uqba bin Amir was in charge of Egypt at that time. He delayed sunset, so Abu Ayoub came to us and said: What is this prayer, O Uqba? He said: We were busy, and he said: By God, I am only saddened by people thinking that you saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing this. I heard The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “My nation will continue to be well or on the right path as long as they do not delay sunset until it clashes with the stars.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it and it has a witness with a valid chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 685 - According to Muslim’s conditions and there is an authentic witness"
"686","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa Al-Farra told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, On the authority of Omar bin Ibrahim and Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The matter of my nation will continue to be on the right path as long as they do not delay sunset until the stars collide.”"
"687","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah told me, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mahrez is originally from Baghdadi in Fustat. Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fajr has two dawns: a dawn in which food is forbidden and prayer is permissible, and a dawn in which prayer is forbidden and it is permissible.” “Food.” This is an authentic hadith based on the two sheikhs’ stipulation of the narrators being fair, and they did not narrate it. I think I saw it from the hadith of Abdullah bin Al-Walid. On the authority of Al-Thawri, it is authenticated, and God knows best, and he has a witness with an explained wording, and its chain of transmission is authentic.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 687 - According to their condition"
"688","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hatim al-Darabardi told us, in Marw, Abdullah bin Ruh al-Madaini told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ibn Abi Dhib reported, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thuban, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fajr is two dawns: As for the dawn that is like the dawn of dawn, prayer is not permissible during it and food is not forbidden. As for the one who goes rectangular on the horizon, he makes prayer lawful and food unlawful.”"
"689","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed us, Ali bin Al-Abbas Al-Bajli informed us, about Kufa, Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, we told him Abu Asim Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid, Sufyan told us, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of what God expiates sins with, and increases “Good deeds?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult times, and waiting for prayer after prayer. Not one of you leaves his house.” So he prays with the imam, then sits and waits for the next prayer, until the angels say: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it is strange from the hadith of Al-Thawri, for I heard Abu Ali Al-Hafiz, saying: He was unique in it. Abu Asim Al-Nabil on the authority of Al-Thawri """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 689 - According to their condition"
"690","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh Al-Jallab told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Abd Al-Rahim told us Bin Sulaiman, Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Nakhi, who said: We were sitting with Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, on his behalf in the Great Mosque and Kufa on that day there was a special session, so the muezzin came to him and said: The prayer, O Commander of the Faithful, for the afternoon prayer, and he said: “Sit down,” so he sat down, then he said that again, and Ali said: “This dog teaches us the Sunnah,” so Ali got up and led us in the afternoon prayer, then we left. So we returned to the place where we were sitting, and we knelt down and as the sun set, we could see it. “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it after they used its narrations as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 690 - True"
"691","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid Al-Bayruti told us, my father told me, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Al-Najashi told me, he said: Rafi’ bin Khadij told me, he said: “We used to pray the afternoon prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we would slaughter the camels. So we divide into ten portions, then we cook and eat ripe meat before the sun sets.” “Al-Bukhari and Muslim agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Najashi, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who said: We used to pray the Maghrib prayer with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then we depart and one of us sees the location of his arrow, and he has two authentic witnesses regarding hastening the prayer, but they did not take it out. The first witness among them is"
"692","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdus Al-Ghubari told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth told me Bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, he said: I heard Bashir bin Abi Masoud, He narrated, on the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to “pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was white and high, then the man would walk until he left.” From there to Dhu al-Hulayfah, which is six miles before sunset. “They agreed on the hadith of Bashir bin Abi Masoud at the end of the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, with a different wording, and as for the second witness.”"
"693","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, and Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd. Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Abi Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hunaif, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “Gabriel led the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the House twice, and he led the noon prayer with him when the sun had set and the traps were set, then he prayed He prayed the afternoon prayer with it when everything had its shade, and he prayed the sunset prayer with it when the fasting person broke his fast, then he prayed the evening prayer with it when twilight had disappeared, then he prayed with it Fajr is when food and drink are forbidden to the fasting person, then he prays the noon prayer the next day when everything is as shaded as it was during the afternoon prayer yesterday, then He prayed the afternoon prayer with it when everything was dark, then he prayed the sunset prayer with it when the fasting person broke his fast, then he prayed the evening prayer with it for the first third of the night. Then he performed the Fajr prayer when he had passed, then he said: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you, and the time is between these two times. As for the hadith of Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad:"
"694","So Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Shaar’ani told us, Jeddy told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubayri told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Abi Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned something similar to it."
"695","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Yahya Al-Barni told us, Abu Ya’la Muhammad told us Ibn Al-Salt Al-Tawzi, Al-Walid Ibn Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman Ibn Nimr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman Bin Yazid bin Jariyah, on the authority of his uncle Mujma’ bin Jariyah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the times of prayer, so he came forward and then delayed it and said: “There is a time between them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. This Ubaidullah is Ibn Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin Abi Su’ayr Al-Athri.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 695 - According to their condition"
"696","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Usayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja’far al-Mu’adhdhin, that he heard Abu Hurairah tell that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told them “that Gabriel came to him and he led the prayer with him at two times except sunset.” He said: “He came to me and led the prayer with me at the time the sun had set, then he came to me the next day and led me in the prayer.” When the sun set, he did not change it.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, as they did not narrate it on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja’far, and I presented two witnesses to it and found He has another valid witness, according to Muslim’s condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 696 - True"
"697","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih Muhammad bin Amr told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is Gabriel teaching you.” Your religion.” He mentioned the times of prayer, then he mentioned that he prayed the Maghrib prayer when the sun set, then when he came the next day, he prayed the Maghrib prayer when it set. The sun at one time
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 697 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"698","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Amr bin Awn Al-Wasiti told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Habib Bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, he said: “I inform people of the time of this prayer, the last evening prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, prays it for a third time after the moon sets. Raqbah bin Masqala followed him, on the authority of Abu Bishr. “Thus, Raqbah and Hushaym agreed to narrate this hadith, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, and it is an authentic chain of narration. Shu`bah and Abu Awanah disagreed with them, and they said: On the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Bishr bin Thabit, on the authority of Habib bin Salem.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 698 - Its chain of transmission is authentic
 As for the hadith of Shu’bah"
"699","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Sa’id bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Shu’bah told us, about Abi Bishr, on the authority of Bishr bin Thabit, on the authority of Habib bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: “I inform people about the time for the evening prayer.” The Hereafter, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray it for the third or fourth time after the moon had fallen.” - Shu’bah doubted -
 As for the hadith of Abu Awanah"
"700","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Abu Al-Fadl told us Awanah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Bishr ibn Thabit, on the authority of Habib ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Bashir, he said: “Indeed, I will inform people of the time This prayer is the last evening prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray it for the third time when the moon was falling.”"
"701","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i narrated to us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, they said: Abbad bin Abbad told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Harith Al-Ansari, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, he said: “I was praying the noon prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I would take a handful of pebbles to cool in my palm and place them on my forehead, prostrating.” Because of the intense heat.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 701 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"702","Al-Hussein bin Abdullah Al-Qattan told us, Abdul Salam bin Abdul Hamid told us, Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Najashi, he said: I heard Rafi’ Ibn Khadij said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite, that he delays the afternoon prayer until the sun is hot? Al-Baqarah (al-Baqarah) prayed. “Muslim narrated the hadith of Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “That is the prayer of the hypocrite, one of them sitting. Even when the sun turns yellow.” Al-Hadith"
"703","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Asim Ibn Umar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: “He was two men farthest away from the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He handed over a house to Abu Lubabah bin Abdul-Mundhir and his family in Quba, and Abu Abbas bin Jabr and his residence in Bani Haritha, and they were They pray the afternoon prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then they go to their people, and they did not pray so that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hastened it.” . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 703 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"704","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari and Abu Muhammad Al-Hasan bin Al-Halim Al-Maruzian informed us of Marw, saying: Abu Al-Mujih told us. Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told us, Abdan bin Othman informed us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Al-Hussein informed us, he told me Wahb bin Kaysan, Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, he said: “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sun had passed the zenith, and he said: Get up. O Muhammad, he prayed the noon prayer, so he stood up and prayed the noon prayer when the sun had passed the zenith, then he stayed until the man’s appearance for the afternoon prayer was the same as it was, so he came and said: Get up, O Muhammad prayed the afternoon prayer, so he stood up and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he stayed until the sun had set, and he said: Get up and pray the sunset prayer, so he stood up and prayed it when the sun had set as well. Then he stayed until twilight had passed, and he came to him and said: Get up and pray the evening prayer. So he stood up and prayed it, then he came to him when the dawn broke and said: Get up, oh. Muhammad prayed, so he stood up and prayed the dawn prayer, then he came to him the next day when the man’s face was like him, and he said: Get up, O Muhammad, and pray the noon prayer, so he stood up and prayed the noon prayer. Then he came to him when the man’s beauty was twice that of his, and he said: Get up, O Muhammad, and pray the afternoon prayer. So he got up and prayed the afternoon prayer, then sunset came to him when the sun had set. At one point he did not stop, so he said: Get up and pray the Maghrib prayer. Then he prayed the Maghrib prayer, then the evening prayer came when the first third of the night had passed. He said: Get up and pray the evening prayer, then the morning came to him when he was very late, so he said: Get up and pray the morning prayer, then, he said: There is a period of time between these two. This is an authentic and well-known hadith from the hadith of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, and the two sheikhs did not narrate it due to the problem of the smaller hadith of Al-Hussein bin Ali. Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Mawwal and others narrated on his authority.” Abu Muhammad Al-Hassan bin Abi Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Uqaili told us, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather Musa bin Abdullah bin Al-Hasan, My father and more than one of our household spoke to me, saying: “Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Al-Hussein was the most similar of Ali bin Al-Hussein’s sons to him in his deification.” And worship.” Al-Hakim said: “This hadith has two witnesses, like its words, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah. As for the first witness.”"
"705","So Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Sawwaf told us, Amr bin Bishr told us Al-Harithi, Burd bin Sinan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he taught him the prayer, so he followed the text with the same hadith as the hadith of Wahb ibn Kaysan, “and as for the second witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 704 - Sahih Mashhour"
"706","So Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Al-Majishun, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Gabriel made me feel safe in Mecca twice.” - So he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner -. “This Abd al-Karim is undoubtedly Ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, and I only cited him as a witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 706 - Abdul Karim Wah"
"707","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman bin Bilal told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith, and Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and led the prayers with him for two times, except Morocco. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has evidence on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri and Abdul-Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith. With its length, Sulaiman bin Bilal summarized the benefit of the hadith with this wording. As for Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith, he is the son of Abdullah bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah Al-Makhzoumi is one of the nobles of Quraysh and is accepted in the narration, and Hakim bin Hakim is Ibn Abbad bin Hanif. Al-Ansari, both of whom are civilians.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 707 - True
 As for the hadith of Al-Thawri"
"708","So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad told us Al-Anbari, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Hani told us, Sahl bin Mihran Al-Daqqaq told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Sawar bin Dawud Abu Hamza, Amr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tell the boys to pray.” for seven years, and beat them for it within ten years, and separate them into their beds.” I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri, saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in, saying: Amr bin Shuaib Trust. Al-Hakim said: “And they only said about this for the sake of sending, for it is Amr bin Shuaib bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr, and Shuaib did not listen.” From his grandfather, Abdullah bin Amr. I heard Professor Abu Al-Walid saying: I heard Al-Hasan bin Sufyan saying: I heard Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanzali saying: If the narrator is On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, trustworthy, he is like Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both.
 Among the chapters on the call to prayer and the iqama"
"709","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Muhammad bin Issa Al-Tarsusi told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Yahya told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us, Abdullah bin Khayran told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ishaq Abi Nasr Al-Darabardi, Bamru, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told me, my father told me about Shu’bah, and Abu told us Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh said: Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad, who is the son of Ja`far, told us by Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Madani, on the authority of Muslim, Abu al-Muthanna al-Qaari, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: “The call to prayer was in the era of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, twice, and the iqama once, except that he says: The prayer has been established twice, so if we hear We performed ablution and then went out to pray.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. This Abu Ja`far is Umayr bin Yazid bin Habib Al-Khutmi. It was narrated on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab and Ammarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, and Sufyan al-Thawri, Shu`bah, and Hammad ibn Thabit narrated on his authority. Salamah and other imams of the Muslims.” As for Abu Al-Muthanna, the reciter, he is one of Nafi’ bin Abi Nu’aym’s teachers, and his name is Muslim bin Al-Muthanna. Ismail bin Abi narrated from him. Khaled, Suleiman Al-Taymi, and other followers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 709 - True"
"710","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Abdul Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commanded Bilal to recite the call to prayer and make the iqamat sufficient.” This A hadith that was transmitted by the imam of the people of hadith and the approved narrators without any defence. He was followed by the trustworthy Al-Ma’mun Qutaybah bin Sa’id.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 710 - It is according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs"
"711","As Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Al-Khidr Al-Shafi’i told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Harawi told us, they said: Abu Ali Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali, Al-Hafiz Al-Balkhi, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “commanded Bilal to recite the call to prayer at the end of the call, and to make the Iqamat Witr.” “The two sheikhs did not give this context, and it is valid according to their condition.”"
"712","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i told us, Abu Hazim, that Sahl bin Saad told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are two things that are not rejected or are rarely rejected: supplication when The call, and at the time of battle when they join one another.” This is a hadith that is unique to Musa bin Ya’qub.” It may be narrated on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Hazim, and Musa bin Yaqoub. Among those about whom uniqueness is found, and he has witnesses, including the hadith of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas, the hadith of Muawiyah bin Qurrah, and the hadith of Yazid bin Ubai Maryam, on the authority of Anas
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 712 - It was unique to Moses and has evidence"
"713","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Munqidh Al-Khawlani told us, in Egypt, Idris bin Yahya told me, Al-Fadl told us Ibn Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Humaid Al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplication is answered between the call.”"
"714","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Al-Qasim bin Maan told us. Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Kathir, the servant of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me to say At the sunset call to prayer: “O God, this is the approach of your night, the end of your day, and the sounds of your supplications, so forgive me.” “This is an authentic hadith, and it was not narrated by Al-Qasim bin Ma’an bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, among the nobles.” The Kufans are trustworthy among those whose hadiths are collected, and I did not write it except on the authority of our Sheikh Abi Abdullah, may God have mercy on him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 714 - True"
"715","Ahmed bin Salman al-Faqih informed us, in Baghdad, of a reading by Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad, and I was listening. Sahl bin Hammad and Abu Rabia, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Affan, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Saeed bin Ayas Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas that He said: O Messenger of God, make me the imam of my people. He said: You are their imam, and follow the example of the weakest of them, and take a muezzin whose call to prayer is not taken. A reward” on the condition of a Muslim, and they did not pay it."
"716","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani told me, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told me, and Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri told me, Musaddad bin Qattan, they said: Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ubaida bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i Sa’id bin Tariq, on many authority Ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Al-Aswad Ibn Yazid, that Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “The prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was It was three feet tall, and in the winter five to seven feet.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Abu Malik al-Ashja’i in al-Saif and Kathir ibn Mudarik as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 716 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"717","Ali bin Issa told us, Abu Mansour told us, Yahya bin Ahmad bin Ziyad told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hushaym told us, Dawud bin Abi told us Hind, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Wahb bin Baqiyya told us, Khalid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Fadalah, on the authority of his father, he said: He taught me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of the things he taught me was “memorize the five daily prayers.” So I said: These are hours when I have work, so tell me something. If I do it, it is sufficient for me. He said: “Keep the two eras.” And it was not our language, so I said: What are the two eras? He said: “Prayer before sunrise, and prayer before sunset.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Abdullah is Ibn Fadalah bin Ubaid, and two hadiths were narrated from him in the Sahih.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 717 - According to Muslim’s condition
 A chapter on the virtue of the five daily prayers"
"718","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Abu al-Rabi` ibn Rishdin told us, and Abu Al-Tahir, they said: Abdullah bin Wahb informed me, Makhramah bin Bukayr told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard Saad and some of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There were two men who were brothers during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them was better than the other, so the one who was the better of them died, then the other lived for forty days after him, then he died, so they mentioned to the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave priority to the first over the other, so he said: “Wasn’t the other praying?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, and there was nothing wrong with him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How do you know what his prayers reached? The example of prayer is like a flowing river at the door of a man, a sweet flood breaking into it five times every day. What do you see remaining of his dirt? You do not know. What did his prayer reach? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. They did not narrate Makhramah bin Bukair, and the reason for it is that a group of the people of Egypt They mentioned that he did not hear from his father because of his young age, and some of them confirmed that he heard it from him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 718 - True"
"719","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith bin Abi Hilal told him that Naim Al-Mujmar told him that Suhayb was the client of the A’tawaris, told him that he heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah narrate on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he sat on the pulpit, then said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul” three times. Then he remained silent, and each of us began to cry sadly to the right of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then he said: “There is no servant who performs the five daily prayers. And he fasts Ramadan and avoids the seven great sins, except that the gates of Paradise will be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection, to the point that they will clap. Then he recites {Indeed “Avoid the great things that you are forbidden. We will remit your evil deeds from you” (An-Nisa: 31). This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and what I have is that they neglected it in order to mention Suhaib, the client of the Atawaris, among Naim bin Abd. “God and Abu Hurairah have agreed on the authenticity of Nu’aym’s narration on the authority of the Companions, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 719 - True"
"720","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Salamah bin Abdullah told us, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahmi told us, Nuh bin Qays told us, on the authority of his brother Khaled bin Qais, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, said: A man said: O Messenger of God, how many prayers has God made obligatory for His servants to perform? He said: “Five prayers.” He asked: Was there anything before or after them? He said: “God has made five prayers obligatory upon His servants,” so the man swore by God that he would not add more to them nor take away from them, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed He who speaks the truth will enter Paradise.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and Muslim narrated it in the Sahih with three sources with this chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 720 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"721","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Abd Al-Malik bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who transmitted it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “When your children reach seven years of age, separate their bedding. And when they reach ten years of age, encourage them to pray.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He used Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi’ ibn Sabra as evidence, on the authority of his fathers, then not one of them narrated it. This hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 721 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"722","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Salih and Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Yaqoub told us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani told us, Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, that he said: O Messenger of God, make me The imam of my people, he said: “You are their imam, follow the example of the weakest among them, and appoint a muezzin who does not take any reward for calling to prayer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s condition, and they did not narrate it like this. Rather, Muslim narrated the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Uthman Ibn Abi Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you lead a people” - Hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 722 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"723","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli told us, and Abu Ja’far Muhammad told us Bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaibani, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail told us, they said: We told us: Israel, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: “Bilal used to give the call to prayer and then give a pause, and when he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He went out and performed the prayer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Rather, Muslim mentioned the hadith of Zuhayr, on the authority of Simak: “Bilal used to give the call to prayer when you refuted The sun
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 723 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"724","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told us, and Dawud bin Rashid told us, they said: We told us: Al-Walid bin Muslim, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Masoud Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib Radi On his authority, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the mosque when prayer was being held, and when he saw them for a short time, he would sit down and pray. He saw them all together and prayed.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and this is Masoud, Abu Al-Hakam Al-Zarqi.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 724 - According to their condition"
"725","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation in the month of Rajab in the year three hundred and ninety-four. Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us and the wording. To him, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: I saw Bilal giving the call to prayer and turning and following his mouth here, here, there, with his two fingers in his ears, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in A red dome from Adam, so Bilal came out in front of him with the goat, and placed it on the foot, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed to it, passing between His hands are the dog and the donkey, and he is wearing a red suit, as if I am looking at the shine of his legs."
"726","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Qattan told us, in Baghdad, Ali bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Al-Shawareb told us, narrated to us Ibrahim bin Bashar, Ibrahim bin Utbah told us, on the authority of Al-Thawri, and Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Aun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descending with Al-Abtah, and he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Malik ibn Mughal and Umar ibn Abi Zaida, on the authority of Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, in a narration of His revelation, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is the most basic, except that they did not mention inserting the finger into the ears or turning around during the call to prayer, and it is It is authentic according to all of their conditions, and they are both Sunnah Masnunun."
"727","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah Al-Adl told us about Marwa, Yahya bin Sasawayh told us, Abdul Karim bin Muhammad Al-Sukkari told us, He said: I heard Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq saying: “When Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak saw the muezzin not putting his fingers in his ears, he would shout. With it, I breathed with Kush, I breathed with Kush.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 727 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"728","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Abdi told us, Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad told us, Al-Hasan told us Ibn Sufyan and Muhammad Ibn Naim, they said: Qutaibah told us, Al-Layth Ibn Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qais Al-Madaini, on the authority of Amer. Ibn Saad, on the authority of Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he hears the muezzin: And I bear witness that no There is no god but God alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I am satisfied with God as Lord and with Muhammad as Prophet, and with Islam as religion. He is forgiven. “It is his fault.” It is authentic, but they did not narrate it. Al-Hakam bin Abdullah is the brother of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Qais bin Makhramah Al-Qurashi, and he is proven superior to Ali. Ibn Abbas Al-Homsi """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 728 - True"
"729","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Affan told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad told us Bin Amr bin Jafar, Abd al-Wahid bin Ghayath narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you hears the call and the vessel is in his hand, he should not put it down until he has relieved himself from it.” In the hadith of Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, something similar. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 729 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"730","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abdullah bin Daoud Al-Khuraibi told us, Al-Walid bin All, on the authority of Laila bint Malik, and Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Ansari, on the authority of Umm Waraqah al-Ansariyya, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted her and said: “Go with us to the martyr and we will visit her.” He ordered that the call to prayer be given to her and that the prayer be performed, and that she lead the people of her house in the religious duties. “A Muslim has cited al-Walid ibn Juma’ as evidence, and this is a strange Sunnah. I do not know of a hadith on the subject with a chain of transmission other than this.” We have narrated “on the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she used to give the call to prayer, perform the iqama, and lead women in prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 730 - Muslim protested against Al-Walid"
"731","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Asam told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Ataridi told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, that she used to “call to prayer, perform the iqama, lead women in prayer, and stand among them.”"
"732","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ali bin Hammad bin Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Munim bin Naim Al-Riyahi, Amr bin Faid Al-Asawari told us, Yahya bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Bilal: “When you announce the call to prayer, proceed with your call to prayer, and when you perform the iqama, go down, and put an amount of space between your call to prayer and your iqama.” When the eater finishes his food, the drinker finishes his drink, and the one who squeezes the juice when he enters to relieve himself.” “This is a hadith whose chain of transmission has no one who is challenged except Amr bin Faid and the rest are the sheikhs of Basra, and this is a strange Sunnah that I do not know about.” with a chain of transmission other than this, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 732 - Al-Daraqutni Amr bin Faid Matrouk said"
"733","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, and Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hassan told me Al-Asadi, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, They said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr. He said: I heard Abu al-Malih, narrating, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “When he heard the muezzin, he would say: ‘As he says until he is silent’.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and it has a witness with an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"734","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Sahl bin Othman Al-Askari told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the muezzin, he would say: “And I and I.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 734 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"735","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, about Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ali bin Khalid Al-Duwaili, that he told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. Then Bilal stood up and called out, and when he remained silent, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says something like this with certainty will enter Paradise.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 735 - True"
"736","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Awdi told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abd told us Allah bin Salih Al-Masry, Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever calls the call to prayer for twelve years, Paradise is guaranteed for him, and sixty good deeds are recorded for him for calling the call to prayer each time, and thirty good deeds for his standing.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and it has evidence from the hadith of Abdullah bin Lahi’ah, and Muslim cited it, may God have mercy on him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 736 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"737","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Abu Al-Tahir and Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever gives permission Twelve years, Paradise was guaranteed for him, and sixty good deeds were written for him for every call to prayer and thirty good deeds for every iqamat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 737 - Cited by Muslim"
"738","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would not call to prayer for any of the prayers while traveling, and would not perform the prayer except for the morning prayer. For he used to give the call to prayer and perform the iqaamah.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Muslim used Abdul-Aziz bin Muhammad as evidence, and Al-Bukhari used Nu’aym bin Hammad as evidence, and the famous one Ibn Umar did it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 738 - Nu’aym bin Hammad narrated it on his authority, so he raised it and added except for the dawn, for he calls the call to prayer and establishes the iqama."
"739","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Asbahani told us, Mahrez told us Ibn Salamah Al-Adni, Abdul-Aziz Ibn Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar “would not give the call to prayer while traveling, nor would he stay in... “Some of his prayers”"
"740","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Affan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Amr bin Hafs told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ghayath told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, Hammad said: Ammar ibn Abi Ammar told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he hears “One of you is calling, and the vessel is in his hand, but he does not put it down until he has fulfilled his need from it.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"741","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Ali Al-Isfaraini told us, Abu Yusuf Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Wasiti told us, Shuaib bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Between the east and the west is a qibla.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Shuaib bin Ayyub is trustworthy and has transmitted it.” It was narrated by Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Muhabir, who is trustworthy, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, with a chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 741 - According to their condition"
"742","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Abd informed us Al-Rahman bin Muhabir, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Between the east and the west is a qibla.” “This is an authentic hadith that was authenticated by a group of Abdullah bin Omar.”"
"743","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Kharraz told us, Dawud bin Amr Al-Dhabi told us, Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Wasiti told us, Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, or on a journey, when clouds shaded us, and we were confused. So we disagreed about the qiblah, and each one of us prayed separately, and each one of us made a line between his hands so that we would know our places, so we mentioned that to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He did not order us to repeat it, but he said: “Your prayer is sufficient.” “This is a hadith whose narrators are relied upon, all of them except Muhammad bin Salem, for I do not know of him with justice or accuracy. I have studied the book of the two Sheikhs and I did not... They bring up something in this section.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 743 - He means Muhammad bin Salem Abu Sahl, and he is weak
 From the book of Imamate and congregational prayer"
"744","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Muammar told us, and Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Harami bin Hafs told us, saying: Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed Al-Maqbari told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, saying: He said: Abu Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If one of you performs ablution in his house and then comes to the mosque, he should be in prayer until he returns, so he should not say like this.” He interlaced his fingers. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Muhammad bin Ajlan followed him on the authority of Al-Maqbari. It is valid according to the condition of a Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 744 - According to their condition"
"745","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, they said: Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, Sa’id told us, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ka’b ibn Ujrah: “When you perform ablution and then enter the mosque, do not interlock your fingers.” It was narrated by Sharik bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, so they misunderstood its chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 745 - Sharik narrated it on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, so Sharik misunderstood it."
"746","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Ezra told us, Abu Ghassan told us, a partner told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you are in the mosque, do not cross your fingers “Thus” means tying it up"
"747","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Bakr Abdul-Kabir bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, Al-Dahhak told us Ibn Uthman, Sa`id al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you enters the mosque, let him pray.” upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O God, save me from the accursed Satan. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 747 - According to their condition"
"748","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl al-Dabbas informed us, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid al-Makki told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubayri, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father Saad said that a man came to pray while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading us in prayer, so he said: When he finished the line: Oh God, give me the best of what You give Your servants. The righteous. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he said: “Who was speaking above?” The man said: I am, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then your horse is hamstrung and you are martyred in the path of God.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 748 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"749","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, about Ata Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered into prayer, he would say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan.” He said: “His whisper: death, and his breath: poetry. And the word “pride” means “pride.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and Al-Bukhari cited Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 749 - Sahih, and Al-Bukhari cited Ata’"
"750","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Ishaq bin Salih Al-Wazzan told us, Abd told us Allah bin Amr bin Hassan, Sharik told us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” “Al-Bukhari cited as evidence this man, who was the snub-nosed Ibn Ajlan, and Muslim cited a partner as evidence. This is an authentic chain of narration and has no defect. And they did not take it out.”"
"751","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani told us, . . . . . . . . “This is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 750 - It is authentic and has no defect"
"752","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa’id, told us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Dhib, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Mahran, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The farthest, the farther from the mosque, the greater the reward.” “This is an authentic hadith, its narrators were Medinans, and Yahya bin Saeed is the imam in criticizing men, and they did not narrate it since it was not narrated otherwise than this.” Attribution
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 752 - True"
"753","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Ismail ibn Qutaibah informed us, Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, Abu Muawiyah informed us, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Prayer in congregation It is equivalent to twenty-five prayers, so if he prays it in the desert and completes its bowing and prostration, it amounts to fifty prayers.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They agreed on the proof based on the narrations of Hilal bin Abi Hilal, and it is said: Ibn Abi Maymunah, and it is said: Ibn Ali, and it is said: Ibn Usama, and they are all one.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 753 - According to their condition"
"754","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Abu Ismat Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil al-Bukhari told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah Al-Qanabi, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Tahla, on the authority of Muhsin bin Ali, on the authority of Awf bin Al-Harith, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then goes and finds the people having prayed, God Almighty will give him a reward similar to Whoever prays it and attends it, that will not detract from their rewards at all.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 754 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"755","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin told us Hawshab, Habib bin Abi Thabit told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not prevent your women from going to mosques. “And their homes are better for them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They all cited Al-Awwam ibn Hawshab as evidence, and Habib’s hearing from Ibn Umar was authentic, but they did not narrate “Therein will be more” and “their homes will be better for them” and “witness thereto”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 755 - According to their condition"
"756","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr told us Ibn Al-Harith, that Darraj Abu Al-Samh told him, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, the client of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “The best mosques for women are the corners of their homes.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 756 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"757","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Asbahani told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muwarriq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “A woman’s prayer in her home is better than her prayer in her room, and her prayer in her bedroom is better than her prayer in her home.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and they all cited as evidence Al-Muwarriq ibn Mushmurj al-Ijli.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 757 - According to their condition"
"758","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, in Marw, Abu Bakr bin Abi Khaythamah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man praying alone, and he said: “Don’t A man gives alms to this man and prays with him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Suleiman the Black. This is Suleiman bin Suhaim. Muslim used it as evidence, and my father Al-Mutawakkil, and this hadith is the basis for performing the congregational prayer in mosques twice.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 758 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"759","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, and he told me Ismail bin Ahmad Al-Tajer, and the pronunciation for him, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asqalani told us, Harmala bin Yahya told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he told me Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Abu Ali al-Hamdani, who said: I heard Uqba bin Amir al-Juhani, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Whoever leads a people and the time is right for him and for them, and whoever diminishes anything from that, it is on him and not on them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 759 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"760","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, Hudhayfah led the people in Medina in a shop, so Abu Masoud took his shirt and pulled it together. When he finished his prayer, he said: “Did you not know? That they were forbidding that? - Or he said: Did you not know that this was forbidden? “He said: Yes, I mentioned it when you extended it to me.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 760 - According to their condition"
"761","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Zakaria bin Yahya told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Hammam, he said: Hudhayfah led the people in prayer in Al-Mada’in and went to a shop, so Abu Masoud took his bundle of clothes, stretched it out, and came back. He finished the prayer. Abu Masoud said to him: “Did you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the imam to stand and the people to remain behind him?” He said: Why did you think that I answered you when you extended it to me?"
"762","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muhammad bin Jasham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Bakr bin told us Ishaq Al-Faqih, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani bin Urwa Al-Muradi, on the authority of Abd Al-Hamid bin Mahmoud said: We prayed behind one of the princes, but the people were forced to pray between two pillars. When we prayed, Anas bin Malik said: “We used to fear this during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 762 - True"
"763","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Khalil Al-Asbahani told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, and Abu Bakr told us Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzaki narrated among others, they said: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, Ali bin Hajar narrated to us, they said: Ali bin Mushar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abi Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in His Almighty saying, “Indeed, the Fajr Qur’an will be witnessed” [Al-Isra: 78] He said: “The angels of the night will witness it, and the angels of the day will gather there.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 763 - Both of them are trustworthy"
"764","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, Yahya bin Saeed, Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, and Abu Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Jaruudi told us, Bakr told us Ibn Khalaf, narrated by Abdul Wahhab Al-Thaqafi, said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed saying: I heard Nafi’, narrating, that Abdullah bin Omar was saying: “When we missed a person during the evening and morning prayers, we would have a bad opinion of him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 764 - According to their condition"
"765","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr Al-Azdi told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, Al-Sa'ib bin Hubaysh Al-Kala'i narrated to us, on the authority of Ma'dan bin Abi Talha Al-Yamari, who said: Abu Al-Darda' said: Where is your residence? He said: A village without Hummus. He said: Abu Darda’ I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There are not three people in a village, not a single Bedouin. Prayer will be performed among them unless Satan overpowers them, in which case you must pray in congregation, for the wolf only eats from the straying sheep.” “This is a truthful hadith whose narrators bear witness to what was mentioned above. It is agreed upon to use its narrations as evidence, except for Al-Sa’ib ibn Hubaysh, who is known from the school of thought. In addition, he only narrates from trustworthy people.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 765 - It is an additional doctrine that it only narrates from trustworthy people"
"766","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abu Ashana, He heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, speaking, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “If a man purifies himself and then passes to If a person attends to prayer, its scribe, or his scribes, record for him ten good deeds for every step he takes to the mosque, and the one who is sitting pays attention to prayer. Like an obedient woman, and he is recorded as one of those who pray from the time he leaves his house until he returns.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 766 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"767","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yaqoub, On the authority of Qais bin Rafi’ al-Qaisi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that he passed by Muadh bin Jabal while he was sitting on He was pointing at his door with his hand as if he was talking to himself, so Abdullah said to him: What is the matter with you, Abu Abdul Rahman, are you talking to yourself? He said: Why would the enemy of God want to distract me from words I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Do not suffer the burden of human sacrifice. She goes out to the mosque and speaks, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever strives in the path of God is a guarantor of God, and whoever He sat at home and did not speak ill of anyone, he was responsible for God, and whoever visited a sick person was responsible for God, and whoever went to the mosque in the morning or went was responsible. “A guarantor of God, and whoever comes to an imam and rebukes him is a guarantor of God. The enemy of God wants to expel me from my house to the assembly.” “This is a hadith narrated by trustworthy Egyptians, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 767 - Its narrators are trustworthy"
"768","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad Al-Basri told us, Yahya bin Al-Harith Al-Shirazi reported, and he was trustworthy, and Abdullah bin Dawud praised him. He said: Zuhair bin Muhammad Al-Tamimi told us, and Abu Ghassan Al-Madani, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad Al-Sa’idi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give good news to those who walk in oppression to The mosques will be fully illuminated on the Day of Resurrection.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it has evidence in an unknown narration, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 768 - According to their condition"
"769","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ayyub narrated, Dawud bin Sulayman bin Muslim narrated, my father narrated, on the authority of Thabit Ibn Aslam Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Give good news to those walking in the darkness of the night to the mosques of full light on the Day of Resurrection »"
"770","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith told you, Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Asbagh bin Al-Faraj told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, Amr told me Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj, narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see “The man frequents the mosque, so bear witness over him of faith.” God Almighty said: “The mosques of God are inhabited only by he who believes in God and the Last Day.” [Al-Tawbah: 18] “.” This is a translation by the Egyptians, and they did not dispute its authenticity and the truthfulness of its narrators, except that my authentic sheikh did not narrate it, and I quoted the statement in “His health in the foregoing.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 770 - A cyclist who does many evil deeds"
"771","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abu Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “None of you should set foot in mosques.” For prayer, God should shake hands with him from wherever he leaves his house, just as the family of the absent person should shake hands with their absent person when he comes to them. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Al-Layth bin Sa’d disagreed with Ibn Abi Dhi’b, and he narrated it on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yassar, that he heard Abu Hurairah says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “None of you has performed ablution and performed his ablution well and did it first, then he comes to the mosque without wanting to “Except for praying therein, unless God rejoices over it just as the family of an absent person rejoices over their absent person.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 771 - According to their condition"
"772","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shakir told us, Affan told us, Wahib told us, Abd al-Rahman bin told us Harmala, and Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdus Al-Ghazi told us, and the pronunciation for it, Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ahmad bin Saleh Al-Masry, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Hamdani, I heard Uqba bin Amir saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever leads the people and the time is right, it is for him and for them, and whoever lacks Anything of that is upon him or against them.” “This is an authentic hadith. Muslim cited Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala as evidence, and al-Bukhari cited Yahya ibn Ayyub as evidence, then they did not narrate it.”"
"773","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli told us, Israel told us about fish, On the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, he said: “The muezzin of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to give the call to prayer and then delay, and when he saw that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had come.” He took up residence.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 773 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"774","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Harmala told us, Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarraj told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “Whoever joins a row, God will bless him, and whoever breaks a row, God will cut him off.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 774 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"775","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid told me, on the authority of Othman Ibn Urwah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God and His angels send blessings upon those They pray in rows.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 775 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"776","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman Al-Adami told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Sahl bin Hammad told us, Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, about Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, said: “The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he asks forgiveness for the front row three times, and once for the second.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they agreed to use as evidence the narration of a non-Companion, based on what I mentioned above from the individuals of the Followers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 776 - True according to both conditions"
"777","Abu Al-Hasan Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad Al-Balkhi the merchant told me, Saeed bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam told me, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on the pulpit, saying to the people: “If one of you enters… The mosque and the people are kneeling, so let him kneel when he enters, then let him continue bowing until he enters the row, for that is the Sunnah.” Ataa said: I saw him do that. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 777 - According to their condition"
"778","Ali bin Issa Al-Janzi told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Muqaddami told us, Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Sadusi told us, Suleiman bin Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, said: While I was in Medina in the mosque, in the front row, I was standing praying, and a man grabbed me. Behind me was Jabdha, so he bowed down to me and took my place, saying: By God, I did not understand my prayer. When he left, he saw Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and he said: “O boy, do not May God displease you. This is the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to us to follow it. Then he faced the Qiblah. Then he said: “The people of the contract perished - three times - By the Lord of the Kaaba, then he said: “By God, I am not saddened by them, but I am saddened by what they have gone astray.” He said: I said: Who do you mean by this? He said: “The princes.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. He cited Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Sadoosi as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 778 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"779","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Hanthali told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Bakr, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the imam says: God Greater, so say: God is great. Then when he says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Our Lord, and to You be praise. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording, but it contains an important Sunnah, which is for the person being led to stand until the imam says “Allahu Akbar.” And do not say “Allahu Akbar” with it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 779 - According to their condition"
"780","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Abu al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad told us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told us, Muhammad told us Bin Shazan, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, they said: Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Samurah bin Jundub told us, And Imran bin Husayn, they remembered, and Samurah bin Jundub narrated that he memorized two silences from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “One silence when he said the greatest. And a silence if he finished reciting it when he bowed. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say “Allahu Akbar” he would be silent between saying “Allahu Akbar” and reciting it, and the hadith of Samurah does not make anyone imagine that Al-Hasan He did not hear from Samurah, for he heard from him and he has a witness with an authentic chain of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 780 - According to their condition"
"781","Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf bin Ya’qub told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told us, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Sam’an, he said: Abu Hurairah came to us in the Mosque of Banu Zurayk and said: Three times were the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He does them and people leave them. “He raises his hands until they are above his ears, and remains silent after reciting for a while, asking God for His bounty.”"
"782","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, Amara bin al-Qaqa’ told us, Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir told us, Abu Hurairah told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “When he got up the second time, he supplicated for the supplication, praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, and did not remain silent.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 782 - According to their condition"
"783","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid told me, Yahya bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Zaid Abi Attab, and Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If You came while we were prostrating, so prostrate and do not regard it as anything, and whoever performs one rak’ah has performed the prayer.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not narrated by Yahya bin Abi Sulaiman, one of the trustworthy Egyptians.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 783 - True"
"784","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Abi Ayyub told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Abdullah bin Farrukh, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was the easiest of people to perform a complete prayer.” He said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would stand up when he said the salutation. Then I prayed with Abu Bakr, and when he said the salutation he would stand in his place.” As if he was standing up from his knees.” “This is an authentic hadith. Its narrators were other than Abdullah bin Farroukh, as they did not narrate it due to any harm in it. This is a used Sunnah that I have not memorized.” It has a chain of transmission other than this, and the hadith of Hind bint Al-Harith, on the authority of Umm Salamah: Women during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were It is written as Qom. It was included by Al-Bukhari."
"785","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi told us, Surayj bin Al-Numan told us, Abd Al-Hamid bin Suleiman told us, On the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Saad, he said: I used to see him presenting young men from his people and they would lead the prayer with him, so I said: You are the companion of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is a credit to you, and you are the first to lead these boys, so they pray for you. Will you not come forward and pray for your people? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Imam is a guarantor, so if he completes it, it belongs to him and to them, and if it falls short, it goes to him or to them, so no “I want to bear that.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 785 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"786","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Abu Hisham Al-Rifai told us, Abu Khaled told us Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah Al-Nakhai, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Stand together in the row, so that the children of the small children do not separate you.” I said: O Messenger of God, what are the children of the small children? He said: “Black sheep shall be found in the land of Yemen.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 786 - According to their condition"
"787","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Part of the good prayer is standing in line.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they agreed on something other than this wording, which is that straightening the row is part of the completion of the prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 787 - According to their condition"
"788","Jafar bin Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Khalidi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “he would ask forgiveness for the front row three times and for the second one once.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration in all aspects, except that the two sheikhs did not narrate it due to the reason for the narration, on the authority of Al-Irbad, and it is from what I have presented. Therein is the saying
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 788 - According to their condition"
"789","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Ali Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, Ibn Abi told us Dhi’ib, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Al-Ala’ ibn Jariyah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whenever one of you goes out of his house to his mosque, one man’s good deeds are recorded, and the other’s bad deeds are erased.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He used as evidence the hadith of Al-Aswad ibn Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “Al-Bir Jabbar,” and he did not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 789 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"790","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, my brother told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, On the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Qaraz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you performs ablution So he performed his ablution well, then he went out to pray, not leaving him to the mosque except for prayer. His left leg did not remove any bad deeds from him. And the right hand will record for him a good deed, until he enters the mosque.” “Kathir ibn Zayd and Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz are two civilians whom we do not know except through truthfulness, and this is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 790 - True"
"791","Abu Hafs Omar bin Ja`far al-Mufid al-Basri told us, Abu Khalifa al-Qadi told us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, Shaddad Abu Talha told us, he said: I heard Muawiyah bin Qurrah, speaking, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he used to say: “It is Sunnah, when you enter the mosque, to start with your feet.” “The right leg, and when you go out, start with your left leg.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Shaddad bin Sa`id Abi Talha al-Rasibi as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 791 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"792","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr Al-Azdi told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, On the authority of Al-Mukhtar ibn Falful, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “urged them to pray, and forbade them to leave before he departed from Prayer. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 792 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"793","Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Muqri narrated to us, in Kufa, Abu Omar Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, and Abu Bakr narrated to us Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Marwazi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ghalib, Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, Yahya bin Hani told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Mahmoud, he said: I was with Anas. Ibn Malik Asli, he said: So they threw us between the pillars, he said: Then Anas was late, so when we prayed, he said: “We used to fear this during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"794","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Muhammad bin Khalaf told us, Uqba bin Mukarram told us, Muslim bin Qutaybah told us, on the authority of Harun bin Muslim, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurra, on the authority of his father, he said: “We were forbidden from praying between the pillars, and were expelled from them.” “Both chains of transmission are authentic, and they did not mention anything in this regard.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 794 - True"
"795","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Humaid Al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “liked for the Muhajireen and Ansar to follow him so that they could learn from him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and there is a valid witness to take from it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 795 - According to their conditions and it has an authentic witness"
"796","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad told us Bin Abdullah Al-Saffar, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let those of you who take “On me” means prayer. “The two sheikhs have agreed on the hadith of Abu Masoud” “May those of you who have dreams and prohibitions be softer for me” only, and this addition with an authentic chain of transmission on Their condition
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 796 - According to their conditions and it has an authentic witness
 Insurance chapter"
"797","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, And Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin al-Husayn bin Dizel told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Suleiman, that Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi told him, on the authority of Bilal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not outpace me, Amen.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and Abu Uthman al-Nahdi is a veteran. He was among the first group of the Companions. This is contrary to the doctrine of Ahmad ibn Hanbal regarding insurance, based on the hadith of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: When the Imam says: “And not those who go astray” [Al-Fatihah: 7], then say: “Ameen.” And the jurists of the people of Medina said, according to the hadith of Sa’id and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. “If the Imam believes, then they believe.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 797 - According to their condition"
"798","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Uthman Al-Tanukhi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Musab bin Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “recited a prostration in the year of the conquest, and all the people prostrated, including the rider. And the one who prostrates on the ground to the point that the rider prostrates on his hand.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, for they did not narrate Mus’ab bin Thabit nor did they mention him with a narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 798 - True"
"799","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram al-Bazzaz told us, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunays told us, Hassan bin Muhammad told us Ibn Ubayd Allah Ibn Abi Yazid, he said: Ibn Jurayj said to me: O Hassan, your grandfather Ubayd Allah Ibn Abi Yazid told me, he said: Ibn Abbas told me, He said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, this night I saw in what the sleeper saw as if I was praying. Behind the tree, I saw as if I recited Sajdah, so I prostrated, and I saw the tree as if it was prostrating with my prostration, so I heard it as it was prostrating, saying: Oh God, write for me a reward for it with You, and make it a reserve for me with You, and relieve me of a burden for it, and accept it from me as you accepted it from your servant. Dawud, Ibn Abbas said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting the prostration, then prostrated, and I heard him while he was prostrating, saying the same as what he said. The man about the words of the tree”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 799 - True
 Muhammad bin Yazid bin Khunais said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid used to lead us in prayer in the Sacred Mosque during the month of Ramadan. So he used to recite the prostration and prostrate and prolong the prostration.” He was told about that, and he said, “Ibn Jurayj told me, your grandfather Ubayd Allah ibn Abi told me. Yazid adds this.” “This is an authentic hadith. Its narrators were Meccans. Not one of them mentioned a jarh, and it is a condition of authenticity, and they did not narrate it.”"
"800","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Muslih Al-Faqih informed us about irrigation, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Yazid Al-Wasiti told us, Wahib bin told us Khaled, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say about prostrating the Qur’an at night: “He prostrated My face is towards the One who created him and split his hearing and his sight, with His might and power.” Wahib continued it, on the authority of Khaled, and Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Khalid, with an addition to it.
 As for the hadith of Wahib"
"801","So Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydlani told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abi Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say in prostration of the Qur’an: My face prostrated to the One who created it and my hearing was strained.” And his sight
 As for the hadith of Abdul Wahhab"
"802","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to say regarding the prostration of the Qur’an: At night, my face prostrated itself before the One who created it, and my hearing and sight were divided by His power and strength. Blessed be God, the best of creators. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 802 - According to their condition"
"803","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The first surah in which the prostration of Hajj was revealed was recited by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he prostrated.” And the people prostrated, except for a man who took the dirt and prostrated on it, and I saw him killed as an infidel. Zakaria bin Abi Zaida followed him, on the authority of Abi Ishaq like this
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 803 - Followed by Zakaria bin Abi Zayd on the authority of Abi Ishaq, according to their conditions."
"804","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi told us Zaydah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The first surah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited on The people performed Hajj until when he recited it, he prostrated, and the people prostrated, except for a man who took dirt and prostrated on it, and I saw him killed as an unbeliever.” “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that the two sheikhs have all the chains of transmission, and they did not narrate it.” They only agreed on the hadith of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited while the star He reminded him of something similar. “Neither of the two hadiths gives an explanation for the other two hadiths, for I do not know of anyone who followed Shu’bah based on the narration of the star other than Qays ibn al-Rabi’, which leads to it. Ijtihad is the authenticity of both hadiths, and God knows best. It has been narrated with the chain of transmission of the narration of Abdullah bin Lahi’ah that there are two prostrations in Surah Al-Hajj.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 804 - Followed by Zakaria bin Abi Zayd on the authority of Abi Ishaq, according to their conditions."
"805","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Silahini told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Musharrah bin Ha’an, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Surat Al-Hajj was preferred by two prostrations, so whoever does not prostrate them should not He reads them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 805 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"806","Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf bin Ya’qub al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “prayed the noon prayer, so we thought that he had recited the revelation of the prostration.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and it is an authentic Sunnah. It is strange that the imam prostrates when he is pleased with the recitation, such as His prostration while it is announced.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 806 - According to their condition"
"807","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr told me Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balwayh, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abdullah bin Khairan, and Amr bin Marzouq told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Hilal bin Yassar, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night with me. She said: I lost him and thought that he He went to one of his wives. She said, “So I sought him out and came to him while he was prostrating. I placed my hand on him and heard him saying, ‘Forgive me for my sins.’” And I did not declare.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 807 - According to their condition"
"808","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hasan Al-Adl told us about Marw, Yahya bin Sasawayh Al-Dahli told us, Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith, Issa bin Yunus told us, Ubayd Allah bin Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We used to sit with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “and he would recite The Qur’an, and perhaps he passed by a prostration, so he prostrates and we prostrate with him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. The Companions’ prostration following the prostration of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, outside of prayer is a Sunnah. Aziza
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 808 - According to their condition"
"809","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Ali Abdullah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Mawhib, Ismail bin Aoun bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: On the day of Badr, I fought some of the fighting, then I came quickly to see. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what he had done, so I came and found him prostrating, saying: “O Ever-Living, O Ever-Living,” nothing more, so I returned to The fight, then I came while he was prostrating, saying that. Then I went to the fight, then I came while he was prostrating, saying that. He continued to say that. Until God granted him victory. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and there is no mention of a defect in its chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 809 - Al-Qazzaz was denied by Abu Dawud, but as for Ibn Wahb, their opinions about him differed, and Ismail’s statement about him is ignorance."
"810","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, and Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, they said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Huwayrith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf said: I entered the mosque and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leaving the mosque, so I followed him, walking behind him while he did not even notice it. He entered a palm tree and faced the Qiblah. He prostrated and prolonged his prostration while I was behind him until I thought that God had given him his soul, so I continued to walk until I came to him. So I lowered my head to look at his face, and he raised his head and said: “What is the matter with you, Abdul Rahman?” So I said: When you prostrated for so long, O Messenger of God, I was afraid That your soul died, so I came to see, and he said: “When I entered the palm trees, I met Gabriel, and he said: I give you good news that God says whoever has delivered I greeted you, and whoever prayed upon you, I prayed upon you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. I do not know of a more correct hadith than this hadith regarding the prostration of gratitude, and I have narrated the hadith of Bakkar. Ibn Abd al-Aziz Ibn Abi Bakra after this """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 810 - According to their condition"
"811","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Jawhari told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Maryam, Nafi’ bin Yazid told us, Al-Harith bin Saeed narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Munin, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “He recited to him fifteen prostrations in the Qur’an: three in the Mufassal, and Surat Al-Hajj two prostrations.” This is a hadith narrated by Egyptians. The two sheikhs cited most of them as evidence, and there is no one more complete in the number of prostrations in the Qur’an than it, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 811 - It was narrated by Egyptians, most of whom protested"
"812","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Al-Alaa Al-Zubaidi, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, And Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished reciting the Umm al-Qur’an, he would raise his voice and say: “Amen.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it with this wording, and they agreed on the imam’s trustworthiness, and on the follower’s trustworthiness, even if he concealed it.” The Imam, and Ahmad ibn Hanbal, in a group of people of hadith, chose to ensure that those who are prayed are safe, according to what he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “So if The Imam said: Not even those who go astray, so say: Amen.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 812 - based on their condition and they did not narrate it with this wording"
"813","Ali bin Abdullah Al-Halimi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, Falih bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Abu Hurairah complained or was absent, so Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri prayed for us, so he shouted “Allahu Akbar” loudly when he opened the prayer and when he bowed. And when he said: God hears whoever praises Him, and when he raised his head from prostration, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head, and when he rose from the two rak’ahs until he completed his prayer according to So, it was said to him: The people have disagreed regarding your prayers, so he went out and stood on the pulpit and said: “O people, by God, I do not care if your prayers differed. Or is it not different? This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.” They only agreed on the hadith of Ghailan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, in brief. “Al-Bukhari narrated the hadith of Ikrimah alone, saying: I said to Ibn Abbas: I prayed the noon prayer with Batha’ behind a foolish sheikh, so he said the takbir two times. And twenty takbeers, the hadith is brief.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 813 - according to their condition and its witness in the Sahih"
"814","Abu Hafs, Omar bin Muhammad bin Safwan Al-Jumahi told us, in Mecca, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bowed, he would spread his fingers apart. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 814 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"815","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, my father told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdullah bin Idris, Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us And he said the prayer, “He said, ‘Allahu Akbar,’ and when he wanted to bow, he placed his hands between his knees and bowed.” He said: This reached Sa’d, and he said: He spoke the truth, my brother. We were We do this, and then we were ordered to do this, meaning to hold on to the knees. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 815 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"816","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, and Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani, Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Qutaibah told us, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salim Al-Barrad, he said: We came to Uqba bin Amr. Abu Masoud, we said: Tell us about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stood before us in the mosque. He placed his palms on his knees, and placed his fingers lower than that, then drew his elbows apart. Then he said: This is how we saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He does. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it contains noble words, and they did not narrate it because they turned away, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib.” I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I asked Yahya bin Ma’in about Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, and he said: “Trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 816 - True"
"817","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us The reciter, Musa bin Ayyub told us, said: I heard my uncle Iyas bin Amir, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, saying: When {So Subhanah) was revealed In the name of your Lord, the Great} [Al-Waqi’ah: 74] The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Put it in your bowing.”"
"818","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Musa bin Ayoub, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir, he said: When {So glorify in the name of your Lord the Great} was revealed [Al-Waqi’ah: 74], the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was revealed to us. And he said: “Put it in your bowing.” When {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} was revealed [Al-A’la: 1], the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Put it in Your prostration.” “This is a Hijazi hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they agreed to use as evidence its narrators other than Iyas bin Amir, who is the uncle of Musa bin Ayyub al-Qadi. And the chain of transmission is straight, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 818 - Iyas is not known
 They only agreed on the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustadrid ibn Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says while bowing: “Glory be to my Lord, the Great,” and may God’s blessings and peace be upon Muhammad and his family."
"819","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Muzani told us about Marwa, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Barti told us, al-Qanabi told us, regarding what was read to Malik, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Malik told us, and Ahmad bin Jafar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, he said: I read from Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abd God Almajmar, on the authority of Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad Al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ Al-Zarqi, that he said: One day we were praying with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he raised his head from the rak’ah, he said: “God hears those who praise Him.” A man said: Our Lord, to You is the praise, very much. It was good and greatly blessed. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, he said: “Who is the one speaking above?” The man said: I am, O Messenger of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw thirty-two angels hastening to see which of them He writes it.” “This is an authentic hadith from the hadith of the Medinans, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 819 - True"
"820","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Thabit bin Yazid told us, Hilal bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Qunoot for a successive month in the noon, afternoon, sunset and evening prayers. And in the morning, at the end of every prayer, when he said: “God hears him who praises Him,” he prayed the last rak’ah, supplicating for a neighborhood from Banu Sulaim on mounts. Dhakwan, and disobedience, and those behind him believed, and he sent to them calling them to Islam, and they killed them. Ikrimah said: This is the key to Qunoot. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 820 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"821","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Asbahani told us, Mahrez told us Ibn Salamah, Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to “place his hands before his knees” and said: He was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, does this. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and it has contradictions from the hadith of Anas and Wael bin Hajar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 821 - According to Muslim’s condition
 As for the hadith of Anas"
"822","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri narrated to us, Al-Alaa bin Ismail Al-Attar narrated to us, Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the takbeer and aligned his thumbs with his ears, then he bowed until every joint was stable, and he leaned down with the takbeer until His knees preceded his hands.” “This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and I do not know of any reason for it, nor did they narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 822 - According to their condition, and I do not know of any reason for it
 As for the hadith of Wael bin Hajar, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he prostrated, his knees would fall before his hands, and when he rose, he would raise his hands.” Before his knees.” “A Muslim has cited Sharik and Asim bin Kulayb as evidence, and perhaps he is delusional and imagines that there is no opposition to another authentic hadith with a sound chain of transmission, and this The delusional person should contemplate the book of Sahih by a Muslim until he sees of this type what he gets bored of. As for the heart in this, it is to The hadith of Ibn Umar is similar to many narrations on this matter from the Companions and Followers.”"
"823","Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Al-Ma’mal bin Hisham told us, Ismail told us, Ayyub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, raised it, saying: “The hands prostrate just as the face prostrates, so when one of you puts his face down, let him place his hands, and if he raises it Let him raise them up.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 823 - According to their condition
 They only agreed on the hadith of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, God, upon him be peace, says: “When a servant prostrates, seven great ones prostrate with him.” The hadith"
"824","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid, Abu Ishaq Amr bin Abdullah Al-Subaie’ narrated to me, saying: I heard Al-Bara’ bin Aazib saying: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to prostrate On the buttocks of the hand. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 824 - According to their condition"
"825","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Dawud bin Qays told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Aqram, on the authority of his father, said that he was with his father in Al-Qaa near Nimrah, when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was praying, and I was looking at my grave. The armpits of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whenever he prostrates.” “This is an authentic hadith based on what I established regarding the son’s uniqueness in narrating from his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 825 - True"
"826","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Abar told us, Al-Harith bin Abdullah Al-Khazen told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, On the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he prostrated, he would join his fingers.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 826 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"827","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad Al-Zuhri told us, My uncle, my father told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Mas’ar ibn Kadam told me, on the authority of Adam ibn Ali al-Bakri, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not spread your arms and rest on your palms, and turn away from your toes, for if you do that every limb will prostrate.” From you with you. “Al-Bukhari cited Adam ibn Ali al-Bakri as evidence, and Muslim cited Muhammad ibn Ishaq as evidence, and this is correct, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 827 - True"
"828","Abu Zakaria Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Nadr al-Hushi told us, Ibrahim ibn Nadhar al-Surini told us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydlani told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah and Ahmad bin Mansour told us, They said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said the salaam, “When he prays, he will go out.” I heard Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari say: “A man makes a loud noise in his prayer when he extends his toes, and he is harsh in bowing and prostrating.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it is one of what is considered in the Ihram of an-Nadr ibn Shumail.” It was narrated by Zuhair bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Irbid Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Al-Baraa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 828 - Al-Nadr was unique in it, and it is according to their condition"
"829","829 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, al-Nufaili told us, Zuhayr told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of al-Tamimi, who He may narrate an explanation, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from behind him, “and I saw the whiteness of his armpits while he was bleeding and he came out ""His hands"""
"830","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Al-Assam, on the authority of his uncle Yazid ibn Al-Assam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “when he prostrated, he would see his armpits exposed.” “This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, but they did not narrate it. It was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah. So Abdul-Wahid disagreed with it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 830 - According to their condition"
"831","Ali bin Issa told us, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Asam, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Maimuna, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prostrated, if an animal wished to pass in front of him, it would pass.”"
"832","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Issa Al-Tarsusi informed us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam informed us, he informed us Yahya bin Ayyub, Amara bin Ghaziyah told me, he said: I heard Abu Al-Nadr, saying: I heard Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, saying: Aisha said: The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was with me on my bed, and I found him prostrating with his heels crossed, facing with the tips of his fingers towards the Qiblah, and I heard him say: “I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and in Your pardon from your punishment, and in You I praise You without I will convey everything that is within you.” When he left, he said: “O Aisha, has your devil taken you?” So I said: Do you not have a devil? He said: “There is no human being who does not have a devil.” So I said: And beware of you, O Messenger of God? He said: “And me, but God helped me against him and he became Muslim.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. I do not know of anyone who mentioned joining the heels in prostration other than what is in this Hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 832 - According to their condition"
"833","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Asim told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, my father told me, on the authority of Tamim bin Mahmoud, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shibl, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the pecking of a crow and the prey of wild animals. And the man should settle in the place as a camel settles in it.” “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it due to what I mentioned regarding the narration being separate from the Companions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 833 - Sahih Tamim’s uniqueness on the authority of Ibn Shibl
 Talk to us"
"834","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sumayyah, A servant of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained about the difficulty of prostrating for them. When they dispersed, he said: “Seek help from the caravans.” Ibn Ajlan said: That is to place his elbows on his knees when he prolongs his prostration and supplicates. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 834 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"835","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Abu Salih Al-Hakam bin Musa told us Al-Qantari, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The worst of people is the one who steals his prayers.” They said: O Messenger of God, how can he steal his prayers? He said: “It is not completed.” Its bowing and prostration.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and what I have is that they did not narrate it due to a disagreement about it between the writer of Al-Awza’i and Al-Walid. Ibn Muslim”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 835 - According to their condition"
"836","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Abd al-Wahid told us, Hisham bin Amara told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Abi al-Ishrin told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The The worst thief among people is the one who steals his prayer. They said: O Messenger of God, and how can he steal his prayer? He said: He does not complete his bowing and prostration. “Both chains of transmission are authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"837","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, and Abu Ali told us Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz, Abdullah bin Muhammad informed us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade, when a man sits during prayer, to lean on his hand.” The left one. And in the hadith of Ishaq: “For a man to rely on his hands during prayer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 837 - According to their condition"
"838","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil Al-Bukhari told us, Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attar told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “It is part of the sunnah of prayer that the tashahhud be hidden.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and it has evidence with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Aisha.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 838 - According to their conditions and it has an authentic witness"
"839","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “This verse was revealed regarding the tashahhud {And do not speak loudly in your prayer, and do not be afraid. With it} [Al-Isra: 110]"
"840","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa told us, on the authority of Abi Hani’, on the authority of Abu Ali al-Janabi, on the authority of Fadalah ibn Ubaid al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man who prayed but was not praised. He did not glorify God, nor did he pray for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he left. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This man has hastened.” So he called him and said to him. And for others: “When one of you prays, let him begin by praising his Lord and praising Him, and send blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then supplicate for whatever he wishes.” . “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 840 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"841","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Tanisi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad Al-Makki told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to “salom one salutation during prayer, facing his face, leaning towards The right side is a little.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 841 - According to their condition"
"842","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Zahid told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yusuf bin Adi told us, Mubashir told us Ibn Ismail Al-Halabi, in the year seventy-five, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, and Abu Ali Al-Hussein Ibn Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad Ibn Al-Hussein informed us Bin Mukarram, in Basra, Amr bin Ali told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Qara bin Abdul Rahman bin Huwayl, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Deleting the greeting is a sunnah.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Qurrah bin Abdul Rahman in two places in his book, and Abdullah bin Blessed is this hadith on the authority of Al-Awza’i.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 842 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"843","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Qurra bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Omitting the greeting is a sunnah.”"
"844","I asked Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari, and he told us about it on the authority of Abu Abdullah, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Ali bin Hakim told us, Al-Mu'tamir bin Sulayman reported, on the authority of Muthanna bin Al-Sabbah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Sa'id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “When Gabriel came to him and recited, ‘In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,’ he knew that it was a surah.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"845","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, and Abu Qutaibah told us Salam bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami, Al-Qasim bin Zakaria Al-Muqri narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabah Al-Bazzar narrated to us, they said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “did not know how to complete the surah until It descends in the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"846","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Suleiman told us, Rahim bin Al-Yatim told us, and Abu Amr told us Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Dair told us, they said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, we told him Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Muslims did not know The completion of the surah until it is revealed in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. When it is revealed in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, they know that the surah has ended. Rahim Saeed bin Jubair was not mentioned. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"847","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Shaybani told us, Abu al-Ala’ Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Kufi told us in Egypt, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And peace be upon him. He recites: {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds} [Al-Fatihah: 2] He cuts it off, letter by letter. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 847 - According to their condition"
"848","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, and Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, in the first book Interpretation: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Saghani told us, Khaled bin Khaddash told us, Omar bin Harun told us, On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “recited in prayer {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] So he counted it as a verse {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds} [Al-Fatihah: 2] two verses, {The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] three verses, {Master of the Day of Judgment} four verses, And he said: Thus, “It is You we worship and You we seek help” [Al-Fatihah: 5] and he added five fingers together. “Umar ibn Harun is based on the Sunnah, but they did not narrate it, but I narrated it as a witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 848 - They unanimously agreed that it is weak, meaning Omar bin Harun, and Al-Nasa’i said it is abandoned."
"849","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam Al-Masri told us, Ubayy and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, they said: We told us: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Ahmad bin Salman told us, Muhammad bin Al-Haytham told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Khalid bin told me Yazid, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Na`im al-Mujmar, he said: I was behind Abu Hurairah and he recited {In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] Then he recited the Mother of the Qur’an until he reached {And not of those who go astray} [Al-Fatihah: 7].” He said: “Amen,” and the people said: “Amen,” and he said whenever he prostrated: “Allahu Akbar.” When he greets him, he says: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I resemble you in prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and he witnessed it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 849 - According to their condition"
"850","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Adl did not tell us in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Ishaq bin Al-Siraj told us, Uqba bin Mukarram Al-Dhabi told us, Yunus bin Bukayr, narrated by Mas’ar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “utter the name of God out loud.” “The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 850 - Muhammad is weak, meaning Muhammad bin Qays"
"851","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Abdul Majeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, about Ibn Jurayj, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told me that Abu Bakr bin Hafs bin Omar told him that Anas bin Malik said: “Muawiyah performed a prayer in Medina in which he recited aloud, and he recited in it “In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful” to the Mother of the Qur’an, but he did not recite “In the Name of God.” Most Compassionate, Most Merciful to the surah that comes after it until he completed that recitation.” Then when he saluted, the Muhajireen and the Ansar from all over the world called out to him who heard that. Place: O Muawiyah, did you steal the prayer, or did you forget? “When he prayed after that, he recited, ‘In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful’ of the surah that comes after the Mother of the Qur’an, and he said ‘Allahu Akbar’ as he fell prostrating.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz as evidence, and all the narrators agree on their justice, and it is a defect. Because of the hadith of Shu’bah and other Qatadah, despite the height of his authority, he distorts and takes from everyone, even though the hadith of Qatada was included in the Sahih. There is evidence against it, one of which is what we mentioned and some of it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 851 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"852","What Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Abi Issa narrated to us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi narrated to us, Hammam and Jarir said: Qatada told us: Anas bin Malik was asked: How was the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “It was a tide, then he recited {In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] He extends the Most Merciful, and He extends the Most Merciful.”
 And from there"
"853","What Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ali bin Ahmad bin Sulaiman bin Dawud Al-Mahri narrated to us, Asbagh bin Al-Faraj narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us. Ibn Ismail, on the authority of Sharik Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Nimr, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “speak out loud.” In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. The narrators of this hadith from the last of them are trustworthy, including:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 853 - Its narrators are trustworthy"
"854","What Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Uthman bin Kharzaz al-Antaki told us, Muhammad bin Abi al-Sari told us. Al-Asqalani said: I prayed behind Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman more times than I can count the morning and sunset prayers, and he “proclaimed, “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” Before and after the opening of the book. I heard al-Mu`tamir say: I should not have followed the prayer of my father. And my father said: I should not have followed the prayer of Anas ibn Malik, and Anas ibn Malik said: Malik: I would not like to follow the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “The narrators of this hadith, on the authority of the last of them, are trustworthy, and among them”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 854 - Its narrators are trustworthy"
"855","Abu Bakr Makki bin Ahmad Al-Baradai did not tell me, Abu Al-Fadl Al-Abbas bin Imran Al-Qadi told me, Abu Jabir Saif bin Amr told us, Abu Jabir Saif bin Amr told us. Muhammad bin Abi Al-Sirri, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Malik told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he followed my father Bakr, the successor of Omar, the successor of Othman, and the successor of Ali, all of them were “reciting aloud In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.” “I only mentioned this hadith as a witness to what was mentioned above. In these reports that we mentioned there is opposition to the hadith that Qatada narrates. Our imams on his authority, and he has survived.” On the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Othman, Ali, Talha bin Ubayd Allah, Jabir bin Abdullah, Abdullah bin Omar, and Al-Hakam bin Umair Al-Thumali, Al-Numan bin Bashir, Samra bin Jundub, Buraydah Al-Aslami, and Aisha bint Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them. “All of them are listed in the chapter I have left out for the sake of lightness, and I have summarized what is appropriate for this chapter, and I have also mentioned in the chapter Whoever among the Companions, followers, and their followers loudly recites “In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful,” may God be pleased with them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 855 - As for the author being ashamed to cite this fabricated hadith, I bear witness by God and by God that it is a lie."
"856","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Samaan said: Abu Hurairah entered the Banu Zurayk Mosque and said: There are three that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to work with. The people left them: “When he stood up to pray, he would say like this - and Abu Amir gestured with his hand, and he did not spread his fingers or join them together.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but it was not narrated and the commentator witnessed it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 856 - True"
"857","What Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Ja’far Al-Hadrami and Abdullah bin Ghanam told us, they said: Abdullah bin Ghannam told us. Saeed Al-Ashjaj, Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Saeed bin Samaan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He used to “spread his fingers out wide during prayer.” “Saeed bin Samaan is a well-known Tabati among the people of Medina.”"
"858","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, And Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Asadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and he told us Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Asim Al-Anazi, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr - and in the hadith of Wahb ibn Jarir, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr ibn Mut’im, on the authority of his father - that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he began the prayer, he would say: “Allahu akbar, great, all praise be to God, and Glory be to God, morning and evening,” three times. I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his whispering, hissing, and his blowing.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 858 - True"
"859","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Talq bin Ghannam told us, Abd Al-Salam bin Harb Al-Mala’i told us, on the authority of Badeel Ibn Maysarah, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Aisha, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began the prayer, he would say: “Glory be to You, O God. And with your praise, and blessed be your name and exalted is your grandfather, and there is no god but you.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Malik bin Anas, may God have mercy on him, did not approve of Harithah bin Muhammad, but his peers were satisfied with him.” Of the imams, and I do not remember what he said, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the beginning of the prayer. Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, it is more correct than these two hadiths. The narration about it was authentic on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, that he used to say it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 859 - According to their condition"
"860","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, about Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, that when he opened the prayer, he used to say: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name, and exalted is your grandfather, and there is no god Other than you. “This hadith was transmitted on the authority of Omar and is not authentic.”"
"861","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Ayyash bin Al-Walid Al-Raqqam told us, Abdul-A’la told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he told me Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us in the noon prayer, and when he said the salutation, he called a man who was at the end of the prayer. rows, and he said: “O so-and-so, don’t you fear God?” Don't you see how you pray? When one of you stands up to pray, he only stands and speaks to his Lord, so let him see how he speaks to Him. You see that I do not see you. By God, I see who is behind me. My back as I see it from my hands.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 861 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, and Abu Muhammad told us Bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, He said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, speaking, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He still God is facing the servant as long as he does not turn around, so if he turns his face away, he will turn away from him.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. This Abu Al-Ahwas is the client of Banu Al-Layth, a Tabi’i from the people of Medina, and he authenticated it.” Al-Zuhri narrated on his authority, and a debate took place between him and Saad bin Ibrahim about its meaning.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 862 - True"
"863","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Tawba Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi told us, Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, that Abu Salam narrated to him, saying: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari narrated to me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He spoke to them, saying: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, commanded Yahya ibn Zakariya with five words to be acted upon. When you set your faces upright, do not Pay attention, for God Almighty sets His face toward the face of His servant until he prays for him, and does not turn his face away from him until the servant is the one who He leaves. “The two sheikhs narrated the narrators of this hadith on the authority of the last of them, and we did not find for Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari a narrator other than Abu Salam, so they left him. I have spoken in this manner in more than one place, so there is no need to repeat it, and the hadith, according to the conditions of the Imams, is authentic and preserved.”"
"864","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Halim al-Marwazi informed us, Abu al-Mawjih informed us, Yusuf ibn Issa informed us, and Abu Ammar informed us, saying: Thana al-Fadl Bin Musa, Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He should turn right and left in his prayer and not twist his neck behind his back.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 864 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition
 They agreed to narrate the hadith of Ash'ath bin Abi Al-Sha'atha', on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding turning around during prayer, and he said: “It is a misappropriation by Satan of the servant’s prayer.” “This turning is different from that, for the permissible turns are for him to notice with his eye to the right and to the left, and he has evidence with an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"865","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz told us in Hamadan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi’ ibn Nafi’, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, Zaid bin Salam told me that he heard Abu Salam say: Abu Kabsha al-Saluli told me that he told him, On the authority of Sahl Ibn Al-Hanzaliyya, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked to Hunayn, he said: “Is there a man who will serve us tonight?” Anas bin Abi Marthad Al-Ghanawi said: I am, O Messenger of God. He said: “Go.” When the next day came, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: “Do you Did you feel your knight?” They said: No, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to pray and turn to the people, and when he greeted, he said: “Your knight has arrived.” When he came, he said: “Perhaps you Did you come down? He said: No, except for one who is praying, or fulfilling a need. Then he said: I looked at the two peoples, and lo, I weighed their grief and their will, and their blessings were heading. To Hunayn, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tomorrow, God willing, there will be spoils for the Muslims.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 865 - True"
"866","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Yunus Al-Dhabi Al-Baghdadi told us, in Isfahan, Muhadhar bin Al-Muwari’ told us, Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “recite Surat Al-A’raf in Morocco.” In both rak’ahs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, if there is no transmission in it and they do not narrate it with this wording. They only agreed on the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was The salaam is recited during the Maghrib prayer, lengthening the two rak’ahs. “This hadith of a lecturer is explained and summarized, and they agreed to use as evidence a lecturer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 866 - There is a break"
"867","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, verbally speaking more than once, Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Sayyar Al-Maruzi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Khallad Al-Iskandarani, Ashhab Ibn Abdul Aziz told us, Sufyan Ibn Uyaynah told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Al-Rabi’, On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Mother of the Qur’an is a substitute for anything other than it, and there is no substitute for it other than it.” “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate this hadith on the authority of Al-Zuhri from various sources other than this wording, and the narrators of this hadith Most of them are imams, and all of them are trustworthy according to their conditions. This hadith has evidence with different wording. They did not narrate it, and its chains of transmission are straight. ""From it""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 867 - They reported it with a wording other than this"
"868","What Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Nahrizi told us, Ayyub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan told us, Fayd bin Ishaq Al-Ruqi told us, Muhammad told us Bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair Al-Laythi, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays a prayer written with the imam, let him recite the opening of the book in his pauses, and whoever ends up with the mother of the book, it is sufficient.” And among them"
"869","What Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Al-Ma’mal bin Hisham Al-Yashkari told us, Ismail told us Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn al-Rabi’ al-Ansari, and he used to live in Ilya’, on the authority of Ubadah ibn The silent one, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, and the recitation became difficult for him, so when he left, he said: “I see you reciting from behind... Your Imam.” We said: Yes, by God, this Messenger of God. He said: “Do not do so except by the Mother of the Qur’an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.” “Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’ came between him and Ubadah Wahb bin Kaysan.”"
"870","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Utbah told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim, more than one of them told me, Sa`id ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Mahmoud, on the authority of Abu Nu`aym, that he heard Ubadah ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you recite while praying with me?” We said: Yes. He said: “Do not do so except according to the Opening of the Book,” and from it."
"871","What Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mihran al-Khazar told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us Al-Razi, Muawiyah bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Al-Rabi’ Al-Ansari said: Ubadah Ibn Al-Samit stood next to me and recited with the imam while he was reading. When he left, I said: O Abu Al-Walid, Do you read and listen while he reads aloud? He said: Yes, we recited with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, but the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a mistake, then he swam, and he said to us when he left: “Did Has anyone read with me? We said: Yes, he said: “I am astonished. I said: Who is this who disputes with me over the Qur’an? When the imam recites, do not read except with the mother of the Qur’an, for it does not A prayer for those who have not recited it.” This is a continuation of Makhul’s narration on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, and he is strong. And if it is the narration of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, then I mentioned him as a witness.”"
"872","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Ahmad ibn Salamah told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr al-Abdi told us, Yahya ibn Sa`id told us. Al-Qattan, Ja`far bin Maimun told us, Abu Uthman al-Nahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “commanded him to go out and call in People say that there is no prayer except by reciting the Fatihah of the Book, and more than that.” “This is an authentic hadith without a doubt. Ja’far bin Maymun Al-Abdi is one of the trustworthy people of Basra, and Yahya bin Sa’id only narrates on the authority of Trustworthy people. The narration has been authenticated on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Omar bin Al-Khattab, and Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them, and that they were “commanding By reading behind the imam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 872 - It is authentic and has no doubts, and Ja’far is trustworthy
 As for the hadith of Omar"
"873","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib reported, Abu Kurayb told us, Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Taymi’s answer, and Ibrahim bin Muhammad Ibn Al-Muntashir, on the authority of Al-Harith Ibn Suwayd, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Sharik, that he asked Omar about reciting behind the imam, and he said: “Recite with the Fatihah.” The book, I said: And if it is you? He said: “Even if it were me.” I said: Even if I spoke out loud? He said: “Even if I speak out loud.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 873 - True
 As for the hadith of Ali bin Abi Talib"
"874","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ali bin Ishaq told me Hamshadh, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Nu’man told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, he said: I heard al-Zuhri, speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abu Rafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, “He used to order the opening of the book, a surah, and a surah to be read behind the imam in the first two rak’ahs. The other two with the opening of the book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 874 - True"
"875","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ishaq bin Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khaled Al-Asbahani told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray something similar to your prayer.” But he used to shorten the prayer. He used to recite in the Fajr prayer “al-Waqi’ah” and similar surahs.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Rather, Muslim narrated with its chain of transmission: It was recited in the Fajr prayer based on the hadith.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 875 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"876","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Qurashi told us, in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: I asked the Messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about the two who seek refuge from the Qur’an? “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed in them during the dawn prayer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Abu Usama narrated it alone, on the authority of Al-Thawri, and Abu Usama is trustworthy and trustworthy.” It was narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi and Zayd bin al-Hubab, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih with another chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 876 - According to their condition
 As for the hadith of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi:"
"877","So Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Salih, on the authority of Al-Alaa Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Qasim, the client of Muawiyah, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amir, he said: I was driving with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He handed over his mount to travel and said: “O Uqba, shall I not teach you the best of the two Surahs ever recited?” I said: Yes, he said: “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” When he descended, he led the morning prayer with them, then he said: “How do you see, O Uqba?” The hadith of Zayd bin Al-Hubab, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, is similar to this chain of transmission. “This chain of narration does not explain the first, for this is a chain of narration for another text, and God knows best.”"
"878","Ali bin Hamshah Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Al-Safar Al-Sukkari told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubairi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas, that a man used to lead them in Quba’, so whenever he wanted to begin a surah He recited it. He recited, “Say, He is God, One.” Then he recited the surah. He did that in his entire prayer. Then his companions said to him: “Will you not leave this one?” Surah or recite “Say, He is Allah, One” and leave it? So he said to them: I will not leave it. If you would like me to lead you in that, I will do it; otherwise, no. He was one of the best of them, but they hated it. That someone else should lead them in prayer. So they came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and mentioned that to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called him and said: “O What prevents you from doing what your friends tell you to do? What motivates you to adhere to this Surah? He said: I love her, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Loving her will admit you to Paradise.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari also protested, citing Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad in places like The Book »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 878 - according to Muslim’s condition and Al-Bukhari cited it as a commentary"
"879","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Qudamah bin Abdullah Al-Amiri told us, He said: Jasra bint Dajaja told us, she said: I heard Abu Dharr say: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited a verse until he began repeating it.” And the verse: “If You punish them, then they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, then indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise” [Al-Ma’idah: 118]. This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 879 - True"
"880","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra’ told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he told us Mas'ar, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, Bishr bin Musa narrated, Al-Humaidi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mas'ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Saskisi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, teach me something that will suffice me with The Qur’an, for I do not read. He said: “Say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, and there is no power nor strength except “By God,” he said: Then the man held it with his hand and said: This is for my Lord, so what do I have to do with it? He said: “Say: Forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, provide for me, and protect me.” He said: He cupped her with his other hand and stood up. “Ja’far bin Aoun added in his hadith. Mas’ar said: I was with Ibrahim while he was narrating this hadith, so I confirmed it from others. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 880 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"881","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammam told us, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi told us Talha, Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, that he was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When a man came and entered the mosque and prayed, then when he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people, and the Messenger of God said to him May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” He mentioned that either twice or three times, and the man said: I do not know what you blamed me for in my prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one’s prayer is complete until he performs ablution as God Almighty commanded him, and washes his face.” And his hands to the elbows, and he wipes his head and his feet to the ankles, then he says “Allahu Akbar” and praises God and glorifies Him, and he recites from the Qur’an what he has declared. God has him in it, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, kneels, and places his palms on his knees until his joints are at ease and he is level, then he says: God has heard whoever He praised Him, and he stood straight until every bone took its place, then he straightened his back, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated, placing his forehead close to the ground. Until his joints are at ease, and he is straight, then he says “Allahu Akbar” and raises his head, and sits straight on his seat and straightens his back. So he described the prayer in this way. Until he finished, then he said: “None of you’s prayer is complete until he does that.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, after Hammam bin Yahya established its chain of transmission, for he is a trustworthy and trustworthy hadith, and whoever distorts his statement The statement is the statement of Hammam, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, they agreed on it on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. Muhammad bin Ismail narrated this hadith in Al-Tarikh Al-Kabir on the authority of Hajjaj bin Minhal and ruled for him to memorize it, then he said: He did not perform it. Hammad bin Salamah"
"882","Tell us about the authenticity of what Al-Bukhari mentioned, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Affan told us, Hammad told us Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ishaq Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Ali Ibn Yahya Ibn Khallad, on the authority of his father, “that a man entered the mosque and... The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed and prayed, “Then he mentioned the hadith, and this chain of transmission was established by Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra’, and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Left, and Ismail bin Jafar bin Abi Kathir. As for the hadith of Dawud bin Qays,"
"883","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, he said: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Dawud bin Qays informed you, Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Dawud bin Qays informed us, Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad told us, my father told me, on the authority of his uncle, who was Badri, who said: “I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting in the mosque. Then a man entered and prayed two rak’ahs, then he came and said the salutations,” and he mentioned the hadith in its length. “As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yasar"
"884","So Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad. Ibn Ishaq, Ali Ibn Yahya Ibn Khallad Ibn Rafi’ Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle Rifa’ah Ibn Rafi’, he said: While We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque when a man from the Ansar came after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had finished. From the prayer, he prayed, then he came until he stood up to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and greeted him, and said: “And on you, go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he mentioned the hadith. “As for the hadith of Ismail bin Jafar.”"
"885","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Abu Issa Muhammad bin Issa Al-Tirmidhi told us, Qutayba bin Saeed Al-Thaqafi told us, And Ali bin Hajr Al-Saadi, they said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad bin Rafi’ al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting in the mosque one day Rifa’ah said: And we With him, a man like a Bedouin came and prayed, then he mentioned the hadith in its length.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 881 - According to their condition"
"886","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, Yahya bin Abd told us Allah bin Bukayr, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, on the authority of Abu Masoud, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people of whom the majority have recited the Qur’an will lead in prayer, and if there is one verse in the Qur’an, then the earliest of them to emigrate will lead. “There was one person during the migration, and he was the most knowledgeable of them in jurisprudence. If they were one in jurisprudence, then he was the oldest of them.” “Muslim narrated this hadith of Ismail bin Raja’ and did not mention in it “the most learned of them in jurisprudence,” and this is a strange and dear word. With this authentic chain of transmission, and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Al-Hajjaj ibn Artaat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 886 - True"
"887","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, may God have mercy on him, Abu Hamid Muhammad bin Harun Al-Hadrami told us, Al-Mundhir bin Al-Walid told us Al-Jaroudi, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Ansari told us, Al-Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The oldest among them in migration will lead the people, and if they were equal in migration, then the most knowledgeable among them is In religion, if they are the same in religion, then recite the Qur’an to them, and let a man not lead in prayer while under his authority, and let him not sit on his throne except with his permission.”"
"888","Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Muhammad bin Abi Usama told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Abi Umayyah told us, Fulayh bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of his father, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No prophet dies unless a man from his people leads him in prayer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and they all agreed on the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying behind Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. May God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 888 - According to their condition"
"889","Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Shaybani told us, Abu Al-Ala’ Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Kufi told us, in Egypt, Muhammad bin Suwar told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up for prayer, he would say like this and like this. On his right and on his left, then he says: “Be equal and equal.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 889 - According to their condition and they extracted its original"
"890","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, he said: It was recited to Abdullah bin Wahb. He informed you. Malik bin Anas, and Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Hamdani told us about it, Ishaq bin al-Jazzar told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Malik bin Anas, narrating on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Busr bin Mihjan, a man from Banu Ad-Dail, on the authority of his father, that he was sitting with the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave the call to prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up and prayed, then he returned and sat in his seat as he had done, and said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: “What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man?” He said: Yes, O Messenger of God, but O Messenger of God, I had prayed among my family. He said: “So when you come, pray with the people, even if you have already prayed.”"
"891","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Zaid bin He became Muslim, so he reminded him of something similar
 This is an authentic hadith, and Malik bin Anas is the ruling on the hadith of Al-Madani, and it was cited as evidence in Al-Muwatta’, and it is of the type that I mentioned earlier. If a companion did not have two narrators, he would not have narrated it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 891 - Muhjin lost his son"
"892","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Ahmad bin Suleiman Al-Faqih told us, In Baghdad, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mina. When he greeted him, he saw two men among the people, so he called them and said: “What prevented you from praying with me?” People? They said: O Messenger of God, we prayed while traveling. He said: “Do not do that. If one of you prays while traveling and then joins the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him.” For it is a voluntary prayer for him.” This is a hadith narrated by Shu’bah, Hisham bin Hassan, Ghaylan bin Jami’, Abu Khaled al-Dalani, Abu Awanah, and Abd al-Malik. Ibn Umair, Mubarak Ibn Fadalah, Sharik Ibn Abdullah and others, on the authority of Ya’la Ibn Ata. “Muslim argued with Ali ibn Ata”"
"893","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Amr bin Aoun, and Abdul-Hamid bin Bayan told us, they said: Hushaym bin Bashir told us, Shu’bah narrated to us, Adi bin Thabit narrated to us, Sa’id bin Jubayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears the call and does not respond, let him not respond.” Prayers for him. “This hadith was authenticated by Ghandar and most of the companions of Shu’bah, and it is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, nor by Hushaym and Qarad Abu Nuh. They are trustworthy, so if he prays it, then what they say about him is theirs, and he has evidence in his chain of transmission on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, including:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 893 - According to their condition"
"894","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz did not tell us. Abu Muhammad Ismail bin Yaqoub bin Ismail Al-Saffar informed us, in Basra. Sawwar bin Sahl Al-Basri, Saeed bin Amer told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears the call and does not come to it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse.” And among them:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 894 - Followed by Dawud bin Al-Hakam on the authority of Shu’bah"
"895","What Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abu Ghassan Malik bin Al-Khalil told us, Abu Suleiman Daoud bin Al-Hakam, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever hears the call and does not come to it, there is no prayer for him unless there is an excuse.” And in the evidence for a division in which there are chain of narrations with a chain of narrations, such as:"
"896","Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih did not narrate to us, in Bukhara, Qays ibn Anif narrated to us, Qutaibah ibn Sa’id narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Mughraa Al-Abdi, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears No excuse prevented him from following the caller, so there was no prayer for him. They said: What is the excuse? He said: “Fear or illness.”"
"897","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Al-Fadl Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Saydlani told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Abdul Aziz Al-Jarwi, Yahya bin Hassan told us, Sulaiman bin Qurm told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears the prayer being called correctly without an excuse and does not perform it, God will not accept it.” He has a prayer at another time. It was said: What is the excuse? He said: “Illness or fear,” including:"
"898","What Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Yahya bin Ishaq told us, Sulaiman bin Dawud Al-Yamami, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer To a neighbor of the mosque, except in the mosque.” The narration about it was authentic on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of his father: “Whoever heard the call but did not respond” - Hadith"
"899","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ismail Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears the call empty and clear does not respond.” There is no prayer for him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 899 - True"
"900","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Zaydah told us, Al-Sa’ib told us Ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Maadan Ibn Abi Talha Al-Amari, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There are no three In any village or in a Bedouin, prayer is not performed unless Satan has taken possession of them, so you must adhere to the congregation.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 900 - True"
"901","Ahmad bin Mansour bin Issa, Al-Hafiz Al-Muzani, told me about Al-Tabaran, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Sahl Al-Ramli told us, Zayd bin Abi al-Zarqa, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abis, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktum, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, the city Abounding with vermin and wild animals. He said: “Do you hear Hail to the prayer, Hail to the farmer?” He said: Yes, he said: “Long live.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, if Ibn Abbas heard it from Ibn Umm Maktum, and he has a witness with an authentic chain of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 901 - True"
"902","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, Abu Jafar Al-Razi told us, Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktum, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, received the people in prayer dinner, and he said: “I intended to go to those who are neglecting this prayer and burn their houses over them.” So Ibn Umm Maktum stood up, He said: O Messenger of God, you know what is wrong with me and I have no leader. He said: Do you hear the Iqama? He said: Yes. He said: “Then bring it.” He said: O Messenger of God, between me and it are palm trees and trees, and I have no guide. He said: “Do you hear the Iqama?” He said: Yes, he said: “Bring it” and he did not give him permission. “And there is another witness to it from the hadith of Asim bin Bahdala.”"
"903","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, and Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah told us Al-Muzani, Abu Khalifa told us, they said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktum that He asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I am a blind man, my house is vast, and I do not have a leader who suits me. Do I have permission to Do I pray at home? He said: “Do you hear the call?” He said: Yes. He said: “I cannot find a permit for you.”"
"904","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Yaqoub al-Adl told us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata told us, and Abu Abd told us By God, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar, and Abu Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi, said: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Saeed bin Amer told us, He said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Bayan narrated to us, Abdullah bin Raja' narrated to us, narrated to us Shu`bah, and Ibrahim bin Ismail al-Qaari told us, Othman bin Sa`id al-Darimi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the morning prayer, and he said: “Is so-and-so watching?” To a group of hypocrites who had not witnessed the prayer, then he said: “Indeed, these two prayers are among the heaviest prayers for the hypocrites, even if they knew what is in them.” “I will not come to them, even if they crawl,” meaning the evening and morning prayers.
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You should stay in the front row, for it is like the row of angels, and if you knew what is in it, you would rush to it.”
 He said: “Your prayer with a man is purer than your prayer alone, and your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with another man, and the more you pray, the more he is more beloved to me.” God Almighty.” This is how it was narrated by the first class of Shu’bah companions: Yazid bin Zuray’, Yahya bin Saeed, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, and Muhammad bin Jafar, and their peers, and this is how Sufyan bin Saeed narrated it, on the authority of Abu Ishaq"
"905","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan. Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, and Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, In Bukhara, Ibrahim bin Ali al-Tirmidhi told us, Abd al-Samad bin Hassan told us, Sufyan told us, Ali bin Hamshadh al-Adl told us, Yazid bin Al-Haytham, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth narrated to us, Al-Ashja’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Usayd bin Asim narrated to us, Abu Sufyan Saleh bin Mahran, Al-Numan bin Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Waki’ informed us, on the authority of Sufyan. Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Ali bin Bishr told us, Luwayn told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Sufyan, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the dawn prayer, and when he prayed, He said: “I am witnessing so-and-so.” They mentioned the hadith similar to the hadith of Shu’bah. Thus it was narrated by Zuhair bin Muawiyah, Ruqabah bin Masqala, Mutarrif, Ibrahim bin Tahman, and others on the authority of Abu Ishaq. It was narrated by Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Basir, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b."
"906","Al-Hasan bin Halim informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed him, so he mentioned him. Thus said Israel bin Yunus, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah al-Masoudi, and Jarir bin Hazim, all of them. They said: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Basir, on the authority of Ubayy, and Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, Khalid bin Maimun, and Zaid bin Abi Unaisah said, And Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, and Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah. “As for the hadith of Al-Thawri.” . . On the authority of Abu Basir, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, and it was said on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith, on the authority of Abu Basir, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka'b. “As for the hadith of Al-Thawri”"
"907","So Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ja’far bin Musa Al-Naysaburi told us, in Baghdad, Ali bin Bakkar Al-Masisi told us, we told him Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar ibn Harith, on the authority of Abu Basir, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b said: He prayed with us The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one morning, and when he greeted him, he said: “I am witnessing so-and-so,” and he mentioned the hadith. “As for the hadith of Abu Al-Ahwas”"
"908","So Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydali told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith, on the authority of Abu Basir, he said: Ubayy bin Ka’b said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the dawn prayer with us. Then he mentioned the hadith. “They differed regarding the hadith regarding Abu Ishaq in four ways, and the narrations regarding it on the authority of Abu Basir and his son Abdullah are all authentic. The evidence for this is the narration of Khalid bin Al-Harith.” Shu'bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq and Mu'adh bin Mu'adh al-Anbari, and Yahya bin Sa'id, on the authority of Shu'bah. “As for the hadith of Khalid bin Al-Harith”"
"909","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin told us. . . ., Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that he told them on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, on the authority of his father. Shu’bah said: Abu Ishaq said: And he I heard it from him, and on the authority of his father. He said: I heard Ubayy bin Ka’b saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer, and he mentioned the hadith. “As for Muadh bin Muadh”"
"910","So Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Quraysh told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh told us, my father told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, Shu’bah said: Abu Ishaq said: I heard it from him and his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, and he mentioned the hadith. “As for the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed”"
"911","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Khazen informed me, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Hasanjani told me, Muhammad bin Khallad told us, Yahya told us Ibn Saeed, Shu’bah told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, Shu’bah said: Abu Ishaq said: I heard it from him and from His father, on the authority of Ubayy, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer,” - and he mentioned the hadith -. “The imams of hadith, Yahya bin Ma’in, Ali bin Al-Madini, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dahli, and others ruled on this hadith With health. I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Mu’in saying: The hadith of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Basir, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, this is what Zuhair ibn Muawiyah says, and Shu’bah says: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, so the saying is the saying of Shu’bah, and he is more reliable than Zuhayr."
"912","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Mahrajani told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, in the hadith of Ubayy bin Ka’b The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer and said: “I am witnessing so-and-so.” It was narrated by Abu Ishaq on the authority of a sheikh from whom he had not heard anything other than this, and he is Abdullah bin Abi Basir. Shu’bah said: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, He heard it from his father and from him, and Al-Ahwas said: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith. “I do not think the hadith is anything but authentic.” And I heard Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih saying: I heard Ibrahim bin Ishaq al-Harbi saying: I heard Ali bin al-Madini saying: He heard Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah bin Abi Basir, and from his father, Abu Basir. Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us: I heard Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Madini saying: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya saying: Yahya’s narration Bin Saeed, and Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, and the words of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith. “All of them have been preserved. The authenticity of the hadith has been demonstrated by the sayings of the imams of hadith, but as for the two sheikhs, they did not narrate it due to this disagreement.”"
"913","Abu Al-Hasan Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, about Musa bin Ibrahim said: I heard Salamah bin Al-Akwa’ saying: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: I will be hunting and I only have a shirt on. One, or one garment, and how much should I tighten it? - Or he said: So visit him? - He said: “Yes, even with a thorn.” “This is an authentic Medinan hadith, for this Moses is the son of Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Makhzoumi.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 913 - The hadith is authentic"
"914","Saeed bin Muhammad Al-Jarmi told us, Abu Tamila Yahya bin Wadis told us, Abu Al-Munib told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade praying in a quilt without covering himself, and he forbade a man to pray in trousers and not wearing a robe.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and they used Abu Tamilah as evidence, and as for Abu Al-Munib Al-Maruzi, he is Ubayd Allah ibn Al-Ataki is one of the trustworthy people of Al-Marawzah, and one of those whose hadiths are collected in Al-Khurasaniyyin.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 914 - According to their condition"
"915","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Mujahid bin Musa told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfud, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Can a woman pray in armor and a veil?” Isn't she wearing a cloak? He said: “If the armor is thick and covers the tops of her feet.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 915 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"916","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Safwan bin Salih Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim, Zuhair bin Muhammad al-Tamimi told us, Zayd bin Aslam told us, he said: I saw Ibn Umar “praying with his garment removed,” so I asked him about that, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 916 - According to their condition"
"917","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Safiyya bint Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “The prayer of a menstruating woman is not accepted unless she wears a veil.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and I think that there is a dispute over it regarding Qatada.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 917 - According to Muslim’s condition and the reason for it is Ibn Abi Arouba"
"918","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed informed us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The prayer of a menstruating woman is not accepted unless she wears a veil.”"
"919","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Amr bin Yahya Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The entire earth is a mosque except The bathroom and the cemetery. He was followed by Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 919 - Followed by Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad on the authority of Amr"
"920","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Amr bin Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of his father Yahya bin Amara, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr bin Ishaq narrated to us. Al-Mufaddal, Amara bin Ghaziyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The entire earth is a mosque except the bathroom and the cemetery.” “These chains of narration are all authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 920 - Both of them mean this hadith and No. 919 according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"921","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told me, Sadaqa bin Left, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray except with a sutrah, and do not let anyone pass in front of you, if he refuses So fight him, for with him is the qarin.” “This is a hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 921 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"922","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Imran bin Musa Al-Jurjani told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Ibn Abi Umar told me, Sufyan told me, Safwan bin Sulaym told me, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you prays, let him pray with a sutrah. And he will approach it, and Satan will not interrupt his prayers.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 922 - According to their condition"
"923","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Mansouri told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Al-Bakhtari told me, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh bin Muadh told us, my father told us, Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not pray in our hair.” And our quilts.” Ubayd Allah said: My father had doubts. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 923 - according to their condition"
"924","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Mansouri narrated to me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abd narrated to us. By God, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Yazid ibn Haritha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “It is parted from the tunic like the back of a saddlebag, even if it is only a hair’s breadth.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not explain it by mentioning the subtlety of poetry.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 924 - According to their condition"
"925","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Harmala bin Abdul Aziz bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should cover his prayers, even with an arrow.”"
"926","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Bamru, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Bukhari, in Nishapur, said: Abu al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, and Ahmad bin told us Al-Layth Al-Kurmini, Muhammad bin Al-Sannu’ told us, Muhammad bin Abi Raja told us, and Muhammad bin Uthman Al-Uthmani told us, they said: Ibrahim bin Saeed told us, On the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi’ ibn Sabrah al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Cover yourself with your prayers, even if only with an arrow,” according to the condition of Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 926 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"927","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Muhammad Ahmad Al-Asam told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Al-Shaham told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Tomorrow, on the authority of his father, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of The grave. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He used its chain of transmission as evidence whether there will be a trial in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and they did not expel him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 927 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"928","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: We were commanded to say “Tasbih” thirty-three times after every prayer, and “thank God” thirty-three times, and to say “Allahu Akbar” Thirty-four, he said: Then a man from the Ansar was brought in his sleep and it was said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to say “Tasbih” at the back of every Such-and-such prayer? He said: Yes, he said: So make it twenty-five, and put the tahlil in it. When the morning came, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “So do it.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on a common hadith.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 928 - True
 On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The people of Al-Dathur took away the wages.” “It does not contain the vision and this increase.”"
"929","Abu Saeed told us Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Hunayn Ibn Abi Hakim Al-Umayyad, on the authority of Ali Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite the Mu’awwidhaat in After every prayer.” “It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 929 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"930","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Ayoub, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays in one garment, let him tighten it around his waist, and do not “Include them like the Jews were included.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not specify how to pray in one garment.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 930 - According to their condition"
"931","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Al-Hussein bin informed us. Dhakwan, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the The man's mouth. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not mention in it a man covering his mouth during prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 931 - According to their condition"
"932","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Hatem bin Ismail, Abu Al-Hassan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Mahran told us, Abi told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Hatim bin Ismail, Abu Hazra Ya’qub bin Mujahid told us, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid, he said: We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, and he said: I walked with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him during an expedition. He stood up to pray, and I was wearing a cloak, so I went to separate the edges of it, then I held myself together so that it would not fall off. I came to the left of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took my hand and turned me around until he made me stand on his right. Then Ibn Sakhr came until he stood on his right. to his left, so he took us all by the hand until we stood behind him. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to look at me while I was not aware. Then I realized With it, he motioned for me to wrap myself around it. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished, he said: “O Jabir.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “If it is wide, fit between its two ends, and if it is narrow, tighten it around your waist.” “This is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 932 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"933","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Kathir bin Kathir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada’ah, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, go out when he finished his circumambulation to The entourage of Al-Mataf, so he prayed two rak’ahs, and there was no one between him and the two tawaaf.” “This is an authentic hadith, and Al-Bukhari mentioned the narration of Al-Muttalib in the history.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 933 - True"
"934","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, and Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was “praying, and a sheep passed in front of him, so he pursued it.” To the Qiblah until he pressed his stomach to the Qiblah.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 934 - according to Al-Bukhari’s conditions"
"935","Abu Nu`aym Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Ghifari told us, with Marwa, Abdan bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Ubaid Allah told us Ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Hanafi, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “A cat does not interrupt prayer because it is a household item.” “This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, due to its martyrdom of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, coupled with other hadiths from Ibn Wahb and not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 935 - Muslim martyred Ibn Abi Al-Zannad"
"936","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail, who is the son of Abraham, told us. Muhammad bin Ishaq, Abdul-Wahid bin Hamza bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in some of his prayers: “O God, give me a simple reckoning.” When he left, I said: Oh Messenger of God, what is the easy reckoning? He said: “Look at his book and ignore it. Indeed, whoever’s account is discussed on that day, O Aisha, will perish. Everything that befalls a believer will be an expiation.” May God bless him, even a thorn pricks him.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 936 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"937","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Muqatil Al-Maruzi told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Umm Sulaim came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, teach me something that I can call upon in my prayer. He said: “Glorify God ten times, praise God ten times, glorify God ten times, then ask God.” “Whatever you want.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 937 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"938","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Al-Azraq bin Qays said that he saw Abu Barzah Al-Aslami praying with the reins of his animal in his hand. When he bowed, the reins escaped from his hand and it set off. Then Abu Barza turned on his heel and did not turn around until he caught up with the animal and took it. Then he walked as he was and then came to the place where he had prayed. He finished his prayer, completed it, then gave the salutation, then said: “I accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on many battles, until he counted several battles, and I saw Because of his generosity and ease, I accepted that. If only I left my animal to join the desert and then set off, old man, wandering in the darkness. “It was harder on me.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 938 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"939","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muammar, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Damdam bin Jus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ordered the killing of The two lions in prayer: the snake and the scorpion. This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it. Damdam bin Jaws is one of the trustworthy people of Al-Yamamah. He heard it from a group of companions and Yahya narrated from him. Ibn Abi Kathir, and Ahmad Ibn Hanbal authenticated him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 939 - True"
"940","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nusayr al-Darabardi told me about Marw, Abu al-Mawjih told us, Abu Ammar told us, al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Sa`id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Thawr bin Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was turning to He prays right and left, and does not twist his neck behind his back.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 940 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari"
"941","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Ali bin Muhammad told me Hamshadh, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you are praying, do not spit in front of your hands or on your right. But spit on your left side if it is empty, or under your feet.” And he said: with his foot, as if he was covering it with his foot. “This wording is the hadith of Abu Al-Abbas. This is an authentic hadith based on what I derived from the Al-Tabābi’s being separate from the Companions and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 941 - True"
"942","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, Al-Jariri told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail told us, Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of his father, That he prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “so he took a deep breath and rubbed it with his left shoe.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. They agreed on Abu Al-Ala’, for it is Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, and he narrated it. Muslim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, the Companion, and the hadith is authentic according to their two conditions.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 942 - Sahih according to both conditions"
"943","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Iyad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to like the magicians who could hold it. in his hand, so he entered the mosque one day with one of them in his hand, and he saw some shavings in the direction of the mosque, so he inspected them until he cleaned them, then He approached the people angrily and said: “Would any of you like to be met by a man and spit in his face? When one of you stands up to pray He only faces his Lord, and the angel is on his right, so he should not spit in front of him or on his right, but should spit under his left foot, or on His left hand, and if he hastens to do so, let him spit in this manner on the edge of his garment.” He responded one to another. “This is an authentic hadith explained in this section according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 943 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"944","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, he was leading his people in prayer, and he came, and the prayer had been performed, and he said: Let one of you pray, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: “When the time for prayer comes and the time for defecation comes, start by defecating.” “This is an authentic hadith, based on what I mentioned, regarding Al-Tabbi’s being separate from the Companions and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 944 - True"
"945","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Muhammad bin Muhajir told us, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Ruwaym, on the authority of Ibn al-Daylami, who lived in Jerusalem, that he rode in search of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas in Medina. So he asked about him, and they said: He had walked to Mecca, so he followed him and found that he had walked to Taif, so he followed him and found him in the land of what is called Al-Waht, he said. Ibn al-Dailami: So I entered and found him walking, confronting a man from Quraysh, and the Quraysh was committing adultery with wine, so I met him and greeted him and he greeted me. He said: What happened with you today, and where did you come from? I told him and then asked him: Did you hear, O Abdullah bin Amr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A man of My nation, his prayers will be accepted for forty mornings.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 945 - according to their condition"
"946","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Ubaid bin Sharik narrated to us, Yahya bin Bukayr narrated to us, Al-Layth narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umayyah bin Abdullah bin Khalid, that he said to Abdullah bin Omar: We find prayer Presence, and the fear prayer in the Qur’an, and we do not find the journey prayer in the Qur’an. Abdullah said: “O my nephew, God has sent to us Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And we do not know anything, so we are only doing what we saw Muhammad doing.” “This is a hadith narrated by trustworthy civilians, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 946 - Its narrators are trustworthy and Medinan"
"947","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Qays, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “praying cross-legged.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 947 - According to their condition"
"948","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Harmala bin Abdul Aziz bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra, on the authority of his uncle Abdul-Malik ibn al-Rabi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Teach the boy to pray, son of Seven years, and beat him for it at the age of ten.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 948 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"949","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed, Ahmad ibn Issa informed. Al-Masry, Ibn Wahb informed me, Jarir Ibn Hazim informed me, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Mihran, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He passed Ali Ibn Abi Talib accused the mad woman of the Banu So-and-so, and she had committed adultery, and Omar Ibn Al-Khattab ordered her to be stoned, so Ali returned her and said to Omar: O Prince Believers, do I translate this? He said: Yes, he said: Or do you not remember that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The pen was lifted from three people, from the insane person who lost his mind. And about the sleeper until he wakes up, and about the boy until he has a wet dream? He said: You are right, so he left her. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 949 - According to their condition"
"950","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Yunus bin Al-Harith told us, On the authority of Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to “pray for “Mats and tanned scalps.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it by mentioning the scalp. Rather, Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Abu Sa’id regarding prayer on the mat.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 950 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"951","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Al-Harith Al-Wasiti told us, Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Zamaa bin Salih told us, On the authority of Salama bin Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he prayed on a carpet, then he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on a carpet.” . “This is an authentic hadith. Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim cited Zam’ah as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”"
"952","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Iyad bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays Let him wear his sandals, or let him take them off between his feet, and not harm anyone else with them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 952 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"953","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: “I attended with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest, and he prayed In the morning, he took off his shoes and placed them on his left. “This is a hadith known as Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar. It was narrated by a witness, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 953 - I cited it as a witness"
"954","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, on the authority of Abi Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you prays, he should not place his shoes on his right, nor on his left, unless it is Someone on his left, and let him put them between his feet.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 954 - according to their condition"
"955","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah informed us, On the authority of Abu Naama, on the authority of Abu Nadhra, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed and took off his shoes, so the people took off their shoes. Their sandals, and when he left, he said: “Why did you take off your sandals?” They said: O Messenger of God, we saw you took off your clothes, so we took off. He said: Gabriel came to me and told me that there was malice in them, so when one of you comes to the mosque Let him turn his shoes over and see if there is any dirt on them, and if he finds any dirt on them, let him wipe them with the ground, then pray in them.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 955 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"956","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Qutayba bin Sa’id told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Maymun al-Ramli, on the authority of Ya`la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Disagree with the Jews, for they do not They pray in their socks, not in their sandals.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 956 - True"
"957","Yusuf bin Yaqoub al-Susi told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Najda al-Houti told us, Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, And the rest, they said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “When one of you prays, let him take off his shoes between his feet, or pray in them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 957 - according to their condition"
"958","Abu Al-Abbas bin Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you speaks while he is in... Let him put his hand on his nose and then leave.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 958 - Some of them based this on their condition
 Muhammad bin Ali Al-Muqaddami continued it, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If “If one of you spoke while he was praying, let him say it with his hand on his face and leave.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it because some of the companions of Hisham bin Urwa stopped it.”"
"959","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Uthman Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Ayoub bin Suleiman told us Bin Bilal, Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays and does not know how many times he has prayed, three or four, let him kneel.” A rak’ah that he performs bowing and prostration well, and he performs two prostrations.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this addition from mentioning the rak’ah, and it has a witness, and they did not narrate it, and it is his saying May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If one of you doubts about the deficiency, let him communicate the excess with you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 959 - According to their condition"
"960","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Samak told us, in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb told us on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, He said: I heard Yahya bin Ayyub, speaking, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj, who said: “I prayed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the Maghrib prayer, so he said the salutation in two rak’ahs, then he left. A man said to him: O Messenger of God, you made a mistake, so you said the salutation. In two rak'ahs, he ordered Bilal to establish the prayer and then completed that rak'ah. So I asked the people about the man who said: O Messenger of God, you made a mistake. It was said: To me: You know him. I said: No, unless I see him. Then a man passed by me and I said: This is him. They said: This is Talha bin Ubaid Allah. It was summarized by Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Habib
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 960 - Al-Layth narrated it on the authority of Yazid in brief, and it is in accordance with their conditions"
"961","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Suwayd bin Qais, He told him, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “prayed one day, then gave the salutation and left, and there was one rak’ah left of the prayer.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration on the condition of the two sheikhs, and it is the type of hadith in which the Companions asked for a follower in the narration, given that all of them had They left like this.”"
"962","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Darabardi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kaysan, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “called the two forced prostrations of forgetfulness.” “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and all its narrators are used as evidence. Abu Mujahid Abdullah bin Kaysan, one of the trustworthy narrators, collected his hadith and did not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 962 - True"
"963","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj, Imran bin Musa told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, that he told him, on the authority of his father, that he saw Abu Rafi’, the servant of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He passed by Al-Hasan bin Ali while he was praying while standing, and his braid had been stuck into the back of his neck. Abu Rafi’ untied it, and Al-Hasan turned to him. He became angry, so Abu Rafi’ said: Continue your prayer and do not get angry, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “That is the devil’s guise.” It means the seat of Satan, it means the place of his plait - “.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and all of its narrators other than Imran were cited as evidence. Ali bin Al-Madini said: “Imran bin Musa bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas Al-Qurashi, brother of Ayyub bin Musa. Ibn Jurayj and Ibn ""Aliya too""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 963 - True"
"964","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm, Al-Hafiz, told us, in Kufa, Abdullah bin Ghanam told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Kamil bin told us Al-Alaa, Habib bin Abi Thabit told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say between the two prostrations: “O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, keep me well, and provide for me.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and Kamil bin Al-Ala’ Al-Tamimi is among those whose hadith is compiled.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 964 - True"
"965","Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ismail bin Ulayya told us, Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Hakim Al-Dhabi, that he was afraid of Ziyad, so he came to Medina and met Abu Hurairah. He said: So seek me out. So I approached him, and he said: O boy, shall I not speak to you? He said: I said: Yes, may God have mercy on you. Yunus said: I think it was mentioned on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The first thing that people will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection.” Among their deeds is prayer. He said: “Our Lord Almighty says to the angels, and He knows best: Consider the prayer of My servant, whether he completed it or incomplete it. Complete, it was written for him as complete, and if he omitted anything from it, He said: See if My servant has any voluntary actions, and if he had any voluntary actions, He said: Complete. My servant has his obligatory portion of his voluntary work, and then deeds are taken accordingly.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it has a witness with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 965 - True"
"966","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, they said: Musa bin Ismail, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said, “The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection will be the prayer. If he completes it, the entirety of it will be recorded for him, and if he does not complete it, he said.” God, Blessed and Most High, said to His angels: Can you find for My servant a voluntary prayer with which to complete what he missed of his obligatory prayers, then zakat like that, then All other works accordingly. Some of the companions of Hammad bin Salamah and Musa bin Ismail were short of it in their hadith.”"
"967","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, and Abu Bakr told me Al-Shafi’i, Hamdoun bin Ahmad Al-Simsar told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Hammad bin Salamah told me, and Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein, Al-Rabi’ bin Yahya told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qais, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, On the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The first thing for which he will be brought to account The servant’s prayer on the Day of Resurrection” - and he mentioned a similar hadith [p. 395]."
"968","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of a man, from Banu Salit, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. “This disagreement over Hammad bin Salamah has been mentioned so that the meditator will know that what we have authenticated is the hadith of Dawud bin Abi Hind in which there is no disagreement over Hammad, and all the narrations contain chains of narrations for Hammad, on the authority of anyone other than David, may God’s prayers and peace be upon Muhammad and his entire family.”"
"969","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, my father told me, Abu Al-Tahir told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, about Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say during his prostration: “O God, forgive me My entire sin, its glory and its subtlety, its beginning and its end, its openness and its secret.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it, rather they narrated it with this chain of narration.” The closest a servant is to his Lord is “prostrate”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 969 - According to their condition"
"970","Ismail bin Ahmad told us, Abu Ya’la told us, Zuhair bin Harb told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited, “Glorify the name of your Most High Lord,” he would say: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 970 - According to their condition"
"971","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “praying and there was a buzzing in his chest, like the buzzing of a cauldron, from crying.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 971 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"972","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, saying: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told me, Sufyan told me, on the authority of Abu Malik al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no deception in prayer or greeting.” Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: What he saw was that he wanted not to greet you but to greet you, and a man is deceived by his prayer to say the salutation while he is in doubt about it. This. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Muawiyah bin Hisham, on the authority of Al-Thawri, but he doubted its chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 972 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"973","Muhammad bin Musa bin Imran Al-Faqih told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Abu Bakr told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I think he raised it. He said: “There is no deception in the salutation or prayer.”"
"974","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ya’qub bin Ka’b Al-Halabi told us, Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Briefness in prayer. Abu Abdullah Al-Abdi said: It is for a man to place his hand on his waist. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. It was narrated by a group on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “He forbade a man to pray briefly.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 974 - According to their condition"
"975","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shayban informed us Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Yasaf, who said: I came to Raqqa and some of my companions said to me: Do you have a man? Who are the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I said: Yes, spoils, so we pushed to Wabisa bin Ma`abad. I said to my companion: Let us begin. He looked at his bucket and saw a hood on it. A sessile with ears, and a shaggy, dusty robe, and behold, he was leaning on a staff in his prayer. We said to him after we greeted him, and he said: Umm Qais bint Muhsin told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he was carrying meat, he took a pillar in prayer to lean on.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, except that they did not narrate Wabisa bin Ma’abad because of the spoilage of the way to him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 975 - according to their condition"
"976","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Khams bin Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin A brother, who said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite the surah in a rak’ah? She said: “From Al-Mufassal.” He said: So I said: Did he pray sitting? She said: “When the tooth destroyed it.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray long nights standing and long nights sitting.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 976 - according to their condition"
"977","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq narrated to us, Tamim bin Al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq bin Yusuf narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, Jami` bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We did not know what to say when we sat in prayer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, knew the essence of the words and their endings. He said: Then he mentioned the tashahhud and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us words, as He teaches us the Tashahhud: “O God, reconcile our hearts, reconcile our relationships, guide us to the paths of peace, deliver us from darkness to light, and protect us from The immoral acts, both apparent and hidden, and bless for us our hearing, our sight, our hearts, our wives, and our offspring, and forgive us. Indeed, You are the Most Merciful, and make us thankful for Your blessings, praising You for them, accepting them, and completing them upon us. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and it has evidence from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a scholar.”"
"978","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Jarir Al-Tabari told us, Othman bin Yahya Al-Qufsani told us, Abdul Majeed bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawwad, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abi Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He teaches us. So he reminded him of something similar
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 977 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"979","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb, Malik bin Anas told you, and Yunus bin Zaid, and Amr bin Al-Harith, that Ibn Shihab narrated to them, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Qari, that he heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, teaching people the Tashahhud on the pulpit, says: “Greetings are to God, the pure women are to God, the good women are to God, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and His mercy God and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.”"
"980","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me about Mecca from the origin of his book. Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abdullah bin Salamah told us. Al-Qanabi, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab used to teach people to recite the tashahhud in prayer. While he was addressing the people on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When one of you bears witness, let him say: In the name of God, the best of names. Pure greetings, good prayers to God, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” Omar said: “Start with yourselves after the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and may peace be upon the righteous servants of God.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but I mentioned it because it has evidence according to what we stipulated regarding the evidence that attests to its chain of transmission.” [P. 399].
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 980 - According to Muslim’s condition and there is evidence"
"981","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Qutaybah Al-Asqalani told us, Safwan bin Salih told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim, told us by Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, Aoun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abdullah bin Abbas took my hand and counted the tashahhud and said: I took your hand just as Omar bin Al-Khattab took me by the hand, and Omar said: I took your hand Just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand and counted in it the tashahhud, greetings, and good and pure prayers for God. He mentioned the hadith similarly. “As for the addition at the beginning of the tashahhud in the name of God, and by God, it is valid according to the condition of Al-Bukhari.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 981 - As for the addition at the beginning, it is according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"982","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim Al-Asbahani told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Ayman bin Nabul told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to teach us the Tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Qur’an, in the name of God and in God, greetings to God.” Abu Abbas said - and he mentioned the hadith - at the end of it: “O God, I ask You for Paradise, and I seek refuge in You from Hell.”"
"983","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Abu Qalaba told us, and Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us about others, they said: Abu Qalaba told us Muslim, they said: Abu Asim told us, Ayman bin Nabul told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He teaches us the Tashahhud just as he teaches us the surah from the Qur’an. In the name of God and in God. Greetings are to God. Good prayers are to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet. And God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger, we ask God for Paradise, and we seek refuge in Him from Hell. Al-Hakim said: “Ayman bin Nabul is trustworthy and was cited as evidence by Al-Bukhari.” I heard Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salama, saying: I heard Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi, saying: I heard Yahya bin Moin, saying: I asked him about Ayman bin Nabul, and he said: Trustworthy. “As for its validity, it is based on the condition of a Muslim.”"
"984","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abdullah bin Qahtaba Al-Talhi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala narrated to us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Ubayy narrated to us, On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. “I heard Abu Ali al-Hafiz, authenticating Ibn Quhtaba, except that he made a mistake in it. It is according to al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Ayman ibn Nabul, as mentioned above. We mentioned him, and may God’s blessings and peace be upon Muhammad and his entire family.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 983 - Ayman was cited as evidence by Al-Bukhari and a group narrated it from him"
"985","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu Muammar Abdullah bin Omar told us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed, Hussein Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Ali, on the authority of Muhjan bin Al-Adra’, he narrated to him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and saw a man who had prayed his prayer while reciting the tashahhud and saying: Oh God, I ask you. By God, the One and Only, the Eternal, Who begets not, nor is He begotten, and to Him there is no one equal, that You forgive me my sins. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. He said: “You have He has been forgiven, he has been forgiven, he has been forgiven.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 985 - according to their condition"
"986","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Kindi told me, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “It is Sunnah to conceal the tashahhud.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 986 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"987","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Azhar told us, and I wrote it from Its origin is that Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: And he told me about praying for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “If The Muslim man prayed for him in his prayers.”"
"988","Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid bin Abdul Rabbo, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr, who said: A man came Until he sat in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were with him, and he said: O Messenger of God, as for peace be upon you, we have known it, so how can we pray for you? If we prayed for you in our prayers, may God’s prayers be upon you? He said: He was silent until we liked that the man did not ask him. Then he said: “If you pray for me, say: O God, bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet. And upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Abraham and upon the family of Abraham, and bless Muhammad the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of Muhammad as You bestowed blessing upon Abraham and upon his family. “Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, so he mentioned sending blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the prayers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 988 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"989","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Haywa told us, on the authority of Abu Hani, on the authority of Abu Ali Amr ibn Malik, on the authority of Fadalah ibn Ubaid Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man who prayed without... He praised God, but did not glorify Him, and did not pray for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he left. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “This man hastened.” So he called him, and he said For him and for others: “When one of you prays, let him begin by praising his Lord and praising Him, then send blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then supplicate with what He wanted. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and no defect is known to it, and they did not narrate it, and there is a valid witness according to their conditions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 989 - according to their condition"
"990","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Kindi told us, Aoun bin Salam told us Ibn Sulaym Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaidah, who said: Abdullah said: “The man bears witness, then prays on The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then prays for himself.” “This hadith was transmitted on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud with an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"991","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Sabbaq, on the authority of a man, from Banu al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “When one of you bears witness in prayer, let him say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and have mercy.” Muhammad, and the family of Muhammad, just as You prayed, blessed, and had mercy upon Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” The most abundant evidence for this rule is for the obligatory prayers.”"
"992","What Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Al-Bari told us, my father told us, Abd told me Al-Muhaymin bin Abbas bin Sahl Al-Saadi said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of my grandfather, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “There is no prayer for one who does not “Ablution for him, and no ablution for he who does not mention God, and no prayer for he who does not pray for the Prophet of God in his prayer.” “This hadith was not narrated according to their condition, as they did not narrate Abd al-Muhaymin.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 992 - Abd al-Muhaymin Wah"
"993","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalabah told us, Bishr bin Omar Al-Zahrani told us, and Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hassan Al-Asadi told me, In Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of his father, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that “in the first two rak’ahs he was as if he were on his knees. He said: We said, ‘Until he rises.’ He said, ‘Until he rises.’” He followed him. Misar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim"
"994","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told us in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Marri told us, Mas'ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, so he mentioned it similarly. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, who did not narrate it. They agreed to narrate the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, On the authority of Abdullah that he was not with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of the jinn.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 993 - It was narrated by Othman bin Saeed Al-Marri, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Sa’d, according to their conditions."
"995","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Othman Al-Tanukhi told us, Saeed told us Ibn Bashir, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samarra, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded us to respond to the imam, to love one another, and to We greet one another.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and Saeed bin Bashir was the imam of the people of the Levant in his time, except that the two sheikhs did not narrate it according to what Abu Mushar described. Because of his poor memory, and something like it does not come down to this extent.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 995 - True"
"996","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, Ahmad bin Ali al-Khazzaz told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Najdah told us, Ash`ath bin Shu`bah told us, Al-Minhal bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qais, he said: An imam of ours, nicknamed Abu Rimthah, led us in prayer. He said: I prayed this prayer or something like it. This prayer was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, were standing in the front row. On his right, and there was a man who witnessed the first takbeer of the prayer, and the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed and then gave the salutations, on his right and on his left. Until we saw the white of his cheek, then he turned around like Abu Ramthah - meaning himself - and the man with whom he had recited the first takbeer of prayer stood up. He interceded, so Omar jumped to him, took him by the shoulder and shook him, then said: Sit, for the People of the Book were not destroyed except that he was not among them. Their prayer was a chapter, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his gaze and said: “May God bless you, O Ibn Al-Khattab.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 996 - Al-Manhaal was deemed weak by Ibn Ma’in, Ash’ath is soft, and the hadith is objectionable."
"997","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Abdul Salam Al-Dair told us, Al-Jarrah bin Mukhlid told us, Abu Qutayba told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, On the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer for one whose nose has not touched the ground.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.” Shu’bah narrated it, on the authority of Asim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 997 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"998","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Abdul Salam told us, Al-Jarrah bin Mukhlid told us, Abu Qutayba told us, Shu’bah told us, about Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “There is no prayer for the one whose nose has not touched the ground.”"
"999","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Abi Issa told us, Ma’an told us, Asad told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Aamir ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded “to place the hands and place The feet in prayer. “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, but it was authenticated according to a condition with a more correct wording than this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 999 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1000","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, he said:, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Aamir ibn Saad ibn Malik, on the authority of his father, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that The palms of the hands, and the erection of the feet in prayer.”"
"1001","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr Al-Azdi told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, On the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: I was with Umm Salamah when a young man with a hood entered by her relative, and he stood up to pray and blew, and said: O my son, do not blow, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to a black servant of ours: “O Rabah, cover your face.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1001 - True"
"1002","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad informed us Bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith, they said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Saeed bin Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah. Ibn Jundub, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to push himself during his prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1002 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"1003","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Qadi told us, Nasr bin Ali told us, Yahya bin Ali told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi told us Zaida, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar bin Murrah, on the authority of Talha bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he raises his head from prostration, he says: “My Lord, forgive me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1003 - According to their condition"
"1004","Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa informed me, Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed me, Abd al-Salam ibn Asim informed me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab told me, Kamil Abu al-Ala told me, On the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say between the two prostrations: “O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, strengthen me, elevate me, guide me, and provide for me.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not narrated by Abu Al-Ala. Kamil bin Al-Ala’ is among those whose hadiths are collected in Al-Kufiyyin."
"1005","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed informed us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade standing still during prayer.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Al-Bukhari, and he did not narrate it, and he has a narration in which it is permissible to sit down. It is authentic according to the condition of a Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1005 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"1006","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari and Ali bin Issa told us, they said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ya’qub told us Ibn Ka'b Al-Halabi, Mukhlid Ibn Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, that he heard a peacock saying: I said to Ibn Abbas in Al-Iqa', He said: “It is the Sunnah.” I said: We see it as rudeness. Ibn Abbas said: “It is the Sunnah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1006 - It is valid to permit this on the condition of Muslim"
"1007","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Hisham bin Yusuf, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade a man while he was sitting, relying on On his left hand while praying, and he said: “It is the prayer of the Jews.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1007 - According to their condition"
"1008","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Ahmad bin Al-Faraj told us, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Maadan, on the authority of Muadh Ibn Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Two steps, one of which is more beloved to God, and the other is a mistake I hate.” To God. As for the step that God Almighty loves, it is a man who sees a defect in the class and spoils it. As for the step that God hates, if he wants A man should stand up, extend his right leg, place his hand on it, and steady the left one, then stand up. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He used Baqiyya ibn al-Walid as evidence in the evidence, but they did not narrate it. “As for Baqiyya ibn al-Walid, if he narrates on the authority of the famous people, then he is trustworthy and accepted.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1008 - No, Khaled’s narration from Muadh is cut off"
"1009","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu told us Bakr bin Balawayh, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan told us, Abu Omar, Muslim bin Ibrahim, and Ali bin Al-Ja’d told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl and Zubaid, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times, raising his voice. “Abdul-Rahman bin Abza is one of those who is confirmed by us to have met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that Most of his narrations are on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b and the Companions. “This chain of narration is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1009 - The hadith is authentic"
"1010","Abu Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us. Al-Muqri, Haywa bin Shurayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Uqba bin Muslim Al-Tajibi, saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli told me, on the authority of al-Sanabihi, On the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand one day, then said: “O Muadh, by God, I love you.” Muadh said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, O Messenger of God - may God bless him and grant him peace - and I, by God, love you. He said: “I advise you, O Muadh, not to give up at the end of every prayer.” To say: O God, help me in remembering You, thanking You, and worshiping You well.” He said: And Muadh Al-Sanabihi recommended that, and Al-Sanabihi recommended that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, and Abu Abd al-Rahman advised Uqba bin Muslim, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1010 - According to their condition"
"1011","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Muslim told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Manhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Hisham bin Abi told us Abdullah and Ali bin Al-Mubarak, who said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, says at the end of every prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, from the torment of the Fire, and from the trials of life and death. “And from the temptation of the Antichrist” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1011 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"1012","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid informed us, Yahya told us Ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Abi Attab, and Sa`id Ibn Abi Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “When you come to prayer while we are prostrating, then prostrate, and do not treat it as anything. And whoever performs the rak’ah has performed the prayer.” This is an authentic hadith. The two sheikhs cited as evidence their narrations from the last of them except Yahya ibn Abi Suleiman, who is a sheikh from the people of Medina who lived in Egypt, and was not mentioned with a trace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1012 - Sahih, and Yahya did not mention Jarh"
"1013","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahboub Al-Tajer informed us, Abu Al-Nadr Ahmad bin Atiq Al-Maruzi told us, Muhammad bin Sinan told us Al-Awqiy, Hammam told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of An-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever prays one rak’ah of Fajr, then the sun rises, let him pray Fajr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, if it is preserved with this chain of transmission. Ahmad bin Atiq Al-Marwazi is trustworthy, but he narrated it another time with another chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1013 - If Ibn Atiq had memorized it and he was trustworthy, we would have told him according to their conditions."
"1014","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Omar bin Ali Al-Jawhari told us, Abu Al-Nadr Ahmad bin Atiq Al-Ateeqi told us, Abu Al-Nadr Ahmad bin Atiq Al-Ateeqi told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Awqi, narrated by Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khallas, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever prays one rak’ah of the morning prayer, and then the sun rises, let him complete his prayer.” Both chains of transmission are authentic. They all cited Khulas ibn Amr as a witness."
"1015","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Badr Abbad bin Al-Walid Al-Anbari told us, Amr bin Asim, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of An-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever does not pray the two rak’ahs of Fajr until the sun rises, let him pray them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1015 - Both chains of transmission are authentic according to their conditions"
"1016","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Ishaq bin Shaheen told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yunus, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on his way, and they fell asleep after the dawn prayer and woke up in the heat of The sun, so they rose a little until it rose, then “the muezzin gave orders and called the call to prayer, then he prayed the two rak’ahs before dawn, then the muezzin stood and prayed the dawn prayer.” This is an authentic hadith based on what we mentioned regarding the authenticity of Al-Hasan’s hearing, on the authority of Imran, and his repeating the two rak’ahs did not narrate it, and there is a witness for it. With an authentic chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1016 - True"
"1017","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he came while the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was praying the dawn prayer, so he prayed with him. When he gave the salutation, he stood up and prayed the two rak’ahs of dawn, and he said: The Prophet has him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “What are these two rak’ahs?” He said: I did not lead them in prayer before dawn, so he remained silent and did not say anything. “Qais bin Fahd Al-Ansari is a companion of mine, and the path to him is correct according to Their condition.” It was narrated by Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Qais bin Fahd
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1017 - Qais bin Fahd is a companion and has a witness"
"1018","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydali told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah Al-Sulami told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Saad bin Saeed told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Qais bin Fahd, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man praying after... The morning prayer consists of two rak'ahs, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The morning prayer twice?” The man said: I had not prayed the two rak’ahs before that, so I prayed them now. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about him."
"1019","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Abi Al-Hussein told us, Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, Ja`far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about prayer on a ship, and he said: How should I pray on board? The ship? He said: “Pray therein standing, unless you fear drowning.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it while it was completely irregular.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1019 - According to the condition of a Muslim, but he is completely anomalous"
"1020","Zaid bin Ali bin Yunus Al-Khuza’i told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Bakr bin Khalaf, and Suwayd bin Saeed told us, they said: Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever collects Between the two prayers without an excuse, he has come to one of the chapters of major sins.” Hanash ibn Qays al-Rahbi, who is called: Abu Ali, one of the people of Yemen, lived. Al-Kufa is trustworthy. “Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and this hadith is based on a prohibition against combining prayers without an excuse, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1020 - Commenting on Al-Hakim’s authentication of Hanash, but rather they weakened him"
"1021","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Musa bin Harun bin Abdullah told me, my father told me, Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told me, Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying cross-legged.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1021 - According to their condition
 They only agreed to narrate Humaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray long nights.” “He is standing,” the hadith, “and this Hamid is Ibn Tariwih al-Taweel, without a doubt about him.”"
"1022","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray a long night standing, and a long night sitting, so when he prayed standing He bowed standing, and if he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting.”"
"1023","Abu Al-Hasan Abd Al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram, brother of Al-Hasan bin Mukarram Al-Bazzar in Baghdad, told us about Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas Al-Sayrifi, Yahya bin Ghaylan told us, Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “We used to open the door to the imams at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith and it has evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1023 - It is authentic and has evidence"
"1024","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul-Samad Al-Tayalisi told us, Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Jariya bin Haram told us, Humaid Al-Taweel told us, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to instruct one another in prayer.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1024 - A female slave is abandoned"
"1025","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, and Muhammad told me Ibn Salih Ibn Hani’, Al-Sari Ibn Khuzaymah told us, Abu Salamah Musa Ibn Ismail told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad Ibn Ahmad Ibn Balawayh told us. Ahmed bin Ali Al-Khazzaz told us, Khalid bin Khadash told us, they said: Bakkar bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Bakra told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when a matter came to him that pleased him, or with which he was pleased, he would fall down in prostration in thanks to God Almighty.” This is a hadith. It is true, even if they did not narrate it, “For Bakkar bin Abdul Aziz is trustworthy in the eyes of the imams.” Rather, they did not narrate it due to their condition in the narration, as We mentioned it above, and Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Bakra had no narrators other than his son, so he said: A valid hadith, and there is many evidence for this hadith. He mentioned it, including the fact that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “saw a monkey and fell down, prostrating.” Among them: that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “saw a man who had been in a state for a long time and fell down, prostrating.” Among them is that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “Ja’far bin Abi” came to him. A student at the conquest of Khaybar fell down, prostrating. Among them is that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a raider, so he fell down, prostrating.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1025 - True
 Friday book"
"1026","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Musa Ibn Abi Uthman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The master of days is Friday, on it Adam was created. And on it I will be admitted into Paradise, and on it I will be expelled from it, and the Hour will not come except on Friday.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, as he cited By Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad, and they did not mention “the master of days.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1026 - Muslim cited Ibn Abi Al-Zannad"
"1027","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Tawba Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi told us, Al-Haytham bin Humaid, Abu Ma’bad Hafs bin Ghaylan narrated to me, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, God will raise the days on the Day of Resurrection in their regular state, and He will raise Friday a bright and radiant Zahraa, and her family will surround her like a bride.” It will be guided to its generosity. It will give them light. They will walk in its light. Their colors will be as white as snow, and their scent will shine like musk. They will wade through mountains. Camphor, heavy people will look at them, and they will not be surprised until they enter Paradise. No one will mix with them except the muezzins who seek reward.” This An anomalous hadith with an authentic chain of narration: “Abu Mu`id is one of the trustworthy people of the Levant whose hadith is collected, and Al-Haytham bin Humayd is one of the notables of the people of the Levant, not “The two sheikhs did not remove it from them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1027 - Anomalous news with an authentic chain of narration"
"1028","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Qadi informed us by dictation, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani informed us, and Yahya bin Al-Mughirah said: Jarir bin Abdul-Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Qartha’ al-Dhabi, and it was Qarath, one of the first reciters, on the authority of Salman, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Salman, what is Friday?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “O Salman, on Friday your father or your father gathered together, and I am telling you about Friday. A man purifies himself on Friday as he was commanded, then leaves his house until Friday comes and sits and listens until he finishes his prayer, unless he Atonement for the Friday prayers that came before it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and the two sheikhs cited all of its narrators as evidence, without quarreling. I heard Abu Ali The reader says: I wanted to collect the isnads of Qarth al-Dhabi, for he was one of the ascetics of the Followers, so he did not provide a complete chain of narrations.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1028 - True"
"1029","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Abu Jafar Ahmad bin Abdul-Hamid Al-Harithi narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Ja’fi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me And he said: “Indeed, one of the best days of yours is Friday. On it, Adam was created, on it he was taken, and on it is the blast, and on it the thunderbolt, so increase your blessings upon me.” In it, your prayers are before me.” They said: How will our prayers be presented to you since you have been rejected? He said: “God Almighty has forbidden the earth to eat the bodies of the prophets.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1029 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"1030","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Malik told us, and Abu Bakr Ahmad told us Bin Salman Al-Faqih, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Barti, and Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, they said: Al-Qanabi told us, on the authority of Malik, Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The best day on which the sun rises is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it he was descended, on it he was accepted, and on it he died, and on it The Hour will come, and there will be no animal but it will make a noise on Friday from the time the sun sets until the twilight of the Hour, except the jinn and mankind, and in it “An hour that no Muslim servant encounters while he is praying and asks God for something except that He gives it to him.” Ka’b said: “Is that a day every year?” So I said: Rather, every Friday. Then Ka’b recited the Torah, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth. Abu Hurairah said: Then I met Abdul Allah bin Salam, so I spoke to him while I was sitting with Ka’b, and Abdullah bin Salam said: “I have learned what time it is?” Abu Hurairah said: So I told him and he told me about it. Abdullah bin Salam said: “It is the last hour of Friday.” So I said: How is the last hour on Friday? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No Muslim servant will meet her while he is praying,” and is that the hour in which he does not pray? Abdullah bin Salam said: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever sits in a sitting area waiting for prayer is in prayer until he prays” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, rather they agreed on letters from the beginning “in the hadith of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah” The best day of Talaat “On it, the sun will be on Friday.” Muhammad bin Ishaq Yazid bin Al-Hadi continued his narration, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi. With increases in it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1030 - According to their condition"
"1031","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim al-Ghifari told us, Ya`la bin Ubaid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I came to the Mount and there I found Ka`b. The rabbis, so I spoke to him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he spoke about the Torah. They did not differ until I passed by on Friday. He said: I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every Friday there is an hour that no believer goes to while he is praying and asks God for something but He gives it to him.” Ka'b said: Is that every year? So I said: What is that? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Then he came back and recited, and then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth about every Friday. He said: Abu Hurairah, then I met Abdullah bin Salam and spoke to him while I was sitting with Ka’b. “He mentioned the hadith in a similar manner to the hadith of Malik.”"
"1032","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Sa’id told me Al-Harith, that Al-Jalah bin Kathir told him that Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told him on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “On Friday there are twelve hours, and there is no Muslim servant who asks God for anything except that God gives it to him, so seek it again.” “The hour after the afternoon prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He used Al-Jalah ibn Kathir as evidence, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1032 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1033","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Fulayh bin Suleiman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I said: By God, if I had come to Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri and asked him about this hour, perhaps That he had knowledge of it, so I came to him and said: O Abu Saeed, Abu Hurairah told us about the hour that falls on Friday. Do you have any knowledge of it? He said: We asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it, and he said: “I knew it, then I forgot it just as I forgot the Night of Decree.” Then I went out. From him, I went to Abdullah bin Salam, then he mentioned the hadith: “This is authentic evidence according to the conditions of the two sheikhs for the hadith of Yazid bin Al-Hadi. And Muhammad bin Ishaq, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1033 - True"
"1034","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, he said:, Ubaidah bin Sufyan al-Hadrami told me, on the authority of Abu al-Ja`d al-Dhamri, who was a companion of his: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He left three plurals out of neglect, and God put a seal on his heart.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1034 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1035","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam bin Yahya told us, Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Qudamah ibn Wabarah al-Ju’fi, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever neglects the Friday prayer is Without an excuse, let him give a dinar in charity, and if he does not have it, then half a dinar.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and there was no disagreement about it from Sa’id bin Bashir and Ayyub bin Al-Ala’, for they said: On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qudamah bin Wabarah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as a messenger.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1035 - True"
"1036","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Abdul Wahid told us, Abu Al-Jamahir told us, Saeed bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Qatada, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Hisham Muhammad bin Yazid told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Al-Ala, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qudamah ibn Wabarah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever misses Friday Without an excuse, let him give in charity a dirham, or half a dirham, or a saa’ of wheat, or half a saa’. This is the wording of the hadith of al-Anbari, and we have not added anything more. Sheikh Abu Bakr in it on the message “"
"1037","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, he said: I heard my father and he was asked about a hadith Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, and Khallad bin Al-Ala’ about him, so he said: Hammam, in our view, is better at memorizing than Ayyub bin Al-Ala’."
"1038","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, Mawla al-Muttalib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that two men from the people of Iraq came to him and asked about washing on Friday. Is it obligatory? Ibn Abbas said to them: Whoever washes is better and purer, and I will tell you: When the washing began, the people were in the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They were in need of wearing wool and watering the palm trees on their backs. The mosque was narrow and close to the roof. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. Peace be upon him, on Friday, on a very hot summer day, and his pulpit was short, but only three steps. He addressed the people, and the people sweated in the wool. Then their bodies were stirred by the smell of sweat and wool, to the point that they were almost harming one another, until their souls reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was On the pulpit, he said: “O people, when this day comes, wash yourself, and let each one of you touch the best perfume or ointment he can find.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1038 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"1039","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b, he said: I was my father’s commander. When his sight went away, I went out with him to Friday prayer, and he heard the call to prayer. He prayed for Abu Umamah Asaad bin Zurarah and asked forgiveness for him. So I stayed. He often does not hear the Friday call to prayer unless he does that, so I said: O my father, did you see that you asked Abu Umamah for forgiveness whenever you heard the call to prayer for Friday? Him? He said: “My son, he was the first one to gather with us in the city in Hazm al-Nabt from Harrat Bani Bayadah, which is called Naqi’ al-Khadimat.” He said: I said: How old were you that day? He said: “Forty men.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1039 - According to Muslim’s condition
 He witnessed the hadith that was uniquely narrated by Al-Bukhari from the hadith of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “The first “Friday in Islam, after Friday in the city, Friday in the city of Abd al-Qais.”"
"1040","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Abdul-Hamid Al-Harithi told us, Hussein bin Ali Al-Ja’fi told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Aws, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said and mentioned Friday: “Whoever washes and takes a bath, and goes in the morning and prays early, and approaches, and listens and listens, will be forgiven for what occurred between him and Friday, plus three days, and whoever touches the pebbles has lost his mind.” Narrated by Yahya bin Al-Harith Al-Dhimari and Hassan bin Attiya, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1040 - It was narrated only on the authority of Al-Ashja’i Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth, and it is weak, and its wording is objectionable, but others followed it with it.
 As for the hadith of Yahya bin Al-Harith"
"1041","Then Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Yazid bin Al-Haytham Al-Quta’i told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told me, Al-Ashja’i told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Aws Al-Thaqafi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever washes and performs ablution, then in the morning and wakes up early, and sits close to the imam and listens and listens, will have for every step he takes the reward of a year of fasting.” And its resurrection”
 As for the hadith of Hassan bin Atiyya:"
"1042","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, Abdullah told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Hassan bin Attiya, Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani told me, Aws bin Aws Al-Thaqafi told me, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Who He washed and bathed on Friday, then he rose early and early, so he approached and listened and did not cancel. For every step he took, he had the reward of a year of action for performing it. And her fasting.” This hadith has been authenticated with these chains of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And I think it is a weak hadith that cannot be justified, such as These are similar chains of narrations, and it is a hadith:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1042 - It has a wasted defect"
"1043","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil told us, Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham told us, Ruh ibn Ubadah told us, Thawr ibn Yazid told us, on the authority of Uthman Al-Shaybani, that he heard Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, narrating on the authority of Aws bin Aws Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever performs the ritual ablution on Friday, performs ablution, approaches the imam, approaches, and listens and listens, will have the right to every step of the way.” They will receive the reward for fasting a year and standing in prayer.” This does not explain the proven and authentic hadiths from the following aspects: The first of which is that Hassan bin Atiyya / 63 He mentioned hearing Aws ibn Aws from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Secondly: Thawr ibn Yazid is below those who used him as evidence. Third: Othman Al-Shaybani is unknown.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1043 - Othman is unknown"
"1044","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Musa bin Harun, Saleh bin Muhammad Al-Razi, and Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, they said: Surayj bin Yunus told us, Harun bin Muslim Al-Ijli, Aban bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, he said: He entered upon me My father, I was taking a bath on Friday. He said: A bath for ritual impurity or for the Friday prayer? He said: I said: from ritual impurity. He said: Repeat another bath, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever bathes on a Friday will be in purity until Friday.” The other: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Harun bin Muslim al-Ijli is an old sheikh of the Basra people, called Al-Hanaa’i is trustworthy. Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abdullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated on his authority.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1044 - According to their condition"
"1045","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Abu Saeed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever washes himself on Friday, cleanses himself, wears his best clothes, and perfumes himself with perfume if he can find it, then comes and does not cross the path of people, and prays as long as God wills.” He prays, and when the imam comes out, he remains silent, that is atonement until the next Friday.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. It was also narrated by Ismail Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, similar to the narration of Hammad Ibn Salamah, and he attributed it to Abu Umamah Ibn Sahl. coupled with Abu Salamah """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1045 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1046","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, and Abu Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Abu Sa’id They said: We heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever bathes on Friday, cleanses himself, and touches perfume, if he has it and wears it, will do better.” His clothes, then he came to the mosque, and did not go beyond the necks of the people, then he bowed as long as God wished to bow, then he listened when his imam came out until He prays as an atonement for what was between it and the Friday prayer that was before it.” Abu Hurairah says: “And three additional days. Indeed, God has “He rewarded a good deed ten times more.” Ismail Ibn Ulayya was one of the trustworthy people who agreed to perform it.”"
"1047","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal in the year three hundred and ninety-five, Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Tabbaa told us, Musab bin Salam told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Ghaz, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he went out on Friday and sat on the pulpit, Bilal gave the call to prayer.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Hisham ibn al-Ghaz is one of those whose hadith is collected, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1047 - Musab is not an argument"
"1048","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sat on the pulpit on Friday, and said: To the people: “Sit down.” Ibn Masoud heard him while he was at the door of the mosque, so he sat down, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Come, Ibn Masoud.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1048 - According to their condition"
"1049","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail told us, Abdul Hamid told us, Al-Zayyadi’s companion, Abdullah bin Al-Harith, cousin of Muhammad bin Sirin, told us that Ibn Abbas said to his muezzin on a rainy day: If you say I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so do not say, “Live to prayer.” Say: “Pray in your homes.” It was as if the people had denounced that, and he said: “That one has done it.” He is better than me: Indeed, the Friday prayer is an appointed time, and I hated to send you out so that you would walk in mud and water.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1049 - True"
"1050","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad told us Ibn Ahmad Ibn Balawayh, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad Ibn Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khubayb Ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ma’n, on the authority of Bint Harithah bin Al-Nu’man, who said: “I did not memorize the Qur’an except from among the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It is recited every Friday.” She said: “Our enlightenment and the enlightenment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one.” This hadith. It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. “And the daughter of Harithah ibn al-Nu’man was named by Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar in a narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1050 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1051","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Hisham bint Harithah bin al-Numan, she said: “I read the glorious Qur’an from In the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he used to recite it every Friday when he addressed the people. Yahya bin Abdullah is Ibn Abdul Al-Rahman bin Asad bin Zurarah"
"1052","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ubayy and Shuaib told us, they said: Al-Layth told us, Khalid bin told us. Yazid, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us one day, and he recited P.S., when he passed by the prostration, he descended and prostrated, and we prostrated, and he recited it again. When he passed by the prostration, we rejoiced about the prostration. When he saw us, he said: “It is only The repentance of a prophet, but I see that you have prepared to prostrate, so he came down and prostrated and we prostrated. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. As for the prostration in the Book of Friday, it was included by Al-Bukhari, but the purpose of narrating it in this way in the Book of Friday is that when the Imam recites the prostration On Friday on the pulpit, it is part of the Sunnah for him to come down and prostrate.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1052 - According to their condition"
"1053","Hamza bin Abbas Al-Qanabi told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Hibban told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, and he told me Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi, and the pronunciation for him, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Yunus bin Abi told us Ishaq Al-Subaie, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, on the authority of Jarir ibn Abdullah, who said: When I approached the city of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I choked I mounted my mount, removed my robe, put on my suit, and entered while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering the sermon, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted me. People stared at me, so I said to my friend: O Abdullah, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention anything about my situation? He said: Yes, he mentioned you with the best of dhikr. He said: “Indeed, one of the best of Yemen will enter upon you from this door - or from this gate - from the best of Yemen. His face had the air of a king.” So I thanked God for what He had done for me. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it is the basis of the imam’s words in the sermon.” “As it seems to him at the time.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1053 - According to their condition"
"1054","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, entered on Friday and Marwan bin Al-Hakam was giving the sermon, so he got up to pray and then came The guards asked him to sit him down, but he refused until he prayed. When Marwan left, we went to him and said to him: May God have mercy on you, if they were about to do that to you. He said: I would not leave it after something I saw from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he mentioned a man who came on Friday and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He was delivering the sermon, then the next Friday came and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was giving the sermon, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered People wanted to give alms. The man threw off one of his clothes and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. Then he rebuked him and said: “Take your dress.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This man has entered the form of a garment, so I ordered the people to give alms.” So this man threw one of his garments on, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to pray two rak’ahs. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He is a witness to the hadith that came before him, and he has another witness according to Muslim’s condition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1054 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1055","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Khuza’i told us, in Mecca, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Zakaria Al-Makki told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us Al-Muqri, Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Rifa’ah Al-Adawi, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he He was giving a sermon, so I said: O Messenger of God, a strange man came asking about his religion. He does not know what his religion is? “So he came to me and left his sermon. A chair was brought with iron on its legs, and he began to teach me what God had taught him. Then he delivered his sermon and completed the last one
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1055 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1056","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Ya’qub bin Ka’b Al-Halabi told us, Mukhlid bin Yazid, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on the pulpit, he said: “Sit down.” Ibn Masoud heard this and sat at the door of the mosque. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him and said: “Come, O Abdullah bin Masoud.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1056 - According to their condition"
"1057","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Muhammad Al-Muqri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Saad Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr ibn Abi Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra al-Sawai’i, who said: Who told you that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He preached while sitting on the pulpit, but he lied. I witnessed him saying, “He used to deliver the sermon standing up, then he would sit down, then he would get up and deliver another sermon.” He said: I said: How was his sermon? He said: “The words he used to preach to the people, and he recites verses from the Book of God and then descends, and it was intentional - meaning his sermon - and his prayer was intentional.” In the direction of the sun and its bright morning, and the sky and the setting, except for the morning prayer and the noon prayer. Bilal used to call the call to prayer wherever the sun was setting, so if the Messenger of God came May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He stayed in prayer, otherwise he remained silent until he came out, and the afternoon prayer is similar to what you pray, and the Maghrib prayer is similar to what you pray, and the afterlife is He delays it from your prayers a little.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context, rather they included two brief expressions. From the hadith of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Simak: “He used to deliver two sermons with a sitting between them, and his prayer was intentional.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1057 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1058","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud told us, and Wahb bin Jarir Al-Hafiz told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak Bin Harb, he said: I heard Al-Numan bin Bashir, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivering a sermon, saying: “Did I warn you of the Fire? I warned you. Fire? Even if a man had been in the market, he would have heard it from this place of mine until a piece of sand fell on his shoulders at his feet. “This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1058 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1059","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, and Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal, they said: Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon, when Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came, wearing red shirts, stumbling and getting up. He came down and picked them up. So he placed them in his hands, then said: “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth {Indeed, your wealth and your children are a test} [Al-Taghabun: 15] I saw these two of my sons, and I did not “I was patient until I came down and took them.” Then he began his sermon. “This” is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He did not narrate it, and it is the basis of the hadith. “Cutting the sermon, and coming down from the pulpit when necessary.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1059 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1060","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Zahid told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us Ibn Abi Kathir, Sharik Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Nimr told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: I entered the mosque while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He delivered a sermon, so I sat close to Ubayy ibn Ka’b. “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited Surah Bara’a,” so I said to Ubayy, “When was this revealed?” Surah? “This hadith is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1060 - I do not think Ata’ caught up with Abu Dharr"
"1061","Ahmad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Adl Al-Saidalani told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abd Al-Rahman told us Ibn Mahdi, Muawiyah Ibn Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah Ibn Busr on Friday, and he continued to talk to us. Until the imam came out, and a man came, stepping on people’s necks while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering the sermon, so he said to him: “Sit down, for you have been hurt and have suffered.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1061 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1062","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ubaid bin Muhammad Al-Ijli told us, Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told me, Ishaq told me Ibn Mansour, Huraym Ibn Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Muhammad Ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of Qays Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abi Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Friday is a right and obligatory for every Muslim in a group except four: a owned slave, or a woman, Or a boy, or a sick person. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They all agreed to use Huraym ibn Sufyan as evidence and did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, “He did not mention Abu Musa in his chain of transmission, and Tariq ibn Shihab is among those who are counted in “Companions”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1062 - True"
"1063","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Malik bin Ismail told us, Israel told us, Othman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Iyas bin Abi Ramla Al-Shami, said: I witnessed Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan asking Zayd bin Arqam: Did Did you witness with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two Eids that came together in one day? He said: Yes. He said: How was it made? He said: He prayed the Eid prayer, then made a concession on Friday. He said: “Whoever wants to pray, let him pray.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and it has a witness according to Muslim’s condition.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1063 - True"
"1064","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Kathir Al-Humsi told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Baqiya told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Maqsim Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “On this day of yours, two Eids have gathered, so whoever wishes may do so from the Friday prayer, and we are unanimously agreed.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of Muslim’s condition: “There is no disagreement about Baqiyya ibn al-Walid’s truthfulness when he narrates on the authority of the famous people, and this is a strange hadith from the hadith of Shu’bah.” Al-Mughirah and Abd al-Aziz, and all of them are among those whose hadiths are collected.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1064 - Sahih Gharib"
"1065","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rufay’, on the authority of Tamim al-Ta’i, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, that a preacher delivered a speech to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Whoever obeys God and His Messenger has Rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray. He said: “Arise or go, for you are a miserable preacher.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1065 - According to their condition"
"1066","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman Al-Hadrami told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, My father, Al-Alaa bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rashid, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us “By shortening the sermons” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it has a valid witness according to the condition of Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1066 - True"
"1067","Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith told me, Ja'far bin Muhammad Al-Faryabi told me, Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told me, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, he told me Shayban Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prolong the sermon on the day of Friday, but they are simple words.”"
"1068","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, Muadh bin told me Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yahya ibn Malik, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bring Male, and come closer to the Imam, for the man will continue to distance himself until he is brought back into Paradise, even if he enters it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1068 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1069","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told me, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told me, Abu Marhum, on the authority of Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the crowding on Friday, “And the imam is giving the sermon.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1069 - True"
"1070","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, about Marw, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descend from the pulpit, and a man came to him in need, and he stood with him until “He fulfills his needs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1070 - According to their condition"
"1071","Mukhlid bin Ja`far al-Baqarhi told me, Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Faryabi told me, Zuhair bin Harb told us, Hushaym told us, Yahya bin Sa`id informed us, On the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in his room, and people were approaching him from behind the room.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1071 - According to their condition"
"1072","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Darbardi told us about Marwa, Abu al-Muwajih told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Abd informed us Al-Hamid bin Ja’far, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “If he was in Mecca and prayed the Friday prayer, he would come forward and pray He prayed two rak'ahs, then he went forward and prayed four. If he was in the city, he prayed Friday prayers, then he returned to his house and prayed two rak'ahs, but he did not pray in The mosque.” He was told, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. In this context, they only agreed on the hadith of Ibn Umar regarding the two rak’ahs in his house, and for a Muslim alone who used to pray four rak’ahs after Friday. Ibn Jurayj continued Yazid bin Abi Habib on his narration on the authority of Ata’ like this.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1072 - According to their condition"
"1073","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Anmati told us, Harun bin Abdullah told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, said: Ata’ told me that he saw Ibn Umar “praying on Friday, and he moved forward from his place of prayer in which he had prayed Friday.” A little, not a lot, so he should perform two rak’ahs. He said: “Then he would walk a little longer than that and perform four rak’ahs.” I said to Ata’: How often did you see Ibn Umar? Does he do that? He said: repeatedly"
"1074","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Sa’id told us Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Wadi’ah, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever takes a bath on the day Friday, so he washed well and purified himself well, and he put on the best of his clothes, and he touched what God had ordained for him of perfume or the oil of his family. “And he did not separate between two people except that God forgave him until the next Friday.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1074 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1075","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you falls asleep on Friday in his sitting... Let him leave that sitting.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1075 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1076","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Jundub, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, said: “We used to pray Friday prayers with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we used to hasten the spoils, but what “It will be only the size of one or two feet.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Rather, Al-Bukhari narrated it, on the authority of Abu Khaldah, on the authority of Anas, without This word """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1076 - True"
"1077","Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Iskandarani told me in Mecca, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Antaki told me, Muhammad ibn Maimun al-Iskandarani told me, al-Walid told me Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Who knows who? The Friday prayer is one rak’ah, and he has completed the prayer.”
 Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us,"
"1078","Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Usama bin Zaid Al-Laythi told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs a Friday rak’ah, let him pray it.” Other.” Osama said: I heard from the people of the council, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad and Salem that they used to say that.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1078 - It was narrated by Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar on the authority of Al-Zuhri in Sahih"
"1079","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, And Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who knows who? Friday prayer, let him perform another rak’ah.” All of these three chains of narrations are authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. They agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs one rak’ah of prayer, and whoever He completed one rak'ah of the afternoon prayer, and for a Muslim there is an extra rak'ah in it, he only performed all of it."
"1080","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Amr bin Khaled Al-Harrani told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to a people who were missing the Friday prayer: “I was planning to “I order a man to lead the people in prayer, then I burn their houses for a people who do not stay away from Friday prayer.” This is how it was narrated by Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, on the authority of Zuhair. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this, rather they narrated it by mentioning Al-Utma and the rest of the prayers.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1080 - According to their condition"
"1081","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam Al-Masri told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, Ibn Abi told us Dhib, on the authority of Usayd ibn Abi Usayd al-Barrad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Whoever neglects to pray Friday prayers for three days without necessity, God will put a seal on his heart.”"
"1082","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibn Abi Uwais told us, my brother told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Usayd bin Abi Usayd, so he mentioned him in a similar way. This is a hadith. In what was mentioned above in this book, I extracted from the hadith of Al-Thawri and others on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of Ubaida bin Sufyan Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Al-Ja’d Al-Damri, “I authenticated it according to the conditions of Muslim, and this is the eminent witness.” I found it later, and it has another witness from the hadith of Muhammad bin Ajlan, which is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1081 - True"
"1083","Abu Al-Qasim Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, in Nishapur, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Maadi bin Suleiman told us, Ibn Sufyan told us Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Is it possible that one of you takes a libation from the sheep on At the head of a mile or two, then it is difficult for him to graze at the top of a mile or two, so he rises until Friday comes, and he does not witness it until it is printed on the His heart
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1083 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"1084","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Abu Salamah Al-Tabudhaki told us, Nasih bin Al-Alaa, Ammar bin Abi Ammar told me, he said: I passed by Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah on Friday and he was by a river with water flowing over his servants. And his client, so I said to him: O Abu Saeed, it is Friday. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When there is heavy rain, then pray in your saddlebags.” Nasih bin Al-Ala Basri is trustworthy. “It is only” the stabbed one. Abu Abdullah Al-Muhallimi Al-Kufi advises on it, for Samak bin Harb narrated the evils from him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1084 - Al-Nasa’i’s weakness means Nasih bin Al-Ala’, and Al-Bukhari said the hadith is rejected."
"1085","Yahya bin Mansour al-Qadi told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin al-Nadr al-Jarudi told us, Nasr bin Ali al-Jahdhami told us, Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, that he witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the time of Al-Hudaybiyyah And they were struck by rain on the day of Friday, which did not wet the bottoms of their sandals. “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to pray on their saddles.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, and the two sheikhs used its narrations as evidence, and it is of the type in which they asked for the successors of the successors on the authority of the companions, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1085 - True"
"1086","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Handali told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Omar bin Ata bin Abi Al-Khawar told me that Nafi bin Jubayr sent him to Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid to ask him about something he had seen from him. Muawiyah, and he said: I prayed with him in the shrine, so I got up to pray in my place, and he said: “Do not pray until you have passed in front of that person or he has spoken, for The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do so.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1086 - According to their condition"
"1087","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, about Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “None of you should raise his brother from his place of sitting and then succeed him in it,” so I said Him: It is Friday. He said: “On Friday and other days.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not include it by adding additional mention of Friday. “Another [p. 433] Friday book
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1087 - according to their condition and they did not mention the end of it
 The Eid prayer book"
"1088","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abu Qalaba told us Al-Raqashi, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ali bin Hamshadh, and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, they said: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, They said: Abu Asim narrated to us, Thawab bin Utbah narrated, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He does not go out on the Day of Breakfast until he has eaten, and he does not eat on the Day of Sacrifice until he returns.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And Thawab Ibn Utbah Al-Mahri spoke little, and he did not use any type of hadith that would be dropped, and this is a cherished tradition in terms of extensive narration in the land of Muslims »
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1088 - True"
"1089","Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahan Al-Jazzar and Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Saffar told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Amr bin Aoun, narrated to us by Hushaym, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hafs bin Ubayd Allah bin Anas, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He breaks his fast on the Day of Fitr with dates before dawn.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness to his condition.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1089 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1090","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist, told us in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Zuhair informed us, and Abu Aoun the butcher, in Mecca, informed us, Ali informed us. Bin Abdul Aziz, they said: Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail told us, Zuhayr told us, Utba bin Al-Dhabi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Anas told us, He said: I heard a person saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not go out on the day of the breaking of the fast until he had eaten three dates, or five, or seven, or “Less than that, or more than that.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1090 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"1091","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina and they had two days to play, so he said: “What are these two days?” They said: Two days when we used to play during pre-Islamic times. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has given you something better in exchange for them. “Al-Adha and the Day of Fitr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1091 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1092","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan bin Amr told us, Yazid bin Khumayr al-Rahbi said: Abdullah bin Busr, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with the people on the day of Eid al-Fitr or Eid al-Adha. He denied that the imam was slow, and said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had finished this hour of ours, and that was when the glorification was glorified. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1092 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"1093","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Halim al-Marwazi told us, Abu al-Mawjih told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he finished the prayer, he said: “We will deliver the sermon. So whoever likes to sit for the sermon, let him sit, and whoever likes to go, let him go.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “They bring it out.” This is the meaning of the hadith about which people are asked during the holidays, except that it is on the authority of Ibn Abbas.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1093 - According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs"
"1094","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Issa bin Abdul told me. Al-A'la bin Abi Farwa, that he heard Abu Yahya Ubayd Allah Al-Taymi narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that they were struck by rain on the day Eid “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the Eid prayer with them in the mosque.” This “hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it.” Abu Yahya al-Taymi is authentic. “The wounded person was Yahya bin Ubaid Allah, his son.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1094 - According to their condition"
"1095","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Abu Ammar told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs bin Omar bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that “on the day of Eid he went out to the prayer place, but he did not pray.” Before or after it,” “and he mentioned that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording. But they agreed on the hadith of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray before or after it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1095 - True"
"1096","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad told us bin Zaid, and Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed before the sermon on the day of Eid.” This is the wording of the hadith of Ahmad ibn Abdah. And in the hadith of Suleiman there is a shortening: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1096 - According to their condition"
"1097","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, they said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far al-Ansari told me, Wahb bin Kaysan told me, He said: I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr in Mecca, and he was a prince, and it fell on the day of Fitr, or on Friday, “so he delayed going out until the day had risen. So he went out and climbed the pulpit and delivered a long sermon, then he prayed two rak’ahs but did not pray the Friday prayer. So some people from Banu Umayyad ibn Abd blamed him for it. Shams, and this reached Ibn Abbas, and he said: Ibn al-Zubayr was correct in the Sunnah, so this reached Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: “I saw Omar ibn al-Khattab when two sticks of wood were gathered together.” “He did something like this.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1097 - According to their condition"
"1098","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the day of Eid on one road, then returned on another road.”"
"1099","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Fulayh bin Suleiman, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to celebrate the two Eids, he would return on a different route.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” And the hadith before it, which is the hadith of Abdullah bin Omar
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1099 - according to their condition"
"1100","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Al-Tirmidhi told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Ibrahim bin Suwayd told us, Unays bin Abi told me Yahya, Ishaq bin Salim, from Banu Nawfal bin Adi, told me. Bakr bin Mubashir told me, he said: “I was going in the morning with the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. We will go to the prayer place on the day of Eid al-Fitr, and we will go through Buthan until we reach the prayer place, and we will pray with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we will return. To our homes”"
"1101","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Sakan told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, Dawud bin Qays told us, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out on the Day of Fitr and perform the fig prayer.” The two rak'ahs, then he would say the salutation, then he would stand up and face the people while they were sitting and say: “Give in charity, give in charity.” Most of the women who gave in charity were earrings. And the conclusion: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1101 - According to their condition"
"1102","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, Jandal bin Waqiq told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And when he returned from the prayer area, he said the salaam and prayed two rak’ahs. This is an honorable Sunnah, with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1102 - True"
"1103","Jafar bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ishaq bin Ismail Al-Talqani told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The people began fasting in the morning to complete thirty days, then two men came and testified that they They saw the crescent yesterday, “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the people to break their fast.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1103 - According to their condition"
"1104","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin al-Nadr al-Azdi told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, On the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I saw the crescent. Tonight. He said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?” He said: Yes. He said: “Arise, O Bilal, and give the call to the people so that they may fast.” Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim cited Samak as evidence. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission is circulated among the jurists, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1104 - True"
"1105","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Baghdadi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Hubaysh al-Dimashqi told us, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ata told us, Al-Walid bin Muhammad told us, Al-Zuhri told us, Salem bin Abdullah told me that Abdullah bin Omar told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to say “Allahu Akbar” on the day of Fitr from the time he left his house until he came to the place of prayer.” This hadith has a strange chain of transmission, and the text says “but the two sheikhs did not They use Al-Walid bin Muhammad Al-Muqqari as evidence, nor Musa bin Ata’ Al-Balqawi, and this is a Sunnah that was circulated by the imams of Ahl Al-Hadith, and it is authentic. The narration on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar and other companions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1105 - They are abandoned"
"1106","Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to “go out of the mosque on the two Eids and say takbir until he came to the place of prayer.”"
"1107","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Qubaysah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: “They were more severe in saying “Allahu Akbar” during breaking the fast than they were in saying “Allahu Akbar” during Eid al-Adha.”"
"1108","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ishaq bin Issa told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say takbeer on the two Eids, except for the takbir twelve times.” The opening, and the Glorious Qur’an will be recited, and the Hour has drawn near.” This is a hadith that was unique to Abdullah bin Lahi’ah, and he cited it as a martyr. Muslim in two places: “And in the chapter on the authority of Aisha, Ibn Umar, Abu Hurairah, and Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them,” and the paths to them. It is corrupt, and it was said on the authority of Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Aqeel.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1108 - Ibn Lahi’ah narrated it alone"
"1109","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Amr bin Khalid told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pronounce seven takbeers during the first two Eids, and in The second: Five takbeers before reading."
"1110","Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, in Hamadan, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Mahan told us, Musa bin Hazzam al-Tirmidhi told us, Abu Usama, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Umar were They pray the two Eids before the sermon.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they narrated the hadith of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas without this wording."
"1111","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Anbas Al-Qadi told us, Saeed bin Othman told us. Al-Kharaz, Abdul-Rahman bin Saeed Al-Muazzin told us, Fitr bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Ali and Ammar, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He would recite “In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful” aloud during the obligatory prayers, and he would recite Qunoot in the Fajr prayer, and he would say “Allahu Akbar” for the morning prayer on the day of Arafat. It is interrupted by the afternoon prayer, the last day of Tashreeq. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and I do not know of any of its narrations attributed to al-Jarh. It was narrated in Chapter on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah and others, “As for the verbs of Omar, Ali, Abdullah bin Abbas, and Abdullah bin Saeed, it is authentic from them.” Takbeer from the morning of Arafat until the end of the days of Tashreeq. As for the narration in it on the authority of ‘Umar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1111 - Rather, it is weak news, as if it were fabricated"
"1112","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh informed me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah ibn al-Hajjaj said: I heard Ata’, narrating on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab “used to say takbir after the dawn prayer on the day of Arafat until the noon prayer on the last day of Tashreeq.”
 As for the hadith of Ali"
"1113","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, Hanad told us, Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Ali “used to say “Allahu Akbar” after the Fajr prayer on the morning of Arafat, then he would not stop until the imam prayed on the last day of Tashreeq, then he would say “Allahu Akbar.” After the afternoon”
 As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas"
"1114","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Yahya bin Saeed told me, Al-Hakam bin Farrukh, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to “say takbir from the morning of Arafat until the afternoon prayer on the last days of Tashreeq.”
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud"
"1115","So Abu Yahya Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Samarqandi informed us, Muhammad ibn Nasr informed us, Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, Hushaym informed us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, he said: Ibn Masoud came to us and he used to “rejoice the takbir from the morning prayer on the day of Arafat until the afternoon prayer on the last day of Al-Tashreeq"
"1116","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, my father told us, he said, I heard Al-Awza’i, and he was asked about The takbeer on the day of Arafat, and he said: “He says takbeer from the morning of ‘Arafah until the end of the days of Tashreeq, just as Ali and Abdullah said takbeer.”
 The last book of the two Eids
 The Book of Witr"
"1117","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us dictation, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdullah bin Hamdan told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam, Abu Ja`far bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Amra Al-Najjari, that he asked Ubadah bin Al-Samit Concerning Witr, he said: It is a good matter, “the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Muslims after him did it, but it is not obligatory.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but there is evidence for it, including some.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1117 - According to their condition"
"1118","Maymun bin Ishaq Al-Hashimi told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, and Abu Muhammad told us Ibn Abdullah Al-Muzani, Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Ahmad Ibn Yunus, Al-Alaa Ibn Amr Al-Hanafi, and Muhammad Ibn Yazid. Al-Rifai and Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Kindi, they said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: Ali said May God be pleased with him: The Witr is not obligatory like your obligatory prayers, but the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the Witr and then said: “O people The Qur’an: “Recite Witr, for God is Witr. He loves Witr.” Among the evidences of this hadith are:"
"1119","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Abu Badr Shuja’ bin Al-Walid told us, Yahya bin Abi told us Hayya, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There are three things that are obligatory for me and for you are voluntary: sacrifice, And the Witr prayer, and the two rak’ahs of dawn.” Al-Hakim said: “The basis for this is the hadith of faith and the question of the Bedouins to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about prayers.” The fifth, he said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” And the hadith of Sa’eed bin Yasar on the authority of Ibn Omar in the Witr prayer on the camel, and the two sheikhs agreed to perform it in ""The correct one""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1119 - What Al-Hakim spoke about while he was a stranger and reprehensible"
"1120","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Yahya bin Ishaq al-Silahini told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: “When will you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I perform the Witr prayer before I sleep, and he said to Omar: “When do you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I sleep and then pray Witr. So he said to Abu Bakr: “You took it by force” or by the document, and he said to Omar: “You took it by force.” This is a hadith. “It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a witness with an authentic chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1120 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1121","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Ali bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein bin Idris told us. Al-Ansari, they said: Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Makki told us, Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Abu Bakr: “When do you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I perform Witr and then sleep. He said: “You took it with Jazm,” and he asked Omar and he said: “When do you perform Witr?” He said: I sleep, then I get up during the night and perform the Witr prayer. He said: “The strong verb, so I did.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1121 - True"
"1122","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, about Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Abu Nadhrah told me that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri told them that they asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace On the authority of the Witr prayer, he said: “Perform the Witr prayer before dawn.” Muammar ibn Rashid followed him, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir."
"1123","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Abd al-A’la told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do Witr before you rise in the morning.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it and he has a valid witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1123 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"1124","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Harun bin Ma’rouf told us, Ibn Abi Zaida told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Hasten to perform the witr prayer before dawn.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1124 - Sahih"
"1125","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein Al-Kisa’i told me, Abu Salamah Musa bin Ismail told us, Hisham bin Abu Abdullah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever catches the dawn prayer and does not perform the Witr prayer “There is no Witr for it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and it has a witness with a correct chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1125 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1126","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Suleiman bin Musa told me, Nafi’ narrated to me, that Ibn Umar used to say: Whoever prays at night should make his last prayer a witr prayer, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He gave the order for that, so when dawn came, all the night prayers and Witr prayers were cancelled, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform the Witr prayer.” ""before dawn""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1126 - Sahih"
"1127","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar told us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad bin Mutarrif, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who “If he fell asleep or forgot to perform Witr prayer, then let him pray it in the morning or remember it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1127 - according to their condition"
"1128","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib and Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, they said: Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Yusuf, Al-Awza’i told us, Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The Witr is a right, so whoever wishes may pray the Witr with five, and whoever wishes may pray the Witr with three, and whoever wishes may pray the Witr with one.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. “It was followed by Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Zubaidi, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and Sufyan bin Hussein. And Muammar bin Rashid, Muhammad bin Ishaq, and Bakr bin Wael on raising it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1128 - according to their condition
 As for the hadith of Al-Zubaidi"
"1129","So Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad the grammarian told us in Baghdad, Abd al-Karim bin al-Haytham told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin al-Tabba’ told us, Yazid bin Yusuf Al-Himyari told us, Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The string is five, or three, or one.”
 As for the hadith of Sufyan bin Uyaynah:"
"1130","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ismail bin Al-Abbas Al-Mustamli told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Hassan Al-Azraq told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Witr is a right, so whoever wishes He may pray the Witr with three, and whoever wishes may pray the Witr with five, and whoever wishes to pray the Witr with one may pray the Witr with one.”
 As for the hadith of Sufyan bin Hussein:"
"1131","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The witr is five. If you are able, then with three, if you are not able, then with one, and if you are not able,” then nod.
 As for the hadith of Muammar bin Rashid"
"1132","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Yahya bin Al-Ward told us, Ubayy told us, Adi bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The witr is true,” so he mentioned it similarly.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1132 - Adi left him
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Ishaq"
"1133","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: “The witr is true,” so he mentioned it as a condition for Abu Ayyub.
 As for the hadith of Bakr bin Wael"
"1134","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak, Quraysh narrated to us. Ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Bakr Ibn Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The string is true,” so he mentioned it in a similar way. Al-Hakim said: “I have no doubt that the two sheikhs left this hadith to stop some of al-Zuhri’s companions.” Oh, this is something that does not explain a hadith like this, and God knows best.”"
"1135","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Hatem bin Salem Al-Basri told us, Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed told us, On the authority of Khaled al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: Perhaps “I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performing witr prayers, and he rose People for the morning prayer” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1135 - Sahih"
"1136","Abd Al-Baqi bin Qani’ Al-Hafiz told us, Ziyad bin Al-Khalil Al-Tustari told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Hilal bin Ali, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If “If one of you wakes up in the morning and has not performed the Witr prayer, let him perform it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1136 - According to their condition"
"1137","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Tahir bin Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq told us, and Abu Yahya Ahmad bin Muhammad told us Al-Samarqandi, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Taher bin Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq told us, Ubayy told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray Witr with three prayers. Maghrib, but pray the Witr with five, or seven, or nine, or eleven rak’ahs, or more than that.”"
"1138","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman, and Abdul-Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not pray Witr with three prayers, and do not imitate the Maghrib prayer. Pray Witr with five, or with seven.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1138 - According to their condition"
"1139","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed informed us, and he told us Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Saad ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not greet The first two rak’ahs of Witr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And it has evidence, including”:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1139 - According to their condition"
"1140","What Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Shayban bin Farroukh bin Abi told us Shaybah, told us by Aban, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he made the Witr salaam with three salaams, only in the last of them. This is the Witr of the Commander of the Faithful Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. “And the people of The city »"
"1141","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salih al-Samarqandi told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Ja`far al-Darimi told us, Hibban bin Hilal told us, Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, Habib the teacher told us, he said: It was said to Al-Hasan: Ibn Umar used to say the salaam in the two rak’ahs of the Witr prayer, and he said: “Umar was more knowledgeable than him. He used to get up the third time by saying “Allahu Akbar.”"
"1142","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Fadl told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim, and Suleiman bin Harb told us, they said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, On the authority of Qays ibn Saad, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to “receive the Witr prayer with three prayers, not sitting during them, nor reciting the tashahhud except in the last of them.”"
"1143","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Saeed bin Ufayr told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra bint Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the two rak’ahs after which he would recite the tasbih in Witr.” “The name of your Lord is Most High, and say, ‘O you disbelievers.’” And it is recited in the Witr prayer with “Say, He is Allah, One and Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” Saeed bin Abi Maryam followed him, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub"
"1144","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani, they said: Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to pray the Witr prayer with three rak’ahs, reciting in the first rak’ah, “Glorify the name of your Most High Lord,” and in the second, “Say, O you disbelievers.” And in the third, “Say, ‘He is Allah, One,’ and say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of creation,’ and ‘Say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.’” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “Saeed bin Ufayr is the imam of the people of Egypt, without any defence, and he brought the hadith with a correct interpretation, indicating that the second rak’ah which is the Witr prayer is not... The two rak’ahs before it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1144 - Its narrators are trustworthy on his authority and it is according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"1145","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Omar told us, Hammam told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, My father told me that Aisha told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with five rak’ahs, and he would not sit except in the fifth, and he would not He acknowledges except in the fifth: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1145 - according to their condition"
"1146","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Abu Al-Munib Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The witr is a right, so whoever does not perform the witr is not From us"
"1147","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Abdullah told us Al-Ataki, so he mentioned it in a similar way. “This is an authentic hadith,” and Abu Al-Munib Al-Ataki is a trustworthy Maruzi whose hadith is combined “and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1147 - Al-Bukhari said: He has evil deeds"
"1148","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, and Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Qays bin Anif, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, they said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rashid Al-Zufi, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Murrah al-Zufi, on the authority of Kharijah bin Hudhafa al-Adawi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: “Indeed, God has provided you with a prayer that is better for you than red camels, which is the Witr prayer, and He placed it for you between the evening prayer and the dawn prayer.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Its narrators were Madani and Egyptians, and they did not abandon it except for what I mentioned about Al-Tabābi’s reluctance to “The Companion”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1148 - True"
"1149","Abdullah Muhammad bin Musa told me, Ismail bin Qutaybah told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, about Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the Witr prayer with thirteen times, but when he grew old and weak, He performed the Witr prayer with seven.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer with thirteen, and one Ten, nine, seven, five, three, and one, and the most correct of his Witr prayers, may God bless him and grant him peace, is with one rak’ah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1149 - according to their condition"
"1150","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Amr. Al-Fazari - Al-Darimi said: He is the oldest sheikh of Hammad bin Salamah - on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of his Witr prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and in Your pardon from Your punishment. And I seek refuge in You from You. I do not praise You as You have praised Yourself.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “The End of the Book of Witr”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1150 - True
 From the book of voluntary prayers"
"1151","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Orouba, and Ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya, who is Ibn Sa’id, told us, on the authority of Saeed, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurarah bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two rak’ahs of dawn are better than this worldly life.” All of them.” And in the hadith of Yazid bin Zuray’, “It is better than the world and all that is in it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1152","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Tamim bin Muhammad told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, Uthman told us Ibn Hakim, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, often recited in the two rak’ahs of Fajr: {Say, “We believe in God and in what was revealed to us and what was revealed to Abraham} [Al-Baqarah: 136] until the end of the verse and in the second rak’ah: {Say, O People of the Book Come to a common word between us and you} [Al Imran: 64] to his saying {And bear witness that we are Muslims} [Al Imran: 52] “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1152 - According to Muslim’s conditions"
"1153","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Amr bin Asim told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, On the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever forgets the two rak’ahs of dawn, let him pray them when the sun rises.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1153 - According to their condition"
"1154","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Waki’ told us, Salih bin Rustam, and Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, and the wording is his, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Mahmoud Al-Maruzi narrated to us, Abu Ammar narrated to us, Al-Nadr bin Shumayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The prayer was established, so I stood up and prayed the two rak’ahs. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, pulled me in and said: “Do you perform the morning prayer with four days?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1155","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, transmitting it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace be upon him, was asked: Which prayer is better after the obligatory prayer? Which fast is better after the month of Ramadan? He said: “The best prayer after the obligatory prayer is prayer in the middle of the night, and the best fasting after the month of Ramadan, God’s month of Muharram.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1156","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Muawiyah bin told me Salih, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “You must perform the night prayers, for it is the practice of the righteous before you, and it brings you close to your Lord, an expiation of evil deeds, and a prohibition from Sin” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1157","Abu Turab Ahmad ibn Muhammad, who reminds us of the camels, told me, Tamim ibn Muhammad told me, Muhammad ibn Aslam al-Zahid told us, Ma’mal ibn Ismail told us, Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, found something one night, and when morning came it was said: O Messenger By God, if the effect of the pain on you becomes clear, he said: “Indeed, I am only as you see, praise be to God. I have recited the long seven.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1158","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Yazid bin Khumayr, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Qais say: Aisha said to me: Do not neglect the night prayer, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not neglect it. And when he was sick or lazy, he would pray sitting.”"
"1159","Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, so he mentioned him. With the same chain of transmission and text as a whole, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1160","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sunni informed us about Marw, Abu Al-Muwajih told us, Abdan informed us, Abu Hamzah informed us, about Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever memorizes these prescribed prayers will not He will be written as one of the heedless, and whoever recites a hundred verses in one night will be written as one of the obedient.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1161","Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir informed us, Sa`d ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far told us, Abd al-Rahman Abi al-Zinad told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Salman, on the authority of his father, Abu Abdullah Salman Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays One night with one hundred verses will not be recorded as one of the heedless, but whoever prays two hundred verses one night will be recorded as one of the obedient and sincere. This hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1162","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, Sulaym bin Amir, Damrah bin Habib, and Nu’aym bin Ziyad told me, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, he said: Amr bin Absa told me, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was staying in Ukaz, and I said: O Messenger of God, is there any invitation nearer than another, or an hour remaining? Or should it be mentioned? He said: “Yes, the closest the Lord comes to the servant is in the middle of the night, so if you are able to be among those who remember God at that hour, then be.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1163","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya told me, my father told me, Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj told me, Abu Bakr told me. Ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qais, on the authority of the mothers of the believers, that they told him that God gave his Prophet evidence, and he said To them: Indicate to me what his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had indicated, so they said: “Indeed, God has guided him to praying the night prayers.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1164","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on a man who got up during the night and prayed and woke up His wife, if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. May God have mercy on a woman who gets up during the night and prays and wakes up her husband. If he refuses, she sprinkles water on her face. “The face of the water.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1165","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ya’la bin Mamlik, that he asked Umm Salamah about the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night, and she said: What’s the matter with you? His prayers? “He used to pray, then he would sleep as much as he prayed, then he would pray as much as he had slept, then he would sleep as much as he had prayed until morning,” and his recitation was described to him, so if It was described as “a reading explained letter by letter.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1166","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Ubayy told us, Imran bin Zaida bin Nashit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Khaled al-Walbi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that “when he got up during the night, he would raise his voice loudly, And he lowered it a step.” He used to mention that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1167","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me that Abdullah Ibn Abi Qais told him that he asked Aisha: What was the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the night? Was he reciting aloud or reciting quietly? She said: “He used to do all of that, sometimes out loud, and sometimes quietly.” He said: I said: Praise be to God who has made the matter expansive. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim.” A witness to the hadith of Abu Khaled, on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"1168","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told me, Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Silahini told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by Abu Bakr, While he was praying, he lowered his voice. He passed by Omar while he was praying, raising his voice. He said: When they met with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said to Abu Bakr: “O Abu Bakr, I passed by you while you were praying. Did you lower your voice?” He said: I heard the one I spoke to. He said: “I passed by you, O Omar, and you were raising your voice?” He said: O Messenger of God, I hope that with it I will awaken the teeth. He said: Then he said to Abu Bakr: “Raise your voice a little.” He said to Omar: “Lower your voice.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1169","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’, and Muhammad bin Yahya told us, they said: Abd told us Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet secluded himself May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in the mosque, and he heard them reciting aloud while he was in his dome, so he revealed the curtain and said: “Isn’t it that each of you is speaking to his Lord, and He does not “You annoy one another, and do not raise one over another in recitation in prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1170","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Raja bin Al-Sindi told us, Abu Kuraib told us, and Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, They said: Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Jafi narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abdah bin Abi Lubaba, on the authority of Suwayd. Ibn Ghafla, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever goes to his bed intending to stay up during the night So his eyes overwhelmed him until the morning, what he intended was recorded for him, and his sleep was a charity for him, a charity from his Lord.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and what I have is that they explained it with a pause that was narrated on the authority of Zaida.”"
"1171","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaydah narrated to us, so he mentioned it with its chain of transmission. From the words of Abu al-Darda’, and this is something that should not be weakened, for “Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Ja’fi is the oldest, most memorized, and most knowledgeable of the hadith of Zaydah than others. And God knows best.”"
"1172","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not specialize on Friday. “By fasting from among the days, and do not single out Friday night for spending the nights in prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1173","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Al-Layth told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Yahya bin Bukair told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, On the authority of Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, on the authority of his sister Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs on a day, God will build for him a house in Paradise, four before noon, and two after noon.” After that, two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer, two rak’ahs after sunset, and two rak’ahs before dawn.” Both of the chains of narrations are authentic on the condition that Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” The evidence for it is all authentic: among them is the follow-up of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, Makhoul Al-Faqih, and Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’.
 As for the hadith of Al-Numan bin Salem"
"1174","So Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yaz told us.
 As for the hadith of Makhulid bin Harun, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muadh told us Ibn Al-Muthanna, Musaddad told us, Bishr Ibn Al-Mufaddal told us, Dawud Ibn Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man Ibn Salim, on the authority of Anbasa Ibn Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays twelve prostrations voluntarily, God will build a house for him in Paradise »"
"1175","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, Al-Numan bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that she told him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever performs four rak’ahs before noon and four after it, God will condemn him to Hellfire.”"
"1176","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Musaddad told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal, my father told me, saying: Ismail, who is Ibn Ulayya, told us, on the authority of Uyaynah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: He said Buraidah: One day I went out to do something, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walking. I thought he wanted something, so I stopped. I continued to do that until he saw me and pointed to me, so I went to him and he took my hand. We all started walking, and I saw a man between Our hands pray, bowing and prostrating a lot. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you see this being seen?” So I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “So he sent out his hand and applied three passes between his hands. He raised his hands and straightened them and said: ‘You must provide a gift. You must follow an intentional guidance, for whoever overpowers this religion will be defeated by it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1177","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Zaid bin Hubab told us, Israel bin Yunus, on the authority of Maysarah bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that “he prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Maghrib prayer, then he prayed until he prayed the evening prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1178","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Abdullah bin Farroukh, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Honor your homes with some Your prayers
 The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Pray in your homes, and do not take them as graves.”
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Farukh, “His wording is amazing. He was an honest sheikh from the people of Mecca. He lived in Egypt and died there.”"
"1179","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid, Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: One day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Bilal and said: “O Bilal, what Did you race me to heaven? Yesterday I entered Paradise, and I heard your voice in front of me.” Bilal said: O Messenger of God, I have never called the call to prayer without praying two rak’ahs, and no event has ever happened to me without me performing ablution with him. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “With this,” this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1180","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Madini, he said: I heard Amara bin Khuzaymah, narrating on the authority of Uthman bin Hunaif, that a blind man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Pray to God to grant me health. He said: “If you want, you can delay that, and that is better, and if you want, I can pray.” He said: Call him. He said: So he ordered him to perform ablution and perform it well, and to pray two rak’ahs and say this supplication, saying: “O God, I ask you, And I turn to you through your Prophet Muhammad, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I have turned to you to my Lord regarding this need of mine, so that it may be fulfilled for me. Oh God, intercede for him on my behalf. “And grant me my intercession therein.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"1181","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ahmed bin Najda told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abdullah bin Wahb bin Muslim Al-Qurashi told us, he told me Haywa bin Shuraih, that Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid told him that Ayoub bin Khalid bin Abi Ayoub Al-Ansari told him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Keep the sermon, then perform ablution, and perform your ablution well, then pray what God has ordained for you. Then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: Oh God, you are able and I am not able, and you know and I am not aware, and you are the Knower of the unseen, so if you see so-and-so for me You call it by its name, which is better for me in my religion, in this world, and in my hereafter, so ordain it for me, and if other than it is better for me than it in my religion, in this world, and in my hereafter, then make up for it “Or say: ‘Decree it for me.’ This is the Sunnah of the Istikharah prayer, dear and unique to the people of Egypt, and its narrations from the rest of them are trustworthy, and none He brings him out.”"
"1182","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ismail bin Ubaid Allah bin Zurarah Al-Raqi told us, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one performs the Duha prayer regularly except one who is steadfast.” He said: “It is the prayer of the returnees.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1183","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Bakr bin Mudar told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told us, On the authority of Bukayr ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi, he narrated it on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On a journey, he prayed eight rak'ahs of the morning prayer, and when he left, he said: “Indeed, I prayed a prayer of desire and awe. I asked my Lord for three, and He gave me two.” And he denied me one thing. I asked him not to kill my nation with years of age, and he did. I asked him not to appear to them as an enemy, and he did. I asked him not to wear them. Shiites, but he refused me.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Umm Hani regarding the eight rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer. Just """
"1184","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told me, Uthman ibn Abu Suleiman, that Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told him that Aisha told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die until Most of his prayers were sitting. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1185","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein Al-Kisa’i told me, Al-Rabi’ bin Yahya told us, Yazid bin Ibrahim Al-Tustari told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq Al-Uqaili, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying standing and sitting, then... If he began the prayer standing, he bowed standing, and if he began the prayer sitting, he bowed sitting.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this. The wording: “I narrated it before this from the hadith of Humayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, and this is its place, and the hadith of Ibn Sirin, this is evidence It is true for what was mentioned above."
"1186","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abraham Bin Tahman, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu'allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, that Imran bin Husayn said: I had a fistula, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Pray standing, and if you are not able, then sitting, and if you are not able, then on your side.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Yazid bin Zuray’, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, in brief."
"1187","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, my father and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, they said: We told us: Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Busra Al-Ghaffari, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, that he said: “I traveled Eighteen journeys were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, abandon the two rak’ahs when the sun set. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 It was narrated by Fulayh bin Suleiman, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Busra Al-Ghafari, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, who said: “I traveled with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “I did not see him abandoning the two rak’ahs before noon.”"
"1188","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Abdul Salam told us Ibn Hashim, Othman Ibn Saad Al-Kateb told us, and he had courage and reason, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not He descended a certain place unless he bid farewell to it with two rak’ahs.” This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it. “And Uthman bin Sa’d al-Katib is among those whose hadith is collected in The Basrians"
"1189","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Shaiban told us, On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Al-Aghar, Abu Muslim, on the authority of Abu Sa'id, and Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever wakes up during the night and wakes up his family and prays two rak’ahs together, is recorded as one of the men and women who remember God frequently.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1190","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, and he told me Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzaki told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Abdi told us, they said: Abu Ayyub bin Abdul Rahman al-Dimashqi told us, said: Al-Walid bin Muslim, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, and Ikrimah, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that while he was He was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Ali bin Abi Talib came to him and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God, this one has escaped. The Qur’an is from my heart, and I do not find that I am capable of it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Abu Al-Hasan, shall I not teach you words that will benefit you? May God bless them, and will they benefit whomever you teach them, and will what you have taught become firm in your heart? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God, teach me. He said: “If it is Friday night, then if you are able to get up during the last third of the night, then It is a marked hour, and supplications will be answered in it. It is what my brother Jacob said to his sons, “I will ask my Lord for forgiveness for you until Friday night comes.” If you are not able, then stand in the middle of it, and if you are not able, then stand in the beginning of it, and pray four rak’ahs, in the first of which you recite the Fatihah of the Book, And Surat Yasin,And in the second rak'ah with the Fatihah of the Book and the prostration, and in the third rak'ah with the Fatihah of the Book, and the smoke, and in the fourth rak'ah With the opening of the Book, and Blessed be the detailed one, so when you have finished reciting the tashahhud, praise God, and praise God best, and bless me and the rest of the prophets. And do good, and ask forgiveness for your brothers who preceded you in faith, and ask forgiveness for the believing men and believing women, then say at the end of that: O God Have mercy on me in abandoning sins as long as You keep me, and have mercy on me from being burdened with things that do not concern me, and grant me good consideration of what pleases You with me, O God. Creator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty, honor, and glory that is incomparable, I ask you, O God, O Most Merciful, by your majesty and the light of your face, Make my heart oblige to memorize Your Book as You have taught me, and grant me to recite it in a way that pleases You with me, O God, the Creator of the heavens and the earth. Glory, honor, and glory that is incomparable. I ask you, O God, O Most Merciful, by your majesty and the light of your countenance, to enlighten my sight with your book, and to You free my tongue with it, and you relieve my heart with it, and you open my chest with it, and you occupy my body with it, for no one can help me to the truth except you. And no one gives it except You,There is no power nor strength except in God, the Most High, the Great, Aba Al-Hasan. You can do that in three plurals, or five, or seven. He will be answered, God willing. By the One who sent me with the truth, he never made a mistake as a believer.” Abdullah bin Abbas said, “By God, Ali did not stay with me except five, or seven, until he came.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in such a gathering and said: O Messenger of God, I was recently not learning four verses or So if I recite them to myself, they slip away. As for today, I am learning forty verses and the like, so if I recite them to myself, Just as the Book of God is before my eyes, and I used to hear the hadith and if I wanted it, I would slip away, and today I hear the hadiths, but if I narrated them I would not Knock out a letter from it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him at that: “A believer, and the Lord of the Kaaba is Abu Al-Hasan.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not narrate it.”"
"1191","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hatim informed us about Marw, Abu al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, he informed us Ikrimah bin Ammar, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha informed me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that Umm Sulaim went to visit the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And she said: Teach me words to say in my prayer, and he said: “Glorify God ten times, glorify God ten times, or praise Him ten times, then ask what Whatever you want, he says: Yes, yes “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and its witness is the hadith of the Yemenis regarding the Tasbih prayer.”"
"1192","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Ubaidullah told us, Bishr bin Al-Hakam told us Al-Abdi, Musa bin Abdul-Aziz Al-Qunbari told us, in Aden, and Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq informed us Bin Yusuf, Abdul Rahman bin Bishr bin Al-Hakam bin Habib Al-Hilali told us, Musa bin Abdul Aziz Abu Shuaib, who is called: Al-Qanbari in Aden, Al-Hakam bin Aban told us, Ikrimah told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib: “O Abbas, O his uncles, should I not give you, should I love you, should I not do ten good things to you? If you do that, may God forgive you.” Your sin, the beginning and the end, the old and the recent, the mistake and the intentional, the small and the big, the secret and the open: to pray four rak’ahs. In each rak'ah, you recite the Fatihah of the Book and a surah. When you finish reciting in the first rak'ah, you say while standing: Glory be to God, and praise be to God. To God, and there is no god but God, and God is the greatest fifteen times, then you kneel and say it ten times while you are bowing, then you raise your head and say it Ten, then you prostrate and say it ten, then you raise your head and say it ten, then you prostrate and say it ten, then you raise your head and say it Ten, that is seventy-five in each rak’ah, which you should do in four rak’ahs. If you are able to pray it every day, then do so. If not, You do it once every Friday. If you do not, then once every month. If you do not, then once every year. If you do not, then during your lifetime. Once: “This is a hadith that was transmitted to Musa bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, and it was narrated by Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq and Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath and Abu Abd Al-Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib in Al-Sahih, they narrated it on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Bishr, and Ishaq narrated it Ibn Israel, on the authority of Musa Ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Qanbari,"
"1193","Muhammad bin Harun bin Sulayman al-Hadrami told us, Ishaq bin Abi Israel told us, Musa bin Abdul Aziz Abu Shuaib al-Qanbari told us.” So he mentioned the hadith in one word similar to it. As for the situation of Musa bin Abdul Aziz, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub told me, narrated to me. Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz, Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us, he said: I heard Abdul Razzaq, and he was asked about Abu Shuaib. Al-Qunbari was praised well, and as for Al-Hakam bin Aban’s condition, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Wasil Al-Bikandi told me, my father praised us, he told me Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Bukhari, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, he said: I asked Yusuf bin Yaqoub: How was Al-Hakam bin Aban? He said: That is our master. He said: That is our master. As for Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban sending this hadith, on the authority of his father"
"1194","So Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, and Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, they said: Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hakam told me. Ibn Aban, my father told me, Ikrimah told me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his uncle Abbas, and he mentioned the hadith. “This transmission does not weaken the connection of the hadith, for the increase in confidence is more important than the transmission, given that the imam of his time in hadith was Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanathili established this chain of narration, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban, and transmitted it.”"
"1195","Abu Bakr ibn Quraysh informed us, Al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanthali informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn al-Hakam informed us. Aban, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Musa bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Hakam “The narration is authentic, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught his cousin Jafar bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, this prayer as his uncle Al-Abbas, may God be pleased with him, taught it.”"
"1196","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating from the original of his book, Ahmed bin Dawud bin Abdul-Ghaffar narrated to us in Egypt, Ishaq narrated to us. Ibn Kamil, Idris Ibn Yahya told us, on the authority of Haywa Ibn Shuraih, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He took Ja’far ibn Abi Talib to the land of Abyssinia. When he came, he embraced him and kissed him between his eyes, then said: “Shall I not give you a gift? “Shall I give you good news, shall I not give you good news, shall I not reward you?” He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “You pray four rak’ahs, reciting in each rak’ah the praise and a surah, then you say after the recitation while standing before bowing: Glory be to Him.” God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, God is great, and there is no power but from God fifteen times, then you kneel down and say them. Complete this rak’ah ten times before you begin the second rak’ah. Do the three rak’ahs as I described until you complete four. Rakats “This chain of transmission is authentic and beyond doubt, and what is evidence of the authenticity of this hadith is the imams’ use of We taught them this and they persevered in it and taught the people, among them was Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, may God have mercy on him.”"
"1197","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Jarrah Al-Adl told us about Marwa, Yahya bin Sasawayh told us, Abdul Karim bin Abdullah Al-Sukkari told us, Abu Wahb Muhammad ibn Muzahim narrated to us, saying: I asked Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak about the prayer in which the tasbih is recited, and he said: “You say takbeer and then you say: Glory be to You.” Oh God, and with your praise, and blessed be your name, and exalted is your grandfather, and there is no god but you, then you say fifteen times: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god Except Allah, and Allah is the Greatest, then you seek refuge and recite In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful and the Opening of the Book and a surah, then you say ten times: Glory be to Him God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great, then you kneel and say it ten, then you raise your head and say it ten, then You prostrate and say it ten, then you raise your head and say it ten, then you prostrate the second and say it ten, then you raise your head and say it Ten times you pray four rak'ahs in this manner, and that is seventy-five tasbihs in each rak'ah, and that is the completion of three hundred, so if he prays it at night So I would love for him to say the salaam in the two rak’ahs. If he prays during the day, then he can say the salaam if he wishes, and if he wishes, he should not say the salaam.” The narrators of this hadith are on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak. They are all trustworthy and proven, and Abdullah cannot be accused of teaching him unless his chain of transmission is authentic.”"
"1198","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Awdi told us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Samina told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Fudayl, Rashidun bin Kurayb told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The two rak’ahs before the dawn prayer The end of the stars, and the two rak’ahs after sunset, the end of the suhoor.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. He did not narrate it, and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Hammad. Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zaid, on the authority of Aws Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and it is not a condition of this book.”"
"1199","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, and Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told me, Muhammad bin Ayoub, they said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Faid Abu Al-Warqa’ Al-Attar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of God came out against us. One day, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he sat down and said: “Whoever has a need from God, or from one of the sons of Adam, let him perform ablution and do good.” his ablution, then let him pray two rak’ahs, then praise God, and send blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Gracious. Glory be to God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. I ask you for your forgiveness, protection from every sin, and safety from... Every sin “Fa’id ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Warqa’ is a Kufi, numbered among the Successors, and I have seen a group of his followers, and he is upright in hadith However, the two sheikhs did not narrate it, but rather I made this hadith of his as a witness to what was mentioned above.”"
"1200","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Hasanjani told us, Abu al-Tahir Ahmad ibn Amr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Hayy bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Indeed, in Paradise there are rooms whose outside can be seen from their inside, and their inside from their outside.” Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari said: Who are they for, O Messenger? God? He said: “For the one who speaks kindly, gives food, and spends the night standing while the people are asleep.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1201","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh narrated to me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr narrated to me, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Talha Ibn Yazid Al-Ansari, on the authority of Hudhayfah Ibn Al-Yaman, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, one night of Ramadan, in a room made of palm leaves. He said: Then he stood up and said, “Allahu Akbar, the Possessor of power and kingdom, and the Possessor of Pride and greatness,” “Then Al-Baqarah opened and recited,” so I said: He reaches the head of a hundred, then I said: He reaches the head of two hundred. He said: “Then Al-Imran opened and recited it, then Al-Nisa’ opened and recited it. He did not pass by the verse of intimidation except he stood and sought refuge, then he bowed as he had done.” He stood up and said: “Glory be to my Lord the Great,” repeating them, then he raised his head and said: “God hears those who praise Him. O God, our Lord, praise be to You.” Like He bowed, then prostrated as he had stood, saying: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,” and between the two prostrations he said: “My Lord, forgive me.” He only prayed four rak’ahs. From the dark prayer from the beginning of the night until the end, “until Bilal came and called him to the morning prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 The book of forgetfulness"
"1202","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz told us, dictating, in Rajab in the year three hundred and ninety-five. Muhammad told me Ibn Al-Qasim Ibn Abdul-Rahman Al-Atki, Ismail Ibn Qutayba Al-Sulami and Ahmad Ibn Muhammad Ibn Sirin Al-Jurjani told us, they said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him reject the doubt, and build on certainty. The perfect one prostrated two prostrations. If his prayer was complete, the rak'ah was voluntary and the two prostrations were voluntary, and if it was incomplete, then the rak'ah was complete. For his prayer, and the two prostrations force the nose of Satan.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context."
"1203","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ayoub bin Bilal bin Suleiman told us, Abu Ismail told me Bakr bin Abi Uwais, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad Zaid bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul God Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you prays and does not know how many times he has prayed, three or four times, let him bow one rak’ah in order to do good.” His prostration and bowing, then he prostrates two prostrations.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1204","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Muhajir told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Suleiman bin Daoud Al-Mahri told us, Abdullah bin Wahb, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim told me, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Buhaynah, that he said: “He prayed The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us one of the prayers, so he stood up after two prayers and recited the rosary in it, and proceeded on until he finished his prayer, and nothing remained but the greeting. He prostrated two prostrations while sitting before he said the salutation.” This is an authentic, interpreted hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1205","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiya told us, Ismail bin Abi told us Khalid, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, that “he stood up in the two rak’ahs, and they recited the tasbih with him, and he remained complete, then he prostrated with two prostrations.” Forgetting” when he left and said: Did you see me sitting? I only did as “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1206","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Daqqaq told us, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us My father, he said: I heard Yahya bin Ayyub, speaking on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj, who said: “I prayed with The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed Maghrib and said the salutation in two rak’ahs, then he left.” Then a man said to him: O Messenger of God, you made a mistake and performed the salutation in two rak’ahs. So he ordered Bilal to establish the prayer, then he completed that rak’ah. So I asked the people. On the authority of the man who said: O Messenger of God, you made a mistake and it was said to me: Do you know him? I said: No, unless I see him, then a man passed by me and I said: This is him. They said: This is Talha bin Ubaid Allah. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1207","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told me, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Hanzali told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik Al-Hamrani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abi Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited the tashahhud during the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said the salutations.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but they agreed on the hadith of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, and there is no mention of the tashahhud for the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"1208","Abu Ahmad bin Abi Al-Hasan told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Ash’ath told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Khaled al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed With them, he made a mistake in his prayer, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after saying salaam and speaking.”"
"1209","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hatim Al-Adl told me about Marw, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told us, Yusuf bin Issa told us, Al-Fadl bin told us. Musa, Abdullah bin Kaysan told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the two forced prostrations of forgetfulness.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not narrated by “Abu Mujahid Abdullah bin Kaysan, trustworthy, from among those whose hadiths are compiled in al-Marawaza.”"
"1210","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Bayan told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Harb bin Shaddad, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, Iyad told me, he said: I asked Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri, and I said: One of us prays and does not know how many times he prayed. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays and does not know how many times he has prayed, let him prostrate twice, and when Satan comes to one of you He said: You have told something, so let him say, “You lie,” unless he feels a scent in his nose, or hears a sound with his ear. “This is an authentic hadith, subject to the condition.” The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”"
"1211","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Salam told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Rasibi told us, Ammar bin Matar Al-Rahawi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Thabit told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever makes a mistake in his prayer on three or four days, let him complete it, for the extra “Better than decrease.” This is an interpreted hadith with a sound chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it."
"1212","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Yahya bin Saleh Al-Wahazi told us, Abu Bakr told us Al-Ansi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no oversight in “The leap of prayer is one of standing from sitting, and sitting from standing.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1213","Abu Zakaria Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Anazi narrated to us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja`far al-Muzaki narrated to us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Al-Abdi, Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib Al-Harrani told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: I sat with Omar bin Al-Khattab, who was a caliph, and he said: O Ibn Abbas, I did not hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or from anyone. Who among its companions mentions what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded if a person made a mistake in his prayer? I said: No, have you not heard, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: No, then Abdul Rahman bin Awf entered and said: What are you doing? Omar said: I asked him whether he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or one of his companions mention what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had ordered. And peace be upon him if a person makes a mistake in his prayer, and Abdul Rahman said: I have knowledge of that, so Omar said: Come, you are just and satisfied, so Abdul said The Most Gracious: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If one of you doubts about two, let him make them one, and if he doubts about two, let him make them one. And the three, let him make them two, and if he is in doubt about the three and four, let him make them three, then complete the remainder of his prayer until it is The illusion of adding more, then he prostrates two prostrations while sitting before he gives the salutation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim who witnesses the hadith of Abd Al-Rahman bin Thabit bin Thaban, whom I dictated to before these two hadiths.”"
"1214","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Munqidh Al-Khawlani told us, Idris bin Yahya told us, Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib said that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Shamasa al-Mahri say: “Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani led us in prayer, and he stood up with a seat on him,” so he said People: Glory be to God, Glory be to God, “So he did not sit down and continued standing, so when he was at the end of his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting,” so when he saluted He said: “Indeed, I just heard you saying: Glory be to God, so that I may sit, but the Sunnah that I have established” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
 The book of rain"
"1215","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us Al-Umari, Muhammad bin Aoun bin Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim bin Shihab Al-Zuhri told me, Abu Salamah told me, Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A prophet from among the prophets went out to draw water, and behold, it was an ant.” Raising some of its legs to the sky, he said, “Return, for I have answered you because of the ant.”
 This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1216","Abu Ja`far Abdullah bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Al-Mansur told us, in the house of the Commander of the Faithful Al-Mansur, dictation, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us Ibn Issa Ibn al-Tabba’, my uncle Ishaq Ibn Issa told me, Hafs Ibn Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ja’far Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “He drew water for The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he turned his robe to avoid the drought. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1217","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told me, Sahl bin Bakkar told me, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abdul told me. Al-Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, said: Marwan sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about the Sunnah of raining rain, and he said: “It is Sunnah.” Asking for rain is the Sunnah of prayer on the two Eids, except that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned his robe over, placing his right side over his left, and his left over To his right, he prayed the two rak'ahs, saying ""Allahu Akbar"" seven times in the first, and reciting ""Glorify the name of your Lord Most High"", and in the second he recited ""Has a hadith reached you?"" Al-Ghashiya, and he said “Allahu Akbar” five times. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it."
"1218","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Othman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Ismail bin Rabi’ah bin Hisham bin Ishaq said: I heard my father telling, on the authority of his father Ishaq bin Abdullah, that Al-Walid sent him To Ibn Abbas, and he said: O son of my brother, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do when praying for rain on the day he asked people for rain? He said: “The Messenger of God came out God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, humbly humbled, submissive, and humble, so he did therein what He does at Breakfast and Eid al-Adha.” This hadith was narrated by Egyptians. And civilians, and I do not know of any of them attributed to some type of wound and they did not remove it.” It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Hisham ibn Isaac"
"1219","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Saffar told us, in Baghdad, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, we told him Waki`, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of his father, he said: One of the princes sent me to Ibn Abbas, I asked him about praying for rain. Ibn Abbas said: What prevented him from asking me? “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out humbly. He was arrogant, humbled, supplicating, and begging. He prayed two rak’ahs as he prays on Eid, but he did not propose to you.”"
"1220","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not raise his hands in any of his supplications except when praying for rain.” Shu’bah said: So I said to Thabit: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to God. I said: Did you hear from Anas? He said: Glory be to God. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Muslim narrated it, from the hadith of Yahya bin Abi Bukayr, on the authority of Shu’bah.”"
"1221","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, about Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked for water, and he was wearing a khamisah.” It was black, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to take the bottom of it and make it the top of it. When it became heavy for him, her heart was heavy on her. “Ataqih” They agreed to narrate the hadith of Abbad bin Tamim, but they did not narrate it with this wording, and it is authentic according to Muslim’s condition."
"1222","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, Mas’ar bin Kadam told us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: She came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, weeping, and he said: “O God, give us abundant rain, bitter and horrific, urgent and not Later, beneficial and not harmful, so the heaven closed over them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1223","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umair, the client of Abu al-Lahm, that “he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the oil stones He draws water, covering his hands with his hands, calling like this.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And Umair, the servant of Abi Al-Lahm, has companions and is in good health.” That »"
"1224","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Qutaibah told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Umair, the servant of Abi Al-Lahm, He said: “I witnessed Khaybar with my masters, and they spoke to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that I am a mamluk, so he gave me an order, so I took up the sword, and lo and behold, I I rewarded him, so he ordered me some of my belongings, and I showed him a ruqyah that I used to recite ruqyah for insane people, so he ordered me to throw some of it away, and keep some of it away.”"
"1225","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told me, Khaled bin Nizar told me, Al-Qasim bin Mabrur, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: People complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. The rain began to dry, so he ordered a pulpit to be placed in the prayer area, and he promised the people a day on which they would go out. Aisha said, so the Messenger of God came out When the visor of the sun appeared, he sat on the pulpit and said the takbir and thanked God, then he said: “You have complained about the barrenness of your homes. And keeping the rain from its appointed time, and God has commanded you to call upon it, and He has promised you that He will respond to you, then He said: “Praise be to God, Lord.” Of the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment, there is no god but God. He does what He wants. Oh God, you are there is no god but You, the Rich, and we “The poor, send down upon us rain, and make what You have sent down for us strength and enlightenment for a while.” Then he raised his hands and continued to raise them until they appeared white. His armpits, then he turned his back to the people, and he turned or turned his robe while raising his hands, then he turned to the people, got down and prayed two rak’ahs. Then God created clouds, and they thundered and flashed, and then it rained, God willing. He did not come to his mosque until the floods poured in. When he saw their haste to He laughed until his molars became visible, and he said: “I bear witness that God has power over all things, and that I am the servant of God and His Messenger.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"1226","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abd al-Rahman bin told me Al-Husayn Al-Qadi, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja'd, on the authority of Shurahbil bin Al-Samit, that he said to Ka'b bin Murrah or Murrah bin Ka'b: Narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicating for Mudar, so I went to him and said: O Messenger of God, God has given you and has answered you. And if your people have perished, then pray to God for them, and He said: “O God, give us rain that is quick to relieve, quenching, and quickly pouring in a steady stream, not fouling, beneficial, not harmful.” It was only one Friday or so ago that they were given water to drink. “This is an authentic hadith whose chain of narration is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs.” Bahz bin Asad Al-Ammi, trustworthy and proven. “He narrated it, on the authority of Shu’bah, with his chain of transmission, on the authority of Murrah ibn Ka’b,” and there was no doubt about it, and Murrah ibn Ka’b al-Bahzi was a famous companion."
"1227","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Suleiman told us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani told us, Bahz bin Asad told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Shurahbil ibn al-Samat, on the authority of Murrah ibn Ka’b, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, prayed for rain, and said: “O God, give us abundant rain, quick relief, abundant rain, hastening without spoilage, beneficial and not harmful.” So what It was only a Friday or the like until they were given water for the last [p. 478] Book of Rain.
 The book of eclipses"
"1228","Abu Qutaibah Salam bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami told us in Mecca, Abu Shuaib Al-Harrani told us, Ibn Abdullah Al-Madaini told us, Salim bin Nuh told us. Al-Attar, Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Hayyan bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samra, who said: “While I was shooting arrows, they were exposed The sun, so I threw it away, and went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and came to him while he was standing, raising his hands, glorifying, glorifying, and giving thanks. And he prayed to his Lord until the time came, and he recited two surahs in two rak’ahs.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1229","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Abbas Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “The sun eclipsed during the time of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and stood for a long time until it was said that he should not kneel, then he kneeled and prolonged the bowing until He was told not to rise, then he raised his head and prolonged his standing until he was told not to bow, then he bowed and prolonged his bowing until it was said not to rise, then he raised his head. So he prolonged his standing until it was said that he should not prostrate.” The rest of the hadith was mentioned by the hadith of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, an authentic stranger. “The two sheikhs protested.” “By Mu’mal bin Ismail, and they did not narrate it. As for Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, they did not narrate it.”"
"1230","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Zuhayr told us, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Abu Nu’aym told us, Zuhair told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, Tha’labah bin Abbad Al-Abdi, from the people of Basra, told me that He witnessed a sermon one day by Samurah ibn Jundub, and he mentioned in his sermon that Samurah said: One day while I and a boy from the Ansar were throwing a target for us During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, even when the sun was the size of two or three spears in the eye of the observer from the horizon, it became black until It shone as if from sleep, so he said: One of us to his friend, go with us to the mosque, and by God they will tell the Messenger of God about this sun. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. There was an event in his nation, so we went to the mosque, and behold, it was prominent. “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, agreed with us when he came out. To the people. He said: Then he came forward and led us in prayer like the longest he had ever led us in prayer, and we could not hear his voice. Then he kneeled with us like he had kneeled with us the longest. He prayed without us ever hearing his voice. Then he prostrated with us like the longest he had ever prostrated with us in prayer. We never heard his voice. He said: Then he did the rak’ah. The second is like that. He said: The rising of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak’ah.He said: Then he greeted, thanked and praised God, and testified that there is no god but God, and testified that he is His servant and Messenger. Then he said: “O O people, I am only a human being and the Messenger of God, so I remind you of God if you know that I have fallen short in conveying the messages of my Lord when You told me that I would convey the messages of my Lord as they should be conveyed, even though you knew that I had conveyed the messages of my Lord when You informed me. He said: Then the people stood up and said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your nation, and fulfilled what was owed to you. He said: Then They remained silent, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for what follows, there are men who claim that the eclipse of this sun, the eclipse of this moon, and the disappearance of These stars are from their rising because of the death of great men from the people of the earth, and indeed they lied, but they are signs of God with which He tempts His servants. Let him see who among them repents. By God, I have seen since I rose up praying what you will encounter in this world and the hereafter, and it is By God, the Hour will not come until thirty liars come out, the last of whom is the one-eyed Antichrist. From the Ansar, and when he comes out, he claims that he is God.So whoever believes in him, believes him, and follows him, no good deeds of his predecessor will benefit him, and whoever disbelieves in him and disbelieves in him, no good deeds of his predecessors will benefit him, and indeed he He will appear over the entire earth except the Sanctuary and the Holy House, and He will confine the believers in the Holy House and they will be shaken severely. Then Jesus, the son of Mary, will become among them, and God will defeat him and his soldiers, to the point that the wall and the roots of the trees are bruised to the point of calling for the believer. This is an infidel. He hides himself from me, so come and kill him.” He said: “That will not happen until you see matters escalating within yourselves and ask among yourselves: Was it Your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned to you a mention of it, until the mountains were removed from their moorings, and then as a result of that arrest,” and he indicated With his hand, he said: Then he witnessed another sermon. He said: He mentioned this hadith, neither the beginning nor the end of it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1231","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Jaafar bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi told us, Yaqoub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah told us Al-Uwaisi, Muslim bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the sun was eclipsed on the day Ibrahim Ibn The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people thought that it had been eclipsed due to his death, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and said: “O people, it was just the sun.” The moon is two signs of God that do not eclipse due to the death or life of anyone, so if you see that, then rise to prayer and to the remembrance of God. “And pray and give in charity.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1232","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, and Abu Bakr told us Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa bin Masoud told us, they said: We told us: Zaida, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded “By emancipation during a solar eclipse.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it has a valid witness according to the conditions of Muslim."
"1233","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl and Muhammad Al-Shaarani informed us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when the sun was eclipsed."
"1234","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Adl and Ahmad ibn Yaqoub al-Thaqafi told us, saying: Omar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi told us, Asim ibn Ali told us, al-Layth ibn Saad told us, On the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace - so he mentioned the hadith - And he said in it: “If you see that, pray to God and pray, and give alms, and set free.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs."
"1235","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, Zakaria bin Dawud Abu Yahya Al-Khafaf told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar bin Maysarah, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that the sun was eclipsed, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. He prayed two rak’ahs of prayer until the end, then he said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse due to the death of anyone, but they are created by His creation, and it occurs God does what He wills with His creation. Then, when God, Blessed and Most High, manifests Himself to any of His creation, it submits to it. So whichever of them is subverted, pray until He is exalted. “Or God will cause something to happen.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1236","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Musaddad bin Qattan told us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, He said: Tell me who I believe. He means Aisha. She said: “The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up.” He made a strong standing, standing with the people, then bowing, then standing, then bowing, then standing, then bowing, so he bowed two rak’ahs, three rak’ahs in each rak’ah. rak'ahs, so he bowed the third, then prostrated to the point that some men would faint from what they had done on that day, to the point that streams of water would be poured on them. He says: When he bows, he says: God is great, and when he rises, he says: God hears whoever praises Him until the sun shines. Then he says: The sun and the moon do not “They are eclipsed due to the death of someone or his life, but they are two of the signs of God through which God makes His servants fearful. So when they eclipse, then prepare for prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Muslim narrated it, from the hadith of Muadh bin Hisham, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, with a word other than this."
"1237","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa, the judge in Bukhara, informed us. Muhammad bin Ayyub informed us. Muhammad bin Abdullah informed us. Ibn Abi Ja`far al-Razi, my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, he said: “The sun was eclipsed. During the time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed with them, reciting a lengthy surah, bowed five rak’ahs, and prostrated He performed two prostrations, then he stood up for the second time, recited for a long time, then he bowed five rak’ahs, prostrated two prostrations, then he sat as he was facing the Qiblah. He will pray until its eclipse becomes clear.” The two sheikhs abandoned Abu Ja’far al-Razi, and did not depart from him, and his condition according to the rest of the imams is in good condition. “This hadith contains certain words, and its narrators are truthful.”"
"1238","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Qilabah, on the authority of Qubaisa al-Hilali, said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he went out in fear dragging his garment, and I With him that day in Medina, he prayed two rak'ahs, prolonging them in standing, then he left and she calmed down and said: “Indeed, these verses make God fear With it, if you see it - meaning - then pray like the last prayer you have prayed from the prescribed ones. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. What I have is that they explained it with the hadith of Rayhan bin Saeed, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Hilal bin Amir, On the authority of Qabisa, and a hadith narrated by Musa bin Ismail, on the authority of Wahib, which is not explained by the hadith of Rayhan, and Abbad.”"
"1239","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told me, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Layth al-Razi told me, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`d told me, my uncle told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Hisham bin Urwa, and Abdullah bin Abi Salama told me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, each of them told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha said: “The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and led the people in prayer. He said: So I guessed his recitation, and we saw that he recited Surat Al-Baqarah, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he said: So he prolonged the recitation, so I guessed his recitation, so I saw That he recited Surah Al Imran “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, rather they agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri and Hisham bin Urwa In other words"
"1240","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid told us, my father told me, Al-Awza’i told us, Al-Zuhri told me, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited a long recitation aloud during the eclipse prayer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”"
"1241","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Muhammad Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abi Safwan told us, Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Al-Nadr, my father told me, he said: There was oppression during the reign of Anas bin Malik. He said: So I came to Anas bin Malik and said: O Abu Hamza, was there Something like this happened to you during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: God forbid, “If the wind is strong, he hastens to the mosque.” Fear of the Resurrection” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And this Ubaidullah is Ibn al-Nadr ibn Anas ibn Malik, and he They used “al-nadr” as evidence."
"1242","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Idris Al-Ansari told us, Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us, Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abbad, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us in prayer during an eclipse from which we could not hear a sound.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1243","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh al-Jallab told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ahmad bin al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr, an additional narration, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The sun eclipsed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. They do not eclipse due to the death or life of anyone, so when you see them, give alms and pray. “And grow great, and call upon God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1244","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told me, Yusuf ibn Ya`qub told me, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr told me, Khalid ibn al-Harith told me, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs like your prayer during an eclipse of the sun and the moon,” and they did not narrate it. May God’s blessings be upon Muhammad and his entire family.”
 Fear prayer book"
"1245","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Ahmad bin Jafar told us Al-Qutay’i, and the pronunciation for it, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Al-Ash’ath told me Ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Al-Aswad Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah Ibn Zuhdam, he said: We were with Sa’id Ibn Al-Aas in Tabaristan, and he said: “Which of you prayed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear? Then Hudhayfah stood up, and the people lined up behind him in a row, in a row parallel to the enemy, and he led one rak’ah in prayer for those behind him, then they departed in their place. And he came to those people and he prayed one rak’ah with them, but they did not perform it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this."
"1246","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatem Al-Zahid, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani informed us, Muhammad bin Jasham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i informed us, Abd Allah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Yahya told me, on the authority of Sufyan, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Jahm told me, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led Dhul Qard with the prayer of fear, one rak’ah after a rak’ah, and they did not make it up.” This is evidence. For the hadith that preceded it, “and it has an authentic chain of narration.”"
"1247","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna reported, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Jahm, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the prayer of fear in front of a monkey, and he lined up behind him in a row, parallel to the enemy, so he prayed. He performed one rak'ah with him, then they went to the ranks of those people, and those people came to the ranks of those people, and they prayed one rak'ah with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then “He greeted them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with these words."
"1248","Abu Amr bin Abi Jafar Al-Muqri told me, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Uqba bin Khaled Al-Sakouni told me, Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about praying while bowing. So he said: “Stretch in the bow and cast the horn.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration if Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi heard from Salamah bin Al-Akwa’. He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about praying in the bow, and he said: “Pray in the bow, and put down the horn.” They did not take it out."
"1249","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi informed us, Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, he informed us Yahya bin Ayyub, Yazid bin Al-Had narrated to me, Sharhabeel bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And in the prayer of fear, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and a group behind him, and a group behind the group that was behind the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They all bowed their faces towards the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said “Allahu Akbar.” So I said “Allah’s Greatest.” The two groups kneeled, and the group behind him kneeled with him, while the others were sitting. Then he prostrated, and they also prostrated, while the others were sitting. Then he stood up, and they stood up and set back. Behind him until they were sitting in the place of their companions, and the other group came, so he led one rak’ah and two prostrations with them, then he said the salaam while the others were sitting, then Then the two groups stood up and prayed one rak’ah for themselves and prostrated two rak’ahs and two prostrations.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not They narrate it, and they cited all of its narrators as evidence other than Sharhabeel, who is a Tabi’i Madani and not accused.”"
"1250","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubair told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear. She said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the people two shocks, and a group lined up behind him, and a group stood up, and the enemy came. She said: So he said ‘Allahu Akbar’. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the group of people who were lined up behind him said “Allahu Akbar,” then he bowed and they bowed, then he prostrated and they prostrated, then he raised his head and they rose. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained seated and they prostrated to themselves the second prostration, then they stood up, then they turned on their heels and walked. They retreated until they stood up behind them, and the other group approached, so they lined up behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said “Allahu Akbar,” then they bowed. for themselves, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated his second prostration, and they prostrated with him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose in I kneeled it and they prostrated for themselves the second prostration, then both groups stood up and lined up behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he kneeled with them. He performed a rak'ah and they all bowed, then he prostrated and they all prostrated, then he raised his head and they raised with him, all of that from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, very quickly and without They hoped that he would lighten it as much as he could. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted them and they saluted. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose and the people had joined him. In all of his prayers, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” He is the most complete hadith, and he cured it in the fear prayer.”"
"1251","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed me, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told me, Muhammad bin Muammar bin Rabi’ Al-Qaisi told us, Amr bin Caliph Al-Bakrawi, Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik Al-Hamrani told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led the people in prayer In the fear prayer, the Maghrib prayer is three rak’ahs, then he left, and the others came and he led three rak’ahs with them. I heard Abu Ali al-Hafiz, saying: This is a strange hadith. Ash’ath Al-Hamrani did not write it except with this chain of transmission.” Al-Hakim said: “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"1252","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl al-Dabbas informed us, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zayd al-Sayegh told us, Sa`id bin Mansour, Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Ayyash al-Zarqi, who said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In Usfan, and against the polytheists, Khalid bin Al-Walid, we prayed the noon prayer, and the polytheists said: We have been caught by surprise. We have been caught unawares. If only we had been We charged them while they were in prayer, and the verse about shortening the prayer between noon and afternoon was revealed. When the time of afternoon came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose. Facing the qiblah and the polytheists in front of him, he lined up a row behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and after that row another row lined up, so he bowed down. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they all bowed down, then he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated, and the others stood up and guarded them. When these people prayed They performed the two prostrations, and they stood up, and the others who were behind them prostrated, then the next row advanced to the position of the others, and they all bowed, then the row prostrated. The next row and the others stood up guarding them. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the next row sat down, the others prostrated, then they all sat down. So he greeted them, and he prayed it in Usfan and he prayed it on the day of Banu Sulaym. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1253","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywah bin Shuraih, Abu Al-Aswad reported that he heard Urwa ibn Al-Zubayr narrating, on the authority of Marwan ibn Al-Hakam, that he asked Abu Hurairah, “Did you pray with him?” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear? Abu Hurairah said: Yes. Marwan said: When? Abu Hurairah said: “In the year of the Battle of Najd, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose to pray the afternoon prayer, and one group and another group rose with him.” Others, facing the enemy, with their backs to the Qiblah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” and all those with him and those opposite said “Allahu Akbar.” The enemy, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled one rak’ah, and the group behind him kneeled, then he prostrated and the group following him prostrated. The others stood up facing the enemy, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and the group that was with him stood up, and they went to the enemy and faced them. The group facing the enemy came and they knelt down and prostrated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing as he was. Then they got up and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knelt down. May God bless him and grant him peace, another rak'ah, and they knelt with him and prostrated with him, then the group that was facing the enemy came and they knelt down and prostrated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He and those with him were sitting, then the greeting came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted them and they all greeted, so it was for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “And he said the salaam two rak’ahs, and each man from the two groups has one rak’ah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 Funeral book"
"1254","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ubayy and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, they said: Al-Layth bin Saad reported, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Hind bint Al-Harith, on the authority of Umm Al-Fadl, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered And Abbas, the uncle of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was complaining. Abbas wished for death, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O uncle, no. You wish for death, for if you were a doer, then if you delay it, you will add good deeds to your good deeds, which is better for you, and if you were an offender, then if you delay them, you will be reproached. “Whatever you do is better for you, so do not wish for death.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, they agreed on a hadith. Qais, on the authority of Khabbab, “If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had not forbidden us to wish for death, we would have wished for it.”"
"1255","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Ayoub bin Bilal bin Suleiman told us, Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Suleiman Bin Bilal, Zaid bin Aslam said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir said, I heard Jabir bin Abdullah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the better of you than the worst of you?” They said: Yes, he said: “The best among you are the longest-lived and the best in deeds.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and there is a witness for it. “Sahih according to the conditions of a Muslim”"
"1256","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Kateb told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, Yunus, and Thabit, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that a man said: O Messenger of God: Which of the people is best? He said: “He who lives long and does good deeds.” He said: Which people are evil? He said: “He whose life is long and whose deeds are bad.”"
"1257","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Muhammad narrated to us Salih bin Hani, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Suwar told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Ismail bin Ja’far told us, all of them, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God wants good for a servant, He uses it.” He said: So it was said: How does He use it? He said: “He will enable him to do good deeds before death.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it has a witness with an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"1258","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Hamq, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God loves a servant ""His honey."" He said: O Messenger of God, and what is his honey? He said: “He will be granted success in doing good deeds before his time until his neighbors are satisfied with him.” Or he said: “Those around him.”"
"1259","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Muhadhar bin Al-Muwari’ told us, Al-A’mash told us, and Ali told me Bin Issa Al-Hiri, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Hurashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Jarir reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Every servant will be resurrected after he died.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari"
"1260","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he informed us Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that when death approached him He called for new clothes and put them on, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The dead person is resurrected in the clothes in which he died.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 Abdullah bin Wahb, I am Abu Hani Al-Khawlani, and Amr bin Malik Al-Janabi heard Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Whoever dies on one of these levels will be resurrected on it on the Day of Resurrection,” according to their condition."
"1261","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Abu al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Saskiki, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, more than once or twice, saying: “If a slave does work... He was righteous, but illness or travel distracted him from that. Whatever he did was recorded as being righteous, and it is authentic and established. This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1262","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Hayyan bin Malaab told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, he informed us Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani bin Saeed told us, Abu Al-Hasan bin Abdul Samad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Salama, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to return Abdullah bin Ubayy during his illness in which he died, and when he entered upon him he knew that he was dead. He said: “I had been forbidden from loving the Jews,” so he said: Saad bin Zurarah hated them with his mouth, and when he died, his son came to him and said: O Messenger of God, Abdullah bin Ubayy has died, so give me your shirt. I shroud him in it. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took off his shirt and gave it to him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1263","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, saying: Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit me neither riding a mule nor “Bardhun” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1264","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no man who visits a sick person in the evening without seventy thousand angels going out with him.” They ask forgiveness for him until morning, and there is autumn for him in Paradise, and whoever comes to him in the morning, seventy thousand angels go out with him, seeking forgiveness for him until in the evening, and there was autumn in Paradise.” This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it because a group of narrators stopped it from saying it. Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, and Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, from the hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of them, and I am on “I pray in the ruling for the narrator of the addition.”"
"1265","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufaili told us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited me because of pain in my eyes.” This hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it has authentic evidence from the hadith of Anas bin Malik.”"
"1266","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Katheer Al-Humsi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Musaffa told us, Muawiyah bin Hafs, Malik bin Mughal narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned Zayd bin Arqam from an ophthalmia that he was suffering from.”"
"1267","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, in Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, al-Ja’id bin Abd al-Rahman told us, On the authority of Aisha bint Saad, that her father said: “I complained in Mecca, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me to visit me, and he placed his hand on My forehead, then he wiped my chest and stomach, then he said: “O God, heal Saad, and complete his migration.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1267 - They did not narrate it with this wording"
"1268","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Adl informed me of Marw, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Qadi told us, in Hamdan, Ibrahim ibn Al-Hussein, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hassan told us, Yazid Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever visits a sick person who has not attended his appointed time, and says he has seven Several times: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you. May God heal you from that disease. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1269","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever visits his Muslim brother, sits by his head, then says seven times: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Great Throne, to Awfi will heal you if his time has not yet arrived. “This is a strange, authentic hadith from the narration of the Egyptians, on the authority of the Medinians, on the authority of the Kufans.” We write it as high except on his authority, and Al-Hajjaj ibn Artaat differed from the trustworthy narrators in this hadith on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr.”"
"1270","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Hajjaj bin informed us Artaat, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What From a Muslim who visited his brother and entered upon him, and his time of death had not come, and he said: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal so-and-so from his illness. Seven times, God cured him of him. “This is not considered a dispute, for Al-Hajjaj bin Artaat came before Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id and Abu Khaled Al-Dalani.” In memorization and perfection, if the hadith of Abdullah bin Al-Harith is proven from this narration, then it is evidence of Saeed bin Jubayr.”"
"1271","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Bari’ told us, Al-Qanabi told us, regarding what was read to Malik, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, Abu al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Muzaki told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Qutaibah bin Sa`id told us, Ismail bin Ja`far told us, Yazid bin Khusayfa, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Ka’b Al-Sulami, that Nafi’ bin Jubayr told him that Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was gripped by pain that almost paralyzed him, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “Put your right hand on the place where you complain, and wipe it seven times, and say: I seek refuge in the glory and power of God from the evil that I find in myself.” Every anointing “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Muslim narrated it, from the hadith of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid bin. Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, with a wording other than this."
"1272","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukair told me, Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Ziyadah ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Fadalah ibn Ubaid, that two men came seeking healing Of urine, so he went with them to Abu al-Darda’, where they mentioned the pain of their females to him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever complains about something about you, or a brother of his complains about him, let him say: Our Lord, God who is in heaven, hallowed be thy name. Your command in heaven and earth, just as I have had mercy on you. in heaven, so show Your mercy on earth, and forgive us our sins and sins. Indeed, You are the Lord of the good, so send down a mercy from Your mercy and a healing. From your recovery in this regard, he will be cured, God willing. “The two sheikhs have cited as evidence all the narrators of this hadith except Ziyada ibn Muhammad. He is an old man from the people of Egypt and speaks little.”"
"1273","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, my father told me, Abu Al-Tahir told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yahya bin Abd told us. God, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you visits a sick person, Let him say: O God, heal your servant who treats you as an enemy or walks for you to pray. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1274","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Yahya bin Ayyub Al-Bajli told us, he reported Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man will have a status when... God, whenever He achieves it with an action, He will continue to test him with what He hates until He achieves that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1275","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Darabardi told me about Marw, Abu al-Mujih told us, Sa`id bin Mansour told us, and Ali bin Hajar told us, they said: We told him: Hushaym, Yunus ibn Ubaid informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father told me, Ismail, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “When Adam, peace be upon him, was present, he said To his sons: Go and gather for me some of the fruits of Paradise. He said: Then his sons went out and the angels met them and said: Where do you want, O sons of Adam? Our father sent us to reap for him the fruits of Paradise. He said: “Go back, for you have had enough.” He said: “So they returned with them until they came to Adam, and when Eve saw them, she was terrified of them and began to come closer to Adam and cling to him, so he said To her, Adam: To you on my behalf, to you on my behalf, because before you I came, come between me and the angels of my Lord. He said: So they took his soul, then they washed him and embalmed him. They shrouded him, then they prayed over him, then they dug for him, then they buried him, then they said: O children of Adam, this is your practice in your dead, so do likewise. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it is of the type in which there is no narrator for the successors except one narrator, for Utai ibn Damrah al-Saadi is not It has a narrator other than Al-Hasan, and I believe that the two Sheikhs explained it with another reason, which is that it was narrated on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ubayy, without mentioning Utai.”"
"1276","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Omar told me Ibn Malik Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abdullah Ibn Usama Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Adam was a tall man” - so he mentioned a long hadith, and at the end of it - he said: “Be alone between me and the messengers of my Lord, for you have entered upon me.” So they took his soul and washed him with water and lotus leaves three times, and they shrouded him and prayed over him and buried him, then they said, “This is the Sunnah of your children after you.” This does not explain the hadith of Yunus bin Ubaid, for he is more knowledgeable about the hadith of Al-Hasan than the people of Medina and Egypt, and God knows best.”"
"1277","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Ash’ari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned sick from Aak was there, and Abu Hurairah was with him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Rejoice, for God says: It is My fire that I will shed over My faithful servant in This world so that he may have his share of the Fire in the Hereafter. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1278","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, saying: Hisham ibn Ali al-Sirafi informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Adl told us: Hopefully, Harb bin Shaddad told us that Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to him, that Abu Qalaba narrated to him, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “A pain struck the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he started tossing and turning on his bed.” So I said: O Messenger of God, if he had done this Some of us feared that you would find fault with him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer will be distressed, but no believer will be afflicted by calamity. Or pain unless God removes his sin and raises his status.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1279","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim al-Razi told me, Sa`id bin Kathir bin Ufayr told me, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, he told me Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned An Ansar woman.” He said to her: “Is she Umm Muldam?” She said: Yes. So God cursed her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not take her captive, for she washes away the sins of the servant just as the furnace removes the impurities from iron.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording. Rather, Muslim narrated it, without this wording, from the hadith of Hajjaj ibn Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair"
"1280","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Tamim bin Muhammad told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, he said: A fever came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she asked permission to come to him, and he said: “Who are you?” She said: I am Umm Muldam. He said: “Will you give gifts to the people of Quba?” She said: Yes. He said: So he came to them and they had a fever, and they suffered from it severe, so they complained to him and said, O Messenger of God, what kind of fever we experienced. He said: “If you wish, I may supplicate to God and He will remove it from you, and if you wish, it may be for you as a purification.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1281","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad informed us Bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer’s affliction never ceases within himself.” And his wealth and his children until he meets God, and no sin is upon him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has an authentic witness."
"1282","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he informed us Israel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “And The believer is an atonement for his sins.”"
"1283","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a Bedouin: “Has Umm Muldam ever taken you in?” He said: Who is Umm Muldam? He said: “Free, between skin and flesh.” He said: I never found this. He said: Have you ever had a headache? He said: What is a headache? He said: “A race strikes a person in the head.” He said: I have never seen this. When he left, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Hell, let him look.” To this: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1284","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Imran bin Zaid Al-Taghlabi told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No believer strikes a race except May God remove a sin from him, record a good deed for him, and raise his status because of it. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Imran bin Zaid al-Taghlabi A sheikh from the people of Kufa.”"
"1285","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ali bin Ubaid told us, Talha bin Yahya told us, On the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Muawiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is nothing that afflicts a believer in his body that harms him except He pardoned for him some of his bad deeds.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"1286","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ahmad bin Issa told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Salman Al-Hajri, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Indeed, God will afflict His servant with sickness until that expiates every sin from him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1287","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told me, Muawiyah bin Najda told us, Qubaisa told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib, Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no Muslim who is afflicted with an affliction in his body except that God commands the guardians who guard him, ‘Write for My servant every day. And a night of goodness for what he used to do, as long as he was locked up in my bonds.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1288","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Yazid, Ja’far bin Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Sa’ib, that Abdul-Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Azhar narrated it, on the authority of his father Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Azhar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The likeness of a believing servant when he is afflicted by illness or fever is like an iron that enters Fire, and its impurity goes away, and its goodness remains.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Its narrators were Medinans and Egyptians, but they did not narrate it."
"1289","Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Ataki told me, Bishr bin Sahl Al-Labad told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, on the authority of my father Halbas Yazid bin Maysarah said that he heard Umm al-Darda’ saying: I heard Abu al-Darda’ saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “ God said: O Jesus, I will raise up after you a nation. If what they love happens to them, they will praise God, and if what they hate happens to them, they will seek refuge. And they were patient, and there was no forbearance or knowledge. He said: O Lord, how can this be for them when they have no forbearance or knowledge? He said: I give them of my forbearance and knowledge. This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, they did not narrate it.”"
"1290","Bukayr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told me, in Mecca, Abu Muslim Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Ali bin al-Madini told us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, Asim bin Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God Almighty said: When I put My believing servant to trial, and he did not complain to me against him, I would release him from My captivity, then I would exchange him for meat better than His flesh, and blood better than his own, then the work resumes. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1291","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, that a woman was a prostitute in pre-Islamic times, and a man passed by her - or she passed by him - and he extended his hand To her, she said: Oh, God removed polytheism and brought Islam, so he left her and turned away, and began to look at her until his face hurt. The wall, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him and said: “You are a servant. God wants good for you. Indeed, if God, Blessed and Most High, wants “He did good to a servant, hastening the punishment for his sin for him until he is fulfilled on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1292","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Abu Al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah told us Bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, they said, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jafar told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hakim bin Aflah, On the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “A Muslim has four obligations over another Muslim: he answers him when he calls him; He visits him when he is sick, smells him when he sneezes, and takes him to his funeral when he dies. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.” They only narrated it from the hadith of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. “The right of a Muslim over another Muslim is five times.”"
"1293","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Kurayb said: Abu Muawiya told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila, who said: Abu Musa came Al-Ash'ari visits Al-Hasan ibn Ali, and Ali said to him: Did you come to return, or to gloat? He said: Rather, I came as a returnee. Ali said: If you come as a returnee, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever comes to his brother as a returnee, it is In the myth of Paradise, when he sits, mercy will overwhelm him, and if it is in the morning, seventy thousand angels will pray over him until the evening, and if it is in the evening, they will pray over him. “Seventy thousand angels until morning.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it due to a dispute over the ruling on it."
"1294","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed us, Ali bin Al-Abbas Al-Bajli informed us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’, who said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari Al-Hasan bin Ali returned and Ali was with him, so Ali said: A visitor Are you coming or are you coming back? He said: Rather, he is returning, and Ali said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no Muslim who visits a sick person without seventy thousand angels going out with him.” They will accompany him, if it is in the morning until the evening, and he will have a fall of Paradise, and if it is in the evening, seventy thousand angels will accompany him until the morning, and he was “For him is the autumn of Paradise.” This is of the type that I have mentioned more than once. This does not explain it, for Abu Muawiyah was the most memorized of the companions of Al-A’mash, and Al-A’mash is more knowledgeable about the hadith of wisdom than anyone else.”"
"1295","Ismail bin Ibrahim Al-Qaari informed us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym informed us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever visits a sick person will never stop He immerses himself in mercy until he sits, and when he sits, he immerses himself in it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not take him out."
"1296","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told me, Musa bin Ali bin told us. Rabah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not force your sick to eat, for God “He feeds them and gives them drink.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1297","Muhammad bin Al-Khalil Al-Asbahani informed us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi informed us, Munjab bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Tarif Al-Harithi, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Yahya bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his father, that Omar saw him gloomy, so he said to him: What is the matter with you? You are upset about your cousin’s wife. He said: No, and he praised Abu Bakr, but I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A word that he does not say.” When a servant dies, God relieves him of his distress and makes his complexion shine.” Nothing prevented me from asking him about it except his ability to do it until he died, so Omar said: I know it, so Talha said to him: What is it? Then Omar said to him: “Do you know a word that is greater than the word that his uncle commanded: There is no god but Allah.” Talha said to him: By God, it is. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. As for the illusion that Muhammad bin Abd al-Wahhab, on the authority of Masar. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . ."
"1298","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, dictating, narrated to us Al-Harith bin Abi Usama, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of His father, that Othman bin Affan, narrated to Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them both, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “I “I do not know of a word that a servant would not say truly from his heart and die except that it would be forbidden to Hell.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and he did not inform us of it. Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “I am telling you about it. It is the word of sincerity that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded his uncle Abu Talib to do.” At death: testimony that there is no god but God, and it is the word with which God honored Muhammad and his companions. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it in this context, but Muslim alone narrated the hadith of Khalid al-Hadha:
 On the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Hamran, on the authority of Uthman, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but God He entered Paradise.”"
"1299","Abu Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi bin Rustam told us, Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Abdul Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Salih bin Abi Urayb, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever’s last speech is, there is no god Except Allah, He will enter Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not expel it. “And I had dictated the story of Abu Zar’ah, and his last words were a context This hadith"
"1300","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Malik told me, and Abu Bakr bin told us Abu Nasr Al-Marwazi, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Al-Qanabi told us, in what was read to Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabir bin Atik, that Atik bin Al-Harith bin Atik, who is the maternal grandfather of Abdullah bin Abdullah, told him that Jabir bin Atik He told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to return Abdullah bin Thabit and found him defeated. He shouted to him but he did not answer him, so he returned. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have defeated you, O Abu al-Rabi’.” The women shouted and cried, so Ibn Atik made them silence him and said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave them, and if it is necessary, do not weep.” They said: O Messenger of God, what is obligatory? He said: “If he dies.” His daughter said: By God, I was hoping that you would be a martyr, for you had killed yours. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has granted him his reward according to his intention, and what do you count as martyrdom?” They said: Killing in the cause of God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Martyrdom is seven other than killing in the cause of God: the stabbed is a martyr. The one who drowns is a martyr, the one who suffers from pleurisy is a martyr, the one who dies under fire is a martyr, the one who burns is a martyr, and the one who dies under the demolition is a martyr. And the woman dies as a martyr. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” Its narrators were civilians from the Quraysh, and with Malik’s hadith, it was plural. Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj started with this hadith from Malik’s sheikhs."
"1301","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us in Baghdad, Ubayy told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Qaza’ah bin Suwayd told us, on the authority of Humaid Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Labid, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you attend the dead So lower your gaze, for the sight follows the spirit, and speak good, for the angels confirm the supplications of the People of the House. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1302","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Aadmi informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Qatada, on the authority of Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When a believer is dying, angels come to him.” Mercy with a white robe, and they say: Go out, content and pleased with you, to the Spirit of God, and a fragrance, and a Lord who is not angry, and it comes out like a pleasant scent. musk to the point that they would hand it to one another and smell it until they would bring it to the gate of heaven and say: How pleasant is this scent that Did it come to you from the earth? So whenever they come to heaven, they say that so that they may bring it to the souls of the believers.” He said: “They are more happy with him than any of you are with him when he is absent when he comes to him.” He said: “Then they ask him, ‘What did so-and-so do?’” He said: “So they say: Leave him until he rests, for he was in the distress of this world, but when he says to them: Did he not come to you? Then he has died.” He said: “And they say, ‘He was taken to his mother, Sheol.’” He said: “As for the disbeliever, the angels of torment come to him and say: Go out, angry with you, to the punishment of God, and His wrath, and then he will go out.” It is like the smell of a carrion. Then they will take it to the door of the earth and say: What is this smell? Whenever they come to the earth they will say that until They bring with it the souls of the infidels.” Hisham bin Abdullah Al-Dastawwi followed Muammar bin Rashid in his narration, on the authority of Qatada: on the authority of Qasamah Ibn Zuhair,"
"1303","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Muqaddami told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar, and Hammam ibn Yahya said: On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza, on the authority of Abu Hurairah"
"1304","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “When death approaches a believer, the angels of mercy attend him.” Then He mentioned the hadith in a similar manner: “These chains of narrations are all authentic, and the hadith of Al-Bara’ ibn Aazib bears witness to them, and I dictated it in the Book of Faith.”"
"1305","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, Jeddi told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told me, about Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina, he asked about Al-Bara’ bin Ma’rur. They said: He died and he bequeathed a third of it to you, O Messenger of God, and he bequeathed that it be directed to the Qiblah when he was dying. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “He was fitrah, and I have returned a third of it to his son.” Then he went and prayed over him, and said: “O God, forgive him and have mercy on him. And admit him to your Paradise, and you have done.” This is an “authentic hadith.” Al-Bukhari cited Nu’aym ibn Hammad as evidence, and Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj argued as evidence. By Al-Darawardi, and they did not narrate this hadith, and I do not know of anything other than this hadith regarding the dying person’s turning to the Qiblah.”"
"1306","Abu Qutaybah Salem bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami told me in Mecca, Ibrahim bin Hashim Al-Baghawi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, we told him Abu Muawiyah, Abu Burdah Buraid bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: “When they took In the washing of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when they heard a call from within, “Do not remove from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his shirt.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1307","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told us, On the authority of Sharhabeel bin Sharik Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever washes If someone dies and conceals it, he will be forgiven forty times, and whoever shrouds a dead person, God will cover him with silk, and he will look forward to Paradise, and whoever digs a grave for a dead person. So I put him in heaven therein, and I will reward him with a reward like the reward of a dwelling in which he will reside until the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1308","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, he reported Ismail bin Qutaibah, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Yahya bin Sulaym informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of your clothes is white, so clothe your living ones with them, and shroud your living ones in them.” “Your dead.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “And its witness is authentic, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub.”"
"1309","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib reported, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wear white clothes, and shroud your dead in them, for they are purer and more pleasant.”"
"1310","Ali bin Issa told me, Ahmad bin Najda told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told me, Qutbah bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you perform the funeral prayer for the dead, perform Witr prayer.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1311","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Hushaym told us, he told us Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, said: “You saw us with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were almost “We will sand the funeral with sand.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and it was witnessed with an authentic chain of narration on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar Al-Tayyar."
"1312","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Abi Talib in Al-Baqi’, when he saw a funeral procession, and Ibn Ja’far came to us and was astonished by He slowed down their walking with it, and he said: “It is amazing how people’s condition has changed. By God, if it was anything but jamaz, and if the man was to keep up with another man.” Then he says: O servant of God, fear God, as if he had stopped at you in astonishment at your slowness in walking.”"
"1313","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Saeed bin Ubaidullah Al-Thaqafi told us, Ziyad bin Jubayr bin Hayya, on the authority of his father Jubayr bin Hayya, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one walking in front of the funeral, And the passenger is behind her, and the child is prayed over.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it."
"1314","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Thawban, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, attended a funeral, so he was brought An animal, but he refused to ride it, so when he left, an animal was brought and he rode it. He was told: He said: “Indeed, the angels were walking, but I was not.” To ride while they were walking, and when they went - or he said: they stopped - I rode. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and there is a witness for it.” With a word more healing than this.”"
"1315","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muzaki and Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khafaf informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salamah told us, we told him: Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Isa bin Yunus reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Thawban, he said: “He came out The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at a funeral and saw people kneeling, so he said: “Aren’t you ashamed? The angels of God are on their feet, and you are on The appearance of animals"
"1316","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Amr al-Hushi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, about Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was attending the funeral, he would not sit. Until it is raised or put down.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. “And he has a witness with a similar chain of transmission, on the authority of Abu Sa’id.”"
"1317","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Wahib told us, Suhail bin Abi Saleh told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When you follow a funeral procession, do not sit until it is placed.” The two sheikhs agreed on Narrating the hadith of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Aamir ibn Rabi’ah, “Whoever follows it should not sit until it is placed,” and this is a hadith other than that of “Al-Ziyadah al-Dafn” and others.”"
"1318","Abu Ahmad bin Abi Al-Hasan Al-Darimi told me, Muhammad bin Sulayman bin Faris told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, he informed us Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... A funeral passed by him and he stopped until it passed by him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “This is not the text of the hadith of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Aamir ibn Rabi’ah, for this text is about conducting a funeral, and this is about standing up for a funeral, despite the many different narrations regarding it.”"
"1319","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub ibn Ahmad ibn Mihran al-Zahid told us, Musa ibn Harun told us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabi al-Zahid told us, And Abu Musab Ahmad bin Abi Bakr, they said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, that he witnessed a funeral. Marwan bin Al-Hakam prayed over her, so Abu Hurairah went with Marwan until they sat in the cemetery, then Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri came and said to Marwan: Show me your hand. So he gave him his hand and said: Get up. So he got up. Then Marwan said: Why did you make me stand up? He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a funeral, he would stand up and pass by it and say: “Indeed, death is a fear.” Marwan said: Is that the truth, Abu Hurairah? He said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from telling me? He said: You were an imam, so you sat, so I sat. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”"
"1320","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Issa Al-Tarsusi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us Al-Muqri, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, Rabia bin Saif Al-Maafiri told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr Ibn Al-Aas, that he said: A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, will the funeral of the infidels pass by us so we stand for it? . He said: “Yes, stand up for her, for you are not standing up for her. Rather, you are standing up to honor the One who takes souls.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1321","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abu Ammar told us, Al-Nadr bin Ismail told me, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, “The funeral of a Jew passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stood up,” so they said: O Messenger of God. It was the funeral of a Jew, and he said: “I only stood for the angels.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording except that they They agreed to narrate the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Maqsim, on the authority of Jabir, about standing up for the funeral of a Jew.”"
"1322","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Surayj bin Al-Nu’man told us, Fulayh bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid. Ibn al-Sibbaq, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, said: “We were in front of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the deceased among us was brought to us. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called us to So he attended him and asked forgiveness for him until when we came, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and those with him departed, and perhaps they stayed until he was buried, and perhaps his imprisonment was prolonged. That is up to the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When we feared the difficulty of that, some of the people said to others: If only we had not given the call to prayer to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted someone until he was taken, and when his ears were taken, there was no hardship or imprisonment in that, so we used to call him to the dead after he died. So he comes to him and the prayer is prayed over him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1323","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, that he heard Saeed bin Abi Saeed, He says: Ibn Abbas prayed at a funeral, and he loudly praised God, then he said: “I only spoke loudly so that you would know that it is a Sunnah.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. Muslim “They have unanimously agreed that the Companion’s statement is a Sunnah, a hadith with a chain of transmission, and it has evidence with an authentic chain of transmission.” Narrated by Al-Bukhari"
"1324","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf said: I prayed behind Ibn Abbas at a funeral, and I heard him reciting the opening of the book, so when he left, I took in his hand, so I asked him and said: Do you read? He said: “Yes, it is the truth and the Sunnah,” and there is an explicated witness from the hadith of Ibrahim bin Abi Yahya."
"1325","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the takbir at our funerals four times, and recite the opening of the book in The first takbeer”"
"1326","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Al-Hakam bin Musa told us, Haql bin Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Whenever he prayed at a funeral, he would say: “O God, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, and our remembrance.” And female, O God, whomever You make alive among us, let him live as a Muslim, and whomever You cause to die among us, cause him to die as a believer.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs, and he did not narrate it, and he has an authentic witness to Muslim’s condition.”"
"1327","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim Al-Yamami told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: I asked Aisha, the Mother of the Believers: What was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May peace and blessings be upon the dead. She said: He used to say: “O God, forgive our living and our dead, our males and females, those who are present and those who are absent. And young and old, O God, whoever among us You make alive, let him live in Islam, and whoever among us You cause to die, cause him to die in faith.”"
"1328","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Rahman al-Khallal told us, in Mecca, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq al-Katib told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami, Al-Hussein bin Zaid bin Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah Ibn Rukanah Ibn Al-Muttalib said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up for a funeral to pray over it, he would say: “O God, your servant. And the son of your nation needs your mercy, and you are free from his torment. If he is a doer of good, then increase his benevolence, and if he is an offender, then exceed it. On his authority - this is an authentic chain of narration - Yazid bin Rukana and his father Rukana bin Abd Yazid are two companions of Banu Al-Muttalib bin Abd Manaf. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1329","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i told me, Shurahbil bin Saad, he said: I was present with Abdullah bin Abbas. He prayed with us at a funeral with Al-Abwa and said the takbir, then he recited the Umm Al-Qur’an, raising his voice in it, then He prayed upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then said: “O God, your servant, the son of your servant, and the son of your female nation bear witness that there is no god but You alone. You have no partner, and he bears witness that Muhammad, your servant and messenger, has become in need of your mercy, and you have become free from his torment, and will be freed from this world. And its people. If he is pure, then purify him, and if he is wrong, then forgive him. O God, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him.” Then he said “Allahu Akbar” three times. Then he left and said: “O people, I did not recite publicly except so that you would know that it is the Sunnah.” The two sheikhs did not use Sharhabeel bin as evidence. Saad, and he was one of the followers of the people of Medina. I only narrated this hadith as a witness to the hadiths that we have presented, for they are brief and comprehensive. This is an explained hadith.”"
"1330","Ali bin Hamshadh al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Mandah told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, and Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim told us Ibn Al-Hussein, Adam Ibn Abi Iyas told us, Ahmad Ibn Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Jaafar, they said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, who said: A daughter of his died, so he followed her on the authority of A mule walked behind the funeral procession, and women were inheriting it. He said: Either they inherit, or they do not inherit. “For the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade inheritances.” . Let one of you say the takbir as much as she wants, then “he prayed over her and said the takbir upon her four times, then he stood up after the fourth for the amount of time between the two takbirs.” He asks forgiveness for her and prays.” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do this.” This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it, and Abraham Ibn Muslim Al-Hijri was not retaliated against with any justification.”"
"1331","Ismail bin Ahmad Al-Tajer told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Asqalani told us, Harmala bin Yahya told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunaif told me, and he was one of the great leaders of the Ansar and their scholars, and the sons of those who They witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Men from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him during the funeral prayer, “... The imam says “Allahu Akbar,” then he sends blessings upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he concludes the prayer with the three “Allahu Akbar,” then he gives a silent salutation when he leaves. The Sunnah is for someone to do behind him the same as he did in front of him.” Al-Zuhri said: Abu Umamah told me about that, and Ibn al-Musayyab heard but did not deny it. Ibn Shihab said: I remembered what Abu Umamah told me from the Sunnah about praying for the dead by Muhammad bin Suwayd. He said: And I heard Al-Dahhak bin Qais narrated, on the authority of Habib bin Maslamah, in a prayer he prayed for the dead, like what Abu Umama told us: “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it, and there is nothing in the single salutation at the funeral more authentic than it, and the hadith of Abu Al-Anbas is witnessed by Sa’id bin Kathir.”"
"1332","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Ghannam bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Al-Anbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed at a funeral and said four takbirs over it, and greeted him with salutations.” “The one greeting at the funeral.” The narration has been authenticated about it, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, Abdullah bin Omar, and Abdullah bin Abbas, Jabir bin Abdullah bin Abi Awfa and Abu Hurairah said that they used to greet the funeral with one greeting."
"1333","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, and Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, Muhammad bin Bashar, and Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, they said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Al-Muthanna bin told us. Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer He will die by the sweat of his brow.” This hadith is according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1334","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, and Ahmad bin Jafar Al-Qutayi, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, kissed Uthman bin Mad’un when he was dead and he was crying.” He said: “And his eyes were streaming.” This is a hadith circulated among the imams, except that the two sheikhs did not use Asim bin Ubaid Allah as evidence, and his true witness is The well-known hadith is the hadith of Abdullah bin Abbas, Jabir bin Abdullah, and Aisha, “that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was dead"
"1335","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh told us Al-Adl, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Omar Al-Hudhi told us, and Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, and Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ali told us. Ibn al-Abbas al-Bajli, Abu Kurayb told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Khalid bin Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best perfume is musk,” followed by Al-Mustamir ibn Al-Rayyan, on the authority of Abu Nadra."
"1336","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Hamid bin Sahl told us, Abu Muammar told us, Abd al-Warith told us, on the authority of al-Mustamil bin Al-Rayyan, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about musk and he said: “It is the best of your perfumes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration: “Khalid ibn Ja’far and Al-Mustamir ibn Rayyan are numbered among them as trustworthy, and they did not narrate anything from them,” and he has evidence on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, “and to him went Ahmad bin Hanbal.”"
"1337","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Humaid bin Abdul Rahman al-Rawasi told us, Al-Hasan told us Ibn Salih, on the authority of Harun Ibn Saad, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: “Ali had musk, so he recommended that he be embalmed with it. He said: And Ali said: ‘And it is The surplus of the spices of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1338","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Yaqoub told us, Ahmad ibn Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn With Al-Wayh, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Burdah narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, he said: “When they began to wash the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a caller called to them from within, ‘Do not remove your On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his shirt “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it” and Abu Burdah, this is Burayd bin Abi Burdah bin Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari is cited as evidence in the two Sahih books.”"
"1339","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, said: Ali bin Abi Talib said: “I washed the Messenger of God, so I went to see what was from the dead, but I did not see Nothing, and he was good, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his family, alive and dead, and those responsible for his burial, and his companions, apart from the people, were four: Ali, Al-Abbas, and Al-Fadl. Salih, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, joined a grave, and bricks were erected on it. “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not take anything from it other than al-Lahd.”"
"1340","Abu Muhammad Abdullah Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us in Mecca, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin The reciter Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Sharik Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever washes a dead person and conceals it, he will be forgiven forty times, and whoever shrouds a dead person, God will cover him with a sandal and a shade of veil.” Paradise, and whoever digs a grave for a dead person and puts him in it, will be rewarded for him like the reward of a dwelling until the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1341","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja’ Al-Sindi informed us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Malik bin Hubayra, and it was his Companionship, he said: And when a funeral was brought to pray over it, and its people gathered together, he would divide them into three rows and pray over it, and he says that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are no rows of Muslims lined up for a funeral but it makes it obligatory.” This wording is the hadith of Ibn Ulayya in The wording of the Beloved is, “Unless he is forgiven.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1342","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Asbahani told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Issa bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jubayr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: There was a Jewish boy serving the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he fell ill, so he visited him and said: “Say, ‘I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that you are the Messenger of God.’” So the boy looked at his father and said: Say: What Muhammad tells you. He said: When he died, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray for your brother.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1343","Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hassan Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Saeed bin Ubaidullah bin Jubayr bin Hayya, my uncle Ziyad bin Jubayr bin Hayya told me, Abu Jubayr bin Hayya Al-Thaqafi told me, that he heard Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the one walking close to it, and the child is being prayed over.” Narrated by Yunus ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr"
"1344","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Yunus told us Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Jubayr Ibn Hayya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah - he said: Yunus, and some of his family told me that he He submitted it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace - he said: “The rider walks behind the funeral procession, and the one walking to its right and left is close by, and the one who has fallen is prayed and supplicated.” May his parents be well and have mercy.” Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib said after this hadith. He said: Yunus ibn Ubaid, and some of them told me His family said that he referred it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, according to the narration of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubayd Allah bin Jubayr bin Hayya: “This A hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. He used as evidence in Sahih the hadith of Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Saeed bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, On the authority of Jubayr bin Hayya, on the authority of Al-Mughirah. The long hadith. The evidence for these hadiths is the hadith of Ismail bin Muslim al-Makki, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr."
"1345","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ismail Al-Makki informed us, about... Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a boy makes his inheritance, he inherits, and the funeral prayer is sent over him.” The two sheikhs did not protest. “By Ismail bin Muslim.”"
"1346","Ahmad bin Ishaq bin Ayyub Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya. Bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Amra, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Khaybar, and a man among us died from... He encouraged, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray for him.” So we went to look and found Jewish beads, equivalent to two dirhams. “Narrated by the people, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed.” Abu Amra, this is a man. From Juhayna he was known for his honesty, but they did not expel him.”"
"1347","Abu Al-Abbas Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mahran bin Khaled Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra, who said: A man died during the reign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came to him and said: He died. So-and-so, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “He did not die.” Then he came to him a second time and said: So-and-so died, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He did not Then he came to him the third time and said: So-and-so died. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How did he die?” He said: He slaughtered himself with a knife he had with him, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray for him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra, that “a man killed himself and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray over him” on the condition of a Muslim."
"1348","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi told us, Asad bin Musa told us, and Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, In Baghdad, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Sulaiman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi told us, they said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, On the authority of his father, Abu Qatada, he said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was invited to a funeral, he would ask about it, and if he praised it well, he would pray over it. If he praised her other than that, he said to her family: “What is your business with her?” and did not pray for her. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1349","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Abu Al-Hussein Surayj told us. Ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari, Fulayh ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Ubaid ibn al-Sabbaq, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: “We were the predecessors of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When the dead person among us is brought to us, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called us out, attended him, and asked forgiveness for him, until when he was arrested, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, departed. And peace be upon him, and those with him until he is buried, and perhaps the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was imprisoned for a long time, so when we feared that this would be difficult for him, some people said For some: If we had not given the Prophet the call to the Prophet until he was arrested, then when his permission was arrested, there would be no hardship or imprisonment for him in that, so we did so. That was when we used to call him to the dead after he had died, and he would come to him and pray over him. Sometimes he left, and sometimes he stayed until the dead person was buried, so we were on That was for a time, then we said: If the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had not been diagnosed, and we carried our funeral to him so that he could pray over him at his house, that would have been the case. He agreed to it, so we did, and that is the matter to this day. “This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and I dictated it in the past.” Briefly"
"1350","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Muhajir told us, Abu Al-Taher and Harun bin Saeed told us, they said: Abdullah bin Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of His father, that Abu Talha “called the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Umair bin Abi Talha when he died, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to them.” He greeted him and prayed over him in their house. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and Abu Talha was behind him and Umm Sulaym was behind Abu Talha. “There should be others with them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and a strange Sunnah in permitting women’s prayer at funerals, and they did not narrate it."
"1351","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, they said: Usama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, said: When it was the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Hamza bin Abdul-Muttalib, who had been mutilated and mutilated. He said: “If Safiya had not found it, she would have left him until God gathers him from the bellies of birds and wild beasts.” So he shrouded him in a nimar when his head was covered. His feet were uncovered, and when his feet were covered his head was uncovered, so his head was covered, and he did not pray for any of the martyrs other than him, and he said: “I am a witness.” upon you today.” He used to gather the three and two in one grave, and ask: “Which of them has recited the Qur’an the most?” Then he brings him into the grave, and shrouds the two and three men in one garment."
"1352","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Osama told me Ibn Zaid Al-Laythi, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him, that Anas Ibn Malik narrated to him: “The martyrs of Uhud were not washed, and they were buried in their blood, and no prayers were performed.” “On them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari alone narrated the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not “He prays upon them.” It does not contain these combined expressions that were uniquely used by Usama bin Zayd al-Laythi, on the authority of al-Zuhri.
 They all agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed over someone who was killed, as he prayed over the dead.” And God knows best."
"1353","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in Shawwal of the year three hundred and ninety-five. Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Abdullah bin Raja’ told us, Hammam told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh told me, he said: Musa bin told us Harun, Zuhair bin Harb told us, Waki` told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “When you place your dead in their graves, say: In the name of God and according to the religion of the Messenger of God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “They narrate it.” Hammam bin Yahya is proven and trustworthy if he narrates such a hadith. It cannot be attributed to anyone if Shu’bah narrated it."
"1354","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and he told me Al-Hussein bin Ali, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bundar told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that “when the dead person was placed in his grave, he would say: In the name of God and in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God.” The hadith of Al-Bayadhi, which is well-known among the Companions, is a witness. According to the hadith of Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, with a chain of narration"
"1355","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam, and Ibn Bukair told us, They said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Ibn Al-Had told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Hazim, the client of the Ghifaris, he said: He told me Al-Bayyadi, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the dead person is placed in his grave, let those who place him say when he is placed in the grave: In the name of God, by God, and according to the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1356","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, and Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, saying: Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Saleh Al-Wahazi told us, they told us: Abd al-Uzayr ibn Muhammad, Anas ibn Abi Yahya, the client of the Muslims, told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet passed by and prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, with a funeral at a grave. He said: “Whose grave is this?” They said: So-and-so is an Ethiopian, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no god but God. There is no god but God. He was driven from his land.” And His heavens to His soil from which He was created.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And Unays bin Abi Yahya Al-Aslami is the uncle of Ibrahim bin Abi Yahya, and Anis, trustworthy and trustworthy.” There is evidence for this hadith, most of which are authentic."
"1357","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih did not tell us in Baghdad, Al-Hussein bin Bashar Al-Khayyat told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq told us, Daoud told us Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jundub Ibn Sufyan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God wants to arrest a servant On land in which he has made a need for himself.”
 And from there"
"1358","What Ali bin Abbas Al-Iskandarani Al-Adl told me, in Mecca, Abu Ja’far Ahmad bin Abdul-Wahid Al-Homsi told me, Kathir bin Obaid Al-Madhaji, Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Wahbi told us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is in possession of a land and his need is available to him, then he should go to it and be as utmost as possible.” A trace of it and his soul will be caught in it, and the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: My Lord, this is what You have entrusted me with. Among them are:"
"1359","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari did not tell us about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza Al-Sukkari told us, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Matar ibn Ukamis al-Abdi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The term of a man is not appointed in any land except that it is appointed He has a need therein, including:"
"1360","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz did not tell us more than once. Al-Hussein bin Nahar Al-Askari told us, Zayd bin Al-Harish told us, Imran bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Urwa bin Mudarris, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God wills, He will take A servant of land who had a need for it.”"
"1361","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Hamid Abu Jafar Al-Harithi told us, Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Saluli told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Muslim Al-Taifi, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, that a man was raising his voice when dhikr, and a man said: If only this reduced the His voice, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is weak.” He said: Then he died and a man saw fire in his grave, so he came to him and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in it and he said: “Come to your friend.” So, this is the man who used to raise his voice when mentioning"
"1362","Ali bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, Ibrahim bin Nasr told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Taifi told us, On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I saw a fire in the graves, so I went to them, and behold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in The grave and he said: “Give me your companion.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a witness with a problematic chain of transmission.”"
"1363","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, my father told me, Waki’ told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, narrated to me Muhammad bin Ishaq, Bundar told us, Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Yunus, who is Hatim bin Abi Saghira, who said: I heard a man who was in Mecca. He was a Roman - and in the hadith of Shu'bah, his name is Waqqas narrated - on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: A man was circumambulating the Kaaba and he was saying: In his supplication, Oh. Oh, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is very weak.” Abu Dharr said: So I went out one night and saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the graves burying that man, and he had a lamp with him."
"1364","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father told me, and Abu Zakaria Yahya ibn Muhammad Al-Anbari, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim, and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, they said: I am Abdul Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj, Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah speaking, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave a sermon one day, and he mentioned a man from His companions were arrested, he was shrouded in a useless shroud, and he was buried at night. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, discouraged the man from being buried at night so that the funeral prayer could be offered over him. Unless a person is forced to do so, and he says: “If one of you shrouds his brother, let him shroud him well.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it is not He brings it out.” And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Wahb ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Jabir"
"1365","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, Abdul Karim bin Ismail told us. Al-San’ani Abu Hisham, Ibrahim bin Aqeel bin Maqil bin Munabbih told us, on the authority of his father Aqeel, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, he said: This is what I asked On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, he told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon one day and mentioned a man from his companions who had been arrested. He was wrapped in a useless shroud and buried at night. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, discouraged the man from being buried at night and not praying over him unless someone was forced to do so. That, and he said: “If one of you protects his brother, let him protect himself.”"
"1366","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, and Ahmad bin Najda told us Jafar Al-Qutayi, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, that Ali said to Abi Hayaj: “I send you to do what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me, not to leave any statue unless “You have obliterated it, and there is no honorable grave except that You have leveled it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. I think that there is a disagreement about it, on the authority of Al-Thawri, because he once said: On the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Al-Hayaj, and it is authentic that Abu Wa’il heard from Ali, may he be pleased with him. ""God bless him"""
"1367","Abu Hafs Omar bin Ahmad Al-Jumuhi told us in Mecca, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Isbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa informed me, Ismail bin Qutaybah told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, they said: Waki` told us, Waki` told us. Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Al-Hayyaj, he said: Ali told me not to send you for what the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, sent me for. May God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner."
"1368","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, he said: It was read to Abdullah bin Wahb, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik Al-Madani, on the authority of Amr bin Hani, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: I entered upon Aisha and said: O mother, Reveal for me the graves of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his two companions. You revealed to me three graves, neither overlooking nor lying flat, lying flat on top of them. The Red Arsah, “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, advancing, and Abu Bakr with his head between the shoulders of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Omar “His head is at the feet of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1369","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman Al-Hadrami told us, Salam bin Junada bin Salam Al-Qurashi told us, Salam bin Junada bin Salam Al-Qurashi told us. Hafs bin Ghiyath Al-Nakhai, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade building on graves. Or plastered, or sitting on it, and he forbade writing on it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he narrated its chain of transmission other than writing. It is a strange, correct word.” Likewise, it was narrated by Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj."
"1370","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Sami told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade plastering graves, writing in them, and building On it, and sitting on it.” These chains of transmission are authentic, “and not working on it, for the imams of the Muslims from east to west have written on Their graves, and it is an action that the successors adopted from the predecessors.”"
"1371","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Wahb, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My nation - or this nation - is still in A share of her religion as long as they do not entrust the funerals to their families.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration if this Al-Sanabihi is Abdullah. Abd al-Rahman bin Usayla al-Sanabihi, for he differed regarding his hearing from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1372","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hisham bin Yusuf Al-San’ani told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Buhair, on the authority of Hani, the servant of Uthman, who said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a funeral at a grave. And its companion was buried, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ask forgiveness for your brother, and ask God to make him steadfast, for now he is being asked.” An authentic hadith on the condition of its chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1373","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Hisham bin Yusuf Al-San’ani told us, Abdullah bin Buhair told us: I heard Hani, the servant of Uthman bin Affan, saying: Whenever Othman bin Affan stood on a grave, he cried until He wets his beard, and it is said to him: You may remember Paradise and Hell, so do not cry. And you cry because of this, and he says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The grave is the first stage of the Hereafter, so if one is saved from it, then what comes after it is easier than it, and if one does not escape from it, then what comes after it is more severe.” The Messenger of God said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I have never seen a sight except that the grave was more horrific than it.”"
"1374","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, my father told me, Al-Mufaddal bin Muhammad told us Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Omar bin Ya’la bin Murrah, on the authority of his father, who said: “I traveled with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, more than once, and I never saw him pass by a human corpse except He was ordered to bury him, not asking whether he is a Muslim or an infidel. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1375","Abu Ahmad Hamza bin Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl bin Al-Harith Al-Aqbi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Dawud told us Suleiman bin Dawud al-Tayalisi, Imran bin Dawud al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For every A person has three companions: As for Khalil, he says, “Whatever you spend is yours, and whatever you retain is not yours, that is his money.” As for Khalil, he says: “I am with you.” So when you come to the king’s gate, I leave you and come back, then that is his family and his decency. As for Khalil, he says: I am with you wherever you enter, and wherever you go out, that is the case. His work, so he says: If you are the least worthy of the three, then this is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Imran Al-Qattan is not the wounded person whose hadith is left out, and they agreed on the hadith of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad Ibn Amr Ibn Hazm, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a dead person dies, three people follow him.”"
"1376","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz in Hamadan told me, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told me, Abu Salamah al-Tabudhaki Musa ibn Ismail, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The example of a man The example of death is that of a man who has three intimates, and one of them said: This is my money, so take from it whatever you want, and the other said: I am with you as long as you live. So if you die, I leave you, and the other says: I am with you, I will go in and out with you if you die, and if you live, then as for the one who said, Take from him what you want and leave what Whatever you wish, it is his money, as for the other, it is his family, and as for the other, it is his work. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1377","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Ja’far bin Khalid bin Sarah told us. Al-Makhzoumi, my father, who was a friend of Abdullah bin Ja’far, told me that he heard Abdullah bin Ja’far say: When Ja’far was mourned, the Prophet said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “Make food for Ja’far’s family, for something has come to them that will occupy them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. And Ja’far b. Khaled bin Sara is one of the most prominent sheikhs of Quraysh, and he is as Shu’bah said: Write about the nobles, for they do not lie. It was narrated Other than this hadith, it is explained.”"
"1378","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Tamim Al-Handali told us in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, he told me Ja'far bin Khalid bin Sarah, and Ibn Jurayj told us about him, saying: My father told me that Abdullah bin Ja'far said: If you saw me and stood And Ubayd Allah ibn al-Abbas were playing when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by on an animal and said: “Carry this to me.” So he put me in front of him, then he said Qutham said: “Carry this to me.” He left it behind him, as he was ashamed of his uncle Abbas to carry Qutham and leave Ubayd Allah behind him. Then he wiped my head three times. When he wiped, he said: “O God, make Ja’far’s successor in his son.” I said to Abdullah bin Jafar: What did Qutham do? He said: He was martyred. I said to Abdullah: God and His Messenger knew best about him. He said: Yes."
"1379","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, that Rawh bin Ubadah told them that Ibn Jurayj said: Ja’far told me Ibn Khalid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Jaafar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped my head with his hand. He said: - I think he said Third - When he wiped, he said: “O God, grant Ja’far successor in his son.” Ja’far bin Khaled brought two dear things: one of them was wiping the orphan’s head. And the other is to provide the people of calamity with what they will sustain themselves during the night. “May God grant us success in relieving it from him.”"
"1380","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Nahwi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Al-Aswad bin Shayban told us, Khaled told us Ibn Samir, Bashir bin Nahik told me, Bashir of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, and his name in pre-Islamic times was Zahm bin Ma’abad, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: “What is your name?” He said: Zahm ibn Ma'bad, and he said: “You are Bashir,” and that was his name. He said: While I was walking with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “O son of the elite, do not take revenge on God. You have now walked with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” “Peace be upon him.” So I said: I am not averse to God for anything. All good has been done by the Prophet of God. So he came to the graves of the polytheists and said: “These have indeed done great things.” Three times, then he came to the graves of Muslims and said: “These have attained much good.” Three times, while he was walking, it came to him. He looked, and behold, there was a man walking between the graves wearing a sandal, and he said: “O owner of the two Sabbaths, woe to you, cast down your two Sabbaths.” So he looked, and when he knew The man, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took off his shoes and threw them away."
"1381","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki` told us, about the lions. Ibn Shayban, on the authority of Khaled Ibn Samir, on the authority of Bashir Ibn Nahik, on the authority of Bashir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, When he greeted, he saw a man walking in two sandals between the graves, and he said: “O owner of the two Sabbaths, throw them away.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. In the type in which the Companions are not known except as Tabi’in.”"
"1382","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, he informed us Nafi’ bin Yazid, Rabi’ah bin Saif told me, Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubli told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: We buried a man with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when we returned and were close to his door, he was with a woman whom we do not think he knew, and he said: “Oh Fatima, where do you come from? She said: I came from the people of the dead. I had mercy on their dead and consoled them. He said: “Perhaps you have reached the point of hardship with them?” She said: God forbid that I reach hardship with them, and I heard you mentioning what you mention about it. He said: “If I had reached hardship with them, I would not have seen it.” Paradise until your father’s grandfather sees it” and “Al-Kudda”: the graves “Narrated by Haywa bin Shurayh Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Saif"
"1383","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa told us, Rabia bin Saif Al-Maafiri told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He saw a woman leaving a funeral and asked her: “Where did you come from?” She said: From condoling the people of this dead person, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, if I were to reach their hardship, I would not see Paradise.” Until your father’s grandfather sees it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1384","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told me, Ahmed bin Issa Al-Qadi told me, Abu Al-Walid and Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, they said: We told us: Shu'bah, and Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Yahya bin Mu'in told us, Yahya bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Jaafar said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed us.” May God bless him and grant him peace, those who visit graves and those who place mosques and lamps over them. It is Badhan, and the two sheikhs did not use it as evidence, but it is a hadith circulated among the imams, and I found a continuation of it from the hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri in The text of the hadith, so I took it out.”"
"1385","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Harun Al-Faqih told us, according to his dictation, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman bin Khathim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Bahman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Hassan bin Thabit, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed May God bless him and grant him peace. Visitors of graves. These hadiths narrated in the prohibition of visiting graves have been abrogated.
 The abrogator of it is the hadith of Alqamah bin Murthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I had forbidden you. Concerning visiting graves, “Do not visit them.” God Almighty permitted His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to visit his mother’s grave, and this hadith is narrated in The two authentic books of the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them."
"1386","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, and Abu Al-Abbas told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah told us Al-Hakam, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb told me, Usama bin Zaid told me that Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban Al-Ansari told him that Wasi’ bin Hibban told him that Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri told him that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I forbid you from visiting graves.” So visit it, for therein is a lesson, and I have forbidden you from wine, so renounce, and I do not permit any intoxicant, and I have forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals, so eat and save.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1387","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ayoub bin Hani, on the authority of Masruq bin Al-Ajda’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, I had forbidden you from visiting graves, and from eating the meat of sacrificial animals for more than three days, and from drinking wine from vessels. Do not visit the graves, for they are Be renounced in this world, and be mindful of the Hereafter, and eat the meat of sacrificial animals, and keep whatever you wish, for I have only forbidden you from it, since goodness is little. Expansion on People, a vessel does not forbid anything, for every intoxicant is forbidden.”"
"1388","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Omar Al-Bazzar told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Salam told us Ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Al-Jabir, on the authority of Amr Ibn Amir, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I forbid you “Regarding visiting graves, visit them, for they remind you of death.”"
"1389","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Ahmad bin Imran Al-Akhnasi told us, Yahya told us Ibn Yaman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Murthad, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited the grave of his mother In a thousand masked people, he was not seen crying more than that day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1390","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz and Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us. Al-Farra’, Ya’la bin Ubaid narrated, Abu Munin told Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, visited He greeted his mother’s grave, and he wept and those around him wept, then he said: “I asked my Lord for permission to visit her grave, and He granted me permission, and I asked for His permission to visit her grave.” I ask forgiveness for her, as I have not been given permission to visit the graves, for they remind of death.” This hadith is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1391","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Shuaib Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Harrani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Nufaili told us, Zuhayr, narrated by Zubayd, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, close to a thousand Riding, he alighted with us and prayed two rak'ahs with us, then he turned to us with his face and his eyes streaming with tears, and Omar rose to him and ransomed his mother and father. He says: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “I asked my Lord for permission to ask forgiveness for my mother, but he did not give me permission. So tears came to my eyes out of mercy for her, and I asked my Lord for permission to visit her.” So permit me, and I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, and may their visiting them increase your goodness.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1392","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Muadh bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal Al-Dair told us, Yazid bin Zurai’, Bastam bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, Yazid bin Humaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, that Aisha came to the One day in the graves, so I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, where did you come from? She said: From the grave of my brother Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr, so I said to her: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid visiting Graves? She said: Yes, “He had forbidden, then he was ordered to visit her.”"
"1393","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Bishr bin Moaz Al-Aqdi told us, Amer bin Yasaf told us, Ibrahim told us Ibn Tahman, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abbad, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I forbade you from visiting Graves: Do not visit them, for it softens the heart, brings tears to the eyes, and reminds you of the Hereafter, and do not say, “Forsaking.”"
"1394","Ahmed bin Othman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Saeed bin Othman Al-Ahwazi told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Yahya told us, Abdul Aziz told us Ibn Muslim, and Yahya Ibn Abdullah Al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Amr Ibn Amir Al-Ansari, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so whoever wants to visit a grave should visit it, for it softens the heart. It brings tears to the eyes and reminds one of the Hereafter.”"
"1395","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Musa bin Dawud Al-Dhabi told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Visit the graves.” Remember the Hereafter with it, and wash the dead, for treating his body is an eloquent admonition. Pray over funerals, perhaps that will make you sad. “The sad person in the shadow of God is exposed to all goodness.” This is a hadith whose narrators are trustworthy from the last of them."
"1396","Abu Humayd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamid al-Adl told us about al-Tabaran, Tamim ibn Muhammad told us, Abu Musab al-Zuhri told us, Muhammad ibn Ismail bin Abi Fudaik, Suleiman bin Dawud informed me, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, that Fatima, daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “visit the grave of her uncle Hamza every Friday and pray and cry with him.” This hadith was narrated on the authority of The last of them are trustworthy, and I have investigated the encouragement to visit graves in order to participate in the encouragement, and so that the miserly person in his sin may know that it is a Sunnah. Masnouna, and may God’s blessings and peace be upon Muhammad and his entire family.”"
"1397","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Harb bin Maimun told us, on the authority of al-Nadr. Ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he passed by a funeral, and he said: “What is this?” They said: The funeral of so-and-so who loved God and His Messenger, worked in obedience to God, and strived in it. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is obligatory, it is obligatory, it is obligatory.” And another funeral took place. They said: The funeral of so-and-so, such-and-such who hated God and His Messenger, and committed sin. God is striving for it. He said: “It is obligatory, it is obligatory, it is obligatory.” They said: O Messenger of God, what you said about the funeral and praising it. The first was praised as good, and the last was evil, so you said it is obligatory. It was obligatory, it was obligatory, so he said: “Yes, Abu Bakr. Indeed, God has angels who speak on the tongues of the children of Adam regarding the good and evil that is in a person.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording.”"
"1398","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Anbari, and Tamim bin Muhammad told us, they said: Muhammad bin Aslam told us. Al-Abid, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no Muslim He dies, and four of the people of Abyat, his immediate neighbors, bear witness to him that they do not know anything but good from him, except God Almighty says And Blessed is He: I have accepted your statement - or he said: your testimony - and have forgiven him for what you do not know. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1399","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein informed us Ibn Waqid, narrated by Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, Show me a deed that if I do it, I will enter Paradise. He said: “Be a good person.” He said: How do I know that I am a good person? He said: “Ask your neighbors. If they say: You are a doer of good, then you are a doer, and if they say: You are a bad person, then you are a bad person.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”"
"1400","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hussein bin Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Asadi told us in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Diezel told us, Adam told us Ibn Abi Iyas, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit Al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: It was said, O Messenger of God, who are the people of Paradise? He said: “Who does not die until his ears are filled with what he loves?” It was said: Who are the people of Hell? He said: “Whoever does not die until his ears are filled with what he dislikes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1401","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Asbagh bin Al-Faraj Al-Masry told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Wahb, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Kharijah ibn Zayd informed him that Umm al-Ala, a woman from the Ansar, had pledged allegiance The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I told him that they had divided lots for the immigrants, so Uthman bin Mad’un flew to us and we put him down in Our verses. Then he felt the pain in which he died. When he died, he was washed and wrapped in his clothes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and I said: O Uthman. Ibn Maz'un, may God have mercy on you, Abu Al-Sa'ib. My testimony is that God has honored you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And what makes you know that God honored him? She said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. Who will God honor? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for him, certainty has come to him, and by God, I hope for good for him. By God, I do not know, and I Messenger of God, what will be done to me? She said: By God, I will never purify anyone after him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1402","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Ibrahim bin Abbad Al-Sana’ani informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us dictation, Ahmad ibn Najda al-Qurashi narrated to us, Saeed ibn Mansour narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he reported Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Tawus told me, on the authority of his father, that he used to say words after the tashahhud that he used to venerate greatly. I said: On both. Both? He said: Rather, in the second double after the tashahhud. I said: What is it? He said: “I seek refuge in God from the torment of Hell, and I seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in God from the evil of the Antichrist, and I seek refuge in By God, from the trials of life and death.” He said: And he used to venerate them. Ibn Jurayj said: Abdullah bin Tawus informed him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith based on the condition of the two sheikhs regarding seeking refuge from the torment of the grave, and they did not narrate it, and I have dictated what was authentic based on their condition in this matter. Which they did not mention in the Book of Faith, and I did not dictate this hadith.”"
"1403","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The dead hear the beating of their sandals when they turn away, so if he is a believer.” Prayer was at his head, fasting was at his right, zakat was at his left, and doing good deeds such as charity, prayer, and connections was Kindness and kindness to people are at his feet, and it is brought from his head, and the prayer says: There is no entrance before me, and it is brought from his right. So fasting says, “There is no entrance before me,” and it is given from his left, so zakat says, “There is no entrance before me,” and it is brought from before his feet, so he says, “Doing good deeds.” There is no entrance before me, so it is said to him: Sit, and he sits, and it appears to him that the sun has approached setting, and it is said to him: What do you say about this man who was among you? And what do you bear witness to? He says: Let me pray. They say: You will do so, but tell us what we ask you about. He said: What are you asking me about? They say: Tell us what we ask you about. He says: Let me pray. They say: You will do so, but tell us what we ask you about.He said: What are you asking me about? So they say: Tell us what you say about this man who was among you and what you testify against him? He says: Muhammad, I bear witness that he is the servant of God, and that he came with the truth from God, and it is said to him: On that you lived, and on that you died, and on that You will be resurrected, God willing, then a door of fire will be opened for him and it will be said to him: Look at your abode and what God has prepared for you, if you disobey. His joy and happiness increase, then a door to Paradise will be opened for him and it will be said to him: Look at your abode and what God has prepared for you, and it will increase. Bliss and happiness, and that is the saying of God, Blessed and Most High: {God establishes those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. And God misleads the wrongdoers, and God does what He wills} [Ibrahim: 27] “He said: And Abu Al-Hakam said, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and it will be said to him: “Lay him down. The bride whom no one wakes up except his family members who are dearest to him, or the people who love him the most.” Then he returned to the hadith of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and said: “ And if he is an unbeliever, he will be brought from the front of his head and nothing will be found, then he will be brought from his right and nothing will be found, then he will be brought from his left and nothing will be found, then he will be given By his feet, nothing was found, so it was said to him: Sit down, and he sat down, frightened and terrified.Then it will be said to him: What do you say about this man who was among you, and what do you testify against him? He says: What man? And they say: The man who was among you. He said: He will not be guided to him. He said: Then they say: Muhammad. He says: I heard the people say, so I said as they said. Then they say: For that I lived, and for that. You died, and upon that you will be resurrected, God willing. Then a door from Paradise will be opened for him and it will be said to him: Look at your abode and what God has prepared for you. If you had obeyed him, he would have increased in grief and embarrassment. He said: Then his grave would be narrowed for him until his ribs were separated. He said: That is his saying. Blessed and Most High: {Indeed, he will have a straitened livelihood, and We will gather him blind on the Day of Resurrection} [Taha: 124]”"
"1404","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, he hears the beating of their sandals when they turn away from him.” Then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner, except that the hadith of Saeed bin Amir completed “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1405","Abu Bakr bin Sulayman al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud Sulayman bin al-Ash’ath told us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, in the words of God Almighty: “a straitened living” [Ta-ha: 124] He said: “the torment of the grave.”"
"1406","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ibrahim, the Ismaili jurist, told us, Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Harun bin Ishaq told us. Al-Hamdani, told us by Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Abi Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to a funeral, and with him was Omar ibn al-Khattab, and he heard women crying, so Omar called them out, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O Umar, leave them alone, for the eye is watering, the soul is afflicted, and the era is near.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1407","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Usama bin Yazid told us, Al-Zuhri told me, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar crying and said: “But Hamza does not Weeping.” This reached the women of the Ansar and they cried for Hamza, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell asleep, then he woke up and they were crying, so he said: “Oh! Woe to them, they have been crying since today, so let them remain silent and do not cry over someone who has perished after today. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not They bring it out: “It is the most famous hadith in Medina, for the women of Medina do not mourn their dead until they mourn for Hamzah, and to this day.”
 The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, the debate between Abdullah bin Omar and Abdullah. Ibn Al-Abbas in crying over the dead, and their return to the mother of the believers, Aisha, and her saying: By God, what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. And peace be upon him: The dead person is tortured because of someone’s crying, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the infidel is tormented by the crying of his family in the sight of God.” Severe, and indeed it is God who laughs and makes us cry, and no woman who bears the burden of another bears the burden of another.”"
"1408","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Al-Qadi told us, Sulaiman bin Daoud told us, Abu Usama told us, Hammad bin Zaid told me, Ali bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi reported, Bishr bin Musa told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abu Usama Hammad bin Usama told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, said: Fatima said: O Anas, did you please your souls to throw dust on the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: And Fatima said: “O my father, he answered his Lord’s call to him. O my father, what is closer to his Lord? O my father, the Garden of Firdaus is his abode. “Father, to Gabriel, he mourned him.” Saeed bin Mansour added in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Usama, he said: I heard Hammad bin Zaid saying: “I saw Thabit Al-Bunani 149 When he told us this hadith, he cried until I saw his ribs shaking. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1409","Azhar bin Ahmad, the herald of Baghdad, informed me. Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Sayegh told us, Affan bin Muslim, and Abu al-Walid told us, saying: Shu'bah, and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Saydalaani told us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad ibn Bashar told us, they said: We told us: Shu'bah, I heard Qatada speaking, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shakhir, on the authority of Hakim ibn Qays ibn Asim, on the authority of his father, that He advised them upon his death, saying: “If I die, do not mourn over me, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not mourn over him.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, and it was not narrated by “Qais bin Asim al-Muqri, the master of Banu Tamim, and he has no other chain of transmission on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This letter, for he dictated his commandment: Do not mourn over me, for “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding mourning,” and witness this. The hadith is the hadith of Hasan Al-Basri, on the authority of Qais bin Asim, in mentioning his lengthy will, and there is evidence for it on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"1410","We informed him of Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Ismail al-Qaari, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When Abraham, the son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, Usama bin Zaid cried out, and said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is not of me, and it is not right for the heart to grieve and the eye to shed tears, but the Lord will not be angry.”"
"1411","Abu Ishaq al-Muzaki told us dictation, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Uqba bin Sinan al-Basri told us, Uthman bin Uthman al-Ghatfani told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, said: Abu Hurairah said: “If I die, do not mourn over me, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not mourn.” Accordingly, “This addition from Abu Hurairah is very strange, except that Othman Al-Ghatfani is not a condition of this book of ours.”"
"1412","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Hakim al-Wazir told us dictation, Hammad ibn Ahmad al-Qadi, and Muhammad ibn Hamdawayh al-Sanji told us, they said: We told us: Ali bin Hajr, Sharik told us, and Ali bin Mushar, they said: Abu Ishaq Al-Hijri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, he said: “The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He forbids lamentations.” Ibrahim bin Muslim Al-Hijri is not abandoned, except that the two sheikhs did not use him as evidence, and this The hadith bears witness to what was mentioned above, and it is strange and authentic, for Muslim has used Sharik bin Abdullah as evidence.”"
"1413","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Amer Al-Aqdi told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Salam, he said: Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, among my nation Four matters of pre-Islamic times are not to be abandoned: pride in lineage, discrediting lineages, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing over The dead, for if the mourning woman does not repent before she gets up, she will rise on the Day of Resurrection wearing robes of tar, and then it will boil over them. Shields from the flames of fire “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Muslim narrated the hadith of Aban bin Zaid, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir It is brief, and they did not include it with the additions that are in the hadith of Ali bin Al-Mubarak, and it is one of their conditions.”"
"1414","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muzaki informed us, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan informed us, Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, Abu Muawiyah informed us, Asim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: “When the verse was revealed: {When the believing women come to you, they will pledge their allegiance to you} [Al-Mumtahana: 12] To his saying: {And let them not disobey you} [Al-Mumtahana: 12] He was made to mourn, and I said: O Messenger of God, except the family of so-and-so, for they made me happy in Pre-Islamic times, so I must make them happy. He said: “Except the family of so-and-so.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1415","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Saeed bin Othman Al-Tanukhi told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Ismail bin Ubaid told me God, he said: Karima Al-Muzniyah told me, she said: I heard Abu Hurairah, while he was in the house of Umm Al-Darda’, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “There are three forms of disbelief in God: cutting one’s pocket, wailing, and disputing one’s lineage.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it."
"1416","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Bashir bin Muhajir told us, and Bukair bin Musa told us Muhammad bin Al-Haddad Al-Sufi, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the Ansar and visit them. He asked about them, but he was told about a woman from the Ansar whose son had died and she had no one else, and that she was greatly distressed by him, so he came to her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded her to fear God and be patient, so she said, O Messenger of God: I am a slave woman who cannot give birth, and I have no one else. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The slave woman whose offspring remains,” then he said: “There is no man or Muslim woman who will die for three days.” Children, except that God admits them to Paradise for them.” Then Omar said: O Messenger of God, may my father, my mother, and two be sacrificed for you. He said: “And two.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and it was not They bring it out with the remembrance of punishment.”"
"1417","Abu Al-Safar Ahmad bin Al-Fadl, the writer of Hamdan, told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Qurra, and Ahmad Ibn Ja’far told us, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad told us, Ubayy told us, Muhammad Ibn Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Qurra, He talks about his father, that a man used to come to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his son was with him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Do you love him?” He said: May God love you as you loved him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lost him and said: “What did so-and-so do?” They said his son had died, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Aren’t you happy if you never go to one of the gates of Paradise unless you find him waiting for you?” Then a man said: “For him specifically, or for all of us.” He said: “Rather, for all of you.” This is a hadith with a valid chain of narration, since I presented the mention of the uniqueness of the single follower. By narration on the authority of the Companions”"
"1418","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli narrated to us, Ma’mal bin Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Asbahani, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The children of the believers are in a mountain in Paradise.” “Abraham and Sarah will be responsible for them until he returns them to their fathers on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1419","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud bin Sulaiman told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Raja bin Muhammad Al-Adhari told us, Amr bin Muhammad told us Muhammad bin Abi Razin, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of his uncle, that Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah insulted Ali bin Abi Talib Then Zaid bin Arqam stood up to him and said: O Mughirah, did you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade cursing the dead, so why did you curse Ali?” And he died? This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it like this.”
 They only agreed on the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not curse the dead, for they have They achieved what they presented.”"
"1420","Ali bin Ahmad bin Qarqoub Al-Tamar told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, Shuaib bin Abi told me Hamza, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Hussein, Nawfal bin Musahiq told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not harm a Muslim by cursing an infidel.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1421","Abu Bakr bin Ja`far al-Muzaki told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Remember the virtues of your dead, and refrain from their injustices.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, and they did not narrate it. I found these hadiths in the chapter after the book on funerals was transmitted and they were narrated in its places before this.”"
"1422","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, Abu Muslim Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Bakr and Uthman told us, The sons of Abi Shaybah, they said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not defile your dead, for a Muslim does not defile himself alive or dead.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1423","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu al-Walid Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ahmad bin Burd al-Antaki told us, told us Al-Haytham bin Jamil, Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The angels said the greatest for Adam four times, and Abu Bakr said the greatest for The Prophet said four times, Omar said “Allahu Akbar” to Abu Bakr four times, Suhaib said “Allahu Akbar” to Omar four times, Al-Hasan said “Allahu Akbar” to Ali four times, and Al-Hussein said “Allahu Akbar” to Al-Hasan. Four: This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah is from the people of asceticism and knowledge, in a way that his like is not invalidated. However, the two sheikhs did not narrate it due to its poor memory, and there is evidence for this hadith.”"
"1424","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shakir told us, Khunays bin Bakr bin Khunays told us, Al-Furat told us Ibn Al-Sa’ib Al-Jazari, on the authority of Maymun Ibn Mahran, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, he said: “The last time the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the greatest “Funerals are four.” Omar said “Allahu Akbar” on Abu Bakr four times, Abdullah Ibn Omar said “Allahu Akbar” on Omar four times, and Al-Hasan Ibn Ali said “Allahu Akbar” on Ali. Four times, and Al-Hussein bin Ali said “Allahu Akbar” for Al-Hasan four times, and the angels said “Allahu Akbar” for Adam four times. It is not a requirement of this book, but I have brought it out as a witness.”"
"1425","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Ali, the preacher in Bukhara, told us, Ali bin Abdullah bin Mubashir Al-Wasiti told us, Ahmed bin Sinan told us, Abdullah told us Al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, he said: “Ibn Abbas prayed at a funeral, So he recited the opening of the book, so I told him and he said: It is from the Sunnah, or from the completion of the Sunnah. “This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1426","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Hamdani told us, Abu Shaybah Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “You do not have to wash your dead body if you wash it, for your dead body is not unclean, so it is sufficient for you to wash your hands.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it. It contains a rejection of a disputed hadith on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, with chains of narration: “Whoever washes a dead person, let him wash.”
 Zakat book"
"1427","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Imran bin Daoud Al-Qattan told us, Muammar told us Ibn Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, the Arabs reverted, so Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: O Abu Bakr, do you want to fight the Arabs? He said: Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but God and that I Messenger of God, and they establish prayer and pay zakat. By God, if they withhold from me a single caretaker of what they used to give the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I will fight them for it.” Omar said: When I saw Abu Bakr’s opinion explained to him, I knew that it was the truth. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, except that the two sheikhs did not narrate Imran. Al-Qattan, and they have no argument for leaving it, for it is an upright hadith, and the hadith of Abu Al-Anbas witnessed it, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1428","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Abu Al-Anbas Sa’id told us Ibn Kathir, my father told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no There is no god but God, and they establish prayer and pay zakat. Then their blood, their property, and their reckoning were forbidden to me from God Almighty.”"
"1429","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madani told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Aamir bin Shabib Al-Uqaili told me that his father told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The first three to enter Paradise were shown to me, and the first three to enter Hell. As for the first three to enter Paradise: So the martyr, and a slave slave who worshiped his Lord well and was sincere to his master, and a chaste, self-sufficient person with dependents, and as for the first three to enter Hell: a prince. A ruler, possessing wealth that does not fulfill God’s right to his wealth, and poor and immoral. “Amer bin Shabib Al-Uqaili is an upright sheikh from the people of Medina. The hadith, and this is the basis of this topic. Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated it alone on the authority of him, and he did not narrate it. Its evidence is the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority Abdullah bin Murrah"
"1430","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Naqid told me, Yahya told us Ibn Issa Al-Ramli, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, who said: “The servant of God is not the one who consumes usury and his client, and when they witness it, Those who teach him, the woman who wears the tattoo, the woman who wears the tattoo, the one who carries out charity, and the apostate Arab after the Hijra will be cursed, according to the words of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Judgment. “The Resurrection” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He cited Yahya bin Isa al-Ramli as evidence, but they did not narrate it."
"1431","Da'laj ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi told me, in Baghdad, Hisham ibn Ali al-Sadusi told me, Abdullah ibn Raja' told me, Sa`id ibn Salamah ibn Abi told me. Al-Hussam, Imran bin Abi Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In I gave charity on camels, I gave charity on sheep, I gave charity on cows, I gave charity on wheat, and whoever raises dinars and dirhams or dust and silver will not He prepares it for a creditor, and does not spend it in the way of God, for it is a treasure with which it will be burned on the Day of Resurrection.” Continued by: Ibn Jarir, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas"
"1432","Abu Qutaibah Salim bin Al-Fadl Al-Aadmi informed us in Mecca, Musa bin Harun told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, Muhammad bin Bukair told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Imran ibn Abi Anas, on the authority of Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In “I gave it in charity on camels, on sheep I gave it in charity, and on land I gave it in charity.” Both chains of transmission are authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"1433","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to Yemen, and he said: “Take the grain from the grain, the sheep from the sheep, the camel from the camels, and the cow from the cows.” This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. It is authentically heard from Ata’ bin Yassar on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, for I am not perfect in it.”"
"1434","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Arabism, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja`d al-Ghatfani, on the authority of Ma`dan bin Abi Talha al-Yamari, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever leaves behind him a treasure will be represented to him on the Day of Resurrection as a brave man. Two raisins will be called to him, and he will follow his mouth and say: Woe to you.” “I am your treasure that you left behind.” He continues to follow him until he touches his hand, and he bites it, then the rest of his body follows him. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness to his condition as well.”"
"1435","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Salih told us, and Ibn Bukair told us: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There will be a treasure On the Day of Resurrection, one of you will be a brave man with two raisins. He will follow his companion while he seeks refuge from him, and he will continue to follow him even though he is fleeing from him. Until he touches him with his two fingers.” The two sheikhs agreed to present the hadith of Ibn Masoud and Ibn Amr in this section for the sake of brevity, and in The strictness that prevents zakat, except that they did not narrate the hadith of Abu Hurairah and Thawban.”"
"1436","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, about Abu Yahya bin Amir Al-Kalai said: I heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on His stout camel had his legs in the stirrups stretched out, listening to people, so he said: “Don’t you hear my voice?” Then a man from among the people said, “What do you entrust to us?” He said: “Worship your Lord, pray your five daily prayers, fast every month, pay the zakat on your wealth, and obey those who command you. You will enter the Paradise of your Lord.” He said: I said: O Abu Umamah, who will you be like that day? He said: “I, my nephew, at that time, thirty years old, was pushing the camel and moving it closer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1437","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja`far, that Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata’ told him on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, he said: We entered upon Aisha. The wife of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon me and saw a piece of paper in my hand, and said: ‘What is this, O Aisha? So I said: I made them to adorn you with them, O Messenger of God. He said: “Do you pay their zakat?” I said: No, or whatever God wills of that. He said: “It is sufficient for you from the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"1438","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Anbasa bin Ahmad bin Al-Faraj told us, Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar told us, Muhammad bin Muhajir, on the authority of Thabit bin Ajlan, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that she was wearing veils of gold, so she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. Peace be upon him. She said: Is it a treasure? He said: “If you pay his zakat, it is not a treasure.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1439","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Al-Muhajir told us, Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Wahb, Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If you pay zakat “What is the matter with you? You have kept away from his evil.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it, and the witness to it is authentic from the hadith of the Egyptians."
"1440","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj Abi Al-Samh, on the authority of Ibn Hujayrah al-Akbar al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you pay zakat, you have fulfilled what you owe. And whoever collects illicit wealth and then gives it in charity, he will not receive any reward for it, and his insistence on it is obligatory.”"
"1441","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, And Hisham bin Ali, they said: Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: I took from Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas a book that claimed that Abu Bakr wrote it to Anas, and on it was the seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he sent him to authenticate him and wrote it for him, and lo and behold, in it was: “These The obligation of charity that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imposed on the Muslims and which God commanded his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to do. Whoever is asked about it Whoever submits according to its standard, let him give it, and whoever is asked for more than that, let him not give it, with regard to less than twenty-five camels, and a sheep for every herd. If she reaches the age of twenty-five, then she has a woman in labor until she reaches thirty-five, and if she does not have a woman in labor, then Ibn Labun. A male. If she reaches the age of thirty-six, then she is entitled to a Bint Labun up to forty-five. If she reaches the age of forty-six, then she is entitled to the right of a stallion. Up to sixty, and if she reaches sixty-one, then there is Jad`ah in it, up to seventy-five, and if she reaches seventy-six, then there are Bint Labun in it, up to Ninety, so if it reaches ninety-one, then it has two heqaqahs equal to the number of stallions, up to one hundred and twenty.If it exceeds one hundred and twenty, then in every forty there is a Bint Labun, and in every fifty there is a hqqah. If the teeth of camels differ in the obligatory duties. Alms: If someone has the amount of alms of a jud`ah but does not have a jud`ah, and he has a right, it will be accepted from him, and he must provide two sheep with it. If they are available for him, or twenty dirhams, and whoever has the amount of zakat that is due, but he does not have a due, and he has a judah, it will be accepted from him. The donor gives him twenty dirhams or two sheep, and whoever has the zakat of Bint Labun and has nothing but a right, it will be accepted from him. The donor shall give him twenty dirhams and two sheep, and whoever has the amount of zakat of Bint Labun, and he has nothing but the daughter of Makhad, it will be accepted. From it, two sheep or twenty dirhams, and whoever has the zakat of Bint Makhad and does not have anything but a male Ibn Labun, it will be accepted from him. And he does not have anything with him, and whoever does not have except four, then there is nothing in it unless its Lord wills it, and in the case of the flock of sheep if it is forty. Then it includes one sheep up to twenty and a hundred, and if it exceeds twenty and a hundred, then it includes two sheep until it reaches two hundred, then if it exceeds If it exceeds three hundred, then there is three sheep in it until it reaches three hundred. If it exceeds three hundred, then in every hundred sheep there is one sheep.Do not take for charity an old or one-year-old sheep, or a male goat of a sheep, unless the giver wishes. He should not combine separate ones, nor separate between combined for fear of charity, and as long as they are of a mixture, they are separated from each other in equal measure. If the man’s half-married woman does not reach forty, then he is not There is nothing in it unless its Lord wills, and in Raqqa there is a quarter of a tenth. If the wealth is only one hundred and ninety, then there is nothing in it except if He wills. Her Lord.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it like this. “Rather, Al-Bukhari was the only one to narrate it from another source, on the authority of Thumama.” Ibn Abdullah” and the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah is more correct, more correct, and more complete than the hadith of Al-Ansari."
"1442","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmed bin Salamah told us, and Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: We took this letter from Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas, who narrated to him, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner to the hadith of Musa bin Ismail, on the authority of Hammad, in its length, There is evidence for these words from the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father.”"
"1443","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Nufaili told us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter of charity and did not take it out to He worked with him until he was killed, so he tied it to his sword, and Abu Bakr worked with it until he was killed, then Omar worked with it until he was killed, and it was like: “On five camels. A sheep, and in ten there were two sheep, and in fifteen there were three sheep, and in twenty four sheep, and in twenty-five bent Makhad, to thirty-five. If it increases by one, then it has a Bint Labun up to forty-five, and if it increases by one, it has a right of right up to sixty, so if it increases by one It contains a jud`ah up to seventy-five, and if it is increased by one, then it contains two pints of laban, up to ninety. If it exceeds one, then it contains two hiqahs. Up to one hundred and twenty, and if the camels are more than that, then a hqqah is paid for every fifty, and for every forty is a Bint Labun, and for every sheep in every forty. Forty sheep up to one hundred and twenty sheep, then if it exceeds one, then two sheep up to two hundred, and if it exceeds one over two hundred, then Three sheep to three hundred, and if the sheep are more than that, then for every hundred sheep there is one sheep, and there is nothing in it until it reaches one hundred, and no It should be separated among a group, and it should not be combined among the dispersed for fear of charity, and if there are two mixtures, they will return to being equal, and it is not taken into account of charity. Old and without any blemish.” Al-Zuhri said: “When the certifier comes, you divide the thing into thirds: a third for the bad, a third for the good, and a third in the middle, and he takes The one who confirms from the middle.” Al-Zuhri did not mention Al-Baqar. This is a major hadith on this subject, which is attested by the many rulings in the hadith. Thumama, on the authority of Anas, except that the two sheikhs did not narrate Sufyan bin Husayn Al-Wasiti in the two books, and Sufyan bin Husayn is one of the imams The hadith was authenticated by Yahya bin Ma’in, and he entered Khorasan with Yazid bin Al-Muhallab, and from there he entered Nishapur. A group of our sheikhs heard from him. Al-Khundazis such as Mubashir bin Abdullah bin Razin and his brother Omar bin Abdullah and others, and he authenticated it according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, a hadith Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and if there is even the slightest transmission in it, then it is a true witness to the hadith of Sufyan bin Husayn"
"1444","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Muzaki Al-Maruzian informed us of Marwa, saying: Abu Al-Mujib informed Muhammad bin Amr, Abdan bin Uthman informed, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed me, Yunus bin told me Yazid, and Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, and the pronunciation is his, Abu Al-Muthanna informed us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: This is a copy of the letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in which he wrote about charity. It is with the family of Omar bin Al-Khattab. He said: Ibn Shihab taught it to me, Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar, and I found it on her face, and it is the one that was abrogated. Omar bin Abdul Aziz, from Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar and Salem bin Abdullah, when he was appointed commander of Medina, so he ordered his workers to work With it, he wrote it to Al-Walid, so Al-Walid ordered his workers to work with it, then the caliphs continued to order that after him, then he ordered Hisham copied it to every Muslim worker, and commanded them to act according to what is in it, and not to transgress it, and this is a book that explains it, “No Zakat is given on some camels until they reach the age of five, and if they reach five, then a sheep until they reach ten.If it reaches ten, then it has two sheep until it reaches fifteen, and if it reaches fifteen, then four sheep until it reaches five. And twenty-five, then when it reaches twenty-five, it is assigned, and there is an obligation of Bint Makhad, and if there is no Bint Makhad, then Ibn Labun is male until She reaches the age of thirty-five, and if she reaches the age of thirty-six, then she is entitled to Bint Labun until she reaches forty-five, and if she is forty-six. Then there is the Haqqa of a camel until it reaches sixty, and if it is sixty-one, then it includes a Ja’ma until it reaches seventy-five, then If she reaches the age of seventy-six, then she is entitled to Bint Labun until she reaches ninety. If she is ninety-one, then she is entitled to two haqqat taruqat al-jamal until When she reaches one hundred and twenty, then if she is one hundred and twenty-one, then she has three daughters of Labun until she reaches one hundred and twenty-nine, then If it is one hundred and thirty, it contains Bint Labun, and one heqqah until it reaches one hundred and thirty-nine. If it is one hundred and forty, it contains two heqqahs. And Bint Labun until she reaches the age of one hundred and forty-nine. If she is one hundred and fifty, then she has three rights until she reaches fifty-nine. And one hundred, so if it is one hundred and sixty, then it has four daughters of Labun until it reaches one hundred and sixty-nine.If it is one hundred and seventy-nine, then it has three daughters of Labun and a Haqqah until it reaches one hundred and seventy-nine. If it is one hundred and eighty-nine Then there are two Haqqaq and two daughters of Labun until it reaches one hundred and eighty-nine, and when it is one hundred and ninety, then there are three Haqqaq and three daughters of Labun. Until it reaches one hundred and ninety-nine, and if it is two hundred, then in it are four heqaqs, or five daughters of Labun, whichever age you find it took. To the extent of what we wrote in this book, then everything from camels is taken according to what we wrote in this book, and it is not taken from sheep. Zakat until it reaches forty sheep. If it reaches forty sheep, then one sheep until it reaches twenty and one hundred. If it reaches twenty-one. If it is one hundred sheep, then there are two sheep in it until it reaches two hundred, and if it is one sheep, and two hundred sheep, then there are three sheep in it until it reaches three hundred, then if it is more. On three hundred sheep, there are only three sheep in it until it reaches four hundred sheep, in which there are four sheep until it reaches five hundred sheep, then If it reaches five hundred, then there are five sheep in it until it reaches six hundred sheep, then there are six sheep in it, and if it reaches seven hundred, then there are seven sheep in it, until It reaches eight hundred sheep. If it reaches eight hundred sheep, then it has eight sheep until it reaches nine hundred sheep.If it reaches nine hundred sheep, then there are nine sheep in it until it reaches a thousand sheep, and when it reaches a thousand sheep, then there are ten sheep in it, then in each One hundred sheep is more than one sheep.” Among the things that bear witness to the authenticity of this hadith is “"
"1445","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ibn Ishaq told us, and Habib bin Abi told us. Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, that Abu Ar-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated to him, that when Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz was appointed successor He was sent to Medina to seek the pledge of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his pleasure in giving alms. He found with the family of Omar ibn al-Khattab a letter from Omar to his workers in Alms are like the letter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Amr ibn Hazm, so Omar ibn Abdul Aziz ordered his workers on the alms to take what In those two books, it was said in them: “The zakat for camels is more than ninety one zakat, up to twenty and one hundred. At one hundred and twenty-nine, it includes three daughters of Labun until it reaches one hundred and twenty-nine, if the camels are more than that. There is nothing in it that does not amount to ten of them until it reaches ten.” As for the letter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Amr ibn Hazm, it Its chain of transmission is a condition of this book, and for that reason I mentioned the context in its length.”"
"1446","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr and Muhammad, the two sons of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of their father, on the authority of their grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The letter that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wrote to Amr ibn Hazm: “If the value of the gold reaches two hundred dirhams “For every forty dirhams, there is a dirham.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it is evidence of the explained and interpreted book."
"1447","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hakam bin Musa, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Abdi told us, Abu Saleh told us Al-Hakam bin Musa Al-Qantari, Yahya bin Hamza told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazzm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, “On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he wrote to the people of Yemen a book containing the duties, the sunnahs, and the blood money, He was sent with Amr bin Hazm, and I recited to the people of Yemen, and this is its transcript: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad the Prophet to Sharhabeel Ibn Abd Kulal, Al-Harith Ibn Abd Kulal, and Nu’aym Ibn Kulal. It was said that Dhu Ra’in, Ma’afir, and Hamadan, as for what follows: “Your messenger has returned. And you were given of the spoils one-fifth of God’s, and of what God has decreed for the believers of a tenth in the property whatever the sky watered, or there was menstruation, or there was Ala’. It includes a tenth if it reaches five awsuqs, and what was irrigated by irrigation, and the Daliyah includes half a tenth if it reaches five awsqs, and for every fifth Of the wandering camels is a sheep until it reaches twenty-four years of age,If it is more than one over twenty-four, then it contains a daughter in labor, and if there is not, then a male son of Labun until she reaches thirty-five. If it is more than thirty-five, then it includes a daughter of Labun until she reaches forty-five. If it is more than one, then five Forty, it includes the right of the stallion’s truce until it reaches sixty, and if it is more than sixty, it includes one lump sum until it reaches five. And seventy, if it is more than one over seventy-five, then there is a daughter of Labun in it until she reaches ninety, if it is more than one over ninety There are two camels in it until it reaches one hundred and twenty, and if it exceeds one hundred and twenty, then in every forty there is a daughter of Labun, and in every Fifty hijkats are the size of a camel, and for every thirty bawkarahs you sell a log, and for every forty bawqoras you sell a cow, and for every forty free-roaming sheep you sell a sheep up to Until it reaches two hundred and one hundred and twenty, then if it is more than one hundred and twenty, then there are two sheep in it until it reaches two hundred, and if it is more than one. There are three sheep in it until it reaches three hundred, and if it exceeds, then for every hundred sheep there is a sheep, and there should not be an old or a lean person in the zakat. Nor a defective woman, nor a male goat of sheep, unless the confirmer wishes, and he should not combine separate ones.There is no distinction between a community regarding charity, and whatever is taken from the two mixtures is returned to them equally, and in every five times of paper Five dirhams, and whatever exceeds that, there is a dirham for every forty dirhams, and nothing is less than five uuqs, and for every forty dinars there is a dinar. Charity is not permissible. For Muhammad, nor for the family of Muhammad. It is only zakat, purifying themselves and for the poor believers, for the sake of God, and for the wayfarer, and not for the sake of the believers. A slave, and there is nothing in a farm or its workers if she pays her alms from the tithe, and there is nothing in a Muslim slave or in his horse.”
 He said: And it was in the book: “Indeed, the greatest sins in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection will be associating partners with God and killing the believer’s soul unjustly. And fleeing in the cause of God on the day of march, and disobeying one’s parents, and accusing one’s property, and learning magic, and consuming usury, and consuming the orphan’s wealth, and Umrah is the minor Hajj, and no one should touch the Qur’an except one who is pure, and there will be no divorce before possession, and no emancipation until it is bought, and none of you should pray in a garment. And the part of it is bare, and none of you will pray with his hair tied, and none of you will pray in a single garment with nothing on his shoulders.”And it was in the book: “Whoever assaults a believer and kills him out of clear evidence, there is a retaliation for him unless the guardians of the killed person are satisfied, and the blood money is included in the soul.” One hundred camels, and the blood money is due on the nose that he stricks, and the blood money is due on the tongue, and the blood money is due on the lips, and the blood money is due on the two eggs, and the blood money is due on the male, The blood money is due for the cross, the blood money for two eyes, half the blood money for one man, a third of the blood money for a female mother, and a third of the blood money for a dead animal. And in the mancala are fifteen camels, and on each finger of the hand and toe are ten camels, and in the tooth are five camels. Camels, and in the illustration there are five camels, and that the man should be killed with the woman, and the owner of the gold must pay a thousand dinars. This is a great, authentic hadith. Explained in this section, the Commander of the Faithful, Omar bin Abdul Aziz, bears witness to it, and the scholars of his time, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Zuhri, affirmed In authenticity, as I mentioned above, and Suleiman bin Dawud al-Dimashqi al-Khawlani is known as al-Zuhri, although Yahya bin Ma’in winked at him. Others have modified it “as Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali told me, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Hatim told us,He said: I heard my father and he was asked about the hadith of Amr ibn Hazm in the book of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which he wrote down for him regarding alms, and he said: Solomon Ibn Dawud Al-Khawlani, among us, is among those with whom there is no problem. Abu Muhammad Ibn Abi Hatim said: And I heard Abu Zur’ah say that. Al-Hakim said: “The I have exerted my utmost effort to produce these explained and summarized hadiths on zakat, and this book cannot do without it. He explained it, and I proved its authenticity with authentic chains of transmission from the caliphs and followers, accepting it and using it, including what is rich in it for those who He gave her to her, and our imam Shu`bah used to say in the hadith of Uqba bin Amir al-Juhani regarding ablution, because something like this is true for me on the authority of the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was more beloved to me than myself, my money, and my family, and that is a hadith in the voluntary prayer, so how about these Sunnahs that are the rules? Islam, and God is the Granter of success, and He is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.”"
"1448","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Bahz bin Hakim told us, and Ahmad told us Bin Salman, Ahmed bin Issa told us, Abu Muammar told us, Abd al-Warith bin Saeed told us, Bahz bin Hakim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “In every forty of Ibn Labun’s camels, the camels are not separated from their reckoning, who gave them If it is rented, he will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it, and he will divide his camel in half, one of the punishments of our Lord, none of which is lawful for the family of Muhammad.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of transmission based on what we mentioned in the authentication of this document, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1449","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to Yemen and ordered him to take one cow from every thirty cows.” A dinar, and from every forty old cows, and from every dreamer a dinar, or an equivalent of a clean garment. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1450","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Malhan told us, Yahya ibn Bukayr told us, al-Layth told me, Hisham told me Bin Saad, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdullah bin Ma’bad bin Abbas, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada Al-Ansari, on the authority of Qais bin Saad bin Worshiping the Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him on a quest, and his father said: Do not go out until you speak to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He made a promise, and when he wanted to leave, he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Qais, do not come on the day of On the Day of Resurrection, on your neck will be a camel that will howl, or a cow that will moo, or a sheep that will be bleating, and do not be like Abu Rughal.” He said: Sa’d and Abu Raghal? He said: “Mossadeq was sent by Saleh and found a man in Taif with a spoil of nearly a hundred sheep, except one sheep, and a young son who had no mother. The milk of that sheep was his livelihood. The owner of the sheep said: Who are you? He said: I am the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He welcomed him and said: These are my sheep. So take what you like. He looked at the milky sheep and said: This one. The man said: This boy, as you can see, has no food or drink other than her. He said: If you love milk, then I love it. Then he said: Take two sheep in their place, but he refused. So he continued to increase it, and he continued to increase it until five sheep were given to him. A fishing rod was in its place, but he refused. When he saw that, he went to his bow and shot it, killing it. He said: It is not befitting for anyone to come to the Messenger of God. Someone before me said this news, so the owner of the sheep, Salih, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told him, and Salih said: Oh God. Curse Abu Rughal, O God, curse Abu Rughal.” Saad bin Ubadah said: O Messenger of God, spare Qays from watering. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. They did not narrate it, and there is brief evidence of it. The condition of the two sheikhs”"
"1451","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Sulaiman told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Sa’id bin Yahya bin Sa’id Al-Umawi told us, we told him My father, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Saad bin Ubadah He believed it, so he said: “O Sa’d, be careful not to bring a camel on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel that has a burden on it.” He said: I cannot find it, nor will I bring it. So he pardoned him."
"1452","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah, on the authority of Amara bin Amr bin Hazzm, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me as a notary, so I passed by a man and he collected his money for me, but I could not find He has nothing to do with it, except for a woman in labor. So I said to him: Give a woman in labor, for she has told the truth to you. He said: That is something that has no milk or blood in it, but this one. A great, fat camel, and I said to him: I will not take what I have not been commanded to do, and this is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, near you. If you would like to come to him and offer him what you have offered me, then do so. If he accepts it from you, I accept it, and if he returns it to you, I return it to him. He said: So I will do it. He said: So he went out with me, and he left with the she-camel that he had shown me until we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Prophet of God, A messenger of yours has come to me to take from the charity of my wealth, and by God the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has never taken part in my wealth, nor has his Messenger ever before him, so I collected He has my money, so he claimed that I had nothing in it but a woman in labor, and that was something that had no milk or blood, and I offered him a great she-camel for him to take. But Ali refused, and here it is, I have brought it to you, O Messenger of God. Take it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “That is what you owe. If you volunteer to do good, God will reward you for it and we will accept it from you.” He said: Here it is, O Messenger of God. I have brought it to you, so take it. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that it be seized, and he called for it. What is his blessing? “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1453","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad informed us, Saeed bin Sulaiman informed us, Muhammad bin Muslim informed us, Amr bin Dinar, who said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no charity in Raqqa.” Until it reaches two hundred dirhams.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he witnessed it with explanation in the hadith of Asim bin Damrah."
"1454","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is nothing in one hundred and ninety, so if It amounted to two hundred, so there were five dirhams in it.”"
"1455","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, and Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, In Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, they said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He sent to a man and he sent to him a missing detachment. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who confirms God has come to him, and the one who confirms it has come.” His Messenger, so he sent with a lost herd. Oh God, do not bless him or his camels. The news of this reached the man, so he sent him a beautiful she-camel. And her beauty, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “So-and-so reported what the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, so he sent a she-camel of her beauty. Oh God, bless him and his camels.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1456","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Saydalani told us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudharib, who said: Some people from the Levant came to Omar, may God be pleased with him, and they said: We have acquired wealth: horses. We would like to have zakat and purification from it. He said: Whatever my companions did before me, I will do. So Omar consulted Ali, may God be pleased with them both, regarding A group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ali said: “It is good if it is not a tribute for which they take a salary.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, except that the two sheikhs did not narrate it on the authority of Haritha, but rather I mentioned it in this place due to the regular hadiths that were imposed. In. . . """
"1457","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Sinan told us, Ahmad bin Sinan told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Uthman, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, said: We have the book of Muadh ibn Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that it was only “He took charity from wheat, barley, raisins, and dates.” This hadith has been used as evidence by all its narrators, but they did not narrate it. “And Musa bin Talha A great follower, and it was not denied that he lived in the days of Muadh, may God be pleased with him.”"
"1458","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Umair bin Mirdas told me, Abdullah bin Nafi’ Al-Sayegh told me, Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Regarding The sky, Baal, and the flood watered the tithe, and of what was irrigated with a sprinkler, half the tithe, and that only occurred in dates, wheat, and grains. As for the cucumbers, melons, pomegranates, and reeds, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pardoned them. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He narrates it, and he has a witness with an authentic chain of narration.”"
"1459","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Nasr al-Marwazi told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, we told him: Sufyan, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, and Muadh bin Jabal, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent them to Yemen teaches people about their religion: “Do not take charity except from these four: barley, wheat, raisins, and dates.”"
"1460","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Muslim man does not have to pay zakat on his vineyard, nor on his crops.” If it is less than five wasqs” this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1461","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Abu Al-Walid told us, Sulayman bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, on the authority of his father, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two types of dates: juror and Al-Hubaiq said: There were people who performed tayammum for the worst of their fruits, so they gave them as charity, but they prohibited two types of dates, so the verse was revealed: {And do not perform tayammum The evil of it you spend} [Al-Baqarah: 267] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.” Sufyan bin Hussein and Muhammad bin Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri
 As for the hadith of Sufyan bin Hussein:"
"1462","So Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Saeed bin Sulayman told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan. Bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the giving of charity, so a man from This lizard is like porcupine - Sufyan said: meaning the porcupine - so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who brought this?” And no one brought anything except that it would be attributed to the one who brought it, so the verse was revealed: {And do not spend from it the evil one.} [Al-Baqarah: 267] He said: “And the Messenger of God forbade God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of Al-Jarur and the color of Habeek, to be taken as charity. Al-Zuhri said: “Two colors of dates for charity.”
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Abi Hafsa:"
"1463","So Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed him, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed, about... Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunaif, on the authority of his father, he said: There were people who used to perform the evil of their fruits, So God Almighty and Majestic revealed: {And do not spend from it the evil, and you will not take it unless you close your eyes to it} [Al-Baqarah: 267] He said: “So the Messenger of God forbade God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of two colours: on the basis of scars and on the authority of the huebeek color.”"
"1464","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya and Abdul Rahman told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, narrating on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Masoud bin Nayyar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, he said: He came to us while we were in the market, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you cut, take and leave a third, but if you do not take or leave a third - Shu’bah doubted the third. - So they called a quarter. Al-Hakim said: “You agreed between Yahya and Abd al-Rahman, and there is no doubt in the hadith of Wahb bin Jarir, Shu’bah. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission” and it has a witness with a chain of transmission whose authenticity is agreed upon. Omar ibn al-Khattab ordered it."
"1465","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Left, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, sent him to harvest dates and said: “When you come to a land So cut it down, and leave for them as much as they eat.”"
"1466","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Umar al-Ghadani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man from Banu Amir passed by him, and it was said: This is one of the most wealthy people, so Abu Hurairah invited him So he asked him about that, and it was said: Yes, I have a hundred red ones, and I have a hundred bloody ones, and I have such-and-such sheep, so Abu Hurairah said: Beware of wearing shoes. Camels, beware of the hooves of sheep. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no man who owns camels who does not pay their rights to them.” I helped her, and He sent her through hardship and ease, except that a gurgling spot appeared to him, and she came to him as the most nourishing and fattest he could be, or The greatest of them - Shu'bah Shuk - tramples him with her loafers and gores him with her horns. Whenever she passes over him with the last of them, the first of them will be returned to him on a day that was Its length is fifty thousand years until it passes among the people and its path is seen, and there is no servant who owns cows who does not fulfill his right to help them. And her messengers.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And I helped her, and her messengers, through her hardship and her ease, but a gurgling bottom appeared to him like the softest it could be. And he captured him and made him fatter and larger, and she would trample him with her hooves and gore him with her horns. Whenever she passed the first part of it over him, the last part of it would be returned to him in A day whose equivalent is fifty thousand years, until God judges between the people and sees His way. Then Al-Abbas said to him: What is the right of camels? Kitten? He said: “You give generously, and you give generously, and you make the back poor, and you give the stallion to drink and give milk to drink.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They narrate it, but Muslim narrated some of these words from the hadith of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Abu Omar Al-Ghadani is said to be: Yahya bin Ubaid Al-Bahrani. If that is the case, then a Muslim has used it as evidence, and I do not know of anyone who narrated it, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Aaron, and we did not write it down mostly except on the authority of Abu al-Abbas al-Mahboubi. Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Nasa’i told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Sahl told us, They said: Yazid bin Harun told us something similar."
"1467","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah Bin Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Bilal bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took “The Qibliya is charity, and he cut all the aqeeqs for Bilal bin Al-Harith.” When Omar, may God be pleased with him, said to Bilal: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, God, peace and blessings be upon him, did not cut you off so that you could keep him from people. He only cut you off so that he could do something. He said: So Omar bin Al-Khattab cut the aqeeq for the people, “Al-Bukhari cited Nu’aym bin Hammad as evidence, and Muslim cited Al-Darawardi, and this is an authentic hadith. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1468","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Shu’bah told us, and he told us Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a man from Banu Makhzum to provide charity, and he said to Abi Rafi’: Accompany me as I have had a share of it, and he said: No, until I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him, and he said: “Indeed Charity is not permissible for us, and the people’s loyalists are from themselves.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1469","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, about Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Shamasa, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The owner of a tax will not enter Paradise.” Yazid bin Harun said: “meaning the tax collector.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1470","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed me, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Malhan informed me, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani informed us, Ubaid Allah told us Bin Amr Al-Raqi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Awf Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, he said: Umm Salamah told us that While the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in her house and some of his companions were talking, when a man came and said: O Messenger of God, how much charity? Such and such dates? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Such and such dates.” Then the man said: So-and-so transgressed against me, and took such-and-such from me, and it increased. Saa’, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So what if someone is named after you who is transgressing against you worse than this transgression?” So the people panicked and panicked. The hadith until a man among them said: O Messenger of God, if a man is absent from you regarding his camels, his cattle, and his crops, then he pays the zakat on his money. So the truth was transgressed against him, so how could he act while he was absent? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever pays the zakat on his wealth, it will be good for himself. With him the face of God, and the Hereafter, he did not lose any of his wealth, and he established prayer and paid zakat, but the truth transgressed against him, so he took his weapon and fought. So he was killed, so he is a martyr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1471","Abu Ishaq bin Firas Al-Faqih told us in Mecca, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Shuaib bin Yahya Al-Tajibi told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, On the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, that when it was the year of Ramadi and the land became barren, Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote: To Amr ibn Al-Aas: From Abdullah Omar, Commander of the Faithful, to Amr ibn Al-Aas, Al-Amri told me, “Don’t care if you get fat,” and before you. That I am weak, and before me, and O Ghutha, so Amr wrote: “Peace be upon you. As for what follows: Labayk Labayk, a caravan has come to you, the first of which is with you. I have the last one, although I hope to find two ways to carry it in the sea.” When the first caravan came, he called Al-Zubayr and said: “Go out at the beginning of this.” Bring it to me tomorrow, and carry to every household what you are able to carry for me, and whoever you are not able to carry, pass to every household. with a camel according to what it is upon, and command them to dress the people as they came, and to slaughter the camel, and to bear its hair, and to prepare its flesh, and to imitate His skin, then let them take a handful of chickpeas, a handful of lard, and a handful of flour, and let them cook and eat until God brings them. Sustenance.” Al-Zubayr refused to leave, so he said: “By God, you will not find someone like her until you leave this world.” Then he called another, whom I think is Talha. So he came, then he called Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah and he went out about that. When he returned, he sent him a thousand dinars, and Abu Ubaidah said: I did not work. To you, Ibn Khattab, I only worked for God, and I do not take anything from that. Omar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has given us some things.” We sent a mission to it, but we disliked it, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, refused to do so, so accept it, O man, and seek help from it in your worldly life.” Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah accepted it, saying, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1472","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Hayyan bin Malaab told us, Abu Asim told us, Abd al-Warith bin Saeed, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever we employ to do work So We provided him with sustenance, and whatever he took after that was deceit.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1473","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told me, Al-Hussein bin Idris Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us. Al-Mawsili, Al-Mu’afa bin Imran told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Al-Harith bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Shaddad said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever is a worker for us, let him get a wife, even if he does not have a servant.” Let him find a servant, and whoever does not have a home, let him find a home.” He said: And I was informed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever If he takes something other than that, then he is an extremist, or a thief.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1474","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Asim Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Labid, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who works to give charity in truth is like a fighter in the cause of God until he returns to his home.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1475","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Sana’ani told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of his mother, Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, Sufyan said: She had prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two qiblahs. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The best charity is given to one with open kinship.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a witness. With an authentic chain of transmission.”"
"1476","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, according to dictation, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzar told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Hafsa Bint Sirin, on the authority of Umm Al-Raih bint Sulay, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Giving charity to the poor It is charity, and there are two things owed to a relative: charity and connection.”"
"1477","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Mawsili told us, Ali bin Harb told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, It is said, “It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to a straight person.” This hadith is according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Witnessed by the hadith of Abdullah. Bin Amr"
"1478","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Awwam told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of his father, and Abd al-Rahman told us Ibn Al-Hasan Al-Qadi, Ibrahim Ibn Al-Hussein told us, Adam Ibn Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Rayhan Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to a powerful person.” This is what Al-Thawri said. And Shu`bah, and in the hadith of Ibrahim bin Saad, “Suway”"
"1479","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hakim Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asked And he has something that will enrich him. He will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches, scratches, or soreness on his face. It was said: O Messenger of God, what is wealth? He said: “Fifty dirhams or its value in gold.” Yahya bin Adam said: Abdullah bin Uthman said to Sufyan: My guess is that Shu’bah He did not narrate, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, Sufyan said: Zubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid."
"1480","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Ziyad informed us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible Charity is given to a rich person, except for five things: to one who fights in the cause of God, or to one who works for it, or to a debtor, or to a man who has a poor neighbor, so you give in charity. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it because Malik ibn Anas sent it to him on the authority of Zaid.” Ibn Aslam"
"1481","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Marwazi told us, Ahmad bin Issa told us, Al-Qanabi told us, regarding what was read to Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Charity is not permissible except for five people.” He mentioned the hadith. This is from a policeman in a sermon. The book is authentic, so Malik may send a hadith and he transmits it or transmits it with trustworthiness, and the statement about it is the statement of trustworthiness that transmits it and transmits it with trustworthiness.”"
"1482","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Bashir bin Salman informed us, On the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is afflicted with poverty and inflicts it on people, he will not He fills his need, and whoever sends it down by God, God will bring him wealth at the verge of wealth, either by a delayed death or immediate wealth. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1483","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Ubaida bin Humaid al-Ammi told us, Abu Al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father Malik bin Nadlah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hands are three: the hand. God is the highest, and the hand of the giver is next to it, and the hand of the beggar is the lowest, so give the bounty, and do not fail to help yourself. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.” This is witnessed by the well-known preserved hadith on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud."
"1484","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muslim Al-Hijri, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, narrating on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hands are three.” Muscat To complete the conversation"
"1485","So Ahmad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Hijri, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The hands are three: the hand of God that is highest, and the hand of the giver that Follow it, and the lower hand of the beggar will remain until the Day of Resurrection, so abstain from begging as much as you are able.”"
"1486","Abu Amr Ismail bin Nujaid told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muslim Al-Hijri, so he mentioned it similarly, and said in it: “So abstain from asking questions as much as you are able.”"
"1487","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ali bin Abdullah bin Al-Madini told us, Yahya bin Ya’la told us Al-Muharbibi, Abi told us, Ghaylan bin Jami’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When it was revealed This verse: {And those who hoard up} [At-Tawbah: 34] gold and silver. This was difficult for the Muslims, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: I will release On your behalf, he went off and said: O Prophet of God, this verse is difficult for your companions, so he said: “God did not impose zakat except to purify what What remained of your wealth, but inheritances were made obligatory - and he mentioned a word - so that they would be for those after you.’ He said: So Omar said: “Allahu Akbar.”
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the best of what is hoarded? “When he looks at her, she pleases a righteous woman, when he commands her, she obeys him, and when he is absent from her, she protects him.” This is an authentic hadith based on The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"1488","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Safar in the year three hundred and ninety-six. Abu Al-Hasan told me Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mihran Al-Ismaili, Ubayy told us, Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told us, Marwan bin Muhammad Al-Dimashqi told us, Marwan bin Muhammad Al-Dimashqi told us Yazid bin Muslim Al-Khawlani, who was a sheikh of Sadiq, and Abdullah bin Wahb used to narrate from him. Sayyar bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Sadafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imposed Zakat al-Fitr as a purification of the fast from idle talk. And concubines, and food for the poor. Whoever gives it before prayer, it is an accepted zakat, and whoever gives it after prayer, it is one of the charitable acts.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 1488 - according to Al-Bukhari’s conditions"
"1489","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul-Aziz bin Abi told us Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “People used to pay zakat al-fitr during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he handed over a Saa of dates, or a Saa of barley, or salt, or raisins. This is an authentic hadith. Rawwad Ayman, and they did not pronounce it with this wording.”"
"1490","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib and Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, they said: Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us. Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: When he imposed the zakat al-fitr as a saa’ of Dates, or a Saa’ of barley, and he would not produce anything except dates. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not produce it in it: “except dates.”"
"1491","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Tha’labi told us, Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymrah, on the authority of Abu Ammar Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us He acknowledged the zakat al-fitr before the zakat was due, and when the zakat was due he did not command us nor forbid us, but we did it. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but I made it in parallel with the hadith of Abu Ammar, so it is recommended, and this is obligatory.”"
"1492","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ali Al-Warraq, whose nickname was Hamdan, told us, Dawud bin Shabib told us, Yahya bin Abbad told us, and he was From the best of the people, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave an order shouting to the interior of Mecca, calling: “Indeed Zakat al-Fitr is an obligatory right for every Muslim, young or old: male or female, free or owned, present or foreign, a saa’ of barley or Dates: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with these words.”"
"1493","Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Qalusi told me, Bakr bin Al-Aswad told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, urged each person to give charity in Ramadan, giving each person a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of dates. of barley, or a saa’ of wheat “This is an authentic hadith, and it has an authentic witness.”"
"1494","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman bin Al-Hadrami told us, Zakaria bin Yahya bin Subaih told us, and Abu Bakr told us Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balwayh, Ahmed bin Al-Kharaz told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim Al-Tarjmani told us, they said: Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us. Al-Jumahi, told us by Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “obligated zakat al-fitr A saa of dates, or a saa of wheat, for every Muslim free man or slave, male or female.”"
"1495","Ahmad bin Ishaq bin Al-Saydalani Al-Adl narrated to us in dictation, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi narrated to us, Abu Abdullah Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us, Ismail bin Aliya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Uthman bin Hakim bin Hazzam, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh said: Abu Saeed said, and he mentioned zakat al-fitr, and he said: “I do not give it except what I used to give it.” During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a saa of dates, or a saa of wheat, or a saa of barley, or a saa of acorns. Then a man from the people said to him: Or a debt of wheat? He said: “No, that is the value of Muawiyah. I will neither accept it nor act upon it.” These are all the chains of narration that I mentioned in mentioning the saa’ of righteousness. Authentic, and the most famous of them is the hadith of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in which we were superior, but I left it as it is not a condition of the Book. It was narrated on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him"
"1496","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muzaki told us, Ahmad ibn Salamah told us, al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah told us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said in “charity Al-Fitr: for every young or old, free or slave, a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of dates. “This is how it was transmitted on the authority of Ali, and others stopped it.”"
"1497","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Amri told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Aziz Al-Ayli informed us, Salama bin Rawh told us, On the authority of Aqeel bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Harith, that he heard Ali bin Abi Talib ordering zakat al-fitr, and he said: “A saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of barley, or a saa’ of wheat, or salt, or raisins.” It was also narrated with a chain of transmission, the same of which appears in Evidence, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"1498","Abu Al-Walid Al-Anazi told us, Abbad bin Zakaria told us, Sulaiman bin Arqam told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaysah bin Dhu’ayb, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and said: “Whoever has food, let him give in charity a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of barley, or A saa of dates, or a saa of flour, or a saa of raisins, or a saa of salt.”"
"1499","Abu Nasr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Hamid al-Tirmidhi told me, Muhammad bin Jabal al-San’ani told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, On the authority of Hisham bin Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother, Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them, that she narrated to him, that they During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they used to pay Zakat al-Fitr with the mudd with which the Ahl al-Bayt sustained food, or with the saa with which they subsisted. With it, all the people of the city will do that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it is the evidence for a debate with Malik. And Abu Yusuf, may God have mercy on them.”"
"1500","Abu Omar Muhammad bin Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Adl told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin al-Bakhtari told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh told us, Abi told us Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Thuban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who will guarantee for me that he will not ask people for anything, so that I will guarantee Paradise for him?” Thawban said: “I do.” He did not ask people anything. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1501","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Sahl bin Mihran Al-Baghdadi told me, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told me, Mubarak bin Fadalah told me, On the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Has anyone among you fed a poor person today?” Abu Bakr said: I entered the mosque, and suddenly I was asked by someone, and I found a piece of bread in Abdul Rahman’s hand, so I took it. So I handed it to him, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1502","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Zuraiq, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks you by God, give him, and whoever seeks refuge in God So seek refuge with him, and whoever calls you, answer him, and whoever gives you a gift, reward him. If you do not find something to reward him, then pray for him until you see that you have “You rewarded him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. “Ammar bin Zurayq was followed in establishing this chain of narration by: Abu Awanah and Jarir bin Abd al-Hamid and Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim al-Qasmali, on the authority of al-Amash, as for the hadith of Abu Awanah"
"1503","So Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Muhammad bin Isa Al-Tarsusi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Awanah told us, and as for the hadith of Jarir"
"1504","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us, Zuhair bin Harb narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, and as for the hadith of Abdul Aziz Bin Muslim"
"1505","So Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Mu’alla bin Asad told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim told us, “These are the agreed upon chains of narrations.” Although it is authentic, it cannot be explained by the hadith of Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Ma’n, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Mujahid, and when Al-A'mash has another authentic chain of narration according to their conditions."
"1506","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir bin Shazan told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks of you by God, give him, and whoever “He seeks refuge with you in God, so seek refuge in him, and whoever calls upon you, answer him.” This is an authentic chain of narration. Both chains of narration are authentic according to Al-A’mash, on the condition that The two Sheikhs, and we adhere to our principles in accepting additions from trustworthy narrators in the chains of transmission and texts.”"
"1507","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Asim Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Labid, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them both, He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came to him with something like an egg made of gold, and he said: O Messenger of God, I got this from Mine, take it, for it is charity. I have no other property. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from it, then he came to him from his right corner. So he said something like that, so he turned away from it, then he came to him from his left corner and he turned away from it, then he came to him from behind him, and the Messenger took it. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, struck him with it. If it had struck him, it would have caused him pain and made him obstructed. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “One of you comes.” With what he possesses, he says, “This is charity,” then he sits begging the people. The best charity is that which is done from the back of wealth. This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1508","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah bin Sa’d heard Abu Sa’id al-Khudri say: A man entered the mosque and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to put out clothes for him, so they put them out for him. So he ordered two garments for him from it, then he urged charity, so he came and threw out one of the two garments and shouted about it and said: “Take your garment.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1509","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim told us, Ibn Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Ja`dah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of God, which charity is better? He said: “The effort of the one you rely on, and start with those you depend on.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1510","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nusayr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us One day we would give alms, and that amounted to money I had, so I said: Today I will outpace Abu Bakr if I ever outpaced him, so I brought half of my money, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “What have you left for your family?” So I said: The same, and Abu Bakr brought everything he had and said: “O Abu Bakr, what have you left for your family?” He said: I have left for them God and His Messenger, and I said: I will never race with you in anything. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1511","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Muhammad bin Arara told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Hassan, on the authority of Saad bin Ubadah, may God be pleased with him, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Which kind of charity do you like most? He said: “Irrigating water,” followed by Hammam, on the authority of Qatada"
"1512","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed, that Saad, may God be pleased with him, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Which charity do you like most? He said: “Water.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1513","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, and he told me Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, Abdah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I had a slave girl. So I freed her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me and said: “May God reward you, but if you had given it to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater.” For your reward.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1514","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza told us, Qubaisa told us, Sufyan told us, and Muhammad ibn Hazim told us Ahmad al-Mahboubi, Ahmad ibn Sayyar told us, Muhammad ibn Kathir told us, Sufyan reported, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered the giving of charity, and a man said: O Messenger of God, I have a dinar. He said: “Give it in charity for yourself.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it to your child in charity.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it in charity to your husband” - or he said: “To your wife.” He said: I have another. He said: “Give it in charity to your servant.” He said: I have another who said: “You can see.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1515","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Qubaisa told us, and Abu Al-Abbas told us Al-Mahboubi, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, Ahmad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah, they said: Sufyan, who is Al-Thawri, narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahb bin Jabir Al-Khaywani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is enough sin for a man to neglect those who feed him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They brought it out, and Wahb bin Jabir was one of the major followers of Kufa.”"
"1516","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, and Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, they said: We told us: Shu’bah, and Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Bishr bin Omar told us, and Wahb bin Jarir told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech. He greeted him and said: “Beware of stinginess, for those before you perished because of stinginess. He commanded them to be stingy, but they were stingy, and he commanded them to cut ties with each other.” So they cut them off, and he commanded them to commit immorality, so they committed immorality.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission. It was not narrated by “and Abu Kathir al-Zubaidi, one of the major followers.”"
"1517","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Harmala bin Imran informed us, That he heard Yazid bin Abi Habib speaking, that Abu Al-Khair told him, that he heard Uqba bin Amir, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. He says: “Every person is subject to his charity until he is judged between the people.” Or he said: “Until he is judged between the people.” Yazid said: Abu Al-Khair was “no.” He will miss a day when he does not give anything in charity, not even a cake or an onion.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1518","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, on the authority of Qurrah, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrated, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, who said: “It was mentioned to me that deeds show off, and charity says: I am the best of you.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1519","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakra Bakkar bin Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Above A dirham is one hundred thousand. They said: O Messenger of God, how can a dirham precede a hundred thousand? He said: “A man had two dirhams, so he took one of them and gave it in charity, and another had a lot of money, so he took one hundred thousand from her offering.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1520","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, and Wahb bin Jarir, they said: Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad told us. Bin Ja`far, Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Rab`i bin Harash, on the authority of Zayd bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, upon him be peace, said: “There are three whom God loves, and three whom God hates. As for the three whom God loves: A man came to a people and asked them. By God, and he did not ask them about their kinship with him, so one of their followers left behind, so he gave him a secret. No one knows about his gift except God and Him. He gave it to him, and some people walked throughout the night until sleep was more beloved to them than what they had to do with it, so they came down and laid down their heads, and a man stood up and flattered me. And he recites My verses, and a man was in a troop and met the enemy and was defeated, so he attacked him until he was killed, or a victory was granted to him, and the three whom he hates God: The adulterous old man, the deceitful poor man, and the oppressive rich man. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1521","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No man gives any zakat until it is redeemed.” “On the authority of her, ‘I live with seventy devils.’ This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1522","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzaz narrated to us, and Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab narrated to us, saying: Saeed bin Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded those who “Every wall has a channel for the mosque.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and its witness is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1523","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Sahl bin Bakkar narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi bin Hibban, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made permission for the naked people to be one wasq, two wasqi, three, and four, and said: “In a judah for every ten A small wasq is given to the poor in the mosque.”"
"1524","Ahmad bin Sahl bin Hamdawayh al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Sa`id bin Sulayman al-Wasiti told us, Al-Layth bin Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bujaid, brother of Banu Haritha, that his grandmother told him, and she is Bujaid’s mother, She claimed that she was among those who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because she said: O Messenger of God, by God, the poor person must stand up for My door, we cannot find anything for him to give him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “Then if you do not find anything to give him except an armful.” Burned, so give it to him in his hand.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take it out."
"1525","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali al-Saghani told us about Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Ubadah told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, and Muhammad informed us Ibn Yaqoub Al-Shaybani, Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim, and Muhammad Ibn Rafi’ told us, they said: Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Many, on the authority of Zayd ibn Salam, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Azdi, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Two jealousies, one of which God loves, and the other God hates, and two imaginations, one of which God loves. And the other things God hates. God loves jealousy without doubt, and God hates jealousy without doubt. And imagination when a man gives charity. God loves it, and God hates imagination due to arrogance.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1526","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, dictating in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “God says God Almighty: I asked my servant for a loan, but he did not lend it to me, and my servant cursed me while he did not know it, saying: And I forbade him, and I forbade him, and I am eternal. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1527","Abu Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah told us Bin Al-Mubarak, Haywa bin Shurayh told us, Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid Abu Uthman informed us, that Uqba bin Muslim told him, that Shafia told him He entered the city and saw a man whom the people had gathered around. He said: Who is this? They said: Abu Hurairah. He said: So I approached him until I sat in front of him, while he was speaking to the people. When he remained silent and became silent, I said: I adjure you by God in truth and truth. When you told me a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you knew it, then Abu Hurairah said: I will, I will tell you a hadith, tell it to me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him his wisdom and knowledge, then Abu Hurairah became anxious, so he stayed for a while, then he woke up and said: I will talk to you. A hadith that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me while he and I were in this house, and no one was with us except me and him. Then Abu Hurairah got busy. Another longing, so he remained like that, then he woke up and wiped his face, and said: I will narrate to you a hadith that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me. He said hello, and he and I were in this house, and no one was with us except me and others. Then Abu Hurairah became anxious.Then he leaned down and fell on his face, and I supported him for a long time, then he recovered and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: “Indeed, God Almighty, when On the Day of Resurrection, He will descend to His servants to judge among them, and every nation will be kneeling. The first to be invoked by Him will be a man who compiled the Qur’an, and a man who will be killed in For the sake of God, and a man with a lot of money. Then God says to the reader: Did I not teach you what I revealed to My Messenger? He said: Yes, O Lord. He said: So what did you do about it? Did you know? He said: I used to do it at night and during the day, and God would say to him: You lied, and the angels would say to him: You lied, and God Almighty would say to him. God Almighty: You wanted it to be said that so-and-so is a reader, and it has been said, and the owner of the money is brought and says: Have I not been generous to you to the point that I have not left you in need of anyone? He said: Yes, he said: What did you do with what I gave you? He said: I was upholding the ties of kinship and giving in charity. Then God says: You lied, and the angels say: You lied, and God says: Rather, you wanted it to be said that so-and-so is generous, and that has been said, and the man who was killed in the cause of God will be brought and it will be said to him: What were you killed for, and he will say: I was commanded By jihad in your cause, I fought until I was killed, and God says: You lied, and the angels say to him: You lied, and God says: Rather, you wanted it to be said So-and-so is bold, and that has been said.”Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck my knee and said: “O Abu Hurairah, these three will be the first of God’s creation to be set on fire on the Day of Judgment. “The Resurrection” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this. “Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid Al-Adhari is a sheikh from the people of the Levant, and it was not taken as evidence.” The two sheikhs, and they all agreed on the evidence of this hadith without this context.”"
"1528","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Muhammad told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Zuhayr told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, may God be pleased with her, who said: “By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave a dinar upon his death.” Not a dirham, nor a male or female slave, except his mule and his weapons, and some land that he left as charity. This is an authentic hadith. Al-Bukhari included it."
"1529","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Ruqi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: When Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, came, he supervised them from Above his house, then he said: “I remind you, by God, do you know that no one drank from Rumah except for a price, so I bought it with my own money? So you made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer? They said: Yes, this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1530","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, and Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Malik, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi told me, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Al-Qanabi told us, regarding what he read to Malik, On the authority of Sa’id bin Amr bin Shurahbil bin Sa’id bin Abbad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he said: Sa’d bin Ubadah went out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, in some of his battles. Umm Saad attended the death, and she was told: I will give a will. She said: What will I give a will? The money was Saad’s money, and she died before Saad came. When Saad came, that was mentioned to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, will it benefit her? Should I give alms on her behalf? He said: “Yes.” Saad said: The wall of such-and-such is a charity on her behalf. The wall called it “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” He did not narrate it, and he has an authentic witness to it. Al-Bukhari’s condition »"
"1531","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, Amr told me Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: His mother died. Will it benefit her if I give alms on her behalf? He said: “Yes.” He said: “I have a sheep, and I bear witness to you that I have given alms on her behalf.”
 The book of fasting"
"1532","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, and he told us Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Ahmed bin Najda told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, and Abu Kurayb told us: Abu Bakr bin told us Ayyash, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the first night of Ramadan The devils were chained up, the jinn were defeated, the gates of Hell were closed, and no door of it was opened, and the gates of Paradise were opened, but no door of it was closed. And a caller called out, “O seeker of good, come forward, and O seeker of evil, desist. And Allah will free you from the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. ""In this context"""
"1533","Ahmed bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, saying: It was read to Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad al-Raqqashi, and I was listening. Abd al-Samad bin told us Abdul-Warith, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Ya’qub, who said: I heard Abu Nasr al-Hilali speaking, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Haywa, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: I said, O Messenger of God, direct me to a job. He said: “You must fast, for there is no justice for it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They narrate it. “And Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub, who was Shu’bah, when he narrated on his authority, says: The master of Banu Tamim and Abu Nasr Al-Hilali narrated to me.” He is Humaid bin Hilal Al-Adawi, and I do not know of a narrator from Shu’bah other than Abd al-Samad, and he is trustworthy and trustworthy.”"
"1534","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us dictation, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Iban bin Yazid Al-Attar told us, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ God inspired Yahya bin Zakariya, peace be upon them, with five words that he must act upon them, and command the Children of Israel to act upon them. It was as if he had delayed them, so Jesus, peace be upon him, came to him and said: God has commanded you with five words to act upon them, and command the Children of Israel to They act on them, so either you tell them, or I tell them. He said: O brother, do not do it, for I fear that if you get ahead of me with them, I will be defeated. And he was tortured. He said: So he gathered the children of Israel in the Holy House until the mosque was full, and they sat on the balconies. Then he addressed them, and said: God has revealed to me With five words: I will act upon them, and command the Children of Israel to act upon them: The first of them is that you do not associate anything with God, for the example of whoever associates By God, like a man who bought a slave out of his pure wealth in the form of gold or paper, then he placed him in a house and said: Work, and come to me, and he made He works and submits to someone other than his master. Which of you would be willing to have his servant like that?For God created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with Him, and when you stand up for prayer, do not pay attention, for God turns from face to face. His servant did not turn around, and he commanded you to fast. The likeness of that is like a man in a group who has a bundle of musk, all of whom like to smell its scent. And the scent of fasting is like the scent of musk. And he commanded you to give charity. The likeness of that is like a man captured by the enemy. So they tied his hand to his neck and brought him near. To behead him, so he began to say: May I ransom myself from you? And he gave a little and a lot until he ransomed himself, and he commanded you. By remembering God often, and the example of God’s remembrance is like that of a man whom the enemy pursues quickly until he comes to a fortified fortress, and he entrenches himself in it. Likewise, the servant is not saved from Satan except by the remembrance of God.
 The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And I command you to do five things that God has commanded me to do: congregation, hearing, obedience, migration, and jihad.” For the sake of God, whoever separates from the group by even a span has taken off the collar of Islam from his neck, or from his head, unless he reconsiders, and whoever claims A pre-Islamic claim, then he is from the prostrate of Hell.” It was said: “O Messenger of God, even if he fasts and prays.” He said: “And if he fasts and prays, he will be called by the supplication of God, which He named you believers with it.“Muslims are servants of God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1535","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Rahman al-Dabbas told us in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid told us, al-Hakam bin Musa told us, al-Walid bin told us Muslim, Ishaq bin Abdullah told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The fasting person has a supplication when he breaks his fast. O God, I ask you for your mercy that You have endeavored to forgive me my sins.” This Ishaq, if Ibn Abdullah was the client of Zaida, then a Muslim departed from him. Ibn Abi Farwa, for they did not bring it out.”"
"1536","Abu Hamid Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Khatib told us about Marw, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin told us Waqid, Marwan bin Salim Al-Muqna’ narrated to us, saying: I saw Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, seizing his beard and cutting off what exceeded a palm. He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast, he would say: “The thirst has gone, the veins are wet, and the reward is certain, God willing.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They cited Al-Hussein bin Waqid and Marwan bin Al-Muqni’ as evidence."
"1537","Ismail bin Nujaid bin Ahmad bin Yusuf Al-Sulami told us, Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Nasr Al-Hafiz told us, Ismail bin Bishr bin told us Mansour Al-Sulami, Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami told us, Maan bin Muhammad Al-Ghafari told us, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The grateful feeder Like the patient fasting person: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1538","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, he said: It was read to Abdullah bin Wahb. Amr bin informed you Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, may God be pleased with him, he said: “We were In Ramadan, during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke his fast, and ransomed the food of a poor person until the verse was revealed: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it} [Al-Baqarah: 185] The verse: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"1539","Mukarram bin Ahmad al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Mala’ab bin Hayyan told us, Abu Asim told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Rawwad told us, Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has made the new moons appointed times, so when you see them, then fast. And when you see it, break your fast, but if it is cloudy for you, attend to it, and know that months do not exceed thirty.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. According to their condition, they did not take it out. And Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Rawwad was a devout, diligent, honorable person.”"
"1540","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, he told me Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qais, said: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He should take precautions regarding the crescent of Sha`ban that he does not observe other crescents, then he fasts until the sighting of Ramadan. If it is cloudy over him, he will count thirty days, then fast.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. Ibn Wahb and others narrated it on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1541","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Salem told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The people saw the crescent, So I informed the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that I saw him “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fasted, and he commanded the people to fast.” It is true on the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it"
"1542","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, we told him Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, he said: We were with Ammar ibn Yasir, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he ordered a praying sheep and said: “Eat.” Then some of the people moved away and said: “I am fasting.” Ammar said: “Whoever fasts on the Day of Doubt has disobeyed his father.” Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1543","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Ja’fi told us, Zaida, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I saw The crescent - meaning the crescent of Ramadan - and he said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?” He said: Yes, he said: “O Bilal, give the people permission to fast tomorrow.” Sufyan al-Thawri and Hammad bin Salamah followed him, on the authority of Samak bin Harb.
 As for the hadith of Al-Thawri"
"1544","So Abdul-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Muhammad bin Bakkar Al-Qaisi told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A Bedouin man came on the night of the crescent of Ramadan and said: Oh Messenger of God, I saw the crescent, so he said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but God, and do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?” He said: Yes, he said: “So he called on the people to fast.” And this is how it was narrated by Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri."
"1545","Al-Hasan bin Halim told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Samak, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A Bedouin came on the night of the crescent of Ramadan and said: O Messenger of God, I have seen The crescent moon, and he said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?” He said: Yes. He said: “So he called for them to fast.”
 As for the hadith of Hammad bin Salamah"
"1546","So Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Simak, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that they doubted the crescent of Ramadan, so they wanted not to get up or fast, so a Bedouin from Al-Harrah came. He testified that he saw the crescent, “so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Bilal to get up and fast.” Al-Bukhari cited the hadiths of Ikrimah as evidence. Muslim used the hadiths of Samak bin Harb and Hammad bin Salamah as evidence, and this hadith is authentic, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1547","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Ghassan Yahya bin Kathir Al-Anbari, narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, said: I entered upon Ikrimah on the day of Ramadan when he was in doubt while he was eating, and he said: Come closer. So eat. I said: I am fasting. He said: By God, you will come close. I said: He told me. He said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not face the month. Facing it, fast to see it, and break your fast to see it. If a cloud or rain comes between you and its sight, then complete the waiting period. Thirty days.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1548","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Count the crescent of Sha`ban for Ramadan.” Sahih according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1549","Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih told us, regarding other of our sheikhs. He said: Abu al-Nadr, the imam of the Muslims in his time, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq, told us. Ibn Khuzaymah, may God make him dwell in His Paradise. Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Mahrez Al-Baghdadi told us in Fustat with strange news. Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us. Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fajr has two dawns: as for the first It does not forbid food, nor does it make prayer permissible. As for the second, it makes food forbidden, but makes prayer permissible. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” And he witnessed it:"
"1550","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq did not tell us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sawadah, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Samurah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not be deceived by Bilal’s call to prayer, nor by this whiteness of the morning pillar until it shines.”"
"1551","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Zamaa bin Salih told us, on the authority of Salamah bin And Haram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Seek help with pre-dawn food.” “Fasting during the day, and taking a nap during the day after praying the night prayer.” Zam’ah bin Salih and Salamah bin Wahram are not among those who were abandoned and not taken as evidence. with them, but the two sheikhs did not deviate from them, and this is part of the deception of the hadith in this matter.”"
"1552","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abd Al-Ala bin Hammad Al-Narsi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you hears the call and the vessel is on his hand, do not “He puts it until he relieves himself from it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1553","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Adami Al-Muqri in Baghdad, and Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi informed me of Marw. They said: Abu Qalabah told us Al-Raqashi, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Ali bin Hamshadh told us, and the wording is his, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anazi, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, said: I heard my father, saying: Al-Hussein, who is the teacher, told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Abu Amr Al-Awza’i narrated to him that Ya’ish ibn Al-Walid narrated to him, that Ma’dan ibn Abi Talha narrated to him that Abu Al-Darda narrated to him, “that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, vomited and broke his fast.” So I found a garment in the Damascus Mosque, so I mentioned it to him, and he said: He is right, I poured water for him. “His ablution” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it due to a disagreement among the companions of Abd al-Samad regarding it. Some of them said: On the authority of Ya’ish ibn Al-Walid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maadan, and this is an illusion on the authority of who said it: “It was narrated by Harb ibn Shaddad and Hisham al-Dastawa’i, on the authority of Yahya ibn My father is very devoted to integrity
 As for the hadith of Harb bin Shaddad"
"1554","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Abdullah bin Raja’ told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr, on the authority of Ya’ish ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Ma’dan ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he vomited and broke his fast.”
 As for the hadith of Hisham"
"1555","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bundar told us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi told us, Hisham al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir said: A man from our brothers told me - Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq said: He meant Al-Awza’i - on the authority of Ya’ish bin Al-Walid Ibn Hisham, Ma’dan Ibn Abi Talha told me, on the authority of Abu Darda’, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a vomit and broke his fast.”"
"1556","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Daoud Al-Burlusi told us, Abu Sa’id Yahya bin Salman Al-Ja’fi told us, Hafs told us Ibn Ghayath, Hisham Ibn Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a fasting person vomits, he breaks his fast, and if he is overcome by vomiting, he does not break his fast.” Followed by Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Hisham"
"1557","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, and Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan and Jafar told us Bin Ahmad bin Nasr, they said: Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is overcome by vomiting does not have to make up for it, and whoever vomits should make up for it.” Sahih according to The conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"1558","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid Al-Bayruti told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Yahya bin Abi told me Many, Abu Qalaba told me, Abu Asma told me, Thawban, may God be pleased with him, told me, he said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He prayed the salaam for eighteen nights during the month of Ramadan. When he was in Al-Baqi’, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at a man using cupping, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The cupper broke his fast, and the one being cupped.” Al-Awza’i established this chain of transmission, made it good, and explained the hearing of each One of the narrators is from his companion. “Shayban bin Abdul Rahman Al-Nahawi and Hisham bin Abi Abdullah Al-Dastawa’i followed him on that.” And they are all trustworthy.” So the hadith is authentic according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it.”
 As for the hadith of Shayban"
"1559","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amrawiyah Al-Saffar told us in Baghdad from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashayb told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Abdullah bin Ahmed told us: Ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Shayban Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Qalaba told me, that Abu Asma al-Rahbi told him that Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking in al-Baqi’ In Ramadan, he saw a man having cupping, and he said: “The cupper broke his fast, and the one who had the cup was cupped.” Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: “This is the most correct of what has been narrated in this matter.” The door
 As for the hadith of Hisham Al-Dastawai:"
"1560","So Abu Amr Ismail bin Nujaid told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abu Omar Al-Hudhi told us, Hisham told us, and Abu Bakr bin told us Ishaq Al-Faqih, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, that Aba Asma Al-Rahbi told him that Thawban told him that he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking in Al-Baqi’ in Ramadan, he saw a man protesting. He said: “The cupper broke his fast, and the one being cupped broke his fast.” These are the chains of narrations in which what is clear is the hearing of the narrators who transmitted them, and the trustworthy and proven ones do not give reason. There is a dispute over which there is among those who dispute the opinion of Abu Qilabah and others, and according to Yahya bin Abi Kathir there is another authentic chain of narration in it according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.”"
"1561","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd Al-Razzaq told us, and Ahmad told us Ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad Ibn Ja’far told me Al-Muzaki, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qariz, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The cupper breaks his fast, and the one having the cupper breaks his fast,” and in the hadith of Ishaq al-Dabari and the cupper, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq said in his hadith I heard Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem saying: I heard Ali bin Al-Madini saying: I do not know about the cupper, and the hadith performed by the cupper is more sound than this one. Followed by Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir"
"1562","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ told us, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qariz, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar, so let him know. The seeker of this knowledge is that the two chains of narration for Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, one of them Ahmad ibn Hanbal was declared authentic, and Ali ibn The debtor to the other is valid, so one cannot give excuses for the other. Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Handali ruled the hadith of Shaddad bin Aws to be valid."
"1563","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, and Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Salamah, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami told us, Wahib told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a man in Al-Baqi’ while he was cupping while holding my hand for eighteen days without... Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper has broken his fast, and the one having the procedure has broken his fast.” So I heard Muhammad bin Salih saying: I heard Ahmad bin Salamah saying: I heard Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he says: This is an authentic chain of transmission that supports the argument, and this hadith has been authenticated with chains of transmission, and he says about it, may God be pleased with our Imam, my father Yaqoub, he ruled that it was authentic due to a hadith whose authenticity was apparent and in which he said, “Al-Thawri and Shu’bah agreed on his narration, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, On the authority of Abu Qilaba like this
 As for the hadith of Al-Thawri"
"1564","So Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani informed us of Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Qubaisah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, and he told me Abu Bakr bin Hatim Al-Maruzi, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by Maqil bin Yasar on the morning of the eighth The ten days of Ramadan while he was performing cupping, he said: “The cupper has broken his fast, and the one being cupped has broken his fast.”
 As for the hadith of Shu’bah"
"1565","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Amr bin told me Jafar Al-Adl, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh told us, Abi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man performing cupping on the seventeenth of Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the one being cupped have broken his fast.” Abu Muhammad Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Isfaraini told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, he said: Hadith Shaddad bin Aws, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he saw a man using cupping during Ramadan. It was narrated by Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, On the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, and it was narrated by Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Thawban, “And I do not see the two hadiths except Both are authentic, so it may be possible that he heard it from both of them. As for the concession for cupping for the fasting person, it was included by Muhammad ibn Ismail. Al-Bukhari in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih:"
"1566","As Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Barti told us, Abu Muammar told us, Abdul-Warith told us, On the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while fasting.” So listen. Now the words of the imam of the people of hadith in his time without any defense regarding this hadith so that you can use it as evidence of the most correct truth.
 I heard Abu Bakr bin Ja`far al-Muzaki saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah saying: The news about The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cupper breaks his fast, and the one who has the cupping breaks his fast.” Some of those who disagreed with us on this issue said: Cupping does not It breaks the fasting person’s fast, and he used as evidence that “the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had cupping while he was fasting and in a state of ihram.” This report does not indicate that cupping does not It breaks the fasting person’s fast, because the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only cupped while he was fasting, in ihram while traveling, not in his home, because he was never a resident ihram. In his country, he was in ihram while he was travelling, and even if the traveler intends to fast, and some of the day has passed, it is permissible for him to eat. And drinking, even if eating and drinking break the fast, not as some scholars have imagined, that if the traveler enters the fast, he does not have the right to He should break his fast until he completes the fast of that day on which he entered it. If he had the right to eat and drink, and he began the fast and intended it and went on. “It is permissible for him to have cupping while traveling during some of the day while he is fasting, even if cupping breaks his fast.”"
"1567","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Ali bin Issa told us, Ahmad bin Al-Nadr bin told us. Abd al-Wahhab, Abu al-Walid al-Faqih told us, al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, and Abu Ali al-Hafiz told me, Abu Ya`la reported, they said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us Zuhair bin Harb, Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Matar Al-Warraq, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, said: We entered upon Abu Musa while he was cupping after sunset, so I said: Did you not cup during the day? He said: You command me to shed my blood while I am fasting. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The cupper and the one having the procedure break his fast.”
 And I heard Abu Ali Al-Hafiz say: I said to Abadan Al-Ahwazi: Is it true, “That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was cupped while fasting?”
 He said: I heard Abbas Al-Anbari saying: I heard Ali bin Al-Madini saying: The hadith of Abu Rafi’ on the authority of Abu Musa is authentic, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “The cupper broke his fast, and the one being operated on broke his fast.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and no Muslim narrated it, and a group of the Companions mentioned this topic. With straight chains of transmission, which is a long explanation in this matter, I heard Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, saying: I heard Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi says: The hadith “The cupper broke his fast, and the one being cupped” is authentic to me, based on the hadith of Thawban and Shaddad ibn Aws, and I say it, and I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he says so, and he mentions that the hadith of Thawban and Shaddad is authentic according to him."
"1568","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid told us. Bin Jabir, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir Abi Yahya Al-Kala’i, who said: Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, told me: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: While I was sleeping, two men came to me, took my hyena, and brought me to a rugged mountain, and they said to me: Go up, and I said: “I I can't stand it."" So they said, ""We will make it easy for you."" So I went up and when I was at the top of the mountain, I heard loud noises. I said, ""What is this? The voices? They said: This is the howling of the people of Hell. Then he took me off, and behold, I was with a people hanging by their ankles with their buttocks torn open, and their buttocks flowing with blood. He said: I said: “Who are these?” He said: These are those who break their fast before their fast begins. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1569","Abu Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Tajer told me, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah told us Al-Ansari, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever breaks the fast in Ramadan out of forgetfulness, let him not He must make up for it and there is no expiation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context."
"1570","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Handali told us, Ubi told us, Anas bin Iyad told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting does not consist of eating and drinking, but rather fasting Of idle talk and obscenity. If someone insults you and speaks ignorantly to you, say: I am fasting. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1571","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Qutayba bin Saeed Al-Balkhi told us, Ismail bin Jafar told us, Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Maybe a fasting person will have his share of “His fasting is due to hunger, and perhaps his share of staying up late will last.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1572","Abu Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim told us, and Ibrahim bin Nasr al-Razyan told us, they said: Abu al-Walid told us Al-Tayalisi, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Saeed bin Suwayd Al-Ansari, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, that he said: I was distracted one day, so I kissed while I was fasting, and I came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So I said: Today I did a great thing, so I came while I was fasting. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What do you think, if you rinse your mouth? Water while you are fasting?” He said: So I said: There is no problem with that, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1573","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Religion will continue to prevail as long as people hasten to break the fast, because The Jews and Christians delayed “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1574","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them, and whoever does not, let him break his fast.” “On water, for it is pure.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1575","Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Qais bin Hafs Al-Darimi told me, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, about Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of her uncle Salman bin Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If If one of you is fasting, let him break his fast with dates. If he does not find dates, then with water, for water is pure. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. And he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness according to Muslim’s condition.”"
"1576","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, Thabit Al-Bunani told me that he heard Anas bin Malik say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to break his fast with fresh dates before... He should pray, if there are no fresh dates, then with dates, and if there are no dates, he should drink a handful of water.”"
"1577","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Zakaria bin Yahya bin Aban told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Wasiti, Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, Saeed bin Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He did not pray the Maghrib prayer until he broke his fast, even if he had a drink of water.”"
"1578","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us something from the origin of his book, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl, and Ishaq ibn al-Hayaj told us, saying: Muhammad bin Naim Al-Saadi, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “By al-`Araj, water poured over his head during the heat while he is fasting.” This is a hadith that has an origin in al-Muwatta’, so if it was Muhammad ibn Nu’aym al-Sa’di. If he memorizes it like this, it is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"1579","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, Al-Qanabi told us, regarding what was read to Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, A servant of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace During his journey, he commanded the people to break the fast in the year of the conquest, and said: “Be strong for your enemy.”
 The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted. Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman said: The one who told me said, “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With lameness, water is poured over his head while he is fasting from thirst.” Or he said: from the heat."
"1580","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Al-Zuhri, he said: Safwan told me Ibn Abdullah Ibn Safwan, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, on the authority of Ka’b Ibn Asim Al-Ash’ari, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not righteousness to fast “In travel.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “The two sheikhs agreed on the hadith of Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami, so they narrated it from The hadith of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that “Hamza” has an interpreted narration from the hadith of the sons of Hamza bin Amr, and he did not He brings him out.”"
"1581","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Shuaib Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Harrani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Majeed Al-Madini said: I heard Hamza bin Muhammad bin Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami mentioning that his father told him, On the authority of his grandfather, Hamzah bin Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I am the owner of a backhaul, I treat him, I travel with him and I force him, and he may have come across me. This month - meaning the month of Ramadan - I am finding strength as a young man, and I find it easier for me to fast, O Messenger of God, than to fast. I delay it and it becomes a debt. Should I fast, O Messenger of God, to maximize my reward, or should I break my fast? He said: “Whatever you want, O Hamza.”"
"1582","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of my father Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, traveled during Ramadan, and fasting became difficult for one of his companions, so I made His camel was leading him under the tree, so he informed the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about his matter. He ordered him to break his fast, then he called for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. With a vessel, he placed it on his hand and then drank, while the people watched, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1583","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Omar bin Saad told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at a passing Dhahran brought food, and he said to Abu Bakr and Omar: “Come closer and eat.” They said: We are fasting, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Work for your friend, go for your friend, come and eat.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1584","Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My nation will continue to According to my Sunnah, as long as her nature does not wait for the stars,” “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was fasting, he would give orders to a man and he fulfilled them on the basis of disobedience. He said: The sun had set, so he broke his fast. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 They only came up with this chain of narration by Al-Thawri: “The people will continue to be well as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast” only."
"1585","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me that Abdullah Ibn Abi Qais told him that he heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, say: “The most beloved month for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to fast in it.” Sha`ban, then he connects it with Ramadan.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1586","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Fakihi informed us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the day Arafat, the Day of Sacrifice, and the days of Tashreeq are our festival, the people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1587","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Hawshab bin Aqeel, Mahdi bin Hassan Al-Abdi told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Peace and blessings of God be upon him, about fasting the day of Arafat with “Arafat.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1588","Yusuf ibn Yaqoub al-Adl told me, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr informed me, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal told me, Abd al-A`la ibn Abd informed us. The highest, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hunaif, on the authority of Masoud bin Al-Hakam Al-Zarqi, on the authority of his mother, that She told him, saying: It is as if I am looking at Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, on the white mule of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in The people of the Ansar and they say: O people, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These are not days of fasting, they are days of eating.” “And he drank and mentioned.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness."
"1589","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Malik told me, and Abu Bakr bin Sulaiman told me. Abu Nasr Al-Marwazi, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi narrated to us, Al-Qanabi narrated to us, in what was read to Malik, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Abu Murrah The servant of Umm Hani’ said that he went to Abdullah bin Amr to see his father, Amr bin Al-Aas, and he brought food to them and said: Eat. Then he said: I will He was fasting, so Amr said: “Eat. These are the days when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order us to break the fast and forbid us from eating them.” Her fasting.” Malik said: “And these are the days of sunrise.”"
"1590","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Saeed bin Masoud told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Qutayi told us, Abdullah bin Masoud told us Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Whoever fasts for a lifetime will neither fast nor break the fast,” or “He will neither fast nor break the fast.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and its witnesses, according to their conditions, are authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1591","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail, who is Ibn Ulayya, told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: It was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “So-and-so does not break his fast during the day.” He said: “He neither fasts nor breaks his fast.”"
"1592","Abu Humaid Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Hamid Al-Adl told us about Al-Tabaran, Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Anbari told us, Safwan bin Saleh told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr Al-Sulami, on the authority of his deaf sister, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Do not fast on the Sabbath except what is required of you, and if any of you finds nothing except the bark of a grape or the stick of a tree.” Let him chew it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it, and it has contradictions with a correct chain of transmission: It was narrated by Hammam’s hadith, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Atki, on the authority of Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her on Friday while she was fasting. He said: “Yesterday’s silence?” She said: No. He said: “So you want to fast tomorrow?” Hadith. So Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, Abd al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, Ibn Wahb told us, He said: I heard Al-Layth narrating, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that when it was mentioned to him that he forbade fasting on the Sabbath, he said: This is a hadith. Homsi “and it has contradictions with an authentic chain of transmission”:"
"1593","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Abdullah bin informed. Muhammad bin Amr bin Ali, on the authority of his father, that Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, informed him that Ibn Abbas and some people were among the companions of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. They sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her about which days the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted the most? She said: On Saturday and Sunday, so I went back to them and told them, and it was as if they had denied that, so they all stood up to her and said: We We sent this man to you on such-and-such occasion, and he mentioned that you had said such-and-such. She said: He is right. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, often said: He used to fast on Saturdays and Sundays, and he used to say: “They are a holiday for the polytheists, and I want to differ from them.”"
"1594","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of my father Saeed, he said: A woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were with him, and she said: O Messenger of God, my husband is Safwan ibn al-Mu’tal. He beats me when I pray, breaks my fast when I fast, and does not perform the Fajr prayer until the sun rises. He said: Safwan is with him. He said: So he asked him about She said, so he said: O Messenger of God, as for her saying: He hits me when I pray, she recites two surahs that I forbade her from, and I said, “If it were a surah One time would be enough for the people, but as for her saying: It breaks my fast if I fast, she goes off and fasts, and I am a young man and I cannot be patient, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on that day: “No woman shall fast except with her husband’s permission,” and as for her saying: “I will not pray until the sun rises.” For we are the people of a household. This has been known to us. We hardly wake up until the sun rises. He said: “Then when you wake up, pray.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1595","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, and he told us Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, told us, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Aamir ibn Ludin al-Ash’ari, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Friday is an Eid, so do not make the day of your Eid a day of your fasting unless you fast before or after it.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, except for this Abu Bishr whose name I did not find, and it is not with the statement of Ibn Bishr nor with Ja’far bin Abi Brutality, and God knows best, and evidence of this in something other than this word is mentioned in the two books.”"
"1596","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us, they said: Abu Hudhayfah, Ikrimah bin Ammar told me, and Abu Yahya Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Samarqandi told me, Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Simak al-Hanafi, Malik bin Marthad told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Abu Dharr So I said: Did you ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the Night of Decree? He said: I used to ask people about it. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about Laylat al-Qadr, is it in Ramadan, or at any other time? He said: “Rather, it is during Ramadan.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, will it be with the prophets as long as they were, and when the prophets are taken away, it will be lifted up, or will it remain until the Day of Resurrection? He said: “Rather, it will last until the Day of Resurrection.” He said: So I said, O Messenger of God, which Ramadan is it? He said: “Seek it in the first ten and the last ten days.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke and spoke, but I was astonished by his negligence. So I said: O Messenger of God, which of the twenty? He said: “Seek it during the last ten nights, and do not ask me about anything after that.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke and spoke, so I was startled. I neglected him, so I said: O Messenger of God, I swore to you that you would tell me, or why did you tell me which of the ten days it was? He said: He became angry with me in a way that He had never been angry with like before or after him. He said: “If God had willed, He would have made it known to you. Seek it in “The Last Seven Nights” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1597","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Abi Uthman Al-Zahid told me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Barawayh Al-Muazzin told me, Yahya bin Yahya told us, he reported Abdullah bin Idris, Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, used to invite me With the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to me: Do not speak until they speak. He said: So he called them and asked them about the Night of Decree. He said: Have you seen? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Seek it in the last ten nights. What night do you see it?” He said: Some of them said: The night of one Sunday, and some of them said: The night of the third, and another said: Five, and I was silent, so he said: Why do you not speak? So I said: If you permit me, O Commander of the Faithful, I will speak. He said: So he said: I did not send to you except for you to speak. He said: So I said: I will speak to you about my opinion? He said: We ask you about that. He said: So I said: The seven. I saw God mentioning seven heavens, and of the earths seven, and creating man from seven. And the growth of the earth emerged from seven, he said: So he said: This you told me what I know. Have you seen what I do not know, what you said about the growth of the earth from seven? He said: So I said: Indeed, God says: {We have divided the earth into fissures} [Abs: 26] to His saying: {And fruit and father} [Abs: 31] And the father made the earth grow from what Animals eat it and people do not eat it. He said: Then Omar said: Are you unable to say as this boy said, whose affairs were not in order? After: By God, I do not see the statement other than as you said. He said: And he said: I have ordered you not to speak until they have spoken, and I command you to speak. With them, Ibn Idris said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same thing. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1598","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of his father, he said: I mentioned Laylat al-Qadr with Abu Bakra, and he said: “I do not seek it except on the last ten nights, on the ninth or “Seven days remain, or five days remain, or three days remain, or on the last night,” so he would not pray on the twentieth except what he prayed during the rest of the year. So when the ten days came, he tried hard, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1599","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Yunus Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, On the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “The fasting person The voluntary person is in charge of himself. If he wishes, he may fast, and if he wishes, he may break his fast.”"
"1600","Sheikh Imam Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, Ja’far bin Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Bundar told us, Yahya bin Abi told us Al-Hajjaj Al-Khaqani, Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, Samak bin Harb told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “The one who makes a voluntary choice may fast if he wishes, and if he wishes he may break his fast.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and these are the narrations. “In opposition to this, none of it is authentic.”"
"1601","Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, Abi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, Humaid Al-Taweel told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seclude himself during the last ten days of Ramadan, and he did not seclude for a year. The following year he performed seclusion for twenty days. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and it has an authentic witness."
"1602","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, and Musa bin Ismail told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to seclude himself during the last days of Ramadan, so he traveled A year, but he did not seclude himself, and he secluded himself for twenty nights of the following year.”"
"1603","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Mahboub Al-Ramli told us in Mecca, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Ramli told us, Muhammad bin Abi Omar Al-Adni told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Sahl bin Malik, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not upon “The one who is in seclusion is fasting unless he imposes it upon himself.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and the jurists of the people of Kufa are against this. I will mention two hadiths, even if they do not support this report in the justice of the narrators. The first hadith:"
"1604","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Ali Al-Hanafi told us, Abdullah bin Badil told us, on the authority of Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that Omar, “during pre-Islamic times he vowed to seclude himself one day, so he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Seclude yourself and fast a day.” The second hadith:"
"1605","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmed bin Umair Al-Dimashqi told us, Muhammad bin Hashim told us, Suwayd bin Abdul Aziz told us, Sufyan told us Bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no seclusion except “By fasting.” The two sheikhs did not use Sufyan bin Hussein and Abdullah bin Yazid as evidence."
"1606","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Urwah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {And those who are able to do it must pay a ransom by feeding a poor person} [Al-Baqarah: 184] one {so whoever Voluntarily do good.} [Al-Baqarah: 184] If it provides food for another poor person, it is better for him. It is not abrogated, except that it was written for the old man who did not He is able to fast, and he commanded him to feed the one whom he knew was not able to fast. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1607","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail al-Faqih told us about irrigation, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Raqqashi told us, Wahib, Khaled Al-Hadha narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The old sheikh was permitted to break the fast and feed on the daily basis.” “He is poor and there is no compensation for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it and there is evidence in it."
"1608","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Balkhi told us in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, Abu Talha bin Ziyad Al-Ansari narrated to me, saying: I heard Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the pulpit of Homs, saying: “We rose with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. During the month of Ramadan he greeted the night of the twenty-third to a third of the night, then we rose with him on the night of the twenty-fifth to midnight, then we rose We stayed with him on the night of the twenty-seventh until midnight, then we stayed with him on the night of the twenty-seventh until we thought we would not catch up with Al-Falah, and we were We call it Al-Falah, and you call it Suhoor.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it. “And it contains clear evidence that: “Tarawih prayer in The mosques of Muslims are a Sunnah, and Ali bin Abi Talib used to urge Omar, may God be pleased with them both, to establish this Sunnah until He established it” is the last of the authentic hadiths that my knowledge has come to in the chapters of the Book of Fasting that were not included by the two sheikhs."
"1609","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, Hajj Every year or once? He said: “One time, so whoever wants may do it voluntarily.” This is an authentic chain of narration, and this Abu Sinan is Al-Du’ali, and they did not narrate it, as they did not narrate it. They were narrated by Sufyan bin Hussein, and he is one of the trustworthy people whose hadiths are collected.”"
"1610","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Sufyan bin Habib told us, Humaid Al-Taweel, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Enjoy this house, for it has been demolished twice, and the third time will be removed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """
"1611","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Munqidh bin Abdullah Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he told me Makhramah bin Bukayr, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Suhail bin Abi Saleh, saying: I heard my father, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The delegation of God is three: the invader, the Hajj, and the Umrah pilgrim.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1612","Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Jaafar bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Marudhi told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, forgive the pilgrim, and whoever asks forgiveness for him.” Al-Hajj: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1613","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abi Hazim, al-Hafiz in Kufa, and Abu Sa`id Ismail bin Ahmad al-Tajir told us, saying: Ali bin al-Abbas told us. Ibn Al-Walid Al-Bajli, Ali Ibn Sa’id Ibn Masruq Al-Kindi told us, Ibn Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in his saying, Blessed and Most High: A path} [Al Imran: 97] He said: It was said: O Messenger of God, what is the path? He said: “The provisions and the camel.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Hammad bin Salamah Sa’id continued on his narration, on the authority of Qatadah"
"1614","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl bin Hamdawayh Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Umayyah Amr told us Ibn Hisham Al-Harrani, Abu Qatada told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He was asked about God’s saying: “Whoever is able to find a way to Him” [Al Imran: 97] and it was said: What is the way? He said: “The provisions and the camel.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it."
"1615","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu Hisham al-Makhzoumi told us, Wahib told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not travel “A woman is a night’s journey, except with a mahram.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1616","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman should not travel by mail unless And with her was a mahram.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1617","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad al-Khazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Hanzalah bin Abi told us Sufyan, that he heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad say: I was with Ibn Omar, and a man came to him and said: I wanted to travel, so Abdullah said: “Wait until I bid you farewell as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bid farewell to us: I bid you farewell to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your work. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”"
"1618","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Ismail bin Hafs bin Amr bin Maymun told us, Yahya bin Maymun told us. Al-Yaman, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Hamran bin Ayan, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Hajj And his companions walked from Medina to Mecca. He said: “Bind your waistbands with your loincloths.” He walked at a trotting pace. “This is an authentic hadith.” chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1619","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marwa, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ja’far bin told me Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, said: Some people complained to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about walking, so he called for them and said: “You must take offspring,” so we offspring. We found it easier for us: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1620","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shurayh informed us, Shurahbil bin Sharik told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: “The best of companions in the sight of God is the one who is best to his companion, and the best neighbors in the eyes of God are the best to his neighbor.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1621","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us in Egypt, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubayy told us, he said: I heard Yunus bin Yazid narrates, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best companions Four, and the best of the armies was four thousand, and twelve thousand were not defeated by a few. This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. There is disagreement about it according to Al-Zuhri from four aspects, which I have explained in the book Al-Talkhees."
"1622","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Abdul Hamid bin Ja`far, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a mission and they He left and said: “What do you have of the Qur’an?” So he studied with them in this manner until he passed by a man among them who was one of the youngest among them in age, and he said: “What is the matter with you, so-and-so?” He said: “I have such-and-such, and Surat Al-Baqarah.” He said: “Go, for you are their leader.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1623","Abu Muhammad Al-Qasim bin Malik Al-Muzani narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: “If There was a group of three, so let them appoint one of them. He is a prince who was commanded by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1624","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Hakam Ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abu Lasas Al-Khuza’i, may God be pleased with him, he said: We carried the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of the weak charity camels for Hajj, so we said, O Messenger of God: We do not think that these will carry us. He said: “There is no camel without a devil on its top, so mention the name of God when you ride it as He commanded you, then treat it for yourselves, for it is only May God bear “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness.”"
"1625","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Hafiz narrated to us in Hamadan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein narrated to us, Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Muadh bin Anas, on the authority of his father, and he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Ride these animals in safety, and create them in safety, and do not use them as chairs.”"
"1626","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khalid told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, Muhammad bin Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami told me, he said: I heard my father saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Over the back of every camel Satan, and when you ride them, remember the name of God, and do not neglect any need.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a witness. ""On his condition"""
"1627","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, upon every top of a camel there is a devil. So make them skilled at riding, for it is the burden of God Almighty.”"
"1628","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, and Al-Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, He said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade “About drinking from a waterskin, and about Al-Jalala and Al-Mujathama.” This is an authentic hadith. Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim cited Hammad as evidence. Ibn Salamah"
"1629","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, I am Abdullah bin Wahb, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, Al-Alaa told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The bell is the flute of Satan.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1630","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ruwaym bin Yazid told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, and Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Aslam Al-Abed told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must use the ice, for the earth is rolling. “At night for the traveler.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it."
"1631","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Balawayh informed me, Muhammad ibn Rumh al-Sammak informed me, Yazid ibn Harun informed me, Hammad ibn Salamah informed me, on the authority of Humaid, On the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was If he weds during the night, he lies on his right, and if he weds before dawn, he erects his arms erect, and places his head on his palm. “This is an authentic hadith.” On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1632","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Yahya Zakaria bin Dawud told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim, and Yusuf bin Musa told us, they said: Jarir told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with On the authority of them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go out less frequently when you have calmed down the man. Indeed, God disperses from His creation what He wills at night.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1633","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id. Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanting to travel, and he said: O Messenger of God, Recommend me. He said: “I advise you to fear God, and to glorify God with all honour.” Then when he went on, he said: “O God, make the land easy for him, and make the journey easy for him.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1634","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Hafs bin Maysarah told me, about Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b narrated to him, that Suhaib, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, never saw a town that he wanted to enter except that he said when he saw it: “O God, Lord of the seven heavens and what they overshadow, and Lord of the seven earths. And they have not diminished, and by the Lord of the devils, and they have not led astray, and by the Lord of the winds, and what they have left, indeed we ask you for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in Protect you from its evil, the evil of its people, and the evil of what is in it. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it."
"1635","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Khayyat told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Abu Asim told us, Uthman bin Saad, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would not go down to a place without saying goodbye to it with two rak’ahs.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1636","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, dawn would appear to him. He said: “Anyone who hears praises God and His grace, and His good affliction upon us. Our Lord, our Companion, bestow upon us, we seek refuge in God from the Fire.” He says that. Three times, raising his voice, he said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1637","Ibrahim bin Firas, the jurist in Mecca, informed us, Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told us, Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan bin Amr told us, on the authority of Shurayh bin Ubaid Al-Hadrami, that he heard Al-Zubayr bin Al-Walid, speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of If God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, invades, or travels and night overtakes him, he says: “O land of my Lord and your Lord is God, I seek refuge in God from the evil of every lion. “And the evil of every lion, snake, and scorpion, and of the inhabitants of the land, and of the evil of a father and his offspring.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1638","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ahmad bin Abi Talib told us, he said: It was read to Abu Bakr bin Ayyash. As I look at this book, I acknowledge it, on the authority of Ya’qub ibn Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “He took a bath.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he put on his clothes, and when he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, he prayed two rak’ahs, then he sat on his camel, and when he had reached the Al-Baida entered into ihram for Hajj.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. Ya’qub bin Ata’ bin Abi Rabah is one whose hadith was collected by the imams of Islam. And they did not produce it, and he has a valid witness to their condition.”"
"1639","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Sahl bin Yusuf narrated to us, Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “It is part of the Sunnah for him to wash himself if he wants to enter ihram, and if he wants to enter Mecca” Authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs”"
"1640","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Hisham bin Urwah, and Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, said: Nasiyah Al-Khuza’i, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he taught me what to do with what was damaged on my body. “So he commanded me to slaughter every body that was damaged, then to dip her sandal in its blood, and then leave it alone.” People eat it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1641","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, my father told us, Al-Awza’i told me, Abd told me Allah Ibn Amir, Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever gives a voluntary gift, then It went astray, and if He wanted, He could change it, and if He wanted, He could leave it, and if it was due to a vow, then He could change it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1642","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl and Ali ibn Muhammad al-Mustamli told us about others who said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad ibn al-Ala told us. Ibn Kurayb, Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “He should not enter ihram for Hajj except during the months of Hajj. “It is part of the Sunnah of Hajj to enter ihram for Hajj during the months of Hajj.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and a debate took place about it. Between me and our sheikh, Abu Muhammad al-Subai’i, he denied it and said, “The people only narrated it” on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of al-Hajjaj ibn Arta’at, on the authority of Al-Hikam: Where did your sheikh bring it from, on the authority of Shu’bah? So I said: Consider what you say, for our sheikh brought all of the chains of transmission, as if I had given him ""a stone"""
"1643","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying at any hour he likes.” “Night or day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1644","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Omar bin Ata’, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no victory in Islam.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1645","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abu Muawiyah Muhammad bin Khazim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, On the authority of Abu Safwan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wants to perform Hajj, let him hasten.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it, and this Abu Safwan was named by others as Mihran, a client of Quraysh, and he is not known by al-Jarh.”"
"1646","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Husayn bin Omar told us. Al-Ahmasi, then Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, saying: “Perform Hajj before “Do not perform Hajj.” It is as if I were looking at a deaf Ethiopian, pushing with his hand a pickaxe demolishing it, stone by stone. So I said to him something to say, “What do you think?” Or I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “No, by the one who split the grain and healed the soul, but I heard it from your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And he greeted"
"1647","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab told us, Abu Umamah told us Al-Taymi, he said: I was a man who was forced to go to this place, and people were telling me: You do not have the right to perform Hajj. So I met Ibn Umar and said, O Abu Abd. The Most Gracious, I am a man who is disgraced in this regard, and some people say to me: You do not have the right to perform Hajj. So He said: Do you not enter ihram, perform the Talbiyah, circumambulate, and perform the funeral prayers? Arafat, and throwing stones? He said: Yes. He said: For you are performing Hajj. A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about something similar to what you asked me about, but the Messenger of God remained silent about him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, but he did not answer him until this verse was revealed: {There is no blame on you if you seek bounty from your Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 198] So he sent for him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse to him and said: “You may perform Hajj.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1648","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “At the beginning of the Hajj, people used to trade at Mina, Arafat, and the market of Dhul Majaz.” And the seasons of Hajj, so they feared sales while they were in a state of sanctity, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: {There is no blame upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 198] During the seasons of Hajj, he said: Ubaid bin Umair told me that he used to recite it from the Qur’an. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1649","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami told us, Wahib told us, Musa bin Abi Uqba told us, Nafi’ and Salem told me that Ibn Umar would “when he passed by Dhu al-Hulayfah, spend the night there until morning, and inform me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to do that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this."
"1650","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, dictating, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, he told me Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, that Abdullah bin Al-Fadl narrated to him, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “It was part of the talbiyah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: ‘Labbayk, the God of Truth.’ This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “coated his head with honey.”"
"1651","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Abd told us The highest, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say the Talbiyah.”"
"1652","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Hamid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abdul Al-Malik bin Abi Bakr bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Khallad bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “He came to me Gabriel, and he said: Order your companions to raise their voices with the greeting of God and the Talbiyah. It has been said: On the authority of Khallad ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khaled Al-Juhani"
"1653","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Ismail bin Qutayba told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Khallad bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Gabriel came to me and said: O Muhammad, order your companions to raise their shouts.” “With the Talbiyah, it is the emblem of Hajj.” It was said: On the authority of Al-Muttalib Ibn Abdullah Ibn Hantab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him."
"1654","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Osama told me Bin Zaid, that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Uthman and Abdullah bin Abi Labid told him about Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Gabriel ordered me to raise the voice for the cries, for he Of the rituals of Hajj.” These chains of narrations are all authentic, and none of them explains the other, as the predecessors, may God be pleased with them, used to gather with them The chains of narration are for one text as they are gathered together now, and the two sheikhs did not narrate this hadith.”"
"1655","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik told me, Al-Dahhak bin Uthman reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yarubu’, on the authority of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which work is best? He said: “Al-Ajj, and Al-Thajj” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and no Muslim narrated it. Abu Ubaid said: “Al-Ajj: raising one’s voice when reciting the talbiyah, and Al-Thajj: “Slaughter the body so that the blood gushes from the slaughter.”"
"1656","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Al-Hussein bin Idris Al-Ansari told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ubaida bin Hamid, Amara bin Ghaziyah told me, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no believer who performs the Talbiyah except that he fulfills what is to his right and to his left, of trees and stones, until the earth is cut off from here to here and to here from here. On his right and on his left.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1657","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, we told him My father, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Khasif ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jazari narrated to me, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Abbas, O son of Al-Abbas: I was amazed at the disagreement among the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding the Ihram of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he made it obligatory, so he said: I I know the people about that. It was only one proof from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but from there they differed.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left. Peace be upon him as a pilgrim, and when he prayed two rak’ahs in his mosque in Dhul-Hulayfah, he made it obligatory for him to sit in his place, so he qualified for Hajj when he finished his two rak’ahs. Some people heard that from him and kept it from him. Then he rode off, and when his camel rode with him, his family met that, and some people realized that from him, and that is because People were coming as messengers, and they heard him pronouncing the ihram when his camel was riding with him, so they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the ihram when she was riding with him. His she-camel, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went on, and when he ascended to the honor of Al-Bayda, he was a family. When he ascended in the honor of Al-Bayda, and I swear by God, he made the obligatory prayer in his place of prayer, and he performed the ritual prayer when his she-camel rode by, and he made the ritual prayer when he ascended in the honor of Al-Baida.” He said Saeed bin Jubayr: “So whoever follows the saying of Ibn Abbas, he will perform the prayer in his place of prayer when he has finished his two rak’ahs.” This is an authentic hadith based on a Muslim condition explained in the door, and they did not take it out.”"
"1658","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in Jumada al-Akhira in the year three hundred and ninety-six. He reported Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Abdullah bin Al-Sammak in Baghdad, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubayy told us, He said: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq speaking, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad bin Abi Waqqas, who said, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, said God said on his authority: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the Far-Fur’ road, he would greet the people of it when his camel rode it.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1659","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan Al-Muhajiri told us, Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Ya'qub bin Abdul Rahman al-Zuhri and Yahya bin Abdullah bin Salim told me that Omar, al-Muttalib's client, told them about Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say: “The meat of game “Wildness is permissible for you, but you are forbidden unless you hunt it or it is caught for you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1660","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Muhammad told us, Ishaq bin Isa bin Al-Tabbaa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: O Zaid bin Arqam, “Did you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was given eggs as a gift? Ostrich, and it is forbidden, so he returned them? He said: Yes, this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1661","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Ibn Jurayj, Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Ammar, he said: I met Jabir bin Abdul By God, I asked him about the hyena, should we eat it? He said: “Yes.”"
"1662","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Jarir Bin Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I said: Can the hyena be eaten? He said: “Yes.” I said: What game is it? He said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Yes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it. Jarir bin Hazim summarized it, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made The hyena was struck by a muhrim like a Najd ram, and he made it part of the game.”"
"1663","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah told us about Marwa, Yahya bin Sasawayh told us, Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub told us, Hassan bin Ibrahim, Ibrahim al-Sayegh told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The hyena is a hunt, and if a person in ihram attacks it, its reward is an old ram and it will be eaten.” This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it, and Ibrahim ibn Maymun Al-Sayegh is an ascetic and a scholar who attained the martyrdom, may God be pleased with him.”"
"1664","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, Amr bin A dinar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped his head while he was in ihram.” This A hadith narrated with its chain of transmission in the two Sahih books without mentioning the head, and it is authentic according to their conditions.”"
"1665","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Abd Al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “did cupping while in ihram on the backs of his feet, due to pain he was experiencing.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not take it out with this increase.”"
"1666","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm Al-Hafiz told us, Ubi told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered a person in ihram to kill a snake in the Sacred Mosque in Mina.” This is an authentic hadith according to The two sheikhs stipulated, and they did not narrate it like this.”"
"1667","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Abdullah told us Bin Idris, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma bint Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as pilgrims, and the fellowship of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was The company of Abu Bakr was the same, so we went down to Al-Arj and our company was with the servant of Abu Bakr. She said, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down. Aisha sat next to him, and Abu Bakr sat next to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the other side, and I sat next to my father. We are waiting for his boy and his companions until he comes to us. Then the boy started walking, not carrying his camel. He said: Then Abu Bakr said to him: Where is your camel? He said: He led me astray tonight, she said, so Abu Bakr got up and beat him and said: One camel led you astray, and you are a man, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, could do no more. Peace and blessings be upon him, provided that he smiles and says: “Look at this forbidden person, what he is doing.” This is a strange hadith that is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. """
"1668","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, On the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them, she said: “We used to cover our faces from the men, and we used to comb our hair.” “Before that, in Ihram.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1669","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Abu Sa`id al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Samad told me, Yahya ibn Yahya told me, Muhammad ibn Ismail informed me Ibn Abi Fudaik, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Saad, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saying: “Why The two sands now, and the unveiling of the places, and God has trampled Islam and exiled disbelief and its people? However, we will not abandon anything that we used to do with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1670","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us dictation, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Muhammad ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, received the stone and received it, then He put his lips on it and wept for a long time.” Then he turned and saw Omar crying, and said: “O Omar, here are the lessons being poured out.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1671","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Mu’ammil bin Al-Hasan bin Isa told me: Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who is Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: We entered Mecca at the high of noon “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the door of the mosque, leaned his mount, then entered the mosque and began to stone.” So he received it, and his eyes filled with tears, then he sanded three times, and walked four times until he finished. When he finished, he kissed the stone, put his hands on it, and wiped them with them. His face: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1672","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Ja’far bin Abdullah told us, and he is Ibn al-Hakam said: I saw Muhammad bin Abbad bin Jafar kiss the stone and prostrated on it, then he said: I saw your uncle Ibn Abbas kissing it and prostrating. On him, and Ibn Abbas said: I saw Omar ibn al-Khattab kiss him and prostrated on him, then he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do this.” So I did. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1673","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzar informed us, Uthman bin Omar informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and he informed us Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jurayj told me, Yahya bin told me Ubaid, Al-Sa'ib's client, said that his father told him that Abdullah bin Al-Sa'ib told him that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, between Rukn Bani Jam, and the black corner says: “Our Lord, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"1674","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Sa’id bin Zaid told us, Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, Sa’id bin Musa told us. Jubayr said: Ibn Abbas used to say: Memorize this hadith, and he used to refer it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he used to pray with it among The two pillars: “My Lord, make me content with what You have provided for me, and bless me in it, and grant good to me for everything that is absent from me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They take it out, because they did not use Sa`id bin Zaid, the brother of Hammad bin Zaid, as evidence.”"
"1675","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Abu Sa’id, the client of Banu Hashim, told us. Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, Israel told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him On their authority, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissed the Yemeni Corner and placed his cheek on it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1676","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria told us, Bishr bin Khalid told us Al-Askari told us Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulaiman, who said: I heard Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Rawwad, narrating on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “Whenever the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated the Kaaba, he would wipe - or he said: touch - the stone and the corner during each circumambulation.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1677","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Ayyub bin Suwayd told us, Yunus bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Musafa’. Al-Hajabi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Rukn and the Maqam are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. “Allah is their light, and had it not been for that, they would have illuminated what is between the east and the west.” This is a hadith that was unique to: Ayoub bin Suwayd, on the authority of Yunus, and Ayoub. Of those who did not protest except for the sake of the sheikhs of the Levant, and there is evidence for this hadith.”"
"1678","It was narrated to us by Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Mihran Al-Thaqafi, dictating from the original of his book. Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi told us Shaybah, Ahmad bin Hisham bin Mihran Al-Madaini told us, Dawud bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Rukn and the Maqam are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise.”"
"1679","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hassan bin Maimun told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Abu Yahya told us Raja bin Yahya, Musafa bin Shaybah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both: I seek refuge in God three times, and he put With his two fingers in his ears, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The corner and the place are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. Their light has been obliterated by God. Had it not been for that, they would have illuminated what is between the east and the west.” This is evidence of the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Musafa’."
"1680","Abd Al-Samad bin Ali Al-Bazzaz told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Thabit bin Yazid told us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, this stone has a tongue and two lips, which will bear witness to the truth of whoever touches it on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. And he has a valid witness"
"1681","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, and Abu Hafs Omar bin Ahmad Al-Faqih narrated to us. In Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, saying: Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mu’mal told us, saying: I heard Ata’, He narrates, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The pillar will come on the Day of Resurrection greater From Abu Qubays: He has a tongue and two lips, and he speaks about the one who received him with intention, and he is the oath of God with which he shakes hands with his creation. This has been narrated. The hadith is an explanatory witness, but it is not a requirement of the two sheikhs, as they did not use Abu Harun Amara bin Juwayn al-Abdi as evidence.”"
"1682","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Salih Al-Kaylini told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us Ibn Abi Amr Al-Adni, Abd Al-Aziz Ibn Abd Al-Samad Al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Abu Harun Al-Abdi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: We performed Hajj with Omar bin Al-Khattab, and when he began the circumambulation, he faced the stone and said: I know that you are a stone that does no harm and does not benefit. Had I not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissing you, I would not have kissed you. Then he kissed him, and Ali bin Abi Talib said to him: Yes, Amir. For believers, it harms and benefits. He said: Then he said: By the Book of God, Blessed and Most High. He said: Where is that in the Book of God? He said: God Almighty said: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam from their backs their offspring, and made them testify against themselves. Am I not your Lord? They said, “Yes.” [Al-A’raf: 172] God created Adam and wiped over his back, confirming to them that he is the Lord, and that they are the servants, and he took their covenants and covenants. And he wrote it on parchment, and this stone had eyes and a tongue, and he said to it, “Open your mouth.” He said: Then he opened his mouth and handed him that parchment and said: Bear witness to the one who fulfilled your death on the Day of Resurrection, and I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him: “On the Day of Resurrection, he will be brought with the Black Stone, and it will have a sharp tongue, which will bear witness to whoever touches it of Monotheism.” So it is, O Prince. It harms the believers and benefits, so Omar said: I seek refuge in God lest I live among a people whom you are not among, O Abu Hassan."
"1683","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Al-Sari told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Abbad bin Al-Awam told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabab, Mujahid narrated to us, he said: My master Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib said to me: I was among those who built the house, so I took a stone and leveled it. So I placed it next to the house. He said: I used to worship him, so if there was something in the house, I would send it to him, even if it was a milk day. It was good, so I sent it to him and they poured it on him, and the Quraysh disagreed about the stone when they wanted to place it, to the point that there was almost a fight between them. With swords, and he said: Make among yourselves the first man to enter through the door. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and they said: This is the trustworthy one, and they were In pre-Islamic times they called him Al-Amin, and they said: O Muhammad, we are satisfied with you. So he called for a garment, spread it out, and placed the stone in it, then said to this man: The belly, and for this belly - except that it is called stomachs -: Let each belly of you take one side of the garment, so they did, then they raised it, and he took it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness to his condition.”"
"1684","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Suraij bin Al-Nu’man Al-Jawhari told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Samak Ibn Harb, on the authority of Khaled Ibn Arara, he said: When Othman was killed, the people on that day were greatly terrified, and the draw of the sword against us was great. So I sat in my house, and something was presented to me in the market, so I went out, and behold, in the shade of the palace, a group of about forty men sitting, and behold, a chain It was displayed at the door, so I wanted to enter, but the doorman prevented me, so the people said: Leave the man, so I entered, and behold, the noblest of people and their faces, so he came A beautiful man in a suit, neither a shirt nor a turban. He sat down and saw Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. Then he said: Indeed, Abraham did not want The builder of the house was fed up and did not know what to do, so God sent the Tranquility, which is a gentle wind, and it folded and he began to build on it every day. He walked while Mecca was very hot, so when he reached the place of the stone, he said to Ishmael, “Go and find a stone.” He placed it here, and he began to walk around. With the mountains, so Gabriel came to him with the stone, and he placed it. Then Ismail came and said: Who brought this? - Or where is this from? Or where did this come from? He said: He who did not rely on my building and your building brought it, so he built it, then it was torn down, so the Amalekites built it, then it was torn down, so Jurhum built it, then It collapsed, and Quraysh built it. When they wanted to place the stone, they quarreled over its placement. He said: The first one to exit through this gate should place it. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out from the gate of Bani Shaybah and ordered a garment to be spread out and he placed a stone in its middle. Then he ordered a man from... Every thigh of the Quraysh was to be taken in the corner of the garment, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it in his hand and placed it. It was agreed upon. The two sheikhs for narrating the long hadith on the authority of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, and Kathir ibn Kathir, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the story of a building The Kaaba was the first thing built by Abraham Al-Khalil, peace be upon him, and this is different from that.”"
"1685","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abi told us Ziyad, and Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, and Salam bin Junada narrated to us, they said: Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us. Al-Thawri, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ziyad told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “He only made throwing The pebbles, the tawaf, the Sa’i between the two rows, and the Marwah are to establish the remembrance of God and no other than Him. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1686","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Saleh Al-Hamdani told us, Abdul-Samad bin Hassan told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Circumambulating the Kaaba is a prayer except that God has made it permissible for you to speak about it, so whoever speaks should speak only good.”"
"1687","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, referred it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: “Circumambulating the Kaaba is like prayer, except that you speak, so who “He spoke, but he does not speak anything but good.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and a group of people attributed it to the Prophet."
"1688","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The stone is from the House because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated the House from behind it,” God said. Blessed and Most High: {And let them circumambulate the Ancient House} [Al-Hajj: 29] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this.”"
"1689","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Malik bin Ismail told us, Abd Al-Salam bin Harb told us, about Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, drank water while circumambulating.” This is a hadith. It is strange and true, and they did not produce it with this wording.”"
"1690","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi informed us, Muhammad ibn Saad al-Awfi informed us, Abu Asim informed us, Ibn Juraij informed us, Sulayman informed me Al-Ahwal is that Tawus told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by the Kaaba a man leading a man with a belt in his nose, so he cut him off. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him by the hand, then commanded him to lead him by the hand. He said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man who was walking around. He crossed his path with a hand, or a foot, or a thread, or something other than that, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut him off and said: “Lead him with your hand.” Ibn Jurayj said: Suleiman al-Ahwal told me this. All of them agreed that Tawus told him that Ibn Abbas said that on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1691","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abu Rabah told him that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “All the chickens of Mecca “A road and a slope.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1692","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Hafs Al-Khathami told us, Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq Al-Kindi told us, Issa bin Sawadah told us, On the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Zazan, he said: Ibn Abbas fell seriously ill, so he called his sons and gathered them together and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “Whoever performs Hajj from Mecca on foot until he returns to Mecca, God will record for him seven hundred good deeds for every step he takes, every good deed.” Like the good deeds of the Sanctuary. It was said: What are the good deeds of the Sanctuary? He said: “For every good deed there will be a hundred thousand good deeds.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1693","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ja`far al-Jaloudi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Mihran told us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf told us, Abu Qurrah told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one day before the tarwiyah “He addressed the people and informed them of their rituals.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it."
"1694","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, Abu Kudaynah Yahya bin Al-Muhallab Al-Bajli, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed five times.” “Prayers in Mina” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it."
"1695","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, he said: “It is part of the Sunnah of Hajj that the imam prays the noon, afternoon and sunset prayers.” And the last evening and morning prayers at Mina, then in the morning he went to Arafat, where he arrived wherever it was decided for him, until when the sun had passed, he addressed the people, then he prayed. noon and afternoon prayers together, then he stood at Arafat until the sun had set, then he left and prayed at Muzdalifah, or wherever God had decided, then he stood in congregation until He travels, and pays off before sunrise. When he stones the big Jamarat, everything is permissible for him that is forbidden to him except women and perfumes, until he visits the House.” This A hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1696","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakra Bakkar bin Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Al-Harith bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman bin Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sukhbra, he said: I went out in the morning with Abdullah bin Masoud from Mina to Arafat. Abdullah was a man with two braids, with the anointing of the people of the desert, and he used to wear the Talbiyah. Then a group of people gathered around him and said: Oh. My Bedouin, this is not a day of talbiyah, rather it is the day of takbir. He said: Then he turned to me and said: Are people ignorant or have they forgotten? By the One who sent Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with the truth, “I went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, from Mina to Arafat, and he did not neglect reciting the Talbiyah.” Until he stoned the Jamarat, unless he mixed it with the words “Allahu Akbar” or “Tahlil.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1697","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Remove from the stomach of a stubborn person, and remove from the stomach of a muhsir.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and its evidence is according to the condition of the two sheikhs. “It is authentic, except that it contains shortcomings in its chain of transmission.”"
"1698","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddaad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he told me Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: It was said: “Avoid a muhsir, and they abstained from ‘Aranat.” As for his saying: “Aranat” So standing with a ‘urnah means do not stand with a ‘urna’, and as for his saying: “on the authority of a mu’shir”, it means to descend in the plural unless they descend with a mu’shir."
"1699","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdullah told us, Sufyan told us, and Ali bin Issa, and the pronunciation for him, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I memorized it from Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Safwan, on the authority of his uncle, Yazid bin Shayban, said: We were standing behind the parking lot, with Amr far away from it. Imam, then Ibn Murbi’ Al-Ansari came to us and said: I am the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to you. He says to you: “Be aware of your feelings.” “This, then you are on a legacy from the legacy of Abraham.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1700","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad told me Bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, He says: I heard Al-Sha’abi speaking, on the authority of Urwa bin Mudarris bin Aws bin Haritha bin Lam, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was in a group, and I said: May I perform Hajj? He said: “Whoever prayed this prayer with us in this place, then stood with us in this position until the imam departed, and who came before that from Arafat? Day or night, his Hajj has been completed and he has completed his fasting.”"
"1701","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Wahb bin Jarir told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Adl informed us of Marwa and the pronunciation of it. Abu Al-Mujih reported, Abdan reported, Abdullah reported, Ismail bin Abi Khalid reported, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Urwa bin Mudarris Al-Tai, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing with a crowd, and I said: O Messenger of God, I came to you from Mount Tayy, and I had crowned I rode, and I exhausted myself. By God, I did not leave a mountain without standing on it. Is there a Hajj for me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs this prayer with us and has come to Arafat before that, day or night, has performed This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of all the imams of hadith, and it is one of the rules of Islam, and he refrained from It was narrated by the two sheikhs Muhammad bin Ismail and Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj according to their originals, that no one narrated about Urwa bin Mudarris except Aamir Al-Shabi. We found Urwa bin Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam narrated on his authority.”"
"1702","Abdul-Samad bin Ali bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Abu Abdullah Ahmed bin Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hassan told us. Al-Tustari with covert, on the authority of Abdul-Wahhab bin Fulayh Al-Makki, Yusuf bin Khalid Al-Samti Al-Basri narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Urwah bin Mudarris al-Tai, may God be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in a position, and I said: O Messenger of God, I came from Mount Tayy. I exhausted my mount and exhausted myself. By God, there is not a single mountain left of those mountains that I did not stand on. He said: “Who? He performed this prayer with us - meaning the morning prayer - and he had come to Arafat before that, day or night, and had completed his Hajj and fulfilled his pilgrimage.” In narrating this Sunnah, one of the Companions, Urwah ibn al-Mudarris, was followed by Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar al-Dawli."
"1703","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri told us, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bukayr ibn Ata’, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at Arafat, and he came to him Some people from the people of Najd, while it was at Arafat, asked him, so he ordered a caller to call out: “Hajj is at Arafat, and whoever comes on the night of Friday prayer before dawn has risen, he has He reached the days of Mina, three days. Whoever hurries on two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays, there is no sin on him.” Then a man went and called."
"1704","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qatbani told me, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahmi told me, Wahb bin Jarir told me, My father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told me, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of his uncle Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father Jubayr bin Mutim said: The Quraysh were just pushing back from Muzdalifah and they were saying: We are the five, so let us not leave the Sacred Mosque, and they abandoned the situation. On Arafat, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in pre-Islamic times standing with the people at Arafat on a camel of his, then he would go out in the morning with his people. At Muzdalifah, he stands with them and pushes them away when they push back.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1705","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Munqidh Al-Khawlani told us, Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Makhramah bin Bukayr, on the authority of his father, He said: I heard Yunus bin Yusuf narrating, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “There is no day on which God will free a servant from the Fire more than the Day of Arafat. Indeed, he will approach, then he will boast. The angels, and he says: What did they mean? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1706","Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Hashimi told us about Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza Al-Ghafari told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us. Al-Qatwani, and Abu Sa’id Abd al-Rahman bin Ahmad al-Mu’adhdhin told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Imam told us, Ali bin Muslim told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: We were with Ibn Abbas With Arafat, he said to me: Lord, why do I not hear people respond? So I said: They are afraid of Muawiyah. He said: Then Ibn Abbas came out of his tent and said: “At your service, O God, at your command, for they have abandoned the Sunnah.” “From hatred for Ali, may God be pleased with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1707","Abu Sa`id bin Abi Bakr bin Abi Uthman told me, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told me, Jamil bin Al-Hassan Al-Jahdhami told us, Mahboub bin Al-Hasan, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stopped at Arafat Then, he said: “At your service, O God, at your service,” he said: “The best is only the best of the hereafter.” Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim protested with Dawud. This hadith is authentic, they did not narrate it.”"
"1708","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God is proud of the people of Arafat, the people of heaven.” So he says to them: Look at my servants, they came to me disheveled and dusty. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1709","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Osama, may God be pleased with them, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, touched his buttocks when he departed from Arafat So he exuded peace, and said: “O people, you must be calm.” And he said: “Righteousness does not consist in driving horses and camels.” I did not see a camel raising her hand. Until he came to Mina: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1710","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Kathir bin Shinzir, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Bedouins of Al-Idha’ were from the people of In the desert, they were standing on the edge of the people, who had hung up their heels and sticks. When they dispersed, they would cackle, and the people would disperse. “And I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “The hoofs of his she-camel cannot touch the ground in motion,” and he said: “O people, rest assured.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1711","Ahmad bin Jaafar bin Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Khawas told us, Al-Harith bin Muhammad Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Awf told us Ibn Abi Jamila, and Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Ja’far told us, we told him Awf, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Husayn, told by Abu Al-Aliyah, who said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said to me, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me On the morning of the Aqaba, he said: “Bring me some of the pebbles of the grave,” and when they were placed in his hand, he said: “In the likes of these, in the likes of these, And beware of extremism in religion, for those before you perished only because of extremism in religion. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1712","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, and Abu Amr told us Othman bin Ahmed bin Al-Sammak told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mansour told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Ali Al-Hanafi told us, and Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, they said: Ayman bin Nabul told us, he said: I heard Qudamah bin Abd. Allah ibn Ammar Al-Kalabi, may God be pleased with him, says: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, throwing the Jamarat on the Day of Sacrifice on a red-haired she-camel. “No beating, no expulsion, and no return to you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1713","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas al-Qurashi told us, Ja`far bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, Al-Hasan bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he narrated it, saying: “When he came Ibrahim, God’s friend, performed the rituals. Satan appeared to him at Jamarat al-Aqaba, and he threw seven pebbles at him until they settled in the ground. Then he appeared to him at The second Jamarat, and he stoned it with seven pebbles until it became hot in the ground. Then he was brought to him at the third Jamarat, and he stoned it with seven pebbles until it became hot. On earth. Ibn Abbas said: “You will be stoned by Satan and the people of your father will be cursed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1714","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani informed us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he informed us Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, on the authority of his mother Musikah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Shall we not build you a building in Mina that will shade you? He said: “There is no climate from those who came before.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1715","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ayyash bin Al-Walid Al-Riqam told us, Abd Al-Ala bin Abd told us. The highest, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Abdullah bin Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “In the year of Hudaybiyyah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a camel to Abu Jahl with a pinch of silver on its head, to enrage the polytheists. Thus, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1716","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, and Ahmad told us Ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Ya’qub Ibn Ibrahim told me, my father told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Yazid bin Abi Habib Al-Masry told me, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Abu Ayyash, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him. God on their behalf, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered two rams on the day of the Eid, then he said when he faced them: “I turned my face to the one who broke the fast.” The heavens and the earth are upright, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my death belong to God, Lord of the worlds, with no partner, and with that I have been commanded. And I am the first of the Muslims. In the name of God and God is the greatest. O God, from you and to you on the authority of Muhammad and his nation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1717","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Abd Al-Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib, the jurist in Egypt, informed us, Muhammad bin Abi told us Many, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slaughtered on behalf of one of his wives who had performed Umrah during the Farewell Hajj.” A cow among them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1718","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulayman Al-Asbahani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Shu’bah told us, and Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun, and Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Shu’bah - and this The wording is the hadith of Abu Abbas - he said: I heard Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, saying: I heard Ubaid bin Fayrouz, saying: I said to Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, He told me about the sacrifices that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked or forbade. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said like this. With his hand, and my hand is shorter than the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There are four things that are not sufficient for sacrifice: the one-eyed woman whose defect is obvious, and the sick woman.” The most obvious is its sickness, and the lame is the clearest of its lameness, and the broken ones that cannot be cleaned. He said: I said, “I hate for there to be a defect in the ear.” And the century. He said: “Whatever you dislike, leave it, and do not forbid it to anyone else.” This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it due to the lack of narrations from Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, and he said: Ali ibn al-Madani demonstrated his virtues and mastery, saying, “This hadith has various witnesses with sound chains of transmission, but they did not narrate it,” including:"
"1719","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi narrated to us, they said: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama narrated to us, Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us, Affan informed us, and Ahmad ibn Ja`far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us. Ibn Hanbal, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Jarry bin Kulayb al-Zuhri speaking, On the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade sacrificing the organs of the horn and ear.” Qatada said: So I mentioned According to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: “Al-‘Adab: half or more than that and from there.”"
"1720","What Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Wahb bin Jarir and Abu Al-Nadr told us, They said: Shu'bah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja'far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja'far told us, Shu`bah, that Salamah bin Kuhayl informed him, saying: I heard Hajjayyah bin Ali Al-Kindi, saying: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, saying: “We commanded The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that we should seek out the eye and the ear, and among them:"
"1721","What Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Munadi told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, On the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Hajjayya bin Adiy, that a man asked Ali, may God be pleased with him, about the cow, and he said: About seven. He said: Al-Qarn. He said: Al-Arj. He said: When the rituals have been completed. He said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look towards the Spring.” And the ear, including:"
"1722","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Tanisi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Sadaqa bin Abdullah Al-Dimashqi told us, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Ru’ayni, said: We were sitting at Utba ibn Abd al-Sulami when Yazid of Misr al-Maqri’i came, Then he said to Utbah: O Abu Al-Walid, we just went out in search of a serious ritual, and we hardly found anything clean except that I found a fat pomegranate. Utbah said: If you had not brought her to us, he said: O God, forgive. Should I leave you, but you will not leave me? He said: Yes, he said: Why is that? He said: You have doubts and I do not doubt. He said: Then he took out the threshold of his hand and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade five: Al-Mawsila, Al-Musaffarah, Al-Baqha’a, Al-Musha’iah, and Al-Kasra’. He said: Al-Mawsila is the one whose horn is uprooted, and Al-Mushafirah. “The one whose ears have been cut off, the one whose eyes are clearly visible, the emaciated or sick mourner who does not follow the sheep.”"
"1723","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Ahmad bin Salih told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told me, Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent He greeted Umm Salamah on the night of the sacrifice, and she stoned the coals before dawn, then she went and made the funeral. That was the second day of her stay. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “is true according to their condition, they did not narrate it.”"
"1724","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Adl informed us of Marw, Abu al-Mawjih told us, Abu Ammar informed us, and Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Ali Al-Hafiz, Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Saji told us, Muhammad bin Zanbour, and Muhammad bin Amr bin Suleiman told us, they said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: “If one of you departs, let his last pledge be with the House except Menstruation, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted them. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1725","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah told us Al-Fazari, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Othman Al-Sawwaf told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Amr told me Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is broken or lame is permissible, and he must perform Hajj from the one before him.” He said Ikrimah: I asked Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, and they said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1726","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz informed us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Muhammad Al-Absi told us, Abi told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with them, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed two Hajj before That he migrated - meaning he performed Hajj after he migrated - a Hajj with which he performed an Umrah. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1727","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Umayyad and Ali bin Abdullah Al-Halimi told us in Baghdad, saying: Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ruh bin Ubadah, Muhammad bin Abi Hafsa told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abi Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Al-Aqra’ bin Habis, may God be pleased with him About them, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked about Hajj every year? He said: “No, but one proof. If I had said yes, it would have been obligatory, and if it had been obligatory, you would not have listened nor been able to bear it.”"
"1728","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Hashim bin Yunus Al-Qassar told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid bin Musafir narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Sinan al-Du’ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O my people, the Hajj has been prescribed for you.” Al-Aqra’ bin Habis said, “Is it for the whole year, O Messenger of God?” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent, then he said: “No, but one Hajj, and then whoever performs Hajj after that is voluntary, even if I say: Yes.” It would have been obligatory for you, then you would not listen nor be able to bear it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1729","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Ismail bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Hajj and Umrah are obligatory for all people except the people of Mecca, for Their Umrah is their circumambulation, so let them go out to Tan’im, then enter it. By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not enter it except as a pilgrim or “Umrah” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and it was transmitted on the authority of Muhammad ibn Kathir with another chain of narration.”"
"1730","Professor Abu Al-Walid told us, may God Almighty have mercy on him, Muhammad bin Al-Mundhir Al-Harawi told us, Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Saeed bin Ghalib told us, Muhammad bin Kathir, Ismail bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Hajj and Umrah are two obligatory duties, and it does not matter whichever one you begin with.” The correct view on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit is his saying:"
"1731","Abu Al-Walid told us, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Yahya bin Ayyub Al-Maqabi told us, Abbad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, that Zayd Ibn Thabit was asked about Umrah before Hajj, and he said: “Two prayers, it does not matter which one you begin with.”"
"1732","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad informed us, Ibrahim bin Musa informed us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, And Abdul Majeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, said: Nafi’, Ibn Omar’s client, told me that Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with him About them he used to say: “There is not one of God’s creation except that there is an obligatory Hajj and Umrah upon him, whoever is able to do so, a way, and whoever adds after it Anything is good and voluntary.”
 Ibn Jurayj said: And I was informed on the authority of Ibn Abbas that he said: “Umrah is obligatory, just as Hajj is obligatory for whoever can afford it.” This is a chain of narration. “Sahih according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"1733","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Hamdawayh al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz informed us, Sa`id ibn Sulayman told us, Hisham told us, On the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her during her Umrah: “Indeed, you will be rewarded according to the amount of your effort and expenditure.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and there is an authentic witness for it."
"1734","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Sulaym Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Al-Fadl Jaafar bin Makram Al-Razi told us, Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Idris Al-Halwani, Mahran bin Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha May God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her during her Umrah: “Your reward for your Umrah is only according to your expenses.”"
"1735","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala, who said: I heard Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Ali and Uthman, may God be pleased with them, performed Hajj, but when they were on some road, he forbade Othman abstained from performing Tamattu’ from Umrah until Hajj, so it was said to Ali that he had forbidden Tamattu’, so he said: “If you see him departing, depart,” so he complied. Ali and his companions performed Umrah, but Uthman did not forbid them. Ali said: “Was I not informed that you are forbidden from performing Umrah?” He said: Yes, then Ali said: “Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tamattu?” He said: Yes, this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1736","Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan Al-Maruzi told us, in Mecca, Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I will perform Hajj and Umrah together.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1737","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Hajj and Umrah, because he knew “He will not perform Hajj after that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1738","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabbah told us, Ismail bin Zakaria told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: Where did you come from? He said: I drank from Zamzam, and Ibn Abbas said to him: Did you drink from it as it should? He said: How is that, Abu Abbas? He said: When you drink from it, face the Qiblah, mention the name of God, exhale three times, and swallow it, then when you finish it, thank God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not neglect Zamzam.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it if Uthman ibn al-Aswad heard from Ibn Abbas.”"
"1739","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Hisham Al-Maruzi told us, Muhammad bin Habib Al-Jaroudi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Water Zamzam when it was drunk for him. If you drink it, you will be healed, may God heal you. If you drink it, seeking refuge, may God protect you, and if you drink it, it will quench your thirst. He cut it off.” He said: Whenever Ibn Abbas drank Zamzam water, he would say: “O God, I ask you for useful knowledge, abundant provision, and a cure for every disease.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration if it was transmitted by Al-Jarudi, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1740","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Abu Sa`id Yahya ibn Suleiman Al-Jufi’i, Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Hussein, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated on the stone.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1741","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub ibn Yusuf informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Ja`far ibn al-Zabarqan told us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh, Sulaym bin Amir told me, I heard Abu Umamah saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: While he was giving the sermon People on his camel during the Farewell Hajj. He says: “O people, obey your Lord, pray your fifth, pay the zakat on your wealth, and fast.” Your month, and obey the one who commands you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.” I said to Abu Umamah: How long have you heard this hadith? He said: I heard, when I was thirty years old, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1742","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Ahmad bin Al-Nadr bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Wahb bin Jarir, my father told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Ibn Abi Najih told us, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: There were many sayings from people, so we went out as pilgrims until there were only a few nights between us and our departure. We were commanded to perform the mission, so one of us would go to Arafat, and he would come out. Dripping with semen, this reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stood up to give a sermon and said: “By God, do you teach me, O people? I, by God, know you best.” By God, and the most pious of you to Him, and if I had received my command, I would not have taken back a sacrificial animal, and I would have permissible as they permissible, so whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him Let him fast for three days, and seven days when he returns to his family, and whoever finds a sacrificial animal, let him sacrifice, for we used to slaughter camels, for seven days.”
 Ata’ said, Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, distributed sheep among his companions on that day, and Saad got Ibn Abi Waqqas had a goat and slaughtered it for himself. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stopped at Arafat, he ordered Rabi’ah ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf, so he stood Under the hands of his camel, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Scream, O people. Do you know what month this is?” They said: The sacred month. He said: “Do you know what country this is?” They said: The Sacred City. Then he said: “Do you know what day this is?” They said: The day of the Greater Hajj. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has made your blood and your property sacred to you, as sacred as your month. “This, and as sacred as this is your country, and as sacred as this day of yours.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, completed his Hajj.
 When he stopped at Arafat, he said: “This is a stopping place, and every Arafat is a stopping place.”
 And he said when he stopped at Qazah: “This is a standing position, and the whole of Muzdalifah is a stopping place.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and it contains some words. From the words of the hadith of Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Sadiq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, and it also contains many additional words."
"1743","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the Jamarat and sacrificed his sacrifice, He gave the barber his right side and he shaved it, then he gave him the left side and he shaved it, then he gave it to Abu Talha and ordered him to divide it among the people. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1744","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Aban bin Yazid told us, Yahya bin Abi told us Many, that Abu Salamah told him, that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid told him, that his father, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, witnessed the He and a man from the Ansar, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shaved his head in his garment, gave it to him, and he divided some of it among the men, and trimmed his nails. So his owner gave it to him. They said: We have it dyed with henna and katam. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1745","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Abu Sa`id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ubaid told us Allah Ibn Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed.” The noon prayer at Mina,” Nafi’ said: Ibn Umar “would perform the sacrifice on the Day of Sacrifice, then return and pray the noon prayer at Mina,” and he mentioned that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he did it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1746","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: It was read to Abdullah bin Wahb, Ibn Jurayj told you, about Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not have sand during the seven days in which he had intercourse.” Ata’ said: “No.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1747","Abu Yahya Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Samarqandi informed me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Imam told me, Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, he informed me Khaled bin Abdullah, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He came to the water-maid and asked for something to drink. Al-Abbas said: O Fadl, go to your mother and bring a drink from her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Give me a drink.” He said: O Messenger of God, they are putting their hands in it, so he said: “Give me a drink.” So he drank from it, then Zamzam came, and they were drawing water. And they worked therein. He said: “Work, for you are doing righteous deeds.” Then he said: “If you had not been defeated, I would have come down to place the rope on this.” Meaning his freedman - and he pointed to his freedman, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1748","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb, he said: Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Salem said that Amr bin Abi Amr, al-Muttalib’s client, informed them, on the authority of al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The meat of wild game is lawful for you, and you are unlawful unless “You hunt it or it is caught for you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And thus it was narrated on the authority of Malik ibn Anas and Suleiman ibn Bilal, on the authority of Amr, with a continuous chain of narration, and as for the hadith of Malik"
"1749","So Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, my uncle told me, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, in Egypt, Muhammad bin Suleiman bin Abi told us. Dawud, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him On the authority of God, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the like, as for the hadith of Suleiman bin Bilal"
"1750","So Abu Al-Hasan Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jdi told us, Saeed bin Kathir bin Ufayr told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abu Amr, on the authority of a man, from the Ansar, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and something similar. This hadith does not explain the hadith of Malik, Suleiman bin Bilal, and Yaqub Al-Iskandarani, for they prayed it and are trustworthy.”"
"1751","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Ishaq, and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, they said: Abd told us Al-Razzaq, Zakaria bin Ishaq reported, on the authority of Sulaiman Al-Ahwal, that he heard Tawus speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The people were leaving Mina facing them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to make their last stay at the House, and he permitted For the menstruating woman: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1752","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told me, Abu Amr Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mustamli told me, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, My father, Yazid bin Sinan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa’id al-Khudri, on the authority of his father Abi Sa’id, he said: We said, “O Messenger of God, these stones that you throw are carried, so you think that they are sinking. He said: “Whatever comes from them will be taken away, and had it not been That is because I saw them like mountains.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “Yazid bin Sinan is not abandoned.”"
"1753","Abu al-Tayyib Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Dhuhli informed us, Ja`far ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Marwan Muhammad ibn Uthman informed us. Al-Uthmani, Abu Damrah Al-Laythi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When one of you has completed his Hajj, let him make the journey to his family, for that is greater for his reward.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"1754","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim told us Al-Sayyari, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, they said: Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “Gabriel came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took him to show him the rituals. Then Thubair was relieved for him, so he entered Mina and showed him the Jamarat. Then he showed him Arafat, so Satan approached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Jamarat, and he stoned himself. He threw seven pebbles until it became hot, then he broke through the second Jamarat, so he stoned it with seven pebbles until it boiled, then he broke through at Jamarat al-Aqaba. So he threw seven pebbles at him until he became hot and he went away.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out."
"1755","Abu Sa`id Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Khasib al-Sufi narrated to us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Al-Alaa bin Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, And Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Hamdani, they said: Humayd bin Al-Khawar told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I will not stone until the sun has set, for Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to stone the stones on the Day of Sacrifice before noon, but after that, when “The disappearance” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1756","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, expanded on He said the salaam at the end of his day when he prayed the noon prayer, then he returned and stayed in Mina during the nights of the days of Tashreeq, throwing the Jamarat when the sun had passed, every Jamarat. With seven pebbles, he says “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble, and stops at the first, and at the second, he prolongs his standing and supplicates, then he stones the third and does not stand. Then, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1757","Abu Zakaria told us Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Yunus told us Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the Jamarat next to the Mina Mosque, he would throw seven pebbles at it. He says “Allahu Akbar” whenever he throws a pebble, then moves in front of it, and stands facing the Qiblah, raising his hands, supplicating. He used to stand for a long time, then he would come. The second Jamarat, he stones it with seven pebbles, saying “Allahu Akbar” every time he throws a pebble. Then he descends to the left side of the valley and stops facing. facing the qiblah, raising his hands, then he goes to the Jamarat near Aqaba and throws seven pebbles at it, saying “Allahu Akbar” at each pebble, then he leaves and does not He will stand up there.” Al-Zuhri said: I heard Salem bin Abdullah narrating something like this, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: And it was Ibn Umar accepts it. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1758","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoob Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, Malik bin Anas told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Al-Badah ibn Adiy, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted the shepherds to stone the Jamarat one day and say supplication “One day” Abu Al-Badah is the son of Asim bin Adi and he is famous among the Tabi’een, and Asim bin Adi is famous among the Companions, and he is the one who used to curse. Whoever says on the authority of Abu Al-Baddah bin Adiyy has attributed his lineage to his grandfather, and what I mentioned is true.”"
"1759","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Dawud Al-Masry told me, in Mecca, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Jarir told us, Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, that Ibn Asim bin Adi, may God be pleased with them, told him on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for herders of camels in the house to throw stones on the day of Sacrifice, then they throw the stones tomorrow, or the day after tomorrow for two days, then they stone the day of sacrifice.”"
"1760","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Asheeb told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Awn bin Abi Juhayfa, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of his father, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praying two rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer with the simplest form.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1761","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa bin Zayd bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Malik Al-Tanukhi in Tinis told us, Amr bin Abi told us Salama al-Tannisi, Zuhayr bin Muhammad al-Makki told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, that Aisha used to say, “It is amazing for a person.” When a Muslim enters the Kaaba until he raises his gaze to the ceiling, he leaves this out of respect and reverence for God. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered “The Kaaba never left his sight behind the place of his prostration until he left it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1762","Abu Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran bin Khalid told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Ismail bin Abd told us Al-Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, left me while he was in a state of peace. He had a good soul, then he came back to me while he was sad, and I said: O Messenger of God, you left me while you were like this and that. He said: “I entered The Kaaba and I wish I had not done it, for I fear that I may have exhausted my nation after me.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1763","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Bukayr told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: I said to Ata’: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: You were only commanded to perform tawaf, but you were not commanded to enter it. He said: He did not forbid us from entering it, but I heard him say: Usama bin Zaid, may God be pleased with them, told me, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the house, and when he came out, he prayed two rak’ahs in He faced the House, and said: “This is the qiblah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this."
"1764","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: I heard Yazid Ibn Ruman narrates, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, who said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Oh Aisha, had your people not been newly ignorant, I would have demolished the house until what they took out of it was inserted into the stone, for they were unable. At his expense, I made two gates for it, an eastern gate and a western gate, and I stuck it to the ground and placed it on the foundation of Abraham.” He said: And it was. The one who invited Ibn al-Zubayr to demolish it and rebuild it, said: Yazid bin Roman, I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr when he demolished it, so he extracted the foundation of the house. Like the humps of a camel intertwined, so I said to Yazid bin Roman while I was circumambulating with him that day: Show me what they took out of the stone from it. He said: I will show you to him now. When he had reached it, he said: This place. Jarir said: I encircled it about six cubits. “This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”"
"1765","Abu Yahya Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Samarqandi told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, and Ali bin Khashram, they said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Musa bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, told him, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, shaved his head during the Farewell Hajj.” He said: People used to shave their hair during Hajj, then they would perform Umrah when they left and say: How does this shave? He says: “Pass the razor over your head.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1766","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Milhan told us, Ibn Bukair told us, Al-Layth told me, that Abu Al-Zubayr He told him, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led Aisha from Tan’im on the night of Dhul-Hijjah. “Measles” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1767","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Uthman bin Al-Haytham told us, Awf bin Abi Jamila told us, about Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a man came to him and said: My father is an old man who has learned Islam, but he did not perform the Hajj, nor did he hold on to a mount, and if I pulled him with the rope on the mount, I feared that I would kill him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with these words."
"1768","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu told us Amr Muhammad bin Jafar Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Sadran told us, Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, I heard Al-Nu’man bin Salem, saying: I heard Amr bin Aws speaking, on the authority of Abu Razin, may God be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of God, my father is an old man who does not He is able to perform Hajj and Umrah and does not make any pretext. He said: “Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1769","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Affan told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us, By Al-Ray, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Abu Al-Walid and Muhammad bin Kathir told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr bin told us Ishaq, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a boy performs Hajj, then it is a Hajj for him until he becomes of sound mind, and if he becomes of sound mind, then he must perform Hajj.” Another, and if a Bedouin performs Hajj, then he has a proof, and if he emigrates, he has another proof.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1770","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, Zayd bin Al-Mubarak Al-San’ani told us, Muammar bin Rashid Al-Sana’ani, on the authority of Abdul Karim Al-Jazari, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I have rewarded myself From a people to whom I left some of my wages so that they would be alone between me and the rituals. Will that suffice for me? Ibn Abbas said: “This is one of those who God Almighty said: “Those will have a share of what they have earned, and God is quick in reckoning.” [Al-Baqarah: 202] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1771","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Utbi told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “At the beginning of the Hajj, people used to make pledges of allegiance at Mina, Arafat, and Souq. Dhul-Majaz, and the seasons of Hajj, so they feared selling while they were in a state of deprivation, so God Almighty revealed: {There is no blame upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord} [Al-Baqarah: 198] Concerning the seasons of Hajj, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1772","Abu Al-Abbas told us Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Ahmed bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Abdullah bin Al-Hasan Al-Harrani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Sulayman bin Jubayr bin Mutim, On the authority of his uncle Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, on the authority of his father Jubayr ibn Mut’im, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before That it should be descended upon him, and he was standing on his camel at Arafat with the people, pushing some of it with them, and that was only by the granting of God Almighty for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1773","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed me, my father informed me, Muhammad ibn Zakaria ibn Bukair informed us, he informed me Ibn Jarih, my father told me, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, may God be pleased with him, who said: I lost a camel of mine on the day of Arafat, so I set off for Arafat. I seek it. “And when I saw Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, standing with the people at Arafat on his camel on the eve of Arafat, and that was after it was revealed to him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr, on the authority of The father of the hadith mentions Al-Hams, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing at Arafat. . . Mecca """
"1774","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of my father Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham said: Marwan sent to Umm Maqil to ask her about this hadith, and she narrated that Her husband was made a virgin for the sake of God, and she wanted to perform Umrah, so she asked her virgin husband, but he refused, so she went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So she mentioned that to him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered him to give it to her, and he said: “Hajj and Umrah are from the path of God, and “Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj” or “it suffices for a Hajj.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1775","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Abu Al-Numan Arim told us, Abd Al-Warith bin Saeed told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi told me Othman, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me that Ikrimah, the client of Ibn Abbas, told him, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Amr Al-Ansari told me. May God be pleased with them both, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever is broken or lame has become lawful, and there is another proof upon him.” He said: I told Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah said: It is true “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.” And it was said: On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, the client of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Amr"
"1776","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, the client of Umm Salamah, said: I asked Al-Hajjaj bin Amr Al-Ansari May God be pleased with them both regarding the imprisonment of a Muslim, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is broken or lame is permissible and must perform Hajj from He will come.” Ikrimah said: I told Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with them, and they said: Al-Hajjaj has spoken the truth."
"1777","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Ammar bin Zuraiq told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Quraysh were called Al-Hums, and they used to enter through the gates during the state of Ihram. The Ansar and other Arabs were not entering through the gates while in ihram, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a garden. From his gate, and Qutubah bin Amir Al-Ansari went out with him. They said: O Messenger of God, Qutubah bin Amir is an immoral man. He went out with you from The door, and he said: “What made you do that?” He said: I saw you do what you did, and he said: “I am an Ahmasi.” He said: “My religion is your religion.” Then God Almighty revealed: “Righteousness is not that “Enter houses from their backs, but righteousness is he who is pious.” [Al-Baqarah: 189] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not take it out with this increase.”"
"1778","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ayyub bin Suwayd told us, Al-Awza’i told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked: What is the righteousness of Hajj? He said: “Providing food and good speech.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it because they did not use Ayyub ibn Suwayd as evidence, but he A hadith that has many evidence"
"1779","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed Al-Anbari told us, On the authority of Amer Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted And the Hajj was greeted. A woman said to her husband: He performed Hajj on me with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I do not have anything on which to perform Hajj on me. She said: So he performed Hajj on me. On your buttocks, and he said: That is what your son and I will follow. She said: Then so-and-so performed Hajj with me on your camel. He said: He is a prisoner in the path of God. She said: So sell Your slave dates. He said: That is my strength and your strength. He said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from Mecca, she sent her husband to him and said: Read to the Messenger of May God’s peace and blessings be upon him, and ask him what qualifies as an argument with you? Then her husband came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my wife extends the peace and mercy of God to you, and she said that I should perform Hajj. You have it with you, so I said to her: I do not have it. She said: Then so-and-so performed Hajj with me on my camel, and I said to her: He is a prisoner in the path of God. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “If you had used her as proof, it would have been for the sake of God.” He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, laughed in astonishment at her keenness to Hajj, he said: And she commanded me to ask you what is equivalent to a Hajj with you? He said: “Give her the peace and mercy of God from me, and tell her that it is equivalent to performing Hajj with me as Umrah in Ramadan.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1780","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us a dictation in Sha`ban of the year three hundred and ninety-six. Abu narrated to us Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zannad told me, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abi Alqamah, on the authority of His mother, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded the people in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said: “Whoever wishes to return “Umrah before Hajj, let him do it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1781","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad, the grammarian in Baghdad, told us, Al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Abd told us. Al-Majid Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sought He made three circumambulations and walked four when he performed Hajj and Umrah when he performed Umrah.”
 Ibn Omar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed two or three Umrahs before his Hajj, and he did not perform Hajj other than one of his two Umrahs in Ramadan.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1782","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said, “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in three types: Among us are those who have performed Hajj and Umrah, and among us are those who have performed Hajj alone, and among us are those who have performed Umrah, so whoever has performed Hajj and Umrah are not permitted to perform Hajj or Umrah. Anything that has been forbidden to him until he has completed the rituals of Hajj, and whoever performs a single Hajj, nothing is permissible until he has performed the rituals of Hajj, and whoever performs an Umrah He circumambulated the House, Safa, and Marwah, performing Hajj, then he performed Hajj. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1783","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, and I asked him about Khallad bin Yazid Al-Ju’fi. Zuhair bin Muawiyah Al-Ju’fi told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, was “carrying Zamzam water, and she was told that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was doing it.”"
"1784",""
"1785","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Amr bin Maymun bin Mahran, Abu Hadir Othman bin Hadhir told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “The people of Hudaybiyyah were ordered to replace The sacrifice was made in the year in which they entered Mecca and exchanged, and the camels became strong, so they were given permission to buy a cow from those who had no camel available.” Narrated by Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yassar, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, interpreted and summarized"
"1786","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad ibn Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun bin Mihran said: I heard Abu Hadhir al-Himyari speaking to Abu Maimun bin Mihran. He said: I went out for Umrah in the year the people of Hazir were besieged. Al-Sham Ibn Al-Zubayr was in Mecca, and men from my people sent with me a sacrificial animal. When we reached the people of Al-Sham, they prevented us from entering the Sacred Mosque, so I slaughtered the sacrificial animal. I took my place, and I made permissible, then I came back, and when it was the following year, I went out to perform my Umrah, so I came to Ibn Abbas and asked him, and he said: Change The sacrificial animal “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded his companions to replace the sacrificial animal that they had slaughtered in the year of Hudaybiyyah for the Umrah al-Qadha.” Amr said: “My father was concerned about those who had slaughtered in the year of Hudaybiyyah, saying: I do not know whether the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, exchanged the gifts they had sacrificed.” In Al-Hudaybiyyah during the Umrah of the missed days, or not, until Abu Hadhir narrated it: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” And Abu Hadhir is a sheikh from The people of Yemen are accepted and honest"
"1787","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To Mecca: “What a pleasant town you have and how beloved you are to me, and had your people not expelled me, I would not have lived in anyone else.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1788","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ya’qub told us, my father told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Nafi’, servant of Abdullah bin Omar, narrated to me. Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him said: “Women are forbidden during their ihram from wearing gloves, the niqab, and anything that touches the wool and saffron of clothing, and to wear after that “Whatever color of clothing she likes, whether yellow, or shawl, or jewelry, or trousers, or sandals, or a shirt.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1789","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, about His father, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father Saad, that he used to leave the city and find one of the woodsmen with him. A wet tree that had been planted by some of the trees of the city, so he would take his spoils and speak to him about it, and Bishr said: So he spoke about it and say: “I will not let “A spoil that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took as spoils, and I am one of the people with the most wealth.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1790","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us in Baghdad, Abdul Rahman bin Marzuq Abu Awf Al-Buzuri told us, we told him Khaled bin Mukhlid Al-Qatwani, Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Mukhurami told us, Ismail bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, that Saad rode to He limited it to agate, and he found a slave cutting down a tree, so he captured it. When he returned, the slave’s family came to him asking him to return to them what he had taken. One of their servants said: “God forbid that I return something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bestowed upon me,” but he did not return anything to them. “This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"1791","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Salih Al-Wahazi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Anis bin Abu Yahya, my father told me, he said: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that a man from Banu Amr bin Awf and a man from Banu Khudra had a disagreement. They visited the mosque that was founded on piety. Al-Awfi said: It is the Mosque of Quba, and Al-Khudri said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, so he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and asked him, and he said: “This is my mosque, and in that is much good.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and Unays bin Abi Yahya differed from his brother Ibrahim.”"
"1792",""
"1793","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Muhammad bin Mahran Al-Jamal told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to often disagree to “Quba’, walking and riding.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it with this wording."
"1794","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr told us Al-Muzaki, Bimrwa, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, they said: Al-Uqabi told us, in what was read to Malik, and Abu Yahya Al-Samarqandi told me, Muhammad told us Ibn Nasr, and Yahya Ibn Mansour told us, Muhammad Ibn Abdul Salam told us, they said: Yahya Ibn Yahya told us, he said: I read to Malik, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abi Alqamah, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, I heard her say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up, put on his clothes, and then went out.” So I ordered my maid Barirah to follow him and see where he was going, so I followed him until “he came to Al-Baqi’ and stood at its bottom as long as God wished for him to stop, then He left and returned.” Barira preceded him. Aisha said: She told me. She said: I did not mention any of that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted me until the morning, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: “I was sent to the people of Al-Baqi’ to pray for them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1795","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told us, dictating in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Yaqoub bin Ishaq al-Hadrami told us, Zaydah told us, On the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from a journey Then he saw his family and said: “By, O, to our Lord, in repentance, which will not leave us alone.” This is an authentic hadith between the two Sheikhs, because Al-Bukhari He alone used Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim used Samak ibn Harb, and they did not bring him out.”"
"1796","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Muzaki informed us of Marw, Abdullah ibn Ruh al-Madani informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, who said: “We came from Mecca on Hajj or Umrah. Usayd bin Hudair was walking in front of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we met young men from the Ansar who were meeting their families when they arrived. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1797","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Abu Farwa Al-Rahwi told us, on the authority of Urwa bin Ruwaym Al-Lakhmi said: I heard Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from an invader, entered the mosque and prayed.” There are two rak’ahs in it, and he used to like it when he came from a journey to enter the mosque and pray two rak’ahs in it, then come out.” So he came to Fatima. So he started towards her, and she faced him and started kissing his face and his eyes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “What’s the matter with you?” She said: O Messenger of God, I see you have turned pale. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “O Fatima, God Almighty has sent He made you cry about something that has not remained on the surface of the earth, not a house of bricks or hair, but God will bring it into glory or humiliation until it reaches where the night has reached.” This is a hadith whose narrators are unanimously agreed that they are trustworthy, except for Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Sinan “and he has a witness from
 The hadith of Ibrahim bin Qu’ais"
"1798","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad ibn Uthman Al-Adami, the reciter in Baghdad, told us, Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya ibn Hammad told us, Abu Awanah, Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Qu’ays, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “And when he went out on a campaign, his first encounter with Fatima would be.” Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith without this wording."
"1799",""
"1800","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq. The jurist, Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Zamaa told us, on the authority of his father, and on the authority of his mother Zainab bint Abi Salamah, they narrated to him, on the authority of Umm Salamah, They all told him about that about her. She said: It was the night that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was coming to me, and Wahb bin Zam’a entered upon me. And with him was a man from the family of Abu Umayyah, wearing disguises. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Wahb: “Did you communicate with Abu Abdullah?” He said: No, by God, O Messenger of God. He said: “Take off your shirt.”"
"1801","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub ibn Yusuf al-Adl informed us, Abu Bakr Yahya ibn Ja`far ibn Abi Talib informed us, Abu Dawud Suleiman told us Ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi, Abu al-Awwam Imran al-Qattan told us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih told us, Abu Muslim informed us, And Muhammad bin Ayyub, and Yusuf bin Yaqoub, they said: Amr bin Marzuq narrated to us, Imran informed us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i narrated to us, Abd narrated to us. Allah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Imran al-Qattan told us, Qatada al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is nothing more honorable to God than supplication.” This hadith The chain of transmission is authentic, and they did not narrate it. As for Muslim, he did not narrate in his book, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, but he is truthful in his narration, and he said Al-Bukhari cited it as evidence in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih, and I, God willing, will follow the information that was revealed to the two sheikhs in the Book of Da’awat according to the school of thought. Abu Saeed Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi in accepting it, for I heard Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari say: I heard Abu al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali, saying: My father was narrating, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, saying: If we narrate, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding what is permissible, what is forbidden, and the rulings, we emphasized the chains of transmission, and we criticized the men, and when we narrated the virtues of deeds and the reward,"
"1802","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Harun bin Suleiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Mansour, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Yasa’ Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Indeed, supplication is worship,” then he recited: “And your Lord says, ‘Call upon Me, I will respond to you.’” [Ghafir: 60] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.” It was narrated by Shu’bah and Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Dhar, and as for the hadith of Shu’bah"
"1803","So Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Mansour told us, on the authority of Dhar, and something similar. As for the hadith of Jarir"
"1804","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ruqaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Dhar, he mentioned it with a similar chain of transmission, and there is evidence for this hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas"
"1805","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sulayman told us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Razi and Ibrahim ibn Sharik al-Kufi told us, they said: Ahmad ibn Abd told us. Allah bin Yunus, on the authority of Kamil bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both: “The best worship is supplication,” and he recited: “And your Lord said, “Call upon Me, I will respond to you. Indeed, those who are arrogant My servants will enter Hell humiliated} [Ghafir: 60]"
"1806","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim Al-Dahhak told us Ibn Mukhlid Al-Shaybani, Abu Al-Malih Al-Farisi told us, Abu Saleh told us, he said: Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever does not call upon God, He will be angry with him.”"
"1807","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Hibban Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Al-Sabah Al-Jarjari told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari, Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And peace be upon him: “Whoever does not call on God, He will be angry with him, and God is angry with whoever does it, and no one else will do that” - meaning in supplication - “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Abu Salih al-Khuzi and Abu al-Malih al-Farisi were not mentioned with the narration, rather they are among the unknown. due to the scarcity of hadith”"
"1808","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no people who sat together and dispersed. “Therefore, they did not mention God therein except as if they had separated from the carcass of a donkey, and it will be a sorrow for them on the Day of Resurrection.” Followed by: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayy Hazim, on the authority of Suhail,"
"1809","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Ismail ibn Abi Uwais told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim told us, On the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. “This is a hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. What I have is that he left it because Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari narrated it on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah.”"
"1810","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzaki told us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi, Abu Salih Mahboub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God have mercy on him. On his authority, he said: “A people never sat together and then dispersed before they remembered God and prayed for His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that it was upon them. Regret on the Day of Resurrection.” This does not explain the hadith of Suhail, as the addition from Suleiman bin Bilal and Ibn Abi Hazim is acceptable, and he narrated it. Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him."
"1811","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A people has never gathered and then dispersed without They mention the name of God as if they had dispersed, except for the carcass of a donkey.”"
"1812","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Qurashi told us, Al-Hasan bin Hammad Al-Dhabi, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Al-Zubayr Al-Hamdani told us, Jafar bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, On the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Supplication is the weapon of the believer, the pillar of religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth.” This is an authentic hadith, for this Muhammad ibn al-Hasan is the hill, or he is truthful in the Kufayyin.”"
"1813","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Abu Muslim informed us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Zakaria bin Manzur, a sheikh from the Ansar, said: Attaf bin Khaled told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Caution is no substitute for destiny, and supplication benefits from what has been sent down and what has not been sent down, and the affliction So that He may descend, and supplication will be received by them, and they will remain in peace until the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1814","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris al-Razi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Darabardi told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No Fate rejects nothing but supplication, and nothing increases one’s lifespan except righteousness, and a man is deprived of sustenance because of the sin that befalls him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1815","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr bin Abu Mulaika, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Supplication It benefits from what was revealed, and from what was not revealed, so you, servants of God, must pray.”"
"1816","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin al-Ja’d told us, Ali told me Bin Ali Al-Rifai, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Muhammad bin Yazid Abu Hisham, Ali bin Ali told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No Muslim He supplicates to God with a supplication in which there is no sin or severing ties of kinship, but He grants him one of three things: either He responds to his supplication, or He turns away. An evil like it will be removed from him, or a reward like it will be stored up for him.” They said: O Messenger of God, then we will increase. He said: “Allah is the Greatest.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, except that the two sheikhs did not narrate it on the authority of Ali bin Ali Al-Rifai’i."
"1817","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, and Musa bin Ismail told us, They said: Saleh Al-Marri narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. He said: “Call upon God while you are certain of the answer, and know that God does not accept a supplication from a heedless and distracted heart.” This is a straight hadith. The chain of transmission was narrated only by Salih al-Marri, who was one of the ascetics of the people of Basra, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1818","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Mu’alla bin Asad al-Ammi told us, Amr bin Muhammad told me Al-Islami, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Do not fail in supplication.” For no one perishes with supplication.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1819","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Yaqoub and Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa al-Adl informed me, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub told us, Abd told us. Al-Ala bin Hammad, Abu Asim Al-Abbadani told us, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Issa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him On their authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “God will call upon the believer on the Day of Resurrection until He makes him stand before Him and says: My servant, I have commanded you.” If you call upon Me and I promised you that I would respond to you, were you calling upon Me? He will say: Yes, Lord. Then He will say: You did not call upon Me with anything other than an invitation? I responded to you. Did you not call upon me on such-and-such a day of distress that befell you to release you, so I released you? Then he says: Yes, O Lord. Then he says: So I hastened it for you in this world, and you called on me on such-and-such day, a distress that befell you, to release you, but you did not see any relief. He said: Yes, O Lord. Then he says, “I have stored up for you such-and-such in Paradise.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God never abandons a supplication with which He called upon His believing servant without making it clear to him that it would be a haste for him in this world. Or it will be saved for him in the Hereafter. He said: Then the believer will say in that place, “If only he had not been hastened in any of his supplications.” This A hadith narrated alone by Al-Fadl bin Issa Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, and the place of Al-Fadl bin Issa is the place of one who is not under the illusion of fabrication.”"
"1820","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Omar told us Bin Abdullah, the freed slave of Ghafra, said: I heard Ayoub bin Khalid bin Safwan Al-Ansari, saying: Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: About them, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us and said: “O people, God has companies of angels that come and stand in the places of remembrance in Earth, so they grew up in the gardens of Paradise. They said: Where are the gardens of Paradise? He said: “Assemblies of remembrance, so go out in the morning in the remembrance of God, and remind Him yourselves. Whoever would like to know his status with God, let him look. How is God’s status with Him, for God brings down the servant from where He sent him down from himself. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1821","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan, the potter in Mecca, told me Ali al-Saffar. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us. Hajjaj ibn al-Aziz informed us. Al-Manhal, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Abu Amr Al-Dareer told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, that Suhail bin Abu Salih told them on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has angels.” traveling, and virtuous men seeking gatherings of remembrance on earth, and when they came to a gathering of remembrance, they would surround one another with their wings to Heaven, and God Almighty says: Where have you come from? And He knows best. They say: Our Lord, we have come from the presence of Your servants glorifying You and glorifying You. And they praise you, and praise you, and ask you and ask you for protection. He says: What are they asking me when I know best? They say: Our Lord, they ask you? Paradise. He says: And have they seen it? They say: No, O Lord. He says: How if they saw it? He says: Why do they seek protection from me when He knows best? They say: From the Fire. He says: Did they see it? They say: No. He says: What if they saw it? Then He says: They bear witness that I have forgiven. And I gave them what they asked of Me, and I rewarded them with what they asked me for. They say: Our Lord, there is a sinful servant among them who sat beside them and was not with them. He says: And I have forgiven him too. They are the people whose companions do not feel miserable about them. “This is an authentic hadith.” Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj was the only one to narrate it. A summary of the hadith of Wahib bin Khaled, on the authority of Suhail"
"1822","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, Amr told me Ibn Qais Al-Sakouni, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Busr, that a Bedouin said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The laws of Islam have become too much for me. So inform me of something that I can cling to. He said: “Your tongue continues to be moist from the remembrance of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1823","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Othman Al-Muqri in Baghdad told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yaqoub, the client of al-Harqa, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. He says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Mufarrids preceded.” They said: O Messenger of God, and what are the Mufarrids? He said: “Those who neglect the remembrance of God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1824","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, God says: I am with my servant.” When he mentioned me and his lips moved with me, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1825",""
"1826","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, and Abu Muslim told us, they said: Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Amara bin Ghaziyeh, on the authority of Salih, the guardian of the twins, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: Abu al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whenever a people sits and sits for a long time, then disperses before they mention God and pray for His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, it is not their duty.” From God once, if God wills, He will punish them, and if God wills, He will forgive them. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission. He did not narrate it, and it is valid and not false."
"1827","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not Then he got up from one sitting and said: “Glory be to You, O God, my Lord, and with Your praise. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.” So I said to him: O Messenger of God, how often you will say these words when you get up. He said: “No one says them when he gets up from his gathering without being forgiven for whatever he did in that gathering.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1828","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Asadi told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Subaih, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God Almighty said: My servant. When you think about me, and I am with you when you remind me, “The mention of suspicion is included in the authentic hadith, and the mention of supplication is strange and authentic, for Muhammad bin Al-Qasim is trustworthy, and in This chain of narration says: “Salih is a carrot.”"
"1829","Ibn Arkan told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Muhammad bin Yazid told us. Al-Rifa’i, Waki’ told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “There is no servant who turns his face to God Almighty in a matter except that God gives it to him: either to hasten it, or to “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1830","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Mahboub the merchant informed us of Marw, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Suleiman Al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Abu Othman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, said: “God is ashamed for the servant to extend His hands to Him to do good and return them.” Khayabatain” This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. It was transmitted by: Ja’far ibn Maimun, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi."
"1831","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ja’far bin Maimun told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Suleiman May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God is Ever-Living, Most Generous. He is ashamed of His servant to extend His hands to Him, then He will return them both disappointed.” He has evidence with an authentic chain of transmission from the hadith of Anas bin Malik."
"1832","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Bishr bin Al-Walid Al-Qadi told us, Amer bin Yasaf told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Omar bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha Al-Ansari said: Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, told me: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Indeed, God is Merciful, Ever-Living, and Generous. He is ashamed of His servant to raise his hands to Him, and then He does not put any good in them.”"
"1833","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr bin Abu Mulaika, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever opens In supplication from you, the gates of Paradise will be opened for him, and no servant will ask God for anything more beloved to him than asking for well-being.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1834","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani informed us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Musa bin Ibrahim bin Bashir bin told us. Kathir Al-Hazami, who said: I heard Talha bin Kharash, saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The best remembrance is ‘There is no god but God’, and the best supplication is ‘Praise be to God.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1835","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Muzaki informed us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Imran bin Ayyub bin Miqlas told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Omar bin Rashid told us, and Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ishaq and Abu Bakr Ibn Balawayh said: Muhammad Ibn Ghalib told us, Abd al-Samad told us, Omar Ibn Rashid told us, Iyas Ibn Salamah Ibn Al-Akwa’, on the authority of Salama bin Al-Akwa’, who said: “I have never heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, begin a supplication unless he opened it with: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. Al-A’la Al-Wahhab “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1836","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Halimi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, Yahya informed me Ibn Hassan narrates, on the authority of Rabi’ah Ibn Amir, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Adorn me, Possessor of majesty and honor.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1837","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us, Khalaf bin Salman al-Nasafi told us, Muhammad bin al-Mutawakkil al-Asqalani told us, Rishdin bin Saad told us, Musa bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he greeted me: “Shine upon Me, Possessor of majesty and honor.”"
"1838","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Kharijah informed us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said To them: “Do you people like to strive hard in supplication?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Say: O God, help me to remember You, to thank You, and to worship You well.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. Except for his narration on the authority of unknown people, and if he narrates on the authority of proven trustworthy people, then his narration is accepted.”"
"1839","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Sa’id bin Kathir told us, and Asbagh bin relief, and Abdullah bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ahmad bin Issa told us, and Muhammad bin Salih told us, Muhammad bin Ismail, Abu Al-Tahir narrated to us, they said: Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that a biker, Abul-Samh, told him, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Increasingly mention God until they say he is crazy.” This A newspaper for the Egyptians with an authentic chain of narration, and Abu al-Haytham Suleiman bin Utba al-Awari is one of the trustworthy people of Egypt.”"
"1840","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ali Al-Abar told us, Hisham bin Khalid Al-Azraq told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When a matter comes to him that pleases him, he says: “Praise be to God, by whose grace good deeds are accomplished.” And if a matter comes to him that he dislikes, he says: “Praise be to God in every condition.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1841","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Sakan told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Ubayy told us, Musa bin Salim told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Those who remember God for the sake of glorification, glorification, greatness, and joy, sympathize around the Throne, there will be a sound like the sound of bees, saying: To their owner: “Doesn’t any of you like to have something with the Most Gracious that reminds him of him?” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1842","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmed told us Ibn Tamim Al-Qantari, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Amr Ismail bin Najid Al-Sulami told us, Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh, they said: Abu Muslim told us, they said: Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Abd told us. Al-Hamid bin Jafar, Saleh bin Abi Urayb narrated to me, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever’s last words are: There is no god but God, he will enter Paradise.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it has a story by my father. Al-Razi’s planting was mentioned in the Book of Knowledge.”"
"1843","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation in the month of Ramadan in the year three hundred and ninety-six. He reported Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Al-Sammak in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Sahl bin Hammad told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal and Abu Zafar told us, They said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit and Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever says a hundred times in a day: ‘There is no god but God alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is over everything. Something powerful and unsurpassed by anyone before him, and no one after him can comprehend it except those who did better than his work.” I heard Professor Aba Al-Walid Al-Qurashi, saying: I heard Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, saying: I heard Ishaq bin Ibrahim, saying: If the narrator, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib is trustworthy. He is like Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar. Al-Hakim said: “I did not bring out from the beginning of the book a narration of Amr to this place.” Ibn Shuaib, and I mentioned at the beginning of the book of Supplication and Praise the doctrine of Imam Abu Saeed Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi regarding forgiveness in the chains of transmission. The virtues of deeds"
"1844","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, about Rashid bin Dawood, on the authority of Ya’la bin Shaddad, he said: Abu Shaddad bin Aws told me, and Ubadah bin Al-Samit, who was present and believed him, said: We are with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is there a stranger among you?” Meaning the People of the Book, we said: No, O Messenger of God, so he ordered the door to be closed, and he said: “Raise your hands and say there is no god but God,” so we raised We held hands for an hour, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lowered his hand and said: “Praise be to God, O God, you have sent me this word. And you commanded me to do it, and you promised me Paradise for it. You do not break your promise.” Then he said: “Rejoice, for God has forgiven you.” Al-Hakim said: “The situation is Ismail bin Ayyash is close to the hadith before this, as he is one of the imams of the people of the Levant, and he was attributed to having poor memorization, and I am on my condition. In people like him”"
"1845","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Al-Hasan bin Atiya told us, Muhammad bin Talha bin Musarrif told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever says: No There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion, to Him is praise, and He is Able to do all things ten times, so it is like freeing a soul. “This is a hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1846","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Ismail bin Aliya, Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri, Hayy Min Anza, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr Radi On his authority, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my mother and father, which words do I love most to God? He said: “What God has chosen for His angels: Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him, Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1847","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nasr al-Khalidi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin al-Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God Almighty, it will be planted for him A palm tree in Paradise “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1848","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Ziyad bin Khalil al-Tustari, and Muhammad bin Ayyub al-Bajli informed us, And Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari, and Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi, they said: Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi Al-Taymi told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Hammad, Hafs bin Sulaiman told us, Talha bin Yahya bin Talha told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaid Allah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding the interpretation of “Glory be to God,” he said: “It is God’s purification from all evil.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1849","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir and Saeed bin Amir told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Ubaidah speaking, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to often say: “Glory be to You, O God. And with Your praise, O God, forgive me.” When the verse “When God’s victory and conquest has come” was revealed [Al-Nasr: 1] he said: “Glory be to You, O God, O God, forgive me. “You are the Wahab.” This is an authentic chain of narration if Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Masoud heard it from his father, and they did not narrate it."
"1850","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Abdul Wahid told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Ibrahim bin Othman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “Whoever says: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, and there is no power nor strength except in God, God said: My servant submitted to Islam and surrendered. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1851","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Qanabi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Qarad Abu Nuh told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abdullah told us. Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “The first to be called to Paradise are those who thank God in good times and in bad.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1852","Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, Musa bin Ibrahim bin Kathir Al-Ansari Al-Madani said: I heard Talha bin Kharash saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The best remembrance is: There is no god but God, and the best supplication is: Praise be to God.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1853","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Abdul Aziz bin Muawiyah Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, that he told him that he heard Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. About them, he says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not a man on earth who says: There is no god but God, and God is great, and Glory be to God. Praise be to God, and there is no power nor strength except with God except that his sins will be expiated from him, even if they are more than the foam of the sea.” Narrated by Shu'bah, on the authority of Abu Balj, Yahya bin Abi Sulaym, so he stopped him"
"1854","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad told us Al-Qanabi, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, that he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God, and God is great, and praise be to God, Glory be to God greatly, and there is no power nor strength except in God. His sins have been forgiven, even if they were more than the foam of the sea.” Hadith Hatim bin"
"1855","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Issa Musa bin Issa Al-Saghir, Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utba told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Al-Numan bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Part of the majesty of God among the things they mention are glorification, praise, and applaud. The throne makes a sound like the sound of bees, reminding them of their companion. Wouldn’t any of you like to have in the presence of God someone to remind him of? This is a hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. He used Musa the reciter as evidence, and he was this son of Jesus.”"
"1856",""
"1857","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Iyad bin Abdullah Al-Fihri told me, about Ibrahim bin Ubaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man say: Oh God, I ask you Indeed, to You is praise, there is no god but You, You are the Benefactor, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honor. I ask You for Paradise, and I seek refuge in With you from the Fire, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He almost called upon God by His name, by which He answered, and when asked, He gave.”"
"1858","Ahmad ibn Kamil ibn Khalaf al-Qadi told us, Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq told us, Malik ibn Mughal told us, and Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Suleiman told us, Saeed bin Amr Al-Ash’athi told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man saying: Oh God, I I ask You that there is no god but You, the One and Only, the Eternal, the One who did not beget nor was born, and there is no one equal to Him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “He has called upon God by His greatest name, by which He gives, when asked, and answers.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And he did not narrate it, and he has a valid witness according to Muslim’s condition.”"
"1859","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabbah told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, Sharik reported, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man saying: Oh God, I ask you That you are one of the steadfast, who did not give birth, nor was he born, and there was no one equal to him, so he said: “He has asked God in His name, the greatest and greatest, who when He is called upon with it, he responds, and when asked with it, he gives.”"
"1860","Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Fasawi told us, Ya`qub bin Sufyan al-Fasawi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Sa`id bin Abi Ayoub told us, On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Thawban, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Ruqayyah, that Abu Al-Darda’ and Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Indeed, the name of God “The greatest, Lord, Lord.”"
"1861","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ala told us, he said: I heard Al-Qasim speaking, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The greatest name of God is in three surahs of the Qur’an, in Surah Al-Baqarah, the family of Imran, and Taha.” Al-Qasim said: “So I sought it. Indeed, He is the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting.”"
"1862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, dictating, Ali bin Maymun Al-Ruqi told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplication of Dhul-Nun when he supplicated while he was in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers. Indeed, no Muslim has supplicated with it in anything.” “Allah never responded to him with it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated on the authority of Al-Faryabi, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq as well, “and it is an illusion on the part of the narrator.”"
"1863","Abu Amr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Ishaq Al-Adl told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jurabah Al-Razi told us, Omar bin Al-Khattab Al-Ahwazi, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The call of Dhul-Nun when He supplicated while he was in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers. No Muslim man ever supplicates with it about anything except that God responds. ""His"""
"1864","So Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ibn Abi Al-Dunya told me, Ubaid bin Muhammad told me, Muhammad bin Muhajir Al-Qurashi told me, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Shall I not inform you of something when a man descends? Is there any of you suffering from distress, or some affliction from the afflictions of this world that he prayed for relief from? It was said to him: Yes, and he said: “The supplication of Dhul-Nun: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.”"
"1865","Al-Zubair bin Abdul-Wahid Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Qutayba Al-Asqalani told us, Ahmad bin Amr bin Bakr Al-Saskini told us, My father told me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Shall I direct you to the greatest name of God, by which He answers, and when asked, He gives?” The call with which Yunus called when he called to him in the three darknesses: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, was it for Yunus in particular or for believers in general? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you not hear the words of God Almighty: {And We saved him from distress, and thus do We save the believers} [Al-Anbiya’: 88]”"
"1866","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Ammar bin Nasr told me, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, Abdullah told me Ibn Al-Alaa Ibn Zubr, Al-Qasim Ibn Abdul-Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The name of God The greatest of three surahs of the Qur’an: in Surat Al-Baqarah, Al Imran, and Taha. “So I searched for it and found in Surat Al-Baqarah the verse of the Throne: {Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} [Al-Baqarah: 255], and in Surat Al Imran: {Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} [Al-Imran: 2], and in Surah Taha: {And faces are devoted to the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} [Taha: 111]"
"1867","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Mahdi Al-Attar told us, in Fustat, ثنا عَمْرُو بْنُ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ، ثنا ابْنُ زَبْرٍ وَهُوَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنِ الْعَلَاءِ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ الْقَاسِمَ أَبَا عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، يَقُولُ: سَمِعْتُ أَبَا Umamah, may God be pleased with him, narrates, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, the greatest name of God is contained in three surahs of the Qur’an.” Then Jesus bin Musa said to him: And I was listening, O Abu Zubr, I heard Ghaylan bin Anas, saying: I heard Al-Qasim Abu Abdul Rahman, saying: I heard Abu Umamah speaking, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, the greatest name of God is contained in three surahs.” Then he mentioned a similar hadith of Amr ibn Abi Salamah, “This does not explain the hadith Al-Walid bin Muslim, for Al-Walid memorized, mastered, and was most knowledgeable of the hadith of his country, even though the two sheikhs did not use Al-Qasim Abi Abd as evidence. “The Most Gracious”"
"1868","Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Ibn Abi Masarra told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ayman told us Al-Makki, on the authority of Ubaid bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, said: It was on the day of Uhud that the polytheists retreated, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Stand straight until I praise my Lord,” so they formed ranks behind him, and he said: “O God, all praise is due to You. what You have taken away, and there is no guide for whom You have led astray, nor a misguider for whom You have guided, nor any giver for what You have withheld, nor any deterrence for what You have given, nor a bringer of what You have sent away, and no far away from what You have brought near. Oh God, extend upon us your blessings, your mercy, your grace, and your provision. Oh God, I ask you for bliss on the Day of Resurrection. And security is the day of fear. O God, we seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us and the evil of what You have withheld from us. O God, make faith beloved to us and beautify it in our hearts. And make us hate disbelief, immorality, and disobedience, and make us among the rightly guided. O God, let us die as Muslims, and give us life as Muslims, and grant us With the righteous, not disgraced, nor tempted. O God, kill the infidels who deny Your messengers and turn away from Your path, and bestow upon them “Your punishment and your torment are the God of Truth.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1869","Ali bin Abdul Rahman bin Mati told us, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hakam Al-Habari told us, Qubaisa told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “A time will come upon you in which only those who pray Al-Ghariq “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1870","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, with Marwa, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Abu Abdul-Rahman Abdullah bin The reciter adds, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of His father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever eats food and says: Praise be to God who fed me this, and provided it for me without any help from me or Power, his previous sins will be forgiven, and whoever wears a garment and says: Praise be to God who has covered me in this without any help on my part, and whoever wears a garment and says: Praise be to God who has covered me in this without any help on my part, will be forgiven. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari.”"
"1871","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Salih bin Muhammad Al-Razi informed us, Ubayy informed us, Abu Muawiyah Abd al-Rahman bin Qays informed us, Muhammad informed us. Ibn Abi Humaid, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What a blessing God has bestowed upon me.” A servant who received a blessing and said: Praise be to God, except that he thanked her for it. If he said it the second time, God renewed his reward for him. If he said it the third time. May God forgive him his sins. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, except that they did not narrate Abu Muawiyah.”"
"1872","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim Al-Yamami told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar, who said: I heard Shaddad Abu Ammar narrating, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, may God be pleased with him, who was Badriya, he said: While they were on a journey, when he descended The people were getting up in the morning, and Shaddad said: Come near this street, we will be fooling around. Then he said: I ask forgiveness from God. I have not spoken a word since I embraced Islam except And I pressed her, and said to her before saying this, that is not the case. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But he said: O Shaddad, when you see the people They hoard up gold and silver, so hoard up these words: Oh God, I ask You for steadfastness in matters, and the determination to guide people, and I ask You Thank you for your blessings, and for your good worship, and I ask you for a sound heart, a sincere tongue, and upright character, and I ask you for forgiveness for what you know, and I ask you From the best of what you know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what you know. Indeed, you are the Knower of the Unseen. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1873","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with them, he said: He taught me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when distress befalls me, I must say: “There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, and blessed be God, Lord of the Throne.” The Great, and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it due to a disagreement over it among the transmitters. “And this is how he established Its chain of transmission: Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b"
"1874","Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahan Al-Khazar in Mecca told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid told us, Sa’id bin Mansour told us, Ya’qub told us Bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of Ali May God be pleased with them. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me these words when I was experiencing distress or distress, to say them: “No.” There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, Glory be to Him, Glory be to Him, Blessed be God, Lord of the Great Throne, and praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds.” He said: “And it was Abdullah Ibn Ja`far taught it to the dead, and breathed it on the sick.” Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated this hadith abbreviated from the hadith of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both"
"1875","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim, the governor of Kufa, told us, Ahmad bin Musa told us, Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Waddah bin Yahya Al-Nahshali told us, Al-Nadr bin Ismail Al-Bajli told us, Abdul-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: Whenever distress or distress befell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would say: “O Living, O Sustaining, by Your mercy I seek help.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1876","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani informed us, Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ismail told us Ibn Abi Fudaik, Saad bin Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger said:"
"1877","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Sulayman Al-Wasiti told us, Fudayl bin Marzuq, Abu Salamah Al-Juhani told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Never has a Muslim been afflicted with worry or sadness and said: Oh God, I am your servant and the son of your nation. My forelock is in Your hand continues to carry out your judgement, justice in your decree, I ask you by every name that is yours by which you have named yourself, or which you have revealed in your book, or which you have taught. No one of Your creation, or whom You have influenced in Your knowledge of the unseen, that You make the Qur’an the spring of my heart, the remover of my sorrow, and the remover of my anxiety. God took away his worry and replaced his place of sadness with joy. They said: O Messenger of God, should we not learn these words? He said: “Yes, whoever hears them should learn them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, if he is safe from the transmission of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd. God, from his father, for he is different in his hearing from his father.”"
"1878","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Khalil Al-Asbahani told me, Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Qazwini told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Sabiq told us, Amr told us Ibn Abi Qais, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Amara, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray and say: “O God, satisfy me with what You have bestowed upon me, bless me in it, and grant goodness to every thing that is absent from me.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1879","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid told me that Suleiman bin Musa He told him, on the authority of Makhul, that he entered upon Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, and said: I heard him mentioning that the Messenger of God was saying: “Oh God “Benefit me with what you have taught me, and teach me what will benefit me, and provide me with knowledge by which you will benefit me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1880","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, on the authority of his father, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before he converted to Islam, and when he wanted To leave, he said: What should I say? He said: “Say: O God, protect me from the evil of my soul, and guide me to guide my affairs.” He said it, then he left, and did not convert to Islam. Then he converted to Islam and said: O Messenger of God. What should I say now that I have converted to Islam? He said: “Say: O God, protect me from the evil of my soul, and guide me to guide my affairs. O God, forgive me what I have done secretly and what I have declared, what I have done wrong and what I have done intentionally. And I did not know and I was not ignorant. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1881","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Shu’bah told us, Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Al-Mughirah, or Al-Mughira, Abu Al-Walid narrating, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. I am a man with a soft tongue, and this has spread to my family. He said: “So where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? I ask forgiveness from God every day and night or night, or a hundred times a day.” Al-Hakim said: “This is Ubaid Abu Al-Mughirah.” Without a doubt, Shu’bah brought the chain of transmission and the text with doubt, and Sufyan bin Saeed preserved it, so I have no doubt about it in the chain of transmission and the text.”"
"1882","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Salam told us, Qubaisah told us, Sufyan told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid, my father Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: I used to lash out at my family. I said, O Messenger of God, I was afraid that my tongue would put me into Hell. He said: “So where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? I ask forgiveness from God a hundred times a day.” Abu Ishaq said: I mentioned that to Abu Burdah, and he said: “And I repent.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”
 Muslim narrated the hadith of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Al-Aghar Al-Muzani, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, my heart is oppressed, and I “I seek forgiveness from God a hundred times a day.” Likewise, a beneficial hadith, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both: “If we are to prepare for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “Peace be upon him”"
"1883","Mukarram bin Ahmad al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba al-Raqqashi told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, my father told me, on the authority of Hussein al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, I I ask Your forgiveness for what I have put forward and what I have delayed, and for what I have announced and what I have concealed. You are the one who brings forward, and you are the one who delays, and you are capable of all things.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1884","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says: I ask forgiveness from God Almighty, who does not There is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting, and to Him I repent three times. His sins are forgiven, even if he is fleeing from the advance. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”"
"1885","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Sulaiman bin Ahmed Al-Wasiti told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Abu Salam al-Aswad told me, Abu Salma, the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, and I met him in Kufa Mosque. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Great, great, with five that are heaviest on the scale: Glory be to God, and praise be to God.” To God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, and a righteous son dies to a Muslim, so he considers it “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1886",""
"1887","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Sawda, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by it while he was planting He planted a plant, and he said: “What are you doing, Abu Hurairah?” He said: Plant a tree. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not direct you to a planting that is better for you than that?” I said: What is it? He said: “Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great. He will plant a tree for you with every one of them.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.” And there is evidence for it on the authority of Jabir"
"1888","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God Almighty, it will be planted for him A palm tree in Paradise.”"
"1889","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi and Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydlani told us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ayyub told us. Al-Bajli, Ahmed bin Issa Al-Masry told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Make abundant of the righteous deeds that remain.” It was said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “The religion.” It was said: What is it? He said: “Allahu akbar, tahlil, glorification, and praise, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah.” This is the most correct chain of transmission of the Egyptians, so they did not narrate it. """
"1890","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Abdul Aziz told us Al-Rahman bin Abi Al-Rijal, Suhail bin Abi Saleh told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says “Allahu Akbar” once, twenty will be recorded for him and twenty will be erased from him, and whoever says “Allahu Akbar” once, twenty will be written for him and twenty will be erased from him, and whoever says “Allahu Akbar” once, twenty will be written for him and twenty will be erased from him. “He praised one woman, thirty were recorded for him and thirty were erased from him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1891","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Husayn, On the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, who said: Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, told us, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There is no servant who said: Praise be to God, according to the number of what God created, and praise be to God, who filled what God created, and praise be to God, according to the number of what is in the heavens and the earth, and praise be to God, according to the number of He counted his book, and praise be to God, he counted everything, and Glory be to God like them. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, glorified that “this An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1892","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Amr bin Awn Al-Wasiti told us, Hushaym told us, he informed us Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Amr bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: Give me some words to say in the morning, and in the evening, and he said: “Say: O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself, and the evil of Satan and his polytheism.” So he said: “Say it then.” “In the morning, and in the evening, and when you go to bed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1893","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim Al-Adl told us, my father told us, Ibrahim bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, Zakaria bin Manzur told us, Muhammad bin Uqba, on the authority of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, may God be pleased with her, said: I said: O Prophet of God, I am a woman who has grown old and weak, so guide me to He did so, saying: “Glorify God a hundred times, praise God a hundred times, and glorify God a hundred times, for it is better for you than a hundred obligatory sacrifices. And it is better than a hundred horses saddled and bridled for the sake of God, and better than a hundred slaves that are slaughtered, and saying: There is no god but God, and He does not leave a sin behind. “And no work is similar to it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and Zakaria bin Manzur did not narrate it."
"1894","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ziyad bin Al-Khalil Al-Tustari told us, Muhammad bin Jami’ Al-Attar told us, Al-Sakan bin Abi Al-Sakan told us Al-Burjami, Al-Walid bin Abi Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “God has not bestowed upon a servant a blessing and he knew that it was from God except that God recorded for him its gratitude before he thanked him for it, and He does not If a servant commits a sin and regrets it, God will write down forgiveness for him before he asks for his forgiveness. And no servant will buy a garment for a dinar, or half a dinar. A dinar, so he put it on and thanked God for it, but it did not reach his knees until God would forgive him.” This is a hadith in which I do not know of anyone who mentioned it. with a wound, and they did not remove it.”"
"1895","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Darbardi told us about Marw, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Isa al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, who said: I heard Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “There is no servant who says in the morning of every day and the evening of every night: In the name of God, with whose name nothing is harmed.” Earth, nor in the heaven, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, three times, and something would harm him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1896","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Musaddad told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Tha’labah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: O God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me.” And I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from everything that I have done, and I confess my sins, so forgive me my sins, for there is no He forgives sins except you, so he died from that day and night and entered Paradise. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not take him out.”"
"1897","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf bin Sufyan Al-Tai told us, Abu Al-Mughirah Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Abu Al-Mughirah told us Bakr bin Abi Maryam, Al-Ahwas bin Hakim bin Umair, and Habib bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Let not a man among you give up doing a thousand good deeds until he says in the morning: Glory be to God and praise be to Him a hundred times, for it is a thousand times.” good deeds, and he did not, God willing, do anything like that on his day of sins, and whatever good he did other than that will be plentiful. “This hadith The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1898","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Muslim told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Omar Al-Numayri, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Yazid Al-Ayli, Al-Hakam Ibn Abdullah Al-Ayli narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: Abu Bakr came to me and said: “Did you hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a supplication that he taught me?” I said: What is it? He said: “Jesus, son of Mary, was teaching his companions. He said: If one of you had a mountain of gold as a debt, and he prayed to God for that, God would pay it off for him: Oh God, the reliever of worry, the remover of grief, the answerer to the prayers of the distressed, the Most Compassionate and Merciful of this world and the hereafter, you have mercy on me, so have mercy on me. You make me free of the mercy of anyone but you.” Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said: I had a remaining debt, and I hated religion, so I was praying for that, so God came to me. With the benefit that God granted me, Aisha said: “Asma’ bint Umays Ali had a dinar and three dirhams, and she used to come to me and I would feel ashamed.” To look at her face because I could not find anything to satisfy her, so I was praying for that, and I only stayed for a little while until God granted me a provision that was With the charity that you gave me as alms, and without any inheritance that I inherited, God settled it on my behalf, and I swore a good oath among my family, and I granted Abd al-Rahman’s daughter three A number of papers and a good bounty for us.” Al-Bukhari cited Abdullah bin Omar al-Numayri as evidence, and this is an authentic hadith, except that they did not use it as evidence. “By Al-Hakam bin Abdullah Al-Aili”"
"1899","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, and Muhammad bin Ayyub Al-Bajli told us, saying: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us Al-Absi, Fudayl bin Sulaiman Al-Numayri told us, Musa bin Uqba told us, Ubaid Allah bin Salman Al-Aghar told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Everything that the son of Adam speaks, it is written upon him. If he commits a sin, he would like to repent.” God, let his exalted one come, and let him extend his hands to God Almighty, then say: Oh God, I repent to you for it and never return to it, for it is He will be forgiven as long as he does not go back on that work. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1900","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa bin Yunus informed us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam Al-Ghassani, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He taught him and ordered him to make a pledge to his family every morning: “At your command, O God, at your command, and your happiness, and goodness in your hands and from you and to you, O God, what Whatever I said, whatever I swore, or made any vow, Your will is in My hands over all of that. Whatever You wished may be, and whatever You did not wish may not be, nor will it be. There is no power nor strength except in You. Indeed, You are capable of all things. Oh God, whatever blessings I have bestowed upon whomever You have bestowed, and whatever curses You have cursed upon whomever you have cursed, You My guardian in this world and the hereafter, make me die a Muslim, and join me with the righteous. O God, I ask You for contentment after judgment, and a pleasant life after Death, the pleasure of looking at your face, and longing to meet you without harmful hardship or misleading temptation, and I seek refuge in You from being unjust or I am wronged, or I am transgressing, or I am being assaulted, or I commit a sin, or a sin that you will not forgive, O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the Unseen. And martyrdom is of majesty and honor, for I entrust you in this world, and I call you as witness, and it is sufficient for you as a witness that I bear witness that no There is no god but You, You are the One, You have no partner, Yours is the dominion, Yours is praise, and You are capable of all things, and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. And I bear witness that your promise is true, and your meeting is true, and that the Hour is coming about which there is no doubt, and that you will raise those from the graves, and that if you entrust me to My soul, you leave me to weakness, shame, guilt, and sin, and I only trust in your mercy, so forgive me all my sins, for He does not forgive Sins except You, and accept my repentance. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1901","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Kumail bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: We were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in some of the walls of the city, and he said: “O Abu Kitten.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “Indeed, the many are the few, except for the one who says such and such with his money,” and he gestured with his hand to his right and to his left, and a few What are they?
 Then he said: “O Abu Hurairah, shall I not guide you to one of the treasures of Paradise?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “You say, ‘There is no power nor strength except in God, and there is no refuge, and there is no refuge from God except in Him.’”
 Then he said: “O Abu Hurairah, do you know what the right of God is upon His servants, and what is the right of His servants upon God?” He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “The right of God upon His servants is that they should worship Him and not associate anything with Him, and the right of His servants upon God is that He should not punish those who do not associate anything with Him.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this.”"
"1902","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubadah bin Muslim al-Fazari, He said: Jubayr bin Abi Sulayman bin Jubayr bin Mutim told me, he said: I heard Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not He, peace and blessings be upon him, recited these words in the morning and in the evening: “O God, I ask you for forgiveness and well-being in my religion, my world, and my family.” And my money, O God, cover my private parts, and secure my beauty, O God, protect me from before me, and from behind me, and from my right, and from my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge By Your greatness, lest I be assassinated from under me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1903","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Muhammad bin Abi Humaid Al-Madani told us, On the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Part of the happiness of the son of Adam is his asking God for guidance, and part of the misery of the son of Adam is his neglecting to ask God for advice.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1904","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, Abu Hani al-Tajibi narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Ali al-Janabi, saying: I heard Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever says: I am satisfied with God as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad as my Messenger, Paradise is certain for him.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1905","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us, Ali bin Ibrahim Al-Wasiti told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Hamdan Al-Zahid, they said: Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu`bah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Aqeel Hashim bin Bilal speaking, on the authority of Abu Salam Sabiq bin Najiya, who said: We were sitting in the mosque of Homs, and he passed by. A man. They said: This served the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I got up to him and asked him. I said, “Tell me a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” The men did not circulate with him among you. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no servant who says: When the evening comes and when the morning comes, I am satisfied.” By God as Lord, by Islam as religion, and by Muhammad as prophet, it is a duty upon God that He should please Him on the Day of Resurrection. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1906","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid al-Hafiz in Hamadan told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Abu al-Nasr Omar bin Muhammad al-Nasri told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Who He said a hundred times in the morning, and a hundred times in the evening: Glory be to God and by His praise, his sins have been forgiven, even if they were more than butter. Al-Bahr: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1907","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, dictating and reading, Harun bin Suleiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would leave his house, he would say: “In the name of “Allah, my Lord, I seek refuge in You lest I slip, or go astray, or be wronged, or be wronged, or be ignorant, or be ignorant of me.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and perhaps someone delusional imagined that Ash-Sha’bi had not heard from Umm Salamah, and that is not the case, as he entered upon Aisha and Umm He greeted them all, then he narrated more about them all.”"
"1908","Abu Qutayba Salem bin Al-Fadl Al-Aadmi told us in Mecca, Muhammad bin Nasr bin Mansour Al-Sayegh told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Hatim told us Bin Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hussein, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: When he left his house, he would say: “In the name of God, there is no power nor strength except in God. “Putting your trust in God” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1909","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Uthman bin Amr told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abd told us Allah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far al-Madani, he said: I heard Amara bin Khuzaymah, narrating, on the authority of Uthman bin Hunaif, may God be pleased with him, that a blind man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: Pray to God Almighty to He will heal me. He said: “If you want, I can delay that, and if you want, I can invite.” He said: So invite him. He said: “So he ordered him to perform ablution, perform the ablution well, pray two rak’ahs, and say this supplication: O God, I ask you, and I turn to you.” Through your Prophet Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the Prophet of mercy, O Muhammad, I turn to your Lord through you regarding this need of mine, and you fulfill it for me. Oh God, intercede for him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1910","Abdullah bin Ja`far bin Darastuwaih the Persian told us, Ya`qub bin Sufyan told us, Qabisah told us, and Muhammad bin Kathir told us, they said: Sufyan told us, On the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Taliq ibn Qais, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: It was part of the Prophet’s supplication May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “My Lord, help me and do not help me, help me and do not help me, plot for me and do not plot against me, guide me and facilitate guidance for me. And grant me victory over him who transgresses against me. My Lord, make me thankful to you, remembering you, fearing you, obedient to you, hiding before you, merciful and repenting. Accept my repentance, respond to my supplication, guide my heart, confirm my proof, direct my tongue, and ease the generosity of my heart.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”"
"1911","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Isbahani told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Isbahani told me, we told him Mahrez bin Salamah Al-Adani, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, this is what Muhammad asked his Lord: “O God, I ask you for the best of matters. The best of supplication, the best of success, the best of work, the best of reward, the best of life, and the best of death. Make me steadfast and heavy on my scales, confirm my faith, and raise My degrees, accept my prayers, forgive my sins, and I ask You for the highest degrees of Paradise. Oh God, I ask You for the beginnings and endings of goodness. And its components, its beginning, its exterior and its interior, and the highest levels of Paradise. Amen, O God, I ask You for the best of what I come to, and the best of what I do. The best of what I do, the best of what is hidden, the best of what is apparent, and the highest levels of Paradise. Amen. Oh God, I ask you to raise my remembrance and humble it. Protect me, set right my affairs, purify my heart, guard my chastity, enlighten my heart, and forgive my sins, and I ask You for the highest levels of Paradise. Amen, Oh God, I ask you to bless me in myself, in my hearing, in my sight, in my spirit, in my creation, in my creation, in my family, and in In my life, and in my death, and in my work, so accept my good deeds, and I ask you for the highest levels of Paradise, Amen.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1912","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, Abdul-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Khaled bin Al-Lajlaj told us, Abdul-Rahman bin Ayish Al-Hadrami told us, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said, “And he mentioned the Lord, Blessed and Most High, and said: “Say: Oh God, I ask of you the good things, to abandon the evil, and to love the poor, and to repent. upon me, and forgive me, and have mercy on me, and if you wish to cause temptation among a people, cause me to die without being tempted.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then teach them. “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they are the truth.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. It was narrated on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1913","Abu Hafs Omar bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Suwayd al-Qurashi told us, In Kufa, my father told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, May God be pleased with him. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delayed the dawn prayer for us until the sun almost overtook us, then he went out and prayed.” With us, he eased his prayer, then he left and turned to us with his face, and said: “Where you are, I will tell you what made me slow you down today in This is the prayer. I prayed this night as much as God willed, then my eyes took possession of me, so I fell asleep and saw my Lord, Blessed and Most High, and He inspired me to say: Oh God, I ask you to do good things, to abandon evil deeds, and to love the poor, and to repent for me, forgive me, and have mercy on me, and if you wish to do so with your creation temptation, so deliver me from it without being tempted. Oh God, I ask you for your love, and the love of whoever loves you, and the love of an action that will bring me closer to your love.” Then he accepted The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is upon us, and he said: “Learn them and study them, for they are true.”"
"1914","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu told us Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Hallab, and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i, said: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, tell me Ubayy, Muhammad ibn Ja`far told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Habib, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq May God be pleased with him. He went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and spoke to him about something he was hiding from Aisha while Aisha was praying, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he greeted him: “O Aisha, upon you be perfect,” or another word. When Aisha left, she asked him about that, and he said to her: “Say: Oh God, I I ask you for all good, both now and in the future, what I know of and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, present and future, what I know of. And unless I know, and I ask you for Paradise and whatever words or deeds bring me closer to it, and I seek refuge in You from Hell and whatever words or deeds bring me closer to it, And I ask You for the best of what Your servant and Messenger Muhammad asked You, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your servant and Messenger Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, sought refuge in You. Peace be upon him, and I ask you, whatever matter you have decreed for me, that you make its outcome righteousness. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1915","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Khurasani told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Uthman bin Amr told us, Abu Naama Al-Adawi told Amr Bin Issa, Jubayr bin Habib told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and something similar. “This is what Abu Naama said, and Shu’bah is better at heart than him, and if he disagrees with him, then the statement is Shu’bah’s saying.”"
"1916","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Harun bin Ma’rouf told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed told us Wahb, Huyay bin Abdullah reported, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray and say: “O God, forgive us our sins and our injustice, our negligence, our transgression, our baptism, and all of that.” We have: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1917","Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Al-Warraq told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Sunayd bin Dawud told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Gabriel, peace be upon him, said: “God commands you to invoke these words, for He has given you one of them: Oh God, I ask you to hasten Your well-being, and patience in your affliction, or an exit from this world to your mercy. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1918","Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulayman told us, Al-Alaa bin Amr Al-Hanafi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: It was from the supplication of the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O God, grant me pleasure with my hearing and my sight, and make them my heirs, and grant me victory over those who wronged me, and show me my vengeance therein.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1919","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hujayra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, advised Salman to do good, and said: “O Salman, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wants to give you words. You ask them for the Most Gracious, and you desire for them, and you pray for them day and night, say: O God, I ask you for health in faith, and faith in Good character and success will be followed by success and mercy from You, well-being, forgiveness and satisfaction from You. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1920","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Abdullah Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Hajri told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Humaid bin Mahran told us, Ataa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: Salman Al-Farisi told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says, O God, I I call you to witness, and I call to witness your angels and the bearers of your throne, and I call to witness all who are in the heavens and all who are on earth, that you are God, and there is no god but You alone. You have no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is your servant and your messenger. Whoever says it once, God will free a third of him from Hell, and whoever says it twice, God will free him. Two-thirds of it is from the Fire, and whoever says it three times, God will free all of it from the Fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1921","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Al-Walid told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abd told us Allah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by me while I was praying, and he said: “Ask and it will be given to you, O son of Umm Abd.” So Omar said: So Abu Bakr and I hastened to him, but Abu Bakr preceded me to him and said: “One of my supplications that I can hardly pray is: O God, I ask you for a blessing beyond He will be exterminated, and the apple of an eye will never run out, and the accompaniment of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the highest Garden of eternity. sending, and they did not bring it out.”"
"1922","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria told us, Mahrez bin Salamah told us. Al-Adani, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to pray with these words: “O God, You are the First and there is nothing before You, and You are the Last and there is nothing after You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every living creature that enters your hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, from the torment of the grave, from the temptation of wealth, and from The temptation of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from sin and debt. Oh God, purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from filth. Oh God. Distance between me and my sin as you distanced between the East and the West.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1923","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ammar ibn Yasir, may God be pleased with him, that he prayed with his companions, and what prayer was summarized in it, so it was said to him: O Abu Al-Yaqzan, you have calmed down. He said: “I do not have to do that. I have made supplications in it with supplications that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: Then a man got up and he, Abu Ata, followed him and asked him about the supplication. Then he came back and told: “O God, by Your knowledge of the unseen, and Your ability to create.” Keep me alive as long as You know that life is good for me, and give me death if death is good for me. O God, I ask You to fear You in the unseen and the witnessed. And I ask you for a word of wisdom in anger and contentment, and I ask you for purpose in wealth and poverty, and I ask you for a bliss that does not fade away, and I ask you The apple of an eye that never runs out or ceases, and I ask you for contentment after the decree is made up, and I ask you for the joy of life after death, and I ask you to look at The pleasure of Your face, and I ask You for the longing to meet You without harmful adversity or misleading temptation. O God, adorn us with the adornment of faith, and make us “Guide us, we will be guided.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"1924","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub al-Alaf told us in Egypt, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin told me Saad, Khalid bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abu Al-Sahba, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to pray: “O God, keep Islam standing, and keep me safe.” with Islam while sitting, and protect me with Islam while lying down, and do not let an envious enemy gloat over me. In Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, the treasuries of which are in Your hand.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1925","Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Hairi told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, Humaid told us Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: It was part of the supplication of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Oh God We ask you for the reasons for your mercy, the assurances of your forgiveness, safety from every sin, the spoils of every righteousness, and the victory in Paradise. “And salvation from the Fire with your help.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"1926","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Asam told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, he said: Bishr bin Ubayd Allah told us, saying: I heard Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, saying: I heard Al-Nawwas bin Samaan Al-Kalabi, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no heart except between two of the fingers of the Most Gracious. If He wills, He can make it straight, and if He wills, He can cause it to move.” And it was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “O God, O converter of hearts, make my heart firm on Your religion, and the scales are in the hand of the Most Gracious, He raises peoples up. And others will be reduced until the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. “And it has evidence with an authentic chain of transmission, on the authority of Anas bin Owner"
"1927","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim told us, Abi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, On the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to often say: “O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion.”"
"1928","Ibrahim bin Asmah told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaida, he said: Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, was asked about the supplication that you prayed with when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Ask, and it will be given to you.” He said: I said: Oh God, I ask you for faith that does not turn away, and bliss that does not end, and to accompany your Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the highest level. Paradise is the eternal paradise “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1929","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Aoun bin Amara Al-Basri told us, Ruh bin Al-Qasim told us, On the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khutami, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunaif, on the authority of his uncle Uthman ibn Hunaif, may God be pleased with him, that a blind man Sight came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication by which I may pray that God will restore my sight. So he said to him: “Say, O God, I I ask you, and I turn to you through your Prophet, the Prophet of Mercy, O Muhammad, I have turned to you to my Lord, O God, grant him his intercession for me, and grant me my intercession for my “Myself,” so he recited this supplication, and he stood up and his follower: Shabib bin Saeed Al-Habti, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, saw “Additions in the text.” And the chain of transmission, and the saying about it is the saying of Shabib, for he is trustworthy and trustworthy.”"
"1930","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl al-Dabbas informed us of Mecca from the origin of his book. Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid Al-Sayegh, Ahmad bin Shabib bin Saeed Al-Habti told us, my father told me, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Madani, and he is Al-Khattimi, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of his uncle, Uthman bin Hunaif, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to him. A blind man complained to him about the loss of his sight, so he said: O Messenger of God, I have no leader, and it has become difficult for me. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go to the watering hole and perform ablution, then pray two rak’ahs, then say: Oh God, I ask You, and I turn to You through Your Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Prophet of mercy, O Muhammad, I turn through you to your Lord and He will clear my sight for me. Oh God, grant him his intercession for me, and grant me my intercession for myself.” Othman said: By God, we did not separate, nor did we talk for long until the man entered as if he had never been afflicted. “This is an authentic hadith according to Al-Bukhari’s condition, and they did not narrate it, but I presented the hadith of Aoun bin Amara because it is our duty to present the highest chain of narrations.”"
"1931","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Ansari told us, and Ismail bin Qutaybah Al-Sulami told us, they said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Dawud Al-Awdi, on the authority of Buraydah Al-Aslami, he said: He said to me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Say, O God, I am weak, so strengthen my weakness in Your satisfaction, and take for me what is good by my forelock, and make Islam the ultimate goal.” My satisfaction, O God, I am weak, so strengthen me, and I am humiliated, so console me, and I am poor, so provide for me.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1932","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fudayl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Abu Salih Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told us, On the authority of Abu Yahya Al-Kala’i, on the authority of Abu Salam Al-Aswad, on the authority of Thuban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “It was said to me: O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, and ask and it will be given to you.” He said: So I said: “O God, I ask you to do good deeds and abandon evil deeds. And love the poor, and that you forgive me and have mercy on me, and if you want to cause temptation against a people, then cause me to die to you, and I am not tempted, O God, I ask you “Your love, and the love of whoever loves you, and a love that makes your love inform me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari."
"1933","Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim told us, Ahmed bin Bakkar Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abdullah bin Wahb bin Muslim Al-Qurashi told us, Hafs bin Maysarah told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: One of the supplications of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: “O God, grant me pleasure with my hearing and my sight until you make them Heir from me, and keep me healthy in my religion and my body, and help me from those who have wronged me until You show me my vengeance for him. O God, I have surrendered myself to You and have entrusted my affairs To You, and I have turned my back to You, and I have turned my face to You, there is no refuge from You except in You. I have believed in Your Messenger whom You have sent, and in Your Book which This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. This is Hussein bin Ali from whom Musa bin Uqba narrated, and he is Hussein the Younger whom Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak met, and he narrated From him the hadith about the times of prayer."
"1934","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told me, Abu Saleh told me, the writer of al-Layth ibn Sa’d, al-Layth ibn Sa’d told me. Saad, that Khalid bin Abi Imran narrated, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not sit in a gathering where anyone was present, and there was no Except he said: “O God, forgive me for what I have done and what I have delayed, and what I have concealed and what I have announced, and what You know better than me. O God, provide me with Your obedience does not prevent me from disobeying you, and grant me from your fear what you convey to me your mercy, and grant me from certainty which you take lightly. against the calamities of this world, and bless for me my hearing and my sight, and make them my heirs. O God, take my vengeance from those who wronged me, and grant me victory over those who Treat me, and do not make the world my greatest concern, nor the amount of my knowledge, O God, and do not give power over me to those who do not have mercy on me.” Ibn Umar was asked about them: He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to conclude his gatherings with them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1935","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, dictating in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Yahya told us Bin Saeed Al-Qattan, Thawr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When the table was raised, he greeted him and said: “Praise be to God, abundantly good, and not sufficient, nor consigned, nor dispensable with, our Lord.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1936","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj Abu Al-Samh, narrated to them, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Moses, peace be upon him, said: O Lord, teach me something by which I will remember You and call upon You by it. He said: O Moses, say: There is no god but God. He said: O Lord, all your servants say this. He said: Say: There is no god but God. He said: There is no god but You, O Lord. I only want something that you can make specific to me. He said: O Moses, if the seven heavens and their ruler were someone other than me, and the seven earths were on a palm, and there is no god but God on a palm that included them, there is no god but God. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1937","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, and Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, they said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair told us, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Aamir bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man from my nation will be shouted over the heads of creation on the Day of Resurrection, and ninety-nine Every record as far as the eye can see. Then it will be said to him: Do you disavow any of this? He will say: No, O Lord. He will say: Do you have an excuse? Or a good deed? So he will be afraid The man, and he says: No, O Lord, and he says: Yes, you have done us good deeds, and there is no injustice done to you. Then a card is brought out for him in which I bear witness that no There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He says: O Lord, what is this card with these records? He says: You are not wronged. He said: The records were placed in a bowl, and the cards were in a bowl, so the records were destroyed, and the card became heavy. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”"
"1938","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Sulaym bin Amir told me, he said: He said: I heard the middle Al-Bajli, on the pulpit of Homs, saying: I heard Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: He said: Then the thought choked him and he cried, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this. The pulpit says in the first year: “Ask God for pardon and well-being, and certainty in the first and the hereafter, for the servant has not been given better after certainty than “Al-Aafiya” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it was narrated with a wording other than this from the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"1939","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Hilal bin Khabab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to his uncle: “Pray often for good health.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and it was narrated with another wording.”"
"1940","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abd Al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach those who converted to Islam to say: “O God, guide me and provide for me, and protect me and have mercy on me.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1941","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Zubayri told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Hamza bin Habib Al-Zayat told us, On the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Oh God Heal me in my body, and heal me in my sight, and make him my heir. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Great Throne, praise be to Allah. Lord of the Worlds. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, if the hearing of a loved one is safe from ‘Urwah, and they do not narrate it.”"
"1942","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Awwam Al-Riyahi told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I said, O Messenger of God, have you seen if Laylat al-Qadr comes, what should I say about it? He said: Say: “O God, You are forgiving and love to pardon, so pardon me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1943","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to seek refuge from five things: cowardice, And stinginess, and a bad life, and the torment of the grave, and the temptation of the chest. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1944","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shayban bin Abd told us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his supplications: “O God, I seek refuge in You from Inability and laziness, cowardice and stinginess, senility and cruelty, heedlessness, poverty, humiliation and poverty, and I seek refuge in You from Poverty, disbelief, immorality, discord, hypocrisy, reputation, and hypocrisy. I seek refuge in You from deafness, mutism, madness, and leprosy. “And leprosy, and bad diseases.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1945","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan and Muhammad bin Ismail told us, they said: Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Abd told us Allah bin Wahb, Huyay bin Abdullah narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray with these words: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the defeat of debt, the defeat of the enemy, and his gloating. “Enemies” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1946","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan and Muhammad bin Ismail told us, they said: Harun bin Saeed Al-Ayli told us, Abd told us Allah bin Wahb, Hafs bin Maysarah, and Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman informed me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray and say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the disappearance of Your grace, and from Your health will improve, and from the suddenness of your vengeance, and from all your anger.” Ibn Wahb said: It was mentioned by Ya’qub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar: “This is an authentic hadith sent by Hafs according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1947","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Yass al-Aas narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us, and Musa ibn al-Hasan ibn Abbad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mus’ab narrated to us. Al-Qurqisani, narrated to us by Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Seek refuge in God from poverty, poverty, and humiliation, and from being wronged or being wronged.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1948","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us, Abd al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Abdullah bin Saeed bin Saeed told us Abu Hind, on the authority of his grandfather Abu Hind, on the authority of Saifi, the servant of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr Al-Sulami, whose name is Ka’b ibn Amr, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to pray and say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from destruction, deterioration, senility, distress, drowning, and burning, and I seek refuge in You from Satan makes me shudder at the time of death, and I seek refuge in You to die in Your way, fleeing, and I seek refuge in You to die in Your way, biting.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1949","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Hamid Al-Harithi told us, Abu Usama told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, On the authority of his uncle, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, spare me from immoral things, whims, deeds, and medicines.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1950","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Khushnam bin Al-Siddiq narrated to us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywa bin Shuraih narrated to us, on the authority of Darraj Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “I seek refuge in God Of disbelief and religion. A man said: O Messenger of God, do you equate disbelief with religion? He said: “Yes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1951","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Razi told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his supplication: “O God Indeed, I seek refuge in You from the evil neighbor in the place of residence, for the neighbor of the desert turns away.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. He was followed by Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Maqbari"
"1952","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Affan told us, Wahib told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Seek refuge in God from the evil of a neighbour. The place, if the traveler wishes to stay, he will move away. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it."
"1953","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri, on the authority of Saad bin Aws, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya Al-Absi, on the authority of Shutair bin Shakal, on the authority of his father Shakal bin Humaid, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, teach me a refuge with which I may seek refuge. So he took my hand and said: “Say: Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing, from the evil of my sight, from the evil of my soul, and from the evil of my semen “until he preserved it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1954","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Handali told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim Al-Nabil told us, Othman Al-Shaham told us, he told me Muslim bin Abi Bakra said: My father heard me say, “O God, I seek refuge in You from worry, laziness, and the torment of the grave.” He said: O Son, from whom did you hear this? I said: I heard you saying them. He said: “Time, for I heard them from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying them.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1955","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab, Abdul-Rahman bin Thabit bin Thuban told us, Abdullah bin Al-Fadl Al-Hashimi told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: “I seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell, the torment of the grave, and the temptation of Life, the temptation of death, and the temptation of the Antichrist.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it."
"1956","Ahmed bin Salman bin Al-Hassan Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hassan bin Makram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Abdullah bin Amir Al-Aslami told us, On the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Seek refuge in God from greed that leads to a good nature, and from greed without desire when there is no desire.” This is a hadith with a straight chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it."
"1957","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Hatim Al-Razi told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us, Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Humaid Al-Araj, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: It was one of the supplications of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, I I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is not beneficial, a heart that is not humble, a supplication that is not heard, a soul that is not satisfied, and from hunger, for indeed it is miserable to waste, and from Betrayal is a wretched nature, and comes from laziness, miserliness and cowardice, from senility, from being sent back to the most miserable age, and from The temptation of the Antichrist, the torment of the grave, and the temptation of life and death, O God, we ask You for weak, hidden hearts that repent in Your way, O God. We ask you for the blessings of your forgiveness, salvation from your command, safety from every sin, the spoils of every righteousness, and winning Paradise. And salvation from the fire.”
 And when he prostrated, he would say: “O God, my blackness and my imagination prostrate to You, and in You my heart believes. I acknowledge Your grace upon me, and this is what I have committed against myself. O Great, O Great, forgive me, for no one forgives great sins except the Lord, the Great. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, except that the two sheikhs did not They narrated on the authority of Humayd al-Araj al-Kufi, but they agreed to narrate the hadith of Humayd bin Qais al-Araj al-Makki. As for the beginning of the hadith, it is about seeking refuge. Of the four: It was narrated, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abdullah bin Amr.
 As for the hadith of Abu Hurairah"
"1958","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Sa’id Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told us, saying: Umar bin Hafs al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Al-Layth bin Sa’d, that Sa’id al-Maqbari told him, on the authority of his brother Abbad bin Abi Sa’id, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “O God, I seek refuge in You from four things: from knowledge that is not of benefit, from a heart that is not humble, from a soul that is not satisfied, and from supplication.” ""is not heard""
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr"
"1959","Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi narrated to us in Marw, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Qubaysah ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from Knowledge that is not beneficial, a supplication that is not heard, a heart that is not humble, and a soul that is not satisfied.”"
"1960","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever asks God Paradise three times. Paradise said: O God, admit him to Paradise, and whoever seeks refuge with God from Hell three times. Hell said: O God, protect him from Hell. This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1961","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us about Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd Al-Razzaq told us, and Ahmad told us Ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, Yunus Ibn Sulaym told me, he said: He dictated to me. Yunus bin Yazid al-Ayli, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Qari, who said: I heard Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: Whenever a revelation was sent down to the Messenger of God, we would hear it in his face like the sound of bees. So it was revealed to him one day. We remained silent for an hour, then he faced the Qiblah and raised his hands and said: “O God, increase us and do not take away from us, honor us and do not degrade us, give us and do not Deprive us, prefer us, and do not prefer us, and be satisfied with us and our land.” Then he said: “Ten verses have been revealed to me: whoever establishes them will enter Paradise, then He recited: {Indeed, the believers have succeeded} [Al-Mu’minun: 1] until he concluded ten verses: “Abd al-Razzaq and Yunus bin Sulaym said: This was his uncle, a governor. He said: He sent me. My uncle went to Yunus bin Yazid until he dictated to me the hadiths of “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1962","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told me, Jamil bin Al-Hassan Al-Jahmi told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Al-Zarqan told us. Al-Ahwazi, Suleiman Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God So that the servant would be ashamed to raise his hands to him and he would return them disappointed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"1963","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ubayy told us, and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us: We told him: Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Usama, on the authority of Umair, the servant of my father Al-Lahm, may God be pleased with him, said that “he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Oil Stones, making supplication while he was masked with his hands.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1964","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Ibn Dhubab, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I did not see the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He raised his hands and made supplication from his pulpit and no one else. He used to place his two toes on the shoes of his shoulders and make supplication. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"1965","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, about Marwa, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man was calling with his two fingers, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Uhud, Uhud” was narrated this year on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas"
"1966","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim told us, Abi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by me while I was praying with my fingers, and he said: “One, one,” and pointed."
"1967","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told me, Nasr bin Ali, and Muhammad bin Musa Al-Kharshi told us, they said: Hammad bin Issa, Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Salem bin Abdullah narrating, on the authority of his father Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Omar Radi God on his authority, “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, extended his hands in supplication, he would not return them until he wiped his face with them.” It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas"
"1968","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Salih bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you ask God So ask Him with the insides of your palms, and do not ask Him with the backs of them, and wipe your faces with them.”"
"1969","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Musa bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Never has a people sat in a gathering in which there has been so much confusion, and someone said before he stood up: Glory be to You, O God, our Lord, and with Your praise there is no god.” Except you, I ask your forgiveness and then I repent to you, unless he will be forgiven for what he was sitting with.” This chain of narration is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, except that Al-Bukhari justified it with the hadith of Wahib, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b al-Ahbar, according to what he said, “And God knows best.” There is evidence for this hadith, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mut’im, Abu Barzah Al-Aslami, and Rafi’ bin Khadij.
 As for the hadith of Jubair bin Mutim"
"1970","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, and Ahmad bin Al-Hussein Al-Lahabi, they said: Dawud bin Qais Al-Farra’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God and with His praise, Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. So he said it in a gathering of idle talk, it was like a stamp being imprinted on him, and whoever said it in a gathering of idle talk, it would be an expiation for him. “This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Barza Al-Aslami:"
"1971","So Abu al-Tayyib Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madili told us, Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Farra told us, Ya`la ibn Ubaid, Hajjaj bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hashim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. At the end of the session, he said: “Glory be to You, O God, and by Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness.” And I repent to you.” Some of us said: O Messenger of God, this is what we used to hear from you. He said: “This is the expiation for what happens in the assembly.”
 As for the hadith of Rafi’ bin Khadij"
"1972","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Dawud Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Musab bin Hayyan, brother of Muqatil, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Riyahi, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When his companions gathered to him and he wanted to get up, he would say: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness.” And I repent to You. I have done evil and wronged myself, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You. So we said: O Messenger of God, these are words. Did you tell them? He said: “Yes, Gabriel came to me and said to me: O Muhammad, this is the atonement for assemblies.”"
"1973","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim informed us, Abi informed us, Yahya bin Yahya informed us, Abu Muawiyah informed us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq informed us. Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: A man came to Ali and said: I mean in my letter, so he said: Shall I not teach you some words? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught them to me. If you were owed a debt like Mount Sabir, God would have paid it on your behalf. Say: “O God, protect me from Your haraam things, and I am free from your grace from anyone else.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1974","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us in al-Ray, and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us in Marw, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi told us Osama, Yazid bin Harun told us, Azhar bin Sinan Al-Qurashi informed us, Muhammad bin Wasi’ told us, he said: I came to Medina and met Salim bin Abd there. God Ibn Omar told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever enters market, and he said: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death, in His hand is goodness, and He is capable of all things. God recorded for him a thousand good deeds, erased from him a thousand bad deeds, raised for him a thousand thousand degrees, and built for him a house in Paradise.” He said: So I came. Khorasan, so I went to Qutaibah bin Muslim and said to him, “I have brought you a gift.” So I told him the hadith, and Qutaibah bin Muslim was riding in his convoy. Until he comes to the door of the market and says it, then he leaves, “This is a hadith that has many chains of narrations (collected, and most of them are) on the authority of Abu Yahya Amr ibn A dinar from the family of Al-Zubayr on the authority of Salim, and Abu Yahya. This is not a condition of this book. As for Azhar ibn Sinan, he was an ascetic. The Basrais were among the companions of Muhammad bin Wasi’ and Malik bin Dinar.And there is evidence for him from the hadith of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zaid bin Abdullah bin Omar, the narrated narration of his hadith in the two Sahih books on the authority of Salem.”
 Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Hammam bin Abi Badr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Omar bin Muhammad bin Zaid told me, a man, Basri, told me, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, with a traceable chain of transmission: who went out to The market, and he said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is Ever-Living and never dies. In His hand is good, and He has power over all things. God recorded for him a thousand good deeds, erased from him a thousand bad deeds, and built for him a house in Paradise.” This is how Abdullah bin Wahb narrated it, and Ismail bin Ayyash narrated it, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Salem
 It was narrated, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever enters the market and says: There is no god but God alone, He has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death. He is alive and will not die. In His hand is good, and He is capable of all things. God has recorded for him a thousand good deeds, and erased from him a thousand bad deeds.And He raised it a thousand degrees, “And we wrote it from the hadith of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar.”"
"1975","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Haidar Al-Baghdadi told us, Masruq bin Al-Murziban, Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever enters the market and buys and sells in it, and says: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is Praise, He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. God recorded for him a thousand good deeds, erased from him a thousand bad deeds, and built a house for him in Paradise “This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and God knows best.” Imran bin Muslim continued it, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar"
"1976","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Al-Shawareb told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Al-Wahhab Al-Hijabi, Yahya bin Sulaym Al-Makki told us, Imran bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says in the market: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner, to Him is the kingdom, and to Him is praise, in His hand. Goodness, and He has power over all things. God recorded for him a thousand good deeds, erased from him a thousand bad deeds, and built for him a house in Paradise. The chapter on the authority of Jabir, Abu Hurairah, Buraydah Al-Aslami, and Anas, may God be pleased with them all, “and the closest to it is the conditions of this book.” Hadith of Buraydah other than this wording.”"
"1977","Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak told us, Muhammad bin Isa Al-Madaini told us, Shuaib bin Harb told us, a neighbor of ours surnamed Abu Amr told us, on the authority of Alqamah. Ibn Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the market, he would say: “In the name of God, O God, I ask You for the good of this market and the good in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. If he is afflicted with an immoral oath, or a losing deal.”"
"1978","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Al-Aswad bin Shayban told us, Abu Nawfal bin Abi told us Aqrab, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was impressed by comprehensive supplications, and he would leave out what was between “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1979","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, and Musa bin Ismail told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Naama, that Abdullah bin Mughaffal heard his son saying: Oh God, I ask you for the White Palace. From the right side of Paradise, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will be in this nation people who will transgress in supplication and purification.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1980","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Yusuf bin Adi told us, Utham bin Ali, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was starving Concerning the night, he said: “There is no god but Allah, the One, the Supreme, Lord of the heavens and the earth, and all that is between them, the Mighty, the Forgiving.” This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"1981","Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastawayh told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Muqri told us, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, On the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyib, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was... He woke up during the night and said: “There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Oh God, I ask You for forgiveness for my sin, and I ask You by Your mercy. Oh God, increase me in knowledge. And do not deviate my heart after You have guided me, and grant me mercy from You. Indeed, You are the Bestower.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1982","Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, Yaqoub bin Sufyan told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Yazid Al-Ahwazi told me, Abu Hammam Muhammad told us Ibn Al-Zabarqan, Thawr Ibn Yazid told us, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Ma’dan, on the authority of Zuhair Al-Anmari, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He took his bed and said: “O God, forgive me, make my devil humble, release my bet, weigh my balance, and place me in the highest dew.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1983","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, Ishaq bin Abdullah informed us Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his supplication: “O God, I seek refuge in You from poverty, poverty, and humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from being wronged or being wronged.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1984","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ghalib narrated to us, Ismail bin Al-Khalil Al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Ali bin Mushar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from The trial of the Fire, and the torment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave, and the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the trial of wealth, and from the evil of the trial of Poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the temptation of the Antichrist. Oh God, wash away my sins with water of ice and hail, and purify me from my sins as You purified me. The white garment from filth, and keep the distance between me and my sins as you distanced the East from the West. O God, I seek refuge in You from laziness. “And the pyramid, and the sinful, and the grave land.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context."
"1985","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Omar Hafs bin Omar told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim, Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Take your Paradise.” We said, O Messenger of God: Who is an enemy present? He said: “I will not protect you from Hell. Say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"1986","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Abu Kurayb told us, Khallad bin Yazid Al-Jafi told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: “O God, I ask you for a pure life and a dead This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1987","Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Hamdawayh al-Faqih told us, dictating in Bukhara, Abu Ali Saleh ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz narrated to us. Al-Baghdadi, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Issa bin Maymun, the client of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: “O God, extend Your provision to me in my old age.” And the end of my life” This is a hadith with a good chain of transmission, and the text is strange in supplication and is recommended for the sheikhs, except that Issa bin Maimun did not use it as evidence. ""The two old men"""
"1988","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir Shazan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Jafar Al-Khattimi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There were two wishes among you: one of them passed, and one of them remained “And God would not punish them while you were among them, and God would not punish them while they were seeking forgiveness” [Al-Anfal: 33] “This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it. They agreed that the companion’s interpretation is a hadith with a chain of transmission, and there is evidence for it on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari."
"1989","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Sadaqa bin Al-Fadl told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, Harmala bin Qays told me, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, said: “There were two trusts on earth: one of them was removed, and the other remained.” {And God would not punish them while you were among them, and God would not punish them while they were seeking forgiveness} [Al-Anfal: 33]"
"1990","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Abu Amr Al-Mustamli told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Bishr told us Ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Who He said, “There is no power nor strength except in God. It is a cure for ninety-nine diseases, the easiest of which is anxiety.” This is an authentic hadith. They did not narrate it, and he gave glad tidings. Ibn Rafi’ al-Harithi is not abandoned, even if they did not narrate it. Likewise, al-Haytham al-Bakaa did not narrate it, and he has a hadith that is unique to him, and this is his location, for he is one of the servants of the Muslims.”"
"1991","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad Al-Saydali told us, Uqba bin Makram Al-Ammi told us, Sharik bin Abdul Hamid, my father’s brother, told us Bakr Al-Hanafi, Al-Haytham bin Jamaz Al-Bikaa narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that Abu Talib fell ill It became heavy, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned to him and said: O son of my brother, pray to your Lord, who sent you to heal me. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Oh God, heal my uncle.” He said: As if he had been loosened from a headband. Abu Talib said: Your Lord has sent you to obey you. He said: “And you, uncle, if you obey God, He will obey you.”"
"1992","Imam Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Ahmad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, They said: Musa bin Ismail told us, Al-Mubarak bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked. Which supplication is better? He said: “A person’s supplication for himself.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"1993","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Hatim told us, Abu Wahb Muhammad bin Muzahim told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ali bin Badhimah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he showed him Auf bin Malik, and he said: O Messenger of God, the children of so-and-so raided me and took my son and my camels, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “The family of Muhammad is such-and-such, the people of a household - and I think he said nine verses - they do not have a saa’ of food, nor a mudd of food. So ask God Almighty.” He said: Then he returned to his wife. She said: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, respond to you? So he told her, and said: The man did not wait long enough to return his camels to him, and his son was the richest of them, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, So he stood on the pulpit and thanked God, praised Him, and commanded them to ask God Almighty and to desire Him, and he recited to them: {And whoever fears God will make a way out for him, and will provide for him from where he does not expect.} [At-Talaq: 3] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"1994","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad bin Hunayn, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Jabir bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And he said: And his sins and his sins, and he said this saying two or three times, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Say, O God Your forgiveness is greater than my sins and your mercy is more important to me than my deeds.” So he said it, then he said: “Come back,” so he came back. Then he said: “Come back,” so he came back and said: “Arise, for God has forgiven you.” A hadith narrated on the authority of the last of them, civilians who did not “One of them was found to have been wounded, but they did not bring him out.”"
"1995","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told me, Saeed bin Abi Maryam, Nafi bin Yazid told me, Yahya bin Abi Usayd told me, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Issa, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a man and he was saying: O Most Merciful of the Merciful, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Ask, for God has looked at you.” Al-Fadl bin Issa is Al-Raqqashi, and I fear that it is his uncle Yazid bin Aban, but I may I found evidence for it from the hadith of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili.”"
"1996","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Omani told us, Masoud bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Kamil bin Talha told us, Fadal bin Jubayr told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has a kingdom entrusted with whoever says: O Most Merciful of the Merciful,” so whoever says it Three times, the angel said: Indeed, the Most Merciful of the Merciful has come to you, so ask."
"1997","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ismail told us, in Baghdad, about the severance, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Alahani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who is pleased with him? That his supplications be answered in times of distress and adversity, so let him multiply his supplications in times of prosperity.” “A hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Al-Bukhari cited Abu Salih as evidence, and Abu Amir al-Ilahani. I think he is al-Hawzani and he is truthful.”"
"1998","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated a dictation on the beginning of Safar in the year three hundred and ninety-seven. Abu reported Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi, in Marw, Ahmed bin Issa Al-Tarsusi told us, and Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, told us Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, and Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, they said: Ismail bin Abi told us Uwais, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Dawud al-San’ani told us, Falah bin Kathir told me, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, descended to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the most beautiful way, the likes of which he had never descended before, laughing and rejoicing. He said: “Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.” He said: “And peace be upon you, O Gabriel.” He said: “God has sent me to you with a gift of the treasures of the Throne. God has honored you with them.” He said: “And what is that gift, O Gabriel?” Gabriel said, “Say, O you who show the beautiful and cover the ugly, O you who are not held accountable for the wrongdoing, and do not Tear the veil, O Greatest Pardoner, O Most Merciful, O Most Forgiving, O Most Stretch of Hands with mercy, O Compassionate of all secrets, and O The end of every complaint, O Most Generous of Forgiveness, O Greatest of Manna, O Initiator of blessings before they are due, O our Lord, O our Master, and O our Master, O the ultimate goal of our desire, I ask you, O God, not to roast my creation with fire. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is the reward for this? The words” - then he mentioned the rest of the hadith after praying about its length -. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, as its narrators are all trustworthy civilians, and I mentioned previously the disagreement among the imams of hadith regarding hearing Shuaib bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr, from his grandfather."
"1999","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Issa bin Maymun, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “What prevents any of you from If he knows the answer from himself, and is cured of an illness, or returns from a journey, he says: Praise be to God, by whose glory and majesty good deeds are accomplished. Issa bin Maimun separated from Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, from Aisha, and Issa is not accused of fabrication.”"
"2000","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabbah, and others told us, they said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he told me Othman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Fatima: “What prevents you from You will listen to what I command you to say in the morning and in the evening: O Ever-Living, O Ever-Subsisting, by Your mercy I seek help, rectify all my affairs for me. And do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2001","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Zuhair bin Harb told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Khalaf bin al-Mundhir told us, Bakr bin Abd told us Al-Muzani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he goes to bed: Praise be to God who He sufficed and sheltered me. Praise be to God who fed me and gave me drink. Praise be to God who bestowed upon me the best. Oh God, I ask you by your glory to save me. From the fire, He has praised God with all the praises of all creation. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2002","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie informed us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, Yusuf bin Abdul Rahman told us, Suhail bin Abi Saleh told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If he comes When one of you goes to bed, let him say, “O God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, our Lord and Lord of all things. You are taking hold of his forelock. You are the first, and there is nothing before you.” And you are the last, so there is nothing after you, and you are the inner one, so there is nothing besides you that enriches us from poverty, and pay off our debt.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. This is Joseph, who is called the master of Sakra.”"
"2003","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Abdul-Ala bin Hammad told us, and Azhar bin Marwan Al-Basrian told us, Bishr bin Mansour Al-Sulami told them, on the authority of Zuhair bin Muhammad, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: A man from the Ansar from the people of Quba invited the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we set off with him, and when he had eaten and washed his hands - or he said: His hand - he said: “Praise be to God who feeds and does not feed. Whoever bestowed upon us, guided us, fed us, gave us drink, and every good test He granted us, praise be to God beyond Deposited, not rewarded, not ungrateful, not dispensed with. Praise be to God who provided food, gave drink, gave clothing from nakedness, and guided those who misguidance, and gained insight from blindness, and was favored over many of his creation. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2004","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ali bin Muslim Al-Abar told us, Al-Haytham bin Kharijah told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Ufair ibn Ma’dan, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “When he calls The caller: The gates of heaven were opened, and supplications were answered. Whoever is beset by distress or distress, let him be patient for the caller. When he says “Allahu Akbar,” they say “Allahu Akbar,” and when He recited the tashahhud, they recited the tashahhud, and when he said: Hail to the prayer, he said: Hail to the prayer, and when he said: Hail to the success, he said: Hail to the success, then he said: Oh God, Lord of this sincere and answered supplication, the call of truth and the word of piety, grant us life for it and grant us death for it. And send us to it, and make us among the choicest of its people, living and dead, then he will ask God for his need.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2005","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hasan bin al-Muthanna told us, Affan told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praising God.” Narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib"
"2006","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Hasan Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra told us, Ali bin Utham bin Ali told us. Al-Amiri, Abi told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “I saw the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace."
"2007","Azhar bin Ahmad Al-Munadi told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abdullah bin Daoud Al-Khuraibi told us, Hani told us. Bin Uthman, on the authority of Humaydah bint Yasir, on the authority of her grandmother, Yasira, may God be pleased with her, who was one of the female emigrants, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “You should practice glorification, glorification, and sanctification, and do not neglect and forget monotheism, and join them with your fingertips, for they will be held accountable.” And inferences »"
"2008","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi narrated to us, Shadh bin Fayyad narrated to us, Hashim bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Kinana, on the authority of Safiya Radi On her authority, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to me and in front of me were four thousand saplings with which I was reciting rosary. He said: “O daughter of Hayy! “This?” I said: I glorify them in them. He said: “I have glorified God more since I rose before your head than this.” I said: Teach me, O Messenger of God. He said: “Say, Glory be to God.” The number of things He created. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. There is evidence for it from the hadith of the Egyptians with a chain of transmission more authentic than this.”"
"2009","Ismail bin Ahmad al-Jurjani told us, Muhammad bin al-Hasan bin Qutaybah al-Asqalani told us, Harmala bin Yahya told us, Ibn Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Saeed bin Abi Hilal told him, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, On the authority of her father, he went in with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to see a woman and in her hands were palm trees or pebbles. I will tell you what is easier for you than this. And better? Say: Glory be to God, according to the number of what He created in the heavens. Glory be to God, according to the number of what He created on the earth. You praise God. He said: Glory be to God, according to the number of what is between that, and Glory be to God. As many as He is the Creator, and God is great like that, and praise be to God like that, and there is no god but God like that, and there is no power but By God, like that.”"
"2010","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told me, Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, Jarir bin Abd told us. Al-Hamid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abdullah, who is the son of Amr, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanding words of terror: “I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from His wrath and from His punishment.” And from the evil of His servants and from the incitements of the devils and from their presence.” He said: “Abdullah ibn Umar and any of his children who reached puberty taught them and told them.” With his people, and whoever among them had not yet reached puberty, he wrote it down and hung it around his neck. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration that is connected to the subject of disagreement.”"
"2011","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Muadh bin Fadala told us, Hisham, the companion of Al-Distawai, told us, Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When one of you goes to bed, an angel and a devil come to him, Satan says: Open with evil, and the angel says: Open with good. So if he mentions God, Satan goes away and the angel comes and eats him, and lo! He woke up and an angel and a devil came to him. The devil said, “Open with good news,” and the angel said, “Open with good news.” Then he said, “Praise be to God who has returned to me.” My soul after her death and he did not kill her in her dream. Praise be to God who keeps the sky from falling on the earth except by His permission. Indeed, God is with people. Kind and Merciful. Praise be to God who gives life to the dead and He has power over all things. So if an animal falls down, it dies as a martyr, and if he stands up, he prays in virtues. “.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2012","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Abu Al-Muwajih told us, Sadaqa bin Al-Fadl told us, Abu Hammam Al-Ahwazi told us, Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Zuhair Al-Anmari, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He took his bed and said: “O God, forgive me my sin, humble my devil, release my bet, heavy my balance, and place me in the highest assembly.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2013","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Asbagh bin Al-Faraj Al-Misri, and Harun bin Marouf Al-Baghdadi told us, they said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Huyay bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a man comes to visit you sick, let him say: O God, heal your servant who is an enemy to you. Or he walks with you to prayer. This is an Egyptian hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and another hadith from the hadith of the Kufans was narrated on this subject.”"
"2014","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ahmed bin Ali Al-Khazzaz told us, Jandal bin Waqiq Al-Taghlabi told us, Shuaib bin Rashid, seller of patterns, Abu Hashim Al-Rummani told us, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, visited me While I was ill, he said: “O Salman, may God heal your illness, forgive your sins, and grant you good health in your body and body for the duration of your life.”"
"2015","Ja`far bin Harun the grammarian told us, in Baghdad, Ishaq bin Sadaqa bin Subaih told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid al-Qatwani told us, Sulayman bin Bilal, Amara bin Ghaziyah told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, speaking, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “The miserly person is the one in whose presence I was mentioned and he does not pray for me.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” There is evidence for this on the authority of Abu Hurairah"
"2016","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Despite the nose of a man before whom I was mentioned, he did not May blessings be upon me.”"
"2017","Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, On the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A people never sat down and remembered By God, they did not send blessings upon their Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, except that it was a sitting over them for a period of time, and no people sat there who did not mention God except that it happened. A period of time is upon them. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2018","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever prays upon me, may God’s prayers be upon him He prayed ten prayers, and ten sins were removed from him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2019","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told me, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told me, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, Amr bin Abi told me Amr, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I met Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he gave me good tidings and said: Indeed, your Lord says: Whoever prays upon you, I pray upon him. And whoever greets you, I greet him, and I prostrate to God in thanksgiving.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not narrated by anyone else [p. 736] in the Book of Supplications.
 The Book of the Virtues of the Qur’an"
"2020","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed told us Ibn Balawayh, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Juraij said: My father told me that Sa’id bin Jubayr, He told him: {And We have given you seven of the repeated verses} [Al-Hijr: 87]. He said: It is the mother of the Qur’an. My father said: And Sa’id bin Jubayr recited to me: {In the name of God The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] The seventh verse, Sa’id bin Jubayr said, and Ibn Abbas recited it to me as I recited it to you, then he said: {In the Name God is the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] The seventh verse, Ibn Abbas said: “So God gave it out to you, and He did not give it out to anyone before you.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Barsani, Abdul Razzaq bin Hammam, Hafs bin Ghayath, and Othman bin Amr, and Abdul Majeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, with different wording.
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak"
"2021","So Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, and Abu Ishaq informed us. Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Harith told us, Saeed bin Yaqoub Al-Talqani told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the seven repeated verses, he said: “They are the opening of the Book.” Ibn Abbas read it with the name God is the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Seventh, Ibn Jurayj said: So I said to my father: Saeed bin Jubayr told you, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: “In the name of God The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, a verse from the Book of God? He said: Yes, then he said: Ibn Abbas recited it in the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful in all two rak’ahs.
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Barsani:"
"2022","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jurayj, my father told me that Saeed bin Jubayr told him that Ibn Abbas said: “And We have given you seven of the repeated Qur’an, and the Great Qur’an.} [Al-Hijr: 87] He said: And Sa’id bin Jubayr recited it to me {In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] when he concluded it, and he said: {In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] The seventh verse, he said: And Saeed bin Jubayr said to me: “God has revealed it to you, but He did not give it to anyone before you.”
 As for the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam:"
"2023","So Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad and Abdullah bin Shirawih told us, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, {And We have given you seven of the repeated times} [Al-Hijr: 87]. He said: “Fatihah The Book” Then he said: “{In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds} [Al-Fatihah: 2] So I said to my father: Sa’id informed you that Ibn Abbas, he said: “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, a verse from the Book of God?” He said: Yes
 As for the hadith of Hafs bin Ghayath"
"2024","So we talked to him. . . . . . . . . ., on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {And We have given you seven of repeated verses} [Al-Hijr: 87] He said: “The Fatihah of the Book.” It was said to Ibn Abbas: Where is the seventh? He said: {“In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful”} [Al-Fatihah: 1]
 As for the hadith of Othman bin Omar"
"2025","So Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Juraij told us, about... His father, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in God Almighty’s words about the seven times, He said: “Count it on me in my hand {In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment. You are the One we worship and thee we seek help. Guide us to the straight path, the path of those who You have bestowed favor upon them, neither upon them with wrath, nor on those who go astray.} Then he said: “God has given it out to you, but He has not given it out to anyone else.”
 As for the hadith of Abdul Majeed bin Abdul Aziz:"
"2026","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub informed us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman informed us, Al-Shafi’i informed me, Abdul Majeed informed me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, My father told me, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, {And We have given you seven of the repeated verses} [Al-Hijr: 87] He said: It is the mother of the Qur’an. My father said: And Sa`id recited it to me Ibn Jubayr when he sealed it, then he said: {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah: 1] The seventh, Ibn Abbas said: «And God has stored it for you, so what He gave it to someone before you.”"
"2027","Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith told me, Ali bin Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Masry told me, Ja'far bin Musafer Al-Tanisi told us, Zayd bin Al-Mubarak told us Al-San’ani, Salam bin Wahb Al-Jundi told us, my father told me, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, asked the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,” and he said: “It is one of the names of God, and what is between it, and the greatest name of God, except As between the blackness of the eye and its whiteness from nearness.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 News about the virtues of the Qur’an in general"
"2028","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh Al-Sahmi told us, Amr bin Al-Rabi’ bin Tariq, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Khalid bin Abi Yazid told us, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever reads the Qur’an has put prophecy between its two sides, except that it has not been revealed to him. The Qur’an is to be ignorant with the one who is ignorant, and not to be ignorant with the one who is ignorant while in his heart is the word of God Almighty.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2029","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Abdul-Warith bin Abdul-Samad bin Abdul told us. Al-Warith, my father told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ The person who recited the Qur’an will come on the Day of Resurrection and say: The Qur’an is lawful, O Lord, and he will wear a crown of honor. Then he will say: O Lord, increase it, O Lord of the Earth. And he will be satisfied with him, and it will be said to him, “Accept it and have mercy on him,” and he will be rewarded with every good sign.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2030","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi, Musaddad bin Qatan narrated to us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najūd, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “It is called the Companion of the Qur’an.” On the Day of Resurrection, recite it, recite it, and recite as you used to recite, for your status is in the last verse you recite.”"
"2031","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abu Hammam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Haywa bin Shurayh told me, On the authority of Aqeel bin Khaled, on the authority of Salama bin Abi Salamah bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The First Book was revealed from one chapter on one letter, and the Qur’an was revealed from seven chapters on Seven letters: prohibitive, commanding, lawful, forbidden, decisive, similar, and similar examples: So make what is lawful what is lawful, and prohibit what is unlawful, and do what you are commanded to do. And abstain from what you have been forbidden, and consider the likes of it, and act according to what is clear, and believe in what is similar and say: We believe in it. It is all from our Lord. “.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2032","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail told us, Zuhair bin Muawiyah, Shuaib bin Khalid Al-Razi told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Take heed of this Qur’an, for it is brutal, more detailed than the breasts of men, than camels, than their brains, and do not say to any of you, ‘I have forgotten a verse. He did so and so, but he forgot. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2033","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ka’b, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Usayd bin Hudair, that he used to recite while on the back of his house, and he had a good voice, so a messenger came May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: While I was reading, something like clouds covered me, the woman was in the house, and the horse was in the house, so I was afraid that she would fall. The woman, and the mare got off and left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Read, O Usayd, for he is an angel who listened to the Qur’an.”"
"2034","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b bin Malik, that Usayd bin Hudayr, may God be pleased with him, came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him - and mentioned the hadith in a similar manner - and said about it: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Recite Usayd, read Usayd, for that is an angel who listens to the Qur’an.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” There is evidence for Muslim’s condition, from the hadith of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Usayd"
"2035","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, and Musa bin Ismail told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Usayd bin Hudayr, that he said: While I was reading Tonight, I recited Surah Al-Baqarah. When I finished the end of it, I heard a whisper behind me, so I thought my horse was letting loose. He said: “Recite, Abu Atik, and I turned around.” Then, behold, things like lightsabers hanging between the sky and the earth. He said: O Messenger of God, by God, I could not pass. He said: So he said: That The angels came down to recite the Qur’an, but if you had gone, you would have seen wonders.”"
"2036","Abdullah bin Sa’d Al-Hafiz told us, Musa bin Abdul-Mu’min told me, Harun bin Sa’id Al-Ayli told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Hayy bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Fasting and the Qur’an intercede for the servant. The fasting person says: My Lord, I have deprived him of food and desires during the day, so grant me intercession for him. And the Qur’an says: I prevented him from sleeping at night, so they will intercede.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2037","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu Sa’id told us Muhammad bin Shazan, Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, and Abdullah bin Sa’d told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq, Ibn Ibrahim, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The one who does not have anything of the Qur’an inside him is like a ruined house.” . “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2038","Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Balkhi, the merchant in Baghdad, informed us. Abu Ismail Muhammad ibn Ismail informed us. Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us. Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah al-Hadrami, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The one who recites the Qur’an openly is like the one who openly gives charity, and the one who recites the Qur’an freely is like one who recites “With charity.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2039","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told us, my grandfather Ahmad bin Abdullah told us, Salamah bin Shabib told us, Ahmad bin told me Hanbal, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zayd bin Arta’at, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will not return to God with anything better.” Of what came out of it” - meaning the Qur’an -. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2040","Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi Al-Faqih told us, Musaddad bin Qattan bin Ibrahim told us, Dawud bin Rashid told us, Salih bin Omar told us, Ibrahim Al-Hijri reported, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “This The Qur’an is Allah’s banquet, so accept from His banquet whatever you are able. Indeed, this Qur’an is the rope of Allah, the clear light, and the beneficial healing. For whoever clings to him, and salvation for whoever follows him. He does not deviate and be blamed, nor is he crooked and straightened, and his wonders will not end, and he is not created from the abundance of"
"2041","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Kathir al-Suri told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Hammad Bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He recited ten verses in one night, and he was not recorded as one of the heedless.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, with an addition in the text."
"2042","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Umair bin Yusuf told us, Abu Salamah Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Yazid told us. Al-Ilahani, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Saluni told us that his father told him, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kaab Al-Qurazi, On the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever recites ten verses in one night will not be recorded as one of the heedless, and whoever He recited one hundred verses written from the obedient ones.”"
"2043","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Bashir bin Muhajir told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Qur’an will come on the Day of Resurrection like a young man.” Then he says to his friend: “I am the one who stayed up all night and made you thirsty during the day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2044","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid told us, Ubi told us, we told us Al-Mu'tamir bin Salman said: I heard my father, narrating on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja'd, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, that a man He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, I bought an allotment for the son of so-and-so in a tent in which there is such-and-such. He said: “Shall I not inform you of what Is it more smelly than it? He said: Is there any? He said: “A man learned ten verses.” So the man went and learned ten verses, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. “If Amr ibn Khalid preserved in its chain of transmission Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, then it is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, except that the Basrais are among the companions of The one who was performing Umrah disagreed with him about it.”"
"2045","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Amr bin Ali, and Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, they said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard My father, he narrated, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Ja’d, or Ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Towards him"
"2046","Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Bashar, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, and Muhammad bin Aban told us, And Muhammad bin Yahya bin Fayyad, they said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Badil told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has a family of people.” They said: Who are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “The people of the Qur’an are the people of God and His chosen ones.” “This hadith was narrated in three ways on the authority of Anas. This is the most typical of them.”"
"2047","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Shazan Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “When we learned ten verses from the Qur’an from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, We have not learned from the ten verses that were revealed after them until we know what is in them.” It was said to a business partner? He said: “Yes.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2048","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told me, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Shall I not teach you a Surah like it that has not been revealed in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Qur’an?” I said: Yes, he said: “I hope that you will not leave that door until you know it.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and I stood with him. So he started talking to me while my hand was in his hand, and I started to slow down, for fear that he would leave before he told me about it. When I approached the door, I said: O Messenger. By God, the surah that you promised me, so he said: “How do you recite when you stand up to pray?” So I recited the opening of the book, and he said: “Here, here, and they are the seven repeated verses of which God Almighty said: {And We have given you seven of repeated verses, and the Qur’an The Great} [Al-Hijr: 87] which I have been given. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. There was a disagreement over Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman regarding it. It was narrated by Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, the client of Amir bin Kuraiz, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, and he narrated it Shu'bah, on the authority of Al-Ala' bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka'b
 As for the hadith of Malik bin Anas"
"2049","So Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Malik bin Anas told us, and he told me Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Sa`id, the client of Amir ibn Kuraiz, informed him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ubayy ibn Ka’b while he was He was praying, and when he finished his prayer, he raised his hand and said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put his hand on my hand and said: He wanted to leave from the door of the mosque. He said: “I hope that you will not leave the mosque until you have learned a surah like it that has not been revealed in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Qur’an.” He said: So I started to walk slowly, hoping for that, then I said: O Messenger of God, the surah that you promised me. He said: “How do you recite it when the prayer begins?” He said: So I recited Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, until I came to the end of it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is this surah, and it is the seventh. Al-Muthani, and the Great Qur’an which I have been given.”
 As for the hadith of Shu’bah"
"2050","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hatim Al-Marwazi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us. Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that he recited to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, until he concluded it, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, it is the Seven Repeated Verses, and the Great Qur’an that I have been given.” . “I found this hadith on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b as a witness to Abu Hurairah hearing this hadith on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b from the hadith of Al-Madani.”"
"2051","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Salamah, Muhammad Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Ubayy ibn Ka’b while he was standing praying, but he did not answer him. He said: “What prevented you from answering me, my father?” So he said: I was I was praying, and he said: “Didn’t God, Blessed and Most High, say, ‘Answer God and the Messenger when He calls you?’ [Al-Anfal: 24] Do not leave the mosque until I teach you.” No Surah has been sent down by God in the Torah, the Gospel, or the Psalms like it, and it is the Seven that have been given in length, and it is the Great Qur’an. Al-Bukhari narrated in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih the hadith of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Praise be to God, the Mother of the Qur’an, the Seven Repeated Verses, and the Great Qur’an,” just this word."
"2052","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim told me, on the authority of Abu Gharza, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, we told him Muawiyah bin Hisham, Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: While Gabriel, peace be upon him, was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he heard something from the sky, he raised his head and said: “A door opened from The heavens had never been opened before him. Then, behold, an angel said: Give good tidings of two lights that you have been given that had not been given to a prophet before you: the Opener of the Book, and the End of the Book. Not a single word of Surah Al-Baqarah was recited from it without being given it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. Thus, Muslim narrated this hadith, on the authority of Ahmad ibn Jawwas al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ammar ibn Ruzaiq, in brief."
"2053","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl al-Balkhi informed us, Makki ibn Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Abi Humaid, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih, on the authority of Maqil Ibn Yasar, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I was given the opening of the Book From under the throne, and from the voluntary voluntary prayers.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2054","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali told us, Jarir told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us to Invaders, or a group, so we passed by the people of Abyat, and we hosted them, but they did not entertain us, so we camped with another one, and their master was stung, so they came to us and said: Is any of you performing ruqyah? I said: I am performing ruqyah. He said: Our companion has left. I said: No, we hosted you but you did not host us. They said: We will make it for you. So they made thirty sheep for us. He said: So I went to him and started anointing him and reciting the Fatihah of the Book and repeating it until he was healed. Then we took the sheep and said: We took it while we did not know how to treat what we were eating with what we were eating until we asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we came to him and reminded us. To him, he said: Then he started saying: “How do you know that it is a ruqyah?” I said: O Messenger of God, I did not know that it was a ruqyah, but rather something that God put into me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat and drink for me.” With you with an arrow.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, they narrated it on the authority of Yahya bin Yahya, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id in brief, and Al-Bukhari also narrated a summary of the hadith of Hisham ibn Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of his brother Ma’bad, on the authority of Abu Sa’id.”"
"2055","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim Abdullah Al-Saadi informed us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, he informed us Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told me, Abu Nu’aym told us, Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Kharijah bin Al-Salt Al-Tamimi, on the authority of his uncle, that he passed by a people and among them was an insane person documented in Iron, and some of them said to him: Do you have anything with which to treat this, for your companion has come well? He said: So I recited to him the Fatiha of the Book. Three days, twice each day, and he was healed, so he gave him one hundred sheep. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said: “Eat whoever He ate a telegram of falsehood, but he ate a telegram of truth.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2056","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Ali bin Abdul-Hamid Al-Maani told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, about Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, and he descended, and a man descended beside him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned and said: “Shall I not inform you of the best of the Qur’an?” He said: “So he recited to it, ‘Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.’” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 News about the virtue of Surat Al-Baqarah"
"2057","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Learn Surah Al-Baqarah and Surat Al Imran, for they are The two flowers will shade their companion on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two clouds, or two flocks of birds in flight. This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2058","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr told us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr told us. Muawiyah bin Amr, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, everything has a hump, and the hump of the Qur’an is Surah Al-Baqarah.” It was narrated by Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, with an addition to it."
"2059","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr Al-Asadi, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Surat Al-Baqarah contains a verse that is the master of the Qur’an. It is not read in A house and there is a devil in it, except that the verse of the Throne came out of it.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. The two sheikhs did not narrate it from Hakim bin Jubayr due to weakness in his narrations, but rather left it out due to his extremism in Shiism.”"
"2060","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abi Qais, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najood, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “For every Something is a hump, and the hump of the Qur’an is Surat Al-Baqarah, and when Satan hears Surat Al-Baqarah being recited, he leaves the house in which Surah Al-Baqarah is recited. Al-Baqarah. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and it was narrated with a chain of transmission traceable to the Prophet with a similar chain of transmission.” Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Dashtaki told us, Ubi told us, Amr bin Ubi told us. Qais, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2061","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abi Humaid told us, On the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was given Surah Al-Baqarah from the remembrance “The first.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2062","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Recite Surah Al-Baqarah in your homes, for the devil does not enter a house. Surah Al-Baqarah is recited in it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” It was transmitted by Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas"
"2063","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Khalid told us, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Hussein bin Ali told us. Al-Jafifi, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite Surah Al-Baqarah in your homes, for Satan does not enter a house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited.”"
"2064","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq bin Yusuf told us, Harun bin Abdullah told us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, Harb bin Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his grandfather Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may God be pleased with him, said that he had two dates of dates, and he used to find them running low, so he guarded them one night, and then he was like a boy. The man who had a wet dream greeted him, and he returned the greeting, saying: Is it sexual, or is it human? He said: Rather, a jinn. He said: Show me your hand and I can see it. So, behold, the hand of a dog and the hair of a dog. He said: This is how the jinn was created. He said: The jinn have known that it is There is not a man among them stronger than me. He said: He did not bring you. He said: We were told that you love charity, so we came to share in your food. He said: What will reward us from you? He said: You read the Throne Verse from Surah Al-Baqarah {Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} [Al-Baqarah: 255] He said: Yes, he said: If you read it In the morning you will be rewarded from us until the evening, and if you recite it in the evening you will be rewarded from us until the morning, my father said, so I went in the morning to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted me, so I told him about that, and he said: “The evil one has spoken the truth.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2065","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Al-Ash’ath informed us Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and He sent down from it two verses with which He concluded a surah. Al-Baqarah, and do not recite the Qur’an in a house, and Satan will approach it for three nights.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2066","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told me, Abdullah bin Salih Al-Masry told me, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, about Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God concluded Surah THE HEIFER (al-Baqarah) with two verses He has given you from His treasure which is under the throne. Learn them, and teach them to your wives, for they are a prayer, the Qur’an, and a supplication. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Abdullah bin Wahb, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, mursal."
"2067","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, he told me Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, may God have mercy on him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same. “Muslim narrated the hadith of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “I was given the rings of Surat Al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne.”"
"2068","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal Al-Buzanjardi told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abd told us Al-Mu’min bin Khaled Al-Hanafi, Abdullah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, he said: I said to Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him: On his authority: Tell me about the story of Satan when you captured him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made me give charity to the Muslims, so I put the fruit in A room, and I found a deficiency in it, so I informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “This Satan is taking it.” He said: So I entered the room. Then I closed the door on me, and great darkness came and covered the door. Then he took the form of an elephant, then he took the form of another form, and entered through a crack. The door, so I tightened my garment around me, and he started eating some dates. He said: So I jumped to him, and I held it, and my hands met on it, and I said: O enemy of God, and he said: Leave me, for I am old and have many children, and I am poor, and I am from the Jinn of Nasibin, and we had this town before he was sent. Your companion, when he was sent, we expelled her from it, and he left me. I will not return to you, so I left him, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, came and informed the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in the morning prayer, and his herald called, “Where is Muadh bin Jabal?” So I stood up to him, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “What did your prisoner do, O Muadh?” So I told him and he said: “As for him, he will come back.” So he came back and said: So I entered the room and closed the door, so he entered through the crack in the door and began to eat. of dates, so I did with it as I had done the first time. He said: Leave me alone, for I will not return to you. I said: O enemy of God, did you not say: No? I come back? He said: I will not return, and the sign of that for me is that none of you recites the end of Al-Baqarah and none of us enters his house that night. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. Abdul-Mu’min bin Khalid al-Hanafi, Maruzi, is trustworthy and his hadith is compiled, and Zaid bin narrated from him. Al-Hubab, this very hadith."
"2069","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Warraq informed us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Anmati informed us, Abu Uthman Saeed bin Uthman informed us. Al-Jurjani, in Baghdad, Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-Ukli told us, Abdul-Mu’min ibn Khalid al-Hanafi al-Khurasani, from the people of Marw told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, said: I said to Muadh ibn Jabal, Tell me the story of Satan - then he mentioned the hadith -"
"2070","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim told me, my father told me, Yahya bin Yahya told me, Ismail bin Ja’far told me, Amr bin Abi told us Amr, on the authority of Habib bin Hind Al-Aslami, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever learns the first seven of the Qur’an is good.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2071","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asqalani informed us, Harmala bin Yahya informed us, Abdullah bin Wahb, Amr ibn al-Harith told me that Sa`id ibn Abi Hilal told him, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd ibn Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Learn the Qur’an, for it will intercede for its people on the Day of Resurrection. And read Al-Zahrawan. It was said: What is Al-Zahrawan? He said: “Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or as if they were two clouds, or as two groups of The birds are white, fluffy, and they flit with their wings away from their companions. Learn the cow, for learning it is a blessing, and abandoning it is a regret. The heroine can do it.”
 Mentioning the virtues of surahs and various verses"
"2072","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Uthman Al-Muqri told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Yahya bin Kathir told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Whoever recites Surah Al-Kahf as it was revealed, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection from his place of residence to Mecca, and whoever recites ten verses from the end of it and then The Antichrist came out without any control over him, and whoever performed ablution and then said: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. It was written on parchment, then printed with a stamp, and it was not broken until the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Hashim, so he attributed it to"
"2073","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, and Muhammad bin Musa bin Imran told me The jurist, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Musa told us, they said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: Whoever recites Surat Al-Kahf - then reminds him of something like it -"
"2074","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr Al-Bari told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl Abu Al-Numan told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, not Al-Nahdi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite Surah Yasin when you die.” It was transmitted by Yahya bin Saeed and others on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi. “And the statement about it is the saying of Ibn al-Mubarak, since the increase in trustworthiness is acceptable.”"
"2075","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abbas Al-Jashmi, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A surah of the Qur’an of thirty verses that interceded for a man until he was forgiven, and it is Blessed be He in whose hand is the kingdom.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2076","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni told us, he told me Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I wished it was in The heart of every believer” - meaning, “Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion.” “This chain of transmission according to the Yemenis is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2077","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Abu Gharza, Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail told us, Israel bin Abi Israel, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated His daughter Umm Salamah went to him and said: You are my concubine. He said: So I came to him and he said: What did the Juwayriyah - or the slave girl - do? -» I said: At her mother’s place. He said: «Then the next time you came.» He said: «You came to teach me something that I would say when I dreamed.» He said: «Read and say, O disbelievers. For it is a release from polytheism.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2078","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Yaman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Anazi informed us Al-Basri, Ata bin Abi Rabah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When it is shaken, it is equivalent to half the Qur’an. And say, “O you disbelievers,” it is equivalent to a quarter of the Qur’an, and “Say, ‘He is Allah One,’ it is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih informed us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz Al-Baghdadi informed us, Ghassan bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Jafar bin Maysarah Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say, O disbelievers, a quarter of the Qur’an.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"2079","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Marwazi told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Jubayr, the client of the family of Zayd Ibn al-Khattab, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I have come With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard a man reciting: 2] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is obligatory.” So I asked him: What, O Messenger of God? He said: “Paradise.” Abu Hurairah said: So I wanted to go to the man and give him good tidings, then I was afraid I would miss lunch with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I ate lunch, then I went to the man and found him gone. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2080","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Mahmoud bin Habib told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Dashtaki told us, Amr bin Abi Qais, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najood, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The yellowest of houses is a house in which there is no book. God is something, so recite the Qur’an, for you will be rewarded for it with ten good deeds for every letter. As for me, I do not say “m,” but I say “alif, lam, and meem.” Someone else narrated it on the authority of Al-Dashtaki. Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah told us. Al-Dashtaki, my father told us, Amr bin Abi Qais told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted him like that. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2081","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi informed us, Ja`far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi informed us, in Egypt, Daoud ibn al-Rabi’ told us, Hafs ibn Maysarah, on the authority of Uqba bin Muhammad bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Can’t any of you recite a thousand verses every day?” They said: Who can do that? He said: “Isn’t any of you able to recite your inspiration for multiplication?” “The narrators of this hadith are all trustworthy, but this one is not well-known.”"
"2082","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Umair bin Mirdas told us, Abdullah bin Nafi’ Al-Sayegh told us, Yahya bin Umair, on the authority of his father Umair, the client of Nawfal bin Adiy, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No “One of you will sleep until he has recited a third of the Qur’an.” They said: “O Messenger of God, how can one of us read a third of the Qur’an?” He said: “Can’t he? To recite: “Say, ‘He is Allah, One,’ and ‘Say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of creation,’ and ‘Say, ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.’” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2083","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Ahmad bin Abdul Hamid Al-Harithi told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, that he asked the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about the two exorcists, said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, believed in them in the dawn prayer.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2084","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Warraq told me, Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abi told us, Talha bin told us. Yahya, Abu Burdah told me, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sent Muadh and Abu Musa to Yemen and commanded them to teach the people the Qur’an. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it like this.”"
"2085","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Qadi told us dictation, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Sanjani told us, Abu Al-Taher and Harun bin Saeed told us, They said: Ibn Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub reported, on the authority of Zaban bin Faid, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever reads the Qur’an and acts according to what it contains, his father will be clothed on the Day of Resurrection with a crown whose light is better than The light of the sun is in the houses of this world and it was in it, so what do you think of the one who did it?” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2086","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Bashir bin Muhajir told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever reads the Qur’an And he learned it and acted upon it. On the Day of Resurrection, he will be clothed with a crown of light, the light of which is like the light of the sun, and his parents will be covered with two robes that he will not wear for this world. They say: “With what we were covered?” It is said: “By teaching your son the Qur’an.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2087","Bakr bin Muhammad told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Humaid told us, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Act upon the Qur’an, and permit what it permits, and prohibit what it prohibits. And follow his example, and do not disbelieve in any of it, and whatever is similar to you in it, refer it to God and to those in authority after me, so that they may inform you, and believe. With the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms, and with what was given to the prophets from their Lord. And let the Qur’an and the explanatory statement therein suffice you, for it is an intercessor who intercedes. Verily, there will be a light for every verse on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, I was given Surah Al-Baqarah from the first remembrance, and I was given Taha, and Tawasin, and the hoverflies. From the Tablets of Moses, and I was given the Opener of the Book from under the Throne.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2088","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Saleh told us Al-Marri, narrated by Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man said: O Messenger of God, what deeds? Better? He said: “The migrating situation.” He said: O Messenger of God, what is the migrating situation? He said: “He recites from the beginning of the Qur’an to the end, and from the end to the beginning.”"
"2089","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Saleh Al-Marri told us, and Abu Bakr bin told me Quraysh, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Salih Al-Marri told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa. Al-Amiri, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man said: O Messenger of God, which deed is best? He said: “The one who is traveling.” He said: O Messenger of God, and what is the situation of the one who is traveling? He said: “The one who recites the Qur’an strikes from the beginning until he reaches the end, and from the end until he reaches the beginning. Whenever he arrives, he travels.” “Salih al-Marri was the only one to narrate it, and he was one of the ascetics of the people of Basra, but the two sheikhs did not narrate it.” There is evidence for this from the hadith of Abu Hurairah."
"2090","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Bakr narrated to us, Miqdam bin Dawud bin Talid Al-Ru’ayni narrated to us, Khaled narrated to us Ibn Nizar, Al-Layth Ibn Saad narrated to me, Malik Ibn Anas narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, which work is best? Or which work is more beloved to God? He said: “The presenter, the traveler who opens the Qur’an and closes it, the one who recited the Qur’an from its beginning to its end, and from its end to its beginning. Whenever he comes, he travels.”"
"2091","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Sufyan told us. Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, on the authority of Saad, may God be pleased with him, he said: I came to him and he asked me who you are So I told him about my lineage, and Saad said: I am a merchant of good fortune. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He is not among us who does not sing the Qur’an.” Sufyan said: “He means he can suffice with it.” “And from Sufyan bin Uyaynah there is another chain of narration in it.”"
"2092","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, and Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, he said: Saad, may God be pleased with him, said to him: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “He is not one of us who does not sing the Qur’an.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it with this chain of transmission.” It was narrated by Saeed bin Hassan Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik. “Al-Layth bin Saad disagreed with them, and Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika said, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, on the authority of Saad, may God be pleased with him.” The narrations of Amr bin Dinar, Ibn Jurayj, and Saeed bin Hassan agreed, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik. “Al-Layth bin Saad disagreed with them, and said: On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik.”"
"2093","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, and Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, in Bukhara, Qais bin Anif, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, they said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, on the authority of Saad Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He is not among us who does not sing the Qur’an.” “The narration of Al-Layth is not refuted by the narrations on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, as they are Tabi’an brothers, and the evidence for the authenticity of the two narrations is The narration of Amr bin Al-Harith, who is one of the proven memorizers on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika.”"
"2094","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Suleiman bin Daoud Al-Mahri told us, and Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarraj, they said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, that he told him about people who entered upon Sa’d. Ibn Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him. They asked him about the Qur’an, and Saad said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is not from us.” Whoever does not sing the Qur’an.” “This narration indicates that Ibn Abi Mulaika did not hear it from a single narrator, but rather heard it from narrators of Saad, and Ubayd Allah ibn Al-Akhnas and Asal bin Sufyan narrated the chain of transmission on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika and brought it with two anomalous chains of narration.
 As for the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Al-Akhnas"
"2095","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan Abu Nuh told us, Ubaid Allah bin Al-Akhnas, Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaika told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “He is not one of us who does not sing the Qur’an.” It was narrated by Al-Harith bin Murrah Al-Thaqafi Al-Basri, on the authority of Asal bin Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Harith narrated with this chain of transmission on the authority of Ibn Abbas"
"2096","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami told us, Al-Harith bin Murrah told us, Asal bin Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He is not one of us who does not sing the Qur’an.” “It is not unlikely that Asal bin Sufyan is a delusion, and the hadith goes back to the hadith of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and God knows best. As for the hadith that The two sheikhs agreed to narrate it in the two Sahih books, but other than this text they agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God bless him and grant him peace. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not given permission to anything. He has not given permission to a prophet who sings of the Qur’an.”"
"2097","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, and Abu Al-Hasan told me Ali bin Abbas Al-Iskandarani, in Mecca, and he wrote it to me in his own handwriting. Saeed bin Hashim bin Marthad Al-Tabarani told us, Duhaim told us, Al-Walid bin told us. Muslim, Abu Amr Al-Awza’i told me, Ismail bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Al-Muhajir told me, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid Al-Ansari. May God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has the greatest ear to the man with a good voice reciting the Qur’an, from one who has faith to “His faith.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2098","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Malik bin Mughul told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Khaled Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Malik told us Ibn Mughal, Talha ibn Musarrif al-Yami narrated to me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.” This is how Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir narrated it."
"2099","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Saghani told us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan ibn Saeed, and Muhammad bin Alwan Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Yunus Al-Qurashi told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God and His angels pray over the advanced rows.” And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Beautify your voices.” “By the Qur’an.” This is how it was narrated by Zaida bin Qudamah, Amr bin Abi Qais, Jarir bin Abdul Hamid, Ammar bin Muhammad, and Ibrahim bin Tahman. On the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir
 As for the hadith of Zaydah"
"2100","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad narrated to us in Al-Wayyah, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr Al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us. Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in a long hadith: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Amr bin Abi Qais:"
"2101","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Hamid bin Mahmoud bin Harb told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Saad told us, Amr bin Abi Qais, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha al-Yami, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa bin Aazib, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Jarir bin Abdul Hamid:"
"2102","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Sa`id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf told us Bin Yaqoub Al-Qadi, they said: Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Ammar bin Muhammad"
"2103","So Abdullah bin Saad told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Dahhak told me, Ammar bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Ibrahim bin Tahman:"
"2104","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Azib, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Ishaq Al-Subai’i, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif"
"2105","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Darim, and Abu Sa`id al-Thaqafi told us, they said: Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Abdullah told us. Al-Hadhari, Ja`far bin Humaid told us, Khadij bin Muawiya told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Talha bin Musarrif narrated to me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first rows. And adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Zubaid bin Al-Harith:"
"2106","So Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Dhuhli told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Ali Al-Khazzaz told us, Jandal bin Waqiq told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Zubaid told us Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.” It was narrated by Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif. The hadith is long, but it did not mention “beautify the Qur’an with your voices.”"
"2107","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Talha bin A conjugator, so he mentioned it
 As for the hadith of Al-A’mash"
"2108","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Ismaili, the jurist, dictation narrated to us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Waki’, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Abd Al-Samad bin Ali bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Al-Abbas bin Mihran Al-Razi, Sahl bin Uthman narrated to us, Waki’, and Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Abdullah bin Sa’d narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq narrated to us. Al-Anmati, Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, and al-Thawri, on the authority of al-Amash, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of"
"2109","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih narrated to us in Al-Tabaran, and Abu Nasr Al-Faqih narrated to us in Bukhara, saying: Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ubaid narrated to us. Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, Talha bin Musarrif narrated to me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.” Abdul Rahman said: I had forgotten this word until Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim reminded me of it. Al-Hakim said: “This hadith was narrated by a group, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Talha. The hadith is in its entirety, and this word was not mentioned.” I had forgotten. Yahya bin Saeed and Moaz Al-Anbari»"
"2110","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, my father told me, my father told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: Musaddad told us, we told him Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah - he mentioned the hadith in its length -
 As for the hadith of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah Al-Nakhi"
"2111","So Abu Ali al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Abu Sa`id al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Khaled al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Abd al-Rahman bin Zubaid:"
"2112","So Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Abu Badr Shuja’ bin Al-Walid told us, Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Zubaid Al-Yami, Talhah Ibn Musarrif told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Awsaja Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to come to the direction of the row, to the farthest side, straighten the chests and shoulders of the people and say: “Do not disagree. Then your hearts will differ. Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first rows.”
 “And adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Hammad bin Abi Suleiman:"
"2113","So Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Zarbi told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Talha al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And He will come to us when the prayer is established, and He will wipe our shoulders and say: “Straighten your ranks, and do not differ lest your hearts differ. And may I be gentle with you.” Those who have dreams and prohibitions, and beautify the Qur’an with your voices. Indeed, God and His angels pray in the front row.”
 As for the hadith of Fitr bin Khalifa"
"2114","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Yahya Abdul-Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Hamani told us, Malik bin Mughal, and Fitr bin Khalifa, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara bin Azib, may God be pleased with About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “wiped our shoulders during prayer” - and he mentioned the hadith -
 Al-Baraa said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of his father"
"2115","So Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Numan told us, Muhammad bin Talha told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may God be pleased with them, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: “Do not differ lest your hearts differ. Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first row, and adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Zaid bin Abi Unaisah:"
"2116","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Zaid bin Abi Anisa told us, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, said: The prayer was performed. He mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Hashim Al-Rummani:"
"2117","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Jabir Al-Saqti told us, Suhail bin Ibrahim Al-Jarudy told us, Amr bin Abi told us. Bishr al-Qaisi, then Salam, on the authority of Abu Hashim al-Rummani, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come while we were praying, and he would wipe our chests and say: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Al-Hasan bin Amara"
"2118","So Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad, the jurist Al-Bukhari narrated to us in Nishapur, Salih bin Muhammad Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Shayban bin Farrukh narrated to us, Abdul Aziz narrated to us. Ibn Muslim Al-Qasmali narrated to us Al-Hasan Ibn Amara, on the authority of Talha Ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman Ibn Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Al-Hajjaj bin Artaat:"
"2119","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aisha told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Artaat, and he told us Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Jaafar bin Ahmed Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Al-Khattab told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Artaat told us, On the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Laith bin Abi Sulaym:"
"2120","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Saleh bin Muhammad Al-Razi informed us, Asim bin Ali told us, Yazid bin Ibrahim Al-Tustari told us, Yazid bin Ibrahim Al-Tustari told us, Laith bin Abi Sulaym, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara bin Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Issa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami:"
"2121","So Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Ahmad bin Nasr told me, Abu Nu’aym told us, Issa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami told us, on the authority of Talha bin Musharraf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Adorn the Qur’an.” With your voices
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Fazari:"
"2122","So Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Karabisi informed us, al-Hakim ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, On the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the blind hadith of Abu Al-Yasa’:"
"2123","So Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Uqba told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Anbas told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafis told us, Abu Al-Yasa’, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’ ibn Azib, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar:"
"2124","So Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Aban Al-Muqri told us, Surayj bin Yunus told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.” “We found followers of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’, in narrating this hadith, on the authority of al-Bara’, and they are Zazan Abu Omar, Adi bin Thabit and Aws bin Damaj.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Omar Zazan"
"2125","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Hasanjani narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabbah Al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Abd narrated to us. Al-Rahman Al-Samarqandi, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Sadaqa bin Abi Imran told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices, for a beautiful voice increases the beauty of the Qur’an.”
 As for the hadith of Adi bin Thabit"
"2126","So Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Sarafi told us, Al-Abbas bin Ahmad bin Al-Hasan bin Saeed bin Othman Al-Khazzaz told us, my father told me, he said: I found in my grandfather’s book, Husayn bin Mukhariq told us, Abu Maryam Abdul Ghaffar bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Aws bin Damaj:"
"2127","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman told us, Malik bin Mughul told us, And Fitr bin Khalifa, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Adorn the Qur’an with your voices.” “Then we looked and found that Talhah bin Musarrif had two followers in his narration, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, and they were Al-Hakam bin Utaiba. And Zubaid bin Al-Harith”
 As for the hadith of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba"
"2128","So Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Musa Al-Askari told us, Muhammad bin Bashar, narrated to us by Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-Hakam, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’ May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first row.”
 “And adorn the Qur’an with your voices.”
 As for the hadith of Zubaid bin Al-Harith:"
"2129","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Muhammad bin Bakkar told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Adorn the Qur’an.” With your voices
 Sales book"
"2130","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz said: Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us Al-Makki, Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Bakr told us Ibn Balawayh, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, they said: Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah told us, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Amr bin Al-Aas saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for me, so I went to him, and he ordered me to take my clothes and weapons and then go to him. He said: So I did, then I came to him while he was performing ablution, and he looked up at me, then lowered his head, then said: “O Amr, I want to send you with an army. So God will make you rich and give you peace, and I will grant you a good desire of money.” He said: So I said, O Messenger of God, I did not convert to Islam out of a desire for money, but I I converted to Islam out of a desire to become a Muslim and to be with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “O Amr, what a blessing with good wealth for a good man.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. They did not narrate it, but rather narrated it in the permissibility of asking for money. “The hadith of Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri” from who took it. By His right, the best help is “only.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2130 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2131","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, and Ismail bin Muhammad told me Ibn Al-Fadl, my grandfather told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, Abdullah bin Suleiman bin Abi Salamah told me that he heard Muadh Ibn Abdullah Ibn Khubayb Al-Juhani narrates on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to them with signs of washing. He was of a kind soul. He said, “We thought that he felt sorry for his family, so we said: O Messenger of God, we see that you have become a kind soul.” He said: “Yes, and praise be to God.” He said: Then he mentioned wealth, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no harm in wealth for the one who is pious, and good health.” “For whoever fears Allah is better than wealth and a good soul is blessed.” This is a Madinan hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and the companion who did not name him was Suleiman. Bin Bilal is Yassar bin Abdullah Al-Juhani.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2131 - True"
"2132","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, and Yahya bin Bukair told us, They said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, and Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, and Abu Sa’id Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour informed us, saying: We told him Othman bin Hafs Al-Sadusi, Asim bin Ali told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Abdullah Bin Khalid bin Hazzam, on the authority of his grandfather Khaled bin Hazzam, that Hakim bin Hazzam raided with two horses on the day of Khaybar, and they were wounded, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: My horse was damaged, O Messenger of God, so he gave it to him, then he increased it, and he increased it, then he increased it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “O Wise One, this money is a sweet vegetable, and whoever asks people, they will give him, and the one who asks for it is like one who eats and is not satisfied.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2132 - True"
"2133","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, Rabi’ah bin Sulaiman told me. Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Saeed bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be diligent in seeking this world, for each will be granted ease for what has been decreed for him of it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2133 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2134","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Layth Al-Maruzi told us, Ahmad bin Issa told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not delay sustenance, for no servant was to die until he had reached the last sustenance that was his, so be generous in seeking. “Taking what is permissible and leaving what is forbidden.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And he witnessed it on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir.” It is authentic according to ""Muslim condition""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2134 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2135","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you will die until he has completed his livelihood, so do not Seek provision, and fear God, O people, and be generous in your request. Take what is permissible and leave what is forbidden.” There is also evidence of this on the authority of Ibn Masoud. With extra words
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2135 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2136","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Milhan told us, Ibn Abi Bukair told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, On the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Umayyah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yunus bin Bukayr, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no work that brings one closer to Paradise, except that I have commanded you to do it, and there is no work that brings one closer to Hell, except that I have forbidden you.” On his authority, do not let any of you delay his sustenance, because Gabriel, peace be upon him, impressed upon me that none of you will leave this world until He will complete his sustenance, so fear God, O people, and be generous in seeking, for if any of you is slow in sustenance, let him not seek it by disobeying God. For God does not obtain His grace through disobedience.”"
"2137","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari, Ali bin Issa, and Abu Bakr bin Jafar narrated to us. They said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to us. Al-Abdi, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, Al-Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hanash bin Qais Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who collects money without it being permissible should not be deceived, - or he said: without his right, - If he gives alms, it will not be accepted from him, and whatever remains is his food for the Hellfire. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2138","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi narrated to us, Al-Humaidi narrated to us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: I heard it from Asim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Ayan, and from Jami’ ibn Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abi Wa’il, on the authority of Qais ibn Abi Gharza, who said: We were a people called Brokers, and we were selling in Al-Baqi’, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us and called us with a better name than ours and said: “O merchants! This transaction is attended by lies and oaths, so they tainted it with charity.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it “because I mentioned it.” Abu Wael was the only one to narrate on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Gharza, and this is how it was narrated by Mansour ibn al-Mu’tamir, al-Mughirah ibn Maqsim, and Habib ibn Abi Thabit on the authority of Abi Wael.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2138 - True
 As for the hadith of Mansour"
"2139","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, Abu Hudhayfah and Muhammad bin Many, they said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, and Abu Muhammad bin Musa told us, saying: Muhammad informed us Ibn Ayyub, Yahya Ibn Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi reported, Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Gharza Al-Ghafari, He said: We were in the city, selling and buying goods, and we called ourselves brokers, and people called us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us. One day, he greeted us and called us by a name better than the one we named ourselves and the people called us, and he said: “O merchants, he is witnessing your sale.” Idle talk and swearing, confuse it with charity.”
 As for the hadith of Al-Mughirah"
"2140","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, and Abu Amr told us Ibn al-Sammak, Ali Ibn Ibrahim al-Wasiti told us, Wahb Ibn Jarir told us, and Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein narrated to us, Adam bin Abi Iyas narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh narrated to us, they said: He reported Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Muslim bin Ibrahim narrated to us, they said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abi Wa’il, on the authority of Qais bin Abi A stitch. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us to the market and said: “O merchants, this market is filled with swearing, so mix it with charity.”
 As for the hadith of Habib bin Abi Thabit"
"2141","So Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, and Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein narrated to us, Adam bin Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far narrated to us. Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Gharza, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while we were selling slaves in Medina, and we were called The brokers, so he called us better than what we called ourselves, and said: “O merchants, this sale is attended by idle talk and faith, so distort it. “With charity.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Thawri."
"2142","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani narrated to us, Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, Kulthum bin Jawshan narrated to us. Al-Qushayri, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The honest, trustworthy and Muslim merchant is with the martyrs.” On the Day of Resurrection.” This Kulthum Basri spoke little, and they did not narrate it, and he has a witness in Al-Hasan’s correspondence.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2142 - Kulthum bin Jawshan was deemed weak by Abu Hatim"
"2143","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ali bin Ubaid told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The honest and trustworthy merchant is with the prophets and the truthful.” And the martyrs”"
"2144","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari narrated to us, Mu’la bin Mansour narrated to us, Ismail bin Zakaria, that Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told them, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the prayer place in Medina, and he found people making pledges of allegiance, so he said: “O merchants!” So they responded to him, and raised their eyes and necks to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “The merchants will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2144 - True"
"2145","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour al-Harithi told us, Muadh told us Bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Rashid Al-Habrani told me, that he heard Abd al-Rahman bin Shibl He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The merchants are the ungodly.” They said: O Messenger of God, has not God permitted trading? He said: “Yes, but they swear and sin, and they speak and lie.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And he mentioned Hisham bin Abi Abdullah heard Yahya bin Abi a lot from Abu Rashid, and Hisham is trustworthy and trustworthy, and Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar entered. Among them is Zaid bin Salam
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2145 - True"
"2146","It was narrated to us by Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl, it was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn Issa ibn al-Sakan al-Wasiti, it was narrated to us by Affan ibn Muslim, it was narrated to us by Aban ibn Yazid Al-Attar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Rashid Al-Habrani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shibl, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The merchants are the ungodly, the merchants are the ungodly.” They said: O Messenger of God, has not God made trading permissible? He said: “Yes, but they say something and they lie, and they swear and they sin.”"
"2147","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, and Abu Bakr told us Ibn Ishaq Al-Faqih, and Abu Bakr Ibn Ja’far Al-Quta’i. Abu Bakr Ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal reported, My father told me, Wahb bin Jarir told us, my father told us, he said: I heard Yunus bin Ubaid, speaking on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Amr bin Taghlib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of the signs of the Hour is that money will overflow, ignorance will increase, temptations will appear, and trade will spread.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and its chain of narration according to their condition is correct, except that Amr bin Taghlib has no narrator other than Al-Hasan.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2147 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2148","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani and Ibrahim ibn Ismat al-Adl narrated to us, saying: Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa narrated to us. Ibn Masoud, Zuhair Ibn Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Muhammad Ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Jubayr Ibn Mutim, on the authority of his father, that a man He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, which country is evil? He said: “I don’t know.” When Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him, he said: “O Gabriel, which country is evil?” He said: I do not know until I ask my Lord. Then Gabriel departed and stayed as long as God wished for him to stay, then he came and said: O Muhammad, you asked me what... Countries are evil, and I said, “I do not know.” Indeed, I asked my Lord and said: “Which countries are evil?” He said: Its roots: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Qais bin al-Rabi’ and Amr bin Thabit bin Abi al-Miqdam. On the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, and he has an authentic witness.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2148 - Zuhair Dhu Munkar, this is one of them, and Ibn Aqeel is soft on it and has an authentic witness, then he mentioned Hadith No. 2149"
"2149","It was narrated to us by Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa al-Adl, it was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn Ayyub, it was narrated to us by Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hasanjani, and Yahya ibn Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: A man came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, which place is best? He said: “I don’t know.” He said: Which places are evil? He said: “I do not know.” Then Gabriel came to him and said: “Ask your Lord.” Gabriel said: “We are not asking him about anything.” He jumped up, almost being struck by shock. Among them was Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. When Gabriel ascended, God Almighty said: Muhammad asked you which place is best? You said: I don't know. He asked you: Which places are evil? You said: I don't know. He said: He said: Yes. He said: Tell him that “the best places are the mosques, and the worst places are the markets.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2149 - True"
"2150","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoob Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, Khalid Al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “May those among you who have dreams and prohibitions be relenting, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And do not differ lest your hearts differ. “And beware of the turbulence of the markets.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not narrated by Al-Bukhari.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2150 - Al-Bukhari did not narrate it, and it is according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2151","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin told us Hawshab, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saskiski, on the authority of Ibn Abi, he fulfilled it, so this verse was revealed: “Indeed, those who buy God’s covenant and their oaths for a price A little bit} [Al Imran: 77] The verse is Ibrahim al-Saskiski, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, that a man set up a commodity for himself, so he swore to God that he would be given with it what he had not It is given: “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, but rather they agreed on the hadith of Amr bin Dinar and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Kitten: A man who swore on his property. Hadith, and this is different from that, with the addition of the revelation of the verse and other things.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2151 - True"
"2152","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Wahb bin Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya Ibn Ayyub, narrating, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Shamasa, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “A Muslim is the brother of another Muslim, and it is not permissible for a Muslim, if he makes a sale from his brother in which there is a defect, not to explain it to him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2152 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2153","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, saying: Bishr bin Musa informed us, Al-Humaidi narrated to us, narrated to us Sufyan, Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man selling food. He liked it, so he put his hand into it, and behold, it was wet food. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He who deceives us is not one of us.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it like this.” It was narrated by Muhammad and Ismail Ibn Ja’far Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Al-Ala.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2153 - Narrated by Muslim with another wording
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Jafar"
"2154","So Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anbari told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, he informed us Muhammad bin Jafar, Al-Alaa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the market and saw ripened wheat. So he put his hand into it and found it wet, so he said: “Whoever deceives us is not one of us.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2154 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 As for the hadith of Ismail bin Ja’far bin Abi Kathir:"
"2155","So Da'laj bin Ahmad Al-Sijzi told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, and Abu Al-Fadl bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yazid, Ali bin Hajar narrated to us, they said: Ismail bin Jafar narrated to us, Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Kitten, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a piece of food, so he put his hand in it, and his fingers got wet, and he said: “What is this, O The food companion? He said: The sky struck it, O Messenger of God. He said: Why did you not place it above the food so that the people could see it? Then he said: “Whoever deceives us is not of me,” and he came out. Muslim Hadith Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever deceives us is not one of us.” As for the explanation of the situation in this case He did not narrate the hadiths, and they are all authentic according to the conditions of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2155 - Narrated by Muslim in brief"
"2156","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Jawab Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq, Abdullah bin Issa told us, on the authority of Umayr bin Saeed, on the authority of his uncle, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Al-Baqi’ and saw He put his hand in and brought out something he hated and said: “Whoever cheats with us is not one of us.” This is an authentic hadith. “And the uncle of Umair bin Saeed is Al-Harith bin Suwayd Al-Nakhai
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2156 - True"
"2157","Abu Bakr bin Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us Hashim bin Al-Qasim, Abu Ja’far Al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Malik, Abu Siba’ narrated to us, he said: I bought a she-camel from a poor house. Ibn Al-Asqa’, when I went out with it, Wathilah met me while he was pulling his garment, and said: O Abdullah, what did you buy? I said: Yes, he said: Explain to you what is in it? I said: What is wrong with her? She is fat and appears to be healthy. He said: Did you want to travel with it or did you want meat with it? I said: I wanted to perform Hajj with it. He said: So take it back. Its owner said: You only wanted this. May God bless you. You will spoil me. He said: For I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “It is not permissible for anyone to sell anything unless he explains what is in it, and it is not permissible for someone who knows"
"2158","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri narrated to us, Al-Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Wael bin Dawud, on the authority of Jamei’ bin Umair, on the authority of his uncle Abu Burdah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked which of the earnings is better or better? He said: “The man’s work is with his own hands, and every sale is acceptable.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2158 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2159","Abu Al-Abbas narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad narrated to us, Al-Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated, on the authority of Wael bin Daoud, on the authority of Saeed bin Umair, on the authority of his uncle, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked which income is better? He said: “An accepted profit.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “Wa’il bin Dawud and his son Bakr are trustworthy, and Yahya bin It is certain that the uncle of Saeed bin Umair is Al-Baraa bin Aazib, and if the revolutionary and a partner disagree, then the ruling goes to the revolutionary.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2159 - True"
"2160","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Al-Masoudi narrated, on the authority of Wael Ibn Dawud, on the authority of Abaya Ibn Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, on the authority of his father, he said: It was said: O Messenger of God, which earnings are better? He said: “A man’s earnings are in his own hands, and every sale is justified.” This is a third disagreement over Wael bin Dawud, except that the two sheikhs did not deviate from Al-Masoudi. And its place is honesty.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2160 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2161","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah Al-Qanabi told us, Abdullah told us Al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man owed his debtor ten dinars, and he said: By God, I will not leave you until you fulfill my judgment or bring me a burden. He said: So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bore her and brought him as much as he had promised him, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: “Where did you get this gold?” He said: From a mineral. He said: “We have no need for it as there is no good in it.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fulfilled it for him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2161 - True"
"2162","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan narrated to us, Ali bin Issa narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated to us, they said: Wahb bin Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khaled bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A time will come upon the people during which no one will remain except that he has consumed usury. “His dust” Our imams differed regarding Al-Hasan’s hearing on the authority of Abu Hurairah, so if it is authentic that he heard it from him, then this is an authentic hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2162 - Al-Hasan hearing this from Abu Hurairah is authentic"
"2163","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Ezra told us, Ja`far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade monopolizing Food.” Muslim narrated the hadith of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Muammar bin Abd Allah bin Nadlah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one monopolizes except a sinner.” This hadith is one of the things that cannot be contradicted if it does not It is authentic that a hadith of a companion is not narrated by two Tabi’is, because this Muammar had no narrator other than Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab. As for the hadith of al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah is not in that word, and it was narrated in rebuking, about hoarding food and abstaining from consoling Muslims in distress. News must be"
"2164","What Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he told us Israel, on the authority of Ali bin Salem bin Thawban, Ali bin Zaid told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “The monopolist is cursed,” including:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2164 - Ali bin Salem is weak"
"2165","What Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqaili informed us, Asbagh ibn Zaid Al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He hoarded food for forty nights, then he is innocent of God, and God is innocent of him. And any of the people of Arsah among whom a hungry person becomes hungry, then you will be innocent. Some of them are under the protection of God,” including:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2165 - Amr bin Al-Husayn Al-Uqaili left it, but Usbaa bin Zaid Al-Juhani was soft about it."
"2166","What Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Usayli told us, Abdul-A’la bin Hammad Al-Narsi told us, he told us Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever monopolizes wants If he exaggerates this against the Muslims, then he is a sinner, and he has been freed from the protection of God.” Among them are:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2166 - Al-Usaily was stealing hadiths
 What Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Aziz al-Dabbas told us, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid al-Sayegh told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Yahya, Suleiman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abi Alqamah, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He who spends the night full while his neighbor is hungry next to him is not a believer,” including:"
"2167","What Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told me, my grandfather told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Muhammad bin Talha told me, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr bin al-Mughirah, on the authority of his uncle Al-Isa bin al-Mughirah, he said: The Messenger of God passed by May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He saw a man in the market selling food at a price that was cheaper than the market price. He said: “You are selling in our market at a price that is cheaper than Our price? He said: Yes, he said: “Patience and seeking reward?” He said: Yes. He said: “Rejoice, for the one who brings it to our market is like a mujahid in the path of God, and the one who monopolizes our market is like an atheist in the Book of God.” Among them:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2167 - Disgusting news and a dark chain of transmission"
"2168","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih did not tell us, Muhammad bin Yunus told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, Zaid Abu Al-Mu'alla, and Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying: Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated to us, Amr bin Ali narrated to us, Al-Mu'tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, He said: I heard Zaid Abul-Mu’alla, speaking on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil ibn Yasar. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever enters into Some of the prices of the Muslims were to be exorbitant to them. It was God’s right to throw him into most of Hell, with his head down.” These hadiths I asked for the six and took them out in their place in this book out of hope for the distress people are in. And God reveals them even if it is not from Condition of this book """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2168 - I do not know Zayd, so consider these six hadiths"
"2169","Ahmad bin Kamil told us, Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Sa’id bin Amir and Affan told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, and he reported Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Yahya bin Muhammad narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid bin Zurayi narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abi Al-Jawza, said: I asked Al-Hasan ibn Ali what he mentioned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard him say: “Let What gives you doubt, to what does not make you doubt, for good is reassurance and evil is doubt.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it was narrated verbally. ""another""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2169 - True"
"2170","It was narrated to us by Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari, and Abu Bakr bin Jafar, Ali bin Issa, and Abdullah bin Saad narrated to us. They said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to us. Al-Abdi, Abu Salih Mahboub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah Al-Nakhi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abu Maryam, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza, said: I said to Al-Hasan bin Ali: Like the one you were during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what did you understand? About him? He said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you, for Evil is doubt and good is reassurance.” Witnessed by the hadith of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2170 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in this matter"
"2171","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, he told us هِشَامٌ الدَّسْتُوَائِيُّ، وَ"
"2172","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh, and Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, On the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Nawwas bin Samaan Al-Ansari, he said: I asked the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about righteousness and sin, he said: “Righteousness is good character, and sin is what is wavering in your heart and you hate for people to find out about it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2172 - True"
"2173","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Usama bin Zayd reported, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was hungry one night, and it was said Why did he keep you up? He said: “I found a fallen date and ate it, then I remembered dates. We had charity dates, so I do not know if that was the date. “Or from the dates of my family, that kept me awake.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2173 - True"
"2174","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Muhammad bin Rafi’, and Muhammad bin Yahya told us, They said: Abdul Razzaq narrated to us, Muammar narrated, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I do not know whether I am followed by a cursed one or not, and I do not know whether Dhul-Qarnayn is a prophet or not, and I do not know the punishments are expiations.” To her family or not.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2174 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2175","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Amr bin Abi Salamah narrated to us, Abu Ma’bad Hafs narrated to us. بْنُ غَيْلَانَ،"
"2176","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, about Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that a man bought a boy from another man in the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had God willing, then he returned him for a defect he found, and the man said when the boy responded to him: O Messenger of God, he had taken advantage of my boy since he was with him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The tax is guaranteed.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2176 - True"
"2177",""
"2178","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us, Muhammad bin Al-Jahm told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, and Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, they said: Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Omar bin Ja’far Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Ibn Abu Dhib, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Al-Ja’d told us, Ibn Abi told us Dhi’ib, on the authority of Mukhlid ibn Khafaf, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The tax is guaranteed.” And the hadith of Asim: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided that the tax is subject to security.” It was narrated by Al-Thawri, Ibn Al-Mubarak, and Yahya bin Sa’id on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib “As for the hadith of Al-Thawri”"
"2179","So Bukayr bin Muhammad told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Qubaisa told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Abdullah al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Mukhlid bin Khafaf, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “decided that the tax should be guaranteed.” As for the hadith of Ibn Al-Mubarak, “"
"2180","So Al-Hasan bin Halim informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, on the authority of Mukhald Ibn Khafaf, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The tax is guaranteed.” As for the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed,"
"2181","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Mukhald Ibn Khafaf, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “decided that the tax should be guaranteed.”"
"2182","Sheikh Abu Al-Walid told us, Ahmad bin Al-Hasan bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Khaythamah told us, Zuhair bin Harb told us, Muadh told us Ibn Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two With the option, as long as they do not separate, and each one of them takes from the sale what he likes.” He said it three times. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.” They did not take it out with this increase.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2182 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2183","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in Jumada al-Akhira in the year three hundred and ninety-seven, he reported Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq, Musa ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, Abdullah bin Buraida told me, on the authority of his father, that when Salman came to Medina, he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With a gift on a plate, he placed it in his hands and said: “What is this, Salman?” He said: It is charity for you and for your friends. He said: “I do not eat charity.” So he took it up and then brought him the next day a similar one, so he placed it in his hands and said: “What is this?” He said: A gift for you. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companions: “Eat.” He said: “Who are you for?” He said: To some people. He said: “Then ask them to write to you.” He said: Write to me about such-and-such a palm tree that I will plant for them, and he will stand on it. Salman until it is fed. He said: So they did. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and planted all the palm trees, except for one palm tree that Omar planted and fed. His palm trees are from his age, except for that palm tree. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who planted it?” They said: Omar, “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, planted it from his own hand, and he carried it during its year.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. “He narrated it.” Sheikh Abu Bakr, in the chapter on the license regarding the seller’s stipulation of the service of the sold slave, at a specified time. He has evidence from the hadith of Ibn Abbas. On the authority of Salman, it is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2183 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2184","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’la bin Mansour told us, Yaqoub Abu Yusuf told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq reported, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Salman told me, that a Jewish man He bought it and brought it to Medina. He said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a gift and said: This is charity. So he said to his companions: “Eat.” He did not eat, then he mentioned the hadith similar to it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2184 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2185","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman bin Harb narrated to us, Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed narrated to us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad narrated to us Ibn Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, Yahya Ibn Muhammad Ibn Yahya narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid Ibn Zurayi narrated to us, all of them on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr Ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to advance or sell, nor are there any conditions in a sale, nor is there any profit. “He is not guaranteed, and he does not sell what you do not have.” This is a hadith that, according to the condition of a group of Muslim imams, is authentic. “And this is how it was narrated by Dawud ibn Abi Hind.” And Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman and others, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, and it was narrated by Ata bin Muslim al-Khorasani, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib With extra words
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2185 - True"
"2186","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, on the authority of Abu al-Shawareb al-Qurashi, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi, Yazid bin Zurayi Al-Ramli narrated to us, Ata Al-Khurasani narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdul Allah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas said: I said: O Messenger of God, I hear things from you that I fear I will forget. Do you give me permission to write them down? He said: “Yes.” He said: It was in what was written on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that when he sent Attab bin Usayd to the people of Mecca, he said: “Tell them that it is not permissible to make a sale in a sale, nor to sell something that one does not own, nor to make an advance sale, nor to impose any conditions in a sale.”"
"2187","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Ahmad bin Qarqoub Al-Tamar told me in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, he told me Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah, that his uncle, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him. Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi and Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Ibn Ziyad narrated to us. Abu Uwais, my brother Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah, that His uncle, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought a horse from a Bedouin man. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed him to pay the price of his horse. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked quickly and slowed down. The Bedouin, and men began to oppose the Bedouin and bargain with the Persians, not realizing that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had bought him. Some of them increased the amount of the Bedouin, and when they had increased, the Bedouin called out: O Messenger of God, if you are the buyer of this horse, then buy it, otherwise I sold it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up when he heard the call of the Bedouins, until the Bedouin came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Or Didn't I buy it from you? He said: No, by God, I did not sell it to you. He said: “Rather, I bought it from you.” Then the people began to seek refuge with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Bedouins, and they were They retreated, and the Bedouin began to say: Come, bear witness that I have pledged allegiance to you. Then Khuzaymah said: I bear witness that you have pledged allegiance to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached Khuzaymah and said: “To what do you bear witness?” He said: Because you believe me. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made “the testimony of Khuzaymah the testimony of two men.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and its men, by agreement of the two sheikhs, are trustworthy. They did not narrate it. “And Ammarah bin Khuzaymah also heard this hadith from his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2187 - True"
"2188","Professor Abu Al-Walid told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib and Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, they said: Abdah bin Abdullah told us Al-Khuza’i, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Muhammad bin Zurarah bin Abdullah bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit told me, Amara bin Khuzaymah told me, On the authority of his father, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought from Sawa ibn al-Harith al-Muharbi a horse, but he denied it and testified. He had Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “What made you bear martyrdom when you were not with him?” He said: You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of God, but I believed what you said and I knew that you were only saying the truth. He said: “Whoever witnesses his calamity and bears witness against it, it is sufficient for him.”"
"2189","Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahan Al-Khazzaz in Mecca told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We sold the mothers of the children during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He and Abu Bakr, peace and blessings be upon him, and when Omar forbade us, we finished.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it and he has a valid witness.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2189 - According to Muslim’s conditions and his witness is authentic"
"2190","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us, and Yusuf ibn Yaqoub informed us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq informed us, he informed us. Shu’bah, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, who said: “We used to sell the mothers of children at the time of the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2190 - True"
"2191","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz and Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Asbahani told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman who gives birth to her master is free after his death.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. “They bring it out.” Abu Bakr bin Abi Sabrah Al-Qurashi followed him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2191 - Hussein is abandoned
 Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara. Abu Ismah Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil told us. Abdullah bin Maslamah Al-Qanabi, Abu Bakr bin Abi Sabrah told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the mother of Abraham when she gave birth to him: “He freed her son.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2191 - Hussein is abandoned"
"2192","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Affan bin Muslim and Hibban bin Hilal told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of love until it becomes strong, and the sale of grapes until they turn black, and about selling dates until they turn red and turn yellow.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “But they agreed on a hadith Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, regarding the prohibition of selling dates until they ripen.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2192 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2193","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz and Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati informed us, saying: Atiq bin Yaqoub Al-Zubayri told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr Al-Makki, he said: I heard Abu Sa’id al-Sa’idi and Ibn Abbas giving a fatwa for one dinar for two dinars. فَقَالَ لَهُ أَبُو أُسَيْدٍ السَّاعِدِيُّ وَأَغْلَظَ لَهُ، قَالَ فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: مَا كُنْتُ أَظُنُّ أَنَّ أَحَدًا يَعْرِفُ قَرَابَتِي مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says to me like this, O Abu Usayd. Abu Usayd said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The dinar In dinars, dirhams for dirhams, a saa of wheat for a saa of wheat, a saa of barley for a saa of barley, and a saa of salt for a saa of salt, there is no preference between them in “Something of that.” Ibn Abbas said: “This is just something I was saying, and I had not heard anything about it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not They brought it out in this context, and Atiq bin Yaqoub was a Qurayshi sheikh from the people of Medina.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2193 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2194","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi and Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Nasr Abd al-Malik bin Abd al-Aziz al-Tamar told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, A man said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so has a palm tree, and I am setting up my wall with it, so command him to give me the permission to set up my wall with it. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Give her a palm tree in Paradise.” He refused, and Abu Al-Dahdah came to him and said, “Send me a palm tree near my wall.” He said: So he did. He said: Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have bought the palm tree in my garden, so he made it his own. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “How many fresh stalks of Abu Ad-Dahdah will be in Paradise” repeatedly, so he went to his wife and said, “O Umm Ad-Dahdah, come out of The wall, for I sold it for a palm tree in Paradise, and she said: You have won the sale, or a word similar to it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim” and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2194 - According to the conditions of Muslim and his witness, then he mentioned Hadith No. 1295"
"2195","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Hatim al-Adl told us about Marw, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah al-Nahdi told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: There is such-and-such person in my neighborhood who has hurt me and made it difficult for me to find the place where he was, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him and said: “Sell me.” He said: “Give it away.” So-and-so said: “Give it away.” He said: “So sell it for a bunch in Paradise.” He said: “No.” Peace be upon him: “I have not seen anyone more stingy than you except the one who is stingy with greetings.”"
"2196","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us. He said, “I think it was once.” Hilal bin Al-Ala’ bin Hilal bin Omar Al-Raqi narrated to us. My father narrated to us. Al-Alaa bin Hilal, Abu Hilal bin Omar narrated to me, Abu Omar bin Hilal narrated to me, Abu Ghalib narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “It is enough of a lie for a person to narrate everything he has heard, and it is enough of a stinginess for a person to say, ‘Taking my rights, no.’” “I leave something of it.” This is an authentic chain of narration, for the fathers of Hilal bin Al-Ala are trustworthy imams, and Hilal was the imam of the people of the Peninsula in his time.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2196 - Sahih and Hilal’s fathers are trustworthy"
"2197","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani narrated to us, Musa bin Dawud Al-Dhabi and Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Al-Walid narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “bought Safiyya from Dihya al-Kalbi for seven heads.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2197 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2198","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir Al-Juhani, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In the custody of a slave Three nights.” Saeed said: So I said to Qatada: How can this be? He said: If the buyer finds a defect in the commodity, he returns it within those days, and does not ask for proof. If days have passed, then he does not He has the right to return it unless there is proof that he bought it and that is a defect in it. Otherwise, the seller swears an oath that he did not sell it and that there is a defect in it. This is what Saeed and Hammam said, on the authority of Qatada, and likewise it was narrated by Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2198 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2199","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Yunus told us Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uqba ibn Aamir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no covenant for more than four.” As for the disagreement Hisham Al-Dastawai, both of them"
"2200","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hisham told us, and Ali bin Hamshadh, Ahmad bin Salamah narrated to us, Bundar and Abu Musa narrated to us, saying: Muadh bin Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The custody of a slave is for four nights.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but it is based on “Sending, for Al-Hasan did not hear from Uqba bin Amir, and he has a witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2200 - The chain of transmission is authentic, but Al-Hasan did not hear from Uqba"
"2201","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Ibn Abi Omar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to me, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Hibban ibn Munqidh was a weak man, and he had been smitten in the head by a woman, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made him He was granted the option while he bought three, and his tongue was heavy, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Sell and say: No confusion.” So I used to hear him saying: No cheapness, no cheapness, and he used to buy something and bring it to his family, and they would say: This is expensive, and he would say: Indeed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me the choice to sell
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2201 - True"
"2202","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Faqih told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb al-Dhabi, and Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, They said: Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Mujabar narrated to us, Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she was being judged and it was said to her: What do you have to do with the debt when you do not have the right to pay it? She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no servant who has the intention of performing his religion except that he will have help from God. I am seeking that help.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “It was narrated on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Aisha Like him
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2202 - Ibn Mujbar and Abu Zur’ah narrated it, and Al-Nasa’i said it is abandoned, but Ahmad authenticated it."
"2203","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Ali says: Aisha was being condemned, so she was asked: What do you have to do with your debt? She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There is no servant who has the intention of performing his religion except that he has help from God, so I am “Am I seeking that help?” And the hadith of Maimuna bears witness to it."
"2204","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, and Professor Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Jarir narrated, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ziyad bin Amr bin Hind, on the authority of Imran bin Hudhayfah, on the authority of Maimunah, that she used to be judged and used to sin frequently, so she was told about that and she said: “No.” I leave debt, because it has help from God, and I seek that help.”"
"2205","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Khalidi informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, Abu Nu`aym Dirar ibn Surad informed us, Muhammad informed us Ibn Ismail Ibn Abi Fudaik, then Yahya Ibn Mansour Al-Qadi informed me, Abu Bakr Muhammad Ibn Muhammad Ibn Raja’ told us, he told us Yaqoub bin Humayd bin Kasib, Ibn Abi Fudayk told us, Sa’id bin Sufyan Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God is with the creditor until he pays off his debt, as long as it is not something that He dislikes.”"
"2206","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Al-Manhal told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Bishr bin Numayr, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever owes a debt, and it is within his soul to repay it, and then he dies, God has transgressed from him and satisfied his adversary with whatever He wished. And whoever owes a debt and does not have the soul to repay it, and then dies, God will retaliate for his adversary on his behalf. on the Day of Resurrection”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2206 - Bishr is abandoned"
"2207","Professor Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Quraysh narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Minhal, Yazid bin Zuray’ narrated to us, Amara bin Abi Hafsa narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He (peace and blessings of God be upon him) two garments of thick, rough diameter, so I said: O Messenger of God, your garments are rough and thick, and you wear them in them and they become heavy. On you, and so-and-so was presented with garments from the Levant, so if you sent to him and took two garments from him for a moderate amount, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I know what Muhammad wants. He wants to take my clothes and spoil me with them. So the Messenger came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he told him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “They lied. They knew that I feared God and showed them trustworthiness.” This is an authentic hadith according to Al-Bukhari’s condition, but they did not narrate it. “It was narrated on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hafsa, briefly.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2207 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2208","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Amr bin Marzuq and Amr bin Hakam told us, they said: Shu`bah narrated to us, Ali bin Hamshadh narrated to us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated to us, Muhammad bin Bashar, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, They said: Muhammad bin Ja`far narrated to us, Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I said: Oh Messenger of God, your clothes are thick, so if you took them off and sent to so-and-so merchant, and he sent you two clothes to the ease, he said: “So send to him Send me two clothes to facilitate? He refused"
"2209","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Asbahani told us, and Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ayyub and Al-Hussein bin Bashar said: Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A caravan came and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bought some of it and won a few yards of gold, so he gave it in charity. And he said: “I do not buy what I do not have the price for.” Al-Bukhari protested with Ikrimah, and Muslim protested. Bismak and Sharik “And the hadith is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2209 - True"
"2210","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Bishr bin Ubaid Al-Darisi told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Religion is the banner of God on earth. “That he humiliates a servant and places it around his neck.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2210 - A weak human being"
"2211","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza al-Zubayri told us, Ibn Abi Muzahim told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abu Salih, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to pray With these words: “O God, You are the First, and there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, and there is nothing after You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every living creature that I stumble upon.” In Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, and from the torment of the grave, and from the torment of the Fire, and from the temptation of wealth, and from the temptation of poverty, and I seek refuge in You. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2211 - True"
"2212","Ali bin Hamshadh narrated to us, Hisham bin Ali narrated to us, Abdullah bin Raja narrated to us, Saeed bin Salamah bin Abi Al-Hussam narrated to us, Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Al-Alaa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kathir, the client of Muhammad ibn Jahsh, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahsh, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting where the funerals were being laid out, so he raised his head towards the sky, then lowered his gaze, and placed his hand on the sky. His forehead, and he said: “Glory be to God, Glory be to God, God has not sent down any stress.” He said: So we knew and remained silent, until tomorrow came, I asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, what is the emphasis that has been sent down? He said: “Concerning debt. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if a man were killed in the cause of God, and then lived while owing a debt, he would not enter Paradise until his debt was paid off.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2212 - True"
"2213","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib Al-Abdi narrated to us, Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid informed us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin al-Nadr informed us, he told us Muawiyah bin Amr, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, and Abu Abdullah bin Yaqoub told us, he told us Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, Amer Al-Shaabi narrated to me, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one day, and when he came, he said: “Is there anyone here from the children of so-and-so?” The people remained silent, and whenever he asked them for something, they remained silent. Then he said: Is there anyone here from the children of so-and-so? Then a man said: This is so-and-so. He said: “Your friend has been imprisoned at the gate of Paradise because of a debt he owed.” So a man said: I owe his debt. So he paid it off. This is how Firas narrated it, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi"
"2214","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yahya bin Hammad and Affan bin Muslim told us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, Ali bin Hamshadh narrated to us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Saeed narrated to us Al-Asbahani, Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Dalani, on the authority of Firas, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim and Muhammad bin Ghalib reported, saying: Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Samarra. Ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one day and said: “Is there one of the sons of so-and-so here?” So he called out to three people, but no one answered him. Then he said: “The man who died among you was kept away from Paradise because of the debt he owed. If you wish, So ransom him, and if you wish, hand him over to the punishment of God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it due to a disagreement about it from Sa’id bin ""stolen"""
"2215","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Haytham told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Aban told us, Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Samaan bin Mushinj, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Warraq told me, he told us Al-Hasan bin Sufyan, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Simaan Ibn Mushinj, on the authority of Samurah Ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar. It is unfortunate that he explains the narration of Ismail bin Abi Khaled and Firas bin Yahya from the narration of the imams that is proven from them with something like: These narrations, and God knows best"
"2216","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, he said: I heard Haywa bin Shuraih, speaking, On the authority of Bakr bin Amr Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Shuaib bin Zur’ah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, that he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said to his companions, “Do not celebrate yourselves.” It was said: O Messenger of God, why should we protect ourselves? He said: “By religion.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2216 - True"
"2217","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, he informed us Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Ma`dan bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever separates the soul and body and is innocent of three things will enter Paradise: deceit, debt, and arrogance.” Abu Awanah followed him, on the authority of Qatadah in Establishing this chain of narration
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2217 - Abu Awanah followed it according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2218","Ahmad bin Sulaiman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, and Affan bin Muslim, they said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Whoever dies and is innocent of three things: arrogance, deceit, and debt, will enter Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”"
"2219","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih, Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl, and Da’laj ibn Ahmad al-Sijistani informed us. They said: Hisham ibn Ali Al-Sirafi, Abdullah bin Raja’ told us, Sa’id bin Salamah bin Abi Al-Hussam told me, Saleh bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Sa’ad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The soul of the believer is attached to his religion until “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs,” and they did not narrate it due to the narration of Al-Thawri in which he said on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar bin Abu Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he is Ibrahim bin Saad, due to his memorization and mastery, he is more knowledgeable about his father’s hadith than anyone else.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2219 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2220","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of his father, and he told me Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih, in Bukhara, Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz narrated to us, and Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, he informed us Ahmad bin Bishr bin Saeed Al-Murtadi, they said: Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Warkani narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Sa’d narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The soul of the believer is dependent on his debt until it is paid off.”"
"2221","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, I am Abu Al-Muthanna, Musaddad told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim Al-Hijri told us, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Satan despairs of having idols worshiped.” In the land of the Arabs, but apart from that, he will be satisfied with the deplorable deeds of your deeds, which are the evils. So avoid injustices as much as you can, for The servant will come on the Day of Resurrection, and he will have good deeds that he believes will save him. And still a servant will stand up and say: O Lord, so-and-so has wronged me. Darkly, so it is said: Erase some of his good deeds until no good deeds remain of him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2221 - True"
"2222","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Zuhayr told us, Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Yahya bin Rashid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whose intercession is impossible Without any limit from the limits of God, God has gone against Him in His matter, and whoever dies while owing a debt, then there is no dinar or dirham, but rather good deeds and evil deeds. He disputes wrongfully while he knows it. He will remain in the wrath of God until he is removed, and whoever says about a believer what is not in him, he will be imprisoned in the stench of delusion until he comes. Based on what he said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2222 - True"
"2223","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, My father told me, Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Ubaid bin Abdul Wahid told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “A man who did not He never did good, and he used to pay people in debt. He would say to his Messenger, “Take what is easy, and leave what is difficult.” He moved beyond, perhaps God would overlook us. When he died, God said: Have you ever done good? He said: No, except that I had a boy, and I used to pay debts to people, so when I sent him to be paid, I said to him: Take what is easy, and leave what is difficult. And go beyond, perhaps God will go beyond us. God said: I have overlooked you. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2223 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2224","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Makki told us, Hatim bin Ismail, on the authority of Abu Harzah Ya’qub ibn Mujahid, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: My father and I went out to seek knowledge in this neighborhood of The Ansar, before they were destroyed. The first person we met was Abu Al-Yusr, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with him was a boy of his, and upon him A Maafari sack, and his servant was wearing a Maafari sack, and he had a bundle of newspapers with him, and my father said to him: It is as if I see a flash of anger on your face. He said: Yes, I had money from so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, a thief, so I went to his family and said, “Is it a sin?” They said: No, so his son came out and I said to him: Where is your father? He said: He heard what you said, so he entered my mother’s couch. So I said: Get out, for I know where you are. So he came out to me, and I told him: What made you hide from me? He said: By God, I will speak to you and not lie to you. I was afraid, by God, that I would speak to you and deny you, or that I would promise you and break your promise, and you were the companion of the Messenger. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so I said: By God, and by God, were you insolvent? So I said: By God. He said: By God. So I said: By God. He said: By God. He said: So he unfolded the scroll and erased the truth, and said, “If you find a judgment, then fulfill it. If not, you are in a state of law.” I bear witness, “These eyes of mine have seen it.” And he put He placed his fingers on his eyes, and these ears of mine heard. He put his fingers in his ears, and my heart understood him, so he pointed to the circles of his heart. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever looks after a distressed person and provides for him, God will shade him in His shade.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not take it out. “And likewise It was narrated in brief on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, Rabi’ bin Harash, and Hanzalah bin Qais, all of them on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2224 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2225","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani and Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, saying: Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Affan told us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed told us, Muhammad bin Jahadah told us, On the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever looks after a distressed person, for him is a charity every day. Before the debt is due, then when the debt is due, then pay it back after that, and for every day the debt is due as charity.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2225 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2226","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us of the origin of his book. Ahmad ibn Sayyar informed us. Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, Sufyan told us, Al-A’mash told me, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Badri, he said: A man was held to account but no good was found for him, and he had money. He used to lend money to people, and he used to say to his servants: Whoever you find rich, take from him, and from whomever you find in need, spare him, perhaps God will He goes beyond me, so God said: “I have the right to go beyond him.” This is an authentic chain of narration on the condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Numayr, on the authority of Al-Amash,"
"2227","Abu Hamid Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, my father told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Badri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man was judged accountable, but no good was found for him, so he mentioned him. In the same way
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2226 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2228","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, On the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man owed his debtor ten dinars, and he said to him: By God, I do not have it. A matter I will fulfill today. He said: By God, I will not separate from you until you finish, or bring a burden to carry for you. He said: By God, I do not have anything to do, and I cannot find anyone to carry it for me. He said: He took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, this is necessary for me. I waited for him for one month, but he refused until I will make it up for him or bring him a burden, so I said: By God, I cannot find a burden nor do I have to make up for it today. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Are you waiting for him for more than one month?” He said: No. He said: “I will bear it on your behalf.” He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shouldered it on his behalf, so the man went and brought as much as He promised him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Where did you get this gold? He said: From a mineral. He said: “Then go, for we have no need of it and there is no good in it.” He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fulfilled it for him. “This is a hadith.” “Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari” “by Amr bin Abi Amr and Al-Darawardi according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2228 - True"
"2229","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he told me Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Saeed bin Hani, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah Al-Sulami, who said: I was sold to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as a virgin. So I came to pay him, and I said: O Messenger of God, pay the price of my firstborn. He said: “Yes, I will not judge him except for the time being. Then he judged me, and he did well. Then a Bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of God, judge my firstborn. He completed it without a long time, and he said: O Messenger of God, this is better than my firstborn. So he said: “It is for you. Indeed, the best of people is the one who is best in judgment.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2229 - True"
"2230","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i informed us, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi informed us, In Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri told us, he said, I heard Sufyan bin Saeed al-Thawri, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Samak Ibn Harb, on the authority of Suwayd Ibn Qais, he said: Makhramah Al-Abdi and I brought clothing from Hijr or Bahrain, so when we were in Mina, the Messenger of God came to us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He bought from us trousers, cloaks, and a weighing scale for the rent. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, paid the price to him and he said: “Adorn.” And it is more likely.” Narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Samak bin Harb"
"2231","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Ma’mal bin Ismail, Shu`bah narrated to us, Ali bin Hamshadh al-Adl narrated to us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman bin Harb narrated to us, Shu’bah told us, Abu Ahmad bin Abi Al-Hasan told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Khalid Al-Askari told us, he told us Muhammad ibn Ja`far, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abu Safwan say: I sold pants from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “So he weighed for me and I prevailed.” Abu Safwan, nicknamed Suwayd bin Qays, was one of the companions of the Ansar. “The hadith is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2232","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Khaled bin Abdul told us By God, on the authority of Hussein bin Qais, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those who have measure and weight: “Indeed, you have been entrusted with a matter in which there is the destruction of the previous nation.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2232 - Hussein bin Qais is weak"
"2233","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, and he told me Abu Amr Ismail bin Nujaid Al-Sulami, Abu Muslim reported, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Space, and Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Mu’tamar told us Ibn Sulaiman, Muhammad Ibn Fadha’ told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Alqamah Ibn Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said, “He forbade breaking the coins of the Muslims that were permissible among them, unless it was out of necessity, or if the dirham was broken, so it was made into silver, and the dinar was broken.” Then it will be made of gold.” Al-Ansari did not mention Alqamah’s father in his hadith, but Al-Mu’tamir mentioned him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2233 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2234","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid the reciter, Haywa bin Shurayh informed, Malik bin Al-Khair Al-Zubadi informed, that Malik bin Saad Al-Tajibi told him that he heard Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Gabriel came to me and said: O Muhammad, God has cursed wine and the one who drinks it. And the one who squeezes it, and the one who drinks it, and the one who carries it, and the one to whom it is carried, and the one who sells it, and the one who carries it, and the one who waters it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” The hadith of Abdullah bin Omar witnessed it, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2234 - True"
"2235","Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qazzaz al-Razi informed us in Baghdad, and Abdullah ibn Musa al-Adl in Nishapur, they said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Junaid told us, Al-Mu’afa bin Sulaiman told us, Fulayh bin Fulayh told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of His father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has cursed wine, and He has cursed its server, its drinker, its presser, the one who squeezes it, and its carrier. And what was carried to him, and he sold it and bought it, and ate its price.”"
"2236","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Yahya bin Salam told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought carrots with dates from a Bedouin, and he thought that he had some dates, so suddenly some He had some of it, and some of it he did not have, so he said: “Can you take some of your dates and some to the juz?” He refused, so the Prophet begged him and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He gave them to him, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2236 - Yahya bin Salam is weak and no one came out against him"
"2237","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Firas told us, the jurist in Mecca, Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf al-Tanisi told us, Abdullah told us Bin Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Zayd bin Sa’ana was one of the Jewish rabbis. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to receive compensation, and he received He pulled his garment off his right shoulder, then he said: O Banu Abdul Muttalib, you are people of arrogance, and indeed I am acquainted with you. He said: So Omar rebuked him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Umar, he and I were in need of anything other than this from you, for you to command me to do justice. And you command him to be fair in his dealings. Go, O Omar, and fulfill his rights. If there are three left for him, increase it by thirty saa’s for your fraud on him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2237 - Sent"
"2238","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami informed us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam informed us, Yahya bin Ayyub informed us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja`far, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever truly seeks So let him seek with sufficient chastity, or not. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. “And it has a witness on the authority of Abu Hurairah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2238 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2239","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Mujib told us, Saeed bin Yasin Al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Yamin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the one who has the right: “Take your right to chastity,” - and count it. He said: - Sufficient. ""or not sufficient"""
"2240","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim Al-Basani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hasan bin Waqid, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, that Ikrimah told him on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Medina, they were “one of the people who are most low in measure, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed {Woe to those who exaggerate} [Al-Muttaffin: 1], so they measured well after that. “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it.” It has an interpreted witness on the authority of Abu Hurairah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2240 - True"
"2241","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Marwazi told us, Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, Khuthaym bin Arak bin Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Khaybar, he succeeded Saba’. Ibn `Urfatah al-Ghifari, so we came and witnessed the morning prayer with him. In the first rak’ah, he recited {Kahya’as} [Maryam: 1] and in the second, {Woe to the mutaffifins} [Al-Muttaffifeen: 1] Then I said to myself: Woe to the father of so-and-so who has two measures. He takes one measure and underpays with another. So we went to Siba’ bin Arafat and prepared us. “So we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a day before the conquest or a day after it?”"
"2242","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati informed us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Sharik told us, My father, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, and Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “It is not permissible to dowry for an adulteress, nor “The price of the dog.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “And it has a witness on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2242 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2243","Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, my grandfather Ahmad bin Ibrahim told us, Amr bin Zurarah told us, Hushaym told us, Husayn told us, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, the reward of a soothsayer, and earning cupping"
"2244","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Bawari Al-Kufi told us, Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of dogs and cats.” Issa bin Yunus followed him, On the authority of Al-A'mash
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2244 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2245","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Adl informed us of Marw, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Qadi informed us, Abdullah ibn Maslamah informed us. Al-Qanabi, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of a dog. And the felines,” followed by Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir"
"2246","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Sadaqa bin Al-Fadl told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Omar bin Zaid, from the people of Sana’a, told us On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating a cat and eating its price.” The hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan “Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2246 - Omar bin Zaid Wah"
"2247","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib informed us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata informed us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba informed us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the milk of the Majesty, and the eating of Al-Mujathama and about drinking from the waterskin.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but he did not narrate it. “And it has evidence on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, and my father Hurairah” As for the hadith of Ibn Umar “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2247 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition
 As for the hadith of Ibn Omar"
"2248","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz informed us, Muhammad bin Ammar al-Mawsili informed us, Issa bin Yunus informed us, about Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating jalala. And its milks"
"2249","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told me, Muhammad bin Nu’aym told me, Ahmad bin Abi Shurayh Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Jahm told us, Amr bin Abi told us. Qays, on the authority of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the Jalala, - meaning camels - from To ride on it, or to drink from its milk.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Hurairah"
"2250","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abd al-Samad bin al-Nu’man told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the grave and the jalala.”"
"2251","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Yazid Al-Asbahani told us, Yahya bin Al-Daris, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Tahman, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade “On the sale of a sheep for meat.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It was narrated on the authority of the last of them by trustworthy and trustworthy imams, but they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari protested. With Al-Hassan, on the authority of Samurah, “And he has a witness sent to Malik’s place.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2251 - Al-Bukhari cited Al-Hasan on the authority of Samra"
"2252","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ narrated, Al-Shafi’i narrated, Malik narrated, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyib, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of meat from animals.”"
"2253","Muhammad ibn Saleh ibn Hani and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Zahid told us, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abdullah ibn رَزِينٍ السُّلَمِيُّ، ثنا يَحْيَى بْنُ يَحْيَى، أَنْبَأَ مُسْلِمُ بْنُ خَالِدٍ الزَّنْجِيُّ، عَنْ مُصْعَبِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ الْمَدَنِيُّ، عَنْ شُرَحْبِيلَ، مَوْلَى Al-Ansar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Whoever buys a theft, knowing that it is a theft, has engaged in Its disgrace and its sin.” Shurahbil, this is Ibn Saad Al-Ansari. Malik Ibn Anas narrated from him after he had a bad opinion of him. And the hadith is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2254","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram al-Bazzaz told me, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told me, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, and Affan bin Muslim told us, And Muslim bin Ibrahim, they said: Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any man who sells something to one or two men is the first of them, and any woman who is married to a guardian is the first of them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2254 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2255","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, Bishr bin Musa, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, and Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad informed us, And Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maymun Al-Harbi, they said: Hudha bin Khalifa told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ikrimah bin Khalid told me that Usayd bin Hudayr bin Samak narrated it to him, saying: Muawiyah wrote to Marwan: If a man steals and finds that he stole, he has more right to it wherever he found it. He said: So Marwan wrote to me about that while I was on Al-Yamamah. I wrote to Marwan that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “decided when he was The man who is not accused, then if her master wishes, he can take her for the price, and if he wishes, he can follow his thief.” Then Abu Bakr and Omar ruled that after him. And Othman said: So Marwan wrote to Muawiyah in my letter, and Muawiyah wrote to Marwan: Neither you nor Usayd will judge me regarding what you have appointed. But I command you both, so do what I commanded you to do. Marwan sent Muawiyah’s letter to him and said: By God, I will never judge it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2255 - This Usayd died during the time of Omar and Ikrimah did not meet him."
"2256","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Musa Al-Sinani told us, Harun bin Musa told us, Abu Damra told us, on the authority of Yahya Bin Saeed, Ibn Jurayj told me, and Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If You sold dates to your brother, and an epidemic struck him, so it is not permissible for you to take anything from him, or to take your brother’s money without his permission.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. “And it was narrated by Muhammad bin Thawr on the authority of Ibn Jurayj
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2256 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2257","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-Sana’ani told us in Mecca, Ali bin Mubarak Al-Sana’ani told us, Yazid bin Mubarak told us Al-Sana'ani, Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is permissible?” “Would one of you take care of his brother if a plague from the sky struck him?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. “The original in this matter is the hadith of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Humaid al-Taweel, who:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2257 - According to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim. This is what he said, according to the condition of Muslim"
"2258","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Malik bin Anas told me, on the authority of Humaid Al-Taweel, On the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you think that if God forbade the date, then by what means would one of you make his brother’s wealth lawful?”"
"2259","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ghalib informed us. Amr bin Ali told us. Ibn Abi Adi told us. Shu’bah, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Usury has seventy-three chapters. The easiest one is like a man having intercourse with his mother, and if he commits usury then the Muslim man will do so.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2259 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2260","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Ibrahim bin Khathim bin Arak bin Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ There are four people who have a right from God that He will not admit them to Paradise or let them taste its bliss: the alcoholic, the one who consumes usury, the one who unjustly consumes the orphan’s wealth, And the one who is disobedient to his parents: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and they agreed on Khathim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2260 - Ibrahim bin Khathim bin Arak bin Malik said Al-Nasa’i is abandoned."
"2261","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told me, Ya’qub bin Yusuf al-Qazwini told me, Muhammad bin Sa’id bin Saqiq told us, Amr bin Abi Qays told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade buying fruit to provide food, and he said: If adultery and usury appear in a town, then they have inflicted upon themselves the punishment of God. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2261 - True"
"2262","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, we told Israel, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, and Ahmad bin Ja’far Al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, he told us Abu Kamil and Hajjaj said: Israel told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of his father Al-Rabi’ bin Umaylah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Usury, even if it is great, its consequence will be small.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2262 - True"
"2263","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Jurayj, that Abu Al-Zubair, narrated to him, said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of al-Sabra from Dates, their measure is not known with the specified measure of dates.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2263 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2264","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Malik told us, Ali bin Issa told us Al-Hiri, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Hurashi, Jaafar bin Muhammad Al-Bazzi, and Musa bin Muhammad Al-Dahli told us: Yahya bin Yahya told us: I read from Malik, and Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Abu Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Abu Muhammad ibn Musa informed us. Al-Walid al-Tayalisi, he said: I asked Malik ibn Anas, and he told us on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid, on the authority of Zayd Abi Ayyash, he said: I asked Sa`d about The white one with the basket, and he said: There is a difference between them. They said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, being asked about fresh dates with dates. He asked those around him: “Does it decrease when it dries?” They said: Yes. He said: “Then no.” Abu al-Walid said: And I heard Malik bin Anas another time, he said: He hated it. This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Al-Walid, continued by Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, the client of Al-Aswad bin Sufyan.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2264 - Malik narrated it once, but he disliked it"
"2265","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Ismail bin Umayyah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyash, said: Two men pledged allegiance during the reign of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and he said: Two men pledged allegiance during the reign of the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with broad and fresh dates. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Does fresh dates decrease when they dry up?” They said: Yes. He said: “Then no.” And this is how Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated it on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah."
"2266","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu told us Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmed bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, we told him Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Yazid, on the authority of Zayd Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Saad bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about fresh dates with dates, and he said: “Is it lacking? When it dries up? They said: Yes, he said: “So he forbade it.” Yahya bin Abi Kathir followed them, based on his narration on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid."
"2267","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, they said: Hisham bin Ali told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, told us by Abdullah bin Yazid, that Abu Ayyash told him that he heard Saad bin Abi Waqqas say: “The Messenger forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of selling fresh dates for dates for bad money. And he is decisive in all the hadiths that he narrates, as nothing was found in his narrations except the authentic ones, especially in the hadiths of the people of Medina. Then to continue. These imams mentioned it in his narration on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid and the two sheikhs did not narrate it because they feared the ignorance of Zayd Abi Ayyash.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2267 - Sahih, but they did not publish it because they feared the ignorance of Abu Ayyash."
"2268","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq and Abu narrated Yahya Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Bazzaz, they said: Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abu Dawood told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, he said: I heard Abu Othman Al-Nahdi narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A scroll will be raised for a man on the Day of Resurrection, so that he will see that he is saved. The injustices of the children of Adam will continue to follow him until he has no good deeds left, and their evil deeds will be added to him.” He said: So I said to him, or Asim said to him: From whom? O Abu Othman? He said: On the authority of Salman, Saad, Ibn Masoud, and two other men whom he did not memorize. Shu’bah said: I asked Asim about this hadith, and he narrated it to me. On the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, and Uthman bin Ghayath told me that he heard Abu Uthman narrating this on the authority of Salman and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and his family and grant them peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” I do not know of Shu’bah on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath of any hadith with a chain of transmission other than this.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2268 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2269","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Ali Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, Ismail told us Bin Ibrahim bin Muhajir, I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade And peace be upon him, on the authority of Majesty, that its meat may be eaten, its milk may be drunk, and no human beings may be carried upon it, and people may not ride it until it has foraged for forty. “Night” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration due to what we mentioned regarding Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2269 - Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Muhajir and his father are weak"
"2270","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about it, and Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “he forbade goods to be sold where they were bought, until the one who bought them takes possession of them until his departure, and if he were to send men who would strike us for that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and according to Muhammad ibn “Ishaq has another chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2270 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2271","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Hunayn, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I bought oil in the market, and when I needed it, a man met me. So he gave me a good profit with it, so I wanted to strike at his hands, then a man behind me took my arm, so I turned to him, and there was Zayd bin Thabit He said: Do not sell it where you bought it, until you have it on your way, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade selling goods where they were bought, until “The merchants take it with them while they go.”"
"2272","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade all wild lions with fangs, and the killing of “The two children, and about sharing the spoils until it is divided.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context. “And it has an authentic witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2272 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and its witness is authentic"
"2273","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zannad told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the sale of the spoils, until they are divided.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2273 - True"
"2274","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Ali bin Abdullah told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Qais, on the authority of Suleiman bin Atiq, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “established pandemics.” Ali bin Al-Madini said: It was Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he “imposed pandemics.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2274 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2275","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, about Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Iyadh bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: A man was injured during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Fruits he bought, and his debt increased, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They gave him alms, so they gave him alms, but that did not amount to the repayment of his debt.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take what you find and you have nothing but that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2275 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2276","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr told me, Abu Nu’aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn told me, Bukayr ibn Amir told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Nu’aym told us, Rafi’ ibn Khadij, that he planted land and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by him while he was watering it and asked him: “Whose crops were they and for whom?” The earth? He said: “I planted with my seed and worked half for me and half for the son of so-and-so.” So he said: “You raised me, so return the land to its people, and take your expenses.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it. “They only agreed to debate with Abdullah bin Omar and Rafi’ bin Khadij about it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2276 - Bakir is weak"
"2277","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Isa Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, and Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman al-Rawasi, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Ziyadah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nasi, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Tha’labah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I taught writing and the Qur’an to some people from the people of the Suffah, and one of them gave me a bow. I said: It is not money, and I will shoot at it for the sake of By God, I will go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and ask him. So I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, a man gave me a bow from one of my I teach him writing and the Qur’an, not with money, and I throw stones at her in the path of God. He said: “If you would like to be surrounded by a circle of fire, then accept it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2277 - Mughirah bin Ziyad Salih Al-Hadith, and Ibn Hibban left it"
"2278","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Aban bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qarith, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qariz, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The profit of a cupper is evil, the price of a dog is evil, and the dowry of a prostitute is evil.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2278 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2279","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, Tariq told us Ibn Abdul Rahman Al-Qurashi said: Rifa’ah Ibn Rafi’ came to the Ansar Council and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us.” Today he greeted, and mentioned some things, and said: “He forbade us from the nation earning anything except what it did with its own hand, and he said this with his finger about “Spinning, baking, and fluffing.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And it has a witness on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2279 - Tariq was soft about it and did not mention that he heard it from Rifa’ah."
"2280","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Al-Junaid told me, Ahmad bin Salih told me, Ibn Abi Fudaik told me, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Hurair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade attacking the nation to the point of Does he know where he is from?
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2280 - We produced it as a witness"
"2281","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the spoiling of a stallion.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it: “Ali bin Al-Hakam Al-Bunani is trustworthy and trustworthy, one of the most distinguished scholars of insight.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2281 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2282","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hayyan bin Ubaidullah Al-Adawi told us, he said: I asked Abu Majliz about the morphology, and he said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, did not see anything wrong with it for a long period of his life, as long as it was not a bad thing. He means hand to hand, and he used to say: Usury is only in the interest. So Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri met him and said to him: O Ibn Abbas, don’t you fear God? How long will people be charged with usury? Have you not heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said one day while he was with his wife Umm Salamah: “I crave Ajwa dates.” So she sent two saa's of dates to a man from the Ansar, and instead of the two saa's came a saa' of dates, an ajwa, so she got up and presented it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him. When he saw it, he liked it, so he ate a date, then he stopped and said: “Where did you get this?” Then Umm Salamah said: I sent two saa’s of dates to a man from the Ansar, and he brought us this one saa’ of dates instead of two saa’s, and here he is, eat them and throw them away. The date was in his hands and he said: “Give it back, I have no need of it. Dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, gold for gold. And silver for silver, hand for hand, kind for eye, like for like, so whoever increases it is usury.” Then he said: “Similarly is that which is measured and weighed as well.” He said Ibn Abbas: May God reward you with Paradise, Abu Saeed, for you have reminded me of something I had forgotten. I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him. After that, he strictly prohibited it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2282 - Hibban bin Ubaidullah Al-Adawi has weakness and is not evidence."
"2283","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Makhramah bin Bukair told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas said: I heard Abu Ayyash saying: I asked Saad bin Abi Waqqas about buying baskets of dates, and Saad said: Is there a difference between them? They said: Yes. He said: It is not valid. Saad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about buying fresh dates with dates, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is there a surplus between them?” They said: Yes, the rutab is decreasing. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is a hadith with a sound chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2284","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abi Musa told us, Israel, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about. . . . » It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2285","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Uqabi told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Simak Ibn Harb, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I used to sell camels for Naqi’, so I would sell them for dinars and take In dirhams, and I sell for dirhams and take dinars, and I fell in love with that, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the house of Hafsa or He said: When he left the house of Hafsa, I said: O Messenger of God, please take your time, I ask you. I sell camels in Al-Baqi’, so I sell for dinars and take I sell dirhams for dirhams and take dinars. He said: “There is no harm in taking them for their daily price as long as you do not separate and there is nothing between you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim and he did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2285 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2286","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Aba Al-Minhal says: I heard Iyas bin Abdul-Muzani, and he saw a man selling water, and he said: Do not sell water, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, “forbids the sale of water.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2286 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2287","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Ibn Juraij told me, about Amr bin Dinar, that Abu Al-Minhal informed him: that Iyas bin Abdul-Muzani said to the people: Do not sell surplus water, for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the people: May God bless him and grant him peace, “He forbade the sale of water,” and Ibn Jurayj has another chain of transmission in it."
"2288","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Handali told us, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of water, and the beating of a camel, and that A man sells his land and water.” These chains of narrations are all authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. “The best of what is in this regard is the hadith of Hussein Ibn Waqid who:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2288 - According to Muslim’s condition
 Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Handali told us, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of water, and the beating of a camel, and that A man sells his land and water.” These are all authentic chains of narration according to Muslim’s condition, but he did not narrate it. “The best of what is in this regard is the hadith of Hussein Ibn Waqid” who:"
"2289","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he informed us Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the sale of water.” Al-Hussein bin Waqid narrated it alone, on the authority of Ayyub, and it is not authentic.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2289 - Gharib Sahih, unique to Hussein"
"2290","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyeh, Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, he said: We invaded with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Levant, and Nabataeans from the Levant were coming to us. “And we would give them advances in wheat and oil for a specified price. And for a specified time, then it was said to him: And from whom did that happen? He said: We did not ask them, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission,” and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2290 - True"
"2291","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, and Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hassan Al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud told us Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, they said: Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, they said: Yahya bin Ma'in, on the authority of Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever opposes a Muslim, God will forgive his transgression.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2291 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2292","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Saydalani told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi told us Zaida, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells two sales in one sale, “Then he is entitled to their share or usury.” It is valid according to the condition of a Muslim, but they did not pay it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2292 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2293","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani, Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, and Ibrahim bin Asmah told us, they said: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs told us. Ibn Ghayath, my father told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash’ath ibn Qays informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: Al-Ash’ath bought one of the five slaves from Abdullah for twenty thousand, so Abdullah sent him the price for them, and he said: It is only I took them for ten thousand, so Abdullah said: Choose a man to be between you and me. Al-Ash'ath said: You are between me and yourself. Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If there is a disagreement... “The two sales, and there is no evidence between them, it is what the owner of the commodity says or they leave it alone.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2293 - True"
"2294","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad told us Ibn Ahmad Ibn Balawayh, Abdullah Ibn Ahmad Ibn Hanbal told us, my father, Abdullah Ibn Omar Ibn Maysarah, and Uthman Ibn Abi told me. Shaybah, they said: Muhammad bin Jaafar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A man gives birth from his earnings, from the best of his earnings, so eat from their wealth.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition The two sheikhs did not narrate it: “And on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, there is another chain of narration with a different wording, and neither of the two chain of narrations explains the other.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2294 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2295","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, and Ali bin Sayyar told us. Hamshadh, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of his paternal aunt, that she asked Aisha: Is there an orphan in my care, should I eat from his money? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best things a man eats are from his own earnings, and his children are from his earnings.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2295 - True"
"2296","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Talaq bin Ghanam told us, Sharik and Qais told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Return the trust to the one who has entrusted you, and do not betray the one who has betrayed you.” He said Al-Abbas: I said to Talq: Write “partner” and leave “Qais”? He said: You can see. “The hadith of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Husayn, is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it” and he has a witness on the authority of Anas.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2296 - According to the conditions of Muslim and his witness"
"2297","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Qutaybah narrated to us, Ahmad bin Al-Fadl Al-Asqalani narrated to us, Ayyub bin Suwayd narrated to us, Ibn Suwayd narrated to us. Shawdhab, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Return the trust to the one who has entrusted you, and do not betray the one who trusts you.” betrayed you"
"2298","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Abu Al-Muthanna, he said: Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, Husayn Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas Radi God is on their behalf, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “It is not permissible for a man to give a gift, or to give a gift, for anyone to take it back except the father. In what he gives to his child, and the example of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog eating, and when he is full, he vomits, then returns to his vomit.” This “A hadith with an authentic chain of narration. I do not know of any disagreement regarding the justice of Amr ibn Shuaib. Rather, they disagreed regarding his father’s hearing from his grandfather.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2298 - True"
"2299","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali and Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, saying: Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, and Habib Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No It is permissible for a woman to control her property if her husband owns it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “I heard Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz says: I heard Abu Bakr bin Ziyad, the Nisaburi jurist, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Ali bin Hamdan Al-Warraq saying: I told Ahmad Ibn Hanbal: Did Amr Ibn Shuaib hear something from his father? He said: He is Amr bin Shuaib bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr, and it is correct that Amr bin Shuaib heard from his father Shuaib, and it is correct that he heard Shuaib from his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2299 - True"
"2300","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sharik informed us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Rufa’i, on the authority of Umayyah Ibn Safwan Ibn Umayyah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, borrowed armor from him on the day of Hunayn and said: Are you usurped, O Muhammad? He said: “No, but a secured, naked one.” And he has a witness on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both."
"2301","Ahmed bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad Al-Hafiz told us, Ishaq bin Abdul-Wahid Al-Qurashi told us, Khalid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, borrowed from Safwan ibn Umayyah wore armor and teeth in the Battle of Hunayn and said: O Messenger of God, are loans to be paid? He said: “A naked woman brought back.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2301 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2302","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Saeed bin Amir, and Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, they said: Saeed bin Ata told us. Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The hand has not taken until You pay it.” Then Al-Hasan forgot his hadith and said: He is your trustworthy person, there is no guarantee on him. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and did not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2302 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2303","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Jawhari told us in Baghdad, Abu Al-Walid Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Burd told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us Al-Musaysi, Al-Awza’i told us, Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Jamahir bin Muhammad Al-Ghassani told us, in Damascus, Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi, Al-Faryabi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Haram bin Muhayyasah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib Radi On their behalf, he said: He had a ferocious she-camel, and she entered a wall and made a mess in it. He spoke to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it, and he decided. Maintaining walls during the day is the responsibility of their owners, and maintaining livestock at night is the responsibility of their families, and the responsibility of the people of the livestock is the responsibility of what befalls them. “Their livestock.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, although there is a disagreement about it between Muammar and Al-Awza’i. Muammar said: On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Haram bin Muhaiysah, on the authority of his father
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2303 - Sahih, but there is a dispute over it between Muammar and Al-Awza’i"
"2304","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Sa’id bin Salim Al-Qaddah told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ismail bin Umayyah told him on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Ubaid. He said: I attended Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Masoud and he came to him. Two men exchanged goods, and one of them said: I took such-and-such. The other said: I sold for such-and-such. Abu Ubaidah said: Abdullah bin Masoud told me about something like this. He said: I attended the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about something like this. So he ordered The seller must swear an oath, then the buyer has the choice, whether he wants to take it or leave it.” This is an authentic hadith. “If Saeed bin Salem memorized it in Its chain of transmission is Abd al-Malik ibn Ubaid. Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us. My father narrated to me. Muhammad bin Idris Al-Shafi’i, so he mentioned the hadith and at the end of it, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal was informed on the authority of Hisham bin Yusuf, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Ubaid, Ahmad bin Hanbal said: And the one-eyed Hajjaj said, “Abd al-Malik bin Ubaid”"
"2305","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Hilal ibn al-Ala al-Ruqi told us, al-Mu’afa ibn Sulayman told us, Musa ibn Ayan told us, about Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, that Abu al-Zubayr, told him, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bought from A Bedouin, I thought he said: From Bani Amir bin Sa’sa’a, he carried a lamb, and when it became obligatory for him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Choose,” and he said. The Bedouin: If I saw someone like you today, may God protect you, who are you? He said: “From Quraysh,” followed by Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2305 - Ibn Wahb continued it on the authority of Ibn Jurayj according to Muslim’s condition"
"2306","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Sulaiman bin Al-Ash’ath told us, Wahb bin Yazid bin Mawhib told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he reported Ibn Jurayj, that Abu Al-Zubair Al-Makki, narrated to him, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bought from a Bedouin a lamb of lamb. When the sale became necessary, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Choose.” The Bedouins said, “May God protect you as long as you sell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"2307","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz informed me, Ali bin Al-Abbas Al-Kufi told us, Muhammad bin Bashar and Ali bin Muslim told us, they said: Abu Dawud, told us by Shu’bah bin Abdullah Al-Zaafrani, who said: I heard Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji, speaking, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The taker and the giver are equal in usury.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2307 - True"
"2308","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Rahman al-Dabbas told me in Mecca, Muhammad bin Ali bin Zaid al-Sayegh told us, Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Shafi’i, he said: I heard Abu Muhammad bin Al-Abbas, speaking, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A dinar for a dinar and a dirham for a dirham, there is no preference between them, so whoever has If he has a need with a piece of paper, let him spend it with gold, and whoever has a need with gold, let him spend it with a piece of paper, and exchange it here and there.” This is a hadith. It is strange and true, and they did not narrate it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2308 - Sahih Gharib"
"2309","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Kathir bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Muslims are subject to their conditions. Reconciliation is permissible between Muslims.” The narrators of this hadith are Madani, but they did not narrate it, and this is a basis in the Book. “And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Aisha.” And Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with them both.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2309 - He did not authenticate it, and much of it was weak by Al-Nasa’i, and others misunderstood it."
"2310","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Ismail bin Abdullah bin Zurarah told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jazari told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Muslims live on their conditions as long as they agree with the truth.”
 Khasif said: Ata’ bin Abi Rabah told me on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Muslims are at “Their conditions are whatever the truth agrees with.”"
"2311","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Baraki told us, Abdul Hamid bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir told us, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every A favor is charity, and whatever a man spends on himself and his family is recorded as charity for him, and whatever a person protects his honor with is recorded as charity for him, and whatever “If a believer spends anything, then if he leaves it back to God, God is a guarantor, unless it is for the sake of edification or transgression.” So I said to Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir: What did the man protect his honor with? He said: What a poet and one with a pious tongue gives. “This is an authentic hadith. They did not narrate it, and the one who witnessed it is not a condition of this book.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2311 - Abd al-Hamid Dha’fuwah"
"2312","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Saghani told us in Marw, Yahya bin Sasawayh told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, Hamid bin Adam told us, Abu Ismah told us Noah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Badil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is able Whoever of you wants to protect his religion and honor with his wealth, let him do so.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2312 - Abu Isma perished"
"2313","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan bin Al-Marzban Al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Masisi told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The reconciliation between “It is permissible for Muslims.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. He is known as Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Masisi, and he is trustworthy.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2313 - Ibn Hibban said, “He steals the hadith,” meaning Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Masisi."
"2314","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told me, Abu Al-Mu'tamir, on the authority of Omar bin Khaldah Al-Zarqi, and the judge of Medina said: We came to Abu Hurairah about a friend of ours who had gone bankrupt, and he said: This is the one who The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled in it: “Whenever a man dies or becomes bankrupt, the owner of the property has more right to his property if he finds it himself.” This is a high hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2314 - True"
"2315","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib and Yahya bin Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, they said: Abdullah bin Imran Al-Abidi told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mortgage is not closed to him regarding his sheep, and he must pay his debts.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Due to a dispute over it between the companions of Al-Zuhri, and Malik, Ibn Abi Dhib, Sulayman bin Abi Dawud Al-Harrani, and Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Zubaidi followed him. And Muammar bin Rashid is on this narration. “As for the hadith of Malik"
"2316","Abu Ali and Abu Muhammad Al-Maraghi told us, they said: Ali bin Abdul-Hamid Al-Ghadayri told us, in Aleppo, Mujahid bin Musa told us, on the authority of Malik. Ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, so he mentioned it with a similar chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2315 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, but they did not narrate it due to their disagreement over Al-Zuhri.
 As for the hadith of Ibn Abi Dhib"
"2317","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf bin Sufyan Al-Tai told us, Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar Al-Homsi told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mortgage of his sheep is not closed to its owner while he must pay the debt.” It was said on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Saeed and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him"
"2318","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Nasr Al-Asam told us, Shababah told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No The mortgage is closed. The mortgage belongs to the one who mortgaged it, and he must pay the fine.”
 As for the hadith of Suleiman bin Abi Dawud:"
"2319","Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Dibaji told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Yazid Al-Rasibi told us, Abu Maysarah Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Maysarah Al-Harrani, Sulaiman bin Abi Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The mortgage is not closed until you have its share, and you are responsible for its payment.”
 As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Zubaidi:"
"2320","So Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini told us, Imran bin Bakkar told us, Abdullah told us Bin Abdul Jabbar, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mortgage is not closed. He has his share, and he owes his debt.”
 As for the hadith of Muammar bin Rashid"
"2321","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Musa bin Zakaria Al-Tustari told us, Muhammad bin Yazid Al-Rawwas told us, Kurayd Abu Yahya told us, Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No The mortgage is closed, you get its share, and you pay its amount.”"
"2322","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told me, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Muhammad bin Suleiman Al-Masisi told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Al-Zabarqan, Abu Hayyan Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “God says: ‘I am the third of two partners, as long as one of them does not betray his companion. If he betrays, I will depart from them.’ This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2322 - True"
"2323","Abu Ahmad Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Hashimi told us in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan said: I heard Salim bin Abdullah speaking, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Whoever gives a gift has more right to it as long as he does not return from it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not mention it except that we eat. “The burden is on our sheikh.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2323 - According to their conditions, except that we leave the burden on our sheikh."
"2324","Abu Ja`far Abdullah bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Al-Mansur, Commander of the Faithful in Baghdad, told us in the house of the Caliphate. Al-Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Hashimi, Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Ruqi told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the gift is for a relative of a mahram, he will not take it back.” This is an authentic hadith. According to Al-Bukhari’s condition, they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2324 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2325","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Jawhari told me in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Abdul Aziz told us Ibn Yahya Al-Madini, Muslim Ibn Khalid Al-Zanji told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Yazid Ibn Rukana, on the authority of Dawud Ibn Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to expel Banu al-Nadir, they said: Oh Messenger of God, you have commanded us to be expelled while we owe the people unresolved debts. He said: “Waste and hasten.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not expel it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2325 - The Negro is weak and Abdul Aziz is not trustworthy"
"2326","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Ja’far bin Ahmad Al-Shamati told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin Saeed told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Mecca is a climate in which all of its quarters cannot be sold, and its houses cannot be rented.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “Witnessed by the hadith of Abu Hanifa which”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2326 - Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Muhajir declared him weak"
"2327","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, and Abu Jafar bin Ubaid Al-Hafiz narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Kari narrated to us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam narrated to us. Al-Arni, Abu Hanifa told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Mecca is sacred, and it is forbidden to sell its quarters, and it is forbidden to rent for its homes.” It has been authenticated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He entered Mecca in greeting peace, and from there:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2327 - Ubaidullah bin Abi Ziyad Lane"
"2328","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih did not tell us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Fadl A’im, and Hadba bin Khalid told us, They said: Salam bin Miskin narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked to Mecca to conquer it. He said to Abu Hurairah: “Cry for the Ansar.” He said: O Ansar, answer the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they came as if they were at an appointment, then he said: “Walk this path and no one will honor you unless you believe in him.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked on. Then God granted it to him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, circumambulated the House and prayed two rak’ahs, then he left through the door next to Al-Safa, and ascended. Al-Safa, so he addressed the people and the Ansar below him, and the Ansar said to one another: As for the man, compassion for his people took hold of him. And the desire in his town, and God sent down the revelation of what the Ansar said, and He said: “O community of Ansar, you say: As for the man, He was overcome by compassion for his people and desire for his village. He said: “Who am I then? No, by God, I am truly the servant of God and His Messenger. Your life, and your death. They said: By God, O Messenger of God, we did not say that except for fear that they would be hostile to us. He said: “You are truthful in the sight of God and in the sight of His Messenger.” He said: “By God, there is not one of them who does not shed tears.” And among them:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2328 - True"
"2329","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Adl al-Saffar did not tell us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr told us, Amr ibn Talha al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed He greeted the people, except for four people and two women, and said: “Kill them, even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba.” Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl, Abdullah bin Khatal, Muqays bin Sababa, and Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2329 - True"
"2330","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Abd Al-Warith told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar, Zaid bin Aslam told us, he said: I saw an old man in Alexandria called Sarq, so I said to him: What is this name? He said: It is a name given to me by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I will not give it up. I said, why did he name you? He said: I came to Medina and told them that my masters had sold me out, and I had consumed their money, so they brought me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “You He stole.” And he sold me for four acres, and said to the creditors who had bought me, “What do you do with him?” They said: We free him. They said: We will not be more ascetic in the Hereafter than you, so they freed me among them, and my name remained: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2330 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2331","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub al-Adl narrated to us, from the origin of his book, more than once. Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ataa Shu’bah reported on the ruling on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, presented captive, so he ordered me to sell two brothers, so I sold them and separated them, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and he said: “I will catch them.” So return them and sell them all together and do not separate them.” This is a strange hadith that is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “It was said about al-Hakam On the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Ali, and it is also authentic.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2331 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim Gharib"
"2332","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Abd al-Mu’min bin Ali al-Razi told us, Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdul Rahman Abi Khaled Al-Dalani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, “He sold a slave girl and her child, and separated them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade him from that.” This is another text with an authentic chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2332 - True"
"2333","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Abdul Rahman bin Yunus Al-Sarraj told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Taliq bin Muhammad, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cursed “Whoever makes a difference” This is an authentic chain of narration and they did not narrate it and its interpretation is in the hadith of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari which “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2333 - True"
"2334","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he told me Hayy bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “Whoever separates a mother from her child, God will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"2335","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Al-Haytham Al-Askari told us, Abdullah bin Amr told us Bin Hassan, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz Al-Tanukhi told us, he said: I heard Makhoul, saying: Nafi’ bin Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of his father, that he heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the separation between a mother and her child. It was said: O Messenger of God, for how long? He said: “Until the boy reaches puberty and the girl menstruates.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2335 - Subject and Ibn Hassan is a liar"
"2336","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us, Ahaid bin Al-Hussein Al-Bamiani told us, in Balkh, Azhar bin Salman Al-Kateb told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Hamawayh told me, my father told me, Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he told me My father, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the Day of Khaybar forbade the selling of spoils until they were divided, and the Pregnant women should be intimated until they give birth to what is in their bellies, and He said: “Do not water someone else’s crops, and abstain from the meat of domestic donkeys, and abstain from the flesh of every fanged animal.” “From wild beasts.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2336 - True"
"2337","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Yashkari, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever has a partner in A wall, so he should not sell his share of that until he presents it to his partner.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2337 - True"
"2338","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, Ishaq bin Ahmad al-Khazzaz told us about irrigation, Ishaq bin Sulayman al-Razi told us, al-Mughirah bin Muslim, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God “He loves the permissibility of selling, the permissibility of buying, the permissibility of the judiciary.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2338 - True"
"2339","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, he told me Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If If you see someone selling or buying in the mosque, say: May God not make your business profitable, and if you see someone seeking a lost item in it, say: No response. May God bless you. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2339 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2340","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Omar Al-Hudhi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Muslim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to prepare an army, but the camels ran out. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to “He took from the Qayyās of charity, so I used to take a camel for two camels.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2340 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2341","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abdullah bin Ismail al-Muqri told us, in Sana’a, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us Al-Juni, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari told us, Sufyan al-Thawri told us, Muammar told me, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the salaf in animal life.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2341 - True"
"2342","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Al-Khasib bin Nasih told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Musa Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the sale of weed for another.” This An authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. “And it was said on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2342 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2343","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mihran told us, Ubayy told us, Al-Miqdam bin Dawud Al-Ru’ayni told us, Dhu’ayb bin Umamah told us, Hamza told us. Ibn Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Musa Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “He forbade selling raw materials for raw materials, cheap for cheap.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2343 - A weak wolf"
"2344","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Abu Nu’aym Al-Jurjani told us, Hammad bin Al-Hasan bin Anbasa told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Talha, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade debate and debate.” And the Munabdha” Professor Abu Al-Walid said: The Mukhadara is that none of it is sold until it turns red or yellow. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It was unique in its narration by Al-Bukhari.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2344 - Sahih, unique in its narration by Bukhari"
"2345","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Muhammad bin Uthman bin Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd told us. Al-Rahman, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya Al-Mazini, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Neither harm nor harm. Whoever harms, God will harm him, and whoever is hard, God will make hard for him.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2345 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2346","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: A man died, so we washed him, shrouded him, embalmed him, and placed him for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted where the funerals are placed, at the position of Gabriel. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave us permission to pray for him, and he came with us in steps, then he said: “Perhaps your friend owes a debt?” They said: Yes, two dinars. So he fell behind, and a man from among us called Abu Qatada said to him: O Messenger of God, they are on me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made them He said: “They are upon you and your property, and the dead person is innocent of them.” He said: Yes, and he prayed over him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made the prayer when he met Abu Qatada said: “What did the two dinars do?” Until the end of that, he said: I have fulfilled them, O Messenger of God. He said: “Now that his skin has cooled on him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2346 - True"
"2347","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Ziyad Al-Faqih in Al-Damghan told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Shayban bin Farukh told us, they said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The mortgage is annulled and compounded.” Al-A’mash said: So I mentioned that to Abraham, but he decided to benefit from it. With something like “This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs,” and they did not produce it due to the consensus of Al-Thawri and Shu’bah on stopping it from Al-A’mash, and I am on I pray the truth in accepting the increase in confidence.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2347 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2348","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih informed us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Hayyan Al-Ansari informed us, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muawiyah informed us. Al-Karabisi, Hisham bin Yusuf Al-San’ani told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he handed over “His property to Muadh and sold it for a debt he owed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2348 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2349","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Qabbani told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Attab Al-Ayn told us, Mansour told us Ibn Salamah Abu Salamah Al-Khuza’i, Othman Ibn Abdullah Ibn Zaid Ibn Haritha Al-Ansari told us, my uncle Amr Ibn Zaid Ibn Haritha told us. Abu Zayd ibn Haritha, may God be pleased with him, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “belittled some people on the day of one of them, Zayd ibn Haritha.” Meaning himself, Al-Baraa bin Aazib, Zaid bin Arqam, Saad, Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, Abdullah bin Omar, and he mentioned Jabir bin Abdullah.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2349 - True"
"2350","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq and Abu Muhammad ibn Musa told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi told us, and Musa ibn Ismail, they said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “The pen was lifted from three people; “A boy until he has a wet dream, an imbecile until he wakes up, and a sleeper until he wakes up.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2350 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2351","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Khalid Al-Razi told us, Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, and Ahmad told us Bin Amr, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mahran, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, Ali passed by an insane woman from the tribe of so-and-so, who had committed adultery, and Omar ibn al-Khattab ordered her to be stoned, so Ali ibn Abi Talib returned her and said to Omar: O Commander of the Faithful, have you ordered this woman to be stoned? He said: Yes, he said: Don’t you remember that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The pen was lifted from three people: from the insane person whose mind is lost, And on behalf of a sleeping person until he wakes up, and on behalf of a boy until he has a wet dream. He said: She spoke the truth, so he let go of her. Abu Abdullah said: “By interdicting a male or female insane person, concerning which I do not know of any disagreement among scholars.”"
"2352","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Daba’i told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Abdul-A’la bin Hammad told us, Omar bin Ali told us, Hisham told us Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “This verse {And reconciliation is best} [An-Nisa: 128] was revealed about a man who had a woman under him. She had been with him for a long time, and she bore him children. He wanted to exchange her for her, so she agreed to him on the condition that she stay with him and he would not divide this “this” to her. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2352 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2353","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi told us Al-Zanad, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Sawda, may God be pleased with her, “made her day for Aisha and I count in That is what was revealed: “And if a woman fears disobedience or rejection from her husband” [An-Nisa’: 128] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2353 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2354","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, On the authority of Asim bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “There was a truce between the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And among the people of Mecca in Al-Hudaybiyyah for four years.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2354 - Rather, he is weak, for Asim was weak, and he was the brother of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar."
"2355","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Hani told me Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, that he heard Fadalah bin Ubaid, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “I am a leader, and the leader is the bearer of whoever believes in me, submits to Islam, and migrates to a home in the outskirts of Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim and did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2355 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2356","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Harawi told us, Hushaim told us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, who said: My mother performed the oath and came to Medina. So people proposed to her, and she said: I will only marry a man who will sponsor this orphan for me. Then a man from the Ansar married her. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would present the boys of the Ansar, and every year some of them would join them.” He caught up with them. He said: I ran forward for a year, and he caught up with a boy, and he pushed me back. I said: O Messenger of God, you caught up with him and you pushed me back, and if I had wrestled with him, I would have wrestled with him. He said: “So wrestle with him.” So I wrestled with him, so I wrestled with him, and he told me, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2356 - True"
"2357","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mala’ab ibn Hayyan told us, and Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Affan ibn Harb narrated to us. Muslim, Wahib told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Abi Al-Sa’ib, that he was a partner of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. At the beginning of Islam, he greeted trade in trade, and when the day of the conquest came, he said: “Welcome to my brother and partner who does not turn away or dispute,” and he mentioned the rest of the hadith. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2357 - True"
"2358","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan al-Kharraz informed us of Mecca, at al-Safa. Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd informed us, Sa`id ibn Mansour, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a fever Al-Baqi’ and he said: “There is no fever except for Allah and His Messenger.” They agreed on the hadith of Yunus on the authority of Al-Zuhri with its chain of transmission, “There is no fever except for Allah and His Messenger,” and they did not He narrates it like this and it has an authentic chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2358 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and the end of it was extracted from it"
"2359","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the selling of water.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Witness with an addition in the text.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2359 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2360","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Dawud bin Abdul Rahman told us. Al-Makki, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Iyas bin Abdan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the sale of surplus water.”"
"2361","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Hajabi told us, Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Abi Al-Rijal, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of his mother Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “It is not forbidden Soaking the well, which is ar-rahu.” Abdul-Rahman said: I heard my father saying: The ar-rahu is that the well is among partners in which there is water, so it is The man has an advantage in it, so his companion does not prevent it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2361 - True
 In this regard, they only agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “The surplus of water is not withheld from To prevent pasture by it.”"
"2362","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Qazzaz Al-Razi in Baghdad, they said: Ali bin Al-Hussein told us. Bin Al-Junaid, Ishaq bin Issa told us, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Rijal, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He decreed in a rushing torrent, and a rushing one that the upper one sends to the lower one, and withholds the size of two ankles.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2362 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2363","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us Al-Muqri, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub narrated to me, Abu Al-Aswad narrated to me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, On the authority of Khalid bin Adi Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever informs him of it will be treated kindly on behalf of his brother by someone other than him.” Asking, nor entrusting a soul, so let him accept it and not reject it, for it is a provision that God led him to.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2363 - True"
"2364","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told me, Al-Humaydi told me, Sufyan told me, Amr bin Dinar told me, he said, I heard Wahb bin Munabhih, in He lived in his house in Sana'a and fed me cereals in his house. He narrated on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not be ambivalent about a question, for by God, none of you will ask me for anything, and the question will bring it out of me for him, so I will give it to him.” And I hate him, so he will be blessed for what I give him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2364 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2365","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told me in Baghdad, and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi informed me of Marw. They said: Abu Qalaba, and Abu Amr bin Nujaid told me, Abu Muslim told us, they said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said that a man gave the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a gift of an infertility, and he rewarded him with six morsels of it, but he became angry with her. The man, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever excuses me from so-and-so, has given me a vaccine, and it is as if I were looking at it in the face of someone else.” His family, so I saved him from him with six gifts, so he displeased them. I was determined not to accept a gift unless it was from a Qurayshi or an Ansari. Or a Thaqafi, or a Dawsi.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2365 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2366","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abdullah bin Dawood told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Bujair, on the authority of Dirar bin Al-Azwar, may God be pleased with him, who said: My family sent me in Balquh to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and gave it to him as a gift. So he said to me: “Milk her and leave the need for milk.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2366 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2367","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation in the month of Ramadan in the year three hundred and ninety-seven. The Sheikh told us Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Ishaq bin Saeed told us, my father told us, Umm Khalid bint told me Khaled said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with a garment containing a small black khamis, and he said: “Whose clothes do you see?” The people remained silent, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bring me Umm Khalid.” She said: So he brought me and dressed me with his own hand, and said: “I will do well.” And behave.” He says it twice, and then he looks at a yellow and red flag on the shirt, and says: “O Umm Khalid, this is a good practice.” And the best thing is In the beautiful language of Abyssinia, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2367 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2368","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Hisham bin Ali and Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the immigrants said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The Ansar took the whole reward. He said: “No, what “You called upon God for them and praised Him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2368 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2369","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed told us Bin Balawayh, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maymun Al-Harbi told us, they said: Surayj bin Al-Numan Al-Jawhari told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever asks you by God, give him, and whoever seeks refuge in God So seek refuge in him, and whoever comes to you with kindness, repay him. If you do not find it, then pray for him until you know that you have repaid him, and whoever seeks protection from you in God. So they hired him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not take it out due to the dispute that arose among the companions of Al-A’mash regarding it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2369 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2370","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us about Marwa, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a donkey while he was walking, and he said: Ride, O Messenger of God. He said: “The owner of the animal has more right to the chest of his animal, unless you give it to me.” He said: I did. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2370 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2371","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bakr ibn Sawada informed him on the authority of Abu Salem al-Jishani, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khaled Al-Juhani, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever shelters a lost woman is lost, as long as he does not recognize her.” The chain of transmission is authentic and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2371 - True"
"2372","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told us, and Abdullah bin Yahya bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, They said: Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked about the snapshot, and he said: “It is known and not hidden, and it is not concealed. If its owner comes, otherwise it is the property of God. He gives it to whomever He wishes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2372 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2373","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, about Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Ibn Uthman al-Taymi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade the pilgrim’s sight.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2373 - True"
"2374","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, he said: We heard it from Dawud bin Shabur and Yaqoub bin Ata, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said regarding a treasure found by a man: “If you find it in an inhabited village, or on the way to a dead person, identify it, and if you find it... In a wasteland of pre-Islamic times, or in an uninhabited village, or in a dead way, then in it and in the five pillars” I have mentioned a lot in this book. The arguments for correcting the narrations of Amr bin Shuaib, if the narrator is trustworthy and is not mentioned from him, are better than these narrations, and I was asking “The apparent proof is in what Shuaib bin Muhammad heard on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, but I have not reached it until this time.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2374 - True"
"2375","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz told me, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Faqih Al-Naysaburi told me, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, Ubaid told us Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, that a man came to Abdullah bin Amr asking him about a mahram who had intercourse with a woman, so he indicated To Abdullah bin Omar, he said: Go to that man and ask him. Shuaib said: The man did not recognize him, so I went with him and he asked Ibn Omar, and he said: Your Hajj is invalid. So the man said, “What should I do?” He said: “Ihram with the people, and do what they do, and when you meet someone nearby, perform Hajj and sacrifice.” So he returned to Abdullah bin Amr and I was with him. He said: Go to Ibn Abbas and ask him. Shuaib said: So I went with him to Ibn Abbas and asked him, and he said to him as Ibn Omar said, so he returned. To Abdullah bin Amr and I was with him, so he told him what Ibn Abbas said, then he said: What do you say? So he said, “My saying is like what they said, “This is a trustworthy hadith whose narrators were memorized, and it is like taking the hand by the hand in the authenticity of Shuaib bin Muhammad’s hearing, on the authority of his grandfather.” Abdullah bin Amr This is the last thing that my diligence led to in terms of the addition to the book of sale based on what was included by Imam Abu Abdullah. Al-Bukhari and Abu Al-Hussein Al-Qushayri, may God be pleased with them. I have mentioned in this book books that Al-Bukhari translated in another The book of sales, including the book of peace, the book of pre-emption, the book of leasing, the book of transfer, the book of tillage, the book of agriculture, and the book of The Book of Misaqah, the Book of Gifts, the Book of Gifts, the Book of Loan, the Book of Capture, the Book of Grievances, and the Book of Abstinence, on the issue, And the mortgage book, and the company book, and the book of emancipation, and the book of offices, and the book of certificates, and the book of reconciliation, and the book of conditions, and the book Wills, and the Book of Endowments, but I explained them at the end of this book so that no one might be under the illusion that I left the Book of Sales out of these. The Books, and God is the Helper in what I do in following the footsteps of the two Imams, may God be pleased with them, and He is my suffice and He is the best disposer of affairs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2375 - True
 The book of jihad"
"2376","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When the people of Mecca expelled the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him. Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, said: To God we belong and to Him we shall return. They brought out their Prophet to destroy us. He said: So “A call to those who fight has been revealed because they have been wronged, and indeed, God has power to grant them victory” [Al-Hajj: 39] and Ibn Abbas used to recite it. “Then,” Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: “I knew it was a fight.” Ibn Abbas said: “This is the first verse revealed regarding fighting.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2376 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2377","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim Al-Qashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf And his companions came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, we were in glory while we were polytheists, but when we believed we became humiliated. He said: “I have been commanded to pardon, so do not fight the people.” When he turned him to Medina, he ordered him to fight, so they desisted, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed {Have you not seen those to whom it was said, “Restrain your hands and establish prayer and give zakat?” But when fighting was prescribed for them, behold, a group of them feared the people. [An-Nisa: 77] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2377 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2378","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, and Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ruh told us, Habib bin Shihab Al-Ghubari told us, he said: I heard my father say: I and a friend of ours came to Ibn Abbas and said: We met Abu Hurairah at Ibn Abbas’s door, and he said: Who are you? So we informed him, and he said: They went to the people on dates and water. A valley only flows according to its capacity. We said: Your goodness has increased. Ask permission for us according to Ibn Abbas. So he asked permission for us, and we heard Ibn Abbas speaking on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a speech on the day of Tabuk. He said: “There is nothing among people like a man who takes a rein and strives in the path of God and avoids the evils of people, and like a man who wanders among his sheep and comforts his guest.” And he fulfills his rights. He said, so I said: Did he say it? He said: He said it three times. So I said “Allahu Akbar” and praised and thanked him, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2378 - True"
"2379","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Abu Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, saying: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Mu’afa bin Suleiman, Fulayh bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar, on the authority of Saeed bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the best status of people?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “A man taking the reins of his horse in the cause of God, until he is killed or dies. Shall I not inform you of what follows him?” “A man secluded among a people, performing prayer, paying zakat, and bearing witness that there is no god but Allah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2379 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2380","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Abu Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He stood up in the year of Tabuk and addressed the people while leaning his back against a palm tree. He said: “Shall I not tell you about the best of people and the worst of people?” Among the best of people is a man who works in the cause of God on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or on his feet until death comes to him. The worst of people is an immoral and bold man who reads the Book of God and does not pay heed to any of it. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2380 - True"
"2381","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Muhammad bin Maan Al-Ghafari informed me. Abu Ma'n, Zahra bin Ma'bad al-Qurashi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, the servant of Uthman, who said: I heard Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, in a mosque Fear in Mina, and he told us that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “One day in the path of God is better than a thousand days in anything else, so let him see.” “Every man for himself.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2381 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2382","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Hisham told me Ibn Sa'd, on the authority of Sa'id Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, passed by a river in which there was a spring of fresh water, and he was impressed by its goodness and beauty. He said: If I were to isolate myself from the people and reside in this river, Then he said: I will not do it until I consult the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Do not do it.” The position of one of you in the path of God is better than his prayers with his family for sixty years. Would you not like God to forgive you and admit you to Paradise? “Fight in the way of God. Whoever fights in the way of God, hiccuping a she-camel, Paradise is guaranteed for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2382 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2383","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Masry told us, Yahya bin Ayoub, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A place “A man standing in line for the sake of God is better in the sight of God than worshiping a man for sixty years.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2383 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2384","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Abu Al-Walid Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Burd informed us. Al-Antaki, Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Masisi told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam May God be pleased with him. He said: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat with us and we said: “If only we knew which deeds are most beloved to God, We did it. Then God Almighty revealed, “All that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth glorify God, and He is the Mighty, the All-Wise” until the end of the surah, so the Messenger of God recited it to us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Thus said Al-Awza’i, and Yahya bin Abi Kathir read it to us in Mecca. Muhammad bin Kathir said, and he read it to us Al-Awza’i said: This is what Abu Al-Walid said, and Ibn Kathir recited it to us. This is how Abu Al-Hasan bin Uqba said, and Abu Al-Walid is like this.” Al-Hakim said: “And Sheikh Abu Al-Hasan Al-Shaybani recited it to us like this.” Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah recited to us: “The Surah From the beginning to the end.” Narrated by Al-Walid bin Muslim on the authority of Al-Awza’i from the beginning of the chain of transmission to the end."
"2385","Ahmed bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Sulayman bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Al-Awza’i, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, Abu Salamah told me, Abdullah bin Salam told me, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, so we said: If we only knew which deeds are most beloved to God, then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” My greatest suspicion is that what made them abandon it was the narration of Al-Haqal ibn Ziyad. Contrary to the narration of Al-Walid bin Muslim and others.”"
"2386","Abu Al-Hasan Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Shaarani told us, Jeddi told us, Abu Salih Abdullah bin Salih Al-Masry told us, Al-Haqal told us Ibn Ziyadah, Al-Awza’i narrated to me, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, Hilal Ibn Abi Maimunah narrated to me, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, he narrated that Abdullah bin Salam, may God be pleased with him, narrated to him, and Al-Awza’i said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Salamah bin Abd narrated to me. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we said: If only we knew which deeds are most beloved to God So he mentioned the hadith. “And this cannot be said to be the hadith of Al-Walid ibn Muslim, for Al-Haqal ibn Ziyad, even if its basis is certainty and reliability, then he doubted its chain of transmission and those who The evidence for the authenticity of the chain of transmission of Abu Salamah is that Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Fazari, the most memorized of the companions of al-Awza’i, narrated it with additional wording. It is mentioned in the first chain of narration
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2384 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2387","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Mahboub bin Musa Al-Antaki told us, Abu Ishaq told us Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, he said: We gathered and discussed which of you comes to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asks him which of the deeds is most beloved to God? Then we separated, and we feared that someone would come to him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to us and gathered us together, making our day to meet one another. “So he recited to us, ‘Glory be to God, whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth’” until the end of the surah. Abu Salamah said: Then Abdullah bin Salam recited it to us until the end. Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Abu Salamah recited it to us from From the beginning to the end, Mahboub said: And Abu Ishaq recited it to us from the beginning to the end, meaning Surat Al-Saff."
"2388","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told me, that Musa bin Ismail told them, he said: Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, On the authority of Abu Imran al-Jawni, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, that he said while he was in line with the enemy: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Paradise is under the shade of swords.” A young man with a shabby appearance said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, so the eyelid of his sword broke along with it, then he said to his companions: Peace be upon you, then he entered the fight «» This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2388 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2389","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Sa’id bin Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Ayyash ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said to me God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you know who will be the first group of my nation to enter Paradise?” He said: God and His Messenger know best, and he said: “The immigrants will come on the Day of Resurrection to the gate of Paradise and open it, and the Keeper will say to them, Or have you been called to account? They say, “For what will we be held accountable?” Indeed, our swords were on our shoulders in the path of God, until we died in that state. He said: Then it will be opened for them, and they will remain there for forty years before the people enter it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2389 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2390","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told us, Hisham bin Abdul-Malik al-Tayalisi told us, Sulayman bin Kathir told us, Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he was asked, “O believers?” Do I have more complete faith? He said: “The one who strives in the cause of God with his life and his wealth, and a man who worships God among a people, for the people have sufficed with his evil.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2390 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2391","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abu Hani told me, about Amr bin Malik al-Janabi said that he heard Abu Fadala bin Ubaid, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “I am a leader - and a leader and supporter - for whoever believes, submits, and strives in the path of God, with a house in the outskirts of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise, and I A leader for whoever believes in a house in the middle of Paradise, and I am a leader for whoever believes, submits to Islam, and emigrates for a house in the outskirts of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise. And a house in the highest part of Paradise. Whoever does that and leaves no search for good, nor escape from evil, he will die wherever he wishes to die.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2391 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2392","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qatada bin Di’amah, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You are still... A group from my nation will fight for the truth, defeating those who have opposed them until the last of them fights the Antichrist. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2392 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2393","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith, that Abu Ushanah Al-Maafiri told him that he heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “Indeed, the first group to enter Paradise are the poor and emigrants, those from whom calamity is avoided. If they are commanded, they listen and obey. And if any of them has a need for authority, it will not be fulfilled for him until he dies while it is in his heart, and God Almighty will call upon him on the Day of Resurrection. Paradise, and it will bring its adornments and its decoration. He will say: “Where are My servants who fought in the way of God, and were killed in My way, and were harmed in My way, and struggled In my way, enter Paradise.” And they will enter it without reckoning, and without torment. Then the angels will come and say: Our Lord, we glorify You at night. And the day, and we sanctify to you who are these whom you have preferred over us? Then the Lord, Blessed and Most High, says: “These are those who fought in My way and were harmed in My way. Then the angels will enter upon them from every door. Peace be upon you.” “Because you have been patient, what a good afterlife is the abode.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2393 - True"
"2394","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “They will not come together in Hell in such a way that they would harm each other, such as a Muslim killing an infidel, then attacking the Muslim, and he approaches, nor will they come together in the belly of a slave.” “Dust in the path of God and the smoke of Hell, and they do not go together in the heart of a servant of faith and miserliness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih with two other chains of transmission, one of them on the authority of Safwan bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah May God be pleased with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2394 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2395","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Safwan bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No dust is collected for the sake of God, and the smoke of Hell will never be in the belly of a servant, and miserliness and faith will never combine in the heart of a servant.” It was said on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym."
"2396","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Mukarram told us, in Basra, Amr bin Ali told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Hammad told us Bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Never will the dust of God and the smoke of Hell gather in the face of a Muslim man.”"
"2397","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Sa’id bin Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Khair bin Nu’aym, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a detachment Then a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of God, you sent this expedition and my husband went out with it, and I was fasting as he fasted. I pray with his prayers, and I worship with his worship, so he guides me to a work by which I can achieve his work. He said: “You pray and do not sit, you fast and do not break your fast, and you remember and do not deceive.” She said: And can I bear that, O Messenger of God? He said: “And if I had overcome that, while by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I would not have reached the tenth of what he did.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2397 - True"
"2398","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Uthman Al-Tanukhi told us, Al-Haytham bin Hamid, Al-Alaa bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger God, grant me permission to travel. He said: “My nation’s journey is jihad for the sake of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2398 - True"
"2399","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Mahran told me, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Al-Musaffa told me, Ali ibn Ayyash told me, Al-Layth ibn Saad, narrated by Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Ibn Shafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Qifla “Like an invasion.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2399 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2400","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bazzaz told me in Baghdad, Samak ibn Abd al-Samad told us, Abu Musahar Abd al-Ala ibn Musahar told us Al-Ghasani, Ismail bin Abdullah told us, Al-Awza’i told me, Sulayman bin Habib told me, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Three, all of whom are guarantors of God; A man goes out as a fighter in the cause of God. He is a guarantor with God until He takes his death, then admits him to Paradise, or returns him with whatever reward or reward he has received. spoils, and a man went to the mosque. He is a guarantor with God until He takes his death, then admits him to Paradise or returns him with whatever reward or reward he received. spoils, and a man who entered his house with peace, so he is a guarantor with God.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2400 - True"
"2401","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Malik told me Al-Sharabi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Jaafar, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Salman Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: He ordered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with a secret group. They said: O Messenger of God, shall we go out tonight or until the morning? He said: “Would you not like to spend the night among the sheep of Paradise?” And autumn is the garden. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2401 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2402","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Qutayba bin Sa’id told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Muslim bin Aidh, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of his father, that a man came to pray while the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He, peace and blessings be upon him, led us in prayer. When he finished the row, he said: Oh God, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he said: “Who was speaking above?” The man said: I am, O Messenger of God. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the path of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2402 - True"
"2403","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi informed me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq informed me, Al-Harith told me Ibn Fudayl Al-Ansari, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Labid Al-Ansari, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “The martyrs are on Bariq - a river at the gate of Paradise - in a green dome. Their provision will be given to them morning and evening.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is on the condition of Muslim and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2403 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2404","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Omar bin Saad Al-Darimi told us, Mahboub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You must wage jihad in the path of God, for it is one of the gates of Paradise, through which God takes away anxiety.” And grief,” and others added to it: “And strive in the cause of God, near and far, and uphold the limits of God in near and far, and do not let yourselves lead you into God.” “Blaming a blameworthy person” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2404 - True"
"2405","Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Qaari informed us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A man will be brought from the people of Paradise, and God will say to him: O son of Adam, how? Did you find your home? So he says: Yes, Lord, the best abode. He says: Ask and hope. He says: What do I ask you and hope for? I ask you to return me to this world so that I may be killed in your cause ten times because of the virtue of martyrdom he saw. He said: And a man from the people of Hell will be brought, and God will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? So he says: What is the Lord of evil? Then the Lord Almighty says: So you can ransom him with gold from the ground? He says: Yes. So he says: “I lied. I asked you for something other than that and you did not do it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it and in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2405 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2406","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Nastas, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: While the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the spirit, some Bedouins from Saraf descended upon them and said: Which of the people do you want? It was said: Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What is the matter with me when I see you wearing your uniform and your weapons being scanty? They said: We wait for one of the two good deeds. Either we will be killed and we will go to Paradise, or we will be defeated and God will gather victory and Paradise for us. He said: Where is your Prophet? They said: Here he is. He said to him: O Prophet of God, I have no interest in taking what is mine and then following up. He said: “Go to your family and take what is best for you.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to lead Badr, and the man went out to his family until He finished his need, then he joined the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Badr, while he was lining up the people to fight in their mobilization, so he entered the line with them. So the people fought, and he was among those whom God called as a martyr. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose up after God had defeated the polytheists and given victory to the believers, and he passed on. In front of the martyrs, and Omar bin Al-Khattab was with him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Here, O Omar, you love hadith, and the martyrs have Lords, nobles, and kings, and this, O Umar, is one of them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2406 - No, by God, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Nastas is weak."
"2407","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him And peace be upon him said: “If the companions of Uhud were mentioned, by God, I wish I had been taken away with my companions in the mountain fortress.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2407 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2408","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Mahboub bin Musa Al-Antaki told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, about Al-A'mash, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in The Battle of Tabuk. He said to me: “If you wish, I will inform you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and its peak.” He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: As for “the head of the matter is Islam, its pillar is prayer, and its peak is jihad,” this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2408 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2409","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abu Sakhr, on the authority of Yazid ibn Qusayt al-Laythi, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, my father told me that Abdullah ibn Jahsh said on the day Uhud: Don’t you come, we will pray to God? So they went away to a place, so he called Saad and said: O Lord, when we meet our people tomorrow, meet me with a strong man whose valor is very strong. Drive him away, so I will fight him for you and he will fight me, then grant me victory over him until I kill him and take his loot. Then Abdullah bin Jahsh stood up and said: Oh God, grant me tomorrow a man with a strong hand, strong in his violence. I will fight him for Your sake and he will fight me, then he takes me and cuts off my nose and ears. I met you tomorrow and said: O Abdullah, why did your nose and ear hurt? So I say: In you and in your Messenger, and he says: You have spoken the truth. Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: O my son, “Abdullah bin Jahsh’s call was better than my call. I saw him at the end of the day, and his call to prayer was “And his nose was hung on a thread.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2409 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2410","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told me about Marw, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Ibn Juraij told us, he said: Suleiman said Bin Musa: Malik bin Yakhamir told us that Muadh bin Jabal told them that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever fights in the way of God If a Muslim man hiccups a she-camel, then Paradise is destined for him. And whoever asks God to kill from his own will, truthfully, and then dies or is killed, then it will be for him. “The reward of a martyr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. “It has an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of the two sheikhs, in brief.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2410 - Rather, it is interrupted, so perhaps it is from the abrogator"
"2411","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us: Muhammad bin Abd told us: Allah bin Bazi’, told us by Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman, he said: I heard my father narrating, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Whoever asks God to kill in the cause of God truthfully, and then dies, God will give him the reward of a martyr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2411 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2412","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Shurayh, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “Whoever asks God for martyrdom truthfully, God will grant him the status of martyrs, even if he dies in his bed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2412 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2413","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Mahboub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim Abul-Nadr, the client of Omar bin Abdullah and who was his clerk, said: Abdullah bin Abi Awfa wrote to him when he went out to Al-Hurriyya wrote a book, and in it was: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people, do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask God for well-being. “So when you meet him, be patient, and know that Paradise is under the shade of swords.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2413 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2414","Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan Al-Adeeb told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed Al-Adeeb told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Zakaria bin Abu Masarra, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shurayh told us, Abu Hani Al-Khawlani told us, that he heard Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubli, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no female warrior who fights in the cause of God. So they gain spoils, unless they hasten two-thirds of their reward from the Hereafter, and a third is left for them. If they do not gain spoils, their reward will be complete.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2414 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2415","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yahya bin Ayoub, and Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Zaban bin Faid, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Prayer, fasting, and remembrance are multiplied seven hundred times over expenditure in the path of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2415 - True"
"2416","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Najda Al-Houti told us, Baqiya bin Al-Walid, Abdul-Rahman bin Thabit bin Thuban told us, returning it to Makhoul, to Abdul-Rahman bin Ghanam Al-Ash’ari, that Abu Malik Al-Ash'ari said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever fights in the cause of God and dies or is killed is a martyr, or his horse snipes him.” Or his camel, or the bite of a large animal, or he dies in his bed by whatever death God wills, then he is a martyr and his is Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2416 - Ibn Thawban was not used as evidence by Muslim, nor is he, and the rest of them are trustworthy, and Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam was not cited by Makhoul, I think."
"2417","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Hani, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every dead person should be sealed “On his work, except the one who is stationed, for his work will continue until the Day of Resurrection, and he will be safe from the calamities of the grave.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Muslim and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2417 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2418","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi and Ibrahim bin Muhammad, the jurist Al-Bukhari, informed us, saying: Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah reported, on the authority of Wahib ibn al-Ward, on the authority of Omar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever dies and does not fight and does not talk to himself about the fight, died on a branch of hypocrisy.” He used this as evidence. Muslim by Wuhayb ibn al-Ward. This is a major hadith by Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak. They did not narrate it, and Abdullah ibn Raja’ al-Makki followed it. Wahib bin Al-Ward based on his narration on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2418 - Narrated by Ibn Al-Mubarak and Abdullah bin Raja’ Al-Makki on the authority of Wahib, according to Muslim’s conditions."
"2419","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever dies and does not He invades, but he does not have the desire to invade. He died on the verge of hypocrisy.”"
"2420","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari, and Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah told us: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan, Muhammad bin Musfa al-Homsi, Ali bin Hajr al-Saadi, and Ali bin Sahl al-Ramli told us, they said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever meets God without “A trace of jihad, he found it with a mark on it.” This is a major hadith on this topic, except that the two sheikhs did not use Ismail bin Rafi’ as evidence.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2420 - Ismail bin Rafi’ is weak"
"2421","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us dictation, Hilal bin Al-Alaa Al-Raqi told us, Abdullah bin Jaafar Al-Raqi told us, Ubaid told us Allah bin Amr Al-Ruqi, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisah, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Abdi told us, he said: I heard Ibn Al-Khasasiyah, He says: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pledge allegiance to him on the basis of Islam, and he stipulated that “You bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad His servant and His Messenger, and you pray the five days of prayer, and fast Ramadan, and pay zakat, and perform Hajj to the House, and strive in the cause of God.” He said: I said: O Messenger By God, as for two, I cannot bear them. As for zakat, I only have ten animals. They are the messengers of my family and their messengers. As for jihad, they claim that it is Whoever takes charge has incurred the wrath of God, and I fear when a battle comes to me. I hate death, and my soul is humbled. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested. Then he moved his hand and said: “No charity and no jihad, so how will you enter Paradise?” He said: Then I said: O Messenger of God, I pledge allegiance to you, so he pledged allegiance to me for both of them. Among those mentioned among the Ansar Companions, may God be pleased with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2421 - True"
"2422","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Al-Layth told me Bin Saad, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Shurahbil, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever labors day and night in the cause of God will have the reward of fasting for a month and praying in prayer, and whoever dies while practicing labor will have a similar reward. And sustenance was bestowed on him, and he was secure from temptations.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and there is no one from the Levant who is a jurist in it.”"
"2423","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Muhammad told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Abd al-Karim bin al-Harith, on the authority of Abi Ubaidah bin Uqba, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Salman Al-Khair, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and similar things.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2422 - True"
"2424","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Thawr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Aidh, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of a night Better than Laylat Al-Qadr? A guard on guard in a land of fear, hoping that he will not return to his family.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah, on the authority of Thawr, and there is an example in Yahya bin Saeed.”"
"2425","Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Asimi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Makhzoumi told us, and Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ahmasi told us, They said: Waki` narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, so he narrated it with a chain of narration.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2424 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2426","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told me, in Mecca, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Khams bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, Mus’ab bin Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, may God be pleased with him, he said: Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, said: On the authority of him, while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit: I am telling you a story, and nothing prevented me from telling it to you except my longing for you. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him said: “A night’s guard in the cause of God is better than a thousand nights of prayer during which the nights are spent and the days of which are fasted.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2426 - True"
"2427","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Strive the polytheists with your wealth and your lives.” “And your tongues.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2427 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2428","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zannad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was next to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was overcome by tranquility. Then the thigh of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell on my thigh, and I did not find the weight of anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. My thigh, then he walked away from him and said: “Write.” So I wrote on my shoulder: “Those of the believers who sit are not equal, except those affected and those who strive in the cause of God.” [An-Nisa: 95] Until the end of the verse, Ibn Umm Maktum, who was a blind man, stood up when he heard the virtue of the mujahideen and said: O Messenger of God, so what about whom? Is it not possible for the believers to wage jihad? When he finished his words, peace came over the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his thigh fell on my thigh, and I felt its weight the second time. Just as I found it the first time. Then he walked away from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Read, O Zaid.” So I recited, “Those who sit are not equal to those who sit.” The believers. So I attached it while He is in whose hand is my soul, as if I was looking at its appendix at a crack in the shoulder. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2428 - True"
"2429","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Sa’id, the client of Al-Mahri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to the Banu Lahyan and said: “Let a man come out from each of the two men.” Then he said to the one sitting: “Which of you is behind the outside in His family and his wealth were well. He had the equivalent of half the wage of a foreigner.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. He did not narrate it with this wording. Muslim alone, the hadith of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid: Whoever prepared an invader for the sake of “God has conquered.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2429 - True"
"2430","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Al-Hafiz, dictation narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Suleiman Al-Saadi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Qasim narrated to us. Al-Asadi, Omar bin Rashid Al-Yamami told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three springs that cannot be touched by fire: a spring that was gouged out for the sake of God, and a spring that was guarded for the sake of Allah.” God, and an eye that wept out of fear of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “It was narrated with another chain of narration on the authority of Abu Hurairah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2430 - Omar bin Rashid, they are weak"
"2431","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Qanabi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, Ubayy told us, On the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Two eyes were forbidden from being touched by the Fire: an eye that wept out of fear of God, and an eye that spent the night guarding Islam and its people from the people of disbelief.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2431 - There is a break"
"2432","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Shurayh, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shamir, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Janabi, on the authority of Abu Rayhana, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in A raid, and we paid with honour, and a severe cold struck us, to the point that one of us was digging the hole, then he entered it and covered it with his quilt. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw this among the people, he said: “Is there a man guarding us tonight? I will pray to God for him with a supplication that he will bestow good on him.” Then a man from the Ansar stood up and said: I am, O Messenger of God. So he supplicated for him. Abu Rayhana said: So I said: I am, so he supplicated for me with a supplication that was different from what he supplicated for the Ansari, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Fire has been forbidden to an eye that has shed tears from fear of God. Fire has been forbidden to an eye that has stayed awake in the path of God.” He said: And I forgot the third. Abu Shurayh said: And I later heard that he said: “The Fire is forbidden to an eye that turns a blind eye to what God has forbidden, or an eye that is gouged out in the path of God.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2432 - True"
"2433","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abu Tawba Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ Al-Halabi informed us, Muawiyah told us Ibn Salam, Zayd Ibn Salam told me, Abu Kabsha al-Saluli told me, that he heard Sahl ibn al-Hanzaliyya, mentioning that they walked with the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on the day of Hunayn, so they continued their journey until it was evening, when prayer came with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and then a man came. Persian and said: O Messenger of God, I set out in front of you until I rose to such-and-such mountain, and behold, I was at Hazin on the ground. With their wealth, their blessings, and their will, they gathered to Hunayn, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and said: “This is the spoils of the Muslims tomorrow. God willing, then he said: “Who is guarding us tonight?” Anas bin Marthad Al-Ghanawi said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: “Ride.” He mounted his horse and came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Go towards this people until you are at the top, and do not flee from them tonight.” So when we became The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to his place of prayer and prostrated two rak’ahs, then said: “Have you noticed your knight?” Then a man said: We did not feel good, so he resumed the prayer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to the people until he finished his prayer, and said: “Rejoice.” “So your knight has come.” He said: So he made us look at the shade of the trees in the valley, and behold, he came until he stood over the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he greeted him and said: I set out until I was at the top of this mountain, where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me. When I woke up, I looked at The two peoples, so I looked and did not see anyone, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Did you come down tonight?” He said: No, except for one who is praying or fulfilling a need. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have obligated, so you do not have to do anything after that.” This The chain of transmission from beginning to end is correct according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, “except that they did not produce the Musnads of Sahl ibn al-Hanaliyah due to the lack of narration.” Those who followed him, and he is one of the great Companions, as I mentioned at the appropriate time.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2433 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, but they did not mention Sahl, and he is a great Companion."
"2434","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Haywa told me Ibn Shurayh, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Aslam Abi Imran, he said: We invaded from Medina, we wanted Constantinople and the group. Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid bin al-Walid and the Romans stuck their backs to the city wall, and a man charged at the enemy, and the people said: Mah, ma, no. There is no god but God. He will throw his hands into destruction. Abu Ayyub said: “This verse was only revealed about us, the Ansar, when God helped His Prophet and revealed Islam. We said: To them: We take care of our wealth and put it in order, so God Almighty revealed {And spend in the cause of God, and do not throw yourself into destruction with your own hands} [Al-Baqarah: 195], so to cast our own hands into destruction is to take stock of our wealth and put it in order, and give up jihad.” Abu Imran said: Abu did not cease Ayoub struggled in the cause of God until he was buried in Constantinople. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2434 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2435","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Haywa bin Shurayh al-Hadrami told us, Baqiya bin Al-Walid told us, Buhair bin Saad told me, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Bahria, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Conquest is two conquests. As for whoever seeks the face of God, obeys the imam, and spends generous, and he is pleased with his partner, and he avoids corruption, for his sleep and his awakening are all rewarded. As for whoever invades pride, hypocrisy, and reputation, and disobeys the Imam And he spreads corruption in the land, he will not return with sufficient means.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2435 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2436","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abdullah bin Ali Al-Ghazal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, Ibn Abi Dhib reported, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ayoub bin Mikraz, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, a man said: O Messenger of God, is there a man who wants jihad for the sake of God and he is seeking some of the worldly goods? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no reward for him.” So he asked him the second and third time, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no reward.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2436 - True"
"2437","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Muzaki told us, Ahmad bin Salama told us, Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Al-Wadah narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Hanan bin Kharijah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr Radi On his authority, he said: O Messenger of God, tell me about jihad and battle. He said: “O Abdullah bin Amr, if you fight a patient patient seeking reward, God will send you patient and seeking reward, and if you fight a frequent hypocrite, God will send you a hypocrite.” Repeatedly, O Abdullah bin Amr, whatever condition you fought or were killed, may God send you to that state.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And Muhammad bin Abi Al-Wahddah. This is Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Muslim bin Abi Al-Wahddah, the disciplined one, trustworthy and trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2437 - True"
"2438","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah told us. Al-Uwaisi, Muhammad bin Saleh bin Qays Al-Azraq told me, on the authority of Saleh bin Muhammad bin Zaida, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God have mercy on the keeper of the guard.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2438 - True"
"2439","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Attab Al-Abdi told us in Baghdad, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abi Al-Awam told us Al-Riyahi, Quraysh bin Anas narrated to us, Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih narrated to us, and the pronunciation of it is, Abu Al-Muthanna Muadh bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sa’sa’a bin Muawiyah, He said: I said to Abu Dharr: What is the matter with you? He said: My money is my work. He said: I said: Talk to me. He said: Yes. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no servant who spends of all the wealth of his two wives in the cause of God. Unless the hosts of Paradise will meet him, all of them inviting him to what he has.” He said: I said: How is that? He said: “If it is men, then two men, and if it is camels, then two camels, and if it is cows, then two cows.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. “And Sa’sa’ah bin Muawiyah is one of the proudest of the Arabs, and the companions of Al-Hasan narrated it from him. “I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub say: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri He says: I heard Yahya bin Mu’in say: Sa’sa’ bin Muawiyah is the companion of Abu Dharr and he is the brother of Juzzi bin Mu’awiyah. I heard Abu Hafs Omar bin Ja`far al-Basri, the memorizer, said more than once: The Basraites do not have a better chapter than the paths of the hadith of al-Hasan on the authority of Sa`sa`ah. Al-Hakim said: “So I asked This hadith was narrated and I collected it, and when we met the second time in Baghdad, I mentioned it to him, and he benefited me from what I did not have, so I narrated Al-Hakim Abu Ahmad Al-Hafiz, may God have mercy on him, one day told me this story, and I reminded him of it, and he said to me: Whoever narrated this hadith on the authority of Abu Dharr other than What a shock? ""I did not memorize""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2439 - True"
"2440","So he told me, saying: Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Sulayman al-Wasiti told us, Abu al-Taqi Hisham bin Abdul-Malik al-Yazani told us, Muhammad bin Harb told us, On the authority of Al-Zubaidi, Suleiman bin Amir told me that he heard that a man asked Abu Dharr what is the matter with you? He said: I have nothing to do with my work, then he narrated the hadith at length, and the two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Al-Zuhri on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever spends two pairs of his money in the path of God,” and his driving is in violation of To contextualize the hadith of Sa'sa'ah
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2440 - And in the two Sahihs there is a similar hadith from Abu Hurairah"
"2441","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us. Al-Azdi, son of the daughter of Muawiyah bin Amr, my grandfather Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ bin Umaila Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Yasir ibn Umaylah, on the authority of Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever spends an expense in For the sake of God, it has been written down seven hundred times. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Muslim used Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ as evidence. He is a Kufi with strong hadith, and his uncle is Yasir bin Umaylah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2441 - True
 He told me that what I mentioned was true"
"2442","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh, narrated to me Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to me, narrated to me Maslamah bin Ja’far, from Bujaila, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ said: My uncle told me, on the authority of Abu Yahya Khurraym bin Fatik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “People are four, and deeds are six, so they are obligatory, and like for like, and ten times, and seven hundred times, so whoever dies as an unbeliever, it is obligatory for him.” Hell, and whoever dies as a believer, Paradise is due for him, and the servant does an evil deed and will not be rewarded except with the like of it, and the servant intends to do a good deed, so it is recorded. He gets ten, and the servant spends what he spends in the way of God, and it is multiplied seven hundred times for him, and the people are four, so he is expanded upon in this world. It will be expanded upon in the Hereafter, and it will be expanded upon in this world, and it will be restricted in the Hereafter, and it will be expanded upon in this world, and it will be miserable in the Hereafter. In this world and the hereafter.”"
"2443","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yahya told me Ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Zaban Ibn Faid, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Muadh Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever reads “A thousand signs for the sake of God, which God has written down with the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2443 - True"
"2444","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “When your brothers were afflicted with Uhud, God placed their souls in the belly of green birds, flowing through the rivers of Paradise, eating from their fruits, and providing shelter.” To golden lamps hanging in the shade of the throne, and when they found good food, drink and rest, they said: Who will inform our brothers about us? Are we alive in Paradise, lest they renounce jihad and do not abandon war? Then God, Blessed and Most High, said: I will inform them about you, and God revealed {And do not think that those who are killed in the cause of God are dead} [Al Imran: 169] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2444 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2445","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Atik, Salamah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Whoever goes out of his house to fight in the path of God, then he says: Then he joined his three fingers, ‘Where are the fighters in the path of God?’ Then he fell down from his mount. Then he dies, then his reward falls on God, and if an animal bites him and he dies, then his reward falls on God, and whoever dies, his nose is cut off, he said: And it is For a word I have not heard from any of the Arabs, first from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning by blowing his nose on his bed, his reward has come. On God, and whoever is killed recklessly will be deserving of Paradise. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2445 - True"
"2446","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Aswad bin Shayban Al-Sadusi told us, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Shakhir Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif Ibn Abdullah, he said: He used to inform me about Abu Dharr, a hadith, and I longed to meet him. So I met him and said: O Abu Dharr, I was informed of a hadith about you and I longed to meet you. He said: By God, your father has met me. He said: I said: Tell me, I have been informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to you. He said: “Indeed, God loves three people and hates three people.” He said: “I do not think I would lie to my boyfriend.” He said: I said: Who are these whom God loves? He said: “A man who fought in the cause of God, being patient, seeking reward, and struggling. He met the enemy and fought until he was killed, and you will find him in the Book of God.” Revealed, then he read this verse {Indeed, God loves those who fight in His way in array, as if they were a solid building} [As-Saff: 4]. I said: And who? He said: A man has a bad neighbor who harms him, and he is patient with his harm until God suffices him for him, either with life or death. I said: And who? He said: A man was traveling with a people who fell asleep until, at the end of the night, they became tired and drowsy, so they hit their heads, then he got up. So he was purified out of fear of God and desire for what is with Him. I said: Who are the three whom God hates? He said: The arrogant and proud one, and you find it in the revealed Book of God {Indeed, God does not like every arrogant and proud person} [Luqman: 18]. I said: And who? He said: The stingy and ungrateful. He said: And who? He said: The allied merchant or seller “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2446 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2447","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Malhan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Al-Layth ibn Sa’d narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn al-Hadi, Abu Uthman al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah al-Adawi, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever shades the leader of a rebel, God will shade him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever prepares a invader until he is independent.” With his device, he will have a reward similar to his. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Al-Bukhari cited Uthman bin Abdullah bin Suraqah as evidence, and he is The son of the daughter of the Commander of the Faithful, Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him.” There is evidence for this hadith from the hadith of Sahl bin Hunaif.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2447 - True"
"2448","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that Sahl told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever helps... Striving in the cause of God, or in debt due to his hardship, or one who is buried in his neck, God will shade him in His shade on a day when there will be no shade but His shade.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2448 - Al-Dhahabi was silent about it in his summary in this place"
"2449","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi informed us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: A man came with a camel that was muzzled and said: This is for the sake of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will have seven hundred for it on the Day of Resurrection, all of them sealed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. Bukhari did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2449 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2450","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yaqoub, on the authority of Qays ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, that he passed by Muadh ibn Jabal while he was standing on the Chapter, then Muadh said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever strives in the path of God is a guarantor of God, and whoever enters upon an imam He pardons him, he is a guarantor against God, and whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone in a bad way, he is a guarantor against God.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2450 - True"
"2451","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Warraq told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told me, Ubaida bin Humaid told me, Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God Almighty be pleased with them, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He wanted to invade, so he said: “O community of immigrants and Ansar, among your brothers are people who have neither money nor a clan. Let one of you join the two or three men to him, and none of us has a back to carry except an obstacle like the obstacle of one of them. He said: So I joined myself. Two or three, I only have the obstacle of one of them: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2451 - True"
"2452","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, Kathir ibn al-Harith narrated to me, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which Is charity better? He said: “The service of a servant, or the shade of a tent or a stall, or a tent for the sake of God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2452 - True"
"2453","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told me in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: On the day of Badr, we were taking three people in turn to A camel, and Ali and Abu Lubabah were my companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was the obstacle of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They say to him: Ride until we walk, and he says: “I am not more deprived of reward than you, nor are you stronger at walking than me.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2453 - True"
"2454","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: I heard Muawiyah Ibn Salih, saying: Nu’aym Ibn Ziyad told me that he heard Abu Kabshah, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks, and their families are helpful to them, and the one who spends on them is like one who extends his hand with charity.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, and they did not narrate it with this addition and there is a witness to it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2454 - True"
"2455","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab bin Habib Al-Abdi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Hisham bin Saad, Qais bin Bishr al-Taghlabi told me, he said: My father used to sit with Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, in Damascus, and there was a man from Damascus in Damascus. The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he is called Ibn al-Hanzaliyya al-Ansari. He passed by us one day and greeted us, and Abu al-Darda’ said to him: A word. It will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that “the one who spends on horses in the cause of God is like one who spreads out his hands for charity and will not take it back.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2455 - We produced it as a witness"
"2456","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Talha bin Abi told us Saeed, that Saeed Al-Maqbari, narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever keeps a horse in On the path of God, out of faith in God and believing in God’s promises, his satiety, his dung, his dung, and his urine will be good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2456 - True"
"2457","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Ruh bin Ubadah told me, Abdul-Hamid bin Jaafar told me, he told me Yazid bin Abi Habib narrated to me, Suwayd bin Qais narrated to me, Muawiyah bin Khadij narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Dhar al-Ghafari, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “There is no Arabian horse without two supplications being given to him every day, saying: O God, as You have appointed me whom You have appointed me, so make me one of those I love.” His wealth and his family to him: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2457 - True"
"2458","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba bin Al-Raqqashi told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Abi told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Ayoub narrated, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ali bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “The best of the horses is the darkest, the most beautiful, the most beautiful, the most beautiful, and the one with the right hand. If it is not the darkest, then I will kill this sheep.” This is a hadith. “It is strange and authentic, and the two sheikhs used all of its narrations as evidence and did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2458 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim Gharib"
"2459","Abu Amr Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Sukkari told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, Ubaid bin In the morning, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “If you want to fight, buy a dark-brown horse with a long, straight-legged horse, for you will gain booty and be safe.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2459 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2460","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told us, Uthman bin Sa`id told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Zuhayr told us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sarjis, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He says: “You have been overshadowed by temptations, like pieces of a dark night, from which the people have been saved by the owner of a high tower eating from the messengers of his sheep, or a man from behind the paths.” “He was holding the reins of his horse and eating from the feces of his sword.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2460 - True"
"2461","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Shaar’ani told me, narrated by my grandfather Abdullah bin Salih, that Abu Shurayh Al-Maafiri told him on the authority of my father Hani’, on the authority of Abu Ali al-Janabi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Who He is satisfied with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger, and Paradise is destined for him.” Abu Saeed said: So I thanked God, said God, and was pleased. With it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And there are other things whereby God will raise its people in Paradise one hundred levels, between every two levels, as shown The heaven and the earth, or the furthest thing between the heaven and the earth.” He said: I said, “What is that, O Messenger of God?” He said: Jihad for the sake of God, Jihad for the sake of God “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2461 - True"
"2462","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Asim Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Kurayb bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Abu Burdah bin Qais, may God be pleased with him, my brother Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, make... “And my nation was destroyed in your cause by slaughter and plague.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2462 - True"
"2463","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad told us, Thabit informed us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, a black man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I am a black man with a stinking odor, an ugly face, and I have no money. If I fight these people until I am killed, where am I? He said: “In Paradise.” He fought until he was killed, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him and said: “May God make your face bright, and your fragrance pleasant, and your wealth increase.” And he said to this man or to someone else: “I saw his wife, a virgin, tearing him away from a cloak of wool that he had, coming between it and his cloak.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2463 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2464","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me of Mecca. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad al-San’ani informed us. Abd al-Razzaq, and Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he informed us Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Passed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a people throwing archery, and he said: “Shoot the children of Ishmael, for your father was an archer.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. They did not bring it out, “and he has a valid witness, according to Muslim’s condition as well.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2464 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2465","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah informed us, Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi told me, and the pronunciation for it was narrated by Abu Al-Mawjih, Al-Hussein bin Harith narrated to us, Al-Fadl bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and some people from Aslam went out to shoot, and he said: “Shoot.” “Children of Ishmael, your father was an archer. Shoot, and I will be with Ibn al-Adra’.” Then the people grabbed their bows and said: O Messenger of God, who are you? With him he conquered. He said: “Aim, and I am with you all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2465 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2466","Abu Amr bin Ismail told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told me, Muhammad bin Miskin Al-Yamimi told us, and Ismail bin Israel told us Al-Lu’lui, they said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, Sulaiman bin Bilal told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by people who were fighting and said: “This is good, O God, twice or Shoot three, and I will be with Ibn al-Adra’. Then the people held their hands and said: By God, we will not shoot with him while you are with him, O Messenger of God. He leads us astray. So he said: “Aim, and I am with you all.” And they said: So he said: They shot in general on that day, then they dispersed alike, some of them astraying one another. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2466 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2467","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Abu Salam Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Zaid, he said: I was an archer, like Uqba bin Amir, and he passed by me one day and said: Oh Khaled, let us go out and shoot, so I slowed down for him and he said: O Khaled, come, I will tell you what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, and I will tell you what he said. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God admits three people into Paradise with one arrow, its Maker, the one who thought there would be good in making it.” And his mutabilah, and the archer: Shoot and ride, and if you shoot, that is dearer to me than that you ride, and there are only three forms of amusement: a man training his horse, And his playing with his wife, and his throwing arrows on behalf of his people, and whoever knows how to shoot and then abandons it, it is a blessing that he will deny.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, but he did not narrate it. “And he has a witness to this summary, and it is authentic according to the condition of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2467 - True"
"2468","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Isbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, Ubayy told us, Suwayd bin Abdul Aziz, Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “Everything of the worldly entertainment is invalid except three: fighting with your bow, training your horse, and playing with your family. The truth.” And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Stand back and ride, and if you stand side by side, it will be dearer to me. Indeed, God brings in three people with one arrow.” Paradise, its maker expects goodness in it, and the one who uses it, and the one who throws it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2468 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2469","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan ibn Abi Talha al-Imari, on the authority of Abu Najih al-Sulami, who is Amr ibn He frowned and said: We besieged Taif Palace, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God will have justice freed.” He said: At that time I reached sixteen arrows. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” And it has a witness on the authority of Amr ibn Absa.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2469 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2470","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, men told me Among the people of knowledge are Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Qasim Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amr bin Absa May God be pleased with him. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Whoever shoots an arrow at the enemy and his arrow hits him, is mistaken or is right and is correct.” neck"
"2471","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Al-Ghaseel, on the authority of Al-Abbas Ibn Sahl Ibn Sa’d, on the authority of his father, and on the authority of Hamza Ibn Abi Usayd Al-Sa’idi, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him They said: When we and the people met on the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “If they pin you down, shoot arrows and stay ahead of them.” “Your nobility” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was included by Al-Bukhari.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2471 - Narrated by Al-Bukhari and it is also according to Muslim’s conditions"
"2472","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, Jeddi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Uhud to the Muslims: “Be noble, Saad. Shoot, O Saad, may God shoot for you. Shoot, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2472 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2473","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, Jeddi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Maan bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Abbad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, on the authority of her father Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, that he said: “Has the Messenger of “By God, I protected my companions with the issuance of this Prophet.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2473 - True"
"2474","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, Abdullah told us, Al-Masoudi told us, and he told me Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Masoudi told us, and Abu Sa’id Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Abdul Rahman bin Ubaidullah Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, and he was Badri. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he said hello to sending us on the expedition. We have nothing to add except a handful of dates. We divide them fist by fist until it turns into one date after another. I said: O my father. How can a date be of no use to you? He said: Do not say that, my son, for we no longer lost her and needed her. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2474 - True"
"2475","Abu Amr bin Ismail told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Ali bin Sahl Al-Ramli told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Hanzala told us Bin Abi Sufyan, that he heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad saying: I was with Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, and a man came to him and said: I wanted to travel. Then Abdullah said: Wait until I bid you farewell, just as the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bid us farewell: “I entrust to Allah your religion, your trustworthiness, and your “Your work” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2475 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2476","Abu Bakkar bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Al-Musaddad told us, Abdullah bin Daoud told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ismail bin Jarir, on the authority of Qaza’ah, said: Ibn Omar said to me, “I bid you farewell as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bid me farewell.” He said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your work.” And there is evidence for this on the authority of Anas bin Malik and Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari.
 As for the hadith of Anas"
"2477","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Sayyar bin Hatim told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, I want a journey, so provide me with a journey. He said: “May God increase your piety.” He said: Increase me. He said: “And he forgave your sin.” He said: Give me more, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: “And goodness will be facilitated for you wherever you are.” H
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2477 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 As for the hadith of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari"
"2478","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi told me, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Jafar told us. Al-Khattami, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, who said: Abdullah bin Yazid was invited to a meal, and when he came, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he bid farewell to an army, he said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the end of your deeds.”"
"2479","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayoub, on the authority of Zaban bin Faid, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “To send a mujahideen on the path of God, and accompany him on his journey in the morning or in the afternoon, something dearer to me than the world and all that is in it.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2479 - True"
"2480","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Taymi told me, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Amr bin Zurarah told us, Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God walked with them May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to Baqi’ al-Gharqad when he directed them to them and then said: “Go in the name of God, O God, help them.” Al-Bukhari cited Thawr as evidence. Ibn Yazid and Ikrimah, and Muslim argued with Muhammad ibn Ishaq, “This is a strange and authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2480 - True"
"2481","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanting to travel, and he said: O Messenger of God, Recommend me. He said: “I advise you to fear God and to glorify God with all honour.” Then when he went on, he said: “O God, make the land easy for him and make the journey easy for him.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2481 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2482","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Saeed bin Sulaiman Al-Wasiti told us, Fudayl bin Marzuq told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, that he was the buttocks of Ali, may God be pleased with him, so when he put his foot in The stirrup, he said: In the name of God. When he sat on the back of the animal, he said: Praise be to God three times, and God is the greatest three times. {Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us. And We would not be associated with Him.} [Al-Zukhruf: 13] Verse. Then he said: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins. Indeed, there is no He forgives sins except you. Then he leaned towards one of his two sides and laughed. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, what makes you laugh? He said: I was the buttocks of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did as I did, so I asked him as you asked me, and the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, God admires a servant when he says: There is no god but You. Indeed, I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins. Indeed, He does not He forgives sins except you. He said: My servant knew that he had a Lord who forgives and punishes. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” And he It was narrated in this context by Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah"
"2483","Ali bin Muhammad Al-Hairi told us, Musaddad bin Qatn told us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali Ibn Rabi’ah, he said: I saw Ali, may God be pleased with him, brought with an animal, and he mentioned a hadith similar to it. “And the hadith of Abu Hurairah bears witness to it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2482 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2484","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf bin Abi Ishaq told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Abbas told us, on the authority of Umair bin Abdul By God, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I am holding the snout of a camel, riding on it until the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is leveled. He greeted her and said: “O God, you are the companion on the journey, and the successor to the family. O God, keep us company, and keep us under a duty. O God, grant me the land, and make travel easy for us. O God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel and the gloom of a turning point.” Abu Zar’ah said. Abu Hurairah was an Arab man. If he wanted to say, “He was afflicted with travel, he would have said, ‘O God, turn us around with a burden. O God, increase the land for us.’” And we walked in it"
"2485","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Mahdi bin Maymun, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, the client of Al-Hasan bin Ali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to me one day behind him, and he confided to me a story that I would not narrate to anyone else. He said: The most beloved thing that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to cover himself for his needs was a tree or a stalk of palm trees, so he entered the enclosure of a man from the Ansar. A camel, and when he saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he longed for it, and his eyes became filled with joy. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him, wiped his back, and he calmed down and said: Who has the Lord? Who is this camel for? He said: Then a young man from the Ansar came and said: He is mine, O Messenger of God. Then he said: “Don’t you fear God regarding this animal that God has given you? “He complained to me that you starve him and train him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2485 - True"
"2486","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Saeed bin Suleiman Al-Wasiti told us, and Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl, Omar bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas Al-Juhani, on the authority of Anas, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ride these animals safely.” “And create them in peace, and do not take them as chairs.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2486 - True"
"2487","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Awf bin Sufyan Al-Tai narrated to us, in Homs, Abu Al-Mughirah Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Shuraih bin Ubaid Al-Hadrami, that he heard Al-Zubayr bin Al-Walid, speaking on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. God on their behalf. He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked or traveled and the night overtook him, he would say: “O land, my Lord and your Lord are God. I seek refuge in God from your evil and the evil of what is within you, and the evil of what He created in you, and from the evil of what has crawled upon you. I seek refuge in God from the evil of every lion, lion, and serpent. And a scorpion, and from the evil of the inhabitant of the land, and from the evil of the father and what he generates.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2487 - True"
"2488","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Hafs told me Ibn Maysara, on the authority of Musa Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b told him that Suhayb, may God be pleased with him, was the companion of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, never saw a town that he wanted to enter unless he said when he saw it: “O God, Lord of the seven heavens.” And they did not mislead, and the Lord of the seven earths, and they did not mislead, and the Lord of the devils, and they did not lead astray, and the Lord of the winds and what they created, so indeed we ask of you the best of these. The town, and the best of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of its people, and the evil of what is in it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2488 - True"
"2489","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Abi told us, he said: I heard Yunus, speaking about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best companions Four, and the best companies are four hundred, and the best armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will not be defeated by a few. This is an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of The conditions of the two sheikhs and they did not narrate it due to a disagreement between those who transmitted it on the authority of Al-Zuhri.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2489 - They did not narrate it due to a disagreement among Al-Zuhri’s companions regarding it"
"2490","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Haywa bin Shurayh informed us, Sharhabeel bin Sharik narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “The best of companions in the sight of God is the one who is best to his companion, and the best neighbors in the eyes of God are the best to his neighbor.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2490 - True"
"2491","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Ibn Jurayj, Ja`far ibn Muhammad told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: Some people complained to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he called for walking. And he said: “You must have descendants,” so we descended, and we found it easier for us. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2491 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2492","Abu Amr bin Ismail told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Abdul Salam bin Hashim told us, Uthman told us Ibn Saad Al-Kateb, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would not go down to a place without saying goodbye to it.” “Two rak’ahs.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but it was not narrated by Uthman bin Saad, who is one of those whose hadiths are compiled.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2492 - No, Abdul Salam was lied to by Al-Fallas and Uthman is soft"
"2493","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Asim bin Muhammad bin Zaid told us. Ibn Abdullah Ibn Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: I heard my father saying: Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If people knew what is in loneliness, I do not know. The rider would never travel alone at night.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2493 - True"
"2494","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Muzaki told us, they said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Nufaili told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both. He said: A man left Khaybar, and two men followed him, and a man followed them, saying: Go back until he overtook them and turned them back, then he said: These are two devils, so read to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and inform him that we are collecting our charity, if it is good for him. We would have sent it to him. He said: When he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he told him, “At that time he forbade being alone with us.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2494 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2495","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik told us, he told me Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that a man came from a journey, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He said: “Who did you accompany?” He said: I have never accompanied anyone. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The rider is a devil, and the two riders are two devils, and the three are riders.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Abu Hurairah witnessed it. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2495 - True"
"2496","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “One is a devil. And the two are devils, and the three are knees.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2496 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2497","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade drinking from someone from a waterskin, and from “Riding the Jalala and the Perched” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr witnessed it with an increase in wording.” “in it”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2497 - True"
"2498","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Ahmad bin Ubaid Allah bin Idris told us, Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami told us, Wahib told us, Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Tawoos, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “On the Day of Khaybar, he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, the Jalalalah, riding them, and eating their meat.”"
"2499","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Musa, and Yahya bin Al-Mughirah told us, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: When God Almighty revealed {And do not approach wealth the orphan except with that which is best} [Al-An'am: 152] and {Indeed, those who unjustly devour the property of orphans} [An-Nisa: 10] to his saying, {A burning fire} [An-Nisa: 10] He said: He who had an orphan went and separated his food from his food and his drink from his drink. He separated something from his food and kept it for him until He eats it, or it spoils, and he throws it away. This became difficult for them, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “So God Almighty, the Majestic, revealed {They ask you about the orphans. Say: “A reform is better for them. But if you mix with them, then they are your brothers} [Al-Baqarah: 220] to {Mighty, Wise} [Al-Baqarah: 220] So they mixed together. Their food for their food, and their drink for their drink. “This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.” Rather, our imams narrated it in the license in the pledge. “In the invasion.” And the commentator witnessed it, the hadith of Wahshi bin Harb.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2499 - True"
"2500","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Sulayman bin Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi told us, al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Wahshi bin Harb bin Wahshi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Wahshi bin Harb, may God be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger By God, we eat and we are never satisfied. He said: “Perhaps you may part ways with your food, gather together over it, and mention the name of God, and He will bless you.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2500 - We produced it as a witness"
"2501","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that a man emigrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace peace be upon him from Yemen, and he said: O Messenger of God, I emigrated. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You have emigrated from polytheism, but he Jihad, do you have anyone in Yemen? He said: My parents. He said: “Do we give you permission?” He said: No. He said: “Go back and ask their permission. If they give you permission, then strive. Otherwise, be kind to them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. In this context, “they only agreed on the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr, so he struggled with them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2501 - Daraj Wah"
"2502","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin al-Faraj al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Juraij said: He told me Muhammad bin Talha bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Jahimah, that Jahimah, may God be pleased with him, came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: I wanted to invade, so I came to consult you. He said: “Do you have a mother?” He said: Yes, he said: “Go and stick to her, for Paradise is at her feet.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2502 - True"
"2503","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas Radi May God be pleased with him, that Abu Talha, may God be pleased with him, recited the Qur’an {Go forth, light and heavy} [At-Tawbah: 41] and said: I see that you should mobilize old men and young men. They said: O our father, you fought with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he died, and with Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, so we are fighting. About you, but he refused, so he sailed on the sea until he died. “And they did not find an island to bury him until after seven days.” He said: “And nothing changed.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is on the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2503 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2504","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abd Al-Mu’min bin Khalid Al-Hanafi told us, he told me Najda bin Nufay’ said: I asked Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, about the words of God Almighty: “Unless you go forth” [At-Tawbah: 39] He will punish you with a torment. Painful, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called out one of the Arabs’ neighborhoods, but they became heavy, so the rain stopped from them, and their torment was.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2504 - True"
"2505","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Sharik reported, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dahni, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who transmitted it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that “his banner on the day he entered Mecca was white.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, witnessed it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2505 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2506","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Silahini told us, Yazid bin Hayyan told us, Abu Majliz Lahiq bin Humaid told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: He was “the banner of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He was white, and his vision was black.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2506 - Yazid is weak"
"2507","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abu Sakhr, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah al-Bajli, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he narrated to him, saying: While I was in Al-Hajr was sitting. A man came to me and asked me about {Al-Adiyat, slaughtering} [Al-Adiyat: 1]. So I said to him: “Horses are when they gallop in the path of God, then they go to the night, so they prepare their food and kindle their fire.” Then he turned away from me and went to Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, while he was under He was watering Zamzam, so he asked him about the ordinary things. He said: Have you asked anyone about them before me? He said: Yes, I asked Ibn Abbas about it and he said: It is the horses when they gallop in the path of God. He said: Go and call him for me. He said: When he stood at his head, he said: You issue fatwas to people without your knowledge. By God, this was the first expedition in Islam. Badr, and we had only two horsemen with us, a horse of al-Zubayr, and a horse of al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, so how could ordinary women be slaughtered? “The ordinary women were only a slaughterhouse” [Al-Adiyat: 1] from Arafat to Muzdalifah, and from Muzdalifah to Mina, {so they soaked therein} [Al-Adiyat: 4] when You trample it with its hoofs and hooves.” Ibn Abbas said: So I renounced my statement and returned to what Ali said: “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not report it. They cited as evidence Abu Sakhr, who is Humayd bin Ziyad al-Kharrat al-Masri, and Abu Muawiyah al-Bajli, who was the father of Ammar bin Abi Muawiyah Al-Dahni Al-Kufi """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2507 - No, by God, there is no mention of Abu Muawiyah in the six books, nor did Al-Bukhari use Abu Sakhr as evidence, and the report is objectionable."
"2508","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Zaydan told us, Abu Saeed Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Kindi told us, he told me Uqba ibn al-Mughirah Abu al-Ala al-Shaybani, Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhaariq ibn Sulaym, he said: I was walking with Ammar on the day of the camel, and he had a hardened horn, on his saddle, in which he was urinating. When the time of battle came, he urinated. Your people, so I said: I am not a invader, and I am in this state today. He said: Nay, O Mukhariq, come to the banner of your people, for I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. “It is desirable for a man to fight under the banner of his people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2508 - True"
"2509","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jabir told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Artat, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Seek me among the weak, for it is only for you that you will be provided for. And you will be supported by your weak.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it in this context. “They narrated the hadith of Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him.” May God bless him because he thought he had superiority over those below him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2509 - True"
"2510","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Al-Qasim bin Zakaria Al-Muttarriz narrated to us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Naqid narrated to us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz bin Imran, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habiba told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the motto of the immigrants on the day of Badr: ‘Abd al-Rahman and al-Aws, Banu Abdullah and al-Khazraj. Bani Ubayd Allah: “This is a strange hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” Rather, they narrated in Al-Sha’ar the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kathir ibn Al-Abbas, on the authority of His father, when it was the day of Hunayn, people were defeated by the length of the hadith in which it mentions the slogans of the tribes.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2510 - Rather, Jacob and Abraham are weak"
"2511","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ismail bin Abdullah bin Zurarah Al-Raqi told us, Omar told us Ibn Salih Ibn Abi Al-Zahiriyah Al-Raqqi said: I heard Abu Jamrah saying: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: A delegation to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace be upon him, four hundred Ahl al-Bayt, or four hundred men from Azd, and he said: “Welcome to Azd, the most beautiful of people. “And I will give him the kindest mouths, and I will be the most courageous in meeting with him, and I will be as safe as you are.” Your slogan, “O Mabrur.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2511 - Rather, Ismail denies the hadith"
"2512","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Al-Abbas told us Al-Mahboubi, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, and Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr Al-Maruzi told us They said: Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufra, he said: He told me Whoever heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If you stay, let your motto be: ‘They will not be helped.’” And this is how it was narrated by Zuhayr bin Muawiyah on the authority of Abu Isaac
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2512 - Followed by Zuhair bin Muawiyah according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2513","Muhammad bin Saleh told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ali bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Omar Al-Harashi told us, they said: Ahmad bin Yunus, Zuhair narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufra, he said: I heard someone, narrating on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: And he said: He was afraid that Abu Sufyan would spend the night, so he said: “If you stay overnight, then if I call you to Islam, they will not be helped.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. However, there is a message in it, so behold, the man whom Al-Muhallab did not name was Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufra, Al-Baraa bin Aazib.”"
"2514","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, Ali bin Hakim told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq said: I heard Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufra, mentioning, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “You will meet your enemy tomorrow, so let your motto be: ‘They will not be helped.’” It was said: On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, Ahmad ibn Muhammad Al-Anazi, Othman bin Saeed told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “You will meet your enemy tomorrow,” like him."
"2515","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “You will meet tomorrow, so let your motto be: ‘They will not be helped.’”"
"2516","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Halim al-Marwazi informed me, Abu al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: I fought with Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. At the time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, our motto, meaning the Companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was: “Death, death.” This was true according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but it was not They bring it out “and he has a valid witness according to the condition of a Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2516 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2517","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih narrated to us in Bukhara, Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, in Bukhara, Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, Sharik, on the authority of Utbah bin Abdullah Abi Al-Umays, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: It was the motto of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “She died, she died.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2517 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2518","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told me, Uthman bin Sa`id al-Darimi told me, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man From Muzainah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man calling out in his slogan: O forbidden, oh forbidden. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O permissible, oh permissible.” It is true according to the two sheikhs’ condition regarding the transmission. “And behold, the man whom he did not name, Muhammad ibn “A lot, on the authority of Al-Thawri Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani.”"
"2519","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told me, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ja’far Al-Qurashi told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith Al-Qurashi told us, Abu Amer told us Al-Asadi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the same.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2518 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2520","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Hisham bin Yunus Al-Qassar told us, in Egypt, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid bin Musafir narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Malik bin Aws bin al-Hadathan used to narrate that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, went out in a meeting while he was in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they were mentioning a company from the companies. They perished in the cause of God, and someone among them says: They are workers of God who perished in His cause, and they are due their reward for it. Someone says: God knows best about them. They will have what they expected. When they saw Omar approaching, leaning on his staff, they remained silent, and Omar approached and greeted them. He said: What were you talking about? They said: We were mentioning this group that perished in the path of God. Someone among us says: They are workers of God who perished in His path, and it was obligatory for them. Their reward is based on it, and someone says: God knows best about them. They will have what they expected. Omar said: “God knows best that among the people there are some who fight, even if their concern is Fighting, but they are not able to do it, and among the people are people who fight out of hypocrisy and reputation, and among the people are people who fight seeking the face of God, so those Martyrs, and every one of them is resurrected for the one he died for, and by God, no soul knows what will be done to it. This is not the man who has made clear For us, his previous sins and future sins have been forgiven, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. “In this regard, they only agreed on the hadith of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him: Whoever fights so that the word of God is supreme is in the path of God.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2520 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2521","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Abu al-Muthanna informed us, Musaddad informed us, and Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, saying: Ismail, who is Ibn Ulayya, narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, Hisham, and Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Al-Ajfa Al-Sulami, said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saying: And another thing you say to those who were killed in your battles. Or he died: so-and-so was killed and he was a martyr, or so-and-so died as a martyr, and perhaps he lost the most valuable of his animal or his mount in gold or paper. He seeks trade, so do not say that, but say as the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed in the way of God or dies will be in Paradise.” This is a major and authentic hadith, and not one of them narrated it, due to the words of Salamah bin Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said: I was informed on the authority of my father. “And I remember, by the will of God, in the Book of Marriage that there is evidence of its validity.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2521 - True"
"2522","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad told us Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Jablah Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Yahya Ibn al-Walid Ibn Ubadah, on the authority of his grandfather Ubadah Ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Whoever fights while not intending to do so except with a head, will get what he intended.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And this is witnessed by the hadith of Ali bin Umayyah, who”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2522 - True"
"2523","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anazi informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi’ ibn Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Bashir ibn Talha, on the authority of Khaled bin Duraik, on the authority of Ali bin Umayyah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to send me to his brigades, so he sent me on the same day. One day, a man was riding, so I told him to leave, and he said: I am not going out with you. I said: Why? He said: Until you give me three dinars. I said: Now when I said goodbye to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? I will not return to him. Go, but you have three dinars. When I returned from my raids, I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Give it to him, for it is his portion of his conquests.”"
"2524","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Yunus bin Yusuf, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yassar, said: The people dispersed from Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, and the brother of the people of the Levant said to him: O Sheikh. Tell us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The first person to be judged on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who was martyred, and he was brought and identified.” He recognized his blessings. He said: What did you do about it? He said: I fought for you until I was killed. He said: You lied, but you fought so that it might be said that he was bold. It was said: Then he was ordered to be dragged on his face, until He was thrown into the Fire, and a man learned knowledge, taught it, and read the Qur’an, and he was brought to him and he made known to him the blessings he had bestowed upon him, and he recognized it, and said: What did you do in it? He said: I learned knowledge from you, I taught it, and I read the Qur’an from you. So he says: You lied, but you learned knowledge so that it is said that he is a scholar, and you read the Qur’an so that it is said that he is a reader. It was said, then he was ordered to do so and it was withdrawn. His face until he was thrown into the Fire, and a man, God made generous blessings upon him and gave him various kinds of wealth, and he was brought to him and he made known to him his blessings, and he recognized them and said: What you have done. In it? He said: I have never known of a thing on which you would like to spend money without spending on it. He said: You lied, but you did so, so that it could be said, “He is Jawad.” It was said, then he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire. “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not narrated by Al-Bukhari.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2524 - Al-Bukhari did not narrate it and he is in accordance with their conditions"
"2525","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Mahbub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa'ib, he said: I heard Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah, saying: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: Beware of these testimonies. You say that so-and-so was killed as a martyr, for the man fights for his sake, and fights for the sake of this world, and fights while he is bold-hearted, but I will tell you what You bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a detachment one day. It did not remain but a short time before he got up and praised and praised him, then he said: “Indeed, your brothers met the polytheists, and cut them off, and not a single one of them remained, and they said: Our Lord, inform our people that we are satisfied. And our Lord is pleased with us, so I am their messenger to you. Indeed, they were satisfied and he was satisfied with them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. If it is safe from the transmission, then it is “Our sheikhs disagreed about whether Abu Ubaidah heard from his father.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2525 - True"
"2526","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Qais, On the authority of Hudhayl bin Shurahbil, he said: People went out and were killed, and they said: So-and-so was martyred. Then Abdullah said: “A man fights for the sake of this world, and he fights to be known, and a man fights to die on his bed, and he is a martyr.” Then he recited {And those who believe By God and His Messengers, those are the truthful ones and the witnesses before their Lord.} [Al-Hadid: 19]"
"2527","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani informed me, Jeddi told me, Nu`aym ibn Hammad told me, Ibn al-Mubarak told me, Muammar told me, about Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man said: O Messenger of God, I am taking a stand and I want to The face of God, and I want him to see my homeland. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond to him anything until the revelation {So whoever hopes to meet his Lord, So let him do righteous deeds, and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord.} [Al-Kahf: 110] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2527 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2528","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Jumahi Al-Makki told us, Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The first people On the Day of Resurrection, three people will enter Hell, and a man will be brought, or he said: one of them, and he will say: My Lord, you taught me the Book, so I read it during the night. And by day he hopes for your reward, and it will be said: You lied, but you were praying. It will be said: A reader is praying, and it has been said: Take him to the Fire. Then another will be brought. He will say, “My Lord, You have provided me with wealth, and with it I have connected myself with my relatives, and I have given it in charity to the poor, and I have given the wayfarer the hope of Your reward and Your Paradise,” and it will be said: You lied. You were only giving alms and praying so that it would be said that you are forgiving and generous. And it was said: Take him to Hell. Then a third would be brought and he would say: My Lord. I went out in your cause and fought for you until I was killed, approaching, not retreating, hoping for your reward and your Paradise. It will be said: You lied. You were only fighting so that it would be said that you Daring and brave, and it was said, “Take him to Hell.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2528 - True"
"2529","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Al-Waddah, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Hanan bin Kharijah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that He said: O Messenger of God, tell me about jihad and conquest. He said: O Abdullah bin Amr, if you fight patiently and seeking hope, God will send you Be patient and seek reward, and if you fight a hypocrite who is a frequent hypocrite, God will send you to be a hypocrite who is a frequent hypocrite. O Abdullah bin Amr, in any case you fought, or your mission was killed. “God is in that state.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"2530","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Yaqoub ibn Ahmad ibn Mihran al-Thaqafi al-Zahid told me, Ali ibn al-Hussein ibn al-Junaid al-Maliki told me about Al-Ray, Ahmed bin Saleh in Egypt, Abdullah bin Wahb Al-Qurashi told me, Asim bin Hakim told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Sibani, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Daylami, that Ya’la bin Umayyah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for the invasion, and I I am an old man and I do not have a servant, so I am looking for a worker who is sufficient for me, and I will pay him his share. I found a man, and when we were about to leave, he came to me and said: I do not know what The two arrows, and whatever the size of my arrow is, he named something for me, whether it was the arrow or not, so I named three dinars for it, and when I brought spoils, I wanted to run. He has his shares, so I mentioned the dinars, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned his matter to him, and he said: What do I find for him in this foray into this world? Except for his dinars, which he called “This is an authentic hadith according to their condition, but they did not take it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2530 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2531","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Our Lord is amazed.” Mighty and Majestic is the man who fought in the cause of God, and his companions were defeated, and he knew what he had done, and returned until his blood was shed, and God, Blessed and Most High, says: To His angels: Look at my servant. He has returned, desiring what is with me, and out of pity for what is with me, until his blood is shed. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not “He narrates it” and there is evidence with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2531 - True"
"2532","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Dizel told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i. Ibn Harash, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Dhabyan, who attributed it to Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There are three whom God loves And there are three whom God hates: As for those whom God loves, a man came to a people and asked them about God, but he did not ask them because they were related to him, so a man left behind after them. So he gave him a secret that no one knows about his gift except God and the one who gave him. And some people walked during the night until, when sleep became more beloved to them, they came down. So they lowered their heads, and a man who was in a company stood up and flattered me and recited my verses. He met the enemy and was defeated, so he attacked him until he was killed or killed. It will be opened to him, and the three whom God hates are the adulterous old man, the deceitful poor man, and the unjust rich man.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2532 - True"
"2533","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told me, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Muhammad bin Amr informed us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that Amr ibn Uqish had a lord in pre-Islamic times who wanted him to surrender until he took him. Then he came on the day of Uhud and said: Where are my paternal aunt’s sons? They said: By Uhud. He said: Where is so-and-so? They said: By Uhud. He said: Where is so-and-so? They said: By Uhud, so he dressed like his female slave, and rode his horse, then headed ahead of them. When the Muslims saw him, they said: Stay away from us, O Amr. He said: I am I believed, so he fought until he was wounded, then he was carried to his family wounded, then Saad bin Muadh came to him and said to his sister: Ask him to protect your people, or to anger them. Or out of the wrath of God and His Messenger? He said: “Rather, out of the wrath of God and His Messenger, so he died and entered Paradise, and he had not prayed a single prayer for God.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2533 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2534","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzaz told me, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Two times will not be rejected, or he said: They will rarely be rejected, the supplication at The call, or at the time of battle when they are fighting each other.” Musa bin Yaqoub said, and Rizq bin Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Madani told me on the authority of Abi Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And under the rain.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2534 - True"
"2535","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl al-Balkhi told us, Khalid bin Yazid al-Amri told us, Abu Ja`far al-Razi told us, On the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must use the ice, for the earth is rolling. “At night.” I had dictated in the Book of Rites from this book the hadith of Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri, on the authority of al-Layth, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, and I tried at that time to find a witness for him, but I did not find, “And this is his witness, if he is safe from Khalid bin Yazid Al-Umari.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2535 - If he delivers from Khalid, then it is good"
"2536","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Husayn bin Numayr told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever inserts a horse between two horses, and does not He who is sure that he will outrun him is not gambling, and whoever puts a horse between two horses and is sure that he will outrun him, then he is gambling.” Saeed bin Bashir Al-Dimashqi continued, On the authority of Al-Zuhri and established its chain of transmission."
"2537","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Razi, Mahmoud bin Khalid Al-Dimashqi, Al-Walid bin Muslim, us. Saeed bin Bashir, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and something similar. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” Even if the two sheikhs did not narrate the hadith of Saeed bin Bashir and Sufyan bin Hussein, they are imams in the Levant. And Iraq, and from those whose hadiths are collected, and what I have is that they relied on the hadith of Muammar on the transmission, for he sent it on the authority of al-Zuhri.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2536 - Followed by Saeed bin Bashir on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Sahih"
"2538","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj: “{O you who have believed, obey God and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [An-Nisa: 59] Abdullah bin Qais bin Adi was sent by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, in secret, Ali bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2538 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2539","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna al-Anbari told me, Yahya ibn Mu’in told me, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd told me. The heir, Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, Humaid bin Hilal told us, Bishr bin Asim told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I armed a man of them with a sword. When we returned to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, blamed us. He said: “Are you unable to appoint someone who will follow my command when I send a man and he does not follow my command?” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2539 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2540","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, Amr bin Othman Al-Homsi told me, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Alaa bin Zubr, that he heard Muslim bin Mishkam, Abu Abdullah, say: Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, may God be pleased with him, told us On his authority, he said: When the people camped, they would disperse through the paths and valleys, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your dispersal in... These reefs and valleys are from Satan. They did not descend after that, but they joined one another until it is said: If a garment had been spread over them, it would have been covered by them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2540 - True"
"2541","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Ismail told us, he is the son of Aliyah, Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, that Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, narrated to them, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “He lags behind on the march, and he pushes the weak, and he goes back and supplicates for them.” It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2541 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2542","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Adl told me about Marw, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us, Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Habib told us, Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Furat ibn Hayyan, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered By killing him, he was Abu Sufyan’s official, so he passed by the Ansar council and said: I am a Muslim, so they took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: He claims to be a Muslim, so he said: “Indeed, among you are men whom We call to their faith, among them is Furat ibn Hayyan.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2542 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2543","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Makki told us, and Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad Al-Ghassani told us, they said: We told us: Muslim bin Ibrahim, Hisham al-Dastawwi told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Ubadah, may God be pleased with him, who said: They were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: “They hate sound when fighting.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2543 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2544","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Al-Hasan bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Hammam, Matar narrated to me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He hated sound when fighting.” This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And the hadith of Hisham Al-Dastawai witnessed it while he was More deserving of the preserved
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2544 - This is more correct"
"2545","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met the polytheists on the day of Hunayn, he “dismounted from his mule and alighted.” It is true according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but it was not They narrate it: “It is not authentic that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, dismounted and fought on foot except from this narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2545 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2546","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad told us, Abu Imran Al-Juniy told us, about Alqamah bin Abdullah Al-Muzani said that Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin, may God be pleased with him, said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he did not fight “From the beginning of the day, he delayed the fighting until the sun had set and the winds had blown.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2546 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2547","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl informed us, saying: Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Baghawi informed us, narrating Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that Abu Talha, may God be pleased with him, used to throw stones on the day of Uhud was in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was behind him. Abu Talha was an archer, and whenever he shot, he would raise the Prophet up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he looked at him to see where his arrow would fall, and Abu Talha was raising his chest and saying: This is how you sacrifice my father, O Messenger of God. A marine arrow will not hit you without you moving. Abu Talha used to feel himself in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would say: O Messenger of God, “I am flogging my people, so command me to do whatever you want.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2547 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2548","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Nufayl told me Al-Harrani, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Harrani told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Abi Aoun told me, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awf, may God be pleased with him, said: Umayyah bin Khalaf said to me while I was between him and his son Ali, taking their hands: O servant of God, which man among you is a teacher with an ostrich feather in his chest? He said: I said: That is Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib. He said: He is the one who did the evil deeds for us. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” Imam Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah included it in the chapter on the concession in the swordsman’s mark himself so that its location would be known.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2548 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2549","He narrated it on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Nufaili, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh narrated to me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi narrated to me, Affan bin Muslim, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Al-Harith bin Hasira told us, Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn when the people departed from him, and I remained with him with eighty men from The Muhajireen and Ansar, so we were on our feet about eighty feet, and we did not turn our backs on them, and they are the ones to whom God sent down tranquility. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on his mule, moving forward, but his mule strayed, so he leaned from the saddle and blocked his throat. I said: He raised you up. God said: “Hand me a handful of dust.” So I handed it to him and he struck their faces with it, and their eyes were filled with dust. He said: “Where are the immigrants and the Ansar?” I said: They are here. He said: “Shout them out.” So they came with their swords in their right hands as if they were meteors, and the polytheists turned their backs. This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2549 - Al-Harith and Abdullah committed evil deeds. This is one of them, then there is a message in it."
"2550","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Ruqi told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says, ‘I ask forgiveness from God, who has no god Except He is the Living, the Ever-Subsisting, and I repent to Him. Three times, His sins are forgiven, even if he is fleeing from the onslaught.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2550 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2551","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, he said: I read from Ibn Al-Yaman that Hariz bin Othman told him about Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, he said: Abu Rashid al-Habrani told me, he said: I met al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, may God be pleased with him, Faris Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sitting on a coffin of the money changers’ coffins, and he separated a bone from them while he wanted to invade, so I said: God has excused me. To you. So he said: “Come to Surah Al-Buhuth. God Almighty said, ‘Go forth, light and heavy.’” [At-Tawbah: 41] meaning Surat Al-Tawbah. “This is an authentic chain of narration, but it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2551 - True"
"2552","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yazid bin Al-Hubab told us, Abd Al-Mu’min bin Khalid told us. Al-Hanafi, narrated by Najda bin Nufay’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “mobilized a group of Arabs alive. So they burdened themselves, and then the verse was revealed: “Unless you disperse, He will punish you with a painful punishment.” [At-Tawbah: 39] He said: “Their punishment was withholding the rain from them.” This is an authentic hadith. “The chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it.” And Abd al-Mu’min ibn Khalid al-Hanafi is one of the trustworthy narrators of al-Marawazah.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2552 - True"
"2553","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Mahboub bin Musa Al-Antaki told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari informed us, On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah informed me, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He was on some of his battles. He passed by people from Muzainah, and a slave of one of their women followed him. When he was on some road, he greeted him and said: “So-and-so?” He said: Yes. He said: “What’s the matter with you?” He said: I will fight with you. He said: “Does your lady give you permission?” He said: No. He said: “Go back to her and tell her, for your example is like a servant who does not pray, if you die before you return to her and recite peace be upon her.” So he returned. He told her the news, and she said: Did God command that you read peace be upon me? He said: Yes. She said: Go back and fight with him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2553 - True"
"2554","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Yazid bin Mawhib Al-Ramli told us, Al-Mufaddal bin Fadala told us, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas Al-Qatbani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Every sin is forgiven for the martyr except debt.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the hadith of Sahl bin “Hanif”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2554 - True"
"2555","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abdul Rahman told me Ibn Saad Al-Mazni, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Abi Umamah Ibn Sahl Ibn Hunaif, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The first thing that is shed of the martyr’s blood will be forgiven his sins.”"
"2556","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Zubaidi told us, that Othman bin Saeed bin Katheer bin A dinar. He told them, saying: Abu Muti’ Muawiyah bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Nasr bin Alqamah, on the authority of his brother Mahfouz bin Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever meets someone and is patient until he is killed or defeated will not be tried in His grave” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2556 - Muawiyah is weak"
"2557","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Mahbub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Abi Hammad Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ibn Aqeel, said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lost Hamza. When the people returned from the fighting, a man said: I saw him by those trees, and he was saying: I am the lion of God and the lion of His Messenger. Oh God, I disavow before you what These people brought it, Abu Sufyan and his companions, and I apologize to you for what these people did when they were defeated. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, leaned towards him, and when he saw his side, he wept, and when he saw what was mutilated by it, he gasped, then he said: Shall there be no shroud? Then a man rose from Al-Ansar threw a garment at him, then another man stood up and threw a garment at him and said: “O Jabir, this garment belongs to your father and this belongs to my uncle Hamza. Then Hamza was brought, and the prayer was prayed over him. Then the martyrs were brought, and they were placed next to Hamza, and he prayed. Then they were raised, and Hamza was left until he prayed over him. All the martyrs. He said: I returned and I was burdened. My father had left me a debt and family. When it was nightfall, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent for me. He greeted him and said: “O Jabir, God, Blessed and Most High, brought your father to life and spoke to him.” I said: “And spoke to him?” He said: “He said to him: I wish.” He said: I hope that you will restore my soul, create my creation as it was, and return me to your Prophet, so that I may fight in the way of God and be killed. Once again, he said: “I have decreed that they will not return.” He said: And he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The master of martyrs in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection will be Hamza.” The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2557 - Abu Hammad is al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah. Al-Nasa’i said it is abandoned."
"2558","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Usama bin Zaid, Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: Hamza was shrouded in a sheet, and when they stretched it over his head, it came out. his feet, and when they stretched them over his legs, his head would come out, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to stretch them over his head, and to place them on His feet were made of Idhkhir, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If Safiya had not been alarmed, we would have left Hamza and not buried him until “Hamza will be gathered from the bellies of birds and wild beasts.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2558 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2559","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khaled Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid Allah told us Bin Musa, Talha bin Khair Al Ansari told us, on the authority of Abdul Muttalib bin Abdullah, on the authority of Musab bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Awf, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, conquered Mecca, then he departed to Taif and besieged them by eight or seven. Then he departed in the morning or evening, then he descended, then left, then said: “O people, I am gracious to you, and I give you my best wishes for your appointment.” Basin, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, that you may establish prayer and pay zakat, or I will certainly send upon you a man of my own accord, or of my own accord, so that they may strike off the necks of fight them, and take their descendants captive.” He said: Then the people saw that he meant Abu Bakr or Omar, so he took Ali’s hand and said: “This is this.” Hadith The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2559 - Talha is not a mayor"
"2560","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Qudama told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Muadh ibn Abi Talha al-Imari, on the authority of Abu Najih al-Sulami, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: We besieged Taif Palace, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God will have justice freed, and whoever “If he reaches an arrow in the path of God, he will have a rank in Paradise.” So on one day he received sixteen arrows. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. Abu Najih, this is Amr bin Abasa Al-Sulami.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2560 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2561","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Qabbani told us, Al-Mundhir bin Al-Walid Al-Jaudiy told us, Abd told us Al-A'la bin Abdul-A'la, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari told us, Abu Al-Zubair told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, He said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Taif during the Battle of Hunayn, and when he reached al-Ji’ranah, he divided money among the people.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2561 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2562","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman told us. Al-Ansari, Abdullah bin Iyadh bin Al-Harith Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “came to Hawazin in... Twelve thousand people of Taif were killed on the day of Hunayn, like someone who was killed on the day of Badr. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a handful of pebbles. “So he threw it in our faces and we were defeated.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2562 - True"
"2563","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madani told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Muslim bin Saeed Al-Thaqafi told us, about Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on some of his raids. So I and a man came to him before we converted to Islam, and we said: We are ashamed for our people to witness a spectacle. He said: “Have you both converted to Islam?” We said: No. He said: “For we do not seek help from the polytheists against the polytheists.” So we embraced Islam and testified with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was killed. A man, and the man struck me, so I married his daughter, and she used to say: No, I executed a man, and he removed this scarf, and I said: No, I executed a man. Your father hastened to the Fire. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” And Khubayb bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad bin Haritha was his grandfather. A well-known companion “and he has a witness on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2563 - Khubayb bin Aswad bin Haritha was found to be a companion"
"2564","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi, Yusuf bin Issa Al-Marwazi, Al-Fadl bin Musa Al-Sinani, told me on the authority of Muhammad Bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of Saad bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Abu Humaid Al-Sa’idi, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out When he left Thaniyat al-Wada’, he saw a group. He said: “Who are these?” They said: Banu Qaynuqa, and he is the family of Abdullah bin Salam. He said: “And they embraced Islam?” They said: No, rather they are following their religion. He said: “Tell them to return, for we do not seek help from the polytheists.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2564 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2565","Ali bin Hamshadh al-Adl, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi, Ismail bin Abi Uwais, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad, told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Al-Murqa’ bin Saifi bin Rabah, brother of Handala the writer, that his grandfather Rabah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded There was a raid at the beginning of it, in which Khalid ibn al-Walid fought. Rabah and his companions passed by a killed woman, which befell the beginning, so they stopped. They were amazed at her creation, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, caught up with them and they delighted him, until he looked at her and said: “Behold, what it was like.” “This one is fighting.” Then he looked into the people’s faces and said to one of them: “Go with Khaled bin Al-Walid, and he will not kill his offspring or a violent man” and so on. It was narrated by Al-Mughirah bin Abdul-Rahman and Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, “The hadith became authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2565 - Narrated by Ibn Jurayj and others on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2566","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, Aban bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Saree’, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a company on the day of Khaybar and they fought The polytheists, so killing led them to the offspring. When they came, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What made you kill the offspring?” They said: O Messenger of God, they were only the children of the polytheists. He said: “Are your choice other than the children of the polytheists?” By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no soul is born except according to nature, until it is expressed by its tongue.”"
"2567","It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mal bin Al-Hussein, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Yunus told us Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Al-Aswad Ibn Sari’, may God be pleased with him, narrated to us, he said: We were on a campaign of ours, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2566 - Yunus followed it on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Aswad narrated this on the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"2568","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah informed us, And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed me, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein, on the authority of Adam ibn Abi Iyas, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Atiya al-Qurazi, may God be pleased with him, said: I was presented to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Qurayza, and they doubted me. “So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered May God bless him and grant him peace. They should look at me. Did I grow? So they looked at me and did not find me showing up, so he abandoned me and took me into captivity.” A hadith narrated by a group of Muslim imams on the authority of Abdul-Malik. Ibn Umair and they did not narrate it “as if they did not think about following Mujahid Ibn Jubayr Abd al-Malik on his narration on the authority of Atiya al-Qurazi.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2568 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2569","As Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Malik told us, Ibn Wahb told me, he told me Ibn Jurayj, and Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Atiyya, a man from Banu Qurayza who told him that the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “They stripped him on the day of Qurayzah, but they did not see the razor. It ran over his hair, meaning his pubic hair, so they spared him from being killed.” So the hadith began with a continuation. Mujahid “Sahih according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2569 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2570","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Asadi, the Hafiz in Hamdan, told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad told us. Al-Farawi and Ismail bin Abi Uwais said: Muhammad bin Saleh Al-Tamar told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, On the authority of his father, that Saad bin Muadh, may God be pleased with him, ruled that the Banu Qurayzah should kill everyone who was touched by the razor, and that the Their wealth and their descendants, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Today they have been judged according to the judgment of God, which He has judged.” From above the heavens”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2570 - True"
"2571","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ataba, on the authority of Muslim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Khubayb, on the authority of Jundub Ibn Makith, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abdullah Ibn Ghalib Al-Laythi was in a company, and I was among them, and he ordered them to launch a raid against the Banu al-Mulawh in Al-Kaddid, so we left until we were in Al-Kaddid. We met Al-Harith bin Al-Barsa Al-Laythi, and we took him. He said: I only came wanting to become a Muslim, and I only went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we said: “If you are a Muslim, our bond will not harm you day or night, but if you are other than that, we will trust you, so We have strengthened it tightly.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2571 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2572","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Hilal bin Al-Alaa Al-Ruqi told us, Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr told us, On the authority of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Dahhak ibn Qais wanted to use a stolen property, so Amara ibn Uqba: Do you employ a man from the remains of Uthman’s killers? Masruq said to him: Abdullah bin Masoud told us, and it was within us that the hadith was reliable, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he wanted He killed his father. He said: “Who is the girl’s?” He said: “The Fire has approved for you what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has approved for you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2572 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2573","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, they said: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak Al-Aishi told us, Sufyan bin Habib, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “made The ransom for the people of pre-Islamic times on the day of Badr was four hundred.” This is an authentic hadith according to their conditions, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2573 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2574","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, from the origin of his book, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Shu`bah reported, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded me I wanted to sell two brothers from the captivity, so I sold them, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him of their sale, and he said: “I dispersed.” Between them? I said: Yes. He said: “Then return them, then sell them and do not separate them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. “And it has a chain of transmission.” Another on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba is also authentic according to their conditions.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2574 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2575","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qatan told me, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told me, Ishaq bin Mansour told me, Abd al-Salam bin Harb told me, on the authority of Yazid. Bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Maymoon bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that he “separated a female slave from her child, so he forbade him.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded to that and returned the sale.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2575 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2576","Abu Abdullah Ahmad bin Qani’, the judge of the Two Holy Mosques in Baghdad, informed me. Abu Shuaib Abdullah bin Al-Hassan Al-Harrani told me, Abd told us. Al-Aziz bin Yahya Al-Khawlani, Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Harrani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu'tamir, on the authority of Rab'i bin Harash, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: Abadan went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of Hudaybiyyah, before the peace treaty, their followers wrote to him, saying: O Muhammad, by God, they did not go out to you out of desire for your religion. Rather, they went out To escape slavery. Some people said: They spoke the truth, O Messenger of God. Give them back. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry and said: “I do not see you stopping, O people of Quraysh, until God sends against you someone who will strike your necks.” “For this.” He refused to turn them back, so he said: “They are freed by God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2576 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2577","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghifari informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Bashir ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No people break the covenant. Never, unless murder occurred among them, and immorality never appeared among a people, unless God imposed death upon them, and no people withheld zakat, except withholding it. “May God protect them from it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2577 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2578","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Abu Ishaq told us Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: Did you use a fifth of the food in The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “We received food on the Day of Khaybar, and a man would come and take from it as much as was sufficient for him, then leave.” This is an authentic hadith according to Al-Bukhari’s condition: “He used Muhammad and Abdullah, the two sons of Abu al-Mujalid, as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2578 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2579","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Al-Sana’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Ibrahim bin Abbad Al-Sana’ani told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh informed us in Nishapur, and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Qutay’i informed us in Baghdad, saying: Abd told us Allah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The scent of Paradise can be felt from a distance of a hundred years, and no servant who kills a soul by treaty will be forbidden.” “May God grant him Paradise, and its fragrance will be the one he finds.” Abu Bakra said: “May God deaf my ears, if I did not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He says: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.” And it has a witness on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr with an authentic chain of transmission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2579 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2580","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hussein bin Uwais Al-Ansari told us, Ali bin Muslim Al-Tusi told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari, Al-Hussein bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi told us, Mujahid told us, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever kills a dead person from among the people of the Dhimma will not smell the scent of Paradise, but its scent There will be such-and-such.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And it has a witness from the hadith of Abu Hurairah.” It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2580 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2581","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami told us, Maadi bin Suleiman told us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Except whoever kills a covenanter, he has a duty. God, and the protection of His Messenger, for he has fallen under the protection of God, and does not smell the scent of Paradise, and indeed its scent is felt from the distance of seventy autumns.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2581 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2582","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, and Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Amra, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, That a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died on the day of Hunayn. They mentioned it to the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Pray for your companion.” The faces of the people changed at that, and he said: “Indeed, your companion has committed militancy in the cause of God.” We searched his belongings and found some Jewish beads, not worth the price. Two dirhams “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and I think they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2582 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, and I think they did not narrate it"
"2583","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anazi informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Mahbub ibn Musa informed us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari informed us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Shudhab, Amer bin Abdul Wahid narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, captured spoils, he would order Bilal to call out to the people, and they would bring their spoils, and he would give them a fifth of them. And he divided it, and after that a man came with a rein of hair and said: O Messenger of God, this is among the spoils we had captured. He said: “Did I hear Bilal calling three people?” He said: Yes. He said: “What prevented you from bringing him?” He said: O Messenger of God, so he apologized. He said: “You bring it on the Day of Resurrection, for I will not accept it on your behalf.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2583 - True"
"2584","Ali bin Issa told us, Ahmad bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Saleh bin Muhammad bin told me. Zaida, he said: Maslama entered the land of the Byzantines and brought a man who had become a slave. He asked Salim about him and said: I heard my father speaking on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab. May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If you find a man who has committed adultery, burn his belongings and beat him.” He said: We found in He had a copy of the Qur’an among his possessions, and Salem was asked about it and he said: “Sell it and give its price in charity.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2584 - True
 The book of the Fay’ section
 The origin is from the Book of God Almighty"
"2585","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Qais bin Muhammad said: I asked Al-Hasan bin Muhammad about the saying of God, Blessed and Most High: {And know that whatever thing you gain, a fifth of it is due to God. And to the Messenger} [Al-Anfal: 41] the verse. He said: “This is the key to the words of God Almighty, what is in this world and the hereafter.” He said: “The people disagreed about these two arrows after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Some said: A kinship share is due to the kinship of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Others said: A kinship is due to the caliph’s kinship, and others said: A share. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the Caliph after him, so their minds were unanimously agreed to place these two arrows in horses and equipment for the sake of God. They were like that during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them.”"
"2586","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Qazwini told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Sabiq told us, Abu Jafar Al-Razi told us, On the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, he said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: “And because I am the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, five The five, and its places were the lives of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and Omar, may God be pleased with them. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2586 - True"
"2587","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, and Abu Nu’aym said: We told us: Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “She was Safiyya from the Safiyyah.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2587 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2588","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Abi told me Al-Zinad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, departed. upon him and grant him peace. His sword, Dhul-Faqar, on the day of Badr. Ibn Abbas said: He is the one who saw the vision about it on the day of Uhud, and that is because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Upon him, when the polytheists came to him on the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that he should stay in Medina and fight them there, so he said to him: People: They did not witness Badr. Will you bring us out, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we will fight them with Uhud, and they hoped that they would strike whoever Virtue is what happened to the people of Badr. They continued to follow the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he wore his tool. They regretted it and said: O Messenger of God, stand up. The opinion is your opinion. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A prophet should not put away his tool after he has put it on, until God judges between him and his enemy.” He said: Among the things that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them that day before he put on the garment was: “I saw that I was wearing strong armor. So I interpreted it as the city, and that I was carrying a ram, so I interpreted it as the ram of the battalion, and I saw that my sword was Dhu al-Faqar, so I interpreted it as a ram among you. And I saw cows being slaughtered, and cows, and God is good, so cows, and God is good.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2588 - True"
"2589","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about the origin of his book, Abu Qalaba Abdul Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, Abdullah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami told me, he said: I To walk with my father, when he passed by people who were disparaging Ali, may God be pleased with him, and they were saying bad things about him. So he got up and said: Indeed, I was trying to get rid of Ali while I was against him. Something, and I was with Khalid ibn al-Walid in an army, and they took spoils, so Ali took one of the five slave girls, so he took her for himself, and he was among There was something between Ali and Khaled, so Khaled said: This is your opportunity, and Khaled recognized what was in my heart about Ali, so he said: So go to the Prophet, may God bless him. So mention that to him. I went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I spoke to him. I was a haughty man, and whenever I narrated a hadith, I was haughty. Then I raised my head and mentioned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the command of the army. Then I mentioned Ali’s command to him, so I raised my head and the Messenger of God’s cheeks. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. It turned red. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever I am his guardian, then Ali is his guardian, and what I have in my heart is gone.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, Al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf. On the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father in brief, “and nothing on this subject is more authentic than this hadith of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, and this was narrated by Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah on the authority of Al-A’mash"
"2590","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that he passed by a gathering and then mentioned the hadith in its length.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2589 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2591","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn. With women and children, camels and sheep, so they arranged them in rows, so that they would outnumber the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Muslims met And the polytheists, so the Muslims turned away, as God Almighty said. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the servant of God and His Messenger,” and he said: “O community of Ansar, I am the servant of God and His Messenger.” So God defeated the polytheists, and he was not pierced with a spear or struck with a sword, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him, said on that day: “Whoever kills an infidel will have his spoils.” Abu Qatada killed twenty men on that day, and took their spoils. Abu Qatada said: Qatada: O Messenger of God, I struck a man on the rope, and he was wearing his armor, so I hastened him to take his loot, so look who he is, O Messenger of God. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, I have taken it, so give it to me. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, remained silent. He was not asked for anything unless he gave it to him or remained silent. Then Omar said: No, by God, God will not do evil to one of his lions. And he gives it to you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at this. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2591 - According to Muslim’s condition
 Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Isfahani Al-Zahid told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr Al-Bari told us, my father told me, Al-Walid told us Bin Muslim, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And Abu Bakr and Omar “burned the valuables of the precious man, withheld his arrows, and beat him” is a strange and authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it."
"2592","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, on the authority of Bishr bin al-Mufaddal, Muhammad bin Zayd told us He is the son of Muhajir Al-Ansari. Umair, the client of Abi Al-Lahm, told me: I witnessed Hunayn with my masters, so they spoke about me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And he greeted, “So he ordered me to undress a sword, and he was informed that I was an slave, so he ordered for me some of the belongings.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2592 - True"
"2593","Abu Ja`far Abdullah bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin al-Mansour, the Commander of the Faithful, dictating in the house of al-Mansour, told us. Abu Ja`far told us Muhammad bin Yusuf bin Al-Tabba’, my uncle Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Tabba’ told us, Muja’ bin Yaqoub bin Muja’ bin Yazid Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of his uncle Muja’ bin Al-Ansari’s slave girl, who was one of the reciters who recited the Qur’an, said: We witnessed Al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when We turned away from it, as the people were shaking with camels, and some of the people said to one another: What do the people have? They said: It was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We went out with the people to ride, and we found the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing on his camel by a graan. The cloud, and when the people gathered over it, he recited to them {Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest} [Al-Fath: 1] Then a man said: O Messenger of God, will it be opened? He said: “Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is a conquest.” So Khaybar was divided among the people of Hudaybiyyah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided it among the people of Hudaybiyyah. Thirteen arrows, and the army was one thousand five hundred, including three hundred knights. So he gave the knight two arrows, and he gave the man an arrow. A major hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2593 - True"
"2594","Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Hairi told me, Ahmad bin Al-Nadr bin Abdul-Wahhab told me, Wahb bin Baqiyya Al-Wasiti told us, Khalid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said On the day of Badr: “Whoever does such-and-such will get such-and-such from the voluntary deeds.” He said, “Then the young men came forward and the sheikhdom joined the banners and did not leave them. When it was opened May God be upon them. The sheikh said: We would be a response to you. If you are defeated, you will come to us, so do not go with the spoils and we will stay, but the boys refused. And they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made it for us, so God Almighty revealed {They ask you about the anfal. Say: The anfal are for God and the Messenger} [Al-Anfal: 1] To {just as your Lord brought you out of your house in truth, even though a party of the believers were averse} [Al-Anfal: 5] He says: So that was better for them. Likewise also, obey me, for I know the outcome of this of you.” This is an authentic hadith. Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and he argued He was a Muslim by Dawud ibn Abi Hind, but they did not produce him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2594 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2595","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in the month of Rabi’ al-Akhir in the year three hundred and ninety-eight, Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told me, Abu Bakr and Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, On the authority of Asim, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr with a sword, and I said: O Messenger of God, Today my chest was healed from the enemy, so give me this sword. He said: “This sword is neither mine nor yours. So I went and said, ‘It will be given to me today by someone who has not afflicted me.’ While we were talking, the Messenger came to me and said: Answer. I thought that some of my words had been revealed, so I came, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You asked me for this sword, but it is not mine and I do not have it.” Yours, and indeed, God has made it for me, so it is yours.” Then he recited, “They ask you about the anfal. Say, the anfal belongs to God and the Messenger.” [Al-Anfal: 1] until the end of the verse. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2595 - True"
"2596","Professor Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Daoud told us, Ahmed bin Saleh Al-Masry told us, Abd told us Allah ibn Wahb, Hayyi told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He came out on the Day of Badr in a group of three hundred and fifteen, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, they are barefoot, so carry them. Oh God, they are naked, so satisfy them. Oh God, they are hungry, so satisfy them. So God granted victory to him on the day of Badr, and they turned when they turned, and what was in them. A man unless he returned with one or two camels, and they were full and satisfied.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not take it out. On using as evidence Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Madhhaji, the client of Suleiman bin Abd al-Malik.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2596 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2597","Professor Abu Al-Walid told me, Abu Bakr bin Abi Daoud told us, Abdul-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, On the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, “used to send out some of those sent from the companies for themselves, especially to volunteer except for the part of the general army, and the fifth in that “It is entirely obligatory.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2597 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2598","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Dhakwan told us, And Mahmoud bin Khalid al-Dimashqi told us: Marwan bin Muhammad al-Dimashqi told us, Yahya bin Hamza told us: I heard Abu Wahb say: I heard Makhol, saying: I was a slave in Egypt to a woman from Hudhayl and she freed me, so I never left Egypt with knowledge, except that I contained it as I see it, Then I came to the Levant and sifted through it all, asking about the supererogatory prayer, but I did not find anyone to tell me anything about it until I met a sheikh called Ziyad bin Al-Tamimi’s slave girl, so I said to him: Did you hear anything during the supererogatory prayer? He said: Yes, I heard Habib bin Maslamah Al-Fihri, may God be pleased with him, saying: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Nafil a quarter” in The beginning, and a third in the return.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2598 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2599","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Musab bin Al-Miqdam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, On the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir al-Shami, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jariyah al-Tamimi, on the authority of Habib bin Maslamah al-Fihri, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “spend a third after the fifth.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2599 - True"
"2600","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Hushaym told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani told us, And Ash'ath bin Sawwar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Mujalid, said: The people of the mosque sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa, to ask him what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had done. Peace be upon him, in the food of Khaybar, so I came to him and asked him about that, so I said: Did he eat five of it? He said: “No, it was less than that, and if one of us wanted something, he would take what he needed from it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2600 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2601","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Musa ibn Harun told us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and Mu’mal ibn Hisham told us, they said: Ismail told us, On the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Arabs used to say: Whoever eats bread will become fat, so when we conquered Khaybar: “We made them eat some bread for themselves, so I sat on it and ate from it until I was satisfied, so I started to look at my backbone. Have I become fat?” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2601 - True"
"2602","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, and Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, they said: Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Anisa, Qays bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: I witnessed the conquest of Khaybar with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the people were defeated and we fell into their camps, the people took whatever islands they found. He said Zaid: These are the livestock. It was not so quick that the pots ran out. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he ordered the pots to be brought out. So it was rewarded. Then he divided it among us and assigned a sheep for every ten. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2602 - True"
"2603","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Asim Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Al-Hakam, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Looting is not permissible, so be repaid.” Pots” and thus it was narrated by Ghandar and Ibn Abi Adi on the authority of Shu’bah, and they mentioned hearing Tha’labah from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “and it is an authentic hadith The chain of transmission, but they did not narrate it, due to the hadith of Samak bin Harb, for he narrated it once, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"2604","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Adl al-Saffar told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr told us, Amr ibn Talha told us. Al-Qannad, on the authority of Asbat ibn Nasr, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He was looted. The people brought sheep on the Day of Khaybar, slaughtered them, and began to cook from them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and ordered the pots to be prepared, and they were filled. He said: “Looting is not appropriate.”"
"2605","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Abu Kudinah told us, On the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He is not one of us.” “Whoever plunders, plunders, or indicates plunder.” Al-Bukhari cited as evidence Abu Kudaynah Yahya bin Al-Muhallab. “This is an authentic hadith and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2605 - Al-Bukhari cited Abu Kadina as evidence"
"2606","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, Abu Asim Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, Wahb bin Khaled told me Al-Homsi, Umm Habiba bint Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, may God be pleased with them, narrated to me. She said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said, “He forbade secrecy and crouching, and from having intercourse with female captives until they put what is in their bellies.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2606 - True"
"2607","Da'laj bin Ahmad al-Sijistani told me, Abd al-Aziz bin Muawiyah al-Basri told me, Muhammad bin al-Jahm al-Khurasani told us, Ismail told us Ibn Ja`far, Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Harith narrated to me, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Musa al-Ashdaq, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah al-Bahili May God be pleased with him, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, that he said: I went out with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. To Badr, we met the enemy. When he defeated them, a group of Muslims followed them, killing them. A group stared at the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and a group of soldiers took control. When God had sufficed the enemy and those they had killed returned, they said: We are the ones who killed them. The enemy, and through us God banished them and defeated them, and those who stared at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are not more deserving of it than we are. For us, we stared at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the enemy did not catch him by surprise, and those who took control of the army said: By God, what You are more deserving of it than we are. We captured the army, so God Almighty sent down “They ask you about Anfal. Say: Anfal belongs to God.” And the Messenger, fear God and make peace between yourselves} [Al-Anfal: 1] until His saying {If you are believers} [Al-Baqarah: 91], so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided it. He conceded among them about a hiccup, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it.” And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi, “It is authentic according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2607 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2608","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Musa Al-Ashdaq, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, who said: I asked Ubadah Ibn Al-Samit about Al-Anfal. He said: Among us, the companions of Badr, was revealed. Then he mentioned the hadith in its length.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2608 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2609","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Ahmad bin Salih told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Haywa bin Shuraih told me, On the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Shurahbil bin Saad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in During the Battle of Khaybar, a group went out, and they took a man who had sheep to herd with him, and they brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to him. May God grant him peace, as long as God wills that he speak, so the man said to him: I have believed in you and in what you have brought, so what about the sheep, O Messenger of God? So it is a trust, and it is for the people, the sheep and the sheep, and more than that? He said: “Count its faces as it returns to its people.” So he took a handful of pebbles or dirt and threw it at its faces, and it came out strengthening until Each sheep went to its family, then it advanced to the line, and an arrow struck it and killed it, and it never made a prostration before God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Bring him into the tent.” So he entered the tent of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, until when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, finished, he entered. Then he went out and said: “Your friend’s Islam has become good. I went in to see him, and he has two wives of his own, among the beautiful virgins.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2609 - Rather, Sharhabeel was accused, as Ibn Abi Dhu’ayb said."
"2610","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abbas, On the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “brought a gazelle in which “Beads from the spoils, so he divided them between the free woman and the female slave alike.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2610 - True"
"2611","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Hamawayh told me, my father told me, Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas May God be pleased with them both. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the Day of Khaybar forbade the sale of spoils until they were divided, and the pregnant woman from being settled in.” Until they put what is in their bellies, and he said: “Will you water someone else’s crops?” And about eating the meat of female donkeys, and about the flesh of any wild animal with fangs, “this hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2611 - True"
"2612","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Ubaid ibn Sharik informed us, Sa`id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi informed us. The trigger, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling spoils until they were divided.” Some of this text was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission on the condition that The two sheikhs """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2612 - True"
"2613","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shayban informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the Day of Khaybar. And about pregnant women from being intimate with until they give birth to what is in their bellies, and about every wild animal that has fangs, and about selling one-fifth until it is divided.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2613 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2614","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, Ibn Abi Gharza told us, Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Asbahani told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, people from the Quraysh came to him and said: Oh Muhammad, we are your allies and your people, but our slaves have joined you. They have no desire for Islam, but have fled from work, so send them back. against us, so he consulted Abu Bakr about their matter and said: They spoke the truth, O Messenger of God. He said to Omar: “What do you see?” So he said something similar to what Abu Bakr said. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people of Quraysh, God will send against you a man from among you who God will test.” His heart is for faith, so he will strike your necks against religion.” Abu Bakr said: Is it he, O Messenger of God? He said: “No.” Omar said: Is it me, O Messenger of God? He said: “No, but he is the one who irons the shoes in the mosque.” He had given his sandals to Ali to have them decorated, then he said: “But I heard him say: “No.” “You lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter Hell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2614 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2615","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yahya told me Ibn Ayyub, Ibrahim Ibn Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Kathir, the client of Banu Makhzum, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He divided for two hundred horses on the Day of Khaybar two shares by two shares.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it with this wording. “Al-Bukhari cited Yahya bin Ayyub and Kathir al-Makhzoumi as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2615 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2616","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, my father told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Malath, speaking on the authority of Numayr bin Aws, on the authority of Malik bin Masruh, on the authority of Amer bin Abi Amir Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes, the living lion, and the Ash’arites, do not flee in battle, nor are they deserted. They are of me and I am.” “From them.” He said: So I told Muawiyah about it, and he said: Not like that. Rather, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They are from me and to me.” So I said: Not. Thus, my father spoke to me, but he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “They are of me and I am of them.” He said: So you know best. According to the hadith of your father, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2616 - True"
"2617","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Ayyub bin Suwayd told us, Abdullah bin Shudhab told us, On the authority of Amer bin Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet When he captured spoils, he commanded Bilal and he called three people, and the people picked up what they had captured. Then he ordered that five should be taken, and a man with reins came to him. From a hair, and the spoils were divided, so he said to him: “Did you hear Bilal calling for three?” He said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from bringing him? So he apologized to him and said to him: “Be the one who takes him on the Day of Resurrection, for I will not accept it from you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2617 - True"
"2618","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani told us in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham bin Jamil told us, Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, about Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, and I was sitting with him, and Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “One of the prophets fought the people of a city to the point that, as he was about to conquer it, he feared that it would be destroyed.” The sun, and he said to it: O sun, you are commanded, and I am commanded by my sanctity over you, except that she remained idle for an hour of the day, he said: Then God imprisoned her until He opened it, and when they captured the spoils, they would offer them as offerings. Then the fire came and consumed them. When they captured the spoils, they would offer them an offering. The fire will come and consume it. They said: O Prophet of God, what is the matter with us that our offering is not accepted? He said: There are deceptions among you. They said: How do we know who has deceptions? He said: They are twelve tribes. He said: The head of every tribe of you pledges allegiance to me. So the head of every tribe pledged allegiance to him. He said: So I touched the palm of the Prophet with the palm of a man. One of them said to him: You have the deceptions. He said: How should I know which tribe he belongs to? He said: Call your tribe and pledge allegiance to them, man by man. He said: So he did, and his palm stuck to the palm of the man who took the spoils, and the fire came and consumed him. He said: Ka'b: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth like this, and God is in the Book of God, meaning in the Torah. Then he said: O Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to you. What prophet was he? He said: No. Ka'b said: He is Joshua bin Nun. He said: So he told you which town it is? He said: No. He said: It is the city of Jericho. “This is a strange and authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2618 - Sahih Gharib"
"2619","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim told us Bin Muhammad bin Arara Al-Sami, Azhar bin Saad Al-Samman told us, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaida, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about the captives on the day of Badr: “If you wish, you can kill them, and if you wish, you can ransom them and seek ransom. And among you was martyred for their number. The last of the seventy was Thabit bin Qais, may God be pleased with him, and he was martyred at Al-Yamamah. This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2619 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2620","Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz told me, Ibrahim Abi Talib told us, Amr bin Ali, and Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, they said: Abu Bahr told us Al-Bakrawi, Shu’bah narrated to us, Abu Al-Anbas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made He said: “For the ransom of the pre-Islamic prisoners, there were four hundred.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2620 - True"
"2621","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told me, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Dawud told us Bin Abi Hind, Ali bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Ishaq bin Shaheen told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: There were some people who were taken captive on the day of Badr and had no ransom. “Then the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Their ransom is to teach the children of the Ansar how to write. He said: Then a boy from the Ansar’s children came to his father. He said: What is the matter with you? He said: My teacher hit me. He said: The wicked seeks at the entrance of Badr, and by God you will never come to him. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2621 - True"
"2622","Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Ubaid bin Ibrahim Al-Asadi told us in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Abu Al-Yaman Al-Hakam told us Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Jubayr Ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf Ibn Malik al-Ashja’i, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to “when a rainy day came to him, he would divide it from his day, and he would give the family two portions and the single portion one portion.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He narrated four hadiths with this same chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2622 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2623","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ruh bin Ubadah, and Abd Al-Wahhab Al-Khafaf told us, they said: Saeed bin Abu Orouba, and Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qays ibn Ubadah, he said: Al-Ashtar and I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, on the Day of the Camel. So I said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, make a covenant with you to the exclusion of the common people? So he said: No, except this one, and he took out the skin of his sword, and in it was: “The blood of the believers will be rewarded, and the lowest of them will strive for their protection. And they are a hand on everyone else. A believer is not killed by an unbeliever, nor is he a covenant person in his covenant.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And there is evidence to him on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Amr bin Al-Aas.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2623 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim
 As for the hadith of Abu Hurairah"
"2624","So Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl informed me, my grandfather told me, Ibrahim bin Hamzah Al-Zubayri told me, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim told us, about many things. Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one who is closest to my nation will be kind to my nation.”"
"2625","As for the hadith of Amr ibn al-Aas, it is known that he killed Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr when he entered upon him and said to him: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr? He said: Yes, he said: Did you come safely? He said: No, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Their blood will be shed on Muslims.” The hadith"
"2626","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told us, Mahbub bin Musa told us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, On the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The obligation of Muslims is one. A reward has passed upon them, so do not hide it, for for every treacherous person there is a sign, by which he will be known on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. In this context, they only agreed to mention the one who left.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2626 - True"
"2627","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ishaq bin Idris told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Do not live with the polytheists, and do not have intercourse with them, for whoever lives with them or has intercourse with them “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2627 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2628","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Ibrahim bin Isma bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, My father told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: There was a man from the Ansar who converted to Islam, then He apostatized and joined the polytheists, then he regretted it and sent to his people to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is there any repentance for me? He said: “So it was revealed: {How will God guide a people who disbelieved after their belief} [Al Imran: 86] to His saying: {Except those who repent after that and make amends. Indeed, God is Forgiving, Merciful.} [Al Imran: 89] He said: “So he sent his people to him, and he submitted to Islam.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2628 - True"
"2629","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, the jurist, told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Abdullah bin Qais, that his father, may God be pleased with him, narrated: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was afraid of a people, he would say: “O God, we place you in their direction, and we seek refuge in you from their evils.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and my greatest suspicion is that they did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2629 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2630","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told me Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray and say: “O God, grant me With my hearing and my sight, and make them my heir. O God, grant me victory over my enemy, and show me my vengeance therein.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2630 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2631","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Musaddad bin Qatan told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a person who has contracted a contract in a manner other than his duties, God will forbid Paradise for him.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2631 - True"
"2632","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl bin Hamdawayh al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Ibrahim bin Maqil al-Nasafi told us, Muhammad bin Amr al-Razi told us He is called a negro. We are told by Salama bin Al-Fadl Al-Abrash. Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, he said: Musaylimah wrote to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And peace be upon him, and Ibn Ishaq told me, on the authority of Saad bin Tariq Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Salama bin Nu’aym bin Masoud Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father Nu’aym May God be pleased with him. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to my messenger, Musaylimah, when he read Musaylimah’s letter: “What do you say?” They said: We say as he said. He said: “By God, had the messengers not been killed, I would have struck your necks.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2632 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2633","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufaili informed us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah told us, Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When the battle was fierce and the people met the people, we would fear the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so let none of us be closer to the people than he. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2633 - True"
"2634","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “One foray by sea is better than ten forays on land, and whoever crosses the sea, it is as if he has crossed all the valleys, and the table. Therein is like one whose blood is smeared.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2634 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2635","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, saying: Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Aqeel, Zahra bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Abu Salih, the client of Uthman bin Affan, who said: I heard Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, God said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “One day’s bond in the path of God is better than a thousand for anything else.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2635 - True"
"2636","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Zahra bin Ma’abad, He heard Abu Salih say: I heard Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, while he was in Mina, saying: I am telling you a story that I had not told you before. I never heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “One day’s bond for the sake of God is better than a thousand for anything else. Have I conveyed this to you?” They said: Yes. He said: “O God, bear witness.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"2637","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed me, Haywa bin Shurayh, Abu Hani Humaid bin Hani al-Khawlani told me, on the authority of Amr bin Malik al-Janabi, he told him that he heard Fadalah bin Ubaid, may God be pleased with him, narrated, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever dies on one of these levels will be resurrected on it on the day of Resurrection: a ritual, Hajj, or something else.
 Fadalah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Every dead person has his deeds sealed, except for the one who died stationed in the path of God. He grows “He will have his deeds until the Day of Resurrection, and he will be safe from the trial of the grave.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"2638","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, Abu al-Muthanna informed us, al-Musaddad informed us, Yahya ibn Sa`id told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Khadij, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “There is not an Arabian horse without two supplications being given to it at dawn every dawn, saying: O God, you have given me authority over the sons of Adam.” So make me love his family and his wealth. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2638 - True"
"2639","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Musa bin Sahl told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan. Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to call a female horse a mare.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2639 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2640","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubayy. Humaid, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Saad bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Happiness for the son of Adam is three things, and misery for the son of Adam is three things. Among the happiness of the son of Adam are: a righteous woman, a good dwelling, And the good boat, and from the misery of the son of Adam: the cramped dwelling, the bad woman, and the bad boat “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2640 - True"
"2641","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Abdul Rahman bin Yazid informed us. Bin Jabir, Zaid bin Artat told me, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Seek Me in your weak ones, for it is only through your weak ones that you are provided for and given victory.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"2642","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told me, Yahya bin Sulayman al-Jafi told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Huyayy, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both: that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out On the day of Badr, with three hundred and fifteen fighters, Taloot also went out, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for them when he went out and said: “O God, they are barefoot, so carry them. O God, they are naked, so feed them. O God, they are hungry, so satisfy them.” Then God opened the day for them. Badr, so they turned, and there was not a man among them who did not return with one or two camels, and they were full and satisfied. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”"
"2643","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anazi told me, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi told me, Abu al-Jamahir Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Tanukhi told me, and Abu Tawbah al-Rabi` ibn Nafi’ al-Halabi, they said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, Rashid bin Dawud al-San’ani told me, Abu Asma al-Rahbi told me, on the authority of Thawban Radhi On his authority, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said while he was walking: “We are walking Tonight, God Almighty willing, neither one who is weak nor one who is difficult will leave with us.” So a man was riding on a camel that had a difficulty, and he fell and his neck was broken. Then he died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that he be buried. Then he ordered Bilal and he called out: “Indeed, Paradise is not permissible for a sinner.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2643 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 The Book of Fighting the People of Transgression, which is the last jihad."
"2644","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Umayy told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdullah bin Hamran told us, Abdul Hamid bin Jafar told us, My father told me, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came A man was dividing dates on the Day of Khaybar and said: O Muhammad, be just. He said: “Woe to you, who will treat you justly if I do not do justice?” - Or from whom will you seek justice after me? Then he said: “A people like this will soon come, reciting the Book of God, while they are His enemies, reading the Book of God with their heads shaved. “So when they go out, strike their necks.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2644 - Muhammad bin Sinan was lied to by Abu Dawud and others"
"2645","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told me about Marw, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid, Othman Al-Shaham told us, Muslim bin Abi Bakra told us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The There are some people from my nation who are very keen. Their tongues are well versed in the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass away from religion as an arrow passes away from its target. “You meet them and kill them, for the one who kills them will be rewarded.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Othman Al-Shaham
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2645 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2646","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl, the jurist in Bukhara, told us about him, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Sulayman bin Dawud told us. Al-Ataki and Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Dhabi, who said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Uthman Al-Shaham, who said: I came to Muslim bin Abi Bakra, and Farqad Al-Sabhi So we went to him and said: Did you hear your father mentioning the hadith of temptations? He said: Yes, I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will be among my nation a people whose tongues are deceived by the Qur’an. So when you see them, make them feel comfortable.”"
"2647","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Al-Azraq bin Qais, on the authority of Sharik bin Shihab, said: I was hoping to see a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would tell me about The Kharijites said: I met Abu Barzah, may God be pleased with him, on the Day of Arafah with a group of his companions, and I said: O Abu Barzah, tell us something. I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying about the Kharijites. He said: I will tell you what my ears have heard and my eyes have seen. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with dinars from the land, and he was dividing them while there was a man with him. He was black, with his hair tied up, wearing two white clothes, and between his eyes there were traces of prostration. He approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to him before. His face, but he did not give him anything, so he came to him from his left, but he did not give him anything, so he came to him from behind him, and said: By God, O Muhammad, you have not done justice since Today in the division. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry and said: “You will not find anyone after me who is more just than you.” He said it three times, then he said: “He will emerge from the direction of the East.” A people as if their guidance was like this. They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass away from religion as an arrow passes from its target, and then no They will return to him, and he will put his hand on his chest. Their marks will fly. They will continue to go out until the last of them comes out, so when you see them... So kill them - Hammad said it three times - they are the worst of creation and creation - Hammad said it three times and he also said - they will not return to it. This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2647 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2648","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr Al-Bari told us, my father told us, Hisham bin Yusuf Al-San’ani told us, On the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There will be disagreement and division in my nation, and there will come A people who admire you, and their own souls admire them. Those who kill them are more deserving of God than they. They speak good words and do evil in deeds. They call to God, but they are not from God in anything, so when you meet them, greet them. They said: O Messenger of God, describe them to us. He said: “Their signs are shaving and resting.” meaning the eradication of shortcomings. He said: “Istibbat means removing the hair.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Al-Awza’i narrated this hadith on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2648 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2649","Ahmed bin Othman Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Masisi told us, Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him: That the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There will be disagreement among my nation. And a group, a people who speak well and do poorly, and recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. One of you will deem his prayer in contempt with their prayer. By his fasting along with their fasting, they are pardoned from the debt like an arrow shot from the target, and it does not come back until the arrow is returned to its head, and they are the worst of creation and creation. Blessed are those who killed them and they killed him. They call to the Book of God and are not of it in any way. Whoever kills them has more right to God than they. They said: O Messenger. God, what is their name? He said: “flying”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2649 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2650","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Qatada bin Di’amah told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with them, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There will be disagreement among my nation. And a group, a people who speak well and do bad, and recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass away from religion as an arrow passes through it. They will not return until the evil of mankind and creation is restored. Blessed are those who killed them and who killed him. They call to the Book of God but are not of it. Something, whoever fights them has more deserving of God than they. They said: O Messenger of God, what is their name? He said: “The flight.” Qatadah did not hear this hadith from Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, rather he heard it from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id."
"2651","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf, the jurist in al-Tabaran, told me: Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi, in Herat, and Ubaid ibn Abd told us Al-Wahid bin Sharik in Baghdad, they said: Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Uthman Al-Tanukhi narrated to us, Saeed bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ali Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Their parable is that of a man shooting an arrow, then he misses the arrow wherever it lands. So he took it and looked at its top, and did not see fat or blood on it. Then he looked at its feathers, and did not see fat or blood on it, then he looked at its blade. He did not see fat or blood in it, just as nothing of fat and blood was attached to it, nor were these people attached to anything of Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2651 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2652","Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Hashimi told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Malik bin Ismail Al-Nahdi told us, Israel bin Yunus reported, on the authority of Muslim Al-Awar, on the authority of Khaled Al-Arni, who said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri and I entered Hudhayfah and said: O Abu Abdullah, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding sedition. Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go with the Book of God wherever it goes.” So we said: If people disagree, who should we be with? He said: “Look at the group in which Ibn Sumaya is, and stick to it, for he is circulating with the Book of God.” He said: I said: And who is Ibn Sumaya? He said: Or what do you know? I said: Explain it to me. He said: “Ammar bin Yasser.” I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to Ammar: “O Abu Al-Yaqzan, you will not die until “The transgressing group will kill you on the road.” This is a hadith that has chains of transmission with authentic chains of narration. They reported some of them but did not mention it with this wording.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2652 - Muslim bin Kaysan was left by Ahmad and Ibn Ma’in"
"2653","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Al-Qasim Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Baghawi told us, Abu Kamel Al-Jahdari told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar, Khaled Al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that he said to him and his son Ali: Go To Abu Saeed, and they heard from him his hadith regarding the Kharijites, so they went off, and they found him in a room of his, making repairs. When he saw us, he took his robe, then He hid himself, then he started speaking to us until he mentioned him in the mosque, and he said: We were carrying one brick after another, and Ammar was carrying two bricks for two daughters. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him and began to shake the dirt off his head, and said: “O Ammar, will you not carry brick by brick as your companions carry?” He said: I want the reward from God. He said: Then he started to shake himself and say: “Woe to Ammar, the transgressing group will kill him.” He said: And Ammar says: I seek refuge. By God, from temptations. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2653 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2654","Abu Al-Hussein bin Musa Al-Hunaini told us, Abu Hudhayfah Al-Nahdi told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Shaddad bin Abdullah Abi Ammar, He said: I witnessed Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, standing at the head of Al-Haruriyya at the gate of Damascus, and he said: “The dogs of the people of Hell - he said it three times - is the best of those killed by those who killed him. His eyes filled with tears, and a man said to him: O Abu Umamah, did you see what you said: “These are the dogs of fire.” Is it something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or in your opinion? He said: I would be daring if I had not heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except once, or twice, or three times, and he counted seven times. I told you about him. A man said to him: I saw you with tears in your eyes. He said: Indeed, when they were believers, they disbelieved after their belief. Then he recited: {And You will be like those who became divided and disagreed after the clear proofs had come to them.} [Al Imran: 105] The verse is for them twice."
"2655","Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Ahmad bin Yusuf Al-Sulami told us, Al-Nadr bin Muhammad told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar, Shaddad bin Abdullah Abu Ammar narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, while he was standing over the heads of the Hurriyah at the gate of Homs - Or the Damascus Gate - and he says: “The dogs of fire are the worst killed under the shade of the sky, the best killed are those who killed them.” Then he moved the hadith towards the hadith of Abu Hudhayfah, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it.” And the hadith of Muslim in the authentic musnad on the authority of Nasr bin Ali bin Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Ammar, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God says: O son of Adam, you are generous.” The hadith, and we have only explained what it says about it because what prevails in this text is the hadith of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Umamah, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2654 - Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions"
"2656","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, from the origin of his book, Abu Umayyah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Tarsusi told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim told us. Al-Yamami, Ikrimah bin Ammar Al-Ijli told us, Abu Zumail Sammak Al-Hanafi told us, Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them, told us, he said: When The Hurriyya came out. They gathered in a house, and they were six thousand. I came to Ali and said: O Commander of the Faithful, come to the house at noon, so that I may go to these people. The people, I will speak to them. He said: I fear for you. I said: No. Ibn Abbas said: So I went out to them and wore the best clothes from Yemen. Abu Zumail said: Ibn Abbas was beautiful and loud. Ibn Abbas said: So I came to them, and they were gathered in their house, saying: So I greeted them, and they said: Welcome, Ibn Abbas. So what are these? The suit? He said: I said: What do you blame me for? I have seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wear the best of apparel, and the following verse was revealed: “Say, ‘Whoever forbids adornment? It is Allah who has brought forth for His servants and good things of provision.} [Al-A'raf: 32] They said: What brings you? I said: I came to you from the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Muhajireen and Ansar, to inform you of what they say. Those who inform you of what they say. It was upon them that the Qur’an was revealed, and they are more knowledgeable of the revelation than you.And among them was revealed: And not one of them is among you. So some of them said: Do not dispute with Quraysh, for God says: {Rather, they are a contentious people} [Al-Zukhruf: 58] Ibn Abbas said: I came to a people whom I did not see. There has never been a people more diligent than them. Their faces were bright from staying up late, as if their hands and knees were being praised. So those who were present went away and said: Some of them: Let us speak to him and see what he says. I said: Tell me, what did you take revenge on the cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his son-in-law, the immigrants and the Ansar? They said: Three. I said: What are they? They said: As for one of them, he made men arbitrate in the matter of God, and God Almighty said: {Indeed, judgment belongs only to God} [Al-An’am: 57] and what belongs to men and what To judge? I said: This is one. They said: As for the other, he fought, and did not take captives, nor did he take any spoils. So if the one who fought were infidels, then their captivity and spoils are permissible, and if they were Believing that it is not permissible to fight them. I said: These are two, so what is the third? He said: He removed himself from the status of the Commander of the Faithful, for he is the Commander of the Unbelievers. I said: Do you have anything other than this? They said: This is sufficient for us. So I said to them: Have you considered that if I read to you from the Book of God and from the Sunnah of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that would refute your statement, would you be satisfied? They said: Yes.So I said: As for your saying: Men rule in the matter of God, I am reciting to you what His ruling was returned to the men regarding the eighth of a quarter of a dirham in a rabbit. And the like of hunting. He said: “O you who have believed, do not kill game while you are inviolable.” [Al-Ma’idah: 95] to his saying: “Some people will judge by it.” Fairer than you.} [Al-Ma’idah: 95] So I appealed to you, by God. Is the ruling of men better regarding rabbits and similar hunting, or is their ruling regarding their blood and the righteousness of their souls? Among them? And that you should know that if God had willed, He could have judged, and that would not have happened to men, and regarding the woman and her husband, God Almighty said: {And if you fear a discord between them, then send an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her people. If they desire reconciliation, God will reconcile between them} [An-Nisa: 35] So He made God gave men a safe Sunnah. Have you deviated from this? They said: Yes. He said: As for your saying: He fought but did not take captives and did not take spoils. Do you take your mother Aisha captive and then make lawful from her whatever is deemed lawful? Other? If you do so, then you have disbelieved, and she is your mother. And if you say: She is not a mother, then you have disbelieved. For God says: {The Prophet has more right to the believers than themselves and their wives and their mothers} [Al-Ahzab: 6] So you are turning between two misguidances, whichever one you have turned to. You have turned into a misguidance, so look. to each other,I said: Did you get out of this? They said: Yes, he said: As for your saying that his name was erased from the Commander of the Faithful, I will bring to you whom you will be pleased with, and I will show you that you have heard that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace On the day of Hudaybiyyah, Suhail bin Amr and Abu Sufyan bin Harb wrote, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Commander of the Faithful: Write, O Ali: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, agreed upon.” Then the polytheists said: No, by God, we do not know that you are the Messenger of God, even if we knew that you Messenger of God, we did not fight you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, you know that I am the Messenger of God. Write, O Ali: This is what has been agreed upon.” Upon him is Muhammad bin Abdullah. “By God, the Messenger of God is better than Ali, and he did not remove him from prophethood when he erased himself,” said Abdullah bin Abbas: Two thousand of the people returned, and the rest of them were killed based on misguidance. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2656 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2657","Ali bin Hamshad told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir Al-Abdi told us, Yahya bin Sulaym, and Abdullah bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hadi, who said: I came to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, while we were When she was sitting, she was returning from Iraq the nights Ali was killed, and she said: O Abdullah bin Shaddad, are you telling the truth about what I am asking you about? He told me about these people that Ali killed. I said: Why don't I believe you? I said: Tell me about their story. I said: When Ali wrote Muawiyah’s letter and ruled on the two arbitrators, eight thousand of the people’s reciters came out to him, and they camped in a land on the side of Kufa called: Haroura, and they disapproved of him, saying: You took off the shirt that God clothed you with and fished with, then you went and judged according to God’s religion, but there was no judgment. Except for God. When Ali heard what they had reproached him for and they left him, he ordered and a muezzin gave the call: “Do not enter the presence of the Commander of the Faithful except a man who has carried the Qur’an.” So when he The house was filled with readers. He called for a great Qur’an, placed it in his hands, and began minting it with his hand, saying: O Qur’an, speak to the people. So the people called him. They said: O Commander of the Faithful,What you are asking about is paper and ink, and we are speaking from what we have seen of it, so what do you want? He said: Your companions who went out, between me and them is the Book of God. God Almighty says regarding a woman and a man: And if you fear discord between them, then send As an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her people, the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more inviolable than a woman or a man, and they took revenge on me because I wrote Muawiyah and Ali bin Abi Talib wrote, and Suhail bin Amr came and we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Hudaybiyyah when he made peace. His people were Quraysh, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote: “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” So Suhail said: Do not write, “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” He said: “So how do I write?” He said: Write in your name, O God. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Write.” Then he said: “Write: from Muhammad, the Messenger of God.” They said: If we knew that you are the Messenger of God, we would not We disagree with you, so it was written: “This is what Muhammad bin Abdullah Quraysh agreed upon.” God says in His Book: “Indeed there is an example for you in the Messenger of God. “It is good for whoever hopes in God and the Last Day.” [Al-Ahzab: 21] So Ali bin Abi Talib sent him to them, so I went out with them until... We mediated their military,Ibn Al-Kawwa stood up and addressed the people and said: O bearers of the Qur’an, this is Abdullah bin Abbas. Whoever does not know him, I know him from The Book of God, this is what was revealed about his people: {Rather, they are a people of adversaries} [Al-Zukhruf: 58] So return it to its owner, and do not belittle it. It is the Book of God. He said: Then their preachers stood up and said: No, by God, we will put the Book of God into place for him. If he brings the truth, we know it and can handle it, and if he brings falsehood. We will certainly convict him of his falsehood, and We will return it to its owner. So they placed it on the Book of God for three days, and four thousand of them returned, all of them repentant. Among them was Ibn al-Kawwa’, until he brought them in to meet Ali, and Ali sent for the rest of them and said: It is our matter and the matter of the people as you have seen. So stand wherever you wish until the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is gathered together, and encamp wherever you wish. Between us and you, we will protect you with our spears unless Whether you cut off the path or prolong bloodshed, for if you do that, We have rejected war to you all the same. Indeed, God does not like traitors. Then Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said to him: O Ibn Shaddad, he killed them? . He said: By God, he did not send against them until they had crossed the path and shed blood without God’s right.They killed Ibn Khabbab and made the non-Muslims lawful. She said: By God? I said: Allah is the one besides whom there is no god. She said: I have not heard anything about the people of Iraq talking about him. They say: The one with the breast, the one with the breast. So I said: I saw him and stood on him with Ali was among the dead, so he called the people and said: Do you know this? Most of those who came would say: I saw him in the mosque of Bani so-and-so praying, and I saw him in the mosque of Bani so-and-so praying, but he did not bring any evidence that he knew. Other than that, she said: What did Ali say when he rose up against him, as the people of Iraq claim? I said: I heard him say: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. She said: Did you hear him say anything else? I said: Oh God, no. She said: Yes, God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, except for the mention of the mammal. Muslim narrated it.” With many chains of narration.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2657 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, from which a mention of Dhul-Thama was extracted."
"2658","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani told us, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza al-Ghifari told us, Ubaid Allah ibn Musa told us, Israel, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, said: I heard Malik bin Al-Harith, saying: I witnessed Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the day of Al-Nahrawan. He came upon him, and his forehead began to sweat, and anguish took hold of him. Then he came upon him and fell down, prostrating, and said: “By God, you have neither lied nor been lied to.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not mention it by mentioning the prostration of thanks, and it is strange and authentic in the prostration of thanks.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2658 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2659","Mukarram bin Muhammad bin Mukarram Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Attab Sahl told us Ibn Hammad Al-Dallal, Abdul-Malik Ibn Abi Nadra told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him: That the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He turned to him and began to strike him with his hand, leading him to the right and to the left. Among them was a man with short clothes, with a handsome appearance, between his eyes the traces of prostration, so he made The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swiped his hand right and left until the money ran out. When the money ran out, he turned away and said: By God, I have not done justice since. Today. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, started turning his palm and saying: “If I do not act justly, then who will do justice after me? A rogue will pass by.” They will pass away from the religion as an arrow has passed away from the target, then they will not return to it until the arrow returns to it. They recite the Qur’an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They speak well and do evil in deed, so whoever meets them should fight them, for whoever kills them will have the best reward, and whoever they kill will have the best reward. Martyrdom, they are the worst of humanity. God is innocent of them. The first of the two groups will kill them justly.” This is an authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it with this. Leadership, and Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Nadrah is one of the dearest of Basra in hadith, and I do not know that I have praised him in a hadith other than this.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2659 - True"
"2660","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, that Kathir bin Hisham told them, Ja’far bin Burqan told us, Maimun told us Ibn Mihran, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I witnessed Siffin and they did not attack a wounded person, nor did they kill a loyalist, nor “They rob a dead person.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration on this subject, and it has an authentic witness.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2660 - True"
"2661","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Abu Sa’id Muhammad bin Shazan told us, Ali bin Hajar told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Yazid bin Dubayyah Al-Absi, he said: The herald of Ammar called out on the Day of the Camel, and the people had turned away: “The wounded shall not be eulogized, nor shall a loyalist be killed, and whoever lays down his weapon is “Safe,” so that was difficult for us. “A chain of transmission has been narrated on this subject.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2661 - True"
"2662","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yusuf bin Abdullah Al-Khwarizmi told us, in Bayt Al-Maqdis, Abdul-Malik bin Abdul Aziz told us. Abu Nasr al-Tamar told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jazzar told me, Abu Nasr al-Tamar told me, Kawthar bin Hakim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abdullah bin Masoud: “O Ibn Masoud, do you know what God’s ruling is regarding the transgressor from this nation?” Ibn Masoud said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “For God’s decree regarding them is that their leader should not be followed, their captive should not be killed, and their captive should not be slandered.” “Their wounded”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2662 - Kawthar bin Hakim is abandoned"
"2663","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, he said: When Ammar bin Yasser, may God be pleased with him, was killed, Amr bin Hazm came to Amr bin Al-Aas and said: Ammar was killed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The transgressing group will kill him.” Then Amr bin Al-Aas got up in fear until he entered upon Muawiyah, and Muawiyah said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: Ammar was killed. Muawiyah said: Ammar was killed, so what? Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The oppressive group will kill him.” So Muawiyah said to him: You have refuted it in your urine, or We killed him, but Ali and his companions killed him. They brought him until they threw him between our spears - or he said: between our swords - “This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not take it out in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2663 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2664","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa informed us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha'arani informed us, Ismail ibn Abi Uwais told us, Ubayy told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, She said: “I have never seen anything like what this nation has desired from this verse: {And two parties of the believers fought each other.” So make peace between them, and if one of them transgresses against the other, then fight the one that transgresses until she submits to the command of God.} [Al-Hujurat: 9] “This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2664 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2665","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari, Abu Muhammad Al-Halimi, all told us about Marw, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ahmad, the jurist Al-Bukhari. In Nisapur, they said: Abu Al-Mujih Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told us, Abdan bin Uthman told us, Abu Hamza Muhammad bin Maimun told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin A relationship, on the authority of Arfaja bin Shurayh Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There will be hardships after me.” And then - and he raised his hands - then whoever you see wants to divide the affairs of the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they are all together, then kill him, whoever he may be among the people. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Rather, I ruled it according to the two sheikhs because Shu’bah ibn al-Hajjaj and Sufyan ibn Saeed, Shayban bin Abdul Rahman, and Muammar bin Rashid have narrated it, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah. Then I found Abu Hazim Al-Ashja’i and Amir. Al-Sha’abi, Abu Ya’fur Al-Abdi, and others followed Ziyad bin Ulaqah on his narration, on the authority of ‘Arfaja, and for me the chapter is compiled in one part. So that made no need for mentioning these narrations. “Muslim narrated the hadith of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If allegiance is given to the two caliphs, then kill the other of them,” and this was explained by the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd, Lord of the Kaaba, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, and it was narrated by Muslim
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2665 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2666","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, and Ahmad bin Jafar Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Dharr, how are you when you die? He afflicts people until the house is clean? - meaning the grave - I said: God and His Messenger have not chosen for me, then he said: How can you be? The hunger afflicts the people until you come to your mosque, but you are not able to return. To your bed, and you are not able to get from your bed to your mosque? I said: God and His Messenger have not chosen for me. He said: “You must be chaste,” then he said: “How can you kill people until the stones of oil are drowned in blood?” I said: God and His Messenger have not chosen for me, or God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Stay home.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, should I not take my sword and strike whoever did that with it? He said: “Then you have joined the people.” I said: O Messenger of God, if he enters my house? He said, “If you fear that the beam of the sword will dazzle you, then say thus, and throw the edge of your garment over your face, and he will bear his guilt and yours, and it will be “From the Companions of the Fire” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it “because Hammad bin Zaid narrated it, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, he said: Al-Munbath bin Tarif - who was a judge in Herat - told me on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted him like that
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2666 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2667","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Yunus bin Al-Musayyab Al-Dhabi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he informed us Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim and Amer Al-Shabi, who said: Marwan bin Al-Hakam said to Ayman bin Khuraym: Don’t you go out? So you fight with us? He said: My father and my uncle witnessed Badr, and they made a covenant with me that I would not fight anyone who says: There is no god but Allah, so if you come to me, With my innocence from the fire, I fought with you. He said: So leave us. He said: So he left and he said:
 [abundant sea]
 I will not kill a man who prays over another sultan from Quraysh.
 He has his dominion and my iniquity is over me... May God protect us from ignorance and recklessness.
 “Should I kill a Muslim for no crime... I will be of no benefit as long as I live.”
 This hadith has an authentic chain of narration on the condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, nor the two companions who mentioned and witnessed Badr. The hadith is within the limits of The cushions
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2667 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2668","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi of Hamdan informed us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Once, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Thawr al-Haddani, he said: Othman ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him, sent Sa`id ibn al-Aas to Kufa, he said: So they went out to him and brought him back. He said: I was sitting with Ibn Masoud and Hudhayfah, and Ibn Masoud said: I did not think he would return. These people, and not a cup of blood was spilled in them, and I did not know anything of that, except something that I knew, and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is alive. “The man is alive.” He wakes up as a believer in the morning, and in the evening there is nothing with him. He goes in the evening as a believer, and in the morning there is nothing with him. He fights in strife today, and God will kill him tomorrow. “His heart will be broken, and his bow will rise above it.” I said: the bottom of it. He said: “Rather, his bow.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2668 - True"
"2669","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Sulayman bin Bilal, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, on the authority of his mother, that there was a boy who was Bubā’s, and Bābī used to beat him about things, and he would punish him, and he used to The boy was hostile to his master, so he sold him. The boy met him one day, and the boy had a sword with him. That was under the command of Sa’id ibn al-Aas, so the slave appeared at my door. He took the sword and swung it at him, but the people kept it from him, so he entered the door of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and told her what the servant had done, and she said Aisha: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever points an iron weapon at one of the Muslims who wants to kill him, his blood must be sacrificed.” She said: Then Babi left her, so he went to the master of the slave from whom he had bought him, and he resigned from him. He dismissed him and returned to him, so Babi took him. So he killed him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2669 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2670","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Muammar bin Rashid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever draws his sword and then puts it down, “His blood was wasted.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2670 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2671","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amara bin Hazm, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “A time will soon come when people will be sifted, and there will remain a bunch of rubbish among the people whose covenants and trusts have been violated, and they disagreed and were “Thus,” and he interlaced his fingers. They said: How about us, O Messenger of God? He said: “You take what you know and leave what you deny, and you accept the affairs of your elite and leave the affairs of your common people.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2671 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim
 Marriage book"
"2672","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad Al-Bazzaz told us in Baghdad, Al-Hussein bin Abi Ma’shar told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, he told me outside. Ibn Musab, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “There is not a single morning without two heralds calling out: Woe to the men from the women, and woe to the women from the men.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2672 - Kharijah Wah"
"2673","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Barsani told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Omar bin Ata told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no In Islam “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2673 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2674","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Abdullah bin Abbas said to me: Did you get married? I said: No. He said: “Get married, for the best of this nation is the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, the majority of which are women, and whatever is stored in your heart, it is He will emerge before the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib followed Al-Mughirah bin Al-Nu’man in His narration
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2674 - True"
"2675","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Sa'id bin Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: “O Sa'id, get married, for the best of this nation are the ones who have the most women.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2675 - True"
"2676","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Sayyar bin Hatim told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Women and perfumes are beloved to me, and the comfort of my eye is made in prayer.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2676 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2677","Ibrahim bin Firas, the jurist in Mecca, told me: Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told me, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Muhammad bin Muslim al-Taifi told us, about Ibrahim bin Maysarah, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not seen for those who love each other Such as marriage. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. They did not narrate it because Sufyan bin Uyaynah and Muammar bin Rashid narrated it from Ibrahim. Ibn Maysara, on the authority of Ibn Abbas"
"2678","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Sa’id told us Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There are three rights that God owes: It helps them: the one who strives in the path of God, the one who is married wants to be chaste, and the one who is freed wants to perform. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it is not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2678 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2679","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abu Al-Sa’ib Salam bin Junada told us, Abu Usama told us, Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Marry women, for they are “He will bring you money.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it on the sole basis of Salim bin Junada with his chain of transmission, and Salim is trustworthy and trustworthy.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2679 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2680","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza told us, Khaled ibn Mukhlid told us, Muhammad told me Ibn Musa, on the authority of Saad Ibn Ishaq Ibn Ka’b Ibn Ujrah, on the authority of his paternal aunt, who said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman is married for one of three characteristics: A woman is married for her beauty, and a woman is married for her beauty. Its religion, and its character, so you must adhere to the same religion, your right hand crossed “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this addition.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2680 - True"
"2681","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa bin Zaid Al-Lakhmi told us, in Tanis, Amr bin Abi Salamah Al-Tanisi told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd informed me, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever has provided God is a righteous woman, so He has helped him with half of his religion, so let him fear God in the second half.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and Abd “The Most Merciful. This is Ibn Zayd bin Uqba Al-Azraq, a trustworthy and trustworthy civilian.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2681 - True"
"2682","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Tamim Al-Handali told me in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked: Which of the women is best? He said: “The best of women is one who is pleased when he looks, obeys when he commands, and does not disobey him regarding herself and her wealth.”"
"2683","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, the jurist, told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Abu Bakr told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad, Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, both on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Likewise, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2682 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2684","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Battah Al-Asbahani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Zakaria Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Bukayr Al-Hadrami, Khalid Ibn Abdullah told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr Ibn Hafs, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Saad, on the authority of His father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Three things are happiness, and three things are misery. Among happiness is: a woman you see that you like. And it is absent, so it is safe for itself and your property. The animal will be gentle and join you with your companions. The house will be spacious and have many facilities. Misery: A woman sees it and it makes you feel bad, and she lashes out against you, and if you are away from her, she does not feel safe about herself, your property, or the animal. It will be a herd, and if you ride it it will make you tired, and if you ride it it will not join you with your companions, and the house will be cramped and have few amenities.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of transmission from Khalid bin Abdullah Al-Wasiti to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was narrated alone by Muhammad bin Bukair, on the authority of Khalid If he memorized it, then it is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2684 - Muhammad said: Abu Hatim is truthful and makes mistakes, and Ya’qub bin Shaybah said: Trustworthy."
"2685","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Muslim bin Saeed told us, Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurra, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may God be pleased with him, said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted him and said: O Messenger of God, I have met a woman of rank, position, and money, but she does not give birth. Should I marry her? So he forbade him, then he came to him the second time and said to him like that, so he forbade him, then he came to him the third time and said to him like that, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Marry men who are loving and fertile, for I will outnumber the nations through you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2685 - True"
"2686","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told me, Harun bin Marouf told me, Abdullah told us Bin Wahb, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jumahi told me that Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Abi Talib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Ali bin Abu Talib, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There are three things, O Ali, do not delay: the prayer when it comes, and the funeral when it comes.” She is present, and the right one is if she finds a suitable one.” This is a strange and authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2686 - True"
"2687","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Kindi told us, Al-Harith bin Imran Al-Jaafari told us, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Make a choice so that we may have your sperm, so get married.” Competent people, and marry to them.” Ikrimah bin Ibrahim continued them, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa."
"2688","Ali bin Issa told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Ikrimah bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, So he mentioned with a similar chain of transmission, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2687 - Al-Harith is accused and Ikrimah is weak"
"2689","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan, the ascetic jurist in Baghdad, told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the people of this world will take this money.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2689 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2690","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Dawud bin Al-Munadi told us, Yunus bin Muhammad bin Al-Muaddeb told us, Salam told us Ibn Abi Muti’, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The account is money. “And generosity is piety.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2690 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2691","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, the jurist Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa Al-Farra told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us The Negro, Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Generosity “The believer’s religion is his religion, his chivalry is his mind, and his character is sufficient for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2691 - The Negro is weak"
"2692","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Hashim bin Yunus Al-Assar told us, in Egypt, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid narrated to me, he is Ibn Musafer, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin al-Zubayr, and Amra bint Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams, and he was among those who witnessed Badr with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, adopted Salim and married him to his brother’s niece Hind, the daughter of Al-Walid bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams. He was the slave of a woman from the Ansar, so he adopted him, just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, adopted Zaid, and he was the one who adopted a man in During the pre-Islamic period, the people invited him to it, and he inherited from his inheritance, until God Almighty revealed about that: {Call them by their fathers; that is fairer in the sight of God. You do not know their fathers, so they are your brothers in religion and your companions} [Al-Ahzab: 5] So return them to their fathers, for whoever has no known father, his master or His brother in religion. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Sahlah bint Suhail bin Amr Al-Qurashi, then Al-Amiri, and she was under Abu Hudhayfah. Ibn Utbah Ibn Rabi’ah, she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when God revealed that, and she said: O Messenger of God, we saw a healthy boy. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had given him shelter, and he used to stay with him and Abu Hudhayfah in one house, and he would see me while I was in favor, and he came down God is concerned about them as you know, so what do you think about him, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Breastfeed him.” She breastfed him five times, and he was deprived of them, and he was in the same position as her own child. Breastfeeding “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it, and it states that the honorable woman is married to every Muslim.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2692 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2693","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Banu Bayadah, marry Abu Hind and marry “To him,” he said: He was a cupper. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2693 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2694","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Ibrahim bin Isma bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us. Al-Muqri, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Marhum, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh, who is the son of Anas Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever gives for God, and withholds for God, and loves for God, and hates for God, and marries for God, has completed “Faith” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2694 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2695","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi informed me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Abdul-Hamid bin Suleiman informed us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Uthaymah Al-Basri, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If someone comes to you... “If you are satisfied with his character and his religion, then marry him. If you do not do so, there will be strife in the land and widespread corruption.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"2696","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Quraysh told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Muqaddami told me, Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Waqid bin Amr bin Muadh, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If one of you proposes marriage to a woman, then if he can see some of the things that will invite him to marry her, then let him do it.” So I proposed to a woman from Banu Sulaym, and I was hiding for her in the roots of palm trees until I saw something in her that prompted me to marry her, so I married her. An authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions, but they did not narrate it. Rather, Muslim narrated in this regard the hadith of Yazid ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, in brief.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2696 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2697","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl and Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told me, saying: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abdullah told me. Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that Al-Mugheerah ibn Shu’bah proposed to a woman, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Go and look at her, for it is more likely that there will be harmony between you.” He said: So he went and looked at her and mentioned her agreement, “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2697 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2698","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Haywa told me Bin Shurayh, that Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid told me that Ayoub bin Khaled bin Abi Ayoub Al-Ansari told him on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather May God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Keep the sermon, then perform ablution, and perform your ablution well, then pray what God has decreed.” Exalted be it to you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: Oh God, You are able and I am not able, and You know and I am not aware, and You are the Knower of the unseen. You see that a certain woman - he calls her by her name - is good for me in my religion, this world, and the hereafter, then decree it for me, for if anything else is better for me in my religion and this world. And my hereafter, so ordain it for me. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2698 - True"
"2699","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to marry a woman, so he sent a woman to look at her, and he said: “Smell her symptoms, and see.” To her necks. He said: Then she came to them and they said: Shall we not lunch with you, mother of so-and-so? She said: I only eat food that so-and-so brought. He said: So I climbed into a shelf of theirs and looked at her hocks, then said: Will you please me? With a structure, he said: So she started to spit it out while smelling its branches. He said: Then she came and reported, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2699 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2700","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abu Muammar told us, and Habib Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Is he not married? “The adulterer is flogged, except for something like him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2700 - True"
"2701","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas told me, on the authority of Amr Bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Marthad bin Abi Marthad Al-Ghanawi, may God be pleased with him, used to carry prisoners in Mecca, and he was There was a prostitute in Mecca, called Anak, and she was his girlfriend. He said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, should I marry Anak? He said: Then he remained silent about me, so it was revealed: “The adulterer shall not marry anyone except an adulteress or a polytheist, and the adulteress shall not be married except an adulterer or a polytheist, and it was forbidden.” That is upon the believers.} [An-Nour: 3] Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited to me and said: “Do not marry her.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2701 - True"
"2702","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The orphan is to be taken care of within herself, and if she remains silent, then it is “With her consent, and if she dislikes it, then there is no compulsion on her.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2702 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2703","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, on the authority of Abu Dhib, on the authority of Omar bin Hussein, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that he married the daughter of his maternal uncle Othman bin Maz’un. He said: So her mother went away To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: By God, my daughter hates it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to separate from her, so he separated from her and said: “Do not marry women until you have taken control of them, for if they remain silent, then it is their permission.” After him, Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah married her, “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2703 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2704","Mukhlid bin Ja`far al-Baqarhi told us, Muhammad bin Harb told us, Sa`id bin Yahya bin Sa`id al-Umawi told us, Ubayy told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin told us Alqamah, Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib told us, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: When Khadija, may God be pleased with her, died Khawla bint Hakim bin Umayyah bin Al-Awqas, the wife of Othman bin Mazun, may God be pleased with him, said, and that was in Mecca: That is, the Messenger of God, Get married? He said: “And who?” She said: If you want a virgin, and if you want a married man, he said: “And who is the virgin?” She said: The daughter of God’s most beloved creation to you is Aisha, daughter of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. He said: “And who is the thieb?” She said: Sawda bint Zam'ah bin Qais believed in you and followed you in what you are doing. He said: Go and remember them. So she came and entered Abu Bakr’s house and said: O Abu Bakr, what good and blessing has God brought upon you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to propose to Aisha. He said: Call the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for me. So she called him, and he came and married him. She was seven years old on that day. This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2704 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2705","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: Abu Bakr and Umar proposed to Fatima, and the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “She is young,” so Ali proposed to her and married her. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2705 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2706","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, and Abdul-Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us, In Hamdan, Muhammad bin Al-Jahm Al-Samari told us, they said: Abu Asim Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: I heard Suleiman bin Musa, saying: We told him: Al-Zuhri said: I heard Urwa, saying: I heard Aisha, may God be pleased with her, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Either A woman was married without the permission of her guardian, so her marriage is invalid. It is correct, and if they quarrel, then the ruler is the guardian of he who has no guardian.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Abu continued Asim mentioned that Ibn Jurayj heard from Sulayman bin Musa, and Sulayman bin Musa heard from Al-Zuhri, Abd al-Razzaq bin Hammam, and Yahya bin Ayoub, Abdullah bin Lahi’ah, and Hajjaj bin Muhammad Al-Masisi, as for the hadith of Abdul Razzaq"
"2707","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Salamah and Muhammad bin Shazan told us, and Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Muhammad, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Juraij told us, Suleiman bin Musa told me that Al-Zuhri told him Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told him that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, told him about the same thing on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 As for the hadith of Yahya bin Ayyub"
"2708","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, saying: Muhammad bin Ismail al-Sulami recited to me while I was listening. Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub reported, Ibn Jurayj told me, that Suleiman bin Musa al-Dimashqi told him, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman shall not be married without the permission of her guardian. If she is married Her marriage is invalid - three times - and if he marries her, she gets her dowry according to what happened to her. If they quarrel, then the sultan is the guardian of someone who has no guardian.”
 As for the hadith of Hajjaj bin Muhammad"
"2709","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah informed me, and Abu Yahya Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Samarqandi told me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Nasr told us, and Abu Amr bin Jafar Al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Ali Al-Dahli told us, they said: Yahya told us. Bin Yahya, Hajjaj bin Muhammad reported on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Suleiman bin Musa told me that Ibn Shihab told him that Urwa He told him that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, told him that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Any woman who is married without permission Her guardian, then her marriage is invalid, and she gets her dowry based on what happened to her. If they quarrel, then the sultan is the guardian of one who has no guardian.” It has been authenticated and proven. With the proven narrations of the imams, the narrators heard each other, so these narrations are not explained, according to the hadith of Ibn Ulayya, and his question by Ibn Jurayj on the authority of him and his saying: I asked Al-Zuhri about him and he did not know him. A trustworthy person who has memorized a hadith may forget the hadith after he narrated it, and he did it. Not one of the memorizers of the hadith.” Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi told us, he said: I heard Ahmad Ibn Hanbal says: And it was mentioned to him that Ibn Ulayya mentions the hadith of Ibn Jurayj regarding: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” Ibn Jurayj said: So I met Al-Zuhri So I asked him about him, but he did not know him. He praised Sulayman ibn Musa. Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: “Ibn Jurayj has written books, but this is not In his books, meaning the story of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Abbas bin Muhammad al-Dawri He says: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in say in the hadith: “There is no marriage except with a guardian” which was narrated by Ibn Jurayj, so I told him: Ibn Ulayya says: Ibn Jurayj said: So I asked Al-Zuhri about it, and he said: I have not memorized it. Yahya bin Ma’in said: No one says this except Ibn Ulayya, but rather Ibn Ulayya showed Ibn Jurayj’s books to Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, and he corrected them for him, but he did not exert himself For the hadith, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Abu Bakr bin Raja told us, Muhammad bin Al-Musaffa told us, Baqiya told us, Shuaib bin Raja told us. Abu Hamza said: Al-Zuhri said to me: An alcoholic person is coming to us, and Suleiman bin Musa, and for the sake of God, Suleiman bin Musa is the one who will protect the two men. He said Al-Hakim: “We returned to the origin from which the two sheikhs could not abandon the two Sahih books, which is the hadith of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Moses"
"2710","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us, and Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us, saying: Abu Qalabah ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad Al-Raqqashi, and Mukhalid bin Jaafar Al-Baqarhi told me, Ibrahim bin Hashim Al-Baghawi told us, saying: Suleiman bin Dawud told us, Al-Nu’man bin told us. Abd al-Salam, on the authority of Shu`bah, and Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” Al-Nu’man ibn Abd al-Salam combined Al-Thawri and Shu’bah in the chain of transmission of this hadith. It was transmitted on their authority by Al-Nu’man bin Abdul-Salam, trustworthy and trustworthy. “It was narrated by a group of trustworthy people, on the authority of Al-Thawri separately, and on the authority of Shu’bah on the authority of So they connected it, and all of that is mentioned in the chapter that my companions heard from me, so that made no need for them to be sent back. As for Isra’il ibn Yunus Ibn Abi Ishaq is trustworthy and the proof in the hadith of his grandfather Abi Ishaq, and he did not differ from him in conveying this hadith.”"
"2711","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Israel bin told us Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hisham bin Al-Qasim told us, and Ubaid Allah bin Musa, they said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and Ahmad bin Sulayman, the jurist, told us: Muhammad bin Sulayman al-Wasiti told us, Abu Ghassan Malik told us Bin Ismail, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalid al-Homsi told us, Ahmed bin Khaled Al-Wahbi, Israel told us, and Ahmed bin Salman, the jurist, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us: Muhammad told us: Ibn Yaqoub, Ahmad Ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harithi informed us, Talaq Ibn Ghannam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” These chains of narrations are all authentic, and it has been We were higher in it than Israel, and the previous imams who revealed it in their narrations on behalf of Israel, such as Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Waki’, Yahya bin Adam, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida and others,They ruled this hadith to be authentic: “I heard Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih in Bukhara, saying: I heard Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Habib Al-Hafiz, saying: I heard Ali bin Abdullah Al-Madini saying: I heard Abd Al-Rahman bin Mahdi saying: “Israel used to protect The hadith of Abu Ishaq, as he memorizes praise. “I heard Abu Al-Hasan bin Mansour, saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq, saying: I heard Abu Musa says: “Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi used to confirm the hadith of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, meaning in marriage without a guardian.” Muhammad told me Ibn Abdullah Al-Shaybani, Ahmed Ibn Muhammad Ibn Al-Hassan told us, Hatim Ibn Yunus Al-Jurjani told us, he said: I said to Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi: What do you say? In marriage without a guardian? He said: “It is not permissible.” I said: What is the evidence for that? He said: Qais bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, I said: Al-Thawri and Shu’bah are sent. He said: So Israel has followed Qais. Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Muhammad bin Al-Mundhir bin Saeed told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Jabla told us,I heard Ali bin Al-Madini saying: The hadith of Israel is authentic regarding “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” I heard Abu Al-Hasan bin Mansour saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam said: I asked Muhammad bin Yahya about this topic, and he said: The hadith of Israel is authentic to me, so I said to him: A partner also narrated it, and he said: Who narrated it? So I said: It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hajar, and I mentioned to him the hadith of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and I said to him: It was narrated by Shu’bah, and Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes, “this is how he narrated it, but they used to narrate the hadith.” So they will send him, until they are told about him, so they can support him.” I heard Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi, saying: I heard Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi, He says: I said to Yahya bin Ma'in Yunus bin Abi Ishaq: Who is more beloved to you or his son, Israel bin Yunus? He said: “All trust.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2711 - True"
"2712","He narrated to us the hadith of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi, Abu Al-Walid Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Ahmad bin Burd Al-Antaki told us, Al-Haytham told us Ibn Jamil, Issa Ibn Yunus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” This hadith was transmitted on the authority of Abu Ishaq after these, Zuhair bin Muawiyah Al-Ju’fi and Abu Awanah. Al-Wahddah: “The people of transmission have unanimously agreed that they should be preserved and preserved.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2712 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 As for the hadith of Zuhair"
"2713","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz and Abu Al-Hasan bin Mansour told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Abu Al-Azhar told us, Amr bin Othman Al-Raqqi, Zuhair bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” Abu Sa’id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Rumaih al-Nakha’i told me, Ibrahim ibn Nasr al-Kindi told me, he said: I heard Saeed bin Hashim Al-Kaghdhi saying: I heard Ahmad bin Hanbal saying: “If you find the hadith from Zuhayr bin Muawiyah, then do not Go back to someone else, for he is one of the people who has confirmed hadith.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Awanah"
"2714","So Abu Bakr bin Salman Al-Faqih, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Abu Al-Hussein bin Makram, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, they said: Muhammad bin Shadhan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” This is how it was narrated by Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi and Waki’, And others, on the authority of Abu Awanah, and this hadith was transmitted, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, a group of Muslim imams other than those we mentioned among them: Abu Hanifa Al-Numan bin Thabit, Ruqba bin Masqala Al-Abdi, Mutarrif bin Tarif Al-Harithi, and Abdul-Hamid bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali, And Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, and others, “and we mentioned them in the chapter, and a group other than Abu Ishaq transmitted it on the authority of Abu Burdah.”"
"2715","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman told us, the jurist Al-Harith bin Muhammad told us, Al-Hasan bin Qutayba told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, Abu Qutaibah Salim bin Al-Fadl Al-Adami told me in Mecca, Al-Qasim bin Zakaria Al-Muqri told us, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Sabah told us, Asbat bin Nasr, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"
"2716","It was narrated to us by Abu Ali Al-Hafiz. Abu Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Dab’i told us in Baghdad. Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us. Qabisah bin Uqba, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” Ibn Askar said: Then Qabisa bin Uqba said to me: “Ali bin Al-Madini came to me and asked me about this hadith. So I told him about it, and Ali bin Al-Madini said: We have found relief from the dispute with Abu Ishaq. Al-Hakim said: “I do not know among the imams of this knowledge.” There is a disagreement over the justice of Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, and that what he heard from Abu Burdah with his father is authentic. Then he did not disagree with Yunus regarding this connection. The hadith contains clear evidence that the dispute that occurred with his father was on the part of its companions, not on the part of Abu Ishaq, and God knows best. This hadith was transmitted on the authority of Abu Burdah himself and Abu Husayn Othman bin Asim Al-Thaqafi."
"2717","It was narrated to us by Abu Ali Al-Hafiz. Abu Yusuf Yaqoub bin Khalifa bin Hassan Al-Ayli reported about Al-Ayla and Saleh bin Ahmed bin Yunus. And Abu Abbas Al-Azhari, they said: Abu Shaybah bin Abi Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Khaled bin Yazid the doctor told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” We used authentic narrations and the sayings of the imams of knowledge as evidence for the authenticity of the hadith of Abu Musa, including what is rich in it for those who contemplate it. And in the chapter On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, Abdullah bin Abbas, Muadh bin Jabal, Abdullah bin Omar, Abu Dhar al-Ghifari, and Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, Abdullah bin Masoud, Jabir bin Abdullah, Abu Hurairah, Imran bin Husayn, and Abdullah bin Amr, Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with them, are the most authentic, and the narrations about the Prophet’s wives were authentic. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Aisha, Umm Salamah, and Zainab bint Jahsh, may God be pleased with them all."
"2718","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us dictation - in Rajab in the year three hundred and ninety-eight - Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi, and Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, they said: Affan bin Muslim told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Abi Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Ka’b Al-Aslami, said: I was serving the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Oh Rabia, won't you get married? He said: So I said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, I do not want to get married, I do not have anything to support a woman and I do not like to be distracted from you. He said: So he turned away from me, then he said to me after that: “O Rabia, won’t you get married?” He said: So I said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, I do not want to get married, and I do not have anything to support a woman, and I do not like for anything to distract me from you, so I will turn away. On my authority, he said: Then I checked with myself and said: By God, O Messenger of God, you know best what will benefit me in this world and the hereafter. He said: And I say to myself: If he had told me the third time, I would have said: Yes. He said: Then he said to me the third time: “O Rabia, won’t you get married?” He said: So I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, tell me what you want or what you like. He said: “Go to the family of so-and-so, to a neighborhood of the Ansar.If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was lax about them, so say to them: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, extends his greetings to you, and commands you to Marry Rabi’ah so-and-so - a woman from among them -.” He said: So I came to them and told them that. They said: Welcome to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And by the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and by God, the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not return unless he has a need. He said: So honor me. They married me off and treated me kindly, but did not ask me for proof. So I returned sad, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What’s the matter with you?” So I said: O Messenger of God, I came to an honorable people, and they married me off and treated me with honor and kindness, but they did not ask me for proof, so where can I get my friendship? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Buraidah Al-Aslami: “O Buraidah, collect for him the weight of a stone of gold.” He said: So they gathered a weight for him. A nucleus of gold. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take this to them, and say, ‘This is her dowry.’” So I took it to them and said: This is her friendship. He said: They said: It is very good, so they accepted and were satisfied with it. He said: So I said: Where do I come from? He said: So he said: “O Buraida, gather for him a sheep.” He said: So they gathered for him a fat ram.He said: And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Go to Aisha and say: Look at the box in which there is food, and send it with it.” He said: So I came. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and I told her that, and she said: Here is that lump, in which are seven s’a’s of barley, and by God, if it becomes ours Other food. He said: So I took it and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Go with it to them and say: Let this be good for you.” “Bread.” He said: So I went with him and the ram. He said: They accepted the food and said: You rams, be enough for us. He said: And people from Aslam came. So they slaughtered, skinned and cooked. He said: Then we had bread and meat in the morning, so I felt pain and called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2718 - Muslim did not protest against Mubarak
 He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me land, and he gave Abu Bakr land, so we disagreed about the stalk of a palm tree. He said: And the world came. Abu Bakr said: This is within my limit, and I said: No, it is within my limit. He said: Then Abu Bakr said to me a word that I hated and regretted it. He said: Then he said to me: O Rabia, tell me what I told you, so that you can be a retaliator. He said: So I said: No, by God, I am not saying to you anything but good. He said: By God, you will say to me as I told you, until you become a retaliator.Otherwise, I will be hostile to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I said: No, by God, I am not saying anything to you except good. He said: Abu Bakr refused the land, and he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I made I recited it, and some of the people of Islam said: May God have mercy on Abu Bakr, he is the one who said what he said, and may God be pleased with you. He said: So I said: Do you know who This? This is Abu Bakr, this is the second of the two, this one has the gray hair of the Muslims. Beware, he does not turn around when he sees you helping me against him, and he becomes angry. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes and becomes angry because of his anger, and God becomes angry because of their anger and Rabi’ah is destroyed. He said: So they turned away from me. And I set off to recite it until the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and told what had happened. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Rabi’ah, what is the matter with you?” And the friend? He said: So I said like what he said. It was such-and-such, so he said to me: Say: Like what I told you, but I refused to tell him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Yes, so do not say to him like what he said, but say: May God forgive you, O Abu Bakr.” He said: So Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, left while he was He cries, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2719","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told me, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, and the pronunciation is his, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, we told him Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, regarding the saying of God Almighty. God Almighty: {Do not prevent them from marrying their wives} [Al-Baqarah: 232] He said: Ma’qil bin Yasar Al-Muzani told me that it was revealed about him. He said: I was I married a sister of mine to a man, and he divorced her. When her waiting period was over, he came to propose to her. So I said to him: I married you off, and I made bed for you, and I honored you. So you divorced her, then you came to propose to her. No, by God, you will never return to her. He said: He was a good man, and the woman wanted to go back to him. He said: Then God revealed this verse, and I said: “Now I will do it.” O Messenger of God. So I married her to him.” Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: “In this hadith there is clear evidence that God Almighty made the marriage contract To the guardians and not to them, and not to the women, even if they are fixed in the marriage contract.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not Narrated by Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2719 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2720","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman he marries And Layan is for the first one, and any two men who make a sale, it is for the first of them.” Saeed bin Abi Arouba and Saeed bin Bashir followed him. Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Qatada
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2720 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition
 As for the hadith of Saeed bin Abi Arouba:"
"2721","So Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whatever man If two men sell something, it belongs to the first of them, and any woman to whom he marries a loyal man, it belongs to the first of them.”
 As for the hadith of Saeed bin Bashir"
"2722","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, the jurist told us Ubaid bin Sharik, Abu Al-Jamahir told us, Saeed bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If two guardians marry, it is for the first, and if He sold the two equivalents, so it is for the first.” Qatada continued on his narration, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik Al-Humrani"
"2723","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al Ansari told us, Ash’ath bin Abdul Malik told me, on the authority of Al Hassan, on the authority of Samra Radi God has it on his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If a man of amending marriage is married, the first is more deserving.” These are the clear ways that I mentioned for this. The entire text is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2723 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2724","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Jari told us, Dawud bin Qays Al-Farra’ told us, Musa bin Yasar told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Our friendship when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us was ten Awaq: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2724 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2725","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Yazid Al-Adami, the reciter in Baghdad, told us, Abdullah bin Al-Hasan Al-Hashimi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Abi Shaybah told us, And Zuhair bin Harb, they said: Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, Abdullah bin Aoun reported, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Ajafa Al-Sulami, he said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, addressed us and said: Do not exaggerate the dowries of women, for if they were honored in this world, or pious in life... By God, he was the most deserving of you with it, and the most deserving of you was Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. “No woman has given more than twelve uqiyahs from any of his wives.” And one of you becomes jealous of his wife’s friendship, to the point that he creates enmity towards her in himself, and says: I have assigned to you the sweat of a closeness.
 And another thing that you say about someone who was killed in these battles of yours, and died: So-and-so was killed as a martyr, and perhaps he had lost the strength of his animal, and he added His mount is gold and paper, he seeks the world, so do not say that, but say as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed or dies in For the sake of God, he will be in Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, Habib al-Martyr, and Hisham ibn Hassan, Salamah bin Alqamah, Mansour bin Zazan, Awf bin Abi Jamila, and Yahya bin Ateeq. All of these are biographies of novels. Authentic on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin and Abu Al-Ajafa Al-Sulami. His name is Haram bin Hayyan and he is one of the trustworthy ones. “I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub He says: I heard Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Dawri saying: I heard Yahya bin Ma’in saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us: “The name of my father’s lean person is Haram.” This hadith was narrated from a straight narration, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, and Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar.
 As for the hadith of Salem"
"2726","Abu Al-Walid, the jurist, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Quraysh told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Shayban bin Farroukh told us, Issa told us. Ibn Maimun, Salem and Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, addressed the people and said: O people, do not exaggerate the dowry. Women, for if they were honorable, there would be no one among you more deserving of them, nor more deserving of them than “the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. his wives, and I do not give any of his daughters more than twelve uqiyahs, and an uqiyah is forty dirhams, so that is four hundred and eighty A dirham, and that is the most expensive thing that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, possessed. I do not know of anyone who exceeded four hundred dirhams.” It was narrated in Authentic report, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Omar"
"2727","Muhammad bin Muzaffar Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, Sa’id bin Abdul Malik told me Ibn Waqid Al-Harrani, Muhammad Ibn Fudayl Al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said On his authority: “Do not exaggerate in women’s dowries.” He said: He mentioned the hadith, and it was also narrated on the authority of Sa’eed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar."
"2728","Abu Al-Hasan bin Mansour told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najiya told us, Kurdous bin Muhammad Abu Al-Hasan Al-Qaflani told us, Mu’alla bin Abd al-Rahman, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, that Omar bin al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, rose to From his pulpit, he thanked God and praised him, and said: Do not go to extremes in women’s alms, for even if they were honorable in this world, or pious in life, By God, those of you who were most worthy of it were your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “None of his wives or daughters have exceeded twelve ounces, and that “Four hundred and eighty dirhams, an ounce is forty dirhams.” Authentic chains of narrations have been narrated regarding the authenticity of the Commander of the Faithful’s sermon. Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and this chapter for me is collected in a large part, and they did not publish it.”"
"2729","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, the jurist told me, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Mu’afia bin Suleiman Al-Harrani told us, Zuhair told us. Ibn Muawiyah, Abu Ismail Al-Aslami told us that Abu Hazim told him on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I married a woman from the Ansar for eight shekels. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was frightened for her and said: “It is as if you were hewing silver from the width of this mountain. Have you seen it? Is there something in the eyes of the Ansar?” He said: I have seen her. He said: “We have nothing, but we will send you on a mission, and I hope that you will do well.” So he sent him from people to people from Bani He frowned, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a she-camel to be brought to them, and they loaded their belongings on it. He did not throw anything but a little while until it was blessed, so they were satisfied. It spread, and there was not among the people younger than the one who got married, so he came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was lying down in the mosque, and he stood up. He touched his head for fear of waking him up, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up and said: O Prophet of God, indeed, with what you have given us, we would like to He sent him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him his right hand, and took his cloak with his left, and placed it on his shoulders, and started walking until he came to her. So he struck her with the sole of his foot, and by the One in whose hand is Abu Hurairah’s soul, she was after that ahead of the commander, and they encamped in the presence of The enemy, and they kindled fires and surrounded them, so they dispersed against them, and they declared “Allahu Akbar” like one man, and God defeated them and captured some of them. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.” Rather, Muslim narrated from the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ismail, On the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: A man got married, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you just look at her?” This Abu Ismail is Bashir bin Sulaiman, and they all used him as evidence.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2729 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2730","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Saeed, and Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Yahya informed. Bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Hadrad Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He was asking for his help with a woman’s dowry, so he said: “How much did you pay for her dowry?” He said: Two hundred dirhams, and he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you were to scoop a bucket of water, you would not have increased.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2730 - True"
"2731","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa bin Zaid Al-Lakhmi told us, in Tinnis, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, Humaid al-Taweel, and another man, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about what God Almighty said: {And the quintals that are surrounded} [Al Imran: 14] He said: “A quintal is two thousand uqiyahs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2731 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2732","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hassan Al-Harbi told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, he told me Omar bin Tufayl bin Sakhbra Al-Madani, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The most blessed of women are those who have the easiest friendships.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2732 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2733","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Quraysh told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Abu Thawr told us, Ibrahim bin Khalid Al-San’ani told us, Abdullah bin Sufyan told us Musab bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married a man to a woman.” “With an iron ring with a silver lining.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2733 - True"
"2734","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, and Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, Omar ibn Abi Salamah told me, on the authority of his mother, Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Whoever is afflicted with a calamity, let him say: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. O God, I consider my calamity to you, so reward me for it, and replace me with good. Among them: “When Abu Salamah died, I said it, and I made sure that every time I reached the age of 18, he would exchange her for me with something better than her. I said to myself: Who is better than Abu Salamah?” Then I said it, and when her waiting period was over, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to her Omar Ibn Al-Khattab to propose to her, and she said to her son: O Umar, get up and marry the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He married him off, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to her to consummate the marriage with her. She saw him take her daughter Zainab and put her on her lap, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned, and Ammar bin Yasser learned of that. He was her breastfeeding brother, so he came to her and said: Where is this ugly, disgusting woman who had harmed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he took it, went with it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and entered upon her, staring at the sides of the house, and said: “I did not do it.” A slut? He said: Ammar came and took it and took it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, built it and said: “I will not deprive you of anything of what I have given you. So-and-so has two palm trees and two jars, and a cloak stuffed with fibres.” And he said: “If I sell seven for you, I will sell seven for my wives.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2734 - According to Al-Nasa’i’s condition"
"2735","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, and Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, and Ismail bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that Abu Talha, may God be pleased with him, gave a speech Umm Sulaym said: “O Abu Talha, do you not know that your God whom we worship is a tree that grew from the earth, drawn by an Ethiopian, the son of so-and-so. You have converted to Islam, and I do not want any other friendship from you.” He said: Until I look into my matter. He said: So he went, then came and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. She said: “O Anas, marry Abu Talha.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and he has authentic witnesses according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2735 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2736","Abu Amr bin Ismail told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abd al-Warith bin Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith bin Saeed Al-Anbari, my father told me, Harb bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The mother of Sulaym married Abu Talha on his conversion to Islam.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2736 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2737","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Khalil told us, Ali bin Mushahir, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamah bin Qais, that a people came to Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and they said: To him: A man among us married a woman, and did not impose a dowry on her, nor did he take her to him until he died. Abdullah said to them: I was not asked about Since I left the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, there has been nothing more difficult for me than these, so go to someone else. They said: So they disagreed with him for a month, then they said to him at the end of that: Who do we ask if we do not ask you, and you are brothers to the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, is in this country, and we find no one but you. So he said: I will express my opinion about it with the utmost effort, and if it is correct, then it is from God alone, with whom there is no partner. And if it was a mistake, then it is from me, and God and His Messenger are innocent of it. “I see that I should give her a dowry like the dowry of her wives, no deceit or excess, and she shall have inheritance, and she has to pay the waiting period of four months and ten.” He said: This was heard by the people of Ashja’, so they stood up and said: We bear witness that you have decreed something similar. What the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled regarding a woman from among us called Roua’ bint Washiq. He said: Abdullah was never seen more happy about anything than he was. On that day, except by his conversion to Islam, then he said: “O God, if it is right, then it is from You alone, with no partner for You, and if it is wrong, then it is from me, and from Satan. And God and His Messenger are free from it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “I heard Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz, It was said to him: I heard Al-Hasan bin Sufyan saying: I heard Harmala bin Yahya saying: I heard Al-Shafi’i saying: If the hadith of Barwa’ bint Washiq is authentic, I said it. Abu Abdullah said: “If I had attended Al-Shafi’i, may God be pleased with him, I would have met the heads of his companions and said: The hadith has been authentic, so speak of it.” He said Al-Hakim: “Al-Shafi’i only said: If the hadith is authentic, because even if this narration is authentic, the fatwa on it is from Abdullah bin Masoud, and the chain of transmission of the hadith is from a group of people from Ashja’, and our sheikh Abu Abdullah, may God have mercy on him, only ruled that the hadith was authentic because he was trustworthy in it. A man from the Companions, and he is Maqil bin Sinan Al-Ashja’i, and what I mentioned is true.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2737 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2738","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, regarding a man who married a woman, and he died without having intercourse with her, and he did not He stipulates for her, and he said: She is entitled to the dowry in full, she is required to observe the waiting period, and she is entitled to the inheritance. Then Maqil bin Sinan stood up and said: “I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judge him in Barwa’ bint Washiq, may God be pleased with her.” So he began “The hadith is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2738 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2739","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman Al-Muradi told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid told me that Safwan Ibn Sulaym narrated to him, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who It grants a woman that her courtship will be easy, her friendship will be easy, and her ties of kinship will be easy.” Urwa said: “It means that her ties of kinship will be easy.” To give birth.” Urwah said: “And I say on my own terms: Among the first of her bad omen is that she has many infidelities.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2739 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2740","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mal informed me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufaili told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad told us Al-Darawardi, Yazid bin Al-Had told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, about the truthfulness of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Twelve ounces and an inch.” So I said: What is an inch? She said: Half an uqiyah. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2740 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2741","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told me, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Umm Habibah, may God be pleased with her, that she was under Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh. He died in the land of Abyssinia, “so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her to her and gave her four thousand dowries for him, and sent them to the Messenger of God.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2741 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2742","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abu told me Al-Asbagh Abdul Aziz bin Yahya Al-Harrani, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahim Khaled bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said to a man: “Would you like me to marry you to so-and-so?” He said: Yes, and said to the woman: “Do you accept that I marry you to so-and-so?” She said: Yes, so one of them married his friend, and he did not impose a dowry on her, nor did he give her anything, and he was among those who witnessed Al-Hudaybiyyah, and he was among those who witnessed Al-Hudaybiyyah witnessed a share in Khaybar, and when death came to him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married so-and-so to me, and I did not oblige. She had a friend, but I did not give her anything, and I bear witness that I gave her my share in Khaybar as a friend, so she took a share and sold it for a hundred thousand. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best friendship is the easiest.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2742 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2743","Abu Amr bin Ismail told me, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Abd al-Warith bin Abd al-Samad bin Abd told us. Al-Warith Al-Anbari, my father told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The greatest sin in the sight of God is a man who marries a woman, and when he fulfills his need with her, He divorced her and took her dowry, and a man employed a man and took his wages, and another killed an animal in vain. This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2743 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2744","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah told us, And Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, narrating on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he taught us the sermon to a woman: “Praise be to God. We praise Him and seek His help and forgiveness, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of ourselves. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever leads astray There is no guide for him, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” Then he recites three verses: “O you who have believed.” Fear Allah as He deserves to be feared, and do not die except as you have submitted.} [Al Imran: 102], {O people, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul. And He created from it its mate, and dispersed from them many men and women, and fear God, by whom you ask one another, and the relatives. Indeed, God is ever a Watcher over you.} [An-Nisa: 1], {O you who have believed, fear God and speak words of righteousness. He will set right for you your deeds and forgive you your sins. And whoever obeys God And His Messenger, he has won a great victory} [Al-Ahzab: 71] Then he mentions his need.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2744 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2745","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told us, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Siwar, and Muhammad ibn Nu’aym told us, they said: Qutaybah ibn Sa’id told us, Abd told us. Al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was If he gets married, he says: “May God bless you, and bless you, and bring you together in goodness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2745 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2746","Yahya bin Mansour al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Ibn Abi al-Sirri al-Asqalani told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj reported, on the authority of Safwan ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man, one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who Al-Ansar, called Basra, said: I married a virgin woman while she was concealed, so I went in to her, and behold, she was pregnant, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “She gets the dowry for what you have made lawful from her private parts, and the child is your slave, so when she gives birth, flog her.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and there is evidence for it from the hadith of Yahya bin Abi Kathir.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2746 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2747","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, On the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Yazid ibn Nu`aym, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Basra ibn Aktham, that he married a virgin woman, He entered with her and found her pregnant, “so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made her child his slave, and separated them.”"
"2748","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Al-Aswad Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Amer Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Announce the marriage.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2748 - True"
"2749","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahran told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: We transferred a woman from the Ansar to her husband, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace be upon him: “Did you have any fun? “The Ansar love entertainment.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2749 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2750","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Balaj Yahya bin Sulaym said: I said to Muhammad bin Hatib: I married two women, and neither of them had a sound - meaning a tambourine - so Muhammad said May God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The separation between what is permissible and what is forbidden is the sound with the tambourine.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2750 - True"
"2751","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, and Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Abbas informed us Al-Bajli, they said: Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, I heard Abu Ishaq, narrating on the authority of Amir bin Saad, that he said: I was with Thabit bin Wadi’ah and Qardha bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with them, at a wedding, and I heard a voice, so I said: Aren’t you listening? They said: “He permitted singing at a wedding and crying over the dead without mourning.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not They narrate it. “And it was narrated by Sharik bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, with a brief explanation.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2751 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2752","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Omar bin Ja’far Al-Muzani told us, Abu Ghassan Malik bin Ismail told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amir bin Saad, who said: I went to see Qardha bin Ka’b and Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them, at a wedding, and lo Neighbors were singing, so I said: Are you the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people of Badr do this to you? They said: If you want, stay with us, and if you want, go, for “He gave us permission to have fun at the wedding, and to cry at the time of calamity,” he said. Sharik: I think he said - other than Nuh.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2752 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2753","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told me, my father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, On the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard people singing at a wedding of theirs, and he gave her a gift. A ram is being slaughtered in a kennel, and your love is in a club, and he knows what is tomorrow. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one knows what is tomorrow except God.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2753 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2754","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Al-Sadi, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to me, and I apologized to him. So he excused me, then it was revealed to him: {Indeed, We have made lawful for you your wives} [Al-Ahzab: 50] the verse """", and she said: I was not lawful for him. I did not immigrate with him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2754 - True"
"2755","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, the jurist, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us - Sheikh Abu Bakr said: He informed, and Ibn Balawayh said: - Secondly: Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr, Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prepared Fatima, may God be pleased with her, in a khamil, a skin-bag, and a pillow made of human beings stuffed with fiber.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2755 - True"
"2756","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail al-Faqih told us about irrigation, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Nuh bin Yazid al-Muddab told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, she said: “My mother wanted to make me fat. Because I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not accept anything of what she wanted, until she fed me cucumbers and fresh dates, and I became fat on them. “Like the best ghee.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2756 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2757","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he reported Whether one of you is a female slave, or a woman, or an animal, let him take her by the forelock, and invoke blessings, and say: O God, I ask You for its goodness. And the best of what it was created for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil, and the evil of what it was created for. And if it is a camel, let it be taken by the top of its hump. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to what we mentioned from the narration of trustworthy imams, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, and they did not narrate it on the authority of Amr in the two books.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2757 - True"
"2758","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jumhan, on the authority of Safina, that Ali, may God be pleased with them both, added a man and prepared food for him, and said: If we invited the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he would eat with us, So they called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came and saw a bed spread near the house. He came back and Fatima said: Go back and tell him: What? Did he return to you, O Messenger of God? So he went and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not for a prophet to enter a decorated house.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2758 - True"
"2759","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist, told us: Jaafar bin Abi Othman Al-Tayalisi told us, Affan, and Muhammad bin Sinan told us, they said: Hammam told us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of An-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If a man has two wives, and he does not treat them equally, then the Day of Resurrection comes, and his half is fallen.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2759 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2760","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, the jurist told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zanad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said to him: O son of my sister, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He did not favor one of us over the other during his stay with us, and there was rarely a day that he did not go around us, approaching every woman without He will remain with her, until he reaches the one who is on that day and spends the night with her.” Sawda bint Zam’ah said when she said that he should separate from her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of God, my day is for Aisha. Before that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: On that day, God Almighty revealed about her and in Similar ones: {And a woman feared disobedience from her husband} [An-Nisa: 128] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2760 - True"
"2761","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khutami, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, takes an oath and is just and says: “O God, this is my oath regarding what I possess, so do not blame me for what You possess and I do not possess.” Ismail al-Qadi said: “It means the heart. “And this is about justice between his wives.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2761 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2762","Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Qadi told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Abbad bin Abbad told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muadhah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to ask for permission, if it was a day The woman is among us after what was revealed: {She may seek from among them whomsoever she pleases, and give shelter} [Al-Ahzab: 51] to you whomsoever she pleases.” Mu’adhah said, so I said to Aisha: What? What were you saying to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: I used to say that if that was up to me, I would not prefer anyone over myself. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2762 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2763","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, said: I came to Al-Hira and saw them prostrating to a satrap of theirs, so I said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Is it more worthy of him to be prostrated to? So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I came to Al-Hira and saw them prostrating to a satrap of theirs, so you are the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, is more deserving of being prostrated to you. He said: “Do you think that if you passed by my grave, would you prostrate to it?” I said: No, he said: “Do not do it. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded women to prostrate to their husbands, God would not have made “They have a right over them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2763 - True"
"2764","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf, the jurist, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Qaza Suwayd bin Hujayr Al-Bahili, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah Al-Qushayri, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what is the right of the wife of one of us? On him? He said: “That he should feed her when he is fed, and clothe her when he is clothed, and not strike her in the face, nor be obscene, and should not leave her except in the house.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2764 - True"
"2765","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Iyas Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abi Dhabab said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not strike God’s female slaves.” Then Omar came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, tell the women to protect their husbands. So he gave permission to hit them, and many women went around the family of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, complaining about their husbands. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Many women have gone around the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining about their husbands. These are not the best of you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2765 - True"
"2766","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muslim bin Khaled told me Al-Zanji, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Abi Salamah, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married his mother Salamah said to her: “I gave the Negus as a gift a few cups of musk and a suit, and I have never seen him unless he died, and I do not see the gift that was given.” To him, will it be returned? If it is returned to me, is it yours or yours?” So it was as the Negus said: When the gift was returned to him, he gave each of his wives an ounce of that musk, and he gave the rest He led Umm Salamah and gave her the suit, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2766 - The Negro is a denier and Muslim"
"2767","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Rabi’ah bin Uthman told us, about Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Nahar Al-Abdi, and he was one of the companions of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a daughter of his, and he said: O Messenger of God, this is my daughter who has refused to be married. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Obey your father.” She said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not get married until you tell me what the husband’s rights are upon me.” His wife? He said: “The husband’s right over his wife is that if he had an ulcer and she licked it, she would not have fulfilled his right.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2767 - Rather, it is reprehensible. Abu Hatim Rabi’ah said that the hadith is reprehensible."
"2768","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Sukkari in Hamadan told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Arni told us, Sulayman bin Dawud told us. Al-Yamami, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him. She said: O Messenger of God, I am so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so. He said: “I have known you, so what is your need?” She said: My need is for my cousin so-and-so, a worshipper. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have known him.” She said: He is proposing to me, so tell me what The right of the husband over the wife. If it is something I can tolerate, I will marry him. If I cannot tolerate it, I will not marry. He said: “Among the rights of the husband over the wife is that if His nostrils gushed blood and pus, so she licked him with her tongue as long as she had fulfilled his duty. If it were necessary for a human being to prostrate to another human being, I would have ordered A woman is to prostrate to her husband when he enters upon her, because God has favored him over her.” She said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry as long as I remain.” In this world, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2768 - Rather, it is Munkar, Suleiman is weak, and Al-Qasim is truthful. He spoke about it."
"2769","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, the jurist told me Bishr bin Musa, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Left, on the authority of Husayn ibn Muhsin, who said: My aunt told me, she said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding some need, and he said: “What are these harms?” Are you Baal? I said: Yes. He said: “How are you with him?” She said: “I am unable to do anything except what I am unable to do.” He said: “So where are you with regard to him?” It is your Paradise and Hell.” This is how it was narrated by Malik bin Anas, Hammad bin Zaid, and Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, and it is authentic. And they did not take it out
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2769 - True"
"2770","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub and Abu Abdullah Ali bin Abdullah Al-Hakimi told us, saying: Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Bishr told us. Ibn Omar Al-Zahrani, Shuaib bin Ruzaiq Al-Taifi told us, Ata Al-Khorasani told us, on the authority of Malik bin Yakhamir Al-Saskiki, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him On his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to call the call to prayer in her husband’s house.” And he is a hater, and do not go out while he is a hater, and do not obey anyone in him, and do not be rude to him, and do not isolate yourself from his bed, and do not hit him, if he He has been unjust, so let her go to him until she pleases him. If it is him, then good for her and a blessing. May God accept her excuse and make her argument successful, and there is no sin. And if he refused with her consent, then she has conveyed her excuse to God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2770 - Rather, it is objectionable and its chain of transmission is interrupted"
"2771","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Maruzi told us, Ismail Al-Qadi told us, Shadh bin Fayyad told us, Omar bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed. Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not look at a woman who does not “She is grateful for her husband, and she cannot do without him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2771 - True"
"2772","Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, about Mansour, and Al-A'mash, on the authority of Dhar, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, and the word for it is, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, he informed us Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Wael bin Mahanat Al-Saadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O women, give in charity, even if it is from your jewellery, for you will be the majority of the people of Hell.” A woman who was not among the elite of women said: Why, O Messenger of God, are we the majority of the people of Hell? He said: “You curse a lot, and you are ungrateful to your spouse, and whatever is found lacking in religion and opinion is more common for men of authority than in their affairs. Women. They said: What is the deficiency in their religion and opinion? He said: “As for the deficiency in their opinion, the testimony of two women is equivalent to the testimony of a man, and as for the deficiency in their religion, one of them stays as long as she wants.” By God, from day and night you will not prostrate yourself ever prostrately before God.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2772 - True"
"2773","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, about Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of his grandfather, said: Muawiyah wrote to Abd al-Rahman bin Shibl, “Teach the people what you have heard from.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The immoral people are the people of Hell.” They said: O Messenger of God, who are the immoral people? He said: “Women.” They said: O Messenger of God, are they not our mothers, our daughters, and our sisters? He said: “Yes, but when they are given they are not grateful, and when they are tested they are not patient.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2773 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2774","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah By God, on the authority of Iyas bin Abdullah bin Abi Dhabab, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not strike God’s female servants.” Then Omar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, the women have complained about their husbands, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission. To beat them. He said: So seventy women went around the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of them complaining to their husbands. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “These are not the best of you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it. “And it has a witness with an authentic chain of narration.” On the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Abu Bakr
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2774 - True"
"2775","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Saeed bin Kathir bin Ufayr told us, And Sa’id bin Abi Maryam, they said: Al-Layth bin Sa’d told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr. May God be pleased with him. She said: The men were forbidden from hitting women, then they complained about them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he left them alone. He beat them, then said: Tonight, seventy women went around the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of whom were beaten. Yahya said: I calculated Al-Qasim said: Then it was said to them after: “And your best will not be struck.”"
"2776","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Fudayl told us, Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may God be pleased with him, he said: I met my uncle and he had the flag. I said: Where do you want? He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to a man who married his father’s wife after him, and he ordered me to behead him.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” And it has evidence on the authority of Adi bin Thabit and on the authority of Al-Bara’, other than the hadith of Adi bin Thabit"
"2777","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Rabi’ Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ bin Umaylah, who said: I heard Adi bin Thabit, narrating on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, may God be pleased with him, who said: He passed by us. People were leaving, so we said to them: Where are you going? They said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent us to “a man who marries his father’s wife to kill him.”
 As for the hadith of Abu Al-Jahm, on the authority of Al-Bara’"
"2778","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahm, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may God be pleased with him, said: I am going around on camels of mine that went astray during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. While I am going around in Verses: “And behold, I was with carriages and horsemen, and they came and went about,” “So they brought out a man, but they did not ask him, nor did they speak to him, until they struck his neck. When They went and asked about him. They said: He married his father’s wife.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2778 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"2779","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi in Marw, Sa’id bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, and Al-Hasan told us Bin Yaqoub Al-Adl, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, said: Ghaylan bin Salamah Al-Thaqafi converted to Islam and he had ten wives. “So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the “Four.” This is how the early companions of Sa’id narrated it: Yazid bin Zuray’, Ismail bin Aliya, Ghandar, and the memorized imams from The people of Basra, and Imam Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj ruled “that this hadith is from what they were concerned about while living in Basra,” so if it was narrated by him He was trustworthy outside the Basra community. We judged him to be valid. I found Sufyan al-Thawri, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi, and Issa bin Yunus. Three of them were Kufans, and they narrated it on the authority of Muammar.
 As for the hadith of Al-Thawri"
"2780","So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, they said: We are Ali bin Abdul Aziz, we are Abu Ubaidah, Yahya bin Saeed On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that Ghailan bin Salamah converted to Islam and had ten wives. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to choose four of them.”
 As for the hadith of the warriors
 So Ismail bin Ahmad Al-Tajer told us, Ali bin Ahmad bin Al-Hussein Al-Ijli told us, Muhammad bin Tarif told us, Al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that Ghailan bin Salamah converted to Islam and had ten wives during the pre-Islamic era. They converted to Islam with him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Choose four of them.”
 As for the hadith of Jesus"
"2781","So Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: Ghailan bin Salamah Al-Thaqafi, who has ten wives, converted to Islam. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to convert to Islam. May God bless him and grant him peace, that he should choose four of them and leave the rest of them.” And this is how I found the hadith among the people of Al-Yamamah on the authority of Ma’mar."
"2782","Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to me, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Sulaiman narrated to me, that Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Yunus narrated to them, my father narrated to me, narrated to me Omar bin Yunus, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: Ghailan bin Salamah Al-Thaqafi embraced Islam. He has eight wives, “so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to choose four of them.” And this is how I found the hadith among the imams. Khorasani on the authority of Muammar
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2782 - Ahmed bin Muhammad is a liar"
"2783","Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Maruzi told me in Bukhara, Abdullah bin Mahmoud Al-Saadi told me, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Khallal told us, Al-Fadl told us Bin Musa, narrated to us by Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that Ghailan bin Salamah Al-Thaqafi converted to Islam, and he has ten wives. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to retain four and separate the rest of them.” What my effort leads to is that Muammar bin Rashid narrated He sent it on his behalf in both directions: he sent it once, and he received it once, and the evidence for this is that those who conveyed it on his behalf were from the people of Basra, so they sent him as well. Reaching is more important than sending, because increasing trust is acceptable, and God knows best.”"
"2784","Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Taymi told us, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Yazid bin Zurai’, Habib Al-Mu’allim told us, he said: A man from the people of Kufa came to Amr bin Shuaib and said: Is it not surprising that Al-Hasan says: “The adulterer A flogged man will only marry a flogged woman like him.” Amr said: “What do you like?” Sa`id al-Maqbari told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “And Abdullah bin Amr used to proclaim it.” This hadith The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2784 - True"
"2785","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, I am Abu Al-Muthanna, na Musaddad, na Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that a Muslim man asked the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to visit a woman, called The mother of Mahrul was fornicating and required that he spend on him, and he asked the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to do so, and her matter was mentioned to him. “So he recited The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {The adulterer shall not marry anyone except an adulteress or a polytheist} [An-Nour: 3] And it was revealed: {No adulterer shall be married except an adulterer or A polytheist} [An-Nour: 3] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2785 - True"
"2786","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub informed us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, and Abd al-Samad bin Hassan told us, they said: We told us: Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {The adulterer does not marry anyone except An adulteress or a polytheist} [An-Nur: 3] He said: “But it is not marriage, but rather intercourse. No one commits adultery with her except an adulterer or a polytheist.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2786 - True"
"2787","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, he said: It was read to Abd al-Malik bin Muhammad while I was listening. Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, he told me My father, Al-Qasim bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If a slave marries without his master’s permission, he is a prostitute.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2787 - True"
"2788","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Ghassan told us, they said: A partner told us, on the authority of Abu Rabi’ah. Al-Ayyadi, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali, may God be pleased with him: “O Ali, do not follow “A look at a look, for you have the first, but you do not have the last.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s condition, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2788 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2789","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih informed us, Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufaili told us, Miskin ibn Bukair, told us by Shu`bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a campaign, and he saw a woman with hair loss, and he said: “Perhaps her companion was hurt by her.” They said: Yes. He said: “I was about to curse him with a curse that would go with him into his grave. How could he leave it as an inheritance when it was not permissible for him, and how could he use it when it was not permissible for him? “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2789 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2790","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jdi told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Qais bin Wahb, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said that he said regarding female captives: “A pregnant woman shall not have intercourse until she gives birth, nor a pregnant woman until she has menstruated.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2790 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2791","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi told us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Al-Asbagh Abd Al-Aziz bin Yahya Al-Harrani, Muhammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: Ibn Umar, and God will forgive him, and they were only this neighborhood from the Ansar, and they are the people of an idol, along with this neighborhood from The Jews, who were People of the Book, saw that they were superior to them, so they used to imitate many of their actions, and it was the matter of the people of The Book is that they should not have sexual intercourse with women except in one instance, and that is the most concealing of what a woman is, so this neighborhood was among the Ansar, they took This is what they did, and this group of Quraysh used to explain themselves to women in a disgusting manner, and they took pleasure from them, whether they came or went back. And lying down. When the immigrants came to Medina, a man among them married a woman from the Ansar, and he went to do that to her. So she rebuked him and said: We were only being brought to one place, so do that. Otherwise, avoid me until their matter is resolved. Then he reached that point. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “So God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: {Your women are your crops, so come to your fields wherever you wish} [Al-Baqarah: 223] “i.e. “The places facing the child, the ones facing the back, and the ones lying down, meaning that is the place of the child.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this. Driving. They only agreed on the hadith of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir in this matter. “This is the last [p. 214] book of marriage.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2791 - According to Muslim’s condition
 Divorce letter In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful"
"2792","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abdullah bin Al-Ma’mal told us, On the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, that Abu Al-Jawza came to Ibn Abbas and said: Do you know that three people used to frequent the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He turned to one woman and said: “Yes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2792 - Ibn Al-Mu’mil declared it weak"
"2793","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed me, Ibn Tawus informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Divorce occurred during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and two years of Omar’s caliphate, the divorce of three is one.” Omar said: “The people have been hasty in a matter. There is patience in it, so if We spend it on them, he will spend it on them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2793 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2794","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Marouf bin Wasil told us, On the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has not permitted anything “More hateful to him than divorce” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and one of the rulings of this hadith is that it begins with it in the book of divorce.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2794 - After Al-Hakim corrected the hadith according to Muslim’s condition"
"2795","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Issa, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Yamar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not “Among us is he who turns a woman against her husband, or a slave against his master.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2795 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2796","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Issa ibn al-Sakan al-Wasiti informed us, Amr told us Ibn Aoun, narrated by Hushaym, Humayd reported on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, divorced Hafsa, he ordered that He reviewed it, so he reviewed it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2796 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2797","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Khidr bin Aban Al-Hashimi told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, On the authority of Salih bin Salih, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divorced Hafsa and then took her back.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2797 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2798","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Asadi, al-Hafiz in Hamdan, informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi told us A wolf, my uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with them both, he said: It was I had a woman whom I loved, and Omar hated her, so Omar said, “Divorce her,” but I refused. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Obey.” He left your father and divorced her.” So I divorced her. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman is the son of my father.” Dhubab Al-Madani, the maternal uncle of Ibn Abi Dhib, they all used him as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2798 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2799","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail told us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that a man came to Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, and said: My mother did not stay with me until I got married. She ordered me to divorce her, but she refused me to do otherwise, so he said: “I am not the one who commanded you to disobey your mother, nor am I the one who commanded you to disobey your mother.” You may divorce your wife, but if you wish, I can tell you what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The father is the center of the gates of Paradise. So keep that door if you wish, or leave it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2799 - True"
"2800","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Habib, that he heard Ataa Ibn Abi Rabah, saying: Yusuf Ibn Mahik told me, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, speaking, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he heard him say: “There are three things that are very serious and serious in their humor: marriage, divorce, and taking them back.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, and this Abd al-Rahman bin Habib is Ibn Ardak, one of the trustworthy ones of the Medinans, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2800 - There is Lin in it, meaning Abd al-Rahman bin Habib bin Ardak"
"2801","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, and Abu Al-Abbas told us, other than Once, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Ayyub bin Suwayd told us, they said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has overlooked my nation’s mistakes and forgetfulness, and they have not been forced to do so.” Accordingly, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2801 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2802","Professor Imam Abu Al-Walid Hassan bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, My father, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Abi Salih, who said: Adi bin Adi sent me to Safiya bint Shaybah, I ask her about things she used to narrate about Aisha, and she said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, told me that she heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “There is no divorce and no emancipation in the event of closure.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “And Abu continued Safwan the Umayyad Muhammad ibn Ishaq, based on his narration, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, but Muhammad ibn Ubaid was omitted from the chain of transmission
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2802 - According to Muslim’s condition, he said, meaning Al-Hakim. I said, “And Muhammad bin Ubaid,” and Muslim did not use him as evidence, and Abu Hatim said, “weak.”"
"2803","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Nuaym bin Hammad told us, Abu Safwan Abdullah bin Saeed told us. The Umayyad, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Safiya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “No Divorce and no emancipation in a closed state”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2803 - Naeem is the owner of evil deeds"
"2804","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi informed us, Abu Zakaria Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Saleh ibn Safwan informed us. Al-Sahmi in Egypt, Abi told us, he said: I heard Al-Layth bin Saad, in the Jami’ Mosque, saying: Abu Musab Musharrah bin Ha’an said, Uqba said Ibn Amer Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Shall I not tell you about the borrowed goat?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “It is permissible, so God cursed the one who made it permissible,” and then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “May God’s curse be upon him.” “The one who is made lawful, and the one for whom the one is made lawful.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Abu Salih, the writer of Al-Layth, mentioned on the authority of Layth that he heard it from “Mishrah Ben Haaan”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2804 - True"
"2805","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mil bin Al-Hasan told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Abu Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: I heard Musharrah bin Haaan, speaking on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you? With a borrowed goat? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “He is the permissible.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse the permissible and the one for whom it is permissible.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"2806","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad bin Mutarrif told us Al-Madani, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, that he said: A man came to Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, and asked him about a man who divorced his wife. Thirdly, a brother of his married her, without a conspiracy on his part, to make her permissible for his brother. Is it permissible for the first? He said: “No, marriage is a desire. We used to consider this to be incest during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2806 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2807","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told me in Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim told me, on the authority of Abu Ezra, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told me, Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Yazid bin Rukana, on the authority of his grandfather Rukana bin Abdul Yazid, may God be pleased with him On his authority: He divorced his wife permanently during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. He said: “What did you mean by that?” He said: I wanted one. He said: “By God?” He said: By God. He said: “It is what you wanted.” The two sheikhs deviated from Al-Zubayr bin Saeed Al-Hashimi in the two Sahihs, “but this hadith has a continuation of “The daughter of Rukana bin Abd Yazid al-Muttalabi,” so the hadith is authentic.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2807 - He has deviated in the two Sahihs from Al-Zubayr bin Saeed, but he has a follower through whom the hadith is authentic."
"2808","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told me, my uncle Muhammad bin Ali bin told me. Shafi’, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Ujayr bin Abd Yazid, that Rukana bin Abd Yazid divorced his wife Suhayma completely, then the Messenger of God came May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “I have divorced my wife Suhayma completely, and by God, I only wanted one.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned her to him. He greeted her.” He divorced her a second time, in the time of Omar, and a third in the time of Uthman, may God be pleased with them. “The hadith has been authenticated by this narration, for Imam Al-Shafi’i mastered it, and he preserved it from his family, and Al-Sa’ib bin Abd Yazid Abu Al-Shafi’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who was Rukana’s brother. Ibn Abd Yazid, and Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Shafi’i, the uncle of Al-Shafi’i, the sheikh of Quraysh in his time.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2808 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2809","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Which “A woman asked her husband for a divorce without any objection. God forbade her from enjoying the scent of Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2809 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2810","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A woman converted to Islam during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So she got married, and her husband came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I had converted to Islam with her, and she learned of my conversion to Islam with her. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, removed her from her other husband and returned her to her first husband.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They narrate it: “And it is of the type that I say: Al-Bukhari cited Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim cited Samak.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2810 - True"
"2811","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned his daughter Zainab to her husband, Abu Al-Aas. Ibn al-Rabi’ with the first marriage, but nothing happened.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2811 - True"
"2812","Ahmed Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told me about Marw, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, Ibn Al-Had told me, Amr bin Abdullah bin Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, his daughter Zainab left Mecca with Kinana - or Ibn Kinana - so they went out after her, and Habbar ibn Al-Aswad caught up with her and continued stabbing her camel with his spear, until She struck her, and she vomited what was in her stomach and shed blood, so Banu Hashim and Banu Umayyah quarreled over her, so Banu Umayyah said: We have more right. There, and she was with their cousin Abu Al-Aas, so she was with Hind bint Utbah ibn Rabi’ah, and Hind used to say to her: This Because of your father. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Zaid bin Haritha: “Will you not go and bring me Zainab?” He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Take my ring.” So he gave it to him, and Zaid went off and blessed his camel. He continued to be gentle, until he met a shepherd, and he said: Who do you care for? He said: To Abi Al-Aas, so he said: Who are these sheep? He said: To Zainab, the daughter of Muhammad, so he walked with him about something, then said to him: May I give you something that you can give to her and not mention to anyone? He said: Yes, so he gave him the ring. So the shepherd went and let his sheep in and gave them the ring. She recognized it and said: Who gave you this? He said: A man. She said: Where did you leave him? He said: In such-and-such place. He said: So she remained silent until, when night came, she went out to him. When she came to him, he said to her: Ride before me on his camel. She said: No, but you ride in front of me. So he rode and I rode after him until she came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was saying: “She The best of my daughters was harmed by me.” This was reported to Ali bin Al-Hussein, so he went to Urwa and said: There is no hadith that I have heard from you that you speak of that detracts from the truth. Fatima? He said: “By God, I do not like to own anything between the East and the West, and I deprive Fatima of a right that is hers. Now, it is up to you not to I will never speak of it.” Urwah said: “This was only before the revelation of the verse: {Call them by their fathers. It is more equitable in the sight of God} [Al-Ahzab: 5] “This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"2813","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil ibn Khalaf al-Qadi informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Nahham informed us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marudhi informed us, Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When Hilal bin Umayyah slandered his wife, he was told: By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will flog you with eighty lashes. He said: God is more just than that, that He strike me with eighty lashes, and He knew that I saw until I was certain, and I heard until I was certain, no. God will never hit me. Then the cursed verse was revealed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called them both when the verse was revealed, and said: “God knows that one of you is a liar. Is there anyone among you who repents?” Hilal said: “By God, I am telling the truth.” He said: “I swear by God, there is no god but Him, that I am telling the truth.” He said that. Four times. If I am lying, then the curse of God is upon me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Stop it at the fifth, for it is obligatory.” So she swore, then said four times: By God, besides whom there is no god, he is one of the liars, and if he is truthful, then the wrath of God is upon her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Stop it at five o’clock, for it is positive.” She hesitated and was about to confess. Then she said: I will not expose it. Get up. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If she brings it with kohl, edging, reaching the buttocks, edging the thighs, edging the legs, then it is for the one who She threw it with it, and if she brought it yellow, striking a tribe, then it belongs to Hilal ibn Umayyah. So she brought it with the description al-Baghih. Ayoub said: And he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin: “The man who informed Hilal ibn Umayyah was Sharik ibn Sahma’, and he was the brother of Al-Bara’ ibn Malik, the brother of Anas ibn Malik to his mother, and his mother was black, and Sharik used to go to Hilal’s house and stay with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and it was not They narrated it in this context, but they narrated the hadith of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ikrimah, in brief.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2813 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2814","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, about Yazid. Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Yunus, that he heard Al-Maqbari narrating, saying: Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me that he heard the Prophet praying May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: When the cursed verse was revealed, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman who enters upon a people who is not among them, She is not from God in anything, and God will not admit her into Paradise, and any man who denies his son while he is looking at him, God will withhold from him and expose him to “The heads of creation, from the first and the last.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2814 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2815","Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Ya`qub ibn Yusuf al-Adl informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad informed us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr Ibn Ata, on the authority of Sulaiman Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Salama Ibn Sakhr Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, he said: I was I have been given a woman in terms of intercourse with women that no one else has been given. When Ramadan came, I separated from my wife, for fear that I might catch something from her some night. And I continue from that, and I cannot leave until dawn overtakes me, while one night she serves me, if something of her is revealed to me. So I remained firm on her, and when the morning rose, I went to my people and told them my news, and I said: Go with me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: No, by God, we will not go with you. We fear that the Qur’an will be revealed about us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will say something about us that will remain upon us. It is her disgrace, so go and do what you want. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him my news, and he said: “Are you that?” So I said: I am that person, so judge according to the judgment of God, for I am patient and seeking reward. He said: “Free a slave.” So I struck the back of his neck with my hand, so I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never been in possession of anything else. He said: “Fast for two consecutive months.” So I said: O Messenger of God, did what happened to me happen to me except during fasting? He said: “Feed sixty poor people.” I said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, we spent the night deprived and could not find dinner. He said: “Go to the one who gave the charity, the charity of Banu Zurayk, and let him give it to you, so feed sixty poor people with a large sized meat of it, and seek help from all of it.” “On your children.” So I came to my people and said: “I found distress among you,” “This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” And it has a witness from a hadith. Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, except that he said: Salman bin Sakhr,
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2815 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2816","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, and Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, that Salman bin Sakhr Al Ansari, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he placed his wife on him like his mother’s back, then he mentioned the hadith similarly to him, “This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2816 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2817","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni told us, Al-Hakam bin He stated, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he had intercourse with his wife, so he fell On her, and he said: O Messenger of God, I had sexual intercourse with my wife, and she had sexual intercourse with her before I could make amends. He said: “What made you do that, may God have mercy on you?” He said: I saw her anklet in the moonlight. He said: “Do not approach her until she has done what God Almighty has commanded.” This was witnessed by the hadith of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, “and he did not provide evidence.” The two sheikhs are named by Ismail, nor by Al-Hakam bin Aban, except that Al-Hakam bin Aban is truthful.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2817 - Al-Adani is not trustworthy"
"2818","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Ammar bin Khaled told us, and Muhammad bin Muawiyah told us, they said: Ali bin Hisham told us, we told him Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man had intercourse with his wife, He saw her anklet in the moonlight, and he liked it, so he fell on it. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said: God Almighty said And Glorious is He: {Before they touched each other} [Al-Mujadila: 3] And He said: That was it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Abstain until you expiate.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2818 - Ismail Wah"
"2819","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, Ata told me, Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “There is no divorce for the one who does not own property, and there is no emancipation for the one who does not own.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the famous hadith in the chapter on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2819 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2820","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi narrated to us, Muslim bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Husayn Al-Mu’allim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, and Ali told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Amer Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Amr Bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no divorce before marriage.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2820 - True
 And in the hadith of Hushaym: “There is no vow for the son of Adam regarding what he does not possess, no divorce regarding what he does not possess, and no emancipation regarding what he does not possess.”"
"2821","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, on the authority of a brother, Al-Hussein bin Waqid and Abu Hamza all reported, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Ibn Masoud did not say it, and if he did say it, then it is a mistake on the part of a scholar about the man. He says: “If I marry so-and-so, she is divorced. God Almighty said: {O you who have believed, when you marry believing women and then divorce them} [Al-Ahzab: 49] And He did not say: When you divorced believing women. Then you married them, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2821 - True"
"2822","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Mazhar bin Aslam, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The divorce of a female slave is two divorces. And her period is two menstruation.” Abu Asim said: So I mentioned it to Mazhahir bin Aslam, and I said: Tell me as you told Ibn Jurayj, so Mazhahir told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The divorce of a female slave is two divorces, and her period is two menstrual periods,” such as It was narrated by Mazhahir bin Aslam, a sheikh from the people of Basra. None of our previous sheikhs mentioned it in a negative light. So the hadith is authentic, and it is not They take it out, and a hadith was narrated on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that contradicts it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2822 - True"
"2823","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, he told me Yahya bin Abi Kathir said that Omar bin Mu’tab told him that Abu Hassan was a client of Banu Nawfal. He told him that he had asked Ibn Abbas for a fatwa regarding A mamluk, there was a slave under him, so he divorced her twice, then emancipated her. After that, is it right for him to propose to her? He said: “Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that.”
 [p. 224]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2823 - The hadith of Ali opposes it"
"2824","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid, he said: I said to Ayoub: Do you know anyone who says that the good deed in your affairs is in your hand, that it is three? He said: No, except for something that Qatadah narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir, the servant of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly, Ayoub said: Then a lot of people came to us and asked him, and he said: I have never narrated this. So I mentioned it to Qatada, and he said: “Yes, but he forgot.” This is a strange and authentic hadith, from the hadith of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, and I mentioned it in the chapter on marriage. Without a guardian, the names of a group of trustworthy hadith scholars, from the Companions, the Successors, and their followers, who narrated the hadith and then forgot it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2824 - Sahih Gharib"
"2825","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzaz told me, in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Abi Uthman al-Tayalisi told us, Ali bin Bahr bin Barri told us, Hisham bin Yusuf, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: The wife of Thabit bin Qais was removed from him, “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made her waiting period a menstrual period.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, except that Abd al-Razzaq sent it, on the authority of “A long time ago”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2825 - Sahih narrated by Abd al-Razzaq on the authority of Muammar, mursal"
"2826","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Muslim, on the authority of Ikrimah, that the wife of Thabit ibn Qays had a khula from him, “so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made her waiting period a menstrual period.”"
"2827","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Hatim told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Muhib, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she wanted to free a husband from two Mamluks, so she asked the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “So he commanded her to start with the man before the woman.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2827 - This Ubayd Allah differed regarding its authentication and they did not produce it."
"2828","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jafar, my father told me, Rafi’ bin Sinan, may God be pleased with him, told me that he converted to Islam, but his wife refused to convert to Islam, so she came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, so my daughter said: Fatim, and Rafi’ said: My daughter. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Rafi’: “Sit on the side.” And he said to his wife: “Sit on the side,” and he said: And the girl sat between them, then he said: “Call her.” So the girl leaned toward her mother, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, guide her.” So she leaned toward her father, and this man took her. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2828 - True"
"2829","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Khalil, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when a man came to him From the people of Yemen, he said: Three of the people of Yemen came to Ali, may God be pleased with him, to dispute with him regarding a child, and they fell upon a woman who was in purity. One of them said to the two of them: This is a good child, and they said: No. Then he said to the two: “This is a good child.” They said: “No.” Then he said to the two: This is a good child, and they said: No. Then he said: You are quarreling partners. I will cast lots among you, so whoever cast lots will get the child, and he must pay his two companions two-thirds of the blood money. So he cast lots among them. So he gave it to the one who knocked.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his molars - or he said: his molars - appeared. “The two sheikhs had agreed to leave Al-Ajlah bin Abdullah Al-Kindi used as evidence, and we only criticized him for one hadith from Abdullah bin Buraidah, and he followed him on that. The hadith is three trustworthy, so this hadith is authentic, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2829 - This hadith is therefore authentic"
"2830","Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told me, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, Abu told me Amr Al-Awza’i, Amr bin Shuaib told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, that a woman said: Oh Messenger of God, this is my son. My belly was a vessel for him, my breasts were his watering hole, and my stone was his Eve, but his father divorced me and wanted to take him away. About me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “You have more right to him as long as you do not get married.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2830 - True"
"2831","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abu Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: My aunt was divorced three times, so she went out to harvest her palm trees, but a man met her and forbade her. So she came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and mentioned that to him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Go out and fight, perhaps you will give alms from him, or “Do good.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2831 - Narrated by Ahmad in Al-Musnad according to Muslim’s condition"
"2832","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Abu Al-Numan Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, and Suleiman bin Harb told us, They said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, Ishaq bin Saad bin Ka’b bin Ujrah told us, Zainab bint Ka’b told me, on the authority of Furay’ah bint Malik, that Her husband went out to seek treatment for him, and he was killed at the edge of the entrance - Hammad said: It was a place of water - She said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I mentioned this to him about my situation, and I mentioned to him the transfer to my brothers. She said: So he granted me permission, and when I had passed, he called me and said: “Stay in your house until The book will reach its term.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2832 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2833","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, he told us Yahya bin Saeed said that Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah told him that his paternal aunt Zainab bint Ka’b bin Ujra told him that she I heard Furay’ah bint Malik, the sister of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, say: My husband went out in search of a slave of his, but he overtook them on the way and they killed him. Then his obituary came to me, and I was in a large house like my family’s. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My husband’s obituary came to me, and I am in A house as large as my family's, and he did not leave me any maintenance or money, and the house is not mine, and if I had turned to my brothers and family, he would have been kinder to me in some ways. My business. He said: “Come.” When I went out to the mosque or the room, he called me, or he ordered me to be called for him, and he said: “Stay in the house where an obituary came to you.” Your husband until the prescribed period has been fulfilled.” So she observed the waiting period for four months and ten days. She said: Then Uthman bin Affan sent for me, and I went to him. So I narrated it to him and he took it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration from both sides, and he did not narrate it. It was narrated by Malik bin Anas in Al-Muwatta’, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Kaab bin Ujrah. Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli said: This is an authentic and preserved hadith. They are two Saad bin Ishaq Ibn Ka'b, who is the most famous of them, and Ishaq Ibn Sa'd Ibn Ka'b, and Yahya Ibn Sa'id Al-Ansari narrated from them all. ""Foolishness about them all.""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2833 - True"
"2834","Abu Hafs Ahmad bin Uhaid al-Faqih informed me of Bukhara from the origin of his book. Abu Ali Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Ali told us Bin Hakim Al-Awdi, Sharik told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Amer, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: A woman was divorced, stayed for twenty-three nights, and she gave birth. Then she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said to her: “Get married.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2834 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2835","Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating, in Dhul-Qa’dah in the year three hundred and ninety-eight. He reported Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us: Hashim bin Yunus Al-Assar told us in Egypt, Ali bin Ma’bad told us, Abu Al-Malih told us Al-Ruqiy, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Qasim narrated to me, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, that she was under the rule of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and she hated him. He was harsh towards women, so she said to Al-Zubayr: O Abu Abdullah, grant me a divorce. She said: That was when she found divorce. He said: What is the benefit to you if I divorce you once and then take you back? She said: I find myself enjoying that. He said: So he divorced her once and then left. She said to her maid: Close the doors. He said: So a slave girl gave birth, and he said: Then Al-Zubayr came and gave her the good news, and he said: The daughter of Abu Mu’it plotted against me, then he went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello and it was mentioned to him, “so he made it clear of him.” This is a strange hadith with a sound chain of narration, and Abu Al-Malih, and if they did not take it out then he is not accused. By the situation, he was the imam of the people of the peninsula in his time, and Umm Kulthum was the daughter of Uqba bin Abi Muayt, and she is the one about whom he narrates. Her son, Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is not a liar who makes peace between people.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2835 - Sahih Gharib"
"2836","Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Hairi told me, Muhammad bin Amr bin Al-Nadr Al-Jurashi told me, Abdullah bin Abi Salamah told me, Abd told me Al-A'la bin Abdul-A'la, Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Raja' bin Haywa, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Abi Dhu'ayb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas Radi God, on his authority, said: “Do not distort for us the Sunnah of our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding the child’s mother when her master dies, her waiting period. “Four months and ten.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2836 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2837","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr Al-Tanisi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir Al-Kala’i, Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, told me: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “While I I was sleeping, when two men came to me, took my hyena, and brought me to a rugged mountain, and said to me: Go up. I said: I can't stand it. They said: We will make it easy for you. So I ascended until I was at the top of the mountain when I heard loud noises. I said: What are these sounds? They said: This is the howling of the people of Hell. Then he set off with me, and saw a people hanging by their ankles, with their jaws split open, and their jaws flowing. Blood, so I said: Who are these? He said: These are the ones who break their fast before the end of their fast. Then they set off with me, and behold, there were people with a very bad smell and a foul odor. And the worst sight, so I said: Who are these people? He said: These are adulterers and harlots. Then he set off with me, and behold, I saw women whose breasts were being bitten by snakes, so I said: What is the matter with these? He said: These are the ones whose children withhold their milk. Then he set off with me and saw two boys playing between two rivers, and I said: Who are these? He said: These are the descendants of the believers. Then an honor came over me when I saw three people drinking from their wine. I said: Who are these? He said: These are Jafar bin Abi Talib, Zayd bin Haritha, and Abdullah bin Rawaha. Then another honor came over me, so I found myself with three A group of people. I said: Who are these people? He said: Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, peace be upon them, are waiting for you. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari protested.” All of its narrators are anyone other than Sulaym bin Amir, and Muslim has cited him as evidence.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2837 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2838","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Abu Thabit Zaid told me Ibn Ishaq bin Ismail bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Qays bin Shammas, Ismail bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Qays bin Shammas told me, on the authority of His father, Muhammad, said that his father, Thabit bin Qais, left Jamila bint Abdullah bin Ubayyi, who was pregnant with Muhammad, so when she gave birth to him, she swore not to She milked him from her milk, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for him, spit in his mouth, and rubbed his mouth with an Ajwa date, and named him Muhammad, and said: “Disagree with him, for God has provided for him.” So I went to him on the first, second, and third day, when an Arab woman asked about Thabit ibn Qais, so I said: What do you want from him? I am Thabit. She said: I saw this in my dream as if I was breastfeeding a son of his, who is called Muhammad. He said: So I am Thabit, and this is my son Muhammad. He said: And her breastplate is being squeezed by her milk. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2838 - True"
"2839","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Al-Hasan bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told me, Masoud told us, Shibl bin Abbad told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, he said: Ataa said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: “This verse was abrogated, her waiting period with her family, so she can observe the waiting period wherever she wants. And it is the Almighty’s saying {without taking it out} [Al-Baqarah: 240] “Ata’ said: “If she wishes, she may stay in the Iddah with her family, and she may reside in her will, and if she wishes It came out due to the words of God Almighty: {There is no blame on you for what they did} [Al-Baqarah: 234] “Ata’ said: “Then inheritance came and residency was abrogated, so she should observe the waiting period wherever She wanted.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2839 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"2840","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Muhammad bin al-Faraj al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: And Ibn Jurayj, Abu Al-Zubayr told us that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: A poor man came to meet some Ansar, and he said: “My master is forcing me to Prostitution, so it was revealed about that: {And do not force your young women into prostitution} [An-Nour: 33] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2840 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"2841","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakra Bakkar bin Qutaybah, the judge in Egypt, told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Hisham bin Abdullah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais Al-Judhami, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees “And God has freed each of its members from the fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And it has a witness on the authority of Ubayy.” Musa Al-Ash'ari and Wathilah bin Al-Asqa'
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2841 - True
 As for the hadith of Abu Musa"
"2842","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel, Adam bin Abi Iyas Al-Asqalani told us, and Abdullah bin Al-Zubair. Al-Humaidi, and Ibrahim bin Bashar al-Ramadi, they said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us. A sheikh from the people of Kufa, called Shu’bah, told me: We were With Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, and his sons with him, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that my father narrated to me? They said: Yes, father, so he told us. He said: My father told me, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever frees a slave - or a slave - His redemption was from the fire, limb by limb.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2842 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 As for the hadith of Wathilah"
"2843","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Ahmad bin Al-Faraj told us, Damrah bin Rabi’ah told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Abla told us, On the authority of Al-Arif bin Al-Daylami, he said: We came to Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him, and we said: Narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, there is no addition or subtraction in it, so he became angry and said: One of you’s Qur’an is hanging in his house, and he adds and subtracts. He said: So we said: This is not what we wanted. We wanted you to tell us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding a friend of ours who made it obligatory - meaning - the Fire, and he said: “Free him from it. God will free every part of him from the Fire.” Arif This is a nickname for Abdullah bin Al-Dailami.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2843 - True"
"2844","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Firas Al-Faqih told us that what I mentioned was true, Bakr bin Suhail Al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Abdullah bin Salem, Ibrahim bin Abi Abla told me, he said: I was sitting in Jericho, and Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ passed by me, leaning on Abd. Allah bin Al-Daylami, so he made him sit, then he came to me and said: It is strange that this sheikh, meaning Wathila, did not speak to me. I said: What happened to you? He said: He told me that I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Battle of Tabuk, and a group of Banu Sulaym came to him and said: O Messenger of God, Our friend has made it obligatory. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Free him from Hell. With every part of it, God will free a part of himself from the Fire.” So it became A strong hadith with these narrations is authentic, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Muslim quoted from the hadith of Abu Hurairah his statement regarding the emancipation of a Muslim man. ""a Muslim woman""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2844 - True"
"2845","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Ayyub bin Suwayd told us, Ibrahim bin Abi told us Abla, on the authority of Abd al-A’la bin al-Dailami, on the authority of Wathilah bin al-Asqa’, heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever frees a Muslim, “His redemption from the Fire will be with every part of this, every part of this.” This Abdul-Ala is also Abdullah bin Al-Daylami, without a doubt. As we said in Arif."
"2846","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, that he heard Abu Habiba, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, narrated to us Abu Nu`aym and Abu Hudhayfah said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Habiba al-Tai, who said: My brother recommended to me a group of His money, so I met Abu Darda and said: My brother has bequeathed to me a group of his money, so where should I put it? Among the poor, the needy, or the immigrants? He said: As for me, if I had not treated the mujahideen justly, then I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The example of one who is freed upon death is like the example of one who is freed upon death. “He who guides when he is full.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Thawri. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2846 - True"
"2847","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, and Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, They said: Ya`la bin Ubaid al-Tanafisi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Maimuna, may God be pleased with her, said: I freed a maid of mine, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to me, and I informed him of her emancipation, and he said: “As for you “If you had given it to your maternal uncles, your reward would have been greater.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2847 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2848","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Abu Amer Saleh bin Rustum told us, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad, the servant of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, and he was Saad belonged to him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, admired his service, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Abu Bakr, Free Saad.” He said: O Messenger of God, we have no other choice. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The men came to you, the men came to you.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2848 - True"
"2849","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa told us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa`id told us, Sa`id ibn Jumhan told us, Safina, may God be pleased with him, told me: Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, said to me: I free you and stipulate that you serve the Messenger of God, may God bless her. He said: I said: “If you had not stipulated that I should not have left the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would not have lived.” He said: “So she freed me and stipulated that I should serve the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as long as I live.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2849 - True"
"2850","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: A man said: Should I emancipate my son, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2850 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"2851","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Qutaybah told us, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Salem told us, they said: Ibrahim told us Bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi, Damra bin Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever owns a mahram relative is free.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2851 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim
 Abu Ali told us, with his chain of transmission, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of loyalty and the gift of it.” I heard Abu Ali Al-Hafiz says: “I only mentioned the second text so that Al-Zuhri could be falsified with it, on the authority of Damra.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. This is supported by the authentic and preserved hadith on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub."
"2852","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali told us, and Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Maruzi told us, they said: Muhammad told us Ibn Bakr Al-Barsani, Hammad Ibn Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, and Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever owns a relative of a mahram is free.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2852 - True"
"2853","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad Al-Hafiz, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani, and Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, And Zuhair bin Harb, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The child of adultery is the worst of the three.” Abu Hurairah said: “Because I would be wielded with a whip for the sake of God, it would be more beloved to me than to free the child of adultery.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it. “And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2853 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"2854","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abu Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The child of adultery is the worst of the three.”"
"2855","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Al-Hasan bin Omar bin Shaqiq told us, Salamah bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, he said: It was reported to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “For me to enjoy a whip in the path of God is more beloved to me than to free a child of fornication.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “The child of adultery is the worst of the three,” and “the dead are tortured by the crying of the living.” Aisha said: May God have mercy on Abu Hurairah. He misheard and injured badly. As for his saying: “Because I am wielded with a whip for the sake of God, that is more beloved to me.” “And that the child of fornication should be freed.” When it was revealed: “But he did not enter the Aqaba, nor would you know what the Aqaba is” [Al-Balad: 12] It was said: O Messenger of God, we do not have it. We are not emancipated except that one of us has a black slave girl who serves him and strives for him. If We commanded them, they would commit adultery and bring children. So we freed them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Because I am more beloved to me with a whip in the path of God than commanding adultery and then being set free.” The boy
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2855 - Salamah was not used as evidence by Muslim, but he was trustworthy and Ibn Rahawayh declared him weak.
 As for his saying: “The child of adultery is the worst of the three,” the hadith was not based on this. Rather, he was a hypocritical man who harmed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me and said: “Who will excuse me from so-and-so?” It was said: O Messenger of God, even though he was born of adultery, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is the worst of the three.” And God Almighty says: “And do not visit One bearer of burden is another burden.” [Al-An’am: 164]
 As for his saying: “The dead are tormented by the crying of the living,” the hadith was not based on this, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a house A Jewish man died, and his family were crying over him. He said: “They are crying over him, and he will be tortured.” And God Almighty says: “No.” God burdens a soul beyond its capacity.} [Al-Baqarah: 286] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"2856","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, and Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab Al-Shaarani told us, they said: Abu Salih Al-Masry Abdullah bin Salih, the writer of Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Omar bin Issa Al-Qurashi, then Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: A slave girl came to Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. She said: My master accused me, so he made me sit on the fire until my private part was burned. Omar said to her: Did he see that on you? She said: No. He said: Did you confess anything to him? She said: No, so Omar said: I have to do it, so when Omar saw the man, he said: Will I be tortured with the punishment of God? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I accused her about myself. He said: Did you see that on her? The man said: No. He said: So she recognized him? He said: No. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, had I not heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A slave shall not be led by his owner, nor a father by his child.” I would have taken her away from you. So he took him out, struck him with a hundred lashes, and said to the maid: Go, for you are free for the sake of God. You are God’s servant. And His Messenger, Abu Salih said: Al-Layth said: “And this saying is to be followed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2856 - Rather, Omar bin Isa denies the hadith"
